{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena","id":1305398,"title":"Exalted: Arena","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-16T21:35:01-07:00","id":1305398,"title":"Exalted: Arena","content":"LLLLLET'S GET READY TO RUMBLEEEEE!!!<br /> <br /> In this thread we pit foes against eachother and I roll out the fights. Exalted is a big complex system with lots of moving parts, how much does soak impact the game, how good is this combo of grapple enhancing charms, ect. Sometimes it's just hard to figure out what to do or how good something is in context. To that end we now have the Arena. Now, the arena isn't necessarily a white room, we might import some trees for cover, or make the whole thing submerged in waist high water. Let's talk about what it is, and what it is not.<br /> <br /> <br /> What it is:<ul><li>A place to gain some insight into how Exalted fights might go in particular situations</li> <li>A place to test some tactical options that you think might be cool, but aren't sure if they work</li> <li>A place to discuss those tactical options and implications</li> <li>A place to see second hand the spectacle of play-by-play exalted combat</li> </ul><br /> <br /> What it is not:<ul><li>A place to see expertly played and constructed perfectly tactical fights</li> <li>A place to figure out what builds/exalted can never beat other builds/exalted in any situation</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> I'll be running though some fights of younger DBs in groups against single Lunars next, probably. I'm going to take some more detailed notes on those to give a better idea of exactly what's going on. If anyone has any suggestions or requests I'm totally open, but keep in mind I'm doing most of these on my own so like, gigantic 10 combatant fights are difficult for me to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> As promised I have spun off a tangential topic from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297489-drlovemonkey-s-holistic-lunar-review\">this</a> thread into it's own thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297489-drlovemonkey-s-holistic-lunar-review?p=1305136#post1305136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've kind of used an Essence 5 DB here; does that imply that Essence 2-3 DBs would fare much worse, or is it more that they'd fare about the same (same kind of levels of probability or win or lose), simply because DBs tools don't really scale much up to Essence 5 in ways which are useful for this matchup? I guess my bias would be to be a bit more sanguine about the latter than former.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used Essence 5 DBs just to give them the best shot possible. They have some effects that are based on their Essence, as well as just giving them mote pools that were comparable to/better than the Lunars in question. As for charm usage, I don't think I used a single DB charm over Essence 3. The higher essence DB charms tend to be bigger and flashier, but not actually more accurate or powerful to be worth their cost on low hit chance attacks. Also a lot of them are teamwork based and that doesn't work in a 1v1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1297489-drlovemonkey-s-holistic-lunar-review?p=1305140#post1305140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not just the initiative, those distract gambits are still applying onslaught. They don\u2019t even need to be especially good at combat to be helpful. Even a non-exalt will most likely have enough i from their JB to contribute an attack that the anathema should Really spend to avoid. Assuming even One hits, it\u2019s about +3 to your eventual damage rolls, plus the onslaught for every attempted distraction.<br /> <br /> On top of that, you need Fire Aura to use it, right? Well, that limits you to the second turn of combat, but it doesn\u2019t mean the first turn is boring. I\u2019d advise focusing on Guard and Defend Other though, which leaves you plenty of room to use your many, many Fire based parry charms. Assuming you\u2019re a Big Target (you\u2019re a high-essence melee specialist so you probably are or can be), you might get the chance to use Fire Incites Water to a Riot of Clouds, but that would be pretty risky. Mostly you just want everyone to hold on to their JB result, then delay so all the distracts are happening before HFA and HFA is before the enemy resets.<br /> <br /> Obviously all this is melee focused, but even if you need to close distance, there\u2019s some fire charms in athletics that can help you out. They key thing is that your target doesn\u2019t want ANY of these things to happen, and has to either spend accordingly or pick and choose. Their best Defense against HFA is Hardness, but even if they\u2019re significantly armoured you probably also have Dragon Soul Burst and you\u2019re already prepped to build an aura for it.<br /> <br /> ANYWAY I won\u2019t do any more DB stuff here. Will gladly contribute to an Arena/theorycraft thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately a character can only benefit from one distract gambit at a time, so stacking them up multiple times on one character isn't doable. Also stacking onslaught penalties is normally a really great idea, but doing it with distract gambits against a celestial exalt isn't really a great idea. Solars have a charm that just flat negates all penalties to defense, and Lunars have one that halves penalties, ignores all penalties from lower initiative attackers, and another one that gives them a turn long defense boost and stops them from accruing onslaught penalties from attacks that miss them.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you're going 5v1 against a young Lunar with relatively experienced DBs the Lunar doesn't really have a chance anyway, as long as everyone can fight well and is taking it seriously. No Essence 1 Lunar has the motes to full excellency and cap-burst their defense/attack, six times a round for even one round, whereas the DBs can keep going for several.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T03:33:51-07:00","id":1305423,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in how effective a Lunar who's all about poison is. I have an Essence 5 snake-Lunar who has Snake Style and poison charms (adder fang, Mamba-and-Cobra x2, Poison Blood). I'm not sure how nasty poison actually is though. Is it something I should rely on?<br /> <br /> I also thought about building mutations; bite, venomous, potent, venom sacs. Potent can be pretty nasty. But that didn't fit with the build I had, of hitting people with Snake Style. You'd need to build a grapple-character really. I wonder how good that would be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there's tons and tons of builds you could try. But if you're not sure what,<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually thought this thread would be an Arena where people would try out their characters against each other, which is quite different. (Not to say your idea isn't good; it is). But would people be interested in some kind of thread like that? I need practice with my PCs in combat, honestly, I tend to forget all the charms they can use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T05:08:23-07:00","id":1305440,"title":"","content":"Aw maaaan. Ah well. Even one distractor backing up HFA is not to be sniffed at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T08:45:11-07:00","id":1305487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305423#post1305423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in how effective a Lunar who's all about poison is. I have an Essence 5 snake-Lunar who has Snake Style and poison charms (adder fang, Mamba-and-Cobra x2, Poison Blood). I'm not sure how nasty poison actually is though. Is it something I should rely on?<br /> <br /> I also thought about building mutations; bite, venomous, potent, venom sacs. Potent can be pretty nasty. But that didn't fit with the build I had, of hitting people with Snake Style. You'd need to build a grapple-character really. I wonder how good that would be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there's tons and tons of builds you could try. But if you're not sure what,<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually thought this thread would be an Arena where people would try out their characters against each other, which is quite different. (Not to say your idea isn't good; it is). But would people be interested in some kind of thread like that? I need practice with my PCs in combat, honestly, I tend to forget all the charms they can use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe poison Lunar is the one who can go 2v1 against the DBs. I didn\u2019t necessarily want to make a thread where people battle out builds against eachother because that can eat up a ton of posts as they go back and forth, and might end up somewhat adversarial. <br /> <br /> EDIT: wait, if they\u2019re Essence 5 we might have do use more than 2 DBs to make it more even.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305440#post1305440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aw maaaan. Ah well. Even one distractor backing up HFA is not to be sniffed at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah absolutely, especially after the recent changes to it that discount charm activations on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-17-2019, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T09:26:06-07:00","id":1305496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305487#post1305487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn\u2019t necessarily want to make a thread where people battle out builds against eachother because that can eat up a ton of posts as they go back and fort</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, after suggesting that I realised it would take ages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if they\u2019re Essence 5 we might have do use more than 2 DBs to make it more even. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be identical to the one I use. I'm just generally interested in how effective poison-builds are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T11:30:58-07:00","id":1305519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305496#post1305496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, after suggesting that I realised it would take ages.<br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be identical to the one I use. I'm just generally interested in how effective poison-builds are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you be using Octopus and Spider Barrage? Because I sense that that will make a very large difference. I can probably run one or two combats today once I know that. I'll adjust the second combat based on how the first one turned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T11:49:02-07:00","id":1305521,"title":"","content":"I don't have it. I guess I could get it in future, but I don't have much of that tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T12:04:12-07:00","id":1305525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305521#post1305521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have it. I guess I could get it in future, but I don't have much of that tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>k I'll run the first one with and if the poison Lunar wrecks faces off I'll try without.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T17:48:23-07:00","id":1305600,"title":"","content":"I would assume that probably the biggest factor in facing a Poison lunar is whether one of the DBs is wood caste.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Tbc, they're not immune, but once they hit bonfire those resistance rolls will be a heck of a lot easier. Not much above Essence 1 in medicine should they have access to it, but even Venom Expulsion Method and the Excellency would be enormously helpful. Even moreso combined with Ailment Sensing Meditation.<br /> <br /> Of course the question of whether the DBs In question KNOW they'll be facing poison and HAVE medicine charms is another one entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-17-2019, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T17:50:24-07:00","id":1305602,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, in addition to my other 'how well do lower essence DB hold up' questions from the last thread, how effective a Lunar with little native combat murder ability can be just rolling with dangerous animal spirit shapes and maybe one or two low Attribute combat charms from Dex or Stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T18:01:12-07:00","id":1305605,"title":"","content":"Okay, wow, that took a long time. I'm not sure I can do much of this on my own. I think I'll definitely need to get some friends to help if I do many more than 3 combatants. First let's look at our combatants<br /> <br /> Lunar<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Lunar Essence 3 Per:18 iph:37 (46)<br /> <br /> Full Moon 5 in physical stats and Wits<br /> <br /> <br /> Offenseive Charms<br /> Snake Style (Entire)<br /> Dexterity up to Supreme Predator Alacrity and Thousand Claw<br /> Strength up to Unstoppable Beast Force Blow<br /> Stamina up to Mamba-and Cobra/Poison Blood<br /> Wits Excellency<br /> <br /> Defensive Charms<br /> Stamina up to Incomperable Bezoar Nature, Stone Rhino Skin<br /> Dexterity up to Sensing Deadly Flow and Fleet Gazelle<br /> 3 Ox Bodies<br /> <br /> Artifacts<br /> Light armor<br /> Daiklave<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> <br /> Attack:<br /> Daiklave 14 (17 damage) O: 5<br /> Parry 7<br /> Soak: 10 Hardness 4<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fire Aspect Swordfighter<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Fire DB Essence 3 Per: 14 iph: 24 (35) <br /> <br /> Fire aspect with 5 dex, 3 in str and sta, all abilities at 5 with specialty<br /> <br /> Offensive Charms<br /> Melee up to Fire Incites Water, Burning Pinacle Strike<br /> <br /> Defensive Charms<br /> Melee up to Fire Incites Water<br /> Resistance up to Earth Bears Witness<br /> 3 Ox Bodies<br /> <br /> Artifacts<br /> Daiklave<br /> Heavy Armor<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> <br /> Attack:<br /> Daiklave 14 (15 damage) O:5<br /> Parry 7<br /> Soak: 14 Hardness: 10<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Water Aspect Brawler<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Water DB Essence 3 Per: 14 iph: 26 (35) <br /> <br /> Fire aspect with 5 dex, 3 in str and sta, all abilities at 5 with specialty<br /> <br /> Offensive Charms<br /> Brawl up to Hammering Wave Tech, Waves Swallow Mountain, Embracing the Violent Flow, Crushing Avalance Grasp, Entangling Roots Embrace<br /> <br /> Defensive Charms<br /> Dodge up to Threshold Warding Stance and Flow with Strife<br /> Resistance up to Earth Bears Witness<br /> 3 Ox Bodies<br /> <br /> Artifacts<br /> Smashfists<br /> Light Armor<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> <br /> Attack:<br /> Fist 16 (13 damage) O:3<br /> Dodge 6<br /> Soak: 8 Hardness: 4<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Round 1:</b><br /> The Lunar and the Dragonblooded square off and join combat! The Lunar rolls in with 16 after a full excellency...and so does the Fire aspect, the water aspect lags behind with 10. We flip a coin to see who goes first and it's Fire aspect! He slices in with a full excellency and Crimson Fang Bite, the Lunar defends with Rhino's Skin, Impenetrable Beast Armor, and the Stamina excellency. Some of those were activated retroactively because the DB hits with his whopping 15 successes! For 10 dice of damage, dealing 4, but with two 1s on the roll it becomes 2 damage.<br /> <br /> The Lunar retaliates with a sharp smash to the DB with her daiklave, full excellency, Striking Cobra Tech, Finding Needle's Eye, Divine Predator Strike AND Armor Penetrating Fang! Fire defends with a full excellency and ISoS. Lunar easily hits the DB getting a near miraculous 22 successes in total with six 10s. Rolling 33 damage and dealing 18 Fire is crashed. Lunar reflexively activates Snake style.<br /> <br /> Water aspect attempts a grapple with full excellency, Inescapable Whirlpool and Entangling Roots Embrace. Failing to connect<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2:</b><br /> Lunar attacks Water with Striking Cobra Tech and 5m excellency. Water defends with full excellency and ISoS. Lunar hits with 13, rolling 18 damage and dealing 12<br /> <br /> Fire attacks with full excellency and Crimson fang, slashing wildly at the confidant Lunar. Hitting by 5 and dealing 5 damage<br /> <br /> Water attempts full excellency and Hammering Wave tech, hitting by 3 for 6 dice of damage, but coming away with only 1 rolled damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3:</b><br /> Lunar attacks with Octopus and Spider Barrage, running out of motes now she needs to get this off while she can still apply 4 poisons in one attack. Going all out in a flurry of attacks with her Daiklave dripping poison. Fire defends with Flame Borne Interception and an excellency, water defends with dodge excellency. The first two attacks both hit water, but by one success each. The third attack hits fire, but the fourth attack misses him.<br /> <br /> Water comes away with 3 rounds of poison applied to her, and fire with only 2. Water also takes 6 total decisive damage and Fire takes 5 from the attacks<br /> <br /> Fire takes some initiative damage from poison, and attacks Lunar with his full excellency, but due to Snake Style and the poison penalties, fails to connect.<br /> <br /> Water takes a lethal from the poison and attacks with full excellency, but due to the same penalties, fails to connect.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 4:</b><br /> Lunar attacks fire with an unenhanced attack, hits by 3 for 5 damage, dealing 2<br /> <br /> Fire takes 2L from poison, attacks with excellency but penalties are too strong, fails to connect<br /> <br /> Water takes 1L from poison, attacking the Lunar with an excellency and hits for 4 damage, dealing 3<br /> <br /> <b>Round 5:</b><br /> Lunar attacks Fire with Finding Needle's Eye, fire does not defend with essence. Lunar hits and deals a total of 3 damage<br /> <br /> Water takes 2 damage from poison and resets to base initiative, attacks Lunar with an excellency, but fails to connect<br /> <br /> Fire attacks Lunar with excellency, fails to connect<br /> <br /> <b>Round 6:</b><br /> Lunar attacks fire with Finding Needle's Eye, fire does not use essence to defend. Lunar rolls badly and does not connect, slipping up in her advantage over the pair of terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Water attacks Lunar, Lunar does not spend essence, but water fails to connect.<br /> <br /> Fire rushes in slashes wildly with a small excellency and hits by 0. Dealing 1 damage for every die rolled Fire gets INITIATIVE SHIFT!!! Blazing back into the fight, veins finally clear of poison, the Fire aspect attacks again immediately with a discounted full excellency, Lunar defends with an excellency and Agile Beast Defense, but to no avail! Fire strikes again and deals another 5 damage<br /> <br /> <b>Round 7:</b><br /> Fire strikes the Lunar with discounted excellency and Crimson Fang, hits again, the Lunar unable to handle the onslaught penalties, and no longer benefiting so much from Snake Form. Taking another 5 damage.<br /> <br /> Water strikes with Pounding Surf Style, hitting and dealing 3 damage.<br /> <br /> Lunar goes in and full excellency attacks Water, trying to avoid being clinched now that she can't rely on dodging a decisive with ease, being so low on motes. Water defends with dodge excellency and is hit, taking 6 damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 8:</b><br /> Fire strikes at the moteless Lunar with full excellency and hits, dealing 3 damage<br /> <br /> Water attacks again and deals 2 damage to the Lunar<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks fire with full excellency, trying to knock Fire out of his discount, but the Lunar fails to connect again thanks to the DB's full excellency defense and a bad dice rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 9:</b><br /> Fire launches a full excellency attack at the Lunar, dealing 8 damage<br /> <br /> Water attacks the Lunar, hits, but deals nothing<br /> <br /> Lunar resets to base initiative and hits Fire, dealing 5 damage and finally resetting his discount<br /> <br /> <b>Round 10:</b><br /> Fire attacks the Lunar with a full excellency and Crimson Fang, dealing 6 damage<br /> <br /> Water attempts to clinch the Lunar with over 20 motes now saved up from not enhancing attacks. Water hits, makes the grapple roll, and full excellencies the control roll, rolling amazing against the moteless Lunar and clinching the lunar for 7 rounds!<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks Water trying to break free, using Ferocious Biting Tooth and Divine Predator Strike to try and clear the clinch. Unwise choice though as the attack misses!!!<br /> <br /> <b>Round 11:</b><br /> With the Lunar clinched and with Fire aspect having 33 initiative, and Water having 10, they decide it's time to end this. Fire attacks with Harnessed Firestorm Assualt, giving as much free excellency to each attack as he can, an also activating Crimson Fang Bite one last time. All attacks hit and deal a total of 18 damage, driving his daiklave into the Lunar.<br /> <br /> Water aspect does a decisive throw using Hammering Wave Technique and releasing the remainder of her rounds of control and dealing a total of 7 decisive damage, ending the fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> AGGHHH my god that took so LONG. It was actually a pretty awesome fight. I skipped over stunts, but I assumes everyone was doing at least a level 1 stunt for each effect, and that any higher level stunts were being canceled. That fight was close though, it could have ended way sooner if the Lunar didn't hit with 3/4 of her Octopus and Spider Barrage of attacks. Also she definitely got a ton of mileage out of Snake Form. Also though, if the DBs didn't have 7 dice to their poison resist rolls they would have been in a much worse way there, and those penalties were crushing.<br /> <br /> So looking back at the viability of the poison build, even against people with a good resistance it was extremely effective, and even while being outnumbered. The penalties it inflicts have synergy with Snake's penalty inflicting form. I wish I'd gotten the chance to check it out with Essence Venom Strike, I think it might have worked out better as a way to try and focus fire down on of the DBs, but I'm not running that fight again to see. I didn't personally record initiative round for round, so it might be difficult to follow that fight up above, but I'm not sure how I could include it without there being information overload.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T18:39:02-07:00","id":1305614,"title":"","content":"Man, really thought the Lunar had it after that first turn Crash, but I guess the motes just Weren't there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T18:53:39-07:00","id":1305618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305614#post1305614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, really thought the Lunar had it after that first turn Crash, but I guess the motes just Weren't there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, when you're trying to defend against two highly competent opponents, it's really hard to keep up. Unfortunately the Lunar didn't have enough initiative to go for full Octopus and Spider poison right off turn 1, because the DBs both had too much hardness, the attacks would have just failed. Against foes without hardness that might have been a better way to go, just get that poison online right away. Then again, that's why Dragonblooded can be scary, they're very often clad in heirloom armor that gives them that kind of protection.<br /> <br /> Also I want to point out that I totally forgot about anima flux, before the Lunar was crashed she had hardness and could just ignore it. A crashed character has 0 hardness though, so she should have been taking 4 damage a turn from the Fire and Water anima banners. In my defense there's a LOT of moving parts here that I have to keep track of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T21:58:50-07:00","id":1305638,"title":"","content":"Oof! Yeah losing hardness on Crash really Amps up the danger from anima flux. Would combo great with White Veil for initiative poison on the DB side.<br /> <br /> Although being On Fire is not particularly thematic for white veil so...<br /> <br /> I\u2019m setting up a fite of my own, I\u2019d like to see how Solars handle an immaculate style. I\u2019ll be testing a fresh Solar Earth Dragon Master against a veteran Fire Dragon Master.<br /> <br /> I expect the solar to clean up handily but any competencies or factors to consider would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T00:06:47-07:00","id":1305654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305602#post1305602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, in addition to my other 'how well do lower essence DB hold up' questions from the last thread, how effective a Lunar with little native combat murder ability can be just rolling with dangerous animal spirit shapes and maybe one or two low Attribute combat charms from Dex or Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could definitely run that, and it would be way easier than what I just did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305638#post1305638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oof! Yeah losing hardness on Crash really Amps up the danger from anima flux. Would combo great with White Veil for initiative poison on the DB side.<br /> <br /> Although being On Fire is not particularly thematic for white veil so...<br /> <br /> I\u2019m setting up a fite of my own, I\u2019d like to see how Solars handle an immaculate style. I\u2019ll be testing a fresh Solar Earth Dragon Master against a veteran Fire Dragon Master.<br /> <br /> I expect the solar to clean up handily but any competencies or factors to consider would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Solar is probably going to dominate that fight, especially if you give him some support abilities. Unless you're pitting Essence 1 MA Supernal Solar against Essence 5 DB, then...could be pretty close?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T04:15:58-07:00","id":1305683,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s the plan. There are more than a few charms in the Dragon styles that go off Essence values, so that swings things to the DB.<br /> <br /> Also, ironically, making a fresh solar and giving them a whole Dragon style actually cuts them Off from something\u2019s. Notably Solar Dodge, there\u2019s just not a lot of room left after 12 charms and you\u2019re still limited to Essence 1 charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T05:27:05-07:00","id":1305700,"title":"","content":"Battle really interesting the Lunar seemed to have a very clear initial advantage but the Dragon-Blooded managed to resist enough and when the poison arrived it was not enough and they ended up winning. Thank you very much for putting so much effort.<br /> It was very even and it seems that the Lunar had bad luck in several key points, could have gone in any direction.<br /> The combat in Exalted has so many variables that there are always surprises or if X had had Z everything could have been different.<br /> Supernatural is always a very considerable advantage for a Solar.<br /> What is the next showdown you plan to do? Are suggestions accepted or do you already have all the confrontations planned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T05:47:45-07:00","id":1305705,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it seemed like it could have gone the other way. Good fight!<br /> <br /> You mentioned Essence-Venom Strike; I don't think it's much better than the much cheaper Adder Fang generally... but it's brutal against Crashed enemies, because they don't get any roll to reduce the poison's duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T05:52:15-07:00","id":1305707,"title":"","content":"If running out of motes is the problem with martial artist lunars alone vs multiple opponents (which makes sense comboing all those charms), I think animal form combat might have a better chance with all the persistent bonuses you get for just 4m.<br /> <br /> Since DBs dont have anything that lets them rise from prone faster unless I've missed something, Tiger Claw Swat (reflexively knock enemies back and prone them after you parry/clash their attack) should be an excellent charm for Lunars fighting DBs. Combine it with pestletail or hellboar form (both of which are very powerfull animal forms that get big bonuses attacking prone enemies) and it could be a world of hurt with Octopus-and-Spider Barrage getting +5 damage on each hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-18-2019, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T13:11:58-07:00","id":1305795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dagurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305700#post1305700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Battle really interesting the Lunar seemed to have a very clear initial advantage but the Dragon-Blooded managed to resist enough and when the poison arrived it was not enough and they ended up winning. Thank you very much for putting so much effort.<br /> It was very even and it seems that the Lunar had bad luck in several key points, could have gone in any direction.<br /> The combat in Exalted has so many variables that there are always surprises or if X had had Z everything could have been different.<br /> Supernatural is always a very considerable advantage for a Solar.<br /> What is the next showdown you plan to do? Are suggestions accepted or do you already have all the confrontations planned?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm always open to suggestions, I'm going to try and satisfy as many as possible with each fight. For example I'm thinking of a less combat optomized Lunar, lower essence, in a shapeshifted form. Probably a tiger form with tiger swatting as her main attack, but not 5s in every stat. I might also bring in some tall grass and let it try and stealth attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305705#post1305705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it seemed like it could have gone the other way. Good fight!<br /> <br /> You mentioned Essence-Venom Strike; I don't think it's much better than the much cheaper Adder Fang generally... but it's brutal against Crashed enemies, because they don't get any roll to reduce the poison's duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, although it's also a simple charm so I can't combo it with OaSB. In retrospect I shouldn't have tried OaSB and just used that Essence Venom to take down one crashed DB for good, and then it would have been a 1v1 which the Lunar would almost certainly win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305707#post1305707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since DBs dont have anything that lets them rise from prone faster unless I've missed something, Tiger Claw Swat (reflexively knock enemies back and prone them after you parry/clash their attack) should be an excellent charm for Lunars fighting DBs. Combine it with pestletail or hellboar form (both of which are very powerfull animal forms that get big bonuses attacking prone enemies) and it could be a world of hurt with Octopus-and-Spider Barrage getting +5 damage on each hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably with the pestletail, but I'm not sure if you can claim the damage bonus with a hellboar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T13:20:35-07:00","id":1305797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305707#post1305707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If running out of motes is the problem with martial artist lunars alone vs multiple opponents (which makes sense comboing all those charms), I think animal form combat might have a better chance with all the persistent bonuses you get for just 4m.<br /> <br /> Since DBs dont have anything that lets them rise from prone faster unless I've missed something, Tiger Claw Swat (reflexively knock enemies back and prone them after you parry/clash their attack) should be an excellent charm for Lunars fighting DBs. Combine it with pestletail or hellboar form (both of which are very powerfull animal forms that get big bonuses attacking prone enemies) and it could be a world of hurt with Octopus-and-Spider Barrage getting +5 damage on each hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean Boar Tusk Crocodile? Or tooth? I forget the T word but I recall that one can savage people knocked down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T13:33:13-07:00","id":1305799,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in seeing a Melee Solar based on full defense and attacking with counterattacks against both Lunars and Dragon-Bloodeds with Ready in Eight Directions Stance and Victorious Wreath. It is a build in which I am very curious.<br /> On the Lunar side one based on Defense of Stamina and / or Berserker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T13:55:30-07:00","id":1305806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dagurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305799#post1305799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in seeing a Melee Solar based on full defense and attacking with counterattacks against both Lunars and Dragon-Bloodeds with Ready in Eight Directions Stance and Victorious Wreath. It is a build in which I am very curious.<br /> On the Lunar side one based on Defense of Stamina and / or Berserker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean against multiple opponents or just one?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, to be clear, you're not talking about flurrying a Full Defense action with Ready in Eight Directions, right? I don't actually think that's possible as RIED is a simple charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-18-2019, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T15:11:28-07:00","id":1305824,"title":"","content":"Multiple opponents against Dragon-Blooded, a unique opponent against the Lunar; although in this last case, against a single opponent it is probably more efficient to limit to using Solar counterattck.<br /> Now that I look at the charms more closely you make me think. REID refers to Solar counterattack which does not count as using action, but REID is Simple. I imagine that Simple has preference and prevents using it with Full Defense. Even without Full Defense I would still like to see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25189,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","user":"Dagurasu","date":". 04-18-2019, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T15:38:03-07:00","id":1305831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dagurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305824#post1305824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple opponents against Dragon-Blooded, a unique opponent against the Lunar; although in this last case, against a single opponent it is probably more efficient to limit to using Solar counterattck.<br /> Now that I look at the charms more closely you make me think. REID refers to Solar counterattack which does not count as using action, but REID is Simple. I imagine that Simple has preference and prevents using it with Full Defense. Even without Full Defense I would still like to see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, the Simple type of REID means that it can only be used on your turn and can't be placed in a flurry, it's a very important thing in keeping some semblance of balance. Without the Full Defense it will still probably dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T15:59:01-07:00","id":1305834,"title":"","content":"Certainly, but at least Solar Counterattack can still be combined with Full Defense, more expensive to respond to multiple counterattacks and nothing prevents a reset to Base Initiative, but it is a good option, especially against a single opponent.<br /> I imagine that the motes gained with Victorious Wreath will still be very valuable. At the very least it makes the +1 of Parry with Dipping Swallow Defense when Fivefold Bulwark is active pay for itself in a successful defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T15:59:58-07:00","id":1305835,"title":"","content":"This is neat, although I have a tiny quibble---why was the initial 16i tie between Lunar and Fire broken with a coin flip when a) Clashes are neat and b) Fire Melee <i>loves</i> Clashes?<br /> Again, a tiny quibble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T16:08:12-07:00","id":1305838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305835#post1305835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is neat, although I have a tiny quibble---why was the initial 16i tie between Lunar and Fire broken with a coin flip when a) Clashes are neat and b) Fire Melee <i>loves</i> Clashes?<br /> Again, a tiny quibble.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my reasoning there was because the Lunar didn't want to clash the DB, for obvious reasons, and wanted an opportunity to activate snake style reflexively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T17:11:49-07:00","id":1305854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305797#post1305797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean Boar Tusk Crocodile? Or tooth? I forget the T word but I recall that one can savage people knocked down</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant Hellboar with &quot;Death Stomp: The hellboar\u2019s decisive stomp attacks deal +5 damage against prone enemies&quot;, which does the same as the Boar Tusks Killing Strike but Hellboars have better stats and merits. Prone them with Tiger Claw Swat when they attack you on their turn, then move in and flurry 4-5 of those with Octopus-and-Spider Barrage and it adds up to an extra 20-25 damage over a flurry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T17:35:29-07:00","id":1305858,"title":"","content":"I think a poison lunar is better served by mutations than snake style. Being able to have Potent and Paralytic venom would make all the difference, though it\u2019d be harder to apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T18:43:01-07:00","id":1305876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305795#post1305795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm always open to suggestions, I'm going to try and satisfy as many as possible with each fight. For example I'm thinking of a less combat optomized Lunar, lower essence, in a shapeshifted form. Probably a tiger form with tiger swatting as her main attack, but not 5s in every stat. I might also bring in some tall grass and let it try and stealth attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>May I make a suggestion, see how far you can get with a Changing Moon with it's only combat stat of Dex at 5 (Str and Sta can be lower, 2 or 3) and maybe just the excellency for Str and Sta. So Social Primary, Mental Secondary and Phys Tertiary, but with a rocking animal style for combat (so a lot like my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread#post1293395\">knight of Bone and Ivory</a>, which is designed to be a more social based character.)<br /> <br /> But try the intimidate trick! (Predator's Menace Latent) I always wanted to see how that would work in actual play! (You'll have to be a Hippo rather than a Pestletail in that case, but you can change back and forth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T19:28:48-07:00","id":1305881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305876#post1305876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> May I make a suggestion, see how far you can get with a Changing Moon with it's only combat stat of Dex at 5 (Str and Sta can be lower, 2 or 3) and maybe just the excellency for Str and Sta. So Social Primary, Mental Secondary and Phys Tertiary, but with a rocking animal style for combat (so a lot like my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread#post1293395\">knight of Bone and Ivory</a>, which is designed to be a more social based character.)<br /> <br /> But try the intimidate trick! (Predator's Menace Latent) I always wanted to see how that would work in actual play! (You'll have to be a Hippo rather than a Pestletail in that case, but you can change back and forth).</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one is that intimidate trick exactly?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also I'm not sure if it's possible to know just the excellency for non-favoured attributes, unfortunately. You need at least 2 charms or to have it rated at 5, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-18-2019, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T20:05:40-07:00","id":1305885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305881#post1305881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which one is that intimidate trick exactly?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also I'm not sure if it's possible to know just the excellency for non-favoured attributes, unfortunately. You need at least 2 charms or to have it rated at 5, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: Intimidate Trick<br /> <br /> If you are in an animal form with an Intimidate Pool (so Gorillas, Hippos, Boar Tusked Crocs etc) you can take a Universal latent talent called Predator\u2019s Menace which allows you to 1/scene strip extra success over foes resolve in Initiative when you roll to Intimidate them. <br /> <br /> So the trick is you really gun the check after JB when their Init pool is low and just crash the whole lot of them. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s a great method for a socially focused Lunar to just blow out the competition Turn 1 (I had a write up on it, give me a sec...) Best part is it bypassed basically every mundane defence against this sort of thing, even Fakharhu is pretty helpless.<br /> <br /> Re:Str and Sta Excellencies: Yeah I know I was recommending taking two charms for each.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, here ya go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1293704#post1293704\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1293704#post1293704\"> [Ex 3 Lunars] Glorious Argent Beastiary! (A Lunar's Character Thread) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1293704#post1293704\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1293704#post1293704 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I originally posted this on RPG.net as I had figured that we had enough preview material released to start making characters (also to drum up some hype, always the </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-18-2019, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T20:17:29-07:00","id":1305888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305885#post1305885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re: Intimidate Trick<br /> <br /> If you are in an animal form with an Intimidate Pool (so Gorillas, Hippos, Boar Tusked Crocs etc) you can take a Universal latent talent called Predator\u2019s Menace which allows you to 1/scene strip extra success over foes resolve in Initiative when you roll to Intimidate them.<br /> <br /> So the trick is you really gun the check after JB when their Init pool is low and just crash the whole lot of them.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a great method for a socially focused Lunar to just blow out the competition Turn 1 (I had a write up on it, give me a sec...) Best part is it bypassed basically every mundane defence against this sort of thing, even Fakharhu is pretty helpless.<br /> <br /> Re:Str and Sta Excellencies: Yeah I know I was recommending taking two charms for each.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, here ya go.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1293704#post1293704\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...04#post1293704</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wow that's crazy, yeah sure I'll give it a shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T20:23:12-07:00","id":1305891,"title":"","content":"I heartily recommend Hippo form while you do this so you can Crash all sorts of dynasts Round 1 (and benefit from the initiative Crashing Others grants you) and also be a walking Tank with Daiklaive equivalent chompers while you are at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T22:07:31-07:00","id":1305903,"title":"","content":"Actually, tell you what, I'll stat up a Chargen Ess 1 Lunar for use, since it was I who suggested? Then you can put it in your bloodsport arena. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T22:39:20-07:00","id":1305910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305903#post1305903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, tell you what, I'll stat up a Chargen Ess 1 Lunar for use, since it was I who suggested? Then you can put it in your bloodsport arena. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that works, considering it's an AoE destruction style build I've been thinking of pitting her up against 3 DBs, an Earth Immaculate, Fire twinblade specialist, and a wood archer. I predict that one of them will be gone in the first turn though so it shouldn't be so bad to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T00:25:24-07:00","id":1305921,"title":"","content":"Oh my god, that Intimidate trick is amazing, and exactly what I need for my own Lunar! Heck yea.<br /> <br /> EDIT: looking it over though, it seems like it\u2019d only apply to one enemy? It says you reduce the Initiative of An Enemy that was intimidated by the excess successes rolled, limit once per scene,<br /> <br /> Still great though! Notably because you can absolutely flurry the intimidate and attack actions. Or Guard, defend other, etc if you prefer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-19-2019, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T00:59:42-07:00","id":1305927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305921#post1305921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god, that Intimidate trick is amazing, and exactly what I need for my own Lunar! Heck yea.<br /> <br /> EDIT: looking it over though, it seems like it\u2019d only apply to one enemy? It says you reduce the Initiative of An Enemy that was intimidated by the excess successes rolled, limit once per scene,<br /> <br /> Still great though! Notably because you can absolutely flurry the intimidate and attack actions. Or Guard, defend other, etc if you prefer</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Vance, it applies to as many as you can normally apply your Intimidate to, sans Orichalcum rule intervention. (Answered on Discord)<br /> <br /> Of course Applying Intimidate to many foes leads to a penalty of multiple targets.<br /> <br /> Of course Lunars have a charm to bypass this. (Argent Songbird Voice)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-19-2019, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T01:24:29-07:00","id":1305929,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is <b>Membe the Mouth</b> for your perusal. More than half his Charms are in Social Trees.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Membe the Mouth</b></u><br /> <br /> Nexus River Rat, Aspiring Crime Lord. Membe was the bastard child of a Guild Factor whose Mother died during childbirth. Never knowing his parentage, he ran with the Urchin gangs of the Nexus Riverways and in time became a charismatic leader of tribes of other Orphans. Exalting when fighting off the Crime Lords of the Nexus Underbelly sent to eradicate them by a greedy Guild Factor (unknowingly, his own father), he wages a one youth war to replace the leadership of the vicious Five Families with himself as the head.<br /> <br /> Bonus fact: Him and Seven Devils Clever were childhood sweethearts in the grime and muck of the Nexus underworld, but over the course of one particularly deadly pitched brawl, they each thought the other dead. Since Seven Devils now operates in secret and Membe wears many faces, they currently don't know about what happened to the other, though they are based literally just 10 blocks apart.<br /> <br /> Caste: Changing Moon<br /> Spirit Shape: Nexus River Horse (Hippo)<br /> Tell: Unusual Hide OOOOO<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attributes:</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Social (Primary)</b><br /> <br /> Charisma OOOOO (Caste)<br /> Manipulation OO<br /> Appearance OOOOO (Caste)<br /> <br /> <b>Physical (Secondary)</b><br /> <br /> Strength OO<br /> Dexterity OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Stamina OOO<br /> <br /> <b>Mental (Tertiary)</b><br /> <br /> Intelligence O<br /> Perception OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Wits OO<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities (8BP Spent)</b><br /> <br /> Athletics OO<br /> Awareness OOO (Specialty: Always Throws the First Punch)<br /> Brawl OOOOO (Specialty: Hippo)<br /> Dodge OO<br /> Integrity OO<br /> Larceny OO (Specialty: Concealing Evidence)<br /> Linguistics O<br /> Performance OO<br /> Presence OOOOO (Specialty: Threatening Glare)<br /> Resistance OO<br /> Socialize OOO<br /> Stealth OO<br /> Survival O<br /> <br /> <b>Merits (3BP Spent)</b><br /> <br /> Unusual Hide OOOOO (Tell)<br /> Backing (Silver Pact) O<br /> Influence (Nexus) O<br /> Followers O (Toughs and Touts)<br /> Heart's Blood O (Pestletail, Cat, Housefly, other Nexus City animals)<br /> Stolen Faces O (5 anonymous workers, prostitutes and functionaries of Nexus)<br /> Language (Riverspeak)<br /> Predator's Menace Latent Ability OOO<br /> <br /> <b>Charms by Attribute (4BP spent)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Universal</b><br /> Quicksilver Second Face<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b><br /> Appearance Excellency<br /> Glance Oration Technique<br /> Predator or Prey Mirror<br /> Feral Smile Tactic<br /> Subtle Silver Declaration<br /> Moon's Hidden Face<br /> <br /> <b>Charisma</b><br /> Charisma Excellency<br /> Argent Songbird Voice<br /> Poised Lion Attitude<br /> <br /> <b>Manipulation</b><br /> Manipulation Excellency<br /> Moonlight Curtain Drawn<br /> Inexplicable Mystery Incarnation<br /> <br /> <b>Dexterity</b><br /> Dexterity Excellency<br /> Sinuous Striking Grace<br /> Agile Beast Defense<br /> Bending Before the Storm<br /> <br /> <b>Stamina</b><br /> Stamina Excellency<br /> Impenetrable Beast Armor<br /> Durant Quicksilver Adaptation<br /> <br /> <b>Perception</b><br /> Perception Excellency<br /> Unwavering Predator's Eye<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment</b><br /> Buff Jacket<br /> Brass Knuckles (as Cestus)<br /> Winning, Unnervingly Wide Smile<br /> Salvaged book of poetry with the following verse that he finds amusing:<br /> <i>I shoot the <b>Hippopotamus</b> with bullets made of <b>platinum</b>, because if I use the leaden one his hide is sure to flatten em.</i><br /> <br /> Any other information needed?<br /> <br /> Combat is:<br /> <br /> 1. Go First thanks to Sinuous Striking Grace<br /> 2. Crash all foes thanks to Predator's Menace (remember to just buy successes with your Excellency due to Argent Songbird)<br /> 3. Murder one of them (Poised Lion Attitude)<br /> 4. Change into Pestletail Form as a Reflexive if needed for 22 Soak (and Sta Excellency can cover after damage has been determined thanks to Charms) but even the Hippo already has 18 soak<br /> 5. Profit.<br /> <br /> Edit: Won't Crashed Dragonblooded (Hardness 0) be susceptible to each other's Aura? Amusing. A battle of self harm and attrition might work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-19-2019, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T05:49:17-07:00","id":1305974,"title":"","content":"Dragon Blooded have blanket anima flux immunity. They don't need any natural hardness or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:03:22-07:00","id":1306210,"title":"","content":"Ok I have statted up a Supernal Earth Dragon specialist and an E5 Fire Dragon Specialist.<br /> <br /> It took me several days because about halfway through I realised I had formatted them in such a way that it would be absolute hell to refer to them while resolving the combat, so I started less complex QC sheets alongside their longform sheets. Aaaaand rewrote the charm text to be easier to refer to.<br /> <br /> Then I reformatted their QC sheets.<br /> <br /> Then I realised I left some stuff off an reformatted them again.<br /> <br /> Then I realised they had a bunch of charms on their QC sheets that they straight up would not use at all.<br /> <br /> Then I realised that taking off those charms had messed up the formatting of the QC sheets.<br /> <br /> I made some mistakes, is what I'm saying. But they're all ready and done now, so I'll post the results of that once I've bashed them against eachother (So like, September, at this rate.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T00:37:30-07:00","id":1306461,"title":"","content":"Say, DrLoveMonkey, did you need anything else for the character I made or is it good to go?<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T00:51:41-07:00","id":1306462,"title":"","content":"No it's good to go, I just had a gigantic exam today so I haven't been able to post anything on anything that I had to actually think about. Hence why I can comment on DB stuff, haha. I'll have actual free time tomorrow for the first time in a week though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T00:55:42-07:00","id":1306464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1306462#post1306462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it's good to go, I just had a gigantic exam today so I haven't been able to post anything on anything that I had to actually think about. Hence why I can comment on DB stuff, haha. I'll have actual free time tomorrow for the first time in a week though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, hope the exam went swimmingly? No hurry, was just wondering if you needed the info in QC format or whatnot. But if its okay, great!<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T01:19:06-07:00","id":1306470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1306464#post1306464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, hope the exam went swimmingly? No hurry, was just wondering if you needed the info in QC format or whatnot. But if its okay, great!<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>It, uh, went okay. It was extremely dull, which is rare at this level. The info in QC format might be helpful though, especially since I'm making a kind of abridged trio of DBs to fight them as well. Even more especially because this is going to be a hell of a long fight if the Lunar can't just end it quick enough, because there's just nothing in the DB charmset that lets them touch that kind of soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T01:54:40-07:00","id":1306476,"title":"","content":"Sure thing, I can see about QC formatting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Membe the Mouth</b><br /> <br /> Essence:2 Willpower :5 Join Battle: 9 dice (+5 for 5m, +10 for 10m)<br /> Personal: 16 Peripheral 38<br /> <br /> Actions (Hippo Form): Threaten 11 dice (+5 for 5m, +10 for 10m) Endure Heat: 5 dice; Feats of Strength: 10 dice (may attempt Strength 5 feats; see Beast of Burden); Resist Poison/Disease: 7 dice; Senses: 8 dice; Swimming: 4 dice<br /> <br /> Resolve: 2, (+1 for 2m, +3 for 6m) Guile: 4 (+1 for 2m, +3 for 6m), Appearance: 5<br /> <br /> <b>Combat</b><br /> Attack (Bite): 11 dice (+5 for 5m, +10 for 10m) (Damage 19L/5)<br /> Attack (Stomp): 11 dice (+5 for 5m, +10 for 10m) (Damage 17B/4)<br /> Attack (Grapple): 11 dice (+5 for 5m, +10 for 10m) (8 dice to control)<br /> Combat Movement: 10 dice (+5 for 5m, +7 for 7m)<br /> Evasion: 4 (+2 for 4m, +5 for 10m); Parry 6 (+2 for 4m, +5 for 10m)<br /> Soak/Hardness: 18 (+3 for 3m / +8 for 8m)/ 7<br /> <br /> <b>Special Abilities</b><br /> Bone-Crunching Bite: An enemy damaged by a hippo\u2019s decisive bite suffers a penalty equal to attack roll extra successes on his Strength and Dexterity rolls that scene, maximum \u22125. Multiple attacks stack their penalties.<br /> <br /> Crushing Bite: Withering bite attacks ignore four points of soak, plus an additional point for each attack roll extra success. This can\u2019t reduce an enemy\u2019s soak below (his Stamina).<br /> <br /> Furious Rampage: When attacking or rushing a crashed enemy, add two automatic successes.<br /> <br /> Trample: When making a stomp attack against an enemy that provoked the hippo\u2019s reflexive movement from a rush on his last turn, a hit knocks the enemy prone. Apply the prone defense penalty (Exalted, p. 202) retroactively when calculating the attack\u2019s threshold successes.<br /> <br /> Predator\u2019s Menace (Latent): Animals with an intimidate pool can be trained with this attack, causing an intimidated enemy to lose Initiative equal to the extra successes over his Resolve, even if he pays Willpower to resist. Once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> Beast of Burden: Double 8s on feats of strength to haul or carry heavy burdens.<br /> <br /> Bottomless Lungs: Hippos can hold their breath for five minutes underwater. In combat, they can hold their breath for an entire scene, but must surface once it ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Shapeshifting</b><br /> <br /> Quicksilver Second Face: (2i, Reflexive, Instant): The Lunar shapeshifts reflexively on her turn, without the usual miscellaneous action Defense penalty. She may do so multiple times in one turn, but not in the middle of an action \u2014 e.g., she can\u2019t make an attack roll in one shape, then shift into another before rolling damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Offensive Charms</b><br /> <br /> Sinuous Striking Grace: (3m, Reflexive, Instant): This Charm must be used at the start of the round. The Lunar adds (higher of Dexterity or Wits *5*) to her Initiative to determine when she acts. If she uses her turn to attack an enemy who hasn\u2019t acted that round, she adds a non-Charm die.<br /> <br /> <b>Defensive Charms</b><br /> <br /> Agile Beast Defense: (1m, Reflexive, Instant): Successfully defending against an attack grants one Initiative, and she can parry lethal damage barehanded. If her attacker\u2019s Initiative is lower than hers or he rolls any 1s, she gains +1 Defense.<br /> <br /> Bending Before the Storm: (2m, Reflexive, Instant): The Lunar halves all penalties, rounded down, to her Defense. Against lower-Initiative attackers, she ignores all Defense penalties. This doesn\u2019t affect penalties from surprise attacks<br /> <br /> Impenetrable Beast Armor: (3m, Reflexive, Instant): She adds (higher of Essence or 3) natural soak against a withering attack or gains Hardness (Stamina) against a decisive attack.<br /> <br /> Durant Quicksilver Adaptation: ( - , Permanent, Permanent): She may use the Stamina Excellency to raise her soak against a withering attack after it hits, but before damage is rolled.<br /> <br /> Hmm, social charms might be a bit long, let me address that next post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-22-2019, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T03:32:00-07:00","id":1306493,"title":"","content":"<b>Social Charms</b><br /> <br /> Glance Oration Technique: (4m, Supplemental, Instant): She uses body language to convey an influence roll or a single sentence, denying her targets the Resolve bonus for lacking a shared language.<br /> <br /> Predator - And - Prey Mirror : (3m, Reflexive, One scene): Characters perceive the Lunar as their natural predator \u2014 she seems an auditor to a corrupt bureaucrat, or a bandit to a humble farmer. he Lunar can leverage its impact as though it were a Minor Intimacy. (Fear)<br /> <br /> Feral Smile Tactic : (3m, Supplemental, Instant): She doubles 9s on a roll to instill a Tie of fear towards herself (or her current form) or threaten her target. Characters with a Tie of fear towards the Lunar\u2019s current human or animal shape lose one Initiative (which she doesn\u2019t gain) if her roll beats their Resolve in combat, even if they resist with Willpower.<br /> <br /> Inexplicable Mystery Incarnation (2m, Reflexive, Instant): She mutes all motes spent to create or enhance an influence roll with any Attribute, read intentions roll, or application of Resolve or Guile.<br /> <br /> Moonlight Curtain Drawn (3m, Reflexive, One Scene): She gains +1 Guile. If an effect opposing her Guile would reveal information inconsistent with her current animal or human shape, potentially revealing her as a shapeshifter or impostor, the bonus increases to +3.<br /> <br /> Argent Songbird Voice (2m, Reflexive, One Scene): Her influence rolls with any Attribute ignore multiple target penalties, and she can use Excellencies to add successes instead of dice for two motes each.<br /> <br /> Poised Lion Attitude (3m, Reflexive, Instant): The Lunar reflexively makes an influence roll with any Attribute on her turn. She can only make one influence roll per turn.<br /> <br /> There you go, that should be everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T20:25:28-07:00","id":1306731,"title":"","content":"I totally forgot about Easter commitments, I haven't forgotten about this OR my other review thread though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T21:50:46-07:00","id":1306751,"title":"","content":"No hurry DrLoveMonkey, Happy Easter!<br /> <br /> Hope the QC stuff is helpful, note: I did not include stunt dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T21:57:09-07:00","id":1307141,"title":"","content":"Side note: Appreciations to this thread for actually getting me to stat out this concept, I kept wanting to do it but never had the willpower. <br /> <br /> This build is meant to be exceptionally dangerous from Ess1, if I was actually going to be playing Membe, I might take a few fewer combat and Appearance Charms (Hippo form covers for a lot of sins) and get a Str and Int Excellency instead (two charms in each for the Excellency). <br /> <br /> In the long run that\u2019s much stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T22:44:44-07:00","id":1307148,"title":"","content":"I'm in the middle of like three critical things right now, but I intend on statting some things out and making them fight for our entertainment sometime. I'm thinking of trying to pit a Resistance Supernal Single Point Solar with decent investment in Melee against a variety of Lunar and DB foes and see what shakes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T16:16:56-07:00","id":1307327,"title":"","content":"So I'm rolling out this fight, I'm about halfway done and I think I grossly misestimated some things. Prototype, who do you want this to fight? Do you want it against a small group of DBs?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just to be clear I thought &quot;Well 3 will be pretty good, the Lunar will go, crash all 3 of them, then bite one to death instantly and then the real fight can start.&quot; but it really didn't work out that way at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T16:26:28-07:00","id":1307329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307327#post1307327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm rolling out this fight, I'm about halfway done and I think I grossly misestimated some things. Prototype, who do you want this to fight? Do you want it against a small group of DBs?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just to be clear I thought &quot;Well 3 will be pretty good, the Lunar will go, crash all 3 of them, then bite one to death instantly and then the real fight can start.&quot; but it really didn't work out that way at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did something bad happen for Membe? All 10s for the deebs? Already bringing out the Decisive Long Knives? I mean, I'm quite aware that the dice can be unkind if they want, so don't sweat it (you said 3, right?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-23-2019, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T16:48:26-07:00","id":1307333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307329#post1307329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did something bad happen for Membe? All 10s for the deebs? Already bringing out the Decisive Long Knives?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the thing is, the idea is that you crash them when their initiative is low right at the start of the fight. The problem that I didn't consider is that your target for crashing an enemy is rolled (Wits + awareness) + 3 + Resolve. So I gave them 8 dice to their Join Battle rolls, max excellency 4m for 2 successes, and 3 resolve, and only gave the Earth aspect an excellency to boost his by 2. Two of the DBs rolled exactly average and one JUST enough that he couldn't force a first turn.<br /> <br /> So this is what we're looking at right now, the fire aspect is just about to act since Cloud Riot doesn't count as your attack action.<br /> <br /> <br /> Combat Tracker<br /> <br /> Roll Join Battle<br /> <br /> Lunar rolls 9m excellency, gets 7 for an initiative of 10<br /> Wood rolls with 4 motes into excellency, gets 6 for 9<br /> Earth rolls with 4 motes into excellency, gets 6 for 9 also<br /> Fire rolls with 4 motes into excellency, gets an incredible 11 for 14<br /> <br /> Lunar is already in Hippo Form<br /> <br /> <br /> Li: 4<br /> Wi: 3<br /> Ei: 9<br /> Fi: 5<br /> <br /> Per: 16 iph: 4 (38)<br /> Wood Per: 14 iph: 30 (35)<br /> Fire Per: 14 iph: 10 (35)<br /> Earth Per: 14 iph: 12 (35)<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Lunar reflexively rolls for intimidate, using 3m Poised Lion, 3m Feral Smile Tactic, 3m Predator and Prey Mirror, 4m Glance Oration Technique, 3m Sinuous Striking Grace 10m full excellency.<br /> <br /> gets 8 against resolve of 3, 3 and 5, stripping 6/6/4 initiative off and burning a willpower each.<br /> <br /> Lunar uses action to attack fire aspect with 10m full excellency. Dragonblooded defends by reflexively clashing with 4m 3i Cloud Riot, 6m full melee excellency and 5m Crossfire Flash<br /> <br /> Both roll abysmally and get 6 to the DBs 9<br /> <br /> DB rolls min damage getting 3 sux and no 10s<br /> -----------<br /> Earth aspect goes, attacks with 6m full excellency and 3m Force of Mountain<br /> <br /> Lunar defends with 1m Agile Beast Defense, 2m Bending Before the Storm as losing a clash gives bad penalties, and her initiative is still higher than Earth's<br /> <br /> Earth rolls 9 successes, beating defense by 2, dealing 3 damage<br /> -----------<br /> Fire attacks Lunar<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I could keep going but I think it's a forgone conclusion. I might need to use less powerful DBs or possibly use something that isn't DBs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T16:59:05-07:00","id":1307339,"title":"","content":"Did you auto buy successes with Argent Songbird? Thats a big part of the bomb. You can turn a 10 dice excellency into 5 successes.<br /> <br /> You can also instill a minor intimacy with Predator and Prey, the minor intimacy is good for another 2 dice on an instill roll (counting as a supporting intimacy). With that you also auto strip one extra initiative with Feral smile.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s my calculation:<br /> <br /> 5 (App) + 5 (Presence) + 2 (Stunt) + 1 (Specialty) + 2 (Minor Supporting Intimacy) + X (5 Appearance - Average Resolve of enemies) + 5 Auto Successes (Argent Songbird) + 1 Auto Success (Feral Predator Smile Auto strips one initiative with Predator and Prey Mirror\u2019s Tie of Fear)<br /> <br /> And Membe got an 8? Wow, the dice really wanted him dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-23-2019, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T17:07:41-07:00","id":1307342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307339#post1307339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you auto buy successes with Argent Songbird? Thats a big part of the bomb. You can turn a 10 dice excellency into 5 successes.<br /> <br /> You can also instill a minor intimacy with Predator and Prey, the minor intimacy is good for another 2 dice on an instill roll (counting as a supporting intimacy). With that you also auto strip one extra initiative with Feral smile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right! I\u2019ll restart with that in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T17:15:46-07:00","id":1307345,"title":"","content":"Err... wait, if you can leverage an intimacy of fear, does that mean they can also defend with intimacies to avoid the fear? Do Lunars have a way to factor intimacies into Threaten rolls?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm also not sure if Appearance affects Threaten rolls either. It's called out specifically as affecting Instill and Persuade, but I'm not sure if that's intentional design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-23-2019, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T17:25:36-07:00","id":1307347,"title":"","content":"Whoops my bad. (It shouldn\u2019t figure into the calculation then) <br /> <br /> If they have an Intimacy that defends against the Primal Fear of getting your face eaten off by a predator, they can apply its bonus to their Resolve. (I\u2019m not sure if they know it\u2019s a Lunar? I do have an array of stealthy charms that hide my identity)<br /> <br /> What Predator and prey Mirror does is it starts them already with a Minor Intimacy of Fear (does not have to be instilled) towards me that penalizes their Resolve when I try to install the belief that \u201cI am going to bite you in two, mortal\u201d. If they have something stronger to combat that, then the penalty is negated/overridden. (+3 major Intimacy vs -2 Minor Intimacy = +1 to Resolve). Do note however that the Intimacy used to contest has to be applicable to the current situation, it can\u2019t just be \u201cI love the Realm\u201d.<br /> <br /> Of course just having Monor Intimacy of Fear towards Membe (no matter what other Intimacies they have) is enough to strip one extra point of initiative from them all with Feral Smile Tactic (which is the main point of P&amp;P mirror) Do note that Feral Smile also makes this Roll Double 9s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-23-2019, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T17:36:06-07:00","id":1307351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307345#post1307345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: I'm also not sure if Appearance affects Threaten rolls either. It's called out specifically as affecting Instill and Persuade, but I'm not sure if that's intentional design.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not a Threaten Roll (which is a specific thing like bargain) it\u2019s an Instill Roll to Instill a Fear based Minor Intimacy using my Intimidate Pool.<br /> <br /> Membe isn\u2019t asking them to do anything, he is just making them believe that the Hippo is going to kill them.<br /> <br /> All the Charms/Predators menace should work on such an Instill roll, but yes, you are right about threaten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:02:00-07:00","id":1307352,"title":"","content":"Also, just to say these Deebs are getting through his 18 Soak and his Cheatery- After-the-fact Stamina Excellency?! I wasn\u2019t giving these guys nearly enough credit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:03:57-07:00","id":1307353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307351#post1307351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not a Threaten Roll (which is a specific thing like bargain) it\u2019s an Instill Roll to Instill a Fear based Minor Intimacy using my Intimidate Pool.<br /> <br /> Membe isn\u2019t asking them to do anything, he is just making them believe that the Hippo is going to kill them.<br /> <br /> All the Charms/Predators menace should work on such an Instill roll, but yes, you are right about threaten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh okay I actually understand what's going on now, haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:17:42-07:00","id":1307354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307352#post1307352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, just to say these Deebs are getting through his 18 Soak and his Cheatery- After-the-fact Stamina Excellency?! I wasn\u2019t giving these guys nearly enough credit.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of them is an earth immaculate who's weapon has an Overwhelming value of 5, so...<br /> <br /> Actually speaking of, just to see what happens I ran a lone DB against a Tyrant Lizard and won without ever taking a hit or leaving Fire Aura as a Water Aspect....due to some shitty shitty rolls it took like 4 times as long as it should have though...<br /> <br /> Water Aspect Swordsman<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Water Essence 3 Per: 14 iph 25 (35)<br /> <br /> Using artifact short daiklaves and medium armor<br /> <br /> 5/5/3 physical spread.<br /> <br /> Charms Melee up to Cloud Riot, Dragon Graced Weapon, Harnessed Firestorm Assault.<br /> <br /> Has a join battle of 10, +3 sux for 6m.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Twinblades for 16 (Damage 15) +6 for 6m and +2 for clashes.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Combat Tracker<br /> <br /> Roll Join Battle<br /> Tyrant Lizard rolls 5 for a total of 8<br /> Water rolls 6 for a total of 12<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ti: 1<br /> Wi: 11<br /> <br /> Per: 0 iph 10 (35)<br /> ===============<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 6m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 17 against 10, dealing 0 damage<br /> <br /> Water enters Fire Aura<br /> ===============<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 5m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 10 against 7, dealing 0 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 5m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 13 against 5, dealing 5 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 4m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 10 against 2, dealing 2 damage<br /> <br /> At this point Water has 17 initiative and could make a decisive attack, but I'm going to do this stylish like. Also wait for motes to build back up to full.<br /> ===============<br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 3m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 13 against 5, dealing 3 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 2m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 10 against 6, dealing 2 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 1m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 11 against 4, dealing 2 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 0m full excellency and 5m Crossfire Flash from personal. Rolling 27 dice against 13. Rolling 13 against 7, dealing 3 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 0m full excellency and 5m Crossfire Flash from personal. Rolling 27 dice against 13. Rolling 8 against 7, dealing 3 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 10<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 0m full excellency and 5m Crossfire Flash from personal. Rolling 27 dice against 13. Rolling 12 against 10, dealing 3 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 11<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 0m full excellency and 5m Crossfire Flash from personal. Rolling 27 dice against 13. Rolling 10 against 3, dealing 1 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 12<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 0m full excellency and 5m Crossfire Flash from personal and 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite. Rolling 27 dice against 13. Rolling 12 against 6, dealing 6 damage, and having a post soak damage of more than 10, also crashing the Tyrant.<br /> ===============<br /> Round 13<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 0m full excellency and 5m Crossfire Flash from personal. Rolling 27 dice against 13. Rolling 17 against 8, dealing 4 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 14<br /> <br /> 10m 1wp Harnessed Firestorm Assault, 0m full excellency, 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite<br /> <br /> Rolling 22 dice against Parry of 5, three times. First two hitting and last one MISSING! MISSING 5 on 22 dice?!<br /> <br /> Dealing max possible damage due to Legendary Size each time for each actual hit.<br /> <br /> Regaining Fire Aura<br /> --------------<br /> Tyrant lizard Talon striking against Water<br /> <br /> Water expends Fire Aura to reflexively clash with 3m 1wp Comet Deflection, throwing in a 6m full excellency. Now at the glowing anima level.<br /> <br /> Tyrant lizard rolls 13 dice against 17, getting 3 against 7.<br /> DB hits<br /> <br /> DB deals 2 Lethal levels<br /> ===============<br /> Round 15<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 4m semi-full excellency from personal. Rolling 23 dice against 13. Rolling 9 against 8, dealing 2 damage<br /> <br /> Water re-enters Fire Aura<br /> ===============<br /> Round 16<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Tyrant Lizard Resets to base Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 4m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 10 against 7, dealing 2 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 17<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 3m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 9 against 7, dealing 2 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 18<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 2m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 9 against 4, dealing 3 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 19<br /> <br /> Water spends 2i to delay to clash<br /> <br /> Clashes Tyrant's Talon attack with a 2m full excellency from personal. Rolling 24 dice against 13. Rolling 16 against 10, dealing 2 damage<br /> ===============<br /> Round 20<br /> <br /> Welp, believe it or not, that's the reset condition for Harnessed Firestorm Assault. Soo....<br /> <br /> 10m 1wp Expend Fire Aura for Harnessed Firestorm Assault, attacking 3 times with 1m full excellency. Actually hitting each time this time.<br /> <br /> Dealing a total of 10 damage and slaying the Tyrant Lizard, with 10<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-24-2019, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:31:22-07:00","id":1307360,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Deebs with Clash bonuses sure do make for tougher fights, something I\u2019m going to have to consider for my next Lunar build...<br /> <br /> Edit: Tyrant Lizard Lunars are crazy scary with Predator\u2019s Menace. They can strip 2 initiative per success with their Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-23-2019, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:02:39-07:00","id":1307374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307347#post1307347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(+3 major Intimacy vs -2 Minor Intimacy = +1 to Resolve).</div> </div> </div> </div>As a side note, that intimacy math there is actually a bit off. Intimacies target resolve directly, not dice, so attacking using a minor is -1, major -2, defining -3 directly to resolve, and intimacies raised in defense of resolve enjoy a natural +1 bonus to their level, so it goes +2/+3/+4. I'm just going to assume they don't have any intimacies to bring to bear, but what intimacies you can bring up might be a bit more broad than you think.<br /> <br /> For example a lot of the more powerful DBs have intimacies of pride for themselves, and that might help them defend against a tie of fear to what they assume is nothing more than a mere animal. Also some Dragonblooded charms let them reflexively develop intimacies on the spot if they see another terrestrial in danger, even social danger.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you are using intimidate as an instill action though you DO get appearance dice, since they apply to all instill actions I'm pretty sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:06:30-07:00","id":1307376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307374#post1307374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note, that intimacy math there is actually a bit off. Intimacies target resolve directly, not dice, so attacking using a minor is -1, major -2, defining -3 directly to resolve, and intimacies raised in defense of resolve enjoy a natural +1 bonus to their level, so it goes +2/+3/+4. I'm just going to assume they don't have any intimacies to bring to bear, but what intimacies you can bring up might be a bit more broad than you think.<br /> <br /> For example a lot of the more powerful DBs have intimacies of pride for themselves, and that might help them defend against a tie of fear to what they assume is nothing more than a mere animal. Also some Dragonblooded charms let them reflexively develop intimacies on the spot if they see another terrestrial in danger, even social danger.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you are using intimidate as an instill action though you DO get appearance dice, since they apply to all instill actions I'm pretty sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>All quite true, that is my bad/misunderstanding. <br /> <br /> And of course a Deeb might have an intimacy to contest. It just has to be applicable to the situation, STs call, that\u2019s all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T20:22:25-07:00","id":1307395,"title":"","content":"Okay so the very important thing to remember here is that Dragonblooded are real legit exalts, and you're going 3v1, so it's really hard.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded Opponants<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 3 Dragonblooded, wood, earth and fire aspect.<br /> <br /> All Essence 3<br /> <br /> Wood aspect with Powerbow and Light Mundane armor<br /> Fire aspect with twin blades and medium artifact<br /> Earth Aspect with Tetsubo and heavy armor<br /> <br /> Wood Per: 14 iph: 30 (35)<br /> Fire Per: 14 iph: 25 (35)<br /> Earth Per: 14 iph: 20 (35)<br /> <br /> Earth Aspect has full Earth Dragon Style and Integrity Excellency. Fire Aspect has Melee up to Cloud Riot, Crimson Fang Bite, Harnessed Firestorm Assault. Wood Aspect has Archery up to Arbor Sentinel, Heartbeats Before Death, Arrow Thorn Technique, Spring Follows Winter. Wood has 3/5/5, Fire has 5/5/3 Earth has 5/3/5. All have 2 ox bodies. All have appearance 2.<br /> <br /> Assume 4 wits, 4 awareness and no specialty<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> <br /> Wood<br /> Powerbow<br /> 16 (Damage 15)<br /> Soak 8/0<br /> Evasion 6<br /> <br /> Fire<br /> Twinblades<br /> 16 (Damage 15)<br /> Soak 11/7<br /> Parry 6<br /> <br /> Earth<br /> Tetsubo<br /> 12 (Damage 19)<br /> Soak 16/10<br /> Parry 6<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Combat Tracker<br /> <br /> Roll Join Battle<br /> Lunar spends 10m full excellency gets 8 for 11 initiative<br /> Wood spends 4m in excellency, gets 8 for 11 initiative<br /> Fire spends 4m in excellency, gets 2 for 5 initiative<br /> Earth spends 4m in excellency, gets 4 for 7 initiative<br /> <br /> =============<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Lunar activates 3m Poised Lion, 3m Feral Smile Tactic, 3m Predator and Prey Mirror, 4m Glance Oration Technique, 3m Sinuous Striking Grace, 10m Argent Songbird.<br /> <br /> Assuming no applicable intimacies from any of the Dragonblooded to help defend.<br /> <br /> Earth aspect will boost by 2 with 4m, all will stunt defense.<br /> <br /> Rolling 15 dice and 5 auto successes against resolves of 3/3/5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 11 successes for a total of 16, thus stripping 14/14/12 initiative. A very solid roll.<br /> <br /> Crashing 3 opponants gives the Lunar a triple initiative break, up to 26 initiative.<br /> <br /> <br /> Using her attack action she will try a decisive attack against the Earth Aspect, using a 10m full excellency<br /> <br /> Earth defends with 6m full excellency defense<br /> <br /> Lunar is rolling 22 dice with 2 auto successes against a parry of 9, getting 11 succeses total.<br /> <br /> Rolling 26 dice for damage and getting 10 successes, also imposing a -2 penalty on the DB for all strength and dex based rolls. Earth is now also in his second last -2, stacking with the -2 penalty.<br /> ------<br /> Wood aspect fires a withering shot, 6m full excellency and 3m Arrow Thorn Technique.<br /> <br /> Lunar will raise defense by 1 for 1m with Agile Beast Defense.<br /> <br /> Attacking with 22 dice against Lunar's defense of 7, rolling 10 successes, Overwhelming of 5 dealing 2 damage.<br /> <br /> Wood enters Wood Aura<br /> ------<br /> Earth activates 9m Earth Dragon Form.<br /> <br /> Enters Earth Aura<br /> ------<br /> Fire attacks with 6m full excellency<br /> <br /> Lunar will activate 1m Agile Beast Defense<br /> <br /> Fire attacks with 22 dice against a parry of 6. Fire gets 11. Rolling Overwhelming of 4 for 4 damage<br /> <br /> Crashing the Lunar who crashed him gives him Initiative Shift, boosting up to 9 initiative and immidiately refreshing his turn.<br /> <br /> Attacking the Lunar again with a withering attack, 5m full excellency.<br /> <br /> Lunar will activate 1m Agile Beast Defence and 2m Bending Before the Storm<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 22 dice agasint a parry of 6. Fire gets 13 successes, rolling minimum damage of 4 for 0 damage<br /> <br /> Fire enters Fire Aura<br /> =============<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Fire activates 10m 1wp Harnessed Firestorm Assault, 4m full excellency and 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite.<br /> <br /> Lunar defends against the first with 1m Agile Beast Defence, 2m Bending Before the Storm and 2m Dex Excellency using the last of the mote pool to break the Fire aspect's discount<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 17 dice against a parry of 7. Failing with only 5<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 6m full excellency 17 dice against a parry of 2 making it with 4, rolling 5 damage and dealing 3 lethal<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 0m excellency for 12 dice against parry of 1, making it with 7, rolling 5 lethal damage and dealing 4, filling the Lunar's last health level<br /> <br /> DB resets to 3 initiative and enters fire aura.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, unfortunately, it looks like it doesn't work at taking out 3 dedicated DB opponents. At least not yet, I'm sure at higher essence with some more combat investment it eventually would. Some ox-bodies would be a good start, although these were the mote pools at the end of the fight:<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunar Per: 0 iph: 0 (38)<br /> Wood Per: 14 iph: 17 (35)<br /> Fire Per: 14 iph: 4 (35)<br /> Earth Per: 6 iph: 10 (35)<br /> <br /> So the 5m drip that you get probably wouldn't be able to keep up with the dogpile with just the extra ox-bodies. You might have gotten an Initiative Shift yourself though, which should have let you finish off the Earth Aspect. Again though, in a much larger brawl with like 5 DBs against 3 Lunars, this tactic will be extremely effective!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-24-2019, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T20:38:34-07:00","id":1307398,"title":"","content":"yeah no matter how you deal with it, even trying to overwhelm them in the beginning fighting multiple DBs is quite hard huh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T20:56:46-07:00","id":1307401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307398#post1307398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah no matter how you deal with it, even trying to overwhelm them in the beginning fighting multiple DBs is quite hard huh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you just can\u2019t deal with the fact that they\u2019re hitting you with artifacts three times a turn or more, and they themselves are only being hit 1/3 of the time, or maybe more. Then once everyone\u2019s mote pools start getting real low, they are and have been regenerating three times as many motes as you the whole fight. Then there\u2019s the signature charms, they\u2019re total game changers. Heartbeats before Death combined with Arrow Thorn Technique and Harnessed Firestorm Assault with the really efficient Melee excellency. <br /> <br /> That initial hit wiped out all of the initiative on the entire board, and then utterly crippled the Earth aspect, since he was going to be hard to farm initiative off of due to his gigantic soak. <br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t help that both artifacts and DB charms have the ability to enhance Overwhelming damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T21:03:32-07:00","id":1307403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307401#post1307401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, you just can\u2019t deal with the fact that they\u2019re hitting you with artifacts three times a turn or more, and they themselves are only being hit 1/3 of the time, or maybe more. Then once everyone\u2019s mote pools start getting real low, they are and have been regenerating three times as many motes as you the whole fight. Then there\u2019s the signature charms, they\u2019re total game changers. Heartbeats before Death combined with Arrow Thorn Technique and Harnessed Firestorm Assault with the really efficient Melee excellency. <br /> <br /> That initial hit wiped out all of the initiative on the entire board, and then utterly crippled the Earth aspect, since he was going to be hard to farm initiative off of due to his gigantic soak. <br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t help that both artifacts and DB charms have the ability to enhance Overwhelming damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m Ruined! Ruined I tell you! Nobody will ever trust a Build I make ever again! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *Ahem* <br /> <br /> No I more or less kind of figured this would be the outcome. Good to get mechanical confirmation. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming 1v1 it would work better? (Or with a Circle for the Lunar, since friendlies can target the crashed foes?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T21:17:03-07:00","id":1307405,"title":"","content":"Yes, both of those things would definitely be better. I\u2019ve yet to see a DB bear a celestial one-on-one, although I do believe it could happen with good/bad luck in combination with good/bad strategy.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t worry so much though, the ability to fight 3 combat capable Dragonblooded and win in a white room is exceptionally difficult. <br /> <br /> The real place that it would shine is either in like a 3v3 or even 5v3, just something where you have allies to take some of the heat and force the DBs to spend motes on Defense. Also teamwork, distract gambits, setting up onslaught penalties, that kind of thing. <br /> <br /> <br /> Orrrr, just use it against things that aren\u2019t Exalts. Like if you went 3v1 against powerful elementals or ghosts or something you\u2019d have a way better time. Anything without a damn anima banner. It shouldn\u2019t be that in Exalted the only things you\u2019re fighting are other exalts, we have a big antagonists section in the book, Hundred Devil Night Parade, all sorts of stuff filled with monsters that this Lunar will tear apart and howl victory for Luna. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll run one of them tomorrow actually, just to show the contrast between fighting exalts and fighting almost literally anything else. Also because I want to see Membe properly tear stuff up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T23:11:33-07:00","id":1307420,"title":"","content":"Would that first decisive attack have killed one of the other two DBs? Because it seems like taking one of them out entirely at the beginning of the fight would have been a better option. Or did all the DBs have lots of Ox Body charms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T08:11:57-07:00","id":1307478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay so the very important thing to remember here is that Dragonblooded are real legit exalts, and you're going 3v1, so it's really hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ghost of 2e and its &quot;your charms don't work on Celestials half the time&quot; clutches its pearls in horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T08:13:06-07:00","id":1307479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307420#post1307420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that first decisive attack have killed one of the other two DBs? Because it seems like taking one of them out entirely at the beginning of the fight would have been a better option. Or did all the DBs have lots of Ox Body charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have helped in theory, but in this particular fight it wouldn\u2019t have made a difference. All the earth aspect did on her turn was activate Earth Dragon Style, which didn\u2019t affect anything.<br /> <br /> In this fight each DB had 2 ox-bodies. So not like anything crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-24-2019, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T09:33:37-07:00","id":1307501,"title":"","content":"Okay, so what happens when Membe goes 3v1 against tree sized carnivorous elementals instead? This.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Roll Join Battle<br /> <br /> Membe spends 5m for 5 dice, getting 7 for 10 initiative<br /> Green1 rolls 8 dice, getting 1 for 4 initiative<br /> Green2 rolls 8 dice, getting 3 for 6 initiative<br /> Green3 rolls 8 dice, getting 4 for 7 initiative<br /> <br /> =============<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Membe activates 3m Poised Lion, 3m Feral Smile Tactic, 3m Predator and Prey Mirror, 4m Glance Oration Technique, 6m Argent Songbird<br /> <br /> Rolls 15 dice plus 3 auto successes, getting 6 for a total of 9 against an effective resolve of 2. Stripping away 8 initiative from each.<br /> <br /> <br /> Membe attacks Greenmaw1 with 5m excellency bite. Rolling 7 successes. Rolling 25 dice of damage and dealing 9 levels, putting Greenmaw1 into his second last -2 health level and imposing a -2 peenalty<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw3 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 rolls 10 dice, gets 3 successes and misses<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw1 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw1 rolls 8 dice, gets 2 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw1<br /> <br /> Greenmaw1 can not defend<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 9 against a defense of 3. Ignoring 6 points of soak and adding 6 to the damage.<br /> <br /> Rolling 21 damage for 9 points.<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw3 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 rolls 10 dice, gets 3 successes and misses<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 7 successes and hits, rolling 1 dice of damage and getting 1<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw1 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw1 rolls 8 dice, gets 5 successes and hits, rolling 1 dice of damage and getting 0<br /> =============<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 5m excellency decisive attack against Greenmaw1<br /> <br /> Greenmaw1 can not defend<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 16 dice to attack, getting 4 against a defense of 3. Rolling 12 damage and getting 5 and slaying Greenmaw1<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw3 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 rolls 10 dice, gets 5 successes and misses<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 7 successes and hits, rolling 1 dice of damage and getting 1<br /> =============<br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw3<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 can not defend<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 5 against a defense of 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 9 damage for 6 points.<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 6 successes and hits, rolling 1 damage for 1<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw3 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 rolls 10 dice, gets 3 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 5m excellency decisive attack against Greenmaw3<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 can not defend<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 16 dice to attack, getting 8 against a defense of 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 26 damage for 15 points, slaying Greenmaw 3<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 will defend with 4m 1i Unbroken Root Endurance<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 9 against a defense of 5. Ignoring 4 points of soak and adding 4 to damage<br /> <br /> Rolling 12 damage for 7 points, crashing Greenmaw2 more than 1 turn after it recovered from crash, thus netting a crash bonus.<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 10 against a defense of 5. Ignoring 5 points of soak and adding 5 to damage<br /> <br /> Rolling 14 damage for 8 points<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 4 against a defense of 5, missing....somehow<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 9 against a defense of 5. Ignoring 4 points of soak and adding 4 to damage<br /> <br /> Rolling 12 damage for 5 points<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 10<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 5m excellency decisive attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 16 dice to attack, getting 12 against a defense of 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 31 damage for 15 points, slaying Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I actually made a small tactical error here on the side of Membe. I think instead of allowing one of the greenmaws to recover from crash so that I could get another initiative break, I should have just kept them in the dirt so that they couldn't use defensive charms. Either way though Membe just wrecked their faces off like they were salad. But they aren't salad, they're terrifying gigantic magical forces of nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-24-2019, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T14:27:00-07:00","id":1307585,"title":"","content":"I also fought a DB against a Nephwrack, just to see what would happen. The DB wasn't super optimized, it's an Earth aspect using the Wood charms from the primarily Water Brawl tree, he doesn't have artifact armor, or even heavy mundane armor, and he only has 3 dex. I'm also going to start putting these things in spoiler tags, since they're very long but not very wide, so that should help the thread.<br /> <br /> Earth Aspect Brawler using Wood<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Has smashfist and medium mundane armor<br /> <br /> Has Brawl up to Entangling Roots Embrace, Body of Deadly Thorns, Inescapable Whirlpool Hold, Rolling Boulder Blow. Resistance up to Earth Bears Witness with wood expansion.<br /> <br /> Resolve of 4, able to boost by 2 for 4m<br /> <br /> Earth Per: 14 iph: 35<br /> <br /> Physical 5/3/5 4 wits<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> <br /> Earth<br /> Smashfist 14 (Damage 15)<br /> Soak 10/0<br /> Parry 5<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actual fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Roll Join Battle<br /> <br /> Nephwrack rolls 11 dice getting 5 for 8 initiative<br /> Earth spends 4m for 2 successes and rolls 8 dice, getting 6 for 9 initiative<br /> =============<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Earth strikes with a smashing attack 5m excellency and 4m Oaken Thew Exertion from peripheral, going up 1 anima level.<br /> <br /> Nephwrack defends by using 5m 4i 1wp Clinging Shadow Miasma, blinding the DB, and 2i Acursed Wraith Body, raising parry to 7<br /> <br /> Rolls 17 dice against Parry 7, gets 7.<br /> <br /> Rolls 3 dice, gets 1 damage, knocking Nephwrack prone<br /> <br /> Enters Wood Aura<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack attempts to flurry a Rise From Prone with a withering attack.<br /> <br /> Rolls 6 dice to rise from prone and fails with 0 successes<br /> <br /> Rolls to attack with Soulsteel Daiklave<br /> <br /> Earth will not defend with 2m excellency<br /> <br /> Nephwrack rolls 7 dice against parry 5, rolling 4 successes and missing<br /> =============<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Earth attempts grapple gambit with 5m Inescapeable Whirlpool Hold, 4m Oaken Thew Exertion, 5m Entangling Roots Embrace, 10m 1a 1wp Body of Deadly Thorns 4m excellency<br /> <br /> Dropping a level of anima and then going back up 2<br /> <br /> Earth rolls 11 dice against Nephwrack's parry of 4, gets 5<br /> <br /> Gambit roll difficulty 2, cost 3i, rolling 9 dice with disapearing 6s, getting 5, grapple successful<br /> <br /> Control roll, rolling 4m on Oaken Thew Exertion, rolling 15 dice against 9 (assumed) earth gets 7 to Nephwrack's 2, holding for 5 turns of control.<br /> <br /> Earth lacks initiative to break through Nephwrack's hardness so will withering savage, activating 4m Oaken Thew Exertion, rolling 14 dice and getting 7 successes<br /> <br /> Rolling 10 damage and getting 8 successes, crashing the Nephwrack. Clinging Shadow Miasma dissapears.<br /> <br /> Earth saps an initiative from Nephwrack due to Entangling Embrace.<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack attempts to attack with soulsteel daiklave<br /> <br /> Prone and grappled the Nephwrack has 9 dice, due to Body of Deadly Thorns Earth's defense remains 5<br /> <br /> Earth will spend 2m excellency to defend<br /> <br /> Nephwrack rolls 4 successes and fails to connect, but does sap a round of control away.<br /> =============<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Earth will sacrifice 2 rounds of control to take a restrain action, which due to Body of Deadly Thorns allows her to also decisively savage, spending 1m to excellency for dissapearing 6s<br /> <br /> Rolling 21 initiative and dealing 8 damage, rerolling 2 6s for 0 additional damage. Nephwrack is in -2 health levels<br /> <br /> Earth saps an initiative from Nephwrack<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack is restrained<br /> =============<br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Earth restrains and decisives rolling 4 dice of damage and getting 1<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack is restrained, but escapes this turn, also returning to base initiative<br /> =============<br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> Due to stealing initiative last round Earth goes first with 4<br /> <br /> Earth attacks with 3m Stone Fist Strike, Nephwrack will defend with 2i Acursed Wraith Body<br /> <br /> 14 dice rolled against a parry of 5, misses with 4<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack attempts to flurry rise from prone with daiklave attack<br /> <br /> Rolling 4 dice due to wound and flurry penalties, makes it with 2<br /> <br /> Attacking with daiklave strike, Earth will not spend motes to defend.<br /> <br /> Rolls 8 dice against a parry of 5, getting 3 successes and missing.<br /> =============<br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> Earth attacks with 3m Stone Fist Strike. Nephwrack can not spend i to defend<br /> <br /> Rolls 14 dice against parry of 5, misses with 3<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack will attack with Soulsteel Daiklave<br /> <br /> Earth will defend with 4m excellency<br /> <br /> Rolling 8 dice against parry of 7, fails with 6<br /> =============<br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> Earth attacks with 3m Stone Fist Strike, Nephwrack can not spend i to defend<br /> <br /> Rolls 14 dice against parry of 5, misses with 3<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack will attack with Soulsteel Daiklave<br /> <br /> Earth will defend with 4m excellency<br /> <br /> Rolling 8 dice against parry of 7, fails with 4<br /> =============<br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> Earth attacks with 3m Stone Fist Strike, Nephwrack can not spend i to defend<br /> <br /> Rolls 14 dice against parry of 5, hits finally with 13<br /> <br /> Rolling 6 damage for 2 final, crashing the Nephwrack<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack will attack with Soulsteel Daiklave<br /> <br /> Earth will defend with 2m excellency<br /> <br /> Rolling 8 dice against parry of 6, fails with 1<br /> =============<br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> Earth will withering smash attack with 1m excellency and 4m Oakten Thew Exertion<br /> <br /> Rolling 14 dice against parry of 5, hitting with 5<br /> <br /> Rolling 3 damage and getting 1<br /> <br /> Bonfire anima automatically switches current Wood aura to Earth Aura, Nephwrack is prone<br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Nephwrack attempts to flurry rise from prone with daiklave attack<br /> <br /> Rolling 4 dice due to wound and flurry penalties, makes it with 2<br /> <br /> Attacking with daiklave strike, Earth spend 2m to defend<br /> <br /> Rolls 8 dice against a parry of 5, getting 3 successes and missing.<br /> <br /> Takes 0 damage from anima<br /> =============<br /> Round 10<br /> <br /> Earth will smash attack with 3m Stone Fist Strike<br /> <br /> rolling 14 against Parry of 5, getting 7<br /> <br /> Rolling 6 damage for 5 successes<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack attempts to flurry rise from prone with daiklave attack<br /> <br /> Rolling 4 dice due to wound and flurry penalties, makes it with 2<br /> <br /> Attacking with daiklave strike, Earth will not spend motes to defend.<br /> <br /> Rolls 8 dice against a parry of 5, getting 8 successes<br /> <br /> Rolling 10 damage and getting 6<br /> <br /> takes 0 damage from anima<br /> =============<br /> Round 11<br /> <br /> Earth will smash attack with 1m excellency 3m Stone Fist Strike<br /> <br /> rolling 14 against Parry of 5, getting 13<br /> <br /> Rolling 7 damage for 3 successes and knocking Nephwrack prone<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack recovers from crash<br /> <br /> Nephwrack attempts to flurry rise from prone with daiklave attack<br /> <br /> Rolling 4 dice due to wound and flurry penalties, rolls 1 and fails<br /> <br /> Attacking with daiklave strike, Earth will not spend motes to defend.<br /> <br /> Rolls 5 dice against a parry of 5, getting 0 successes<br /> <br /> Hardness prevents anima damage<br /> =============<br /> Round 12<br /> <br /> Earth will allow Nephwrack to recover from crash and make a decisive attack, 6m excellency, 5m Rolling Boulder Blow<br /> <br /> rolling 15 dice against parry of 4, getting it with 6<br /> <br /> Rolling 16 damage for 5. Nephwrack is now in -4 health levels<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack attempts to rise from prone rolling 5 dice, getting it with 4<br /> =============<br /> Round 13<br /> <br /> Earth attacks Nephwrack with 1m excellency, 3m Stone Fist strike. Nephwrack defends with 2i Acursed Wraith Body<br /> <br /> Earth rolls 15 dice against 5 Parry, misses with 4<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack attacks with daiklave, Earth defends with 2m excellency<br /> <br /> Nephwrack rolls 9 dice against Parry of 6, makes it with 10!<br /> <br /> Rolling 8 damage due to the Earth aspect anima and getting 5, crashing the Earth!<br /> =============<br /> Round 14<br /> Nephwrack will make a decisive attack with 2i Accursed Wraith Body, Earth will defend with 4m Excellency<br /> <br /> Nephwrack rolls 8 dice against parry of 6, missing with 5<br /> ---------<br /> Earth attacks Nephwrack with 3m Stone Fist, Nephwrack will defend with 2i Accursed Wraith Body<br /> <br /> Rolling 14 against parry of 5, getting 10<br /> <br /> Rolling 6 damage for 2<br /> =============<br /> Round 15<br /> <br /> Earth attacks Nephwrack with 3m Stone Fist, Nephwrack will defend with 2i Accursed Wraith Body<br /> <br /> Rolling 14 against parry of 5, getting 5<br /> <br /> Rolling 6 damage for 6, crashing the nephwrack<br /> ---------<br /> Nephwrack attacks with daiklave, Earth will not spend motes<br /> <br /> Nephwrack rolls 8 dice against defense of 5, misses with 0<br /> =============<br /> Round 16<br /> <br /> <br /> Earth will make a decisive attack, 6m excellency, 5m Rolling Boulder Blow<br /> <br /> rolling 15 dice against parry of 4, getting it with 6<br /> <br /> Rolling 17 damage for 5. Nephwrack is slain<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Hey, the Nephwrack actually crashed him! So that's pretty impressive. There were 4 10s on that roll by the way. Using another aspect aura I could feel it being a little bit restrictive, but it wasn't really so bad. Spending 4m on a defense is pretty okay, and that doesn't boost your anima up a level, and also it was very helpful to have a charm that had a level of anima in its cost to help mitigate things. Although at that point the Earth probably could have just flared since I don't think charms that have an aura activation requirement stop working if you leave aura, only Duration: Aura charms do.<br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure what to do next, maybe a Lunar swatting tiger stealth against something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T14:47:48-07:00","id":1307589,"title":"","content":"I'm curious to see how the &quot;murderkitty&quot; build at Essence 2 fares against the 3 Deebs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T15:08:04-07:00","id":1307594,"title":"","content":"Barebones writeup of a murderkitty build:<br /> Attributes<br /> Dex 5/Strength 3+<br /> <br /> Abilities: Brawl 5, Dodge 5, Probably With Specialties<br /> <br /> Merits: Artifacts (Moonsilver Chain Shirt, Moonsilver Smashfist)<br /> <br /> Cat form (Underfoot Menace)<br /> <br /> Charms - This depends on how many you want to give, but my ordering would be:<br /> Very Good: Last Warrior's Unity, Agile Beast Defense, Golden Tiger Stance, <br /> Good: Ferocious Biting Tooth, Prey Hobbling Bite, Coiled Serpent Strikes, Finding the Needle's Eye, Striking Mospid Method, Mighty Ram Smash, Sinuous Striking Grace, Cunning Beast-Warrior Instinct, Wasp Sting Blur, Quicksilver Second Face<br /> Essence 2: Fleet Gazelle Exercise, Sensing the Deadly Flow, Unerring Fang Technique (Ambush Predator+Underfoot Menace+Not stunting for an attribute makes this easy to hit)<br /> <br /> I think that Last Warrior's Unity is better than Stalking Shadow Hunter+Claws of the Silver Moon (Damage is 10+str/3 vs. 15/1+str, but accuracy is 5 vs 2)<br /> <br /> The character ends up using nearly entirely their own stats, except taking advantage of ambush hunter, underfoot menace, and tiny creature for a constant +3 attack, +2 evasion. And protean benefits. And if they have stamina 1 they can replace their soak with the cat's 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T17:17:07-07:00","id":1307623,"title":"","content":"From the testing I see thusfar, it looks like DB's are...surprisingly dangerous, actually! Essence-wielders in numbers seem like a real tough nut to crack short of Solar-level ubercombos; I wonder if there's some critical threshold combat-focused Solars beyond E1 (and especially at E3) are able to comfortably exceed accuracy/damage-wise that makes them so deadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T17:22:28-07:00","id":1307625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307501#post1307501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so what happens when Membe goes 3v1 against tree sized carnivorous elementals instead? This.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Roll Join Battle<br /> <br /> Membe spends 5m for 5 dice, getting 7 for 10 initiative<br /> Green1 rolls 8 dice, getting 1 for 4 initiative<br /> Green2 rolls 8 dice, getting 3 for 6 initiative<br /> Green3 rolls 8 dice, getting 4 for 7 initiative<br /> <br /> =============<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Membe activates 3m Poised Lion, 3m Feral Smile Tactic, 3m Predator and Prey Mirror, 4m Glance Oration Technique, 6m Argent Songbird<br /> <br /> Rolls 15 dice plus 3 auto successes, getting 6 for a total of 9 against an effective resolve of 2. Stripping away 8 initiative from each.<br /> <br /> <br /> Membe attacks Greenmaw1 with 5m excellency bite. Rolling 7 successes. Rolling 25 dice of damage and dealing 9 levels, putting Greenmaw1 into his second last -2 health level and imposing a -2 peenalty<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw3 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 rolls 10 dice, gets 3 successes and misses<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw1 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw1 rolls 8 dice, gets 2 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw1<br /> <br /> Greenmaw1 can not defend<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 9 against a defense of 3. Ignoring 6 points of soak and adding 6 to the damage.<br /> <br /> Rolling 21 damage for 9 points.<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw3 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 rolls 10 dice, gets 3 successes and misses<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 7 successes and hits, rolling 1 dice of damage and getting 1<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw1 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw1 rolls 8 dice, gets 5 successes and hits, rolling 1 dice of damage and getting 0<br /> =============<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 5m excellency decisive attack against Greenmaw1<br /> <br /> Greenmaw1 can not defend<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 16 dice to attack, getting 4 against a defense of 3. Rolling 12 damage and getting 5 and slaying Greenmaw1<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw3 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 rolls 10 dice, gets 5 successes and misses<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 7 successes and hits, rolling 1 dice of damage and getting 1<br /> =============<br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw3<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 can not defend<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 5 against a defense of 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 9 damage for 6 points.<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 6 successes and hits, rolling 1 damage for 1<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw3 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 rolls 10 dice, gets 3 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 5m excellency decisive attack against Greenmaw3<br /> <br /> Greenmaw3 can not defend<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 16 dice to attack, getting 8 against a defense of 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 26 damage for 15 points, slaying Greenmaw 3<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 will defend with 4m 1i Unbroken Root Endurance<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 9 against a defense of 5. Ignoring 4 points of soak and adding 4 to damage<br /> <br /> Rolling 12 damage for 7 points, crashing Greenmaw2 more than 1 turn after it recovered from crash, thus netting a crash bonus.<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 10 against a defense of 5. Ignoring 5 points of soak and adding 5 to damage<br /> <br /> Rolling 14 damage for 8 points<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 4 against a defense of 5, missing....somehow<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 10m excellency withering attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 21 dice to attack, getting 9 against a defense of 5. Ignoring 4 points of soak and adding 4 to damage<br /> <br /> Rolling 12 damage for 5 points<br /> ------------<br /> Greenmaw2 attacks Lunar with a withering tail slam<br /> <br /> Membe will not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> Greenmaw2 rolls 10 dice, gets 4 successes and misses<br /> =============<br /> Round 10<br /> <br /> Membe makes a 5m excellency decisive attack against Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> Membe rolls 16 dice to attack, getting 12 against a defense of 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 31 damage for 15 points, slaying Greenmaw2<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I actually made a small tactical error here on the side of Membe. I think instead of allowing one of the greenmaws to recover from crash so that I could get another initiative break, I should have just kept them in the dirt so that they couldn't use defensive charms. Either way though Membe just wrecked their faces off like they were salad. But they aren't salad, they're terrifying gigantic magical forces of nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again really appreciate you doing this DrLoveMonkey. So a couple of questions since you experienced the build first hand if that is okay?<br /> <br /> 1. Is having the Brawl at 5 a bit of an unnecessary luxury (ie are those 2 extra dice to hit worth the 4bp I spent on them?)<br /> <br /> 2. What would you view as Membe\u2019s main weakness? Is it the lack of health levels? No good defensive options? (I noticed that in the DB fight you were content to just take minimal damage after complete soak, is that the best tactic with him?)<br /> <br /> 3. How do you feel about this kind of character vs a DBT Full Moon? I personally think you can get away without having to invest in soak and damage and still do on par in combat with Shapeshifters, but accuracy always seems to be the main problem.<br /> <br /> Thanks once again, was an excellent show!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-25-2019, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T23:36:02-07:00","id":1307696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307589#post1307589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious to see how the &quot;murderkitty&quot; build at Essence 2 fares against the 3 Deebs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm...'kay...<br /> <br /> 3 Dragonblooded Shikari<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 3 Dragonblooded, Water Aspect Hammerer, Wood Aspect Archer, Fire Aspect Immaculate<br /> <br /> Water per: 14 iph: 24 (35)<br /> Wood per: 14 iph: 26 (35)<br /> Fire per: 14 iph: 25 (35)<br /> <br /> Wood has 3/5/5<br /> Water has 5/5/3<br /> Fire has 5/5/3<br /> <br /> All have awareness 5 with specialties, wood and water have 4 wits, fire has 5<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> <br /> Water<br /> Hammer 14 (Damage 17/4)<br /> Soak 14/10<br /> Parry 7<br /> <br /> Wood<br /> Powerbow 16 (Damage 15/4)<br /> Soak 10/4<br /> Evasion 6<br /> <br /> Fire<br /> Twinblades 16 (Damage 15/3)<br /> Soak 11/7<br /> Parry 6<br /> <br /> <br /> Have all Essence 3 charms related to their combat ability, as well as ISoS, Wood also has the dodge sig and Virtuous Negation Defense. Each has 2 ox-bodies<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Murderkitty<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Full Moon 5/5/5 stats, 5 wits<br /> <br /> Per: 17 iph: 28 (42)<br /> <br /> <br /> STATS<br /> <br /> Lunar<br /> Smashfist 16 (Damage 15/3)<br /> Soak 10/4<br /> Evasion 8<br /> Parry 7<br /> <br /> <br /> Has all charms listed by autXautY, along with 3 ox-bodies<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Combat Tracker<br /> <br /> Lunar 10m full excellency 21 dice for 11, 14 initiative<br /> Wood 6m full excellency 16 dice for 13, 16 initiative<br /> Water 6m full excellency 16 dice for 14, 17 initiative<br /> Fire 6m full excellency 17 dice for 13, 16 initiative<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunar Per: 0 iph: 0 (42)<br /> Wood per: 14 iph: 1 (35)<br /> Water per: 10 iph: 0 (35)<br /> Fire per: 14 iph: 0 (35)<br /> <br /> ==========<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Lunar uses 3m Sinuous Striking Grace 3m 1wp Sensing the Deadly Flow<br /> ---------<br /> Water uses 3m 2i Flame Warden Stance on Fire<br /> Water enters Fire Aura<br /> ---------<br /> Wood aspect attacks with 6m full excellency, 4m Death From Nowhere, Lunar defends with 4m 1wp Fleet Gazelle Exercise, 3m 2i golden tiger, 1m Agile Beast<br /> <br /> Wood rolls 22 dice against 12 evasion, hits with 12<br /> <br /> Rolls 8 damage for 3<br /> <br /> Wood enters Wood Aura<br /> ---------<br /> Fire attacks using 6m full excellency, 4m 1wp Essence Igniting Nerve Strike. Lunar defends with 1m Agile Beast and 4m excellency<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 22 dice against evasion 13, missing with 9<br /> ==========<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks with 3m Sinuous Striking Grace, 3m Finding Needle's Eye, 2m Ferocious Biting Tooth, 3m Striking Mospid, 1m Unerring Fang, 5m excellency<br /> <br /> Fire will not defend with motes. Water will intervene with Defend Other, and reflexively clash with 6m full excellency, 5m Crossfire Flash, 4m 3i Fire Incites Water to a Riot of Clouds<br /> <br /> Lunar rolls 21 dice, getting 12 with three 1s, two 10s, and other non successes, rerolling for 4 more successes and a total of 16<br /> <br /> Water rolls 20 dice, getting 9 with three rerolls for a total of 10<br /> <br /> Lunar hits by 6, rolling 6 damage for 4<br /> <br /> Water changes to Water Aura<br /> ---------<br /> Wood attacks with 1m 1wp Heartbeats Before Death, 6m Full Excellency, 4m Death From Nowhere. Lunar defends with 1m Agile Beast, 3m 2i Golden Tiger and 4m excellency<br /> <br /> Wood attacks with 25 dice against 13 evasion, rolling 15<br /> <br /> Rolling 10 damage for 3<br /> ---------<br /> Fire attacks with 6m full excellency, Lunar defends with 1m Agile Beast, 2m Excellency<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 22 dice aginst evasion 12, missing with 7<br /> ---------<br /> Water attacks with 6m full excellency. Lunar defends with 1m Agile Beast 2m Excellency<br /> <br /> Water rolls 20 dice against 12 Evasion, rolling 15<br /> <br /> Rolling 10 damage for 7<br /> ==========<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Wood aims<br /> ---------<br /> Water attacks with 6m full excellency. Lunar has no motes to defend<br /> <br /> Water rolls 20 dice against 10 Evasion, misses with 4<br /> ---------<br /> Fire attacks with 6m full excellency 3m Searing Edge Attack. Lunar has no motes to defend<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 22 dice against 10 Evasion, missing with 4<br /> ---------<br /> Lunar attacks Fire with 3m Finding Needle's Eye, 2m excellency. Fire defends with 6m full excellency<br /> <br /> Lunar rolls 18 dice against 9 evasion, hitting with 11<br /> <br /> Rolling 6 damage for 4<br /> ==========<br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Wood attacks with decisive, 6m full excellency, 3m Life Swelling Sap Strike. Lunar has no motes to defend<br /> <br /> Wood rolls 20 dice against 9 Evasion, missing with 3<br /> ---------<br /> Water attacks with 6m full excellency 5m 1wp Roaring River Slash<br /> <br /> Water rolls 17 dice against 9 evasion, making it with 11<br /> <br /> Rolling 36 damage for 17 lethal<br /> ---------<br /> Fire attacks Lunar with 6m full excellency 3m Searing Edge<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 22 dice against 9 evasion, hits with 9<br /> <br /> Rolls 5 damage for 2, and causing an additional 3 lost<br /> ---------<br /> Lunar attacks Water with 3m Finding Needle's Eye, 2m Excellency. Defends with 6m full excellency<br /> <br /> Lunar rolls 17 dice against 9 Parry, hitting with 11<br /> <br /> Rolling 3 dice of damage for 1<br /> ==========<br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> Wood attacks with decisive, 6m full excellency, 3m Life Swelling Sap Strike. Lunar has no motes to defend<br /> <br /> Wood rolls 20 dice against 9 Evasion, Hitting with 10<br /> <br /> Rolling 18 damage for 10 and causing a -1 penalty to evasion for the scene as the arrow grabs hold<br /> ---------<br /> Fire attacks with 6m full excellency, 3m Searing Edge Attack<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 22 dice against Evasion 9, hitting with 13<br /> <br /> Rolls 9 damage for 7 and an additional 3 lost, crashing the Lunar<br /> ---------<br /> At this point I realize the Lunar has taken 27 levels of lethal, and is now in crash and taking 4 dice of lethal every turn from anima flux as this continues. The fight is sadly over.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> That was pretty decent, unfortunately with artifact weapons and the ability to constantly pump full excellency attacks into things, the defenses just were not enough. Three combat focused Shikari are extremely deadly<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307623#post1307623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the testing I see thusfar, it looks like DB's are...surprisingly dangerous, actually! Essence-wielders in numbers seem like a real tough nut to crack short of Solar-level ubercombos; I wonder if there's some critical threshold combat-focused Solars beyond E1 (and especially at E3) are able to comfortably exceed accuracy/damage-wise that makes them so deadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm 100% sure there are builds that can pretty reliably take on 3 combat focused DBs, but they're rare. It's looking more and more like they're definitely the outliers in the group. The dogpile is simply too much. Even if you can ignore the onslaught penalties you still can't full excellency your defense 3 times in a turn, and then fire off a doom combo that hits hard enough to penetrate artifact armor, round after round after round.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307625#post1307625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once again really appreciate you doing this DrLoveMonkey. So a couple of questions since you experienced the build first hand if that is okay?<br /> <br /> 1. Is having the Brawl at 5 a bit of an unnecessary luxury (ie are those 2 extra dice to hit worth the 4bp I spent on them?)<br /> <br /> 2. What would you view as Membe\u2019s main weakness? Is it the lack of health levels? No good defensive options? (I noticed that in the DB fight you were content to just take minimal damage after complete soak, is that the best tactic with him?)<br /> <br /> 3. How do you feel about this kind of character vs a DBT Full Moon? I personally think you can get away without having to invest in soak and damage and still do on par in combat with Shapeshifters, but accuracy always seems to be the main problem.<br /> <br /> Thanks once again, was an excellent show!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, very much!<br /> <br /> 1. This is going to be a kind of crappy answer but it's worth it if you think it's worth it. It will give you an extra parry and 2 extra dice, which could make the difference especially at high power combat, on the other hand they might not make much of a difference at all, and if you can spend those 4bp doing really fun things instead, I'd definitely say do that.<br /> <br /> 2. Lack of health levels is a big one, but i think his defense is pretty good. The DBs were taking min damage just because they couldn't reliably boost their damage up to the level that it tanks through that level of soak, especially with the post attack soak booster, so they boosted their Overwhelming damage instead, which they have artifacts and several charms for. I actually wouldn't really say that Membe is weak at all, there is no shame in losing a 3 on 1 against anathema hunting Exalted. That loss was in no way a failure to make a good and powerful character.<br /> <br /> 3. Accuracy is only really a problem against extremely skilled opponents. If they can boost their parry up to 9 or 10 or something, then that's a problem, but most enemies can't do that. I wouldn't necessarily say that you could keep pace exactly with a DBT Full Moon, unless you also keep up in other charm areas like damaging charms and stuff. The DBT can still use artifacts, and that +(Strength) to damage and soak is really damn good. a DBT in full plate with a Grand Daiklave has a base damage of 24 and soak of 21 before other charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like Membe a lot though! Super cool fun friendly Hippo that turns into a terrifying monster in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T23:45:31-07:00","id":1307698,"title":"","content":"I'm curious how that Hippo Lunar would fare if he had invested in a merit that reduces the DB's number advantage, like Familiar, Retainer, or Command. Given the Lunar's social focus exchanging those two dots of brawl for a Dragonblooded Retainer may be the most interesting choice, as they can more easily fit into non-combat scenes than Tyrant lizard Familiars.<br /> Same for the murderkitty vs 3 DBs, just to test how powerful these Merits really are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T23:59:29-07:00","id":1307699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307698#post1307698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious how that Hippo Lunar would fare if he had invested in a merit that reduces the DB's number advantage, like Familiar, Retainer, or Command. Given the Lunar's social focus exchanging those two dots of brawl for a Dragonblooded Retainer may be the most interesting choice, as they can more easily fit into non-combat scenes than Tyrant lizard Familiars.<br /> Same for the murderkitty vs 3 DBs, just to test how powerful these Merits really are.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Arena that is a somewhat dangerous and slippery slope that I wouldn't necessarily want to go down. If you're letting merits like Command or Retainers onto the field each Terrestrial will get 18 to your 10, for a total inequality of 54 to 10.<br /> <br /> On the other hand in an actual game it's almost certainly the best use of merits, for almost anything. One retainer that shores up a weakness in your character, and who can go away so you can act in two places at once, or team up and tackle one task together in incredibly powerful. I had to institute a rule for my DB chargen that there can't be more Dragonblooded retainers than there are party members. Just to stop everyone from taking 3 allied DBs along with weapons and armor and not even having to dip into bonus points<br /> <br /> Otherwise I'd have the party walk into the Satrap's palace grounds flanked by 15 battle ready young terrestrials. Badass, to be sure, but I'm not running that combat.<br /> <br /> Basically <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QG2hPiTpaWU\" target=\"_blank\">THIS</a> would happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-25-2019, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T00:13:20-07:00","id":1307700,"title":"","content":"Am I wrong or don't defenses take penalties from your health levels? Also i feel this nephwrack doesn't use its magic or abilities to good use. Like why materialize when you could just possess corpses of a fighter while using sorcery as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T00:29:52-07:00","id":1307703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307700#post1307700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I wrong or don't defenses take penalties from your health levels? Also i feel this nephwrack doesn't use its magic or abilities to good use. Like why materialize when you could just possess corpses of a fighter while using sorcery as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do take penalties to Defense due to lost health levels, yes, although the Lunar had a scenelong charm that negated wound penalties.<br /> <br /> The fight against the Nephwrack though was just a pure brawl because I wasn\u2019t really sure where I should draw the line. It bringing in a horde of undead is not really fair unless the DB gets to bring in a horde of Realm soldiers, and possessing a dead body could easily just end in the body being slain, and the Nephwrack just leaving. Or with an entire room full of bodies to possess, but that would have debatably just been worse for the Nephwrack, as you\u2019d basically never find a corpse with the soak and physical attributes of the Nephwrack itself, and if the DB has Spirit Grounding Shout it would amount to very little benefit in the Nephwrack\u2019s favour.<br /> <br /> His other magical abilities also either redirect attacks to other characters, none were available, cost initiative, which are unusable in crash, or required 20+ initiative, which he never got.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m also doing this all by hand and using charmsets that I\u2019m not thoroughly familiar with, I\u2019d be shocked if I didn\u2019t make some math error or tactical mistake somewhere. I realized I made a mistake halfway through the murderkitty fight and had to redo the fight from the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-25-2019, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T00:43:43-07:00","id":1307705,"title":"","content":"Clinging Shadow Miasma used instantly as combat started as well as Dawn of Dead Stars can be a serious threat as well as an essence sink requiring the dragonblooded to maintain close range or be wrecked by the newly created difficult terrain as well as the turn by turn pretty difficult integrity rolls. At this distance the nephwrack could start casting defensive spells while keeping the dragonblooded at medium range unless they had a way to deal with the magical difficult terrain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T01:00:00-07:00","id":1307708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307705#post1307705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clinging Shadow Miasma used instantly as combat started as well as Dawn of Dead Stars can be a serious threat as well as an essence sink requiring the dragonblooded to maintain close range or be wrecked by the newly created difficult terrain as well as the turn by turn pretty difficult integrity rolls. At this distance the nephwrack could start casting defensive spells while keeping the dragonblooded at medium range unless they had a way to deal with the magical difficult terrain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh crap, I completely forgot about that effect of Dawn of Dead Stars, you\u2019re right that would have been a really good opening move. I\u2019ve used Nephwracks as zombie legion commanders before and read the first half of the charm before going \u201coh right the one that boosts the crap out of the zombies.\u201d<br /> <br /> That might have made the difference, especially since DoDS doesn\u2019t end when crashed like Miasma does. I don\u2019t know if the difficult terrain would have mattered though, if you\u2019re not moving through it you don\u2019t provoke rolls for it, and the charm ends if the Nephwrack gets crashed. I could always run it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T01:08:34-07:00","id":1307709,"title":"","content":"Wait I think I see what you mean now. Yeah using that strategy I think the Nephwrack would have won, although I\u2019m not certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T01:11:08-07:00","id":1307710,"title":"","content":"Also with Dawn of Dead Stars activated you can now use Broken Mirror Tragedy without initiative cost creating a fine defensive charm depending on the environment. Also disengaging with Accursed Wraith Body giving you double 9s while at that same moment using Clinging Shadow Miasma could be a fine way to get distance for spell casting and wearing people down with Dawn of dead stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T01:39:25-07:00","id":1307714,"title":"","content":"If I run it again I might do 1v2 to give Broken Mirror something to do, and also attack spells and effects like DoOB and Miasma become better, but I'm not sure if the ganging up would be too much. 1v3 would definitely be too far, but it might be able to do 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T02:06:58-07:00","id":1307717,"title":"","content":"instead of adding another character just set the fight in a temple full of hanging corpses. those should count as another target. As DoOB has no limit the more people with under 8 dice on the integrity roll the better it is. Also the Nephwrack having a Virtuous Guardian of Flame active while having Death of Obsidian Butterflies as a control spell being given double 9s with wraith body while rolling 18 dice then given double 9s again on the damage roll with wraith body is very dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T05:00:54-07:00","id":1307726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307698#post1307698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious how that Hippo Lunar would fare if he had invested in a merit that reduces the DB's number advantage, like Familiar, Retainer, or Command. Given the Lunar's social focus exchanging those two dots of brawl for a Dragonblooded Retainer may be the most interesting choice, as they can more easily fit into non-combat scenes than Tyrant lizard Familiars.<br /> Same for the murderkitty vs 3 DBs, just to test how powerful these Merits really are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From experience I can tell you that having a 2 dot great cat or a 3 dot mega mon is worth <i><b>quite a lot</b></i>. It's one of the &quot;greater than the sum of parts&quot; combos. My circle's Sorcerer has a great cat that defends him while he builds sorcerous motes and actively defends him when he's crashed, and further dogpiles numerical advantage on solo targets when the Sorcerer enters Melee. And that ignores when it's not just killing mooks on it's own. And that's all before it turned into a 3 dot monstrosity- my specific example is that it unlocked the Water God powers of it's mother.Economically, it's a significant power boost for XP compared to the 1 or 2 combat charms you are looking at. <br /> <br /> <b><i>And then</i></b> Survival Charms can come into play, but it barely matters at this stage because the damn thing is basically a Game Balancer on the side of the PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T06:07:38-07:00","id":1307734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1305496#post1305496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, after suggesting that I realised it would take ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember back when Shards came out and someone made a Burn Legend tournament thread. It was fun to play in, but damn, my combat alone took several weeks. Many dropped out along the way and I'm not sure the tournament was ever finished. And that's with players rolling for themselves, using a system that's degrees of magnitude less complex than any edition of Exalted. Yeah, it'd take ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T06:15:13-07:00","id":1307735,"title":"","content":"Huh, I guess other people had radically different ideas on the merits of the cat form. I was thinking of a stealth-focused build that could gain the protean effects of both ambush hunter and tiny creature which are pretty significant. I guess its my fault for not being specific.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the ability to go into stealth will give a significant advantage in lessening the 'ganging-up' potential of the deebs.<br /> <br /> The great cat is another strong candidate for the stealth option, but I feel like double 9s from camouflage isn't as valuable as -2 successes from tiny creature and its stats aren't that much better once you factor in the +2 evasion from the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T06:55:11-07:00","id":1307742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307717#post1307717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">instead of adding another character just set the fight in a temple full of hanging corpses. those should count as another target. As DoOB has no limit the more people with under 8 dice on the integrity roll the better it is. Also the Nephwrack having a Virtuous Guardian of Flame active while having Death of Obsidian Butterflies as a control spell being given double 9s with wraith body while rolling 18 dice then given double 9s again on the damage roll with wraith body is very dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure if hanging corpses technically count as another character, but I\u2019d be willing to allow it for the sake of the Arena.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not so sure about something like Flame Guardian though. If we\u2019re letting people cast spells and buff up before the fight then sorcerers can start doing like, flame guardian, Wood Dragon claw, invulnerable skin of bronze combo. Which admittedly they CAN actually do, but then like you could just take any build and bolt that on and it\u2019s great, but then again isn\u2019t that kind of what the arena is for? I dunno.<br /> <br /> I might run again with the same character but wood aspect, then when he loses I\u2019ll build a Solar, Lunar and DB with the express purpose of beating the Nephwrack and see if they can do it. I Predict Solar beats him first turn, Lunar second, maybe third, and DB is a coin toss if he wins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307735#post1307735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I guess other people had radically different ideas on the merits of the cat form. I was thinking of a stealth-focused build that could gain the protean effects of both ambush hunter and tiny creature which are pretty significant. I guess its my fault for not being specific.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the ability to go into stealth will give a significant advantage in lessening the 'ganging-up' potential of the deebs.<br /> <br /> The great cat is another strong candidate for the stealth option, but I feel like double 9s from camouflage isn't as valuable as -2 successes from tiny creature and its stats aren't that much better once you factor in the +2 evasion from the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly could help. I might test it later but I\u2019m not sure how many more \u201cfight x against 3 DBs\u201d I really want to do. Partly just because it takes a long time and partly because once we do find something that wins I\u2019m a bit worried that it\u2019s going to be treated like some kind of bar of entry, instead of what it probably will be which is extremely powerful and specialized. Like I don\u2019t want people going \u201coh, my character can\u2019t beat three DBs, I must have built him wrong and he sucks. Only X build is a viable combat option.\u201d<br /> <br /> I mean, depending on Essence and stuff. An Essence 5 Dawn I would expect to just win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T07:14:31-07:00","id":1307749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307623#post1307623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the testing I see thusfar, it looks like DB's are...surprisingly dangerous, actually! Essence-wielders in numbers seem like a real tough nut to crack short of Solar-level ubercombos; I wonder if there's some critical threshold combat-focused Solars beyond E1 (and especially at E3) are able to comfortably exceed accuracy/damage-wise that makes them so deadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a certain amount of accuracy/damage that puts the Solars ahead so much, it's their access to ways to bypass or shortcut entire parts of the combat engine, and they have sooo many ways of doing so!<br /> <br /> Example (for added difficulty, I excluded Dawns, and kept it under essence 3):<br /> Supernal Survival up to DBT, from Ride take Master Horseman\u2019s Techniques, Seasoned Beast-Rider\u2019s Approach, Worthy Mount Technique. From Melee War Lion Stance.<br /> Familiar Mount and Rider can defend other each other, and one of them is immune to decisive attacks, so funnel withering to the rider (who can't dismounted btw) and decisive to the mount. Becomes ridiculous with a Tyrant Lizard. Possible at essence 1 and becomes <i>really </i>ridiculous at essence 2 when you add Immortal Rider\u2019s Advantage (shift initiative between rider and mount reflexively) and Rousing Backlash Assault (mount can do decisive counterattacks). The cherry on top would be including something high damage like Righteous Devil to the mix. Can definitely take on groups of DB's of, well, any size.<br /> <br /> This is the worst but there are others, like the sexy, Black Claw using, dodgy battle-dancer who rolls into battle with Respect Commanding Attitude active, capping all of his or her opponents to their Charisma + Performance and flurries a dance action every round to keep that going. This makes most everyone utterly irrelevant. After getting Doe Eyes Defense at essence 2 even the few who had a pool left no longer have one. Turns all combats into Bollywood dance-off social combat which no one but you can win. Should be able to take on groups of DB's as long as the Solar initiates combat on their own terms and doesn't tackle, like, a DB traveling minstrel show.<br /> <br /> Solar Stealth (up to Mind Shroud Meditation and Hidden Snake Recoil) + Single Point's Fatal Stroke Flash + Steel Devil Strike is a way to create an ever increasing initiative total which never resets. Probably the least reliable, as it relies on stealth, and is heavy on the WP use, but done right should be able to casually handle multiple DB's.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Solars, you know, and all three examples hinge on using downright broken Charms and synergies on top.<br /> <br /> Now, I wonder if adding some spell like the Virtuous Guardian of Flame spell to the Lunars we've seen performing in the Arena would put them over the top? Haven't had the opportunity if seeing that in play yet, but it should force them to waste some actions to deal with that first. That perhaps combined with Membe shifting to pestletail to thunder-hammer the earth DB away, making him waste turns to return to the fray, might buy the time to take at least one of them out of the equation, which would change everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T07:37:13-07:00","id":1307755,"title":"","content":"Virtuous Guardian of Flame might help, but in multi-person combats it could also be a bit of a liability. It doesn\u2019t have great soak or boostable Defense, so there\u2019s a reasonable chance that the DBs will just crash it and force it to dissipate for the scene, while getting relatively easy initiative and an initiative break.<br /> <br /> On the other hand it buys the Lunar time, which is pretty key. <br /> <br /> Also, yeah, Solars can be pretty damn broken. I wasn\u2019t kidding when I said I expect the Dawn to kill the Nephwrack on turn 1, before he even gets to act. It\u2019s not even a crazy combo either, just the melee tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T08:20:48-07:00","id":1307764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307742#post1307742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That certainly could help. I might test it later but I\u2019m not sure how many more \u201cfight x against 3 DBs\u201d I really want to do. Partly just because it takes a long time and partly because once we do find something that wins I\u2019m a bit worried that it\u2019s going to be treated like some kind of bar of entry, instead of what it probably will be which is extremely powerful and specialized. Like I don\u2019t want people going \u201coh, my character can\u2019t beat three DBs, I must have built him wrong and he sucks. Only X build is a viable combat option.\u201d<br /> <br /> I mean, depending on Essence and stuff. An Essence 5 Dawn I would expect to just win.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean if your essence 1 char gen social infiltrator Lunar can't casually one shot three experienced Terrestrials in battle clearly the problem lies with the player. I mean gods they're supposed to be stronger and that means in all possible situations and builds or else the devs are just nerfing Solars and Lunars because of clear bias.<br /> <br /> But my shitposting about 2e aside, I note how much a sig charm played in the win against the hippolunar. Without forcing you to run a 3 vs 1 duel again, what is your gut feel about characters at the usual e2 level that char gen DB fall at if they still had numbers?<br /> <br /> As an actual Arena request: kind of want to see solo DB vs some of the nastier animals and mid range spirits just to see how that goes like you did with the nephwrack. My game has always been a five person elemental dogpile on whatever I throw them up at which has given me some warped views I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:33:52-07:00","id":1307782,"title":"","content":"The Dragon-Blooded are a real threat is clear. Although a key factor seems to be that one opponent against several runs out of motes faster. It would be interesting to see how it would be to fight against an opponent who has charms for recovering additional motes during combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:48:56-07:00","id":1307784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307764#post1307764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean if your essence 1 char gen social infiltrator Lunar can't casually one shot three experienced Terrestrials in battle clearly the problem lies with the player. I mean gods they're supposed to be stronger and that means in all possible situations and builds or else the devs are just nerfing Solars and Lunars because of clear bias.<br /> <br /> But my shitposting about 2e aside, I note how much a sig charm played in the win against the hippolunar. Without forcing you to run a 3 vs 1 duel again, what is your gut feel about characters at the usual e2 level that char gen DB fall at if they still had numbers?<br /> <br /> As an actual Arena request: kind of want to see solo DB vs some of the nastier animals and mid range spirits just to see how that goes like you did with the nephwrack. My game has always been a five person elemental dogpile on whatever I throw them up at which has given me some warped views I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence 2-3 Dragonblooded is probably the biggest power jump in the game, by far maybe even. Not only are the signature charms some of the most unique and powerful charms in the DB charmset, but there\u2019s also a bunch of other ones in there like Cloud Riot that are really powerful. Losing those is a big step down.<br /> <br /> That being said if the Lunar plans on fighting until she wins, I feel like she\u2019s going to need to get a bit lucky still. If the DBs are being designed the way players would make them, not literally 5s in everything but if you have 3 charms that key off perception you\u2019ll have a 5 there, it won\u2019t be a cakewalk. <br /> <br /> The signature charms tend to end fights a lot earlier but the long game doesn\u2019t really favour the Lunar. It basically boils down to this, you can win almost any 1v1 as a Lunar vs a DB. Your charms are better, more efficient, and shapeshifting is amazing, some combos probably being powerful to the point of being overpowered. BUT if every DB has 2 ox-bodies, and no that\u2019s not unreasonable, they could have 5, or even 5.5 at E3, then to get to that 1v1 you need to farm up enough initiative to decisive 26 health levels out of 2 targets, while defending yourself from around three attacks every turn. Now factor in that your only sources to farm initiative are encased in jade armor which means you need to deal some serious damage to peak over Overwhelming, and even boosting your defences will only stop them from hitting you more than half the time. Also factor in that every time you regenerate 5m they regen 15, and that\u2019s not even factoring in Willpower, which I\u2019ve been intentionally avoiding including in these fights. They spend a willpower on every attack and Defense, so do you, and even if you have max willpower and they have base you\u2019ll run out first.<br /> <br /> None of those factors change when you drop the DBs to e2. The funny thing is that Lunars are so god damned fucking strong that even with all those disadvantages you still might win, and even if you lose one of the DBs is probably going to die, but unless your Lunar is Essence 4-5 I wouldn\u2019t ever rely on it. Like if you and your two Lunar friends are sitting in the market and get ambushed by 3 badass looking Dragonblooded, the tactically sound responses to that are either you all fight and probably win, or all run and probably get away, but not \u201cYou guys run...I\u2019ll handle this.\u201d And go charging in there on your own. <br /> <br /> Also be hyper aware of your surroundings. Drawing out a group of Lunars with underwhelming odds only to spring the OTHER half of the ambush halfway through the fight is exactly the kind of dirty trick the Wyld Hunt would pull...and remember that for when you decide to get retribution by ambushing THEM inside their own barracks. Nowhere is safe.<br /> <br /> <br /> All also see about running those solo fights, they tend to go a lot faster and I make less mistakes because they\u2019re simpler. Plus against mid port spirits and stuff I feel like I can try some wonky strategies and see how they hash out. Plus those combats are WAAAY the fuck more fun. Powerful Exalt on Exalt is a bit of a slog, Membe the fucking Mouth devouring 3 Greenmaws? Awesome.<br /> <br /> Additionally this is why I don\u2019t name the combatants, I\u2019d get too attached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:00:51-07:00","id":1307788,"title":"","content":"Those three greenmaws also probably should have been a size 0 battle group anyway which would have let him annihilate them in one glorious display of carnage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:06:12-07:00","id":1307789,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve also come to a bit of a realization that the game is most fun, as it should be, when the combatants are more unevenly matched, even if there\u2019s a disparity like numbers or something to make up for it. As it should be, I think. The game is most fun when you\u2019re like, running 2-3 easy fights in a relatively short time against weaker opponents, which is like how an actual session might go. Running two high skill high soak exalts is just pounding away, missing half the time, dealing like no damage even when you do hit because 5 Stamina in artifact full plate with bonus soak charms just does that. <br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t run a lot of combats like this before in my games so I haven\u2019t gotten the chance to really see it. <br /> <br /> Ooh, you know what might be fun? Instead of putting exalts against eachother, what if we have them fight a parade of creatures, progressing to more and more powerful/numbers in a row, then see how far everyone gets! Might end up becoming a slog anyway as everyone runs out of motes, so I\u2019ll stop it if that happens.<br /> <br /> Maybe be a bit ambitious but we can see. Also it doesn\u2019t leave anyone feeling like their character idea is bad, since it actually puts them against scenarios that are, you know, reasonable to have in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:10:57-07:00","id":1307791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307788#post1307788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those three greenmaws also probably should have been a size 0 battle group anyway which would have let him annihilate them in one glorious display of carnage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. VICTORY FOR LUNA! Tree sized carnivorous plant spirits are nothing before doomhippo! If I wasn\u2019t on my phone I\u2019d link a picture of a happy hippo. One with some greenery hanging out of its mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:53:30-07:00","id":1307802,"title":"","content":"If they invest in Ox-Bodies so you can't finish any of them fast multiple DBs (built as PCs) are tough for lone Lunars it seems. I tried comming up with something but even at E3 and using Radiant Basilisc to get Behemoths Footprint Thread early, since this is the kind of fight it's made for, and you do the whole roll join battle twice into a free full excellency with Instinctive Supremacy Approach, you probably can't take them down.<br /> <br /> If you throw everything into it you average 12.8 successes and do ~14 + 2xExtra Successes decisive damage with double 10s, shaving something like 10-12 HLs of each of them but you're down 40m round 1 and they're still all alive, and if you get unlucky on that one attack roll you're really screwed.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually reading it again it seems Limb-Maiming Flourish would work with Behemoth Footprint Thread, which should kick up damage by 40% to ~15 HLs which could get the DBs if they only bought 3 Ox-Bodies.<br /> <br /> Maybe if you do the Predators Menace trick as a Death Moa and crash someone round one into an Octopus-and-Spider Barrage? Against a crashed opponent Death Moa would get +2 successes, extra successes to damage, and double 10s on damage rolls for every attack for free. Then you could use your once-per-day Full Moon anima power to roll join battle again and hopefully another DB is still crashed and you could do the same thing to him.<br /> <br /> Another situational option would be a Strix-shape Lunar with Kraken-Arm Lash grappling the DBs from medium range one by one and dropping them to their death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-25-2019, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T12:27:09-07:00","id":1307816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307802#post1307802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they invest in Ox-Bodies so you can't finish any of them fast multiple DBs (built as PCs) are tough for lone Lunars it seems. I tried comming up with something but even at E3 and using Radiant Basilisc to get Behemoths Footprint Thread early, since this is the kind of fight it's made for, and you do the whole roll join battle twice into a free full excellency with Instinctive Supremacy Approach, you probably can't take them down.<br /> <br /> If you throw everything into it you average 12.8 successes and do ~14 + 2xExtra Successes decisive damage with double 10s, shaving something like 10-12 HLs of each of them but you're down 40m round 1 and they're still all alive, and if you get unlucky on that one attack roll you're really screwed.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually reading it again it seems Limb-Maiming Flourish would work with Behemoth Footprint Thread, which should kick up damage by 40% to ~15 HLs which could get the DBs if they only bought 3 Ox-Bodies.<br /> <br /> Maybe if you do the Predators Menace trick as a Death Moa and crash someone round one into an Octopus-and-Spider Barrage? Against a crashed opponent Death Moa would get +2 successes, extra successes to damage, and double 10s on damage rolls for every attack for free. Then you could use your once-per-day Full Moon anima power to roll join battle again and hopefully another DB is still crashed and you could do the same thing to him.<br /> <br /> Another situational option would be a Strix-shape Lunar with Kraken-Arm Lash grappling the DBs from medium range one by one and dropping them to their death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran into some of the same problems when trying to run not-exploity Solar combats against a full circle of 5 high Essence DBs. It started to get kind of ridiculous when I was saying \u201cOkay no artifact weapons, their attunement bonus is taking up too many motes and they don\u2019t help with the decisive attack anyway, and no armor because if I don\u2019t kill them all before they act I\u2019m dead so who cares.\u201d It was only later that I realized that maybe it was time to stop and just let it go. <br /> <br /> Solars are PLENTY powerful without being able to mow down 5 Immaculate masters in a single turn. There actually are still some ways to do it, but you look at those and I as an ST would probably disallow them after a few uses due to the orichalcum rule and simply the fact that those two effects were probably never meant to combine that way when they were written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:25:11-07:00","id":1307892,"title":"","content":"I'm working on running a battle between an Essence 3 Earth Aspect leading a talon of realm troops vs an Essence 1 Lunar leading a pack of wolfmen. Is it okay if I post it here once I'm done?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T18:46:23-07:00","id":1307916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307892#post1307892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on running a battle between an Essence 3 Earth Aspect leading a talon of realm troops vs an Essence 1 Lunar leading a pack of wolfmen. Is it okay if I post it here once I'm done?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah absolutely, save me some work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:21:13-07:00","id":1307939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307816#post1307816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I ran into some of the same problems when trying to run not-exploity Solar combats against a full circle of 5 high Essence DBs. It started to get kind of ridiculous when I was saying \u201cOkay no artifact weapons, their attunement bonus is taking up too many motes and they don\u2019t help with the decisive attack anyway, and no armor because if I don\u2019t kill them all before they act I\u2019m dead so who cares.\u201d It was only later that I realized that maybe it was time to stop and just let it go.<br /> <br /> Solars are PLENTY powerful without being able to mow down 5 Immaculate masters in a single turn. There actually are still some ways to do it, but you look at those and I as an ST would probably disallow them after a few uses due to the orichalcum rule and simply the fact that those two effects were probably never meant to combine that way when they were written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite really does a number on celestials when the DBs have the numbers, combined with Ox-Bodies being their only really reliable defense it seems DBs should max stamina and get some light artifact weapons if they want to hunt anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:46:55-07:00","id":1307942,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Alright. This Does take a long time, huh? I hope you'll forgive the fiction, I just kinda felt like it.</span></span></span> <hr /></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ledaal Kansi, Flame of Clarity, thought often of her old friend Tunka. He was an outcaste, and had always had a serene bearing that she just couldn't understand. His mastery of the Earth Dragon Style was unparalleled, but he never boasted. Even his lessons were quiet. Musings in tones that one could not discern from glib conversation. Once, when they were walking the lower slopes of Meru, Kansi had seen a great stone at the edge of a cliff above them. It hung dangerously at the edge and she asked, &quot;Fellow Master, what do you think of that Boulder there? Shall we find another route or be ready to strike it from the air?&quot;</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tunka had frowned, and cocked his head, &quot;Does the Boulder threaten you, by where it sits?&quot;. Kansi nodded but had no further answer, and they were silent for a time.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;I think the Boulder has made a promise.&quot; Tunka finally mused, &quot;By its stillness, we can detect no Malice. A day it may have rested there, or a thousand years. Never did it bound up the road, into the temple and splat you as you slept.&quot;</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kansi laughed, &quot;Splat, eh? And you have heard its promise? By your communion with Pasiap?&quot;. Tunka shook his head, &quot;The promise of a stone is all it is. Even should it hang so perilously, a stone it remains. You'd know this if you had learned Pasiap's lessons.&quot; </span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kansi hadn't, and she nodded in respect. She thought often of old Tunka, and visited where he had gone missing.</span></span></span></div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Solar Earth Stylist</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Essence 1 Per:13 iph:33 (46)</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dawn 5 in Physical Attributes and Wits, Dodge, MA, Resistance, and Awareness</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Offensive Charms</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Earth Dragon Style (Entire)</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Thunder Clap Rush Attack</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Defensive Charms</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also Earth Dragon Style (Entire)</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Durability of Oak Meditation</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1-Ox Body</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Pain Tolerance Merit</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fighting Unarmed</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">STATS</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Attack:</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unarmed 14 (17 damage) O: 5</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Parry 7</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Soak: 10 Hardness 4</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fire Dragon Master</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Essence 5 Per: 16 iph: 43 (59)</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fire aspect with 5 in Physical Attributes and Wits, all abilities at 5 with specialty</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Offensive Charms</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Brawl Excellency</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fire Dragon Style (All)</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Erupting Fury Barrage</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Defensive Charms</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dodge and Brawl Excellencies</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fire Dragon Style (All)</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Flickering Candle Meditation</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ember-Amid-Smoke Misdirection</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bonfire Shadow Evasion</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Resistance up to Earth Bears Witness</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">3 or so Ox Bodies? I forget. My QC Sheet was just the HLs.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fighting Unarmed</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">STATS</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Attack:</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unarmed 14 (12 damage) O:0 (3 in CMoFD</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dodge and Parry 5</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Soak: 5 Hardness: 0</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(You'll notice I forgot to take a Specialty in Dodge. uh... Yep.)</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Round 1:</b></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kansi takes Join Battle easily. It's expensive, but worth it as she activates Fire Dragon Form with Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon. As we'll see later, she just won the fight.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Despite this, Boulder takes the first action, coming out with a Thunderclap Rush Attack with Force of the Mountain. With a Smashing attack she knocks Kansi down and actually takes the lead, even surpassing the Initiative effect of CMoFD. As we'll see later, she Almost just won the fight. She also takes a damage from CMoFD.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In one attack, Boulder has gone Bonfire. These charms ain't cheap.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In Return, Kansi has to flurry rising from Prone with her own counterattack. Boulder boosts her Parry all the way to 11 but takes -1 for attempting a Smashing attack. Kansi rolls 10 successes on the dot. Boulder Activates Earth Dragon Form along with Perfection of Earth Body. She is now made entirely of Soak. Fortunately, Kansi's form gives her Overwhelming damage, and she rolls 2, which with Searing Edge Attack. That would be bad enough, but Perfection of Earth Body cost Boulder a Whopping 6i to activate. So she Crashes. Goodbye Hardness. We Hardly knew ye.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kansi gains Fire Aura, which she will keep for the rest of the fight.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Round 2:</b></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kansi has the advantage now, and tries for an Essence Igniting Nerve Strike. Unfortunaterly 3 Overwhelming is just not very much, So even though she hits with 1 damage, no essence is lost. She did use Searing Edge attack though, so Boulder is now Extremely Crashed. Kansi now enters Bonfire.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Boulder is now Crashed, so she doesn't have her Perilous charms, and she's not doing great on Essence either. She Has To Hit Kansi so she just boosts her accuracy as high as she can, and gets a solid hit, 7 damage, but its not enough to escape Crash. She also takes 1 damage from CMoFD.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Round 3:</b></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Miraculously, Boulder is not hurt by Kansi's Flux.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Moving first, Kansi hits with a Smoldering Wound attack. 7 Damage and she resets to 4 Initiative.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Boulder now has 1 HL left before Incapacitated. She's immune to the wound penalties, but every time she hits Kansi she takes a damage die from CMoFD, and if she crashes again she'll get hit by Flux.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In response, Boulder does manage to fight her way out of Crash, but doesn't get Initiative Shift. She also doesn't take Damage from CMoFD.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Round 4, 5, etc, :</b> Ok at this point all they have is 5 motes at a time and they can either spend them all on an attack or defense excellency or split them up with something fancier. Kansi uses Flickering Candle Evasion to get a lot more out of her Defense than the excellency could get her, and her Excellency has the reroll 6s effect which gives her two significant edges.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Boulder's Defensive charms aren't really helpful here, maybe I could've optimized better but honestly she's so mote tapped.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She soaks any attack down to nothing, but the Overwhelming combined with Searing Edge attack is brutal, and when she counter-attacks she's just giving Kansi another chance to hit her.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I called the fight there. Theoretically Boulder could save up her Essence over time and make an attempt at getting some Initiative back, but Kansi's dice tricks far outclass her in terms of mote efficiency.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The girl looked up at Ledaal Kansi, Flame of Clarity. Her golden aura betrayed her sin, the hatred and tyranny engulfing her soul. Kansi's essence beat the air wildly, heating Boulder's skin like stones around a cooking fire.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That was it. Now, after all these years, Kansi hesitated. The girl fought like Tunka, pebbles and dust rising around her fingers. She had joked like him before challenging an Immaculate Master to a friendly spar, like it was a cup of tea. She had shown her curse-mark brazenly, identified it clearly and wasted no words in argument. She had been willing to die, just to fight Ledaal Kansi, the Flame of Clarity. And why?</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She called herself Hanging Boulder Promise, and her hair fell scruffily around her eyes. Those eyes looked up at Kansi now, still not bowed. Not even squinting.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They were Tunka's eyes. Without a doubt, and she knew Pasiap's lessons.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ledaal Kansi, Flame of Clarity, spared the life of an Anathema, the first in all her years. For the promise of a stone to remain a stone, and to know whatever became of old Tunka.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-26-2019, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:50:32-07:00","id":1307944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307939#post1307939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite really does a number on celestials when the DBs have the numbers, combined with Ox-Bodies being their only really reliable defense it seems DBs should max stamina and get some light artifact weapons if they want to hunt anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it helps, but if you're truly anathema hunting I would never underestimate them. A Lunar can look like anyone and hide almost anywhere, they have Might 1 battlegroups of beastmen, they ALSO travel in groups and might even outnumber you, and can attack in ways you might not even consider. Economic damage, social revolt, plagues, unleashing the undead, destroying diplomatic ties with other nations and the gods.<br /> <br /> They can also attack from stealth, deal damage, and retreat, wearing you down slowly over hours or days, sapping health and motes both. BUT if the chips are down and your in a final fight where it's 6 on 1, then probably you're going to live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:53:25-07:00","id":1307946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307942#post1307942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Alright. This Does take a long time, huh? I hope you'll forgive the fiction, I just kinda felt like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing all on your own sucks. That being said, cool addition to the arena! I'm sure nobody will mind actually adding a story to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:05:55-07:00","id":1307948,"title":"","content":"On the mechanical side, Fire Dragon has some interesting advantages. Searing Edge attack is excellent, and combos well even with just Become the Hammer. It really shines with Overwhelming damage. A starting Solar could achieve much of what Kansi did just by having Fire Dragon.<br /> <br /> If you factor in the possibility of a short Daiklaive with Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon you have the potential of 7 Overwhelming. Fire Dragon isn't overly fussed about Soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:06:53-07:00","id":1307949,"title":"","content":"I'm an idiot who can't get spoilers to work for some reason, so apologies in advance for the formatting.<br /> Okay, first the participants:<br /> <br /> <b>Wolf-Totem Revolutionary:</b><br /> Str 5 Dex 5 Sta 5 <br /> Int 5 Wit 5 Per 3 <br /> Cha 3 Man 1 App 5<br /> <br /> War 5 (+1 beastmen)<br /> Brawl 5 (+1 claws)<br /> Awareness 3<br /> Integrity 4<br /> Stealth 3<br /> Athletics 5<br /> <br /> Int: <br /> Predator's Deadly Cunning<br /> Argent Pack Formation <br /> Silver General's Foresight<br /> <br /> App:<br /> Glorious Battle Presence<br /> Victorious Beast-King Spirit<br /> Diving Hawk Inspiration<br /> Wolf Devour Shepherd<br /> Panicked Herd Incitement<br /> <br /> Sta:<br /> Impenetrable Beast Armor<br /> Durant Quicksilver Adaptation<br /> Ox Body x2<br /> <br /> Mundane medium armor<br /> Claws mutation<br /> <br /> Size 2 wolfmen raiders<br /> (Lintha Reavers with +1 Might and Average Drill)<br /> <br /> <b>Earth Aspect Winglord:</b><br /> Str 3 Dex 5 Sta 5 <br /> Int 5 Wit 2 Per 5 <br /> Cha 2 Man 2 App 2 <br /> <br /> War 5 (+1 Thousand Correct Actions)<br /> Melee 5 (+1 big-ass shield)<br /> Awareness 5 (+1 sneaky fuckers)<br /> Integrity 5 (+1 martial pride)<br /> Resistance 5<br /> <br /> Resistance: <br /> Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> Earth Bears Witness <br /> Perfected Scales of the Dragon<br /> Ox Body x3<br /> <br /> Melee:<br /> Stoking Bonfire Style<br /> Flame-Borne Interception<br /> Flame Warden Stance<br /> Blazing Interception<br /> <br /> Integrity:<br /> Granite Curtain of Serenity<br /> Flawless Diamond Heart<br /> Frozen Heart Prana<br /> <br /> War:<br /> Tactics Mean Everything<br /> Excellence of the Dutiful General<br /> Roaring Dragon Officer<br /> Changing Winds Cunning<br /> Enfolded in the Dragon's Wings<br /> Blazing Courageous Swordsman Spirit<br /> Ramparts of Obedient Earth<br /> <br /> Artifact heavy armor<br /> Mundane big-ass shield and sword<br /> <br /> Size 3 realm infantry<br /> (Battle Ready Troops with Average Drill)<br /> <br /> Stats summary:<br /> <br /> <b>Lunar:</b><br /> Parry 6, Soak 10, Resolve 5<br /> -0x1/-1x4/-2x4/-4x5/I<br /> <br /> Claw: Accuracy 15 Dmg 10<br /> <br /> Essence 1 Full Moon Caste<br /> Personal 16<br /> Peripheral 38<br /> Willpower 5<br /> <br /> <b>Size 2 Wolfmen</b><br /> Join Battle: 6<br /> Attack (Axe) 10 (Dmg 15/2)<br /> Defense: 6<br /> Magnitude: 9<br /> Soak: 10<br /> Senses: 5<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> <br /> <b>Dragon-Blooded:</b><br /> Parry 7, Soak 16, Resolve 6<br /> -0x1/-1x4/-2x6/-4x1/I<br /> <br /> Sword &amp; Shield: Accuracy 12 Dmg 12<br /> <br /> Essence 3 Earth Aspect<br /> Personal 14<br /> Peripheral 29<br /> Willpower 6<br /> <br /> <b>Size 3 Legionnaires</b><br /> Join Battle: 6<br /> Attack (Chopping sword) 10 (Dmg 15/2)<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Magnitude: 10<br /> Soak: 11<br /> Senses: 4<br /> Resolve: 2<br /> <br /> <br /> Now onto the battle itself:<br /> <br /> <i>Reports have come in of civilian unrest and some minor uprisings south of Harborhead. A wing of realm soldiers under the command of Winglord Cathak Urias has been dispatched to reinforce the local guards and quell the budding revolution. Unbeknownst to the Realm however, this uprising is the work of Anathema. Smiling Hound, a newly tattooed member of the silver pact eager to prove himself, has decided to lie in wait with his band of wolfmen at a nearby mountain pass. He will make sure that the reinforcements never reach their destination.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Strategic Manoeuvres:</b><br /> <br /> Cathak Urias knows not of the beastmen lying in wait nor its Anathema leader: -2<br /> Smiling Hound has scouted the incoming army but hasn\u2019t heard of this Dynast before: -1<br /> Cathak Urias chooses Ambush (threshold 3) and uses a full excellency with Changing Winds Cunning for 9m, rolls 15 dice and rerolls 6 dice for 7 successes. He enters Earth Aura.<br /> Smiling Hound chooses Ambush (threshold 3) and uses a full excellency with Predator\u2019s Deadly Cunning and Argent Pack Formation for 11m, rolls 19 dice, rerolls 2 dice and adds 1 success for 13 successes. Spends 3m and activates Silver General\u2019s Foresight.<br /> <br /> <i>As the Cathak forces make their way across the mountain pass, they are stopped by a cacophony of howls. Dozens of howling warriors with the fangs and pelts of beasts surge out of cleverly hidden crevices and fall upon the soldiers!</i><br /> <br /> All attacks launched by Smiling Hound\u2019s forces during the first round of combat are considered ambush attacks. All attacks launched by his forces in the following 3 rounds are considered surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Join Battle:</b><br /> <br /> Cathak Urias joins battle with a full excellency and Ramparts of Obedient Earth for 11m1w, rolls 17 dice and rerolls 1 die for 11 successes. His starting initiative is 14. He spends 4 points from Ramparts of Obedient Earth to instantly enact a Fortifications stratagem.<br /> The opposing force begins the fight at long range, and treats the entire battlefield as difficult terrain, whereas the victorious force treats the battlefield as normal terrain.<br /> The realm legionnaires join battle rolling 6 dice for 2 successes. Their starting initiative is 5.<br /> Smiling Hound joins battle with a full excellency and Diving Hawk Inspiration for 11m, rolls 18 dice for 5 successes. His starting initiative is 8.<br /> The wolfmen join battle rolling 6 dice for 1 success. Their starting initiative is 4.<br /> <br /> <i>His soldiers panic, but Urias is a veteran of many battles with nerves of steel. With a surging burst of Anima he strikes the ground, opening great furrows and trenches across the battlefield. The baying pack of wolfmen stalls against the suddenly treacherous terrain, their element of surprise wasted.</i><br /> <br /> It will take 6 turns for Smiling Hound and his battlegroup to make it into close range, far more than the duration of the ambush stratagem. We\u2019ll just fast-forward 6 turns. Urias activates Flame Warden Stance for 5m2i targeting his troops and commands them to aim and then attack as soon as the beastmen come into range. Smiling Hound commands his troops to charge in and attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> Cathak Urias commands his battlegroup with full excellency and Blazing Courageous Swordsman Spirit for 8m, rolls 17 dice and rerolls 4 dice for 8 successes.<br /> Smiling Hound commands his battlegroup with a full excellency and Glorious Battle Presence for 14m, rolls 21 dice and rerolls 5 dice for 14 successes. Gains 1 initiative. Initiative is 9.<br /> Soldiers attack with 18 dice for 9 successes. Lunar defends with Impenetrable Beast Armor and Stamina excellency for 6m. Takes 2 dice for 0 damage. Wolfmen take 8 dice for 2 damage.<br /> Wolfmen attack rolling 24 dice and adding 1 success for 11 successes. Earth Aspect intercepts with defend other, defends with Impervious Skin of Stone. takes 2 dice for 0 damage. Takes 2 dice for 1 damage. He drops to 14 initiative.<br /> Urias\u2019 Earth Anima deals no damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> Urias commands his battlegroup with a full excellency and Glorious Battle Presence for and spends willpower for a success for 8m1w, rolls 17 dice, rerolls 8 dice and adds 1 success for 12 successes.<br /> Smiling Hound commands his battlegroup with a full excellency and Glorious Battle Presence for 14m, rolls 21 dice and rerolls 5 dice for 15 successes.<br /> Soldiers attack with 22 dice for 11 successes. Lunar defends with Impenetrable Beast Armor and Stamina excellency for 6m. Takes 4 dice for 2 damage. Initiative drops to 7. Wolfmen take 10 dice for 4 damage.<br /> Wolfmen attack with 25 dice and 1 success for 12 successes. Earth Aspect intercepts with defend other. Takes 2 dice for 0 damage. Takes 2 dice for 1 damage. He drops to 13 initiative.<br /> Urias\u2019 Earth Anima deals no damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> Urias commands his battlegroup with full excellency and Blazing Courageous Swordsman Spirit for 8m, rolls 17 dice for 7 successes.<br /> Smiling Hound commands his battlegroup with a full excellency and Glorious Battle Presence for 14m, rolls 21 dice and rerolls 5 dice for 11 successes.<br /> Soldiers attack with 18 dice for 8 successes. Lunar defends with Impenetrable Beast Armor and Stamina excellency for 6m. Takes 2 dice for 0 damage. Wolfmen take 7 dice for 5 damage. Wolfmen drop to size 1, Earth Aspect gains an Initiative Break. He raises to 18 initiative.<br /> Wolfmen check for rout, rolling 3 dice for 3 successes. They stand their ground.<br /> Wolfmen attack with 25 dice and 1 success for 12 successes. Earth Aspect intercepts with defend other. Takes 3 dice for 1 damage. His initiative drops to 17. The attack overcomes the defend other and hits the soldiers for 4 dice, 1 damage.<br /> Urias\u2019 Anima deals 2 damage to everyone. He pays 2 initiative dropping to 15. Lunar drops to 5 initiative and faceplants.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 4</b><br /> <br /> Urias commands his battlegroup with full excellency and Blazing Courageous Swordsman Spirit for 8m, rolls 17 dice for 3 successes.<br /> The soldiers and Smiling Hound go at the same time. The soldiers attempt to engage the lunar with 13 dice for 10 successes. Smiling Hound flurries attempting to stand up and clashing the battlegroup with a withering attack. He spends 1 willpower and rolls 4 dice with 1 success for 1 success, slips and falls back down. He clashes from the floor with a full excellency for 10m, rolls 19 dice for 7 successes. He loses the clash, dropping to 2 initiative.<br /> The soldiers and the Lunar roll for control. Soldiers roll 13 dice for 8 successes. The Lunar rolls 10 dice for 3 successes, gets engaged for 5 rounds. The soldiers do a savage against defence 0, rolling 13 dice for 6 successes. The Lunar spends his last 5 motes on Impenetrable Beast Armor and the Stamina excellency. He takes 6 dice for 2 damage and is crashed. Urias gets the Initiative Break. Smiling Hound is at initiative 0, Urias is at 20.<br /> The wolfmen attack to try and save their leader, rolling 10 dice with 1 success for 4 successes. Earth Aspect intercepts with defend other. They miss.<br /> Urias\u2019 Anima deals 1 damage to everyone. Smiling Hound takes lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 5</b><br /> <br /> Urias makes a decisive attack against Smiling Hound, rolling 10 dice and getting 7 successes. The lunar is at defence 1 and has no motes, cannot defend. 20 dice of decisive damage for 13 successes leaves Smiling Hound at -4 with only 2 health levels left. Urias resets to initiative 3.<br /> The wolfmen make a last-ditch attempt to rescue their boss and attack with 9 dice and 1 success and get 10 successes! Earth Aspect intercepts with defend other. He takes 2 dice for 1 damage. Takes 2 dice for 1 damage. Urias drops to 1 initiative. So close, yet so far.<br /> The legionnaires attack the engaged lunar with 10 dice for 7 successes. Smiling Hound spends 5 motes on Impenetrable Best Armor and the Stamina Excellency. He takes 7 dice for 2 successes, just enough to incapacitate him.<br /> <br /> <i>The anathema dies skewered by dozens of spears. The remaining beastmen who witness this drop their weapons in horror and turn to flee, but the Ramparts of Obedient Earth block the way. They surrender and plead for mercy and are taken prisoners to be interrogated.<br /> <br /> Cathak Urias smiles. When he reaches the rebellious province, he will have an army at his back and the head of a Frenzied in a bag.</i><br /> <div align=\"center\"><u><b><i>FIN</i></b></u></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:13:55-07:00","id":1307954,"title":"","content":"Oh I figured out a lunar combo that can maybe actually do it but its kind of silly. First you do the predators menace trick, then reflexively turn back into human form and Behemoths Footprint Thread + Fatal Stroke Flash. Thats all your motes and half your WP gone round 1 but it should blow up pretty much every non-celestial in range with the extra damage dice from FSF.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307944#post1307944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it helps, but if you're truly anathema hunting I would never underestimate them. A Lunar can look like anyone and hide almost anywhere, they have Might 1 battlegroups of beastmen, they ALSO travel in groups and might even outnumber you, and can attack in ways you might not even consider. Economic damage, social revolt, plagues, unleashing the undead, destroying diplomatic ties with other nations and the gods.<br /> <br /> They can also attack from stealth, deal damage, and retreat, wearing you down slowly over hours or days, sapping health and motes both. BUT if the chips are down and your in a final fight where it's 6 on 1, then probably you're going to live.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah there's definitely no safe way to hunt anathema, and if its a group you're pretty much doomed. My meaning was more like 'if you dont want to get splattered round 1 every time'. A DB without any Ox-Bodies is usually just dead as their odds of parrying/dodging against celestial dicepools are real bad, so you have to build around expecting to get hit for a lot of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-26-2019, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:31:05-07:00","id":1307961,"title":"","content":"@badassoverlord<br /> Awesome battle! Just wanted to check, how was Cathak Urias flurrying his defend other with his command actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-26-2019, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:41:49-07:00","id":1307965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307961#post1307961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@badassoverlord<br /> Awesome battle! Just wanted to check, how was Cathak Urias flurrying his defend other with his command actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>He activated Flame Warden Stance while waiting for the beastmen to walk into range. It extends the duration of a Defend Other action to One Scene.<br /> <br /> Man that charm did a lot of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:57:39-07:00","id":1307970,"title":"","content":"I wonder that the DBs are being built in this thread with exactly the charms necessary to counter the Celestial Exalts with the benefits of foresight not extending the other way...?<br /> <br /> Makes for one sided and possibly misleading encounters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:01:53-07:00","id":1307972,"title":"","content":"Awesome story! I never thought of using Defend Other on a battlegroup before. Or defending from a battlegroup for that matter. I'm not really sure if you even can...but I can't see any rule that says you can't so I guess up to the ST at the time.<br /> <br /> Good job on remembering Engage though, I forgot that was even an ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:10:34-07:00","id":1307974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307970#post1307970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder that the DBs are being built in this thread with exactly the charms necessary to counter the Celestial Exalts with the benefits of foresight not extending the other way...?<br /> <br /> Makes for one sided and possibly misleading encounters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey. I have done no such thing. If I wanted to build characters that directly countered Intimidate rolls, trust me, I could have.<br /> <br /> Everyone has max resolve, a specialty in not getting threatened, and everyone has Ten Thousand Dragons Fight As One, Thicker Than Stone, and Waves-Swallow-Mountains Persistance. That's 9 base resolve, with an automatic boost due to reflexive activations of Oath of Ten Thousand Dragons, +3 net for defining intimacies for eachother, +2 non-charm bonus from Thicker Than Stone, and -1 successes for up to two 1s on the threaten roll, for a total effective Resolve of 16.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:11:30-07:00","id":1307975,"title":"","content":"Sure, I agree, and was not specifically referring to that particular fight. <br /> <br /> But Defend other is an Ess 1 Lunar trick that they are VERY good at. (Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance)<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m basically trying to understand how Ess1 Lunar warlord with battlegroup got punked by Ess 3 DB warlord with equivalent battlegroup)<br /> <br /> Edit: I seem to recall it was you who said, all things being equal, Lunars beat DBs one on one? It seems that all things were equal here but one side was not using superior tactics that were by right available to both? That doesn\u2019t sit well with me, apologies for the slight rancour)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-26-2019, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:24:13-07:00","id":1307976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307975#post1307975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I agree. But Defend other is an Ess 1 Lunar trick that they are VERY good at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, good. I just worked very hard to try and make sure that I wasn't building things to counter other things specifically, and instead just tried to make DBs that were kind of reasonable and had a cohesive theme about them.<br /> <br /> I also could have miraculously had Murderkitty fight 3 Fire Aspect brawl DBs with smash fists making smash attacks, cancelling out that tasty evasion bonus, because being prone is an automatic -2 evasion, which she'd need to activate Bending Before the Storm to mitigate for every attack. Then when she's crashed she's taking 9 dice of lethal from the animas every turn. Totally <i>could </i>have done that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:28:35-07:00","id":1307977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307970#post1307970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder that the DBs are being built in this thread with exactly the charms necessary to counter the Celestial Exalts with the benefits of foresight not extending the other way...?<br /> <br /> Makes for one sided and possibly misleading encounters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly didn\u2019t optimise as much as I could have, though to be fair in my case I was making a fresh Solar go up against an essence 5 DB, the DB just had far more XP to work with and dip about.<br /> <br /> Boulder could have gotten some better defensive charms, but she was constrained quite a bit by buying all of Earth Dragon, much of which was simply irrelevant.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10131_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10131\" data-vbnamecard=\"10131\">BadassOverlord</a> aaaaah that makes sense. Yeah what a workhorse of a charm! Much like consuming might of the fire dragon in mine!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-26-2019, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:31:05-07:00","id":1307978,"title":"","content":"Right. No need for you to feel accused. Your fights seemed even handed. <br /> <br /> But you see my point here, right? If Defend other works so well, and the Lunar has access to charms that are as good for it if not better than the DB (Ferocious Guardian is scene long) with no pre-reqs...<br /> <br /> Why not Use it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-26-2019, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:33:40-07:00","id":1307979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307978#post1307978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. No need for you to feel accused. Your fights seemed even handed.<br /> <br /> But you see my point here, right? If Defend other works so well, and the Lunar has access to charms that are as good for it if not better than the DB (Ferocious Guardian is scene long)...<br /> <br /> Why not Use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm also dubious about Defend Other being able to be used on battlegroups by battlegroups as well. I can't find a ruling but I'd probably say it's somewhat nonsensical.<br /> <br /> EDIT: sorry about getting all defensive, it's just a lot of work and I even did almost an entire fight twice because I realized I wasn't using the Lunars motes as efficiently as I could have been on defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-26-2019, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:40:41-07:00","id":1307980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307977#post1307977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly didn\u2019t optimise as much as I could have, though to be fair in my case I was making a fresh Solar go up against an essence 5 DB, the DB just had far more XP to work with and dip about.<br /> <br /> Boulder could have gotten some better defensive charms, but she was constrained quite a bit by buying all of Earth Dragon, much of which was simply irrelevant.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10131_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10131\" data-vbnamecard=\"10131\">BadassOverlord</a> aaaaah that makes sense. Yeah what a workhorse of a charm! Much like consuming might of the fire dragon in mine!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t blame you in any case, a Solar taking an elemental Style is always a mugs game (or often) so if they lost to an Immaculate Master, then makes more sense than not.<br /> <br /> Edit: I\u2019m probably looking for a more proving-ground kind of results as compared to \u201cInteresting Battle Simulator\u201d and the disconnect is my bad. No need to stress it anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-26-2019, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:47:37-07:00","id":1307981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307979#post1307979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: sorry about getting all defensive, it's just a lot of work and I even did almost an entire fight twice because I realized I wasn't using the Lunars motes as efficiently as I could have been on defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no. I apologize, both for tarring you with the same untrue brush and for trying to wrangle something out of this thread it wasn\u2019t set up to give and then getting frustrated about it. That\u2019s my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T00:04:40-07:00","id":1307984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307981#post1307981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no. I apologize, both for tarring you with the same untrue brush and for trying to wrangle something out of this thread it wasn\u2019t set up to give and then getting frustrated about it. That\u2019s my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if it makes you feel better, this is my shitty notes for an Essence 1 Lunar Bear grappler vs an Essence 5 master of Water Dragon Style<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Round 1: Roll for Initiative<br /> <br /> Lunar got 16<br /> DB got 12<br /> <br /> ===========<br /> Round 1<br /> Lunar attacks with full excellency (8m) Finding Needles Eye(3m), Divine Pred Strike (2m), strength excellency (3m)<br /> DB defends with 9 defense<br /> <br /> 16 to hit<br /> dealing 3 damage<br /> <br /> <br /> DB will attack with Drowning in Blood (3m) full excellency (6m) and FLowing Water Defense (4m)<br /> Lunar Defends with Agile Beast Defense (1m) and Full Defense (8m)<br /> <br /> DB misses<br /> ===========<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks with full excellency (8m) Finding Needles Eye(3m), Divine Pred Strike (2m), strength excellency (3m)<br /> DB defends with 10 defense<br /> <br /> 16 to hit with 3 10s<br /> deals 10 damage, but use bear ability to forgo damage to clinch instead with Grizzly Bear Embrace. So with bear ability is rolling. DB defends with Rolling Water and full excellency (10m)<br /> <br /> Lunar wins by 12<br /> <br /> <br /> Immidiately makes mauling bite Unstoppable Beast Blow (2m)<br /> Rolls awful on damage, gets only 8<br /> <br /> <br /> DB will attack with full excellency (6m) Lunar defends with agile beast<br /> <br /> DB doesn't hit<br /> ===========<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Lunar releases with decisive forfitting 10 rounds of control, dead<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, that's what Essence 1 Lunar vs Essence 5 Terrestrial looks like 1v1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T00:04:59-07:00","id":1307985,"title":"","content":"All good! The thread is kind of pulling double duty in that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T04:15:21-07:00","id":1307998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307984#post1307984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar attacks with full excellency (8m) Finding Needles Eye(3m), Divine Pred Strike (2m), strength excellency (3m)</div> </div> </div> </div>Any reason you didn't throw 10m on the Dex excellency? I'm pretty sure Finding The Needles Eye doesn't count against dice-cap since it ignores Defense bonus rather than buffing your attack pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T04:43:14-07:00","id":1308002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307998#post1307998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any reason you didn't throw 10m on the Dex excellency? I'm pretty sure Finding The Needles Eye doesn't count against dice-cap since it ignores Defense bonus rather than buffing your attack pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure what I was thinking, maybe trying to conserve motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T05:45:54-07:00","id":1308012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307984#post1307984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well if it makes you feel better, this is my shitty notes for an Essence 1 Lunar Bear grappler vs an Essence 5 master of Water Dragon Style<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Round 1: Roll for Initiative<br /> <br /> Lunar got 16<br /> DB got 12<br /> <br /> ===========<br /> Round 1<br /> Lunar attacks with full excellency (8m) Finding Needles Eye(3m), Divine Pred Strike (2m), strength excellency (3m)<br /> DB defends with 9 defense<br /> <br /> 16 to hit<br /> dealing 3 damage<br /> <br /> <br /> DB will attack with Drowning in Blood (3m) full excellency (6m) and FLowing Water Defense (4m)<br /> Lunar Defends with Agile Beast Defense (1m) and Full Defense (8m)<br /> <br /> DB misses<br /> ===========<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks with full excellency (8m) Finding Needles Eye(3m), Divine Pred Strike (2m), strength excellency (3m)<br /> DB defends with 10 defense<br /> <br /> 16 to hit with 3 10s<br /> deals 10 damage, but use bear ability to forgo damage to clinch instead with Grizzly Bear Embrace. So with bear ability is rolling. DB defends with Rolling Water and full excellency (10m)<br /> <br /> Lunar wins by 12<br /> <br /> <br /> Immidiately makes mauling bite Unstoppable Beast Blow (2m)<br /> Rolls awful on damage, gets only 8<br /> <br /> <br /> DB will attack with full excellency (6m) Lunar defends with agile beast<br /> <br /> DB doesn't hit<br /> ===========<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Lunar releases with decisive forfitting 10 rounds of control, dead<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, that's what Essence 1 Lunar vs Essence 5 Terrestrial looks like 1v1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that was a lot more lethal than I expected. I would have thought Bottomless Depths Defense would have let them survive at least 1 more round. Poor guy.<br /> <br /> For a genuine question, what charms/equipment would a group of DBs take to go giant monster-hunting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T06:13:04-07:00","id":1308014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308012#post1308012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, that was a lot more lethal than I expected. I would have thought Bottomless Depths Defense would have let them survive at least 1 more round. Poor guy.<br /> <br /> For a genuine question, what charms/equipment would a group of DBs take to go giant monster-hunting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think he had like three ox bodies, and BDD must be declared, like any defensive charm, before any rolling happens, and it\u2019s only once per day. And with 8 health levels left you don\u2019t expect somebody at 3 initiative to be able to kill you, so you save your 1/day PD. Maybe a tactical mistake, but an understandable one.<br /> <br /> Bears are very scary.<br /> <br /> Also if you\u2019re hunting giant monsters take direlances, heavy weapons with the piercing tag, and make piercing attacks to get through their heavy armor. Or use high minimum damage through charms and stuff and high accuracy weapons. Also either wear heavy armor or do not be stingy on the defensive motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T06:20:55-07:00","id":1308015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307975#post1307975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I agree, and was not specifically referring to that particular fight. <br /> <br /> But Defend other is an Ess 1 Lunar trick that they are VERY good at. (Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance)<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m basically trying to understand how Ess1 Lunar warlord with battlegroup got punked by Ess 3 DB warlord with equivalent battlegroup)<br /> <br /> Edit: I seem to recall it was you who said, all things being equal, Lunars beat DBs one on one? It seems that all things were equal here but one side was not using superior tactics that were by right available to both? That doesn\u2019t sit well with me, apologies for the slight rancour)</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of things on this:<br /> - I did give more charms to the DB than to the Lunar on account of him being Essence 3; I feel like the amount of charms available to each fighter was appropriate and the Earth Aspect wound up not using half of them.<br /> - I tried to characterize the commanders somewhat through their choice of powers. The Earth Aspect was a defensive commander who cared about the lives of her men. The Lunar was an aggressive leader commanding fanatical troops. That's the big reason I chose Appearance warfare charms over Charisma ones: they include things like Diving Hawk Inspiration that felt more blitzkrieg-y to me. It's also why I went with medium armor and natural weapons despite it not being the strictly optimal choice.<br /> - More specifically regarding the defend other: I don't think it would have helped the Lunar much; it might have made things worse for him. The wolfmen only lost effectiveness at the very end - the reason they lost was that the Lunar broke first, defending the BG would have only cost him more motes and got him crashed earlier. Meanwhile the DB could tank for days relying solely on his passive soak of 16 without losing motes. Now, if the Lunar had had defend other charms, a medium weapon and heavy moonsilver plate, THAT would have been a very different story. But that feels too much like a different character, and I think this outcome highlights the advantage that DBs have with their greater availability of artifacts.<br /> - The thing that really won that fight was Ramparts of Obedient Earth. Holy shit. If the Lunar could have gotten the ambush he might have been able to put wound penalties on the commander and started a deathspiral of wasting actions rallying instead of giving attack orders. Also in this scenario I didn't give either party ranged attack because I specifically wanted to see an infantry clash. If the realm troops had been given bows, they could have taken 3-4 free shots with orders while the wolfmen were stuck wading through difficult terrain. That would have ended very quickly.<br /> - Lastly, the wolfmen had an advantage from Might 1 and slightly better stats, but the greater size and the ability to Engage wound up counting more in the end, which I didn't expect.<br /> <br /> Hopefully my thought process is a bit clearer. I certainly didn't intent to rig the match or anything.<br /> <br /> EDIT: this was very stream-of-consciousness style so sorry for the shitty redaction/formatting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":10131,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","user":"BadassOverlord","date":". 04-26-2019, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T06:46:21-07:00","id":1308018,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, you played out the combat as you planned it in your head, and I can see your logic. Just a couple of things:<br /> <br /> - Soak-wise, you make a point about how the DB had good soak. You know who has good soak? Lunars have good soak. Better soak than DBs, even better than Solars. (there's a reason the term is &quot;soakbeast&quot;) They can do this entirely without artifacts, which is part of their eternal charm to me (please refer to my Changing Moon for an example). If the Lunar warlord didn't have good soak, then I feel no effort was spent there at all (heck, he could have become a Pestletail for basically no mote expenditure and already had better Soak than the DB).<br /> <br /> - The tactics were as you yourself say, unfortunate, but I cannot blame you if you were actively trying to play the Lunar warlord as dumb.<br /> <br /> But, sure, it was your fight to set up and it played out as you indicated that it did.<br /> <br /> I just wonder what would have happened if the Dragonblooded leader had also made &quot;not strictly optimal&quot; choices. And I also hope the natural reaction of readers is not &quot;Lunar Warlords can't even win when the odds are even!&quot; Because some pretty obvious tactical/charm/build sub-optimal choices were made here for the Lunar.<br /> <br /> Edit: Don't take this the wrong way guys, but having a Solar learn a sub-par martial arts where Mastery means less than dirt and running a pitched battle where unarmed/mundane armor (with no soak charms?) Lunar warlord impales himself onto the gleaming artifacts of a Prince of the Earth just chafes my sense of fair play, even if people didn't mean to rig things.<br /> <br /> It just doesn't seem satisfying at all, these kinds of brawls to hype up DB ability by pitching flawed and easily exploitable challenges at them. But if people want to go that route, I will, with as much grace as I can muster, withdraw from this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-26-2019, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T07:52:42-07:00","id":1308026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308018#post1308018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The tactics were as you yourself say, unfortunate, but I cannot blame you if you were actively trying to play the Lunar warlord as dumb .</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think aggressive necessarily means dumb. This is a thing Lunars can do, raise up resistances and fanatical armies and use them to cause issues for the Realm then dip out just as easily as spending time building a nice, stable, powerful domain.<br /> <br /> Then rinse and repeat four times in three years and see how victorious the Realm feels with rapidly depleting resources while you turn into a bird and fuck off to do it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T08:33:16-07:00","id":1308033,"title":"","content":"Well fuck you too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T08:57:53-07:00","id":1308038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308018#post1308018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Don't take this the wrong way guys, but having a Solar learn a sub-par martial arts where Mastery means less than dirt and running a pitched battle where unarmed/mundane armor (with no soak charms?) Lunar warlord impales himself onto the gleaming artifacts of a Prince of the Earth just chafes my sense of fair play, even if people didn't mean to rig things.<br /> <br /> It just doesn't seem satisfying at all, these kinds of brawls to hype up DB ability by pitching flawed and easily exploitable challenges at them. But if people want to go that route, I will, with as much grace as I can muster, withdraw from this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seriously don't know why anyone but a DB would learn a dragon style. Those feel weaker than normal MAs anyway. Even for E5, I have not seen any of them have charms better than the E3 &quot;Mediocre&quot; styles. I'm not even talking about Single point. They still feel lacking to styles like snake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T09:27:28-07:00","id":1308043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308038#post1308038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seriously don't know why anyone but a DB would learn a dragon style. Those feel weaker than normal MAs anyway. Even for E5, I have not seen any of them have charms better than the E3 &quot;Mediocre&quot; styles. I'm not even talking about Single point. They still feel lacking to styles like snake.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Immaculate styles are extremely powerful, but sometimes they take more finesse to use.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon has a form that gives you a permanent +2 Evasion and an autosuccesse on all stealth, rush and disengage actions, while also doubling 9s on all movement and stealth rolls, also once per turn you can pay 5i to make a reflexive attack out of turn, in addition to your normal attack, which can explicitly be used to clash, and all your chakram attacks count as being from close range regardless of where you launch them from.<br /> <br /> Snake form gives...+Dex to soak and a -3 penalty to attackers, but only if they\u2019re not equal to or higher in initiative, where it\u2019s -1. Yep, definitely seems leagues better than the Air Dragon one, and more versatile too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-26-2019, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T09:32:40-07:00","id":1308045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308043#post1308043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Immaculate styles are extremely powerful, but sometimes they take more finesse to use.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon has a form that gives you a permanent +2 Evasion and an autosuccesse on all stealth, rush and disengage actions, while also doubling 9s on all movement and stealth rolls, also once per turn you can pay 5i to make a reflexive attack out of turn, in addition to your normal attack, and all your chakram attacks count as being from close range regardless of where you launch them from.<br /> <br /> Snake form gives...+Dex to soak and a -3 penalty to attackers, but only if they\u2019re not equal to or higher in initiative, where it\u2019s -1. Yep, definitely seems leagues better than the Air Dragon one, and more versatile too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Keep in mind, -3 penalty on attack rolls is pretty massive, particularly against other Dragon-Blooded who can't really make up for it due to their smaller dice caps. Also, Air Dragon Form doesn't do any of that until you get the capstone at Essence 5 going through like 13 Charms, Snake Form does all of that straight out of E1. Until then it's +1 Evasion, +1 sux on stealth and disengage, Close Range accuracy. The latter doesn't really matter if you intend on combining styles, and the others depend on having decent Dodge and Stealth; Snake does all of what it does just needing you to stay on top of initiative, and everyone and their mother picks Dex 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T09:35:52-07:00","id":1308048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308043#post1308043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Immaculate styles are extremely powerful, but sometimes they take more finesse to use.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon has a form that gives you a permanent +2 Evasion and an autosuccesse on all stealth, rush and disengage actions, while also doubling 9s on all movement and stealth rolls, also once per turn you can pay 5i to make a reflexive attack out of turn, in addition to your normal attack, which can explicitly be used to clash, and all your chakram attacks count as being from close range regardless of where you launch them from.<br /> <br /> Snake form gives...+Dex to soak and a -3 penalty to attackers, but only if they\u2019re not equal to or higher in initiative, where it\u2019s -1. Yep, definitely seems leagues better than the Air Dragon one, and more versatile too.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, that's at E5. Second at E2, snake style gets (dex + essence) soak -1-3 penalty and +2 to withering attacks. Air costs 14m 1wp snake costs 9m 1wp. In addition, it's disingenuous to use a capstone to compare to a base form charm. However, Pound for pound snake style does more and is actually at the level of a martial art without mastery. The dragon styles are not and other than specific charms, most of which can't even be properly used by non-dragonblooded, they are not styles worth taking if you aren't a dragon blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-26-2019, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T10:00:59-07:00","id":1308054,"title":"","content":"Oh ffs. You literally JUST said \u201cEven for Essence 5\u201d so we\u2019re talking about Essence 5. <br /> <br /> Also Snake 100% requires you to take Evasion as well or Serpentine Evasion is literally useless, and even then it\u2019s utter crap unless combined with other charms because your Snake Style parry is always going to be 1 greater than your evasion because you\u2019re wielding medium weapons. If it missed your evasion by 1 it didn\u2019t hit your parry. It\u2019s not even like its a non-charm success, it just lets you wait to activate it. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile Air Dragon gives you insane disengage rolls and the ability to flurry a disengage with an attack or aim action without any flurry penalties or initiative cost. Which is great, because you\u2019re hitting with chakram attacks as though you were Close after you retreat to Short. Since you disengaged instead of using a charm like Hopping Firecracker you also get a free reflexive move away if somebody follows you to give chance.<br /> <br /> You can even start stacking onslaught penalties with yourself, striking and then reflexively launching an attack for 5i, which even if you don\u2019t make back is still worth it for stacking onslaught penalties.<br /> <br /> Also opponents having equal or more initiative than you happens a lot. It doesn\u2019t even have to be your fault, if you make a decisive attack and some enemy in the combat has anything more than 2 initiative your bonus drops. Snake might even be better by some margin, but I can\u2019t fathom how you look at the Immaculate styles and think they\u2019re so much worse that it\u2019s not even worth thinking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T10:23:11-07:00","id":1308058,"title":"","content":"My even for essence 5 part is to note that most styles end at E3. Styles with mastery are stronger even without the mastery keyword than the dragon styles. <br /> <br /> More importantly, for solars, they lose mastery. For lunars and sidereals, they still can't use Auras. Even with auras some effects aren't as powerful. Look at Serpentine Evasion, only bottomless depths is better but it's also more restrictive and costs more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-26-2019, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T11:24:30-07:00","id":1308072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308058#post1308058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My even for essence 5 part is to note that most styles end at E3. Styles with mastery are stronger even without the mastery keyword than the dragon styles. <br /> <br /> More importantly, for solars, they lose mastery. For lunars and sidereals, they still can't use Auras. Even with auras some effects aren't as powerful. Look at Serpentine Evasion, only bottomless depths is better but it's also more restrictive and costs more.</div> </div> </div> </div>For pure power reasons, no, a Solar shouldn\u2019t use an Immaculate style over the ones presented in the corebook. Mastery is too powerful. If you want to impersonate a DB or something then sure, otherwise grab RD or Snek or something.<br /> <br /> But they do have some charms that are better, and are better at some things, than the corebook styles.<br /> <br /> Air dragon isn\u2019t even that good among the Immaculate styles, and it still lets you do shenanigans with disengage. If you\u2019re facing an opponent who isn\u2019t invested heavily into athletics and doesn\u2019t have a good ranged attack, it\u2019s the most frustrating thing in the world. They flurry a disengage with an attack, with an auto success, double 9s and another 4 dice for 4m, they disengage and attack twice. Next turn you reflexively move after them, they get a reflexive move back, you Rush, they contest with double 9s 4 dice for 4m and a free success, if you don\u2019t win this one then next turn they attack twice and reflexively move to medium range, even if you do win they can then attack you with a reflexive attack and then Avenging Wind Strike or Wrathful Winds Kiai and send you hurtling back out of range if your rush, and wasting your turn again. And they just keep doing it over and over. Their chakram has a range of medium too, so if they aim that\u2019s the range. <br /> <br /> <br /> It would drive you fucking insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T11:31:47-07:00","id":1308073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307699#post1307699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Arena that is a somewhat dangerous and slippery slope that I wouldn't necessarily want to go down. If you're letting merits like Command or Retainers onto the field each Terrestrial will get 18 to your 10, for a total inequality of 54 to 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, going into a Merit-race with Dragonblooded is a losing proposition and not really worth it.<br /> <br /> What about a Lunar character that goes fully for the kind of thing Lunars are supposedly best at: Guerilla warfare combining stealth, mobility, and flexibly changing between ranged and melee combat. I.e. a Lunar that is quick enough to stay out of melee range from the dangerous melee fighters, stealthy enough to be invisible to those quick enough to catch him, and good enough at both melee and ranged to shoot the melee enemies and melee/grapple the ranged ones. The fluff tells us Lunars should be able to do this well and relatively early and the flexible nature of Lunar charms seems to support it, but I don't know enough about DB and Lunar charmsets to gauge how realistic that approach it.<br /> Downside is that a Lunar kiting around a bunch of DBs sounds like an extremely long and boring combat to run that I wouldn't wish on my worst enemy<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T11:49:18-07:00","id":1308078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308072#post1308072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For pure power reasons, no, a Solar shouldn\u2019t use an Immaculate style over the ones presented in the corebook. Mastery is too powerful. If you want to impersonate a DB or something then sure, otherwise grab RD or Snek or something.<br /> <br /> But they do have some charms that are better, and are better at some things, than the corebook styles.<br /> <br /> Air dragon isn\u2019t even that good among the Immaculate styles, and it still lets you do shenanigans with disengage. If you\u2019re facing an opponent who isn\u2019t invested heavily into athletics and doesn\u2019t have a good ranged attack, it\u2019s the most frustrating thing in the world. They flurry a disengage with an attack, with an auto success, double 9s and another 4 dice for 4m, they disengage and attack twice. Next turn you reflexively move after them, they get a reflexive move back, you Rush, they contest with double 9s 4 dice for 4m and a free success, if you don\u2019t win this one then next turn they attack twice and reflexively move to medium range, even if you do win they can then attack you with a reflexive attack and then Avenging Wind Strike or Wrathful Winds Kiai and send you hurtling back out of range if your rush, and wasting your turn again. And they just keep doing it over and over. Their chakram has a range of medium too, so if they aim that\u2019s the range. <br /> <br /> <br /> It would drive you fucking insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>To say they are useless, would be wrong, but half those things only apply in air aura. For that kind of investment, there are way better styles celestials could take advantage of. It also doesn't change the fact that those styles are weaker than a normal MA is. Like normal mas don't limit you to your enemies rolling 1s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T12:17:14-07:00","id":1308087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308078#post1308078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To say they are useless, would be wrong, but half those things only apply in air aura. For that kind of investment, there are way better styles celestials could take advantage of. It also doesn't change the fact that those styles are weaker than a normal MA is. Like normal mas don't limit you to your enemies rolling 1s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Falcon Style, Centipede Style, Swaying Grass Style, and Golden Jannisary Style all have charms that rely on your enemy\u2019s 1s, and none of those effects are terrestrial keyword exclusive either. I don\u2019t think any of them even have mastery keywords that make them better.<br /> <br /> Mantis, White Veil and Laughing Monster are the only post-core published styles that DON\u2019T have that effect as far as I can tell. And some of the IMAs don\u2019t have it. Also the Lunar charmset has it even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-26-2019, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T12:27:57-07:00","id":1308088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308073#post1308073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, going into a Merit-race with Dragonblooded is a losing proposition and not really worth it.<br /> <br /> What about a Lunar character that goes fully for the kind of thing Lunars are supposedly best at: Guerilla warfare combining stealth, mobility, and flexibly changing between ranged and melee combat. I.e. a Lunar that is quick enough to stay out of melee range from the dangerous melee fighters, stealthy enough to be invisible to those quick enough to catch him, and good enough at both melee and ranged to shoot the melee enemies and melee/grapple the ranged ones. The fluff tells us Lunars should be able to do this well and relatively early and the flexible nature of Lunar charms seems to support it, but I don't know enough about DB and Lunar charmsets to gauge how realistic that approach it.<br /> Downside is that a Lunar kiting around a bunch of DBs sounds like an extremely long and boring combat to run that I wouldn't wish on my worst enemy</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound like a cool concept for a future battle, but I\u2019m kind of done with \u201cmaybe this can beat 3 DBs.\u201d There\u2019s waaay the fuck too much splat vs splat going on anyway, when such a small percentage of what I\u2019ve seen and run in Exalted was that anyway. Just about the only fight in this whole thread I had a good time running was the one against the Greenmaws.<br /> <br /> Oh also just to prove that I could, but won\u2019t, if I wanted to be an unfair douche about that fight I\u2019d have them face three master archers with wood dragon style. Excellent trackers and hunters that treat all powerbows as Wrackstaves for the purposes of their MA. Almost nothing in Exalted exists without some way to get around it if you try.<br /> <br /> Prototype is also right that it gives skewed ideas about what\u2019s realistic. For one if everyone has soak 15+ it makes minimum damage adders seem like the best thing in the world and damage boosters suck. Also that you need to excellency every attack even if you\u2019re wielding artifacts which is laughable. Half the enemies in this game have a Defense value of like, 4, and no way to boost it. Save your motes for fun stuff, not dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T13:03:07-07:00","id":1308094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308088#post1308088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That does sound like a cool concept for a future battle, but I\u2019m kind of done with \u201cmaybe this can beat 3 DBs.\u201d There\u2019s waaay the fuck too much splat vs splat going on anyway, when such a small percentage of what I\u2019ve seen and run in Exalted was that anyway. Just about the only fight in this whole thread I had a good time running was the one against the Greenmaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. though I hope at some point we get some tests on just how good Lunars really are at the approach to combat that fluff tells us they are supposed to excel at.<br /> Though I don't want to take to much of the thread up with this as I don't have time to build characters or run test combats and I don't want to just come in and keep asking for stuff without doing anything myself.<br /> What would you say would be the most fun non-exalted opponents for such a Lunar to face?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:16:54-07:00","id":1308163,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t speak for every dragon style but I mean, the answer (to the double question of \u2018should non DBs take them\u2019 and \u2018are they as good as other styles\u2019) is threefold.<br /> <br /> A) The cap charms. These supplement the Form, and while they\u2019re expensive, they absolutely make the forms superior to other MA forms. Earth Dragon is a flat +10 to nat soak and Hardness assuming you have 5 stamina. More if you boosted WP. These are lunar numbers and they last the scene.<br /> Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon is +3 overwhelming. If you have an artifact weapon that adds up a lot, and if you don\u2019t have one well congratulations because now you have a pseudo one. You\u2019re also punishing the enemy for hitting you, regardless of how much Hardness they have. Again you don\u2019t have to do Anything. Assuming you won JB you didnt even use up an action. Motes, yes. But your form is providing the effect of several excellent charms every turn for the rest of the combat.<br /> These are significant effects that are matched by few MAs in terms of scene-long effects.<br /> <br /> B) MAs aren\u2019t in competition. If you took every MA and entered optimised splats into a swisse/elimination tournament, like I guess Shining Point would do well? White Reaper would seem kinda bad, actually, without multiple opponents.<br /> Except Righteous Devil and Shining Point would be freaking D e m o l i s h e d by Black Claw. Specifically by table-turning reversal.<br /> The other thing that would happen is you would stop because it take forever and actually not be very fun.<br /> The Dragon styles aren\u2019t great against other MAs because they\u2019re not well suited to countering them. And that\u2019s ok. No one is out here saying Golden Janissary is useless because Solars/DBs/Lunars aren\u2019t Creatures of Darkness.<br /> <br /> C) I mean, they\u2019re really good if you want to fight Rogue Gods or Demons or Elementals? Like really good. Way better than pretty much any other MA. Maybe Golden Janissary against Demons and ghosts, but even then I\u2019m not certain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly. The thread is pulling double duty between cross-comparing combat styles and writing fights that are of interest to us. Running and balancing a combat by yourself is time consuming and difficult, I wouldn\u2019t think that having the fights be narratively compelling is too much to ask.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not pulling a third duty of advocating for any splat or MAs superiority. Like we\u2019re talking about what does and doesn\u2019t work in practice... that\u2019s not the same as arguing for or against builds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:41:31-07:00","id":1308170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308163#post1308163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not pulling a third duty of advocating for any splat or MAs superiority. Like we\u2019re talking about what does and doesn\u2019t work in practice... that\u2019s not the same as arguing for or against builds.</div> </div> </div> </div>It matters because it should be assumed that if the dragon blooded is going to be fighting at his most optimal then his opponent should be as well. The dragon styles are optimal for no one but the dragon blooded. This is the flat out fact. They have amazing form charm caps but the charms in between aren't worth one or two effects when those are easily bested by native charms. In addition, the aura keyword is necessary for these dragon styles to be impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T21:30:52-07:00","id":1308235,"title":"","content":"Okay, well I rolled out another fight against 3 DBs. It took five hours. It wasn't against a Lunar though, it was against an Essence 2 Dawn, Supernal Melee, with 5 in every stat and an assumed specialty always applicable int all abilities, and all 48 melee charms. He had artifact fullplate and a daiklave. Everyone had 2 ox-bodies and thank god for that because if they had more I would have killed myself.<br /> <br /> I did not build the DBs to kill him. They did not have max in every stat, they had two 5s and a 3 in their physical, 4 wits and no awareness specialty applicable. The Fire Aspect melee fighter was wielding a Grand Daiklave. The Water Aspect Brawler was wielding Smashfists with medium armor, and the Wood Aspect Archer had a powerbow and light armor. In the spoiler below is a play-by-play of my thought process trying to get the Solar to win.<br /> <br /> There's a TLDR; after the spoiler if you don't feel like wading through a thousand numbers.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Okay so first off, I need to spend everything I have into this join battle roll because for one it gives me decisive damage I can play with, and for another if I don't, and I roll bad, and one of those DBs goes before me, it could start a huge chain reaction where withering attack after withering attack puts me to the bottom or crashes me. Besides I get 5m back at the start of my turn.<br /> <br /> Solar spends 10m for 21 dice, gets 11 for 14 initiative<br /> Fire spends 4m for 2 successes, gets 5 for 8<br /> Water spends 4m for 2 successes gets 6 for 9<br /> Wood spends 4m for 2 successes, gets 5 for 8<br /> <br /> ==============<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Okay, so now I've gone first, none of the DBs rolled exceptionally well, so that's good. Now what do I do? If I don't activate Fivefold Bulwark right now, I'm vulnerable to onslaught penalties, and with it Dipping Swallow costs 1m and raises Parry by 1.<br /> <br /> I could try to do Ready in Eight Directions Stance, but all that'll happen then is one of the DBs will attack to provoke my reset, and the rest will just aim.<br /> <br /> I could try Heaven Sword Flash but my odds of incapping a DB with one blow are low on 7 initiative.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I could fire off an Incincible Fury of the Dawn, putting 3/3/3/4/4 into the attacks and relying on damage boosters to kill her, using Invincible Fury's move ment to get out from between these two melee fighters. I'd start running away afterwards to start regenerating motes, but then I'd have to start spending on shutting down rush attempts and that would be counterproductive.<br /> <br /> <br /> So that's what I'll do, 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn, 3m Fire and Stones Strike, 3m Excellent Strike, 3m 2i Hungry Tiger Technique, 1wp Perfect Strike Discipline, 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana.<br /> <br /> So a base cost of 18m, 2i, 3wp. Really good. What do I do about the excellency thouigh? I need about 16 dice of damage, with TAP active, to kill her 13 health levels, and I'm doubling a lot of the overflow damage. Her Evasion is 9/8/7/6/5, and I've got 11 dice, rerolling 1s, plus an autosuccess at base, and 1 free full one with Perfect Strike. So I use Perfect Strike on the last one and full excellency the previous 2 and I should be good. If I do that then I'll have 12 motes left, but only 2 opponants.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rolling 11 dice for 4 total successes, no hit<br /> Rolling 13 dice for total of 3 successes, no hit<br /> Note that if I dont excellency this next attack, the Wood Aspect uses her Anima power and I decently risk missing again.<br /> Rolling 23 dice for a total of 13, dealing 9 damage rolling for 5, doubling for 10<br /> Rolling 23 dice for a total of 13, dealing 10 damage rolling for 1, doubling for 2<br /> Rolling 22 dice for a total of 15, dealing 13 damage, rolling for 5, doubling for 10<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> The Wood aspect is SLAIN. Perfect Strike Discipline resets! Supernal is a hell of a thing. Okay, next the Water Aspect goes. Walking over to me he withers me for 6m full excellency, 5m Hammering Wave Technique.<br /> <br /> If this hits me, I am in some deep shit. I have 12m left, and I need 5 for Bulwark Stance or else the onslaught penalties are going to kill me, I'm going to try and get through this with Hail Shattering Practice, which will let me spend motes 1/success to remove an attackers successes post attack roll.<br /> <br /> He rolls 20 dice to hit, and gets it with 12. At Essnce 2 I can't remove enough successes to deal with this. Damage 8, rolling it for 5. I'm crashed and he gets initiative break. Okay, so now I'm targetting him, I need initiative shift to bring this fight back my way.<br /> ----------<br /> The fire aspect attacks, 6m full excellency, 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite, an attack with 18 dice to hit and 24 base damage. Activating Bulwark Stance I have 7m left now.<br /> <br /> She rolls 18 dice for 10 against my Parry of 7, rolling 11 damage for 7<br /> <br /> He enters Fire Aura<br /> ==============<br /> Round 2 starts<br /> <br /> Water goes first, activating 10m 1wp 1a Embracing the Violent Flow<br /> ----------<br /> Fire goes next, activating 3m 2i Flame Warden Stance, targetting Water. Note here that if I hadn't used Bulwark stance they would have been taking advantage of my onslaught penalties to farm some more initiative, or land crippling decisive attacks.<br /> ----------<br /> I go, I activate 5m Fivefold Bulwark Stance. Seems stupid aginst 2 opponants but it also discounts my first parry excellency by a mote each time, so it's saving me 4m this turn alone. I still have 7m for Hail Shattering Practice if I have to.<br /> ==============<br /> Round 3 starts<br /> <br /> Water goes, he attempts a grapple with 6m full excellency, 5m Inescapable Whirlpool Hold. If this hits me it's over, so I spend 1wp and full excellency my defence with Perfect Strike Discipline.<br /> <br /> He rolls 15 dice against my parry of 13 and fails with 7<br /> ----------<br /> Fire goes next, Striking with 5m full excellency, 3m 1wp Crimson Wolf Bite. I could respond with a reflexive clash, but if I lose I'm taking even more initiative damage due to the clash rules.<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 18 to attack for 11, rolling 12 damage for 3<br /> ----------<br /> My turn again, now with 12 motes I need to try and stop Water. But Fire is constantly using Defend Other on him. I'm stuck. I could sit here frugally using motes on defense, but their animas will cut me down even as I block every decisive blow. Assuming they don't just get lucky and kill me<br /> <br /> At this point, it's worth my time to wait for reset. It's free initiative. I simply attack Fire without using motes. He doesn't defend with motes either<br /> <br /> Rolling 14 against 7 I fail with 3<br /> ==============<br /> Round 4 starts<br /> <br /> Water goes and rolls no anima damage. Attacks me with a 6m full excellency I defend with 1m Dipping Swallow. He rolls 20 dice for 7, becoming 8 with EtVF, and I use 1m Hail Shattering Practice to cancel the attack.<br /> ----------<br /> Fire rolls no anima damage. Attacks with 6m Full excellency. I defend with 1m dipping swallow. Rolling 18 dice for 9 I spend 2m and cancel it with Hail Shattering Practice.<br /> ----------<br /> I go reset to 4 initiative. I attack Fire without spending motes. He defends without spending motes.<br /> <br /> I roll 14 dice against 7, getting it with 8. Rolling minimum damage of 5, for 5<br /> ==============<br /> Round 5 starts<br /> ----------<br /> Water uses an Aim<br /> ----------<br /> Fire uses Full Defense<br /> ----------<br /> Water has 20i, fire 12, and me 10. Water stands a very good chance of hitting me next round if I don't bring my full defenses to bear, and right now he's if I don't crash him, but behind. I take a full defense. I could try Ready in Eight Directions Stance, but Fire would just counter clash me with Cloud Riot.<br /> ==============<br /> Round 6 starts<br /> ----------<br /> Water attacks with 6m full excellency, I defend with 1m dipping swallow, 6m Excellency<br /> <br /> Water rolls 20 dice against a parry of 14, geting 7<br /> ----------<br /> Fire attacks with 6m full excellency. I defend with 1m Dipping Swallow, 4m excellency<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 18 dice agasint a parry of 13, missing with 6<br /> ----------<br /> If I attack Fire will Cloud Riot me and I don't have the motes to beat him in a clash. I take a full defense.<br /> ==============<br /> Round 7 starts<br /> Water attacks with 6m full excellency, I defend with 1m dipping swallow, 2m Excellency<br /> <br /> Water rolls 20 dice against a parry of 12, geting 12, I pay a mote to cancel with Hail Shattering<br /> ----------<br /> Fire attacks with 6m full excellency. I defend with 1m Dipping Swallow, 4m excellency<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 18 dice agasint a parry of 11, missing with 9<br /> ----------<br /> If I attack Fire will Cloud Riot me and I don't have the motes to beat him in a clash. I take a full defense.<br /> ==============<br /> Round 8 starts<br /> Water attacks me with a 6m full excellency, I defend with 1m dipping swallow and 2m excellency.<br /> <br /> Water rolls 20 dice against 11, hits with 14. I can not Hail Shattering Practice down to a miss.<br /> <br /> Water rolls minimum damage, which is 8, getting 4. I am now at 3 initiative<br /> ----------<br /> Fire attacks with 6m full excellency. I defend with 1m Dipping Swallow<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 18 dice agasint a parry of 10, missing with 7<br /> ----------<br /> If I attack Fire will Cloud Riot me and I don't have the motes to beat him in a clash. I take a full defense. This keeps happening because I keep needing to feed almost all the motes I get back each turn into defending myself, and the Dragonblooded can't afford to stop forcing me to do that or else I might be able to pull some kind of combo on them.<br /> ==============<br /> Round 9 starts<br /> Water attacks me with a 6m full excellency, I defend with 1m dipping swallow and 2m excellency.<br /> <br /> Water rolls 20 dice against Parry of 11, missing with 10<br /> ----------<br /> Fire attacks with 6m full excellency. I defend with 1m Dipping Swallow<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 18 dice agasint a parry of 10, getting 11, I pay 2m to Hail Shattering Practice it away.<br /> ----------<br /> I have 10m now, slowly creeping up turn after turn but I need to try and avoid being crashed. I attack Fire with 3m Excellent Strike, 7m full excellency. He responds with 6m full excellency, 5m Crossfire Slash, 4m 3i Cloud Riot.<br /> <br /> I roll 25 dice total for 11 successes, he rolls 23 dice for 13, beating me by 2. I have no motes left to Hail Shattering Practice.<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 6 damage for 0. I then take 3 initiative damage for losing a clash, and am crashed, hardness set to 0, and with no motes remaining to dipping swallow.<br /> <br /> I reflexively spend 1m 1wp 3a to peony blossom with 3m excellent strike. Fire defends with 4m excellency.<br /> <br /> I roll 17 dice total against a parry of 8 and miss with 7<br /> ==============<br /> Round 10 starts<br /> <br /> Water rolls 1 lethal and attempts a grapple gambit against me. 6m full excellency 5m inescapable whirlpool hold. I am out of motes to defend<br /> <br /> Water rolls 18 dice against parry of 7, getting 8<br /> <br /> Water easily makes the roll to lock in.<br /> <br /> Water rolls 6m full excellency for control roll, rolling 17 dice against my 11, getting 8 against my 11. I win control of the grapple but he still gets one action, which will be a decisive slam attack, 1m for exellency rerolling 6s<br /> <br /> Rolling 25 initiative damage for 10 damage<br /> ----------<br /> Fire rolls 0 damage with anima and attacks with 6m full excellency decisive.<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 17 dice agasint a parry of 7, getting 3 and missing<br /> ----------<br /> I flurry a rise from prone with an attack against Water<br /> <br /> Rolling 11 dice and getting the rise with 12<br /> <br /> I attack water with 3m excellent strike, 2m excellency, Fire intervenes and does not spend motes to defend<br /> <br /> I roll 16 dice, getting 10 and hitting, rolling 5 damage for 4, pulling out of crash<br /> ==============<br /> Round 11 starts<br /> Fire attacks with 6m full excellency against my parry of 7, getting 8<br /> <br /> Rolling 6 damage for 3<br /> ----------<br /> Water Spends 5m on full excellency attack, rolling 19 and getting 12 against my 7 parry.<br /> <br /> Rolling 8 damage for 5, re-crashing me<br /> ----------<br /> I attack water with 2m excellency, 3m excellent strike, fire intervenes<br /> <br /> I roll 17 dice for 11 against Parry 6, rolling 7 damage for 4, pulling out of crash.<br /> ==============<br /> Round 12 starts<br /> <br /> Fire spends 5m on full exellency decisive attack against my parry of 7, rolling 17 dice and getting 12. Rolling 16 decisive damage for 7, killing me<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Basically in the first turn I used a doomcombo to kill the Archer right away. Then 11 rounds of slogging back and forth, with two poor sods trying to penetrate a Parry DV of base 7 while I had Fivefold Bulwark up and Hail Shattering Practice available. Between the two of those I can effectively raise my parry DV up to 10 for 3m. I gave it my absolute best attempt. I even went back and did some sections over again because I figured out a better way to do them.<br /> <br /> This isn't even remotely realistic for a game anyway. When would this ever happen? Want to see if your Lunar is really good at fighting? Fight 3 Bloodapes at once. If you think that's meaningless because obviously any remotely competent Essence 2 celestial exalt should be able to rip through 3 bloodapes without even thinking, rather than a demonstration of the gut-wrenchingly terrifying power of the Exalted, as far as I'm concerned, that's <i>your </i>problem.<br /> <br /> If you see something that you think I missed, or mistakes I made, or some crazy awesome combo that will definitely work, please, please keep it to yourself. I don't even care if I'm totally wrong and I have no idea how Lunars/Solars are supposed to fight and if I knew I'd have no trouble at all. I am done with this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T21:32:05-07:00","id":1308236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308094#post1308094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fair. though I hope at some point we get some tests on just how good Lunars really are at the approach to combat that fluff tells us they are supposed to excel at.<br /> Though I don't want to take to much of the thread up with this as I don't have time to build characters or run test combats and I don't want to just come in and keep asking for stuff without doing anything myself.<br /> What would you say would be the most fun non-exalted opponents for such a Lunar to face?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that approach will be very good, but I'm not testing it against 3 DBs, and I don't even think it would fare that much better anyway unless you were using it in an actual game and not in the arena.<br /> <br /> As for what might be fun? Well a friend showed me <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0GuqnIGsRuk\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> yesterday. Like Austreech Lunar vs Tyrant Lizard. I am, however, exhausted, and sick of calculating dicepools and rolling dice and puzzling out strategies.It will have to way until later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T21:44:26-07:00","id":1308239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308235#post1308235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't even remotely realistic for a game anyway. When would this ever happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanna know a funny thing? This happened to me. 4 DBs instead of 3, one was very focused on combat while the others were kind of but not as much, against a Melee Supernal with basically all Charms in Melee, Artifact Armor, and a Daiklave. Let's say I'm not excited to repeat the experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T00:41:27-07:00","id":1308249,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've ever played a 12 round fight, we thank you for your sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Actually I just remembered something I asked Vance about ages ago thats a huge advantage for any group of DBs fighting a lone celestial if they have the charms for it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1117984#post1117984\">You can defend other in a clash, and it really dicks the person clashing who doesn't have someone defending other for them.</a><br /> <br /> So as long as 2 or more DBs survive round 1, and know Flame Warden Stance, Portentous Comet Deflection, and Fire Incites Water to a Riot of Clouds, any lunar or solar who doesn't have some way to work around it is going eat penalties for losing a clash every time (s)he attacks even though he hits the DB defending.<br /> <br /> Saying that, its probably not something any ST should pull unless their players are really into the combat rules. If this thread has shown anything it's that QC rules exist for good reason and you should very seldom be building the opposition as combat-optimised PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-27-2019, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T04:18:26-07:00","id":1308276,"title":"","content":"Combat very interesting, and it makes me very clear the value of the charms that allow gain additional motes, especially Victorious Wreath in melee, although it has a cost of 1i per round the amount of earned motes seems worthwhile and helps to get out of the pit of the low initiative. Denying penalties is also absolutely vital,<br /> Even so an extremely long combat that ended up being decided by the expense of motes, but as it is well said is not something that can be seen realistically in a combat.<br /> In the end the Solar had bad luck, lost the Clash, lost with Peony blossom, if one of his attacks had impacted the final turns could have changed everything, the Dragon-Blooded had no charms to deny the penalties for injuries. In this context Blazing Solar Bolt could have been valuable in not requiring initiative to cause damage while ignoring Hardness, everything that puts a penalty for wounds on the enemy is valuable. But nobody have every charm in the game, obviously.<br /> Many thanks for the great effort put into the fight, I am learning a lot with this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T23:15:53-07:00","id":1308430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308235#post1308235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, well I rolled out another fight against 3 DBs. It took five hours. It wasn't against a Lunar though, it was against an Essence 2 Dawn, Supernal Melee, with 5 in every stat and an assumed specialty always applicable int all abilities, and all 48 melee charms. He had artifact fullplate and a daiklave. Everyone had 2 ox-bodies and thank god for that because if they had more I would have killed myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you do such a thing to yourself, friend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T10:29:11-07:00","id":1308483,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to see some more fights against non exalted foes. Hopefully they would be less taxing to run, more representative of the typical play session and a helpful guide to aspiring STs on how to fine tune their own encounters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T15:19:23-07:00","id":1308535,"title":"","content":"I would be interested in a test-duel between two Fire Aspected Melee-specialists. A mirror-match with just one difference.<br /> <br /> Both have Harnessed Firestorm Assault, but one of them uses the Fire Resistance Signature Charm, Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit.<br /> <br /> I just finished writing an entire thread breaking down how to build around that Charm to avoid shooting yourself in the foot with it, but that\u2019s book knowledge and not actual testing.<br /> <br /> If a mirror-match duel is too simple, I would ask that each Exalt is supported by a mortal swordsman that each Exalt targets with Flame Warden Stance, backed up by Blazing Interception.<br /> <br /> I figure that both Exalts use their first turn to set up Flame Warden Stance, and one of them uses his second turn to set up Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit while the other is free to use anything else.<br /> <br /> The point is to get a feel for whether RFDS is an advantage or more of a liability. Or an advantage that requires certain conditions to properly leverage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-28-2019, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T22:43:41-07:00","id":1308612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308249#post1308249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that, its probably not something any ST should pull unless their players are really into the combat rules. If this thread has shown anything it's that QC rules exist for good reason and you should very seldom be building the opposition as combat-optimised PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, most STs shouldn't do that kind of thing unless they expect the entire group to be fighting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dagurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308276#post1308276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat very interesting, and it makes me very clear the value of the charms that allow gain additional motes, especially Victorious Wreath in melee, although it has a cost of 1i per round the amount of earned motes seems worthwhile and helps to get out of the pit of the low initiative. Denying penalties is also absolutely vital,<br /> Even so an extremely long combat that ended up being decided by the expense of motes, but as it is well said is not something that can be seen realistically in a combat.<br /> In the end the Solar had bad luck, lost the Clash, lost with Peony blossom, if one of his attacks had impacted the final turns could have changed everything, the Dragon-Blooded had no charms to deny the penalties for injuries. In this context Blazing Solar Bolt could have been valuable in not requiring initiative to cause damage while ignoring Hardness, everything that puts a penalty for wounds on the enemy is valuable. But nobody have every charm in the game, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, but there were some missed opportunities and bad luck on both sides of that. I'm not sure Blazing Solar Bolt would have been the best thing there. The Fire Aspect can counter that decisive dicepool with a reflexive withering clash, and get many more dice to that roll, most likely crashing the Solar once more and BSB can't be used while you have less than 3i. A key factor is also that it costs 5m to activate, which means that if you even want to match the DB in his excellency you're dropping 3m on Excellent Strike, and another 2 on excellency dice, so now you're up to 10 motes for that attack, and if he's countering with a higher accuracy withering attack, with Crossfire Flash and full excellency. Even if you win, it matters by how much, because if you win the clash by 1, then you're rolling 3 dice of lethal, and there's a really solid chance that won't even do anything.<br /> <br /> I did forget about Vicious Wreath and Essence Gathering Temper, and the Solar did roll badly on his last attacks. If he'd hit properly with those he would have had the opportunity to do some serious damage....buuuut I also forgot about Blinding Spark Distraction and Portentous Comet Deflection, and the DBs were using intentionally sub-optimal stats, weapons and armor for their builds.<br /> <br /> The Solar did also get pretty lucky sometimes too, like with that control roll to clinch 11 dice against 17 with disappearing 6s. If they had both rolled average, or maybe a little off, like 5 to 10, it would have been absolutely devastating. The Solar couldn't hit Water through Fire's Defend Other, so he could only peel off rounds of control one at a time for directing attacks at him. Then while he's doing that Water is savaging him every turn and auto hitting his Defense of 0, and then finishing it off with a decisive killshot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308483#post1308483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be interesting to see some more fights against non exalted foes. Hopefully they would be less taxing to run, more representative of the typical play session and a helpful guide to aspiring STs on how to fine tune their own encounters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I shall absolutely start doing that. Also I'm going to record how many motes and willpower the characters have left at the end. That's a really good way to know if this is a kind of &quot;Lets do this fight at the gate of the palace as we're battling our way in.&quot; kind of fight, or a &quot;Oh god we just barely defeated that Rakshasi Sultan by the barest of margins!&quot; kind of fight. Or even a &quot;Don't run this fight, it's pointless and the PCs are actually going to regenerate motes doing it. Unless that's your goal here.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308535#post1308535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be interested in a test-duel between two Fire Aspected Melee-specialists. A mirror-match with just one difference.<br /> <br /> Both have Harnessed Firestorm Assault, but one of them uses the Fire Resistance Signature Charm, Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit.<br /> <br /> I just finished writing an entire thread breaking down how to build around that Charm to avoid shooting yourself in the foot with it, but that\u2019s book knowledge and not actual testing.<br /> <br /> If a mirror-match duel is too simple, I would ask that each Exalt is supported by a mortal swordsman that each Exalt targets with Flame Warden Stance, backed up by Blazing Interception.<br /> <br /> I figure that both Exalts use their first turn to set up Flame Warden Stance, and one of them uses his second turn to set up Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit while the other is free to use anything else.<br /> <br /> The point is to get a feel for whether RFDS is an advantage or more of a liability. Or an advantage that requires certain conditions to properly leverage.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Shakes head* not a good way to judge if the charm is effective.<br /> <br /> Running a mirror match against a high accuracy DB would give you the impression that, for instance, Hopping Firecracker Evasion is a nearly useless charm, because you so rarely get missed by any withering attack, and never by 2. The same sort of thinking kind of applies to RFDS. You use up an action getting RFDS up, and see no huge benefit until the motes run out, and since you gave the other guy a free turn you stand a good chance of just losing before that's an issue.<br /> <br /> I liked your breakdown of it though! I think a big concern is what abilities are they using, and especially how much Dodge and Essence they have. Fire Dodge is extremely aggressive and offensive. If you're fighting a Blood Ape, or a Dog of the Unbroken Earth or something, and you put up RFDS, then get attacked, and counter with Hopping Firecracker, Ember Amid-Smoke Misdirection, Coiling Dragon Danse, and Unassailable Body of Fire, enhanced by Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion, you're hitting back with 5 dice of withering, 8 dice of decisive, double 10s, and totally going to set it on fire, dealing 5 lethal to them every turn after that, which pretty much forces them to waste a misc action putting themselves out. You even get RFDS's 5 die attack bonus on that counter-attack, and get more than what you lost in soak back from Coiling Dragon for Duration: Aura.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also in case it wasn't obvious, a character with very high defense stats will have to rely on their soak a lot less as well, and Fire Dodge gives the opportunity to turn high defenses into secondary attacks, making them even more appealing. Otherwise, in general, with high soak and against non-exalted enemies it's better just to risk getting slapped by withering attacks and tanking them than spending 6m trying to avoid them. Also Fire Melee making it so easy to reflexive clash, turning your RFDS attack dice into what are essentially defensive dice as well.<br /> <br /> After I do a Lunar fighting a mix of close and long ranged demons I can probably do two quick ones where I run the same combat twice with and without the charm to show you the difference it makes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-29-2019, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T07:19:35-07:00","id":1308679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308612#post1308612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Shakes head* not a good way to judge if the charm is effective.<br /> <br /> Running a mirror match against a high accuracy DB would give you the impression that, for instance, Hopping Firecracker Evasion is a nearly useless charm, because you so rarely get missed by any withering attack, and never by 2. The same sort of thinking kind of applies to RFDS. You use up an action getting RFDS up, and see no huge benefit until the motes run out, and since you gave the other guy a free turn you stand a good chance of just losing before that's an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you suppose that Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit might not be worth using against other Exalted, at least in most duels? Better to use competing Fire Signatures like Inescapable Blazing Advance and Harnessed Firestorm Assault?<br /> <br /> As for motes running out, RFDS's committed motes reward your investment more when its adds dice to more than one roll per round. It makes it cheaper to flurry a rush or attack with any other action, and especially a rush and attack together, and that's before figuring in counter-attack dice pools. Something I didn't fully appreciate until now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I liked your breakdown of it though! </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think a big concern is what abilities are they using </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit seems worse than useless if it doesn't complement your build, or you didn't build to complement it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and especially how much Dodge and Essence they have. Fire Dodge is extremely aggressive and offensive. If you're fighting a Blood Ape, or a Dog of the Unbroken Earth or something, and you put up RFDS, then get attacked, and counter with Hopping Firecracker, Ember Amid-Smoke Misdirection, Coiling Dragon Danse, and Unassailable Body of Fire, enhanced by Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion, you're hitting back with 5 dice of withering, 8 dice of decisive, double 10s, and totally going to set it on fire, dealing 5 lethal to them every turn after that, which pretty much forces them to waste a misc action putting themselves out. You even get RFDS's 5 die attack bonus on that counter-attack, and get more than what you lost in soak back from Coiling Dragon for Duration: Aura. </div> </div> </div>Obviously, I need to revisit my post on how RFDS interacts with Dodge Charms! I failed to look into that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: Also in case it wasn't obvious, a character with very high defense stats will have to rely on their soak a lot less as well, and Fire Dodge gives the opportunity to turn high defenses into secondary attacks, making them even more appealing. Otherwise, in general, with high soak and against non-exalted enemies it's better just to risk getting slapped by withering attacks and tanking them than spending 6m trying to avoid them. Also Fire Melee making it so easy to reflexive clash, turning your RFDS attack dice into what are essentially defensive dice as well. </div> </div> </div>I confess, when I first read Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, I got stuck in some old Second Edition assumptions and failed to realize it until after I was done writing up that thread.<br /> <br /> So, that's another thing I want to go back and readdress.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After I do a Lunar fighting a mix of close and long ranged demons I can probably do two quick ones where I run the same combat twice with and without the charm to show you the difference it makes. </div> </div> </div>That would be great!<br /> <br /> I assume you would be testing a Melee build rather than a Fire Dragon one? Unless you feel it is important to display how Fire Dragon Style (in particular Flash-Fire Technique) performs even with the best of native Fire-aspected Charms to supplement it. I believe you've called Fire Dragon the worst of the lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T17:25:27-07:00","id":1308836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308033#post1308033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well fuck you too</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Yeah, no. This isn't how we talk to people. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T02:53:48-07:00","id":1308903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308235#post1308235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't even remotely realistic for a game anyway. When would this ever happen? Want to see if your Lunar is really good at fighting? Fight 3 Bloodapes at once. If you think that's meaningless because obviously any remotely competent Essence 2 celestial exalt should be able to rip through 3 bloodapes without even thinking, rather than a demonstration of the gut-wrenchingly terrifying power of the Exalted, as far as I'm concerned, that's <i>your </i>problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In this spirit, if somebody here gives me a build they'd like to see in action, and a rough description of what kind of opposition they'd like me to put it up against (&quot;a mortal sorcerer and a couple summoned minions&quot;; &quot;a wood aspect archer in an arena of plant-based difficult terrain&quot;; &quot;a god-blooded mercenary and her battle group of seasoned soldiers&quot;, etc.), I might run a couple fights myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T12:26:03-07:00","id":1309254,"title":"","content":"Okay! Tried out a Lunar who shifts in between close and long ranged combat against different kinds of foes and it actually started out horrible because the Lunar got really bad luck. Like such bad luck I had to run the fight again. This was the second attempt. It's against 2 blood apes and a variation on one of my own custom demons called a Smiling Archer, in this case.<br /> <br /> Smiling Archer<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Motes: 50<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> 5m 1i, reflexively apply Arrow Frog Venom to weapon<br /> 10m, after crashing a target reflexively aim<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> Sawbow 12 at Short Range (Damage 14)<br /> Evasion 4<br /> Soak 5/0<br /> <br /> Join Battle 8 dice<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lunar<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Lunar Essence 2<br /> <br /> Per: 17 iph: 26 (42)<br /> <br /> Light moonsilver armor<br /> <br /> Percepetion 5 but only awareness 3<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> Wounded Beast Flight, Bounding Bharal Technique, Relentless Monster Persuit, Foe-Driving Attack, Many Armed Warrior Panolopy, Coiled Serpent Strikes, Cunning Beast Warrior Reflexes, Hunters Eye Precision, Unerring Fang Technique, Sensing the Deadly Flow, Divine Predator Strike, Durant Quicksilver Adaptation<br /> <br /> <br /> STATS<br /> Powerbow 14 (Damage 17/4)<br /> Daiklave 12 (Damage 17/4)<br /> Parry 6<br /> Evasion 6<br /> Soak 10/3<br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Roll Join Battle<br /> <br /> Lunar spends 10m for 18 dice, rolling 7 for 10 initiative<br /> Smiling Archer 8 dice, rolling for 4 , 7 initiative<br /> Ape1 rolls 7 dice, rolling 5 for 8 initiative<br /> APe2 rolls 7 dice, rolling 5 for 8 initiative<br /> <br /> LU Per: 8 iph: 0 (42)<br /> SA 50<br /> B1 70<br /> B2 70<br /> <br /> Li: 17<br /> 2i:-3<br /> <br /> <br /> ============<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Lunar 2m Cunning Beast-Warrior Reflexes flurries a disengage with an attack action. Spending 1m Bounding Bharal Technique and 2m excellency<br /> <br /> Lunar rolls 13 dice against each blood ape's 10, getting 6 against 3 and 3<br /> <br /> Lunar escapes towards the Smiling Archer and attacks it with 2m Divine Predator Strike, 5m excellency, 1m Unerring Fang Technique rolling 16 dice for 8 successes, beating by 4, then rolling 18 damage for 7, crashing the archer.<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 1 moves towards the Lunar, the Lunar reflexively moves back as per disengage.<br /> <br /> Blood Ape 1 rushes Lunar rolling 10 dice against the Lunar's 11, rolling 6 against 6, successfully rushing<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 2 moves towards the Lunar<br /> <br /> Blood Ape 2 rushes Lunar rolling 10 dice against the Lunar's 11, rolling 4 against 5, failing to rush<br /> --------<br /> Smiling Archer takes a withering shot at the Lunar, Lunar will defend with 1m Agile Beast, 4m excellency, 3m Coiled Serpent Strikes<br /> <br /> Archer rolls 12 against defense of 9, failing with 5<br /> <br /> Lunar counter attacks, reflexivly readying Powerbow and firing a decisive attack, spending 5m on an excellency, 1m on Unerring Fang Technique, 2m Ferocious Biting Tooth<br /> <br /> Rolling 14 dice against evasion of 4, getting 7, rolling 25 damage, dealing 9 and killing the archer.<br /> ============<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Blood Ape 2 moves into close with Lunar, and uses 10m 1wp Principle of Motion to make 2 withering attacks against the Lunar Lunar will defend with 3m 1i Golden Tiger Stance, 4m 1wp Fleet Gazelle Exercise, and 1m Agile Beast Defense against each attack<br /> <br /> Blood Ape rolls 11 dice agasint Defense of 9, getting 3 and missing<br /> <br /> Blood Ape rolls 11 dice agasint Defense of 9, getting 5 and missing<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 1 moves into close with Lunar and uses 10m 1wp principle of motion to make 2 attacks. Lunar will defend with Agile Beast Defense each time<br /> <br /> Blood Ape rolls 11 dice agasint Defense of 9, getting 2 and missing<br /> <br /> Blood Ape rolls 11 dice agasint Defense of 9, getting 8 and missing<br /> --------<br /> Lunar flurries 2m Cunning Beast Warrior disengage with an attack<br /> <br /> Disengaging with 1m Bounding Bharal Technique 2m excellency, rolling 11 dice against each Ape's 10<br /> <br /> Getting 4 against 6 and 6, failing<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks at close range with a withering shot from the powerbow, rolling 6 dice against a parry of 4, failing with 1<br /> ============<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Blood Ape 1 uses 10m 1wp Principle of Motion to make 2 withering attacks against the Lunar, Lunar will defend with 3m 2i Golden Tiger and 1m Agile Beast against each attack.<br /> <br /> Blood Ape rolls 11 dice agasint Defense of 9, getting 7 and missing<br /> <br /> Blood Ape rolls 11 dice agasint Defense of 9, getting 6 and missing<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 1 uses 10m 1wp Principle of Motion to make 2 withering attacks against the Lunar, Lunar will defend with 1m Agile Beast against each attack.<br /> <br /> Blood Ape rolls 11 dice agasint Defense of 9, getting 7 and missing<br /> <br /> Blood Ape rolls 11 dice agasint Defense of 9, getting 5 and missing<br /> --------<br /> Lunar uses 2m Cunning Beast Warrior to flurry a disengage with an attack<br /> <br /> Disengaging with 1m Bharal Technique, 2m excellency, rolling 11 dice against the ape's 10, getting 9 against 1 and 6, successfully disengaging<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks Blood Ape 2 with a withering powerbow shot, rolling 12 dice against a parry of 4, getting 4, hitting rolling 10 damage for 4<br /> ============<br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks Blood Ape 2 with a withering attack and moves back a range band, rolling 14 dice aginast Parry of 4, getting 8, rolling 14 damage for 8, crashing the Ape<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 1 moves toward Lunar and rushes, rolling 10 dice against 11, getting 3 against 4 and failing<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 2 moves toward Lunar and rushes, rolling 10 dice against 11, getting 4 against 7 and failing<br /> ============<br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks Blood Ape 2 with a decisive attack and moves back a range band, rolling 9 dice against a parry of 4, rolling 3 and failing<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 1 moves toward Lunar and rushes, rolling 10 dice against 11, getting 8 against 7, making it<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 2 moves toward Lunar and rushes, rolling 10 dice against 11, getting 4 against 5 and failing<br /> ============<br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> Lunar attacks Blood Ape 1 with a decisive attack and moves back a range band, using 5m full excellency and 1m unerring fang tech, 2m Ferocious Biting Tooth<br /> <br /> Rolling 14 dice against 4 Parry, getting 7 and making it, rolling 27 damage for 8, putting Blood Ape 1 in his -4 Health Level<br /> <br /> Lunar moves back a range band and Blood Ape 1 reflexively follows<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 1 moves into close with the Lunar and uses 10m 1wp Principle of Motion to make 2 withering attacks. The Lunar uses 3m 2i Golden Tiger and 1m agile beast defense on each<br /> <br /> Blood ape rolls 11 dice against defense of 9, getting 5 and missing<br /> <br /> Blood ape rolls 11 dice against defense of 9, getting 6 and missing<br /> --------<br /> Blood ape 2 recovers from crash and moves to within short range of Lunar and rushes, rolling 10 dice against 11 and getting 4 against 6, failing.<br /> ============<br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> Blood Ape 1 uses 10m 1wp Principle of Motion to make 2 attacks against the Lunar, Lunar uses 1m Agile Beast against each to defend.<br /> <br /> Blood ape rolls 11 dice against defense of 9, getting 6 and missing<br /> <br /> Blood ape rolls 11 dice against defense of 9, getting 5 and missing<br /> --------<br /> Lunar makes a decisive attack at close range with the powerbow, rolling 9 dice against parry 2, making it with 3, rolling 6 damage dice for 2 damage, killing Blood Ape 1.<br /> <br /> Lunar moves away from blood Ape 2<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 2 moves towards Lunar and rushes, Lunar spends 2m to excellency rolling 10 dice against her 13, getting 7 against 11 and failing<br /> ============<br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> Lunar withering attacks Blood Ape 2, rolling 14 dice against Parry of 4, making it with 7, rolling 13 damage for 6, crashing the ape.<br /> --------<br /> Blood Ape 2 moves towards the Lunar and rushes, rolling 10 dice against 11 and making it with 6 against 6<br /> ============<br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> Lunar moves away from Blood Ape 2, Ape reflexively moves to follow, Lunar strikes at Ape 2 with a decisive attack, rolling 5m full excellency, 1m Unerring Fang Technique, 2m Ferocious Biting Tooth, 2m Divine Predator Strike. Rolling 14 dice for 11 against a parry of 4, and rolling 21 decisive damage for 10, killing the Ape.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Looks like it went pretty well! The combination of Fleet Gazelle, Golden Tiger and Agile Beast Defense is unbelievable against opponents who can't muster up 20 dice attack pools. It's just free initiative along with not getting hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T18:54:30-07:00","id":1309349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308679#post1308679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you suppose that Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit might not be worth using against other Exalted, at least in most duels? Better to use competing Fire Signatures like Inescapable Blazing Advance and Harnessed Firestorm Assault?<br /> <br /> As for motes running out, RFDS's committed motes reward your investment more when its adds dice to more than one roll per round. It makes it cheaper to flurry a rush or attack with any other action, and especially a rush and attack together, and that's before figuring in counter-attack dice pools. Something I didn't fully appreciate until now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just counter attack dicepools. Look how it interacts with reflexive clash attacks, which Fire Melee has in spades, between Fire Incites Water to a Riot of Clouds and Portentous Comet Deflection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308679#post1308679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit seems worse than useless if it doesn't complement your build, or you didn't build to complement it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find a lot of the Dragonblooded charmset to be this way. It's most powerful effects require a lot of finesse to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308679#post1308679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you would be testing a Melee build rather than a Fire Dragon one? Unless you feel it is important to display how Fire Dragon Style (in particular Flash-Fire Technique) performs even with the best of native Fire-aspected Charms to supplement it. I believe you've called Fire Dragon the worst of the lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire Dragon is probably the worst? But I'll use it anyway because I don't actually think it's that bad, and if it works with Fire Dragon it'll definitely work with Melee.<br /> <br /> I did about half the fight today, but I have to be honest, running so many numbers all on my own without the benefit of a cool Exalted story and stunts and stuff to back it up is draining like crazy. Also dull and taking up hours of my day. I don't know how many more of these I can do for now.<br /> <br /> From what I saw in the fight though, it's good, at least against Dogs of the Unbroken Earth. What you need to be careful of with Fire Dragon though against multiple opponents is to try and stay above them in initiative, and really make sure they don't land those decisive attacks. Quick Characters use the same pool for witherings as they do decisive, so that can be hard to do, but forcing them to drop 4 initiative whenever they miss was a damn hard price to pay.<br /> <br /> As the fight went on the Fire eventually became pretty mote neutral and just let the Fiery Blade bonfires and her anima do all the work while the dogs burned up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T12:10:28-07:00","id":1309486,"title":"","content":"Would it help you if you also added a story layer on top of the fight? I did this when I was first getting into Ex3 and trying to get a feel for combat. It kinda reminds me of the fantastic Combat 301 tutorial, only actually getting to the charms. Granted, it is a whole other additional effort, but it could break up the monotony.<br /> <br /> I did mine in google sheets to keep things orderly, but I'll see if it can be pasted easily enough into a forum friendly format, not that they are the craziest fights.<br /> <br /> First one was a Brawl Supernal ruffian survivalist against a Tyrant lizard after his lunch. I made a mistake in letting Falling Hammer Strike apply Onslaught to the tyrant lizard. Probably would have been a very different fight otherwise. <br /> <br /> Another was a mirror match of sorts, mortals, one in armor, one unarmored, medium weapons. The unarmored one was a Elite Guard turned revolutionary, and the armored one was his previous friend come to hunt him down. I accidentally found out just how powerful Clashes are. Armored boi won the clash, then turned around and one shot him with a decisive.<br /> <br /> Finally I had a Blood Ape against a Fair Folk Cataphract from Core. This only had a thin vaneer of story TBH, The blood ape didn't stand a chance IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T18:49:00-07:00","id":1309556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1309486#post1309486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it help you if you also added a story layer on top of the fight? I did this when I was first getting into Ex3 and trying to get a feel for combat. It kinda reminds me of the fantastic Combat 301 tutorial, only actually getting to the charms. Granted, it is a whole other additional effort, but it could break up the monotony.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered that, but I'm not sure how well it's going to work out, it will be a lot more writing to involve a story into it. Also I think part of the problem is when PCs are running all the exalts I don't have to run strategy, and they also work well as a group to take out enemies fast. So instead of what I've been doing, which has mostly been one hero character against an array of enemies, it's a big trade back and forth that quickly knocks out enemy combatants and makes the fight go smoother. Also often in real game combats the enemy surrenders after half of them get insta-gibbed.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see what you came up with for yours though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T02:47:11-07:00","id":1309603,"title":"","content":"I think one of the reasons the mass combat fight went the way it did was because of defend other.<br /> <br /> Logically it does not make much sense to me how the defend other would be able to help a battle group fighting another battle group. I could not find a place where the rules state directly that, but <br /> <br /> &quot;Defend Other: The character protects an ally within close range (see p. 197)&quot;<br /> <br /> So if the character is not in close range with all the characters in the battle group being attacked I would say he cannot defend other.<br /> <br /> That makes sense, if it is against another individual character <br /> that defending character is standing next to, it would work, but otherwise it does not.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other part is the ambush. I think winning that strategy roll would imply starting very close to the enemy. It is not really an ambush if they see you coming. Bit maybe that would make it too powerful. An argument in favour of that they should start in close range Is that otherwise the first round of Manish does not really make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":80,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","user":"TrueMonk","date":". 05-03-2019, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T04:43:59-07:00","id":1309617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1309603#post1309603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other part is the ambush. I think winning that strategy roll would imply starting very close to the enemy. It is not really an ambush if they see you coming. Bit maybe that would make it too powerful. An argument in favour of that they should start in close range Is that otherwise the first round of Manish does not really make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this fight the DB enacted a successful Fortifications stratagem which specifically says that it forces the enemy to start at long range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T07:23:12-07:00","id":1309639,"title":"","content":"Yeah Battlegroup on Battlegroup might not make much sense. I was thinking about one person on Battlegroup, and I think that works, interposing yourself in front of the enemy whenever they try and advance towards your troops. Battlegroup on singular ward makes sense, dancing around them and keeping the enemy at bay by knocking their spears down. BG on BG though I\u2019m having trouble picturing. I think RAW it works and is allow it at my table, but if it started causing problems I wouldn\u2019t have any qualms about throwing it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T10:31:33-07:00","id":1309681,"title":"","content":"I realise that I might just be repeating what I said above, but I think<br /> <br /> &quot;Defend Other: The character protects an ally within close range (see p. 197)&quot; p. 196<br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> &quot;When a character is at close range, he is in an opponent\u2019s face, close enough to easily attack with a hand-to-hand weapon such as a sword, spear, or his fists. This doesn\u2019t mean that the characters are necessarily within arm\u2019s reach of each other at all times, but rather that they are able to close such a distance in moments.&quot; P. 196<br /> <br /> Excludes that the protection can go out to cover a larger battle group.<br /> <br /> AHH...<br /> <br /> There is a more obvious reason. &quot;&quot;Defend Other: The character protects AN ally within close range (see p. 197)&quot; p. 196<br /> <br /> Not a group of allies. I would say that you can use your defend other on an entire battlegroup just as much as you can use your medicine charms on them.<br /> <br /> Btw. I am really grateful for the battles here. I have only read the book and not played yet and seeing some fights written down helped my understanding a lot! :-)<br /> <br /> (Even if many of the fights were ones you would rarely see in game. Although I guess they are a lot more likely if the players are the DBs)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":80,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","user":"TrueMonk","date":". 05-03-2019, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T23:50:21-07:00","id":1309871,"title":"","content":"Defend Other with Battle Groups is weird.<br /> <br /> Because like, you can convincingly argue that the rules disallow it. But that doesn't make it sensible that a War-oriented character would completely ignore it. Like it'd be kind of weird for a character's Defend Other to do Nothing in mass combat when their regular attacks function just fine.<br /> And thematically it's an excellent field of competence for a dedicated frontline commander to have, which makes me not want it to be like, useless in mass combat.<br /> <br /> Hrmmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T01:28:25-07:00","id":1309875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1309871#post1309871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defend Other with Battle Groups is weird.<br /> <br /> Because like, you can convincingly argue that the rules disallow it. But that doesn't make it sensible that a War-oriented character would completely ignore it. Like it'd be kind of weird for a character's Defend Other to do Nothing in mass combat when their regular attacks function just fine.<br /> And thematically it's an excellent field of competence for a dedicated frontline commander to have, which makes me not want it to be like, useless in mass combat.<br /> <br /> Hrmmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it works definitely defending a single character against a BG, kind of iffy on it being able to defend a BG against a single character, but maybe. It\u2019s just BG on BG. Like when they\u2019re two size 3-5 battlegroups with hundreds of combatants clashing in a huge battle line what exactly is your character doing with a mundane* defend other action to stop those guys from making attacks? Is he like, sprinting like the flash at top speed along the line, knocking down enemy spears? In truest massive battles those lines might extend over 4-5 range bands. It just starts to fall apart for me as an ST.<br /> <br /> <br /> *i mean of course the action is mundane, you might excellency it or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T02:22:16-07:00","id":1309878,"title":"","content":"Well to be fair actual loss of life in Battle Groups is already heavily abstracted. It wouldn't be out of the question to stunt or describe the specific action a commander takes as the protecting one or a few soliders near to them.<br /> At lower sizes this isn't really a disconnect at all.<br /> At higher sizes you could theoretically fluff it as an action that is so inspiring that it girds the troops against losing Magnitude.<br /> But yeah, it's One of Those Things I guess. Not really important until it happens then actually a pretty big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T07:48:03-07:00","id":1309904,"title":"","content":"Could I ask y'all to finally settle <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what%E2%80%99s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar\">the age-old debate?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T08:58:15-07:00","id":1309910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1309904#post1309904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could I ask y'all to finally settle <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what%E2%80%99s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar\">the age-old debate?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah interesting! What essence do you think you\u2019d want to see it at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T09:10:08-07:00","id":1309911,"title":"","content":"Ooh, very interesting.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... there's a huge difference between Essence 1 and Essence 4, because the charm to ignore the 4m mote-cost of being giant is Essence 4.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think Essence 1 would be fine, because at Essence 4 they've got a lot of other charms, and it might be too much about their charms more generally rather than the Warstrider vs giant animal.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, higher essence lets you look at some evocations.<br /> <br /> Alucard, it's your idea, what do you think?<br /> <br /> You also may want to bear in mind, DrLoveMonkey, that a warstrider pilot probably needs to buy some craft charms, and maybe sorcery, just to maintain their own warstrider.<br /> I played a warstrider pilot, and having charms to be able to fix it if it got wrecked was a pretty significant investment. That cut into my combat abilities a lot. Though perhaps this Solar has a Twilight friend who does it for them.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, if you do want a high-Essence Night Caste in a warstrider, I've got one so you don't have to build your own. He was Essence 5 (he's dead now, but I've still got the sheet). Though it's Godspeed Vanguard, the stealth warstrider, which is a bit different, and he's a bit paladin-y (so stronger vs demons than Lunars). He's not very good at defence, relying on stealth and being in a warstrider.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Name: Golden Hero<br /> <br /> Caste: Night</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Icon: A swarm of golden butterflies blazing with white fire</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Limit condition: </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Solar\u2019s allies suffer a setback or defeat because of a mistake he made. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Anima powers: </span> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">For 2 motes, treat all peripheral essence expenditure as personal for a turn.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">For 3 motes, he can ignore 5 points of stealth penalties. This always counts as personal.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">When his anima is at bonfire/iconic, his identity cannot be discerned.</span></li> </ol><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Strength: 4 Charisma: 5 Perception: 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Dexterity: 5 Manipulation: 5 Intelligence: 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Stamina: 3 Appearance: 3 Wits: 3</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Archery: </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Athletics: 5 (+1 Warstriders)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Awareness: 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Bureaucracy: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Brawl: </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Craft (Weaponsmith): 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Craft (Artefacts): 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Craft (Construction): 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Craft (Carpentry): 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Craft (Cooking): 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Craft (Tailoring): 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Dodge: 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Integrity: 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Investigation: </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Larceny: 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Linguistics: 1 </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Lore: 3 (+1 Warstriders)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Medicine: 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Melee: 5 (+1 Two-Weapon Fighting)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Occult: 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Performance: 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Presence: 4 </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Resistance: 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Ride: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Sail: </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Socialise (S): 5 (+1 Staying in-character)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Stealth: 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Survival: 2 </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Thrown: </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">War: 1</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Essence 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Personal Essence: 25/25 </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Peripheral Essence: 46/61 (15 committed)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Willpower: 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Parry: 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Soak: 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Guile: 5 (6 when lying in character)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Resolve: 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><u><b>Join Battle in warstrider:</b></u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Blinding Battle Feint, Stealth excellency, Fleeting Shadow Scout, Transluminal Stride, Aegis of Light and Shadow </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">15 motes and 8 mute motes, 2wp</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Roll 20 dice, +7 successes, (3 for JB, 4 non-charm). If you beat all enemies, get a wp back and hide in thin air, and you can act at any point on your turn (basically, you delay for free).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">For the rest of the scene, has no penalties for stealth in combat or in a warstrider, and can hide in thin air.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><u><b>Charms:</b></u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Athletics:</b>Lightning Speed, Graceful Crane Stance, Increasing Strength Exercise, Monkey Leap Technique, Feather Foot Style, Leaping Tiger Attack, Racing Hare Method</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Craft:</b> Arete-Shifting Prana, Supreme Celestial Focus, Sublime Transference, Brass Scales Falling, Red Anvils Ringing, Chains Fall Away, Craftsman Needs No Tools, Peerless Paragon of Craft, Supreme Perfection of Craft, Thousand-Forge Hands, Flawless Handiwork Method, Experiential Conjuring of True Void</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Larceny:</b> Seasoned Criminal Method, Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Melee: </b>Call the Blade, Excellent Strike, Sandstorm-Wind Attack, Edge of Morning Sunlight, Corona of Radiance, Sharp Light of Judgement Stance, Blazing Solar Bolt</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Medicine:</b> Ailment-Rectifying Method, Plague-Banishing Incitement, Contagion-Curing Touch</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Occult:</b> Spirit-Detecting Glance, Spirit-Cutting Attack, Ghost-Eating Technique</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Presence:</b> Harmonious Presence Method, Majestic Radiant Presence</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Resistance:</b> Whirlwind Armour-Donning Prana</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Socialise:</b> Motive-Discerning Eye, Humble Servant Approach, Wise-Eyed Courtier Method</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Stealth:</b> Blinding Battle Feint, Easily Overlooked Presence Method, Perfect Shadow Stillness, Invisible Statue Spirit </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Evocations:</b> Fleeting Shadow Scout, Transluminal Stride, Horizon-Attaining Pace, Aegis of Light and Shadow</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u><b>Godspeed Vanguard</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Withering attack: 16 dice to hit Withering Damage: +17 Ov4 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Personal Essence: 25/25 </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Peripheral Essence: 41/61 (20 committed)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Willpower: 5</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Parry: 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Evasion: 4 Speed Bonus: +4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Soak: 10</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Hardness: 8</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Health Levels: </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u22120x5/\u22121x5/\u22122x5/\u22124x10 </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-04-2019, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T15:11:28-07:00","id":1309938,"title":"","content":"Both of them being Essence 1 is A-OK by me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T15:20:07-07:00","id":1309941,"title":"","content":"Well, since nobody took me up on my offer, I decided to be proactive.<br /> <br /> Introducing: Immaculate Styles vs 2 blood apes!<br /> <br /> The goal of this is to see how an Immaculate might fare against two blood apes straight out of character creation.<br /> <br /> Basic assumptions:<br /> - Attributes are restricted to values that are achievable with a chargen 8/6/4 spread without spending BPs on primary and secondary attributes.<br /> - Characters have a 5 in their most important ability, 4s in everything else I can think of at the start of the combat, and no specializations. This may not be an accurate representation of how typical player characters are actually created, but my experience is that players who want their character to actually be able to do interesting things are often forced to compromise, and in these cases, interesting things usually come out ahead, because combat competence has diminishing marginal utility.<br /> - In cases where I realize that I actually need an extra ability score mid-combat, it has a default value of 3.<br /> - Characters start with 10 combat-applicable Charms, including excellencies. This is not a lot, but it's still more than what I usually see straight out of chargen. (Of course, the smart thing to do when playing an Immaculate is to only buy the good Charms and pick up the speedbumpy pre-form crap pretty much every style is riddled with during play, but let's ignore that.)<br /> - No Artifacts. This is somewhat unreasonable, but no more unreasonable than artifact arms and armor on every character, and I have actually seen players actively forgo combat artifacts in favor of cool utility stuff anyway.<br /> - combatants start at short range, there's infinite room to maneuver but no terrain features that help or hinder either party<br /> <br /> Air Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 3 Dex 5 Sta 3 | Perception 3, Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Air Dragon 5, Awareness 4, Dodge 4, Stealth 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Air Dragon Style: Air Dragon's Sight, Cloud-Treading Method, Wind Dragon's Speed, Breath-Seizing Technique, Air Dragon Form, Shroud of Unseen Winds<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The combat:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Join Battle!<br /> Air Dragon dumps a full excellency into JB, knowing that winning it is of supreme importance if she doesn't want to get her face pounded in by massive ape fists launching four attacks before she gets to act.<br /> She garners 3 successes on 14 dice. Oops.<br /> Ape #1 and #2 get 6 and 4 successes, respectively.<br /> <br /> TURN 1<br /> Ape #1 at initiative 9, Ape #2 at initiative 7, Air Dragon at initiative 6.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 moves to close range and launches a flurry of 2 attacks with Principle of Motion.<br /> Air Dragon uses a full excellency (peripheral); first attack rolls 13 dice vs Evasion 8 and misses.<br /> Second attack sees Air Dragon add Air Dragon's Sight and a full excellency from personal to keep her Evasion at 8 without flaring. Sadly, the ape rolls exactly 8 successes.<br /> Damage 15-6=9 dice, for a pathetic 2 successes.<br /> Ape #1 at initiative 12, Air Dragon at 3.<br /> Ape #2 moves in and does the same as his companion.<br /> Air Dragon fires off ADS+full excellency again, but the ape miraculously manages to roll 9 successes. 10 dice of damage garner 5 successes.<br /> Air Dragon is crashed at -3 initiative, Ape #2 goes up to initiative 18 and still has an attack to make.<br /> He fires off a decisive at 13 dice plus a WP for an auto-success versus Air Dragon's base 5+1 Evasion minus her onslaught of 3, which she can't even negate because being crashed shut down ADS. She still tosses a full excellency at it, because it's not like her motes will do her any good once she's dead, bringing her up to 5.<br /> The ape rolls 10 successes.<br /> 18 dice of damage can't reliably kill through an ox-body without double 10s, but a -2 wound penalty is still a fight-ender. What an anticlimax, I sigh as I pick up roughly ten million dice.<br /> Then I proceed to roll 4 successes.<br /> Air Dragon is wounded but not out on her last -1 health level, and her opponent just reset to base, potentially setting her up for initiative shift! Reluctant to let her anima banner rise in case she needs to hide later in the scene, she tosses 4 peripheral motes at the attack, bringing her up to 19 dice. Ape spends a WP, but he's still at a less-than-amazing Parry 6.<br /> 19 dice somehow manages to roll only 7 successes, for a total of 11 raw damage, which is brought down to 4 post-soak by the ape's thick hide. This might still be enough for a crash with a <i>tiny</i> bit of luck...<br /> ...Alas, the dice gods fail her. She rolls 1 success and faces the very real possibility of another brutal four-attack beatdown, so she reflexively uses her anima power to summon a swift breeze to dry off the rapidly gathering beads of sweat on her brow, allowing her to enter Air Aura at the end of her turn.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, everybody regains 5m<br /> <br /> TURN 2<br /> Ape #1 at initiative 12, Ape #2 at initiative 3, Air Dragon at initiative -1.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 launches another Principle of Motion flurry.<br /> First withering rolls 13 dice vs a full excellency'd Evasion of now 7 due to her wound penalty... and fails to connect with 5 successes.<br /> For his second action, he'd prefer to go for a defend other on the other ape, but Principle of Motion is very unclearly worded and doesn't say whether otherwise non-flurriable actions can be placed into the flurry created by it, so he goes with a grapple because I'm too lazy to hunt for dev quotes.<br /> 10 dice plus a WP versus a full excellency'd Evasion of 6 doesn't bode well for the Air Dragon, so she tosses in a WP as well, because a successful grapple at this point pretty much spells critical existence failure for her.<br /> He rolls 2 successes for a grand total of 3. Sigh of relief.<br /> Ape #2 uses his last WP for another Principle of Motion flurry. (The assumption is that they started the scene materialized, but haven't had the time to regain the WP from using the Charm.)<br /> As usual, a 13d10 attack vs a full excellency, Evasion 5. Attack garners 7 successes, post-soak damage pool of 11 rolls 8. Air Dragon watches helplessly as the prospect of initiative shift sails further and further away from her eyes, as if carried by a playful breeze.<br /> Knowing how close he got to handing her the means of his destruction last turn, ape #2 decides to play it safe and smack her with another withering attack. Air Dragon is tempted to put no effort into her defense because 13 dice is going to hit an Evasion of 4 <i>anyway</i>, but then decides to toss those 4 motes at it because she'd feel very stupid if he ended up hitting her with 3 successes in the end.<br /> Alas, he rolls 5S and hits, post-soak damage 11 turns into a profoundly underwhelming two successes, but it's not like she isn't screwed anyways.<br /> Air Dragon attempts to enter concealment with Shroud of Unseen Winds, rolling 7 dice after penalties with 2 auto-successes against the apes' 8d on senses.<br /> She gathers a total of 6 successes, while the apes both roll 5. She's safe for now.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, everybody regains 5m<br /> <br /> TURN 3<br /> Ape #2 at initiative 14, Ape#1 at initiative 9, Air Dragon at initiative -11 and on her second turn in crash<br /> <br /> Since the core has no rules for using an action to try finding someone, the two apes are neutered. In the absence of a better option, they both pay 2i to delay their action.<br /> To make matters even more confusing, the rules are incredibly unclear about resolving disengage attempts while concealed.<br /> After flipping through the book and scratching my head for quite some time, I come to the conclusion that a concealed character still needs to disengage, and if she wants to maintain concealment, she also needs to succeed on a Dex+Stealth roll to change hiding places, but the two rolls do not need to be flurried, since reflexively moving away is not an action. In hindsight, I probably should have applied a penalty for blindness on the roll to oppose her disengage, but as we'll see, this hasn't changed anything.<br /> In any case, seeing that if she wanted to go to ground, she'd need to pass three Stealth checks at steadily mounting penalties, Air Dragon decides that attempting to do so while in close range of two demons who are both sitting on a considerable pile of initiative they can immediately unload into her the moment she fails even one roll is a sucker's game. (Air aspects are universally well-versed in probability theory. Having Lore as an aspect ability will do that to you.)<br /> So she disengages with 11 dice and 1 auto-success (keeping her remaining 9 motes for Cloud-Treading Method and Shroud of Unseen Winds) versus her opponents' 9d on combat movement.<br /> ...Well, she spends a willpower just to be safe. Discretion is the better part of valor, after all.<br /> She rolls a total of 7 successes versus 3 and 5. That's a willpower wasted, but at least she can run away.<br /> Now for the stealth. Apparently Shroud of Unseen Winds does not negate the penalty for crossing wide-open terrain despite <i>literally making you invisible </i>(maybe you shimmer like the Predator while you move?), so that's 9d base +2 stunt -1 wound -5 crossing wide-open terrain, of which Cloud-Treading Method negates 3, for a total of 8d and 2 AS.<br /> She rolls a total of 7 successes.<br /> To her dismay, so does ape #2 (can we take a moment to appreciate how tremendously unlikely it is to get 7 successes on 8 dice?). Moreover, since he delayed his action, he can now reflexively use this opportunity to strike at her as she tries to run away.<br /> Decisive 13d claw versus a completely mote-tapped Air Dragon's total Evasion of 5, rolls 6 successes.<br /> 12 initiative is swiftly turned into another 4 levels of damage, dropping Air Dragon to her last -4 health level.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, everybody regains 5m.<br /> <br /> TURN 4<br /> Ape #1 at initiative 7, ape #2 at 3, Air Dragon at -13 and on her third turn in crash. She'll reset to base next turn.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 is still completely unaware of what's going on. He drools a little but otherwise does nothing useful.<br /> Ape #2 moves closer to Air Dragon. She moves away reflexively. If he still had a Willpower, he could use Shattering Roar and have a good chance to finish her off even from base initiative; alas, he doesn't, so the only option he has is rushing with his 9 dice versus her 7. Accepting that she might die here, Air Dragon decides to spend no motes, because I only realized that the opportunity to use Shattering Roar existed when I started to ponder her options, so I didn't check whether he has the WP to actually use it. Thus, I decided to prioritize crashing him in order to shut it down over avoiding the rush.<br /> He rolls 3 successes; she rolls 4. The rush is somehow still avoided.<br /> Air Dragon rolls a chakram attacks with a 1m excellency, because at this point I remember that the ape has no Willpower left. Still, the prospect of an initiative shift is too tempting to not try.<br /> Alas, she rolls 3 successes on 13 dice, and her weapon is unceremoniously swatted away by a hairy paw. She uses her reflexive movement to escape to medium range.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, everybody regains 5m.<br /> <br /> TURN 5<br /> Ape #1 at initiative 7, ape #2 at 3, Air Dragon resets to 3 this turn.<br /> <br /> The chakram attack revealed Air Dragon, but at this point she's at long range from him. Still, he starts moving in case Ape #2 catches up to her and she fails to disengage.<br /> Ape #2 moves closer and rushes, failing once more with 4 successes versus 5.<br /> Air Dragon moves out to medium range once more and starts to withdraw. At this point, I realize that withdraw inexplicably uses Athletics rather than Dodge. She defaults to a score of 3 and no excellency, rolling 6 dice and gathering 2 successes.<br /> <br /> With this, the fight effectively ended - ape #2 attempted to rush but she had more than enough motes to consistently rebuff him, and eventually she managed to gather the required 10 successes to move out to long range, at which point she became impossible to catch up to.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Final result: both apes remained unharmed. Air Dragon managed to escape with her pride and last -4 health level wounded, but at least she didn't have to take crippling.<br /> <br /> Notes:<br /> - quick characters retaining accuracy bonuses on decisives is incredibly painful for deebs<br /> - in future engagements, I probably won't give stunt bonuses to the apes, it's not like they're dramatically significant characters here<br /> - Air Dragon deserves a rematch at some point in the future, those first few rounds went incredibly poorly for her","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T16:13:11-07:00","id":1309945,"title":"","content":"The funny thing is the exact same thing happened when I matched the range shifting Lunar against two blood apes and the smiling archer. The first two rounds the Apes barely missed any of their attacks, it was crazy. It was so bad I scrapped the fight halfway through because poor Lunars have suffered enough in this thread, but I now wish I\u2019d kept it and posted it. Sometimes this kind of thing happens and it\u2019s good to know that.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, don\u2019t fucking underestimate blood apes, they hurt really bad. If all they need is some luck to beat a Lunar in a 2v1 you know they\u2019re scary.<br /> <br /> Edit: also if you try a rematch you might want to immediately start off using Wind Dragon Speed to flurry an attack with a disengage. It\u2019s risky because it will provoke the apes into using their only ranged attack which is super strong, but it might keep you at short range for the rest of the fight. Although opposing rushes is an Athletics roll, so maybe not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-04-2019, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T16:49:19-07:00","id":1309948,"title":"","content":"Assume QCs already have stunt bonuses incorporated into their rolls, as a tip. I say this because their minimal pool is 3 (Which would be Attribute 1, Ability 0, stunt) and their max is 14 (Ability 5, Attribute 5, Specialty, Exceptional Equipment, stunt), barring magic or otherwise inhuman things (Fair Folk usually have very inflated pools but low mote pools for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T04:00:05-07:00","id":1310011,"title":"","content":"I skipped Earth for now, because after Air\u2019s incredibly poor showing, I was really curious how Fire \u2013 which I believe to be the weakest of the five styles \u2013 would fare.<br /> <br /> Fire Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 3 Dex 5 Sta 3 |Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Fire Dragon 5, Athletics 4, Awareness 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Fire Dragon: Flash-Fire Technique, Searing Edge Attack, Flame-Flicker Stance, Perfect Blazing Blow, Fire Dragon Form, God-Immolating Strike<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique x2<br /> <br /> All in all, a very conservative spread. Fire Dragon offers no incentives for unusual attribute spreads, and it has very few out-of-style Charms worth having on a 10 Charm budget. Blade-Deflecting Palm would be a potent complement to Flame-Flicker Stance\u2019s post-roll shenaniganery, but it yanks us right out of aura, negating the benefit we\u2019d want to use it for. Ox-Body Technique has strongly diminishing returns past the second purchase, and the rest of the Resistance Charms are not so hot either. This leaves us with the profoundly mediocre God-Immolating Strike \u2013 mid-combat healing is really not common enough among spirits for the aggravated damage to do anything useful 99% of the time, and between 3d flux damage per turn and Searing Edge Attack, there are more than enough ways for a stylist to ensure that her initiative is higher than her opponent\u2019s at any time she\u2019d want to launch a decisive, so this is just 5m for 2 dice of delayed damage, which is\u2026 a worse Falling Scythe Flash until you hit Essence 4 (and even then you could argue that FSF pulls ahead by virtue of its broader applicability). Still, decisive damage for motes and nothing else is not terrible, I'll take it.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The combat:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> To anybody with even the most rudimentary math skills, an alpha strike will seem like a terrible idea. I\u2019m way too lazy to do the math on Flash-Fire Technique, but I doubt it would reliably get us more successes than the average plus 1 standard deviation \u2013 meaning it would yield 9.5 successes on a full excellency. Even if we round up to 10, this only gives us 13 initiative. We\u2019re not in fire aura yet, so we can\u2019t get a damage bonus from Perfect Blazing Blow, so even in our best-case scenario, we can only expect a total damage pool of 20 dice (13 initiative, plus 5 threshold successes from Flash-Fire, plus 2 from God-Immolating Strike). Even with the excellency rerolls, this averages out to 8.8 damage, just shy of being able to kill even a single blood ape, and setting us up for four attacks in retaliation while we\u2019re hanging at base initiative. Way too risky.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if we manage to win Join Battle, we get a reflexive form activation, allowing us to raise our anima by 1 and giving us a free non-Charm autosuccess on almost every attack roll we make in the scene. This pays for itself in 4 attacks even if the apes launch no decisives in the scene.<br /> <br /> Since the apes only have 6 dice on Join Battle and we\u2019re not planning to go for a turn 1 kill, consistency works in our favor. So we buy 2 auto-successes from the excellency and let the dice gods sort out the rest.<br /> <br /> \u2026And of course <i>now</i> we roll 8 successes on 10 dice, bringing us up to 13i. Ape #1 rolls 7 for 10i, while ape #2 is slacking with 3 successes for 6i. We get to reflexively activate Fire Dragon Form, raising our anima banner to glowing.<br /> <br /> TURN 1<br /> <br /> Our rough strategy is to go in hard, crash one of the apes right out of the gate, then play defense until our flux cooks him alive. It\u2019s 9 dice of free damage over the course of a crash, we\u2019d be stupid to do anything risky like attacking early and setting ourselves up for an easy crash or even an initiative shift if we get really bad luck on the damage roll.<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon moves in with blades whirling, striking at ape #2 with Searing Edge Attack and 2 motes on the excellency, rolling 18 dice vs a Parry of 3. Anima goes up to burning, and we\u2019re entering fire aura at the end of our turn thanks to SEA. This is paramount, because we <i>really</i> need the post-roll activation on Flame-Flicker Stance in order to not hemorrhage motes while the apes pound on us with their four attacks.<br /> <br /> 18 dice roll 7 successes, 4 threshold goes to damage for a total post-soak pool of 7 dice. We get exactly 4 successes, SEA burns away the remaining 2 initiative, crashing ape #2. Fire Dragon at 23 initiative, ape #2 at 0. Things are looking up.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 comes in with the Principle of Motion flurry. We spend 3m on Flame-Flicker Stance and 2m on the excellency, raising our anima banner to bonfire. Roiling flames explode from the Fire Dragon stylist, scorching demonic flesh! We get 3 flux damage against ape #1 and a rather pathetic 1 against ape #2. Too bad, I was hoping to get a wound penalty off of this.<br /> <br /> First attack rolls 6 successes, fails, and inflicts no onslaught.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re throwing 2m at the excellency against the second attack. The chances of him rolling no 1s at all are rather slim (0.9 on the power of 11, roughly 31 percent), so we can afford to skimp on our second point of Parry even though we want to activate Flame-Flicker Stance for the onslaught negation no matter what.<br /> <br /> Second attack rolls 12 successes. Not even FFS is gonna save us from this, and we don\u2019t even get the onslaught negation. 5 threshold successes go into damage, and even with medium armor, we\u2019re looking at 12 dice post-soak. Ouch.<br /> <br /> He rolls 5 successes, bringing him up to 13i while Fire Dragon goes down to 18. If we hadn\u2019t gotten our 3 damage off of our anima flux earlier this round, he\u2019d have a pretty good chance to fire off another two attacks before we get to act next turn, if ape #2 rolls even a single successful attack.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 goes for a PoM flurry as well against the same defense as before. 4 successes vs. Parry 6, reflexive Flame-Flicker Stance negates the onslaught because we want to avoid his next attack so he stays in crash and suffers lethal flux damage next turn.<br /> <br /> Same attack goes up against the same defense once more. Ape #2 rolls a baffling 3 successes, Flame-Flicker stays in our back pocket because we\u2019re gonna reset onslaught next action anyway.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, everybody regains 5 motes, flux damage! Ape #1 takes 1 damage, ape #2 eats 2 and is dropped into -1s.<br /> <br /> TURN 2<br /> Fire Dragon at initiative 18, ape #1 at 12, ape #2 at 0.<br /> <br /> Turn begins with a quick cost-benefit assessment. Keeping ape #2 around costs us 10 motes per turn (4m on the excellency against both attacks, plus 6m on using Flame-Flicker Stance on ape #1\u2019s last and ape #2\u2019s first attack to negate onslaught); moreover, twice as many opponents making twice as many attacks against us doubles the chances of an anomalous occurence ruining our carefully-laid plans. Flux damage did its job, but the remaining 6 dice are unlikely to finish the ape off, in which case we\u2019re gonna have to decisive him anyway, so we may as well get it out of the way now while we\u2019re ahead in initiative. Our full combo of 18 initiative +2 dice of damage from Perfect Blazing Blow +2 from God-Immolating Strike has a nearly 97% chance to eat his remaining 6 health levels with the excellency rerolls. I\u2019m willing to gamble on that.<br /> <br /> (Some would say PBB + GIS are overkill; we\u2019re paying an 8m 1wp premium on increasing our kill chance by ~9%. However, failure would set us up for 8 attacks \u2013 10, if the wounded ape gets an initiative shift \u2013 before we get to act again, and we won\u2019t even be able to negate onslaught at initiative 3. I\u2019m willing to pay that premium for my peace of mind.)<br /> <br /> So we\u2019re spending 1m excellency + 3m 1wp PBB + 5m GIS against Parry 4 -1 wound -1 onslaught. The ape tosses in a willpower in a futile attempt to stave off the inevitable, for a grand total of 3.<br /> <br /> Our 13 dice rolls 10 successes after taking the PBB doubles into account. We have a base damage pool of 20, rerolling 6s until they fail to appear. We get 8 damage; the ape is dead.<br /> <br /> Now we reset and face the prospect of 4 attacks from ape #1 before we can act again. And our onslaught negation no longer works. Crap.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 comes at us with the PoM flurry. First attack rolls 11 dice vs. our Parry of 6; we spend 4m on the excellency because Flame-Flicker\u2019s onslaught negation no longer works, and we <i>really</i> don\u2019t want to get crashed so the consistency is preferable to the potential for saved motes. He rolls 3 successes. Fire Dragon feels kind of stupid.<br /> <br /> Second attack! Our defense is the same as before, but onslaught brings us down to Parry 7 total. He gets 4 successes; we\u2019re off the hook once more.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, everybody regains 5 motes, anima flux fails to deal damage.<br /> <br /> TURN 3<br /> Ape #1 at initiative 12, Fire Dragon at 3.<br /> <br /> Another Principle of Motion flurry comes our way. We pump 2m into the excellency; the difference between the ape\u2019s chances to hit parry 5 and parry 6 is nearly 22%, and we can almost certainly use Flame-Flicker Stance to bridge that gap if we need to.<br /> <br /> Sadly, the ape rolls exactly 6 successes. Not even Flame-Flicker Stance can save us now. We\u2019re looking at 8 dice of post-soak damage.<br /> <br /> The ape rolls two successes. We\u2019re hanging at 1i; he has 15 and another attack left to make.<br /> <br /> 2m brings us up to Parry 4; our logic is the same as before, save that the gap is over 25% now.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 cares not for our carefully calibrated probabilistic reasoning and proceeds to roll 2 successes.<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon\u2019s turn! She puts 1m into the excellency and slashes at her opponent\u2019s 4 points of Parry with 15 dice. Ape #1 considers dumping a WP into enhancing it, because keeping her at 1i is very tempting, but decides that being able to make another PoM flurry is probably more valuable (and also 15 dice has a really good chance to hit Parry 5 still).<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon\u2019s 15 dice yield 8 successes, 4 threshold results in a post-soak damage pool of 7. She successfully reaps 3 initiative from her opponent.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, everybody regains 5m, anima flux deals 3 withering damage to ape #1.<br /> <br /> TURN 4<br /> Ape #1 at initiative 9, Fire Dragon at 5.<br /> <br /> Ape fires off his last Principle of Motion flurry, Fire Dragon uses a 2m excellency. His 11 dice garner exactly 7 successes, but he rolls no 1s! Flame-Flicker Stance is shut off.<br /> <br /> Then he proceeds to roll 1 success on 7 dice of post-soak damage. Mediocre!<br /> <br /> Next attack vs. a Parry of 6 after a 2m excellency rolls 5 successes, fails to connect.<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon goes for another 1-mote wonder, rolling 15 dice vs. Parry 4, hits with 5 successes, then rolls 2 successes on her 4d post-soak pool, making this the second turn when she snatches up the exact same amount of initiative her opponent managed to build.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, everybody regains 5m, anima flux deals 2 damage, bringing the ape down to 7.<br /> <br /> TURN 5<br /> Ape #1 and Fire Dragon sit at 7 initiative both.<br /> <br /> Ape knows he has no chance to win a clash, so he takes a full defense. Fire Dragon spends 3m on Searing Edge and 1m on the excellency, rolling 15 dice against a parry of 5 and hits with exactly 5 successes. 4 dice of damage garner 2 successes; her dreams of crashing him remain unrealized.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, everybody regains 5, anima flux deals 1 damage.<br /> <br /> TURN 6<br /> Fire Dragon at 10, Ape #1 at 3.<br /> <br /> She rolls the same 15d plus SEA combo against his Parry of 4, and somehow manages to miss. He rolls against an unenhanced parry of 6 and also misses.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux damage deals 2 withering.<br /> <br /> TURN 7<br /> Fire Dragon at 10, Ape #1 at 1.<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon tosses a 1m excellency at him; rolls 5 successes vs Parry 4, then proceeds to gain zero successes on 5 dice of post-soak damage. Sensing weakness, the ape Brutal Ape Pounces on her and succeeds with 7 against Parry 6, rolling only a single 1 and thus preventing her from Flame-Flickering the attack away. However, his 8 post-soak damage dice only roll 3 successes, so the knockdown and the decisive do not trigger.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux damage deals 2 withering.<br /> <br /> TURN 8<br /> Fire Dragon at 8, Ape at 3.<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon launches a 1m +SEA attack against him, succeeding with 2 threshold and causing 2 withering damage on 5 post-soak dice. Searing Edge Attack ensures the crash. Ape attempts another pounce and fails.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux damage deals 1 decisive, ape is feeling surprisingly comfortable despite the flames enveloping him and charring his flesh.<br /> <br /> TURN 9<br /> Fire Dragon at initiative 16, Ape at -1.<br /> <br /> Her 1m excellency\u2019d attack hits with 3 threshold, stealing another 3 points of initiative; his pounce attempt fails yet again.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux damage deals 1 decisive, putting the ape on his first -1 health level.<br /> <br /> TURN 10<br /> Fire Dragon at initiative 20, Ape at -4.<br /> <br /> Time for the killing blow: another 1m excellency + PBB + GIS for 10 successes vs Parry 2.<br /> <br /> PBB only managed to double a single die, so 21 dice of damage\u2026 resulting in 9 successes before even starting to reroll the 6s. The ape is dead.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Final result: 2 dead apes and an unharmed Immaculate with some motes and WP left in the tank. Everything went better than expected!<br /> <br /> Notes:<br /> - Searing Edge Attack got us 2 crashes we couldn't have snatched otherwise. Even if we dumped an extra 4m into the excellency, that's just 2 threshold successes, resulting in 1.11 damage on average. It would've been enough to ensure the crash in the second case (at a 1m surcharge compared to SEA), but not the first. This is a niche effect, but far from useless - being able to dump decisive flux damage on an opponent 1 turn earlier than we normally could is a very potent benefit.<br /> - I actually found myself really enjoying playing with Flame-Flicker Stance. It introduces a lot of moment-to-moment decisionmaking into how the style plays (can I afford to take the risk of letting the attack through if it potentially saves me 2 motes? can I afford to not excellency at all and hope that my opponent rolls two 1s? should I launch this decisive now and give up my onslaught negation, or is it better if I hold back?), and provides a massive benefit in saved motes. I probably should've relied on it even more, despite the fact that it failed me at least twice.<br /> - For a Fire Dragon stylist, Perfect Blazing Blow is actually a really good Charm! It compares favorably to White Reaper's Falling Scythe Flash + Bleeding Crescent Strike in half as many Charm purchases and at a considerably lower mote cost. I'd rather blow a WP than 7 motes with the teensy-tiny pools I have as a deeb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T04:27:31-07:00","id":1310013,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to find the time to write down a character generation Lunar and see how good it actually is in combat. I'm thinking at a really &quot;jack-of-all-trade&quot; Lunar, something like a Castless (or Changing Moon) with physical tertiary and the only investiment in combat being the two charms necessary to have the Strenght and Stamina excellency. And maybe a little Heart Blood for some other forms aside her Spirit Shape.<br /> <br /> The moment I have write down the combat stats, who want to test it against a QC Dragonblood? I know it seems like a mismatch, but we are talking about a lunar that have maybe 5 combat charms and her most powerful move is to tranform in a big critter, mauling people and hope is enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T04:51:46-07:00","id":1310017,"title":"","content":"I'm totally up for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T05:51:32-07:00","id":1310025,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in seeing that; I suspect it depends a lot on the DB. Physical tertiary is really bad. Obviously you can go bear or something, but with say, Str 3, Dex 4, Sta 2, and Brawl 3, your withering dice pool is going to max at 11. A DB might well be much higher. And excellencies are just increasing soak and damage by 2.<br /> You might be able to get away with stunting your high Social attributes to increase your caps a lot though. That could make a big difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T09:02:33-07:00","id":1310042,"title":"","content":"Earth Dragon!<br /> <br /> Earth Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 5 Dex 3 Sta 3 | Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Earth Dragon 5, Athletics 4, Awareness 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Earth Dragon: Stone Dragon's Skin, Force of the Mountain, Stillness-of-Stone Atemi, Unmoving Mountain Stance, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique *2, Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> <br /> \u201eEarth Dragon really wants to max out Strength and Stamina\u201d is a meme. Deeb ox-bodies only give you -1 and -2 health levels, so you\u2019ll pretty much never need to negate a full -3 penalty with Stone Dragon\u2019s Skin. Unmoving Mountain Stance <i>does</i> receive a significant benefit from maxed Stamina if you\u2019re up against an opponent who can knock you away, but let\u2019s face it, if you\u2019re up against a Solar brawler with Heaven Thunder Hammer, you\u2019re pretty much screwed no matter what. As for its other use\u2026 meh? Spending 6m to deny your opponent initiative on each attack is not a sustainable strategy, not to mention that you probably won\u2019t even need to do so due to your sky-high soak. UMS is in the same category as Fire Dragon\u2019s Searing Edge Attack \u2013 it\u2019s a powerful niche effect, but the thing about niche effects is that you probably shouldn\u2019t tailor your build to maximize their benefit.<br /> <br /> The thing you <i>do</i> want, however, is Strength. Strength 5 gives you +3 dice on smashing attacks (which, given your predilections, may as well read \u201eevery attack\u201d) and it turns Force of the Mountain into a terrifying +5 withering damage for 3m. Oh, and it also gives you +5 soak in the Form, but that\u2019s a red herring \u2013 if you went for Str 3 Sta 5, you\u2019d have the exact same soak in the Form and 2 more out of it. The important part is that you get to make 17d raw damage unarmed withering attacks with +4 charm dice on top for 4m a pop, and that\u2019s terrifying.<br /> <br /> With the issue of attribute distribution settled, time to turn out attention to Charm selection. I ditched Ghost-Grounding Blow because it\u2019s just a shittier, more expensive Spirit-Chaining Strike, and picked up Impervious Skin of Stone instead. With our low-ish Stamina, this is actually not necessarily an amazing Charm (4m for +3 soak is a really inefficient way to use your motes, even with the post-roll activation taken into account), but once you get your infinite soak engine up and running, it provides an amazing second line of defense against unexpectedly high attack rolls resulting in damage overflow from threshold successes. When your opponent rolls 6 dice of damage, spending 4m to cut that in half suddenly seems like a much better deal.<br /> <br /> However, I did fuck up in an important respect: I really should\u2019ve ditched one of the Ox-Bodies for Effortlessly Rising Flame. With a -2 mobility penalty, any idiot can run circles around the poor Earth Immaculate. Blood apes lack ranged attacks and as such, can\u2019t really take advantage of this, but in a wider context, this is something that can lose her the fight.<br /> <br /> Last but not least is the issue of weapon selection. Unarmed, she has a stunted Parry of 5, 4 after using a smash attack. The blood apes can comfortably hit this, and it\u2019s not worth for her to bother spending motes on the excellency to avoid that when her soak reduces them to 1 die anyway. This means she may as well swing a tetsubo and eat the additional -1 Defense penalty; the +1 raw damage they get from the threshold success is unlikely to change anything.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The combat:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Our battle plan is similar to how we played with the Fire Aspect: go for a consistent join battle result by adding auto-successes (we want to win Join Battle and let one of them hit us so we can activate the Form off the back of that hit), then move in, crash a dude with our initial attack, execute said dude with a followup attack, and trust that our soak will grant us the means to weather the following 4 blows over two turns.<br /> <br /> This battle plan is immediately shot to hell when she proceeds to roll a single success on her Join Battle, bringing her up to 6i, with the apes at 7i and 6i respectively.<br /> <br /> TURN 1<br /> Ape #2 at 7i, Ape #1 at 6i, Earth Dragon at 6i.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 moves in with a Principle of Motion flurry! First attack rolls 11 dice against a Parry of 4 after stunt. Knowing that she\u2019s incredibly vulnerable until she manages to fire up Earth Dragon Form and the soak bonus from bonfire, and that she won\u2019t have a chance to activate EDF if Ape #2 lands even a single point of damage on her, Earth Dragon drops her tetsubo and pumps a full excellency into her Parry, bringing her up to 7.<br /> <br /> 11 dice garner 5 successes, the attack fails. Second attack at 11 dice has a good chance to hit her full excellency\u2019d Parry of 6, so she tosses in a Willpower as well for Parry 7. Ape #2 rolls 4 successes, his second attack fails as well.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 and Earth Dragon act on the same tick! Ape #1 knows fully well that he has no chance to win a clash against a full excellency\u2019d attack and that the 3 automatic levels of post-soak damage withering clashes get by default would ensure that Earth Dragon shoots up to the top of the initiative order and can get a reflexive form activation off of any attack thrown at her, so he decides to stay at short range and use Shattering Roar instead. Thwarted, Earth Dragon goes for a withering attack against ape #2 instead.<br /> <br /> Order of operations suddenly becomes really important, because if she gains any initiative off of the attack, she can activate the Form when Ape #1\u2019s roar hits her. The rule says ties go to the better stunt, which is Earth Dragon\u2019s. She gets to fire off her attack before the roar hits.<br /> <br /> Confident in her abilities (and the +4 accuracy bonus from light weapons), Earth Dragon tosses Force of the Mountain and a 2m excellency into her attack, raising her anima to glowing and entering Earth Aura at the end of her turn. Dex 3 + Earth Dragon 5 + accuracy 4 + excellency 2 + stunt 2 brings her up to 16 dice vs Parry 4. Ape #2 really wants to deny her form activation, so he spends a Willpower to bring his Parry up to 5.<br /> <br /> She rolls 6 successes \u2013 base damage 12 +1 threshold +2 FotM -7 soak is 8 post-soak damage dice, rolling 5 successes. The ape\u2019s ears are ringing under her relentless onslaught.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the other ape rolls a single success on 9 dice against her Parry of 5, and misses the roar. Oops.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5.<br /> <br /> TURN 2<br /> Earth Dragon at 12i, ape #1 at 6i, ape #2 at 2i.<br /> <br /> She launches another attack with 2m + FoM, raising her anima to burning and rolling 16 dice vs parry 3. 10 successes means a total raw damage pool of 24, 17d10 post-soak for a total of 7 successes. Ape #2 is crashed, and Earth Dragon has more initiative than she knows what to do with.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 moves in, PoM flurry; first attack rolls 5 successes against her Parry of 5, hitting exactly. Earth Dragon Form activates reflexively, and her anima rises to bonfire. Flux damage fails to gather any successes against either demon.<br /> <br /> 15 base damage vs. soak 18, ape #1 is reduced to 1 die and rolls no successes.<br /> <br /> Second attack rolls 13 successes vs. Parry 4! 9 threshold goes into damage for a total raw damage pool of 24. Earth Dragon activates Impervious Skin of Stone and cuts this in half; 3 damage dice roll a single success.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 also flurries, tossing 11 dice vs Parry 3 on the first attack and hitting exactly. He is reduced to a single damage die and rolls a failure. Second attack is 11d vs Parry 2, rolling 7 successes and boosting his damage to 20\u2026 of which 2 gets past her soak. He rolls 4 successes, and barely manages to pull out of crash.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux damage! Earth Dragon pays 2i to hopefully knock ape #1 prone, but her flux fails to deal damage. Then she also proceeds to roll no successes against ape #2.<br /> <br /> TURN 3<br /> Earth Dragon at initiative 17, ape #1 at 8, ape #2 at 1.<br /> <br /> She swings her mighty weapon for a smash attack against ape #1, enhanced by 1m and FoM. She rolls 8 successes and deals 9 damage. Ape #1 is crashed and prone; the demons are starting to re-evaluate their life choices.<br /> <br /> At this point, if this was an actual game, the apes would activate Hurry Home instead of waiting for her to unload her infinite initiative, but let\u2019s keep going and see what happens!<br /> <br /> Ape #2 PoM flurries; his first attack hits with 1 threshold and rolls a single damage success; his second one somehow manages to fail against a Parry of 3.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 forgoes PoM and instead uses a regular flurry to rise from prone and get an attack in. 4 dice to rise rolls the required 2 successes; he is up and running, attacks, hits and rolls a 10 on his single die of post-soak damage.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux does nothing.<br /> <br /> TURN 4<br /> Earth Dragon at 27i, Ape #2 at 3, Ape #1 at 1.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon rolls a decisive smash with 2 excellency dice and Force of the Mountain against Ape #1, who spends a WP but is no match for her 7 successes on 15 dice.<br /> <br /> 25 damage dice with double 10s and rerolling 6s results in <b>21 levels of damage</b> and a very, very dead blood ape.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 is out of Willpower. He pounces because there\u2019s literally nothing else he can do with his motes, succeeds on the attack, gets reduced to a single die and fails to roll any successes.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux does nothing.<br /> <br /> TURN 5<br /> Ape #2 at 4i, Earth Dragon at 3.<br /> <br /> Ape pounces, hits, and rolls no successes once more.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon smashes with 1m excellency + 3m FotM, maybe out of a misplaced desire for fair play as she brings herself down to 1i in the process.<br /> <br /> However, her attack connects, rolls 11 successes on 17 post-soak damage dice, and crashes ape #2 once again. It\u2019s been three turns since last time, so she also reaps an initiative break from him.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux does nothing.<br /> <br /> TURN 6<br /> Earth Dragon at 20i, Ape #2 at -6.<br /> <br /> She rolls to finish her prone opponent off with her signature FotM +1m excellency attack, and scores a hit against Parry 2 with 11 successes.<br /> <br /> 20 dice of damage with double 10s and rerolled 6s get 10 successes; another ape bites the dust.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Final result: 2 splattered blood apes and a profoundly bored Earth Immaculate. (No, seriously, she had more than half of her peripheral pool left by the end \u2013 <i>after</i> being on the receiving end of one of the worst opening rounds I\u2019ve ever seen.)<br /> <br /> Notes:<br /> - <i>what is this I can\u2019t even</i><br /> - Earth Dragon OP, pls nerf<br /> - seriously, the fight was effectively over by the time I realized I should be spamming base initiative decisive PoM flurries in the hope that maybe <i>those</i> would do <i>something</i><br /> - not that they would achieve anything against Earth Immaculates in the form they\u2019re encountered in the wild, which is to say bedecked in artifact heavy armor with Hardness 10","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 05-05-2019, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum