| Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Earth Dragon 5, Athletics 4, Awareness 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Earth Dragon: Stone Dragon's Skin, Force of the Mountain, Stillness-of-Stone Atemi, Unmoving Mountain Stance, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique *2, Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> <br /> \u201eEarth Dragon really wants to max out Strength and Stamina\u201d is a meme. Deeb ox-bodies only give you -1 and -2 health levels, so you\u2019ll pretty much never need to negate a full -3 penalty with Stone Dragon\u2019s Skin. Unmoving Mountain Stance <i>does</i> receive a significant benefit from maxed Stamina if you\u2019re up against an opponent who can knock you away, but let\u2019s face it, if you\u2019re up against a Solar brawler with Heaven Thunder Hammer, you\u2019re pretty much screwed no matter what. As for its other use\u2026 meh? Spending 6m to deny your opponent initiative on each attack is not a sustainable strategy, not to mention that you probably won\u2019t even need to do so due to your sky-high soak. UMS is in the same category as Fire Dragon\u2019s Searing Edge Attack \u2013 it\u2019s a powerful niche effect, but the thing about niche effects is that you probably shouldn\u2019t tailor your build to maximize their benefit.<br /> <br /> The thing you <i>do</i> want, however, is Strength. Strength 5 gives you +3 dice on smashing attacks (which, given your predilections, may as well read \u201eevery attack\u201d) and it turns Force of the Mountain into a terrifying +5 withering damage for 3m. Oh, and it also gives you +5 soak in the Form, but that\u2019s a red herring \u2013 if you went for Str 3 Sta 5, you\u2019d have the exact same soak in the Form and 2 more out of it. The important part is that you get to make 17d raw damage unarmed withering attacks with +4 charm dice on top for 4m a pop, and that\u2019s terrifying.<br /> <br /> With the issue of attribute distribution settled, time to turn out attention to Charm selection. I ditched Ghost-Grounding Blow because it\u2019s just a shittier, more expensive Spirit-Chaining Strike, and picked up Impervious Skin of Stone instead. With our low-ish Stamina, this is actually not necessarily an amazing Charm (4m for +3 soak is a really inefficient way to use your motes, even with the post-roll activation taken into account), but once you get your infinite soak engine up and running, it provides an amazing second line of defense against unexpectedly high attack rolls resulting in damage overflow from threshold successes. When your opponent rolls 6 dice of damage, spending 4m to cut that in half suddenly seems like a much better deal.<br /> <br /> However, I did fuck up in an important respect: I really should\u2019ve ditched one of the Ox-Bodies for Effortlessly Rising Flame. With a -2 mobility penalty, any idiot can run circles around the poor Earth Immaculate. Blood apes lack ranged attacks and as such, can\u2019t really take advantage of this, but in a wider context, this is something that can lose her the fight.<br /> <br /> Last but not least is the issue of weapon selection. Unarmed, she has a stunted Parry of 5, 4 after using a smash attack. The blood apes can comfortably hit this, and it\u2019s not worth for her to bother spending motes on the excellency to avoid that when her soak reduces them to 1 die anyway. This means she may as well swing a tetsubo and eat the additional -1 Defense penalty; the +1 raw damage they get from the threshold success is unlikely to change anything.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The combat:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Our battle plan is similar to how we played with the Fire Aspect: go for a consistent join battle result by adding auto-successes (we want to win Join Battle and let one of them hit us so we can activate the Form off the back of that hit), then move in, crash a dude with our initial attack, execute said dude with a followup attack, and trust that our soak will grant us the means to weather the following 4 blows over two turns.<br /> <br /> This battle plan is immediately shot to hell when she proceeds to roll a single success on her Join Battle, bringing her up to 6i, with the apes at 7i and 6i respectively.<br /> <br /> TURN 1<br /> Ape #2 at 7i, Ape #1 at 6i, Earth Dragon at 6i.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 moves in with a Principle of Motion flurry! First attack rolls 11 dice against a Parry of 4 after stunt. Knowing that she\u2019s incredibly vulnerable until she manages to fire up Earth Dragon Form and the soak bonus from bonfire, and that she won\u2019t have a chance to activate EDF if Ape #2 lands even a single point of damage on her, Earth Dragon drops her tetsubo and pumps a full excellency into her Parry, bringing her up to 7.<br /> <br /> 11 dice garner 5 successes, the attack fails. Second attack at 11 dice has a good chance to hit her full excellency\u2019d Parry of 6, so she tosses in a Willpower as well for Parry 7. Ape #2 rolls 4 successes, his second attack fails as well.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 and Earth Dragon act on the same tick! Ape #1 knows fully well that he has no chance to win a clash against a full excellency\u2019d attack and that the 3 automatic levels of post-soak damage withering clashes get by default would ensure that Earth Dragon shoots up to the top of the initiative order and can get a reflexive form activation off of any attack thrown at her, so he decides to stay at short range and use Shattering Roar instead. Thwarted, Earth Dragon goes for a withering attack against ape #2 instead.<br /> <br /> Order of operations suddenly becomes really important, because if she gains any initiative off of the attack, she can activate the Form when Ape #1\u2019s roar hits her. The rule says ties go to the better stunt, which is Earth Dragon\u2019s. She gets to fire off her attack before the roar hits.<br /> <br /> Confident in her abilities (and the +4 accuracy bonus from light weapons), Earth Dragon tosses Force of the Mountain and a 2m excellency into her attack, raising her anima to glowing and entering Earth Aura at the end of her turn. Dex 3 + Earth Dragon 5 + accuracy 4 + excellency 2 + stunt 2 brings her up to 16 dice vs Parry 4. Ape #2 really wants to deny her form activation, so he spends a Willpower to bring his Parry up to 5.<br /> <br /> She rolls 6 successes \u2013 base damage 12 +1 threshold +2 FotM -7 soak is 8 post-soak damage dice, rolling 5 successes. The ape\u2019s ears are ringing under her relentless onslaught.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the other ape rolls a single success on 9 dice against her Parry of 5, and misses the roar. Oops.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5.<br /> <br /> TURN 2<br /> Earth Dragon at 12i, ape #1 at 6i, ape #2 at 2i.<br /> <br /> She launches another attack with 2m + FoM, raising her anima to burning and rolling 16 dice vs parry 3. 10 successes means a total raw damage pool of 24, 17d10 post-soak for a total of 7 successes. Ape #2 is crashed, and Earth Dragon has more initiative than she knows what to do with.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 moves in, PoM flurry; first attack rolls 5 successes against her Parry of 5, hitting exactly. Earth Dragon Form activates reflexively, and her anima rises to bonfire. Flux damage fails to gather any successes against either demon.<br /> <br /> 15 base damage vs. soak 18, ape #1 is reduced to 1 die and rolls no successes.<br /> <br /> Second attack rolls 13 successes vs. Parry 4! 9 threshold goes into damage for a total raw damage pool of 24. Earth Dragon activates Impervious Skin of Stone and cuts this in half; 3 damage dice roll a single success.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 also flurries, tossing 11 dice vs Parry 3 on the first attack and hitting exactly. He is reduced to a single damage die and rolls a failure. Second attack is 11d vs Parry 2, rolling 7 successes and boosting his damage to 20\u2026 of which 2 gets past her soak. He rolls 4 successes, and barely manages to pull out of crash.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux damage! Earth Dragon pays 2i to hopefully knock ape #1 prone, but her flux fails to deal damage. Then she also proceeds to roll no successes against ape #2.<br /> <br /> TURN 3<br /> Earth Dragon at initiative 17, ape #1 at 8, ape #2 at 1.<br /> <br /> She swings her mighty weapon for a smash attack against ape #1, enhanced by 1m and FoM. She rolls 8 successes and deals 9 damage. Ape #1 is crashed and prone; the demons are starting to re-evaluate their life choices.<br /> <br /> At this point, if this was an actual game, the apes would activate Hurry Home instead of waiting for her to unload her infinite initiative, but let\u2019s keep going and see what happens!<br /> <br /> Ape #2 PoM flurries; his first attack hits with 1 threshold and rolls a single damage success; his second one somehow manages to fail against a Parry of 3.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 forgoes PoM and instead uses a regular flurry to rise from prone and get an attack in. 4 dice to rise rolls the required 2 successes; he is up and running, attacks, hits and rolls a 10 on his single die of post-soak damage.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux does nothing.<br /> <br /> TURN 4<br /> Earth Dragon at 27i, Ape #2 at 3, Ape #1 at 1.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon rolls a decisive smash with 2 excellency dice and Force of the Mountain against Ape #1, who spends a WP but is no match for her 7 successes on 15 dice.<br /> <br /> 25 damage dice with double 10s and rerolling 6s results in <b>21 levels of damage</b> and a very, very dead blood ape.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 is out of Willpower. He pounces because there\u2019s literally nothing else he can do with his motes, succeeds on the attack, gets reduced to a single die and fails to roll any successes.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux does nothing.<br /> <br /> TURN 5<br /> Ape #2 at 4i, Earth Dragon at 3.<br /> <br /> Ape pounces, hits, and rolls no successes once more.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon smashes with 1m excellency + 3m FotM, maybe out of a misplaced desire for fair play as she brings herself down to 1i in the process.<br /> <br /> However, her attack connects, rolls 11 successes on 17 post-soak damage dice, and crashes ape #2 once again. It\u2019s been three turns since last time, so she also reaps an initiative break from him.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux does nothing.<br /> <br /> TURN 6<br /> Earth Dragon at 20i, Ape #2 at -6.<br /> <br /> She rolls to finish her prone opponent off with her signature FotM +1m excellency attack, and scores a hit against Parry 2 with 11 successes.<br /> <br /> 20 dice of damage with double 10s and rerolled 6s get 10 successes; another ape bites the dust.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Final result: 2 splattered blood apes and a profoundly bored Earth Immaculate. (No, seriously, she had more than half of her peripheral pool left by the end \u2013 <i>after</i> being on the receiving end of one of the worst opening rounds I\u2019ve ever seen.)<br /> <br /> Notes:<br /> - <i>what is this I can\u2019t even</i><br /> - Earth Dragon OP, pls nerf<br /> - seriously, the fight was effectively over by the time I realized I should be spamming base initiative decisive PoM flurries in the hope that maybe <i>those</i> would do <i>something</i><br /> - not that they would achieve anything against Earth Immaculates in the form they\u2019re encountered in the wild, which is to say bedecked in artifact heavy armor with Hardness 10</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But, you know, Air and Fire Dragon are totally effective combat styles and absolutely comparable to Earth and Water, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T09:29:46-07:00","id":1310046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but once you get your infinite soak engine up and running,</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, your what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T09:30:57-07:00","id":1310047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310043#post1310043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, you know, Air and Fire Dragon are totally effective combat styles and absolutely comparable to Earth and Water, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> hot take: comparing the yawnfest that was the Earth Dragon fight to the tense and exciting Fire Dragon encounter, I'd say the latter comes out ahead in the most important metric of &quot;but is this fun&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310046#post1310046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, your what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not <i>literally </i>infinite, but 18 soak in shitty mortal armor, without maxed Stamina is &quot;infinite enough&quot; by my reckoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 05-05-2019, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T09:40:35-07:00","id":1310050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310047#post1310047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> hot take: comparing the yawnfest that was the Earth Dragon fight to the tense and exciting Fire Dragon encounter, I'd say the latter comes out ahead in the most important metric of &quot;but is this fun&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not <i>literally </i>infinite, but 18 soak in shitty mortal armor, without maxed Stamina is &quot;infinite enough&quot; by my reckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rebuke of hot take: If Earth Dragon makes it easy to fight demons and Air Dragon gets wrecked by them while Fire Dragon can kind of make it out, something's not right in their balance, regardless of which one is more fun to play. (Also, it's not fun to create a combat-based FD character and then constantly lose, while the guy who dipped Earth Dragon steamrolls everything, so even the 'fun' bit is not quite right).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T09:49:09-07:00","id":1310051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310050#post1310050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rebuke of hot take: If Earth Dragon makes it easy to fight demons and Air Dragon gets wrecked by them while Fire Dragon can kind of make it out, something's not right in their balance, regardless of which one is more fun to play. (Also, it's not fun to create a combat-based FD character and then constantly lose, while the guy who dipped Earth Dragon steamrolls everything, so even the 'fun' bit is not quite right).</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't want to be rude but all I'm hearing is &quot;what is a representative sample&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T09:58:54-07:00","id":1310054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310051#post1310051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really don't want to be rude but all I'm hearing is &quot;what is a representative sample&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That said, I'm eager to see how Water and Wood fare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T10:00:10-07:00","id":1310056,"title":"","content":"Rebuke of rebuke of hot take: bad dice rolls can come out of nowhere, and fucks pretty much everyone. It doesn't necessarily mean Air or Fire Dragon is weak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T10:04:45-07:00","id":1310057,"title":"","content":"Also: Fire Dragon won the fight unwounded, with 3 WP and 11 peripheral left in the tank <i>after</i> delivering a massive, arguably unnecessary finishing blow. Earth Dragon won the fight unwounded, with 4 WP and 17 peripheral left in the tank. Admittedly, Earth Dragon won her fight in almost half as much time and off the back of a terrible join battle, but I don't think it's fair to characterize Fire as &quot;kind of making it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T10:06:08-07:00","id":1310058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310056#post1310056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rebuke of rebuke of hot take: bad dice rolls can come out of nowhere, and fucks pretty much everyone. It doesn't necessarily mean Air or Fire Dragon is weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Fire is one where the bad dice rolls might hurt more due to the way it eats motes at first and if those don't go well it is going to take multiple turns of caution to get back to the rhythm it wants you to take, but also lack a lot of good 1 v 1 observation on this. Not all the players in my game are fighters, but enough are that few combats are any single one of them showing up an enemy and the Fire Dragon stylist has only once really botched their initial alpha strike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T10:07:01-07:00","id":1310059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310056#post1310056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rebuke of rebuke of hot take: bad dice rolls can come out of nowhere, and fucks pretty much everyone. It doesn't necessarily mean Air or Fire Dragon is weak.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Earth Dragon got bad rolls too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T10:32:50-07:00","id":1310062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310047#post1310047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not <i>literally </i>infinite, but 18 soak in shitty mortal armor, without maxed Stamina is &quot;infinite enough&quot; by my reckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, if I was playing an Earth monk, I'd be tempted to either be wearing enormous magic armour or no armour at all, so I could increase my soak by 3 without spending initiative.<br /> <br /> Which... is probably subpar, but it looks badass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T10:53:17-07:00","id":1310065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310062#post1310062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tbh, if I was playing an Earth monk, I'd be tempted to either be wearing enormous magic armour or no armour at all, so I could increase my soak by 3 without spending initiative.<br /> <br /> Which... is probably subpar, but it looks badass.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is with Earth Dragon heavy armor is the go-to choice up until you get the capstone, at which point it becomes better to go <i>without</i> armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:09:03-07:00","id":1310067,"title":"","content":"Actually, the supreme choice for a shirtless Earth Dragon build is to combo it with White Reaper: with Impenetrable White Shroud, you get +6 soak straight out of the gate as long as there's a single battle group within striking distance, and potentially +9 if you're willing to make two attacks before swapping to Earth Dragon Form. Additionally, you get top tier penalty negation to your Parry (3m to ignore up to 2 points of wound penalties, 4m 1i to convert onslaught penalties to a bonus), absolutely ungodly withering damage with the combination of Falling Scythe Flash + Force of the Mountain, and you can make use of Bleeding Crescent Strike for extra accuracy on your decisives. With the amount of motes you save on offensive and defensive excellencies, not even the mote-hungry nature of the style can slow you down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:40:57-07:00","id":1310078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310043#post1310043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, you know, Air and Fire Dragon are totally effective combat styles and absolutely comparable to Earth and Water, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So what happens if we have an Air Immaculate fight an Earth Immaculate?<br /> <br /> Earth Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 5 Dex 3 Sta 3 | Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Earth Dragon 5, Athletics 4, Awareness 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Earth Dragon: Stone Dragon's Skin, Force of the Mountain, Stillness-of-Stone Atemi, Unmoving Mountain Stance, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique *2, Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> <br /> Specialties MA Earth Dragon, Athletics Feats of Strength, Resistance poisons.<br /> <br /> <br /> STATS<br /> Tetsubo 10 (Damage 19/5)<br /> Parry 5<br /> Soak 14<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Air Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 3 Dex 5 Sta 3 | Perception 3, Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Air Dragon 5, Awareness 4, Dodge 5, Stealth 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Air Dragon Style: Air Dragon's Sight, Cloud-Treading Method, Wind Dragon's Speed, Breath-Seizing Technique, Air Dragon Form, Shroud of Unseen Winds<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> <br /> Specialties MA Air Dragon and Dodge/Athletics, while in Air Dragon Form<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> Chakram 16 (Damage 13/3)<br /> Evasion 5<br /> Soak 8/4<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> FIGHT<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Both Dragons use 4m to full excellency their Join Battles<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon rolls 8 dice for 2, for 7 initiative<br /> Air Dragon rolls 8 dice for 3, for 8 initiative<br /> <br /> <br /> =========<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Air Dragon uses 5m Wind Dragon Speed to flurry an attack and disengage<br /> <br /> Earth defends with 5m 1i Stone Dragon's Skin<br /> <br /> Air rolls 1m attack for 17 dice against parry 5, scoring 4 and missing.<br /> <br /> Air rolls 10 dice to disengage, spending 4m for 2 autosuccesses against Earth's 5 dice, getting 6 against 1 and disengaging<br /> --------<br /> Earth moves toward Air who reflexively moves back, and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 10, failing with 2 against 4<br /> =========<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Air Dragon spends 8m to activate Air Dragon Form and moves to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and activates 9m Earth Dragon Style<br /> =========<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and missing with 6<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 2 against 6 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and missing with 5<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 5 against 6 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and getting it with 11, rolling 3 dice of damage for 2<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 2 against 3 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and getting it with 12, rolling 3 dice of damage for 3<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 3 against 2 and suceeding!<br /> =========<br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> Air Dragon takes a 1i full defense action, getting ready to spring away again<br /> --------<br /> Earth Dragon moves into close and attacks with 6m full excellency, 3m Force of the Mountain, and 2i smashing attack, trying to knock the air aspect to the ground. Paying for this causes the Earth Immaculate to crash itself, losing an extra 5i, but at least it denies it to the air aspect as a crash bonus.<br /> <br /> Air defends with 4m full excellency<br /> <br /> Earth rolls 16 dice against an evasion of 11, scoring 10 and missing<br /> =========<br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> Air Dragon uses 5m Wind Dragon Speed to flurry a decisive attack with a disengage.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon uses 6m full excellency, Earth Dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against a parry of 7, getting 10 and hitting. Rolling 14 decisive damage for 5, putting Earth Dragon into his last -1 health level<br /> <br /> Air Dragon disengages with 11 dice and 1 success from Air Dragon, against 4 dice from Earth Dragon rolling 1 total of 10 successes against 5 and disengaging<br /> --------<br /> Earth moves into short range and rushes, rolling 4 dice against 11, scoring 1 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Earth dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against parry 8, getting it with 12, rolling 3 decisive damage for 0<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 4 dice against 11, scoring 3 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 10<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Earth dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against parry 8, getting it with 9, rolling 3 decisive damage for 1, putting Earth into -2s<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon resets to base initiative and closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 2 against 6 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 11<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Earth dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against parry 7, failing with 5<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 0 against 4 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 12<br /> <br /> Air Dragon withering attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Eath Dragon spends 6m to full excellency defense. Rolling 20 dice agasint parry 7, scoring 8 and hitting, rolling 3 dice for 1 damage<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 0 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 13<br /> <br /> Air Dragon withering attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Eath Dragon spends 6m to full excellency defense. Rolling 20 dice agasint parry 7, scoring 9 and hitting, rolling 3 dice for 1 damage<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 1 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 14<br /> <br /> Air Dragon withering attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Eath Dragon spends 6m to full excellency defense. Rolling 20 dice agasint parry 7, scoring 9 and hitting, rolling 3 dice for 4 damage, crashing the Earth again<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 0 against 11 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 15<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, with 6m full excellency, rolling 17 dice against Earths 6m full excellency parry ot 7, hitting with 8. Scoring 8 damage off of 17 dice, the Air Dragon slays the Earth<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And there we go. It turns out that facing off against an Air Immaculate who has 5 dex and a -0 mobility penalty really sucks when you've got 3 dex and a -2 mobility penalty. That was even assuming that the Air Dragon didn't also have any athletics charms, which is probably a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:51:27-07:00","id":1310080,"title":"","content":"I feel like <i>somebody</i> was putting their thumb on the scale there a bit, between giving the Air Immaculate more artifacts, better skills and specialties, and explicitly ignoring my advice to ditch an Ox-Body in favor of the Athletics excellency :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:52:23-07:00","id":1310081,"title":"","content":"The Earth dragon user would still be invested in athletics and dexterity. I don't get why you wouldn't. Also, air dragon doesn't combine well with athletics apart from their soaring leap and the charm that lets you run with vertical walls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 05-05-2019, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T12:08:24-07:00","id":1310084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310078#post1310078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what happens if we have an Air Immaculate fight an Earth Immaculate?<br /> <br /> Earth Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 5 Dex 3 Sta 3 | Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Earth Dragon 5, Athletics 4, Awareness 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Earth Dragon: Stone Dragon's Skin, Force of the Mountain, Stillness-of-Stone Atemi, Unmoving Mountain Stance, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique *2, Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> <br /> Specialties MA Earth Dragon, Athletics Feats of Strength, Resistance poisons.<br /> <br /> <br /> STATS<br /> Tetsubo 10 (Damage 19/5)<br /> Parry 5<br /> Soak 14<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Air Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 3 Dex 5 Sta 3 | Perception 3, Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Air Dragon 5, Awareness 4, Dodge 5, Stealth 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Air Dragon Style: Air Dragon's Sight, Cloud-Treading Method, Wind Dragon's Speed, Breath-Seizing Technique, Air Dragon Form, Shroud of Unseen Winds<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> <br /> Specialties MA Air Dragon and Dodge/Athletics, while in Air Dragon Form<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> Chakram 16 (Damage 13/3)<br /> Evasion 5<br /> Soak 8/4<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> FIGHT<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Both Dragons use 4m to full excellency their Join Battles<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon rolls 8 dice for 2, for 7 initiative<br /> Air Dragon rolls 8 dice for 3, for 8 initiative<br /> <br /> <br /> =========<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Air Dragon uses 5m Wind Dragon Speed to flurry an attack and disengage<br /> <br /> Earth defends with 5m 1i Stone Dragon's Skin<br /> <br /> Air rolls 1m attack for 17 dice against parry 5, scoring 4 and missing.<br /> <br /> Air rolls 10 dice to disengage, spending 4m for 2 autosuccesses against Earth's 5 dice, getting 6 against 1 and disengaging<br /> --------<br /> Earth moves toward Air who reflexively moves back, and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 10, failing with 2 against 4<br /> =========<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Air Dragon spends 8m to activate Air Dragon Form and moves to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and activates 9m Earth Dragon Style<br /> =========<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and missing with 6<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 2 against 6 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and missing with 5<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 5 against 6 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and getting it with 11, rolling 3 dice of damage for 2<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 2 against 3 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and getting it with 12, rolling 3 dice of damage for 3<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 3 against 2 and suceeding!<br /> =========<br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> Air Dragon takes a 1i full defense action, getting ready to spring away again<br /> --------<br /> Earth Dragon moves into close and attacks with 6m full excellency, 3m Force of the Mountain, and 2i smashing attack, trying to knock the air aspect to the ground. Paying for this causes the Earth Immaculate to crash itself, losing an extra 5i, but at least it denies it to the air aspect as a crash bonus.<br /> <br /> Air defends with 4m full excellency<br /> <br /> Earth rolls 16 dice against an evasion of 11, scoring 10 and missing<br /> =========<br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> Air Dragon uses 5m Wind Dragon Speed to flurry a decisive attack with a disengage.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon uses 6m full excellency, Earth Dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against a parry of 7, getting 10 and hitting. Rolling 14 decisive damage for 5, putting Earth Dragon into his last -1 health level<br /> <br /> Air Dragon disengages with 11 dice and 1 success from Air Dragon, against 4 dice from Earth Dragon rolling 1 total of 10 successes against 5 and disengaging<br /> --------<br /> Earth moves into short range and rushes, rolling 4 dice against 11, scoring 1 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Earth dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against parry 8, getting it with 12, rolling 3 decisive damage for 0<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 4 dice against 11, scoring 3 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 10<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Earth dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against parry 8, getting it with 9, rolling 3 decisive damage for 1, putting Earth into -2s<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon resets to base initiative and closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 2 against 6 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 11<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Earth dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against parry 7, failing with 5<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 0 against 4 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 12<br /> <br /> Air Dragon withering attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Eath Dragon spends 6m to full excellency defense. Rolling 20 dice agasint parry 7, scoring 8 and hitting, rolling 3 dice for 1 damage<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 0 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 13<br /> <br /> Air Dragon withering attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Eath Dragon spends 6m to full excellency defense. Rolling 20 dice agasint parry 7, scoring 9 and hitting, rolling 3 dice for 1 damage<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 1 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 14<br /> <br /> Air Dragon withering attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Eath Dragon spends 6m to full excellency defense. Rolling 20 dice agasint parry 7, scoring 9 and hitting, rolling 3 dice for 4 damage, crashing the Earth again<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 0 against 11 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 15<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, with 6m full excellency, rolling 17 dice against Earths 6m full excellency parry ot 7, hitting with 8. Scoring 8 damage off of 17 dice, the Air Dragon slays the Earth<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And there we go. It turns out that facing off against an Air Immaculate who has 5 dex and a -0 mobility penalty really sucks when you've got 3 dex and a -2 mobility penalty. That was even assuming that the Air Dragon didn't also have any athletics charms, which is probably a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Translation: Turns out, giving Earth a 3 in the combat godstat and Air a 5, combined with giving Earth the worst weapons and armors for dicepool purposes (-1 attack, -2 mobility) while Air gets the best ones it can (+4 non-Charm dice on withering attacks, no mobility penalties), makes the Air Dragon one have a significant advantage. Color me shocked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T12:23:17-07:00","id":1310087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310080#post1310080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like <i>somebody</i> was putting their thumb on the scale there a bit, between giving the Air Immaculate more artifacts, better skills and specialties, and explicitly ignoring my advice to ditch an Ox-Body in favor of the Athletics excellency :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave BOTH sides artifacts, and if your style is giving you an Evasion bonus you either invest as much into Dodge as you do your MA ability or else waste those bonuses, since otherwise your parry won\u2019t even keep up with your dodge.<br /> <br /> Not doing that is like running a Silver Voiced Nightingale stylist who decided that Performance was cool to leave at 4 with no excellency, or a Black claw stylist who didn\u2019t feel the need to invest into Manipulation or Presence.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon doesn\u2019t really care, it doesn\u2019t dodge, or disengage, or use performance attacks so you can afford to just leave it. I could have given the Earth Dragon a bunch of rush charms, that could have helped, but now I\u2019m building to counter air specifically, and you can\u2019t build to counter every enemy. Where as giving air evasion is just building to complement your own MA, which is good in every scenario.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon loves disengaging and keeping away from its enemy so it can abuse the fact that it\u2019s one of the very few ranged Martial Arts, if you want to use it, use it for what its good at. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also if this battle could have taken place in difficult terrain, or in the dark, or both, if it did it would have been even more one sided. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310084#post1310084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Translation: Turns out, giving Earth a 3 in the combat godstat and Air a 5, combined with giving Earth the worst weapons and armors for dicepool purposes (-1 attack, -2 mobility) while Air gets the best ones it can (+4 non-Charm dice on withering attacks, no mobility penalties), makes the Air Dragon one have a significant advantage. Color me shocked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it\u2019s quite amazing how the form weapons and armor for each style can affect the combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T12:43:18-07:00","id":1310090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310078#post1310078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what happens if we have an Air Immaculate fight an Earth Immaculate?<br /> <br /> Earth Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 5 Dex 3 Sta 3 | Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Earth Dragon 5, Athletics 4, Awareness 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Earth Dragon: Stone Dragon's Skin, Force of the Mountain, Stillness-of-Stone Atemi, Unmoving Mountain Stance, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique *2, Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> <br /> Specialties MA Earth Dragon, Athletics Feats of Strength, Resistance poisons.<br /> <br /> <br /> STATS<br /> Tetsubo 10 (Damage 19/5)<br /> Parry 5<br /> Soak 14<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Air Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 3 Dex 5 Sta 3 | Perception 3, Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Air Dragon 5, Awareness 4, Dodge 5, Stealth 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Air Dragon Style: Air Dragon's Sight, Cloud-Treading Method, Wind Dragon's Speed, Breath-Seizing Technique, Air Dragon Form, Shroud of Unseen Winds<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> <br /> Specialties MA Air Dragon and Dodge/Athletics, while in Air Dragon Form<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> Chakram 16 (Damage 13/3)<br /> Evasion 5<br /> Soak 8/4<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> FIGHT<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Both Dragons use 4m to full excellency their Join Battles<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon rolls 8 dice for 2, for 7 initiative<br /> Air Dragon rolls 8 dice for 3, for 8 initiative<br /> <br /> <br /> =========<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Air Dragon uses 5m Wind Dragon Speed to flurry an attack and disengage<br /> <br /> Earth defends with 5m 1i Stone Dragon's Skin<br /> <br /> Air rolls 1m attack for 17 dice against parry 5, scoring 4 and missing.<br /> <br /> Air rolls 10 dice to disengage, spending 4m for 2 autosuccesses against Earth's 5 dice, getting 6 against 1 and disengaging<br /> --------<br /> Earth moves toward Air who reflexively moves back, and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 10, failing with 2 against 4<br /> =========<br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Air Dragon spends 8m to activate Air Dragon Form and moves to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and activates 9m Earth Dragon Style<br /> =========<br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and missing with 6<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 2 against 6 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and missing with 5<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 5 against 6 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and getting it with 11, rolling 3 dice of damage for 2<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 2 against 3 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> Air Dragon attacks, spending 4m on excellency for 20 dice. Earth spends 6m to raise parry to 8, rolling 20 dice and getting it with 12, rolling 3 dice of damage for 3<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 5 dice against 11, scoring 3 against 2 and suceeding!<br /> =========<br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> Air Dragon takes a 1i full defense action, getting ready to spring away again<br /> --------<br /> Earth Dragon moves into close and attacks with 6m full excellency, 3m Force of the Mountain, and 2i smashing attack, trying to knock the air aspect to the ground. Paying for this causes the Earth Immaculate to crash itself, losing an extra 5i, but at least it denies it to the air aspect as a crash bonus.<br /> <br /> Air defends with 4m full excellency<br /> <br /> Earth rolls 16 dice against an evasion of 11, scoring 10 and missing<br /> =========<br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> Air Dragon uses 5m Wind Dragon Speed to flurry a decisive attack with a disengage.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon uses 6m full excellency, Earth Dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against a parry of 7, getting 10 and hitting. Rolling 14 decisive damage for 5, putting Earth Dragon into his last -1 health level<br /> <br /> Air Dragon disengages with 11 dice and 1 success from Air Dragon, against 4 dice from Earth Dragon rolling 1 total of 10 successes against 5 and disengaging<br /> --------<br /> Earth moves into short range and rushes, rolling 4 dice against 11, scoring 1 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Earth dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against parry 8, getting it with 12, rolling 3 decisive damage for 0<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 4 dice against 11, scoring 3 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 10<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Earth dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against parry 8, getting it with 9, rolling 3 decisive damage for 1, putting Earth into -2s<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon resets to base initiative and closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 2 against 6 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 11<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Earth dragon defends with 6m full excellency. Rolling 17 dice against parry 7, failing with 5<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 0 against 4 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 12<br /> <br /> Air Dragon withering attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Eath Dragon spends 6m to full excellency defense. Rolling 20 dice agasint parry 7, scoring 8 and hitting, rolling 3 dice for 1 damage<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 0 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 13<br /> <br /> Air Dragon withering attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Eath Dragon spends 6m to full excellency defense. Rolling 20 dice agasint parry 7, scoring 9 and hitting, rolling 3 dice for 1 damage<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 1 against 5 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 14<br /> <br /> Air Dragon withering attacks, spending 6m to full excellency, Eath Dragon spends 6m to full excellency defense. Rolling 20 dice agasint parry 7, scoring 9 and hitting, rolling 3 dice for 4 damage, crashing the Earth again<br /> <br /> Air Dragon retreats to medium range<br /> --------<br /> Earth dragon closes to short range and rushes, rolling 3 dice against 11, scoring 0 against 11 and failing<br /> =========<br /> Round 15<br /> <br /> Air Dragon decisive attacks, with 6m full excellency, rolling 17 dice against Earths 6m full excellency parry ot 7, hitting with 8. Scoring 8 damage off of 17 dice, the Air Dragon slays the Earth<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And there we go. It turns out that facing off against an Air Immaculate who has 5 dex and a -0 mobility penalty really sucks when you've got 3 dex and a -2 mobility penalty. That was even assuming that the Air Dragon didn't also have any athletics charms, which is probably a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give the poor dude an Elemental Bolt at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T12:55:58-07:00","id":1310091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310087#post1310087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I gave BOTH sides artifacts, and if your style is giving you an Evasion bonus you either invest as much into Dodge as you do your MA ability or else waste those bonuses, since otherwise your parry won\u2019t even keep up with your dodge.<br /> <br /> Not doing that is like running a Silver Voiced Nightingale stylist who decided that Performance was cool to leave at 4 with no excellency, or a Black claw stylist who didn\u2019t feel the need to invest into Manipulation or Presence.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon doesn\u2019t really care, it doesn\u2019t dodge, or disengage, or use performance attacks so you can afford to just leave it. I could have given the Earth Dragon a bunch of rush charms, that could have helped, but now I\u2019m building to counter air specifically, and you can\u2019t build to counter every enemy. Where as giving air evasion is just building to complement your own MA, which is good in every scenario.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon loves disengaging and keeping away from its enemy so it can abuse the fact that it\u2019s one of the very few ranged Martial Arts, if you want to use it, use it for what its good at.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also if this battle could have taken place in difficult terrain, or in the dark, or both, if it did it would have been even more one sided.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, it\u2019s quite amazing how the form weapons and armor for each style can affect the combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &gt;You can't build to counter every enemy<br /> &gt;Air Dragon build is literally designed to hard counter low mobility targets<br /> <br /> Come on now. This was tilted in favor of the Air Dragon from the get go, particularly by the Dex 3 choice on the highest armor against a MA that has no withering boosters whatsoever. Try an unarmed, unarmored Earth Dragon Stylist with good Athletics and Dex and see how that fares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T12:57:01-07:00","id":1310092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310090#post1310090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give the poor dude an Elemental Bolt at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would definitely help, at least then you can fight the Air Dragon at range...admittedly none of your Earth Dragon charms combo with Elemental Bolt, nor can you Rush and attack with it even in a flurry because EBA is simple, and against an air aspect who\u2019s activated her anima power all your ranged attacks against them are -1 to hit. BUT it\u2019s got the smashing tag, and if you use it with thrown you can combo it with charms that try to raise your opponents mobility penalty, so that\u2019s really good. I think that would be an excellent counter to this tactic.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not really Earth vs Air Dragon though, that\u2019s an Earth aspect with a bunch of charms and abilities that don\u2019t combo with his MA charms except to plug a hole in his defences vs an Air Dragon with complementary abilities so ingrained in the style it has multiple charms that just boost those rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T13:51:06-07:00","id":1310100,"title":"","content":"Well, I promised I would have found time to write the Lunar and here I am. I present you Walker-of-the-Sky, a Castless Lunar Jack-of-All-Trade that do... well, he do a lot of things. A little social, a little combat, a lot of mental stuff. The distribution is Physical Tertiary, Mental Primary and Social Secondary. If I'm ever going to play this guy, I'll probably remain Castless until I have brought some Attributes higher (at least Str 3 and Per 4) before going Changing Moon.<br /> <br /> Here the stats.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attributes: Str 2 Dex 4 (favored) Sta 4 / Wits 5 (Favored), Perception 3, Intelligence 4 / Appearance 4, Manipulation 5 (Favored), Charisma 3<br /> <br /> Abilities: Brawl 3, Dodge 3, Presence 3, Occult 3, Socialize 3, Larceny 3, Integrity 3, Survival 1, Stealth 2, Awareness 2, Lore 1, Melee 1<br /> <br /> Castless: Spirit Shape Tyrant Lizard<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> Universal: Chimera Soul Expression (some kind of little pterosaurs for Wing ooooo and Unusual Hide o)<br /> Apparence: Feral Smile Tactic, Subtle Silver Declaration<br /> Charisma: Poised Lion Attitude, Argent Songbird Voice <br /> Dextery: Emerald Grasshopper Form<br /> Intelligence: Penumbra Witch Mastery, Terrestrial Circle Sorcery <br /> Perception: Ever-Wary Fox Technique, Perceiving the Hidden World, Spirit-Rending Fury<br /> Stamina: Impenetrable Beast Armor, Ox-Body Technique<br /> Strenght: Towering Beast Form, Grizzly Bear Embrace<br /> Wits: Resisting the Lure Madness<br /> <br /> Specialties: Brawl natural weapons, Occult Elementals, Dodge unarmored.<br /> <br /> Merits: Danger Sense, Fleet of Foot, Heart Blood (oo, +o)<br /> <br /> STATS<br /> Resolve 4<br /> Guile 4<br /> Parry 4<br /> Soak 4<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All the bonus points went in Manipulation and Dextery.<br /> <br /> As you can see, I played with the Character Creation rules to have the most of it, for example using the Tyrant Lizard Spirit Shape to grab Towering Beast Form using Stamina. He should have all the Excellency, even if the Strenght one is really not coming up that often.<br /> <br /> In battle, he's mostly going with the most appropriate form (usually a bear or a great cat) and using that to maul people. He don't have a lot of tricks since it's a fresh Chargen character, and there were a lot of Charms I'd like to give him but couldn't. Like some Manipulation Charm, the one to shapeshift reflexively etc.<br /> <br /> So, how want to use this to see how a Lunar just Exalted and not really combat focused or optimized manage against the Core Adversaries? Of course, with Heart Blood, he could assume a lot of shapes, but I want to know how he fare using only his Spirit Shape.<br /> <br /> Oh, this is kind of the first character I ever made on Exalted, so if I did something wrong tell me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T14:22:22-07:00","id":1310104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310091#post1310091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &gt;You can't build to counter every enemy<br /> &gt;Air Dragon build is literally designed to hard counter low mobility targets<br /> <br /> Come on now. This was tilted in favor of the Air Dragon from the get go, particularly by the Dex 3 choice on the highest armor against a MA that has no withering boosters whatsoever. Try an unarmed, unarmored Earth Dragon Stylist with good Athletics and Dex and see how that fares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay,<i> let's</i>.<br /> <br /> Earth Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.