e with Excellent Strike; it may ignore up to (Essence) points of armor soak.<br /> <br /> <u>Speed of Light</u><br /> Cost: 1m per success; Mins: Essence 1; Type: Supplemental Keywords: None Duration: Instant<br /> Quick as a flash, Sunbeam\u2019s wielder may double up to (Essence or 5, whichever is lower) 8's or 9\u2019s on their Join Battle roll.<br /> <br /> <u>Razor of The Sun</u><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 2; Type: Supplemental Keywords: None Duration: One scene. Prerequisite Charms: Cutting Edge<br /> Light pours through any crack, no matter how small. This Charm supplements a successful attack made with Cutting Edge; Sunbeam\u2019s Overwhelm value against that opponent is increased by (Essence) for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Edge of Morning Sunlight</u><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Melee 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Razor Of The Sun<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Cutting Edge is broken OP. 1m for 3 soak negated, every attack? And Speed of Light is the most efficient JB booster in the game at 1m per 1 success. <br /> <br /> Razor of the Sun is ok enough, Overwhelm *ISNT a terribly op mechanic especially for Single Pointers. You didnt include the text of Edge of Morning Sunlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":".  I 05-09-2019, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T17:26:32-07:00","id":1310846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310836#post1310836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cutting Edge is broken OP. 1m for 3 soak negated, every attack? And Speed of Light is the most efficient JB booster in the game at 1m per 1 success.<br /> <br /> Razor of the Sun is ok enough, Overwhelm is a terribly op mechanic especially for Single Pointers. You didnt include the text of Edge of Morning Sunlight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's actually very tame for an Evocation. It's not 1m, it's 4m since it needs Excellent Strike, and it only ignores 3 soak. Hell, a Piercing Attack can ignore more than that, and it's a mundane thing you can just do as a mortal. This is magic you're paying 10 XP for, in a five dot Daiklave. I'd say it's stupid weak. Speed of Light is not super reliable but it makes up for it in efficiency, which is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T17:27:11-07:00","id":1310847,"title":"","content":"Tried my own build idea (Laughing Monster Lunar vs a couple of Immaculates), turns out that when you need to take &quot;-1 Defense and give 1i to your opponent every round&quot; or else find a way around an opponent who can easily outmaneuver you while he deals with your friend 1v1, all while making sure NEVER to end up next to said friend AND taking negative Intimacies against him, it ends up shredding just about any duo, not just Immaculates, though they get hit extra hard if they don't have an Air Dragon Stylist around (which can... poke at you and will more than likely be the one targetted first, so even then). Pretty nasty build but it takes investment to pull off. Mainly, you need six Laughing Monster Charms, at least 2-3 Dexterity Defense Charms, preferably 1-3 offensive Dexterity Charms though I didn't use those in this test (I just noticed they would have helped the Lunar), Perception Join Battle boosters, and a bit of good luck. <br /> <br /> It's basically an alpha strike build but whose initiative gets subtracted by 2 then divided by two (but doubles 10s and adds +Intimacy dice) and rolled against two peeps, who then disrupt each other a ton and feed you initiative for free, and then when one of them attacks you you just wombo-combo Agile Beast Defense, Fleet Gazelle and Furiously Stalling Destiny along with a stunt (7m 1wp total) to make them miss pretty easily, then use Friendship-Dissolving Poison (you won't crash yourself since you gained 1i from Agile Beast) to redirect the attack against the other opponent and make them hate each other and even fight each other. Unitary Forge Being makes that even easier to accomplish if you can pull it off later on, but they'd need a bunch of Ox Bodies to survive that many Decisive attacks anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T20:51:36-07:00","id":1310908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310836#post1310836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cutting Edge is broken OP. 1m for 3 soak negated, every attack? And Speed of Light is the most efficient JB booster in the game at 1m per 1 success.<br /> <br /> Razor of the Sun is ok enough, Overwhelm is a terribly op mechanic especially for Single Pointers. You didnt include the text of Edge of Morning Sunlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Appreciate the feedback! Speed of Light used to just be 'double up to Essence 9s' on a JB, but that honestly felt pretty meh given that I was still capping it at Essence.<br /> <br /> I've been contemplating capping Cutting Edge some, and I may do that. I did reference Piercing as an ability costing 1i when balancing it, but that initiative might be quite a bit more expensive than I was factoring in. <br /> <br /> Edge of Morning Sunlight is as the normal Solar charm.<br /> <br /> Sunbeam's Charms are strong on purpose, given how much effort my players put into acquiring it and making it out of Orichalcum specifically, but you may be right that it's veering into OP, even more than like...the rest of the build is with Single Point and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","user":"Zeesun","date":". 05-08-2019, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T21:07:54-07:00","id":1310912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310908#post1310908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Appreciate the feedback! Speed of Light used to just be 'double up to Essence 9s' on a JB, but that honestly felt pretty meh given that I was still capping it at Essence.<br /> <br /> I've been contemplating capping Cutting Edge some, and I may do that. I did reference Piercing as an ability costing 1i when balancing it, but that initiative might be quite a bit more expensive than I was factoring in.<br /> <br /> Edge of Morning Sunlight is as the normal Solar charm.<br /> <br /> Sunbeam's Charms are strong on purpose, given how much effort my players put into acquiring it and making it out of Orichalcum specifically, but you may be right that it's veering into OP, even more than like...the rest of the build is with Single Point and all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's really not more expensive. 1i and 1m are equivalent to each other in terms of efficiency. And these Evocations imo are not really five-dot Artifact material, if anything they're 3-dot Evocations (directly enhance the user's capabilities without veering too much into the blatantly supernatural until getting to the final Evocations). Nerfing them further would pretty much make the investment very undesirable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T22:20:59-07:00","id":1310924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310229#post1310229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the idea was to put Earth Dragon into a -2 wound penalty, which would have meant that she gets to roll 5 dice against Air Dragon's 11 on every roll to rush or oppose a disengage, tosses out full excellency'd decisives at 13 dice against an Evasion of 8, and effectively gives our withering attacks +2 raw damage from threshold successes. Air Dragon has no useful decisive enhancers besides the excellency, so she'd have needed to build at least 24 initiative to have an over 80% chance for a killing blow, which would've taken her 5 successful attacks on average at OWV 3. 5 turns is just way too many opportunities for the Athletics excellency's exploding 10s to do something unexpected and cause her to get stuck in melee with a tetsubo-flinging maniac.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very true, but you're assuming Air Dragon gets stuck when the Air gets into melee, and that isn't necessarily true. Since you have a turn of warning before Earth catches up by succeeding a rush, you can take a full defense. If you haven't been using your excellency on your high accuracy attacks, which you shouldn't be except maybe 1m for the excellency effect, you should have enough motes to full excellency your defense as well when they close to attack. At THAT point, Earth doesn't stand a fantastic chance of hitting you with the tetsubo. Even if they do hit you though, if you've been building up initiative while burying them, they're not going to change the turn order, so you then do a standard flurry of rise from prone and disengage once more, getting a free success on the disengage.<br /> <br /> Of course if Earth does miss that one attack, then the next round Air is going to Wind Dragon and flurry an attack with a disengage again.<br /> <br /> And all of THAT is assuming that you're just fighting duels in Exalted, which I think only ever happened once in our group since we started playing 3e. In group combats the ability to disengage and just sit outside of the melee while keeping your max accuracy attack and not having to waste a turn disengaging is pretty good. Then again maybe nobody plays exalted the way my group does, I have no idea. I've been shocked before by people saying that their circle of Solars god wiped out by a bunch of mortal hunters using no special tactics, and I can't imagine how that happened<br /> <br /> Either way I am absolutely sick to death of discussing Fire and Air Dragon styles, I do look forward to you pitting Water and Wood up against Bloodapes though. I suspect that Water won't do very well if she wins join battle and starts out with a decisive attack. If it can't kill an ape she has to muscle through 8 attacks in a row before she gets to go again, and I don't see that happening without a ton of luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T23:03:09-07:00","id":1310929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310908#post1310908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Appreciate the feedback! Speed of Light used to just be 'double up to Essence 9s' on a JB, but that honestly felt pretty meh given that I was still capping it at Essence.<br /> <br /> I've been contemplating capping Cutting Edge some, and I may do that. I did reference Piercing as an ability costing 1i when balancing it, but that initiative might be quite a bit more expensive than I was factoring in.<br /> <br /> Edge of Morning Sunlight is as the normal Solar charm.<br /> <br /> Sunbeam's Charms are strong on purpose, given how much effort my players put into acquiring it and making it out of Orichalcum specifically, but you may be right that it's veering into OP, even more than like...the rest of the build is with Single Point and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a cap-bursting join battle enhancer it's pretty cheap at 1m for up to (Essence) non-charm successes. It also has some overlap with Sensory Acuity Prana. Even if it added (Essence) non-charm dice instead that would be a lot closer to a good balance, I think.<br /> <br /> Cutting Edge is probably fine as it is though. There's a crap ton of enemies in Exalted that don't even have armor, so it's not useful at all times. I might change it to higher of (Essence or 3), again not that it matters for your guy. Also don't forget that Piercing attacks cost 1i and lower your defense until your next turn as well, but I still think it's reasonably balanced for 1m.<br /> <br /> Of course on the other hand he's an Essence 3 Dawn with Thunderbolt Attack Prana, Melee and Single Point so balance is more or less up to you coming up with some insane BS to throw down anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T23:52:21-07:00","id":1310937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310924#post1310924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do look forward to you pitting Water and Wood up against Bloodapes though. I suspect that Water won't do very well if she wins join battle and starts out with a decisive attack. If it can't kill an ape she has to muscle through 8 attacks in a row before she gets to go again, and I don't see that happening without a ton of luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Water's actually done now - she did Quite Well but not Earth Dragon well. The two-opponent setup did force her to forgo the strategy her style actually wants her to use, but I think it's a testament to the style's power that she managed to soldier through without even activating her Form. (Expect a detailed writeup later.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T07:41:06-07:00","id":1310976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310937#post1310937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Water's actually done now - she did Quite Well but not Earth Dragon well. The two-opponent setup did force her to forgo the strategy her style actually wants her to use, but I think it's a testament to the style's power that she managed to soldier through without even activating her Form. (Expect a detailed writeup later.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that\u2019s good. Wood probably won\u2019t end up activating their form either just because the reflexive condition is so hard and it\u2019s not really that great at lower essence anyway. Wood Dragon Vitality and Eyes of the Wood Dragon might carry it through, but with only light armor WDV is going to drain motes fast and since Blood Apes don\u2019t wear armor the piercing effect isn\u2019t helpful. Soul Marking Style is going to be a risky venture too, you really want a friend around if you\u2019re going to be doing something like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is all making me want to run a game where every player is an Immaculate and they go around navigating the politics of spirit courts and wrestling hungry ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T10:09:11-07:00","id":1311242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310929#post1310929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a cap-bursting join battle enhancer it's pretty cheap at 1m for up to (Essence) non-charm successes. It also has some overlap with Sensory Acuity Prana. Even if it added (Essence) non-charm dice instead that would be a lot closer to a good balance, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it; do you mean 1m for 1 non-Charm dice? In essence (pun...not intended), turning it into exclusively a cap-breaker?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310929#post1310929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cutting Edge is probably fine as it is though. There's a crap ton of enemies in Exalted that don't even have armor, so it's not useful at all times. I might change it to higher of (Essence or 3), again not that it matters for your guy. Also don't forget that Piercing attacks cost 1i and lower your defense until your next turn as well, but I still think it's reasonably balanced for 1m.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you think so! It's limited applicability was very much by design, and I like your proposed modification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310929#post1310929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course on the other hand he's an Essence 3 Dawn with Thunderbolt Attack Prana, Melee and Single Point so balance is more or less up to you coming up with some insane BS to throw down anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny. On account of his Resistance Supernal he's really focused in on popping Single Point, using Essence-Gathering Temper to keep mote economy up, and layering on scene-longs that give him compounding combat advantage that lets him just -equalize- stuff. With Pain Tolerance and 4 Ox-bodies, wound penalties don't -really- slow him down that, that much either. I don't know if he understands the amount of outrageous Doomcombo murder he could inflict if he really wants to, but since I, as his Storyteller wouldn't like it as much if he just instagibbed everything* instead of being a nigh-unkillable implacable death-machine of dramatic tension, I'm not complaining!<br /> <br /> <br /> *Admittedly, though, at the risk of being left super vulnerable if the combo didn't do enough to swing the fight in his favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","user":"Zeesun","date":". 05-10-2019, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T11:18:28-07:00","id":1311252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1310796#post1310796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Razor of The Sun</u><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 2; Type: Supplemental Keywords: None Duration: One scene. Prerequisite Charms: Cutting Edge<br /> <br /> Light pours through any crack, no matter how small. This Charm supplements a successful attack made with Cutting Edge; Sunbeam\u2019s Overwhelm value against that opponent is increased by (Essence) for the remainder of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this supposed to work? It says it supplements a successful attack and it's suplemental so RAW you'd have to announce it before you roll the attack, is it supposed to work like that and do nothing if you miss?<br /> <br /> If you want to be able to activate it after successfully hitting I think you need to make it Reflexive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T11:20:22-07:00","id":1311253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1311252#post1311252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is this supposed to work? It says it supplements a successful attack and it's suplemental so RAW you'd have to announce it before you roll the attack, is it supposed to work like that and do nothing if you miss?<br /> <br /> If you want to be able to activate it after successfully hitting I think you need to make it Reflexive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T16:26:35-07:00","id":1311450,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, 3e charms which don\u2019t need to be declared in advance all specifically say that and when they can be activated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T19:28:37-07:00","id":1311479,"title":"","content":"When's the Water Bender fight coming out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T03:04:42-07:00","id":1311536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1311479#post1311479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When's the Water Bender fight coming out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have time to write it up today, if everything goes well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T10:35:55-07:00","id":1311815,"title":"","content":"Terribly sorry for the delay, I had some stuff to take care of. Let us proceed, shall we?<br /> <br /> Water Immaculate:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attributes: Str 3 Dex 5 Sta 3 | Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Water Dragon 5, Awareness 4, Athletics 4, Brawl 3<br /> Charms:<br /> Water Dragon: Flowing Water Defense, Rippling Water Strike, Drowning-in-Blood Technique, Shrugging Water-Dragon Escape, Water Dragon Form, Theft-of-Essence Method<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer, Blade-Deflecting Palm<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique<br /> <br /> Another very conservative spread. A 2/4/5 spread probably lets you play to your style\u2019s strengths quite a bit more \u2013 with an in-form base soak of 15 and the option to layer another +5 on top via Impervious Skin of Stone without ruining your Aura, you can almost certainly soldier through a sustained assault at base initiative after landing a strike that was meant to wound rather than kill.<br /> <br /> However, you lose out quite a bit in mote efficiency compared to Earth who can wait with the ISoS activation until after she sees the raw damage pool coming her way, and Rippling Water Strike goes from a middling Charm to an outright bad one. Not to mention that you already have very effective ways to avoid being hit altogether between Flowing Water Defense and Blade-Deflecting Palm, which means that pre-attack soak boosting is way more likely to result in wasting motes than it is with Earth Dragon and her Parry 2.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The combat:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> It\u2019s actually not super important for Water Dragon to win Join Battle \u2013 she has a very good chance to weather an all-out assault from two apes between Flowing Water Defense and Blade-Deflecting Palm enhancing her defenses beyond the excellency, so dropping an opponent right out of the gate is less of a priority for her than it was for the other combatants. Nevertheless, 4m is hardly preposterous for what could be a significant advantage, so she buys two auto-successes and rolls another six for a total of 11i. The apes roll 1 and 4, respectively.<br /> <br /> TURN 1<br /> Water Dragon at 11i, Ape #2 at 7, Ape #1 at 4.<br /> <br /> She rushes in and attacks Ape #1 in the hopes of getting a crash, using Flowing Water Defense and 1m on the excellency. Since we\u2019re not in Aura, Rippling Water Strike would only get us +2 raw damage, which is quite terrible, so we\u2019re holding it back despite the fact that our opponent is very close to getting crashed. Our anima goes up to glowing, and we\u2019re entering Water Aura at the end of the turn.<br /> <br /> 14 dice roll 5 successes for a rather pathetic 4 post-soak damage, of which only a single die comes up as a success. We are <i>so</i> not getting a crash.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 flurries, but we\u2019re at a base parry of 8 after stunt so we don\u2019t even need to spend motes on enhancing defense. First attack misses with 2 successes, second scores 6 and still misses against our post-onslaught parry of 7. Ain\u2019t Flowing Water Defense grand?<br /> <br /> Ape #1 also launches a flurry. We don\u2019t want him to get further away from crash, so we spend 2m on the excellency, bringing us up to Parry 7 once more. He rolls 6 successes and misses, vindicating our investment immediately. We\u2019re spending another 4m on keeping Parry 7 up for the second attack, but we\u2019re proven to be over-cautious when he fails with a 4.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, no anima.<br /> <br /> TURN 2<br /> Water Dragon at 13i, ape #2 at 7, ape #1 at 3.<br /> <br /> <i>Now </i>we get to unleash Rippling Water Strike! We also spend 5m on FWD + the excellency for a total mote expenditure of 10, bringing us immediately up to bonfire. This proves to be tremendously useless because we get no damage out of it and our free bonfire effect doesn\u2019t help in this situation at all, but hey, at least we look cool.<br /> <br /> Attack roll hits with 10 successes against a parry of 4, bringing us up to an absolutely disgusting post-soak damage pool of 14 dice, of which we get 5 successes. Ape #1 is crashed.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 attempts another flurry and fails against an un-excellency\u2019d parry twice, with 4 and 3 successes respectively.<br /> <br /> Ape #1 tries to claw himself back to relevance, but he fails with exactly 6 successes against the 2m excellency just like last time, then once again with 5 vs 7 for good measure.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, anima does nothing useful.<br /> <br /> TURN 3<br /> Water Dragon at 24i, ape #2 at 7, ape #1 at -2<br /> <br /> Water Dragon goes for the killing blow with Flowing Water Defense against a post-reset PoM double tap, 5m on the excellency to offset FWD\u2019s attack roll penalty, and Drowning-in-Blood Technique. Ape spends a willpower, but she still manages to roll 6 successes vs a Parry of 5, landing an absolutely brutal 24 dice of damage with double 10s and rerolling 6s on the demon for a total of 13 damage, a score so high it would\u2019ve killed a mortal twice over. Ape #1 is extremely dead.<br /> <br /> Ape #2 flurries! First attack misses, but the second scores exactly 7 successes against Parry 7. Fifteen base damage would result in 7 post-soak damage dice, which is enough to crash her right out of the gate on an average roll, so she figures that using Blade-Deflecting Palm to force 2 rerolls is a good use of her remaining intiative \u2013 after all, she can still just pump a max excellency and, if needed, a Willpower into her defense on the next two attacks. Sadly, the two dice come up as 9 and 8, respectively \u2013 the hit still goes through!<br /> <br /> 7 damage dice roll 4 successes, vindicating our previous thought process, but moral certainty is cold comfort in initiative crash. And the ape has two more attacks to launch\u2026<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux rolls a single success, changing precious little.<br /> <br /> TURN 4<br /> Ape #2 at 16i, Water Dragon at -3.<br /> <br /> Another PoM flurry! Normally, if I was in a position to attack an opponent who\u2019s sitting on -2 onslaught and is crashed, I\u2019d attempt a grapple, but 8d against a pre-excellency parry of 6 is way too dicey. So ape #2 will just go with another withering. Water Dragon spends 2m to bring her Parry up to 7, but the ape rolls exactly 7 successes once more, and now we can\u2019t even use BDP because we\u2019re crashed. 7 post-soak damage dice produce 7 successes, painfully enough.<br /> <br /> Confident in his ability to kill or maim with 24i, ape #2 launches a decisive as his second attack. Water Dragon spends 4m 1WP to bring her Parry up to 8. The ape misses with 3 successes; how anticlimactic.<br /> <br /> Since she\u2019s unlikely to turn this around with a single attack, Water Dragon spends 4m on FWD and 1 on the excellency \u2013 it\u2019s better for her to steadily raise her initiative and slowly chip away at the ape\u2019s in the hope that she can shoot for an initiative shift later, rather than trying to go all-out on offense and risk barely crawling out of crash without actually crashing the ape. 13d begets 8 successes, for a total of 7 post-soak, which yields 4 damage.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, flux rolls a 10, battering the ape some more.<br /> <br /> TURN 5<br /> Ape #2 at 14i, Water Dragon at -5.<br /> <br /> Out of willpower with which he could fuel PoM and seeing his window of opportunity pass, the demon goes for another withering attack against Water Dragon\u2019s Parry of 8. At this point, I realize that FWD on the previous attack was overkill \u2013 when you face two incoming attacks, it has better returns than the excellency, effectively giving you 4m\u2019s worth of enhancement against both attacks (and the attack penalty is irrelevant against a blood ape when you\u2019re not trying to shoot for big damage from threshold successes), but with only 1 attack, you\u2019re effectively eating the -3 attack penalty for no good reason, since anything above Parry 8 has strongly diminishing returns. My analysis is proven correct when the ape fails to connect with yet another hit, rolling 5 successes this time.<br /> <br /> Water Dragon tosses Rippling Water Strike and a 1m excellency on her attack, and unfettered by a FWD attack penalty, rolls 8 successes. 12 post-soak damage dice turn up 8 successes \u2013 this means no initiative shift for us.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, no flux damage.<br /> <br /> TURN 6<br /> Ape #2 at 6i, Water Dragon at 4.<br /> <br /> Ape launches a withering attack against a Parry of 6 and fails to connect. Water Dragon is now in full-on mote conservation mode, relying on Blade-Deflecting Palm to save her ass if necessary. RWS is a very expensive toy.<br /> <br /> Rippling Water Strike and a single mote on the excellency result in an attack roll with 11 successes and 15 post-soak damage, yielding 7 successes and crashing the ape.<br /> <br /> DING DONG NEXT TURN, regen 5, no flux damage<br /> <br /> TURN 7<br /> Water Dragon at 17i, Ape #2 at -1.<br /> <br /> Trusting in Drowning-in-Blood Technique\u2019s ability to cover for the shortcomings of her low-ish damage pool, Water Dragon launches a decisive with 1m on the excellency. She scores 5 successes vs her opponent\u2019s Parry of 3, and gets a bunch of 10s on damage, resulting in a total of 12 health levels of damage dealt. Ape #2 only makes a slightly lesser splat than his predecessor.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Final result: two dead apes and a self-satisfied albeit largely moteless Immaculate.<br /> <br /> Notes:<br /> - Water Dragon\u2019s ability to weather large numbers of attacks with a comparatively low mote expenditure remains very impressive.<br /> - Theft-of-Essence Method\u2019s weakness against spirits is a large black mark on its record: sacrificing most of my gains from a Crash is not terribly attractive when all I\u2019m getting for it is 2 motes while my opponent\u2019s Charm usage is by and large not constrained by Essence expenditure.<br /> - Still, between 3 potent workhorses and two strong tools in Exalt-vs-Exalt combat, Water Dragon might feature the largest number of useful Charms out of the early lineup of all the Immaculate styles.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T22:13:43-07:00","id":1313442,"title":"","content":"Thanks especially to DrLoveMonkey for running the 3v1 Deebs vs True (all Melee charms) Invincible Sword Princess Ess1.<br /> <br /> That basically solved in my mind if it was possible to 1v3 at Ess1 vs 3 combat specced Shikari (no, unless you can defeat the second coming of Red Sonya, basically).<br /> <br /> A bit/very late, but also apologies to any that I might have offended. Not my intent, but I love my silver demigods so!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T17:03:25-07:00","id":1313583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1313442#post1313442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That basically solved in my mind if it was possible to 1v3 at Ess1 vs 3 combat specced Shikari (no, unless you can defeat the second coming of Red Sonya, basically).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't necessarily say that it's totally impossible, but I wouldn't count on it. You'd need one of the best combat builds and play it pretty perfectly with a little luck. I wouldn't consider even a combat characters inability to do it reliably at chargen as some kind of failure.<br /> <br /> On the other hand consider that not only was the ISP Essence 2 in that scenario, and I also cheated on behalf of the Solar and used Hungry Tiger Technique on a non-crashed target, which isn't allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T20:38:05-07:00","id":1313610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1313583#post1313583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't necessarily say that it's totally impossible, but I wouldn't count on it. You'd need one of the best combat builds and play it pretty perfectly with a little luck. I wouldn't consider even a combat characters inability to do it reliably at chargen as some kind of failure.<br /> <br /> On the other hand consider that not only was the ISP Essence 2 in that scenario, and I also cheated on behalf of the Solar and used Hungry Tiger Technique on a non-crashed target, which isn't allowed.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a low Ess Solar, you pretty much stacked the deck entirely in ISP\u2019s favour. So, no complaint at all there.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s your take on 2v1, just curious (no need to run the combat of course, goodness!)<br /> <br /> Prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T22:23:20-07:00","id":1313622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1313610#post1313610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a low Ess Solar, you pretty much stacked the deck entirely in ISP\u2019s favour. So, no complaint at all there.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s your take on 2v1, just curious (no need to run the combat of course, goodness!)<br /> <br /> Prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>Against ISP? I'd put my money on the ISP almost every time. Barring something stupid like both DBs having Dragons Unfailing Vigor and Fathomless Depths Replenishment that they boost to the max every morning.<br /> <br /> The ISP simply has so much power that they can kill a DB right off the hop, and then it's just basement tier exalt vs ceiling tier exalt. Doing the same with a Lunar is a bit more risky because they don't have the same kind of Invincible Fury of the Dawn, Fivefold Fury Onslaught or whatever, but they do have explosive bear grapples and stuff that can do similar things. One on one almost no DB can beat a combat focused celestial reliably. Even at Essence 5 a DB is probably not beating a young celestial.<br /> <br /> The same thing happens to a lesser extent if you make the DBs Essence 1 or 2. Essence 2 to 3 for Dragonblooded is the biggest power jump in the game right now, probably will be forever, and if you took that away it would go a lot more from a fair fight to favoring the ISP. Signature charms and charms like Cloud Riot and PCD are just huge boons. As long as they're young DBs you could almost definitely take 3 of them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually I just ran the first 4 rounds of that same combat except with depowered DBs at Essence 2, and it wasn't as easy as I thought. Some reasonably bad rolling meant the Wood aspect didn't die in the first round, and it looks like the Solar might eventually win, but it's really hard, the DBs are regenerating 15 per round to attack with and the Solar needs to defend against those 3 while trying to launch attacks back. To do this more fairly the DBs would need to lose the artifacts I think, and every DB antagonist in the book has full artifacts so I'm not sure if that's reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-22-2019, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T14:11:43-07:00","id":1314371,"title":"","content":"So aluminiumtrioxid's immaculate fights made me wonder how well a non-immaculate Dragon Blooded martial artist would actually stack up. It'd be a bit rude to go from lurking to asking someone to do more work on my behalf, so I took a crack at running things myself. I've got to say that I hadn't appreciated quite how time consuming running an unfamiliar character and their opponents through a fight can be, so thanks to everyone in the thread for all your efforts. That out of the way, here's the details:<br /> <br /> Steel Devil Stylist:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Aspect: Water<br /> Attributes: Str 3 Dex 5 Sta 3 / Wits 4<br /> Abilities: Steel Devil 5, Awareness 4, Brawl 4<br /> Charms:<br /> Steel Devil: Naked Fang Draw, Double Attack Technique, Steel Devil Strike, Steel Devil Form, Dual-Slaying Stance, Empty Mind Strike<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer, Blade Deflecting Palm<br /> Resistance: 2 x Ox-Body Technique<br /> Equipment: Medium Armour, Dual Straight Swords<br /> <br /> Starting out with one of the more maligned martial arts, but also one that is suited to fighting opponents without sky high defenses. Standard stat spread and all of the Steel Devil charms went in first. Naked fang draw means you don't need the awareness excellency so you don't have to pick between the second Ox-body and Blade Deflecting Palm. All in all, pretty vanilla.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The fight:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Join Battle:<br /> Blood Ape 1 gets 8, Blood Ape 2 gets 5 and the Steel Devil stylist uses Naked Fang Draw to get 11. The Steel Devil's anima raises one level and she gains one off hand charge, but I opt against transferring any initiative just to hedge against poor early rolls.<br /> <br /> Round One:<br /> BA 1 8i, BA 2 5i, SD 11i<br /> The Steel Devil opens with a full excellency to build anima, avoiding Double Attack Technique because with the Terrestrial keyword it doesn't break even yet. Targeting BA 1 she inflicts 10 damage, crashing him and given the much more comfortable buffer she adds two to her offhand charge.<br /> BA 1 Attacks twice and the second scores what would have been a hit, but Blade Deflecting Palm turns it into a miss.<br /> BA 2 Attacks twice and this time the Steel Devil uses their excellency to up their parry to 6.(2m on the first attack, 4m on the second) The first attack would have landed, but once again Blade Deflecting Palm does it's job.<br /> <br /> Round Two:<br /> BA 1 8i, BA 2 -5i, SD 23i<br /> Steel Devil goes for another full excellency in order to hit bonfire, targeting BA 1. She only inflicts 4 initiative damage, one of which she transfers to off hand charge.<br /> BA 1 Attacks twice both of which miss by one.<br /> BA 2 Attacks twice with Steel Devil once again maintaining a Parry of 6. The second attack needs BDP to stop it, but neither hit.<br /> <br /> Round Three:<br /> BA 1 4i, BA 2 -5i, SD 26i<br /> Steel Devil's Anima does no damage.<br /> She uses 3 motes on her excellency this time and adds Double Attack Technique in her attack against BA 1. She inflicts 9 damage to crash him and immediately follows up with a Steel Devil Strike. This lands essentially automatically due to onslaught but only inflicts 2 decisive damage from 9 dice.<br /> BA 1 is at -1 wound penalty. He attacks twice and the first attacks hits with two threshold successes, so BDP can't help. However he only manages to inflict 2 withering damage.<br /> BA 2 Attacks twice (Blah blah, Parry 6) BDP once again makes it no hits.<br /> <br /> Round Four:<br /> BA 1 -2i, BA 2 -5i, SD 29i<br /> Steel Devil's Anima inflicts one more decisive damage on BA 1<br /> She tries to hit BA 2 with a decisive attack, feeling that she still have enough motes to prevent any initiative shift form BA 1 and wanting to prevent an initiative reset. She uses a single excellency die to get rerolled 6s, but he spends willpower int increase his parry and it pays off as she ends up one short with 4 successes.<br /> BA 1 attacks twice and misses both times.<br /> BA 2 attacks twice(Parry 6), but once again the best he can do is force one use of BDP.<br /> <br /> Round Five:<br /> BA -2i, BA 2 -5i, SD 29i<br /> Steel Devil's Anima hits BA 1 again bring him down to his last -1 health level<br /> She's reached the end of her mote pool, having only the 5 mote drip but the blood apes are reaching the end of their willpower with BA 1 having the last point left between them. As BA 2 can only make one attack and will reset and become ineligible for initiative shift she instead targets BA 1 with her second decisive attack. BA 1 spends willpower, but this time Steel Devil gets 10 successes. She inflicts 10 decisive damage and BA 1 goes down.<br /> BA 2 resets to base initiative and attacks using Brutal Ape Pounce because why not at this point? It rolls a 6 which misses due lack of onslaught.<br /> <br /> Round Six:<br /> BA 1 DEAD, BA 2 3i, SD 3i<br /> Steel Devil's anima role's a 10 and inflicts 2 withering damage on BA 2.<br /> She throws 1 Excellency die and a Double attack technique at him. This hits by 10 and inflicts 5 damage to crash BA 2 a second time. Steel devil ups her offhand charge by 2.<br /> BA 2 misses once again with 6 successes.<br /> <br /> Round Seven:<br /> BA 2 -4i, SD 12i<br /> Steel Devil's Anima has no effect<br /> The Dragon blood repeats her attack from last turn and only just hits with 4 successes. However she goes on to get 5 successes from 5 dice.<br /> BA 2 finally manages to roll 7 success, but blade deflecting palm once again turns the attack into a miss.<br /> <br /> Round Eight:<br /> BA 2 -9i, SD 17i<br /> Anima once again does nothing<br /> Steel Devil uses the same attack for a third time and this time inflicts 11 initiative damage. Using the few motes she's been saving she fires off an empty mind strike which automatically hits and inflicts 2 decisive damage from 6 dice.<br /> BA 2 attacks and botches. Given what's coming next round I don't both inflicting a penalty.<br /> <br /> Round Nine,<br /> BA 2 -20i, SD 29i<br /> Anima inflicts 1 damage<br /> Steel Devil's decisive attack inflicts 11. BA 2 dies<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So... mote tapped or not the Steel Devil won pretty comfortably, taking a single hit and always being ahead on initiative. However, a lot of that was the combination of Blade Deflecting Palm with medium weapons which seems pretty damn effective. The Blood Apes would have been a lot more threatening with stunt bonuses, but a big part of that would have been mitigated with a specialty so I'm prepared to call it a wash as part of the scenario.<br /> <br /> I tried to take advantage of Steel Devil Strike and Empty Mind strike, but I think it's fair to say that they didn't make a major difference on this occasion. I can see that they could make a big difference, but that wasn't how the dice fell today. Double Attack Technique with Terrestrial takes some build up before it's useful but it did help. Neither of the Forms got used as I went straight for the attack. I don't think Steel Devil Form would have helped much, a turn wouldn't have been worth the few motes saved or the extra Offhand Charge pool size we never filled, but at some point I'd like revisit and see what happens if you open with Dual-Slaying Stance and sit on the flat +2 Parry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","user":"Speedbump","date":".  Typos, typos everywhere 05-26-2019, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T21:36:39-07:00","id":1340725,"title":"","content":"I was wondering the past few days if I could do this thing, and finally get a win where a Solar kills 3 DBs. I also wanted to know how badly DBs performed if they were E2 instead of E3, so I rolled it all out and...Well I did it, at long last, or I basically did anyway. I don't know if anyone at all cares but I did all this work for myself anyway so I figured I might as well post it. Starting the fight off with heaven Sword Flash, combo'd with Thunderbolt Attack Prana, I basically killed three Essence 2 DBs with two ox-bodies each in a single turn.<br /> Characters<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Solar max everything</b><br /> <br /> Daiklave 14 (Damage 17/5)<br /> Parry 7<br /> Soak/Hardness 17/10<br /> <br /> Resources: 45m (56) 10wp<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Swordsman</b><br /> 5/3/3<br /> <br /> Grand Daiklave 10 (Damage 19/6)<br /> Parry 5<br /> Soak/Hardness 15/10<br /> <br /> Resources 33m (44) 5wp<br /> <br /> <b>Brawler</b><br /> 4/4/4<br /> <br /> Smashfists 15 (Damage 14/3)<br /> Parry 5<br /> Soak/Hardness 12/7<br /> Resources 34m (44) 5wp<br /> <br /> <b>Bowman</b><br /> 3/5/3<br /> <br /> Powerbow 15 (Damage 15/4)<br /> Dodge 6<br /> Soak/Hardness 8/3<br /> Resources 35m (44) 5wp<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight 2<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Roll Join Battle<br /> <br /> Solar will use full excellency and Sensory Acuity Prana for 15m<br /> All DBs excellency for 2 successes<br /> <br /> Solar: 30m 10wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar gets 12 for 15 initiative<br /> Sword gets 2 for 7<br /> Brawl gets 8 for 13<br /> Bow gets 2 for 7<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar acts first and uses:<br /> <br /> 7m 1wp Heaven Sword Flash<br /> 1wp Perfect Strike Discipline<br /> 3m Excellent Strike<br /> 3m Fire and Stones Strike<br /> 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana<br /> <br /> Solar: 13m 7wp<br /> Bow: 31m 5wp<br /> <br /> Attacks with 23 dice getting 10, rerolling three 1s and also getting a straight to activate 1m Rising Sun Slash. Ending up with a total of 14 successes, enough to max out fire and stones.<br /> <br /> Rolling 18 damage dice for 7, doubling to 14 and killing both close range DBs. Solar resets to base 4 initiative.<br /> <br /> Solar: 12m 7wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar now uses reflexive movement to close to range with archer, and uses Peony Blossom Attack 1m 1wp, with Perfect Strike Discipline 1wp. DB will defend with max dodge excellency, raising defense to 10 with stunt.<br /> <br /> Solar: 11m 5wp<br /> Bow: 25m 5wp<br /> <br /> Solar rolls 26 dice, getting 10 and just hitting. Dealing only 1 withering damage. Solar will now reflexively activate Invincible Fury of the Dawn 5m 1wp, enhanced with Thunderbolt Attack Prana 4m 1wp, and 2 dice into Fire and Stones Strike. Dividing initiative up 1/1/1/4/4. DB will enhance only last 2 with full excellency and Wood anima power, for 15m.<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 3wp<br /> Bow: 10m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar gets 3 for attack one<br /> Solar gets 5 for attack two, but can't penetrate hardness<br /> Solar gets 10 for attack three, but can't penetrate hardness<br /> Solar gets 5 for attack four, and misses<br /> Solar gets 6 for attack five, and hits by 1. Rolling 5 damage for 2, doubling to 4, putting Bow into solid -1s.<br /> <br /> Solar resets to 3i as Peony Blossom stopped the bonfire anima power. Bow is at 6i<br /> ---------<br /> Bow will attempt to disengage, and will enhance with 5m from excellency, Solar can not enhance.<br /> <br /> Rolls 15 dice for 7. Solar rolls 11 dice for 3. Bow disengages<br /> <br /> Solar 5m 3wp 3i<br /> Bow 10m 5wp 4i<br /> =========<br /> Bow attacks with a withering shot, Solar will not raise parry to defend. Bow rolls 14 dice against parry 7, getting 8, but with two 1s and 2s the Solar will cancel the attack with Hail Shattering Practice. Bow reflexively moves to Medium Range.<br /> ---------<br /> Solar moves to short with Bow, who then reflexively retreats to medium as-per Disengage. Solar uses full defense<br /> <br /> Solar 8m 3wp 3i<br /> Bow 15m 5wp 4i<br /> ========<br /> Bow will aim at Solar<br /> ---------<br /> Solar will close to short and rush, activating Lightning Speed 3m and 2m Excellency. Bow will not use motes to defend.<br /> <br /> Solar rolls 13 dice for 4, rerolling 3 for a total of 7. Bow rolls 8 dice for 5 and fails.<br /> <br /> Solar 8m 3wp 3i<br /> Bow 20m 5wp 4i<br /> =======<br /> Bow will make a withering attack against the Solar with 6m full excellency and 2m Spring Follows Winter. Solar will defend with 2m excellency<br /> <br /> Bow rolls 23 dice for 19 to hit, Solar can not Hail Shatter this. 8 over Parry bow rolls 9 damage for 4, crashing the Solar<br /> <br /> Solar 7m 3wp -1i<br /> Bow 13m 5wp 14i<br /> -------<br /> Solar closes to close range, withering with Excellent Strike for 3m, and 3m into Fire and Stones Strike. Bow will defend with 6m full excellency and 3m<br /> <br /> Solar rolls 15 dice against dodge of 9 for 7, no rerolls, missing by 2. Bow activates Hopping Firecracker Evasion for 3m 2i and escapes to Medium range.<br /> <br /> Solar 5m 3wp -1i<br /> Bow 6m 5wp 12i<br /> =======<br /> Bow will wither Solar, who will not spend motes to defend. Bow rolls 14 dice against parry 7, getting 7, Solar will cancel with Hail Shattering.<br /> <br /> Bow reflexively moves to medium range<br /> ------<br /> Solar will close to short and rush with Lightning Speed for 3m. Bow will not contest with essence<br /> <br /> Solar rolls 11 dice, getting 4, rerolling 2 for 1 more. Bow rolls 8 for 3 and fails<br /> <br /> Solar 6m 3wp -1i<br /> Bow 11m 5wp 12i<br /> =======<br /> Bow takes a full defense action<br /> ------<br /> Solar closes to range and withers with Excellent Strike and 3m excellency. Bow Defends with 6m excellency.<br /> <br /> Solar rolls 17 dice against parry 10, getting 9 with one reroll for no help, missing.<br /> <br /> Solar 5m 3wp -1i<br /> Bow 10m 5wp 11i<br /> =======<br /> Bow will attempt to disengage, Solar will not spend essence to contest. Rolling 10 dice Bow gets an amazing 10 to the Solars also very good 7<br /> -------<br /> Solar will move and attempt to rush with Lightning Speed 3m. Bow will contest with 2m excellency. Solar rolls 11 dice for 7, rerolling 1 for no help, Bow gets 4, failing.<br /> <br /> Solar 8m 3wp 3i<br /> Bow 13m 5wp 9i<br /> =======<br /> <br /> This is going to take forever and the bow user can't really damage the Solar effectively anyway.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> So I'll actually start with the second fight I ran because the first one wasn't satisfying for me, because I missed the first major decisive attack. In this one though, you can see how crazy that first turn was for the Solar. Killed both DBs right off the bat, and then proceeded to get in a lengthy chase game with the bow user until I called it for the Solar. The really crazy thing is, it doesn't matter if there were 2 DBs in there, or 5, or even if they were Lunars or Solar exalted. The only thing that'd let them live is if they'd had 3-4 ox-bodies.<br /> <br /> But is this reasonable? Well the character who has max stats in literally everything isn't, of course, but the actual combo? Totally reasonable. It only needs max dex and melee, TAP, Heavy Sword Flash and a few charms that lead up to HSF. I think this is a totally plausible thing that a PC might do. All I can say is &quot;That's what you get when a Solar spends all his resources in one single turn.&quot; Just about anything near you except for Fair Folk Cataphracts or second circle demons is going to be toast. Just don't get too cocky, if you have this combo and you think you can just go fight the entire Imperial Palace at once you're going to die, or worse. Almost certainly worse.<br /> <br /> As an ST I'd advise against using this on your players though, even if it is somewhat plausible, unless all the people that might be hit by it have 4-5 ox-bodies or something. For one, that up there can just happen and all your PCs are dead, even if they're Solars there isn't much defense, and for another what happened when I FIRST ran the combat could happen, which is this...<br /> <br /> Fight 1<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Roll Join Battle<br /> <br /> Solar will use full excellency and Sensory Acuity Prana for 15m<br /> All DBs excellency for 2 successes<br /> <br /> Solar: 30m 10wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar gets 23 for 26 initiative<br /> Sword gets 2 for 7<br /> Brawl gets 4 for 9<br /> Bow gets 6 for 11<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar acts first and uses:<br /> <br /> 7m 1wp Heaven Sword Flash<br /> 1wp Perfect Strike Discipline<br /> 3m Excellent Strike<br /> 3m Fire and Stones Strike<br /> 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana<br /> <br /> Solar: 13m 7wp 26i<br /> Sword: 29m 5wp 7i<br /> Brawl: 30m 5wp 9i<br /> Bow: 31m 5wp 11i<br /> <br /> <br /> Dragonblooded will full excellency their parry, also stunt, giving 9 parry.<br /> <br /> Attacks with 23 dice getting 7, with no straight, and rerolling two 1s for 1 extra success. Solar misses and loses 3i for missing a decisive.<br /> ---------<br /> Bow fires a withering shot, enhancing with 6m full excellency. Solar will defend with 6m excellency. Bow rolls 21 dice against parry of 10, getting 9, missing<br /> <br /> Solar: 7m 7wp 23i<br /> Sword: 29m 5wp 7i<br /> Brawl: 30m 5wp 9i<br /> Bow: 25m 5wp 11i<br /> ---------<br /> Brawl attempts a grapple gambit with 6m full excellency, 5m Inescapable Whirlpool Hold and 5m Entangling Roots Embrace. Solar will defend with 5m Bulwark Stance and 2m Excellency. Brawl rolls 16 dice against parry 8, getting it with 11.<br /> <br /> Brawl rolls 9 dice to lock in the gambit, getting it with 5.<br /> <br /> Brawl will use 6m full excellency on control roll, Solar is out of motes. Brawl rolls 16 dice and gets 9, rerolling a 6 for another success. Solar rolls 11 dice for 4. Brawl gets 5 rounds of control.<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 7wp 23i<br /> Sword: 29m 5wp 7i<br /> Brawl: 13m 5wp 9i<br /> Bow: 25m 5wp 11i<br /> <br /> First round, Brawl will withering strike rolling 15 dice for 6, rolling 3 damage for nothing.<br /> ---------<br /> Sword attempts a withering strike with 6m full excellency and 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite, rolling 16 dice against parry 7, getting 5 and missing.<br /> <br /> Solar: 5m 7wp 23i<br /> Sword: 25m 4wp 7i<br /> Brawl: 18m 5wp 10i<br /> Bow: 30m 5wp 11i<br /> ========<br /> Solar uses Fivefold Bulwark Stance 5m 1wp<br /> ---------<br /> Bow fires a 6m full excellency withering shot. Rolling 21 dice for 9 against parry 7. Rolling 4 damage for 1<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 6wp 22i<br /> Sword: 25m 4wp 7i<br /> Brawl: 18m 5wp 10i<br /> Bow: 24m 5wp 13i<br /> ---------<br /> Brawl withering strikes with 2m Pounding Surf. Rolling 15 dice for 10, dealing 7 dice of damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 6wp 19i<br /> Sword: 25m 4wp 7i<br /> Brawl: 16m 5wp 14i<br /> Bow: 24m 5wp 13i<br /> ---------<br /> Sword attempts a withering strike with 6m full excellency and 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite, rolling 16 dice against parry 7, getting 4 and missing.<br /> <br /> Solar: 5m 6wp 19i<br /> Sword: 21m 3wp 7i<br /> Brawl: 21m 5wp 14i<br /> Bow: 29m 5wp 13i<br /> ========<br /> Solar withers Brawler with 3m Excellent Strike, 2m Excellency, brawler will not spend essence to defend.<br /> <br /> Solar rolls 26 dice against parry 5, hitting with 12, rolling 6 damage and taking 2 rounds of control.<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 6wp 27i<br /> Sword: 21m 3wp 7i<br /> Brawl: 21m 5wp 14i<br /> Bow: 29m 5wp 13i<br /> ---------<br /> Brawl will withering strike, rolling 15 dice for 7, hitting parry of 7. Rolling 3 damage for 0<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 6wp 27i<br /> Sword: 21m 3wp 7i<br /> Brawl: 21m 5wp 15i<br /> Bow: 29m 5wp 13i<br /> ---------<br /> Bow will aim<br /> ---------<br /> Sword attempts a withering strike with 6m full excellency and 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite, rolling 16 dice against parry 7, getting 10 and hitting.<br /> <br /> Rolling 10 damage and getting nothing<br /> <br /> Solar: 5m 6wp 27i<br /> Sword: 20m 2wp 8i<br /> Brawl: 26m 5wp 15i<br /> Bow: 34m 5wp 13i<br /> ========<br /> Solar will attempt to decisive attack Bawl, 3m excellent strike, 2m excellency, Brawl will defend with 6m excellency.<br /> <br /> Solar rolls 14 dice for 10, getting it. Rolling 27 decisive damage for 11 levels killing the brawler.<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 6wp 4i<br /> Sword: 20m 3wp 8i<br /> Bow: 34m 5wp 13i<br /> ---------<br /> Bow attacks with a withering strike, 6m full excellency, 4m Death from Nowhere. Rolling 24 dice for 12 against parry 7, then rolling 6 damage for 2<br /> ---------<br /> Sword aims<br /> <br /> Solar: 5m 6wp 2i<br /> Sword: 25m 2wp 8i<br /> Bow: 29m 5wp 16i<br /> ========<br /> Solar will attempt to wither sword with 3m excellent strike, 2m Fire and Stones, Sword will not spend motes to defend.<br /> <br /> Solar rolls 14 dice against parry 5, making it with 7, then rolls 6 damage for 1.<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 6wp 4i<br /> Sword: 25m 3wp 7i<br /> Bow: 29m 5wp 16i<br /> ---------<br /> Bow attacks with withering strike, 6m full excellency. Rolling 21 dice for 8, hitting. Rolling 4 damage for 4, crashing the Solar.<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 6wp 0i<br /> Sword: 25m 2wp 7i<br /> Bow: 23m 5wp 26i<br /> ---------<br /> Roll 2 dice for anima flux, getting 2<br /> <br /> Sword withers with 6m excellency, rolling 16 dice, getting 7, then rolling 6 damage for 4<br /> <br /> Solar: 5m 6wp -4i<br /> Sword: 24m 2wp 12i<br /> Bow: 28m 5wp 26i<br /> ========<br /> Bow will aim<br /> ---------<br /> Sword rolls 2 dice of anima damage, getting none<br /> <br /> Sword will aim<br /> ---------<br /> Solar will attempt to disengage toward Bow, with 2m Dust Motes Whirling and 3m Excellency. Fire will not spend motes to contest.<br /> <br /> Solar rolling 14 dice for 11, fire rolling 8 dice for 4.<br /> <br /> Solar: 5m 6wp -6i<br /> Sword: 29m 2wp 12i<br /> Bow: 33m 5wp 26i<br /> ========<br /> Bow rolls 1 die of anima damage getting 1. Solar must roll for poison, rolling 11 dice against duration 5, getting 3.<br /> <br /> Bow will flurry a disengage with an attack. 6m on the disengage, Solar will spend 5m to contest. Bow rolls 14 dice against 15, getting 9 against 7, successfully disengaging.<br /> <br /> Then Bow will attack with 3m Arrow Thorn Technique, 2m Spring Follows Winter, and 6m excellency. Rolling 17 dice getting 5, rerolling 2 for 2i with Spring Follows Winter for no help, and thus missing.<br /> <br /> Solar: 5m 6wp -6i<br /> Sword: 29m 2wp 12i<br /> Bow: 16m 5wp 21i<br /> ---------<br /> Fire will move into range with Solar, and decisive attack, using a 6m full excellency. Rolling 19 dice, and getting 8, then rolling 12 damage for 7, putting Solar into -2s.<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 6wp -6i<br /> Sword: 23m 2wp 3i<br /> Bow: 16m 5wp 21i<br /> ---------<br /> Solar attempts to wither Sword with 12 dice to attack, sword will full excellency defend for 6m. 12 dice turn up 6 successes and miss<br /> <br /> Solar takes 1 poison damage<br /> <br /> Solar: 5m 6wp -6i<br /> Sword: 22m 2wp 3i<br /> Bow: 21m 5wp 21i<br /> ========<br /> Bow will attempt to wither with 6m full excellency. Solar will defend with 1m dipping swallow. Bow rolls 17 dice for 8, Solar will Hail Shatter to stop it.<br /> <br /> Solar: 5m 6wp -6i<br /> Sword: 22m 2wp 3i<br /> Bow: 15m 5wp 18i<br /> ---------<br /> Sword rolls flux damage, dealing nothing<br /> <br /> Sword delays to clash with Solar.<br /> <br /> The two clash. Sword uses 5m Crossfire Flash, 6m full excellency, Solar uses 3m Excellent Strike, 2m excellency.<br /> <br /> Sword rolls 18 dice getting 9, and rerolling for 10. Solar attacks with 14 dice, getting 6, rerolling for 7. Sword deals 4 dice for 2 damage, then an additional 3 for winning a clash.<br /> <br /> Solar: 0m 6wp -1i<br /> Sword: 11m 2wp 9i<br /> Bow: 15m 5wp 18i<br /> <br /> Solar takes 2 poison damage and dies.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Even with that insane starting initiative, the unlucky decisive strike missing just killed it. After that there were no motes left to pull the same combo off, and by the grace of rolling 23 successes on 23 dice he had enough initiative to slay the brawler outright, and then in spite of having max stats in everything got dragged down and died to the wood aspect anima poison, ultimately. I definitely felt the sting of not having Essence 3 though, the lack of signature charms is a major power downgrade, even if the DBs ultimately won this crazy fight.<br /> <br /> I'd also advise any STs out there to maybe lay off so many enemies with incredibly high soak combined with very high defense and Hail Shattering Practice. It makes the fight very static, with initiative shifting at a slow crawl. It's not really fun or dynamic. If you're going to do something like that with 18 soak, maybe leave their defense at 3-4 without any way to boost it or something.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that was the last of my curiosity about that kind of thing, I think. If I do any more it's going to be things like lone exalts vs 1-3 monstrous things that probably don't even have charms, and fights where the rounds only take a minute or two to roll out and the fight's over much faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T04:34:45-07:00","id":1340759,"title":"","content":"Very interesting, thank you. <br /> Regardless of how strong an exalted celestial is always correpeligro against 3 Dragon-Blooded, even if they don't have signature charms, that's a big difference.<br /> Although according to the books most Dragon-blooded do not reach Essence 3.<br /> Of course, spending a huge amount of motes in an initial attack as powerful as possible is a great risk, if it goes wrong, it remains at a disadvantage for the rest of the possibly doomed to a slow defeat.<br /> If it goes well then the fight is also decided, in favor of the Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T22:16:49-07:00","id":1340906,"title":"","content":"My game has been running a long while now, and The Sword, my Resistance Supernal Dawn has had to fight a pretty alright number of Dragon-Blooded and battle groups. What I have been surprised by is just how effective Essence-Gathering Temper has proven to be in large combats. Between Single Point and it, one-on-many fights of attrition actually end up going my player's way more times than not. Part (OK, a lot) of that is on Single Point being nuts, part of it of it is on account of Resistance Supernal, certainly, but in truth Essence-Gathering Temper does a -lot- of lifting, especially starting at Essence 3 and beyond. Mote regen of any kind is just so important where every individual Essence user with an excellency mechanic gets -so much- replenishing combat power every turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T22:22:46-07:00","id":1340907,"title":"","content":"How easy do you find the reset condition to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T03:02:16-07:00","id":1340924,"title":"","content":"I dont have anything meaningful to add, I just wanna thank <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> for this awesome thread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T22:01:36-07:00","id":1341051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1340924#post1340924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont have anything meaningful to add, I just wanna thank <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> for this awesome thread</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! In honour of Thanksgiving I rolled out three combats between an unoptimized but still combat focused Solar, Lunar and DB against three Death Moa each. I got 90% the way done with the final one before family obligations have me until Monday.<br /> <br /> In each case though, the exalt won but at the cost of all their motes, and the Solar even had to glitter his castemark. Although he did have a more left to re-banish his daiklave to Elsewhere. Not bad considering Death Moa are nine foot tall predatory birds of death. I should be able to post them Monday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T19:08:14-07:00","id":1341197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341051#post1341051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not bad considering Death Moa are nine foot tall predatory birds of death.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>sweats in Australian</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T19:21:17-07:00","id":1341548,"title":"","content":"Ported from discussion on Ask a Question thred.<br /> <br /> Okay, so Soaring Zephyr Flight is really good in cases where your enemy has little to no ranged attacks and you do. That goes double for archers, because if an enemy is in close range with you as an archer you lose six dice to all your attack rolls, and you spend a bunch of turns/flurries/initiative trying to disengage so you can try to get back where you want to be. If you've got Soaring Zephyr Flight you can just sit above them firing powerbow shots down on them.<br /> <br /> If they've got some ranged power, like a size 2 battlegroup of nomads lead by a commander, you might still come out on top. For one, if you're using a powerbow, excellency, Death From Nowhere, and have 5/3/3 you're doing about 8 initiative damage to them per turn. With a bit of luck you'll drop them to size 1 with a single attack, but almost 100% after two.<br /> <br /> Math on your attacks<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attack is 20 (3 Dex + 5 Archery + 5 Accuracy + 1 Specialty + 6 Excellency)<br /> Defense is 4, normally they have 3 Evasion but with average drill it goes to 4<br /> <br /> So you're looking at 10 successes and 6 overflow.<br /> <br /> Damage is 23 (6 overflow + 5 Strength + 12 base)<br /> Their soak starts at 8, but with Size 2 it jumps to 10, but subtract 3 for the Essence 3 Death From Nowhere without aiming.<br /> <br /> Final damage is 16 for an average of 8<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But every other turn they get to attack back. Why every other turn? Because you can dip in and out of range. Soaring Zephyr Flight starts you at medium range on the turn you use it. Then next turn you can drop to close and fire, then they get to go and shoot. The next round starts and you fire and reflexively move back to medium range, they go but now you're back out of range. They also can't delay their action to attack you as you return to Close range, you can only delay your action to a later tick in the same round, if the round ends and you didn't act then you don't go. So they're dealing about 3i damage to you every other round assuming they have a solid commander.<br /> <br /> Math on their attacks<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attack is 20(11 base + 2 Size + 3 aim + 4 command)<br /> Defense with 3 dex but max dodge is 5<br /> <br /> So that again with 10 successes and 5 overflow<br /> <br /> Damage is 17 (10 base + 2 Size + 5 overflow)<br /> Soak with 3 stamina, artifact light armor and Impervious Skin of Stone is 11.<br /> <br /> Final damage is 6, which because battlegroups do not enjoy double 10s to damage is slightly under 3i average.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you're using a full attack excellency, Death From Nowhere, and Impervious Skin of Stone you're spending 10m on attack every turn, and 4m on defense every other turn, with 5m/round regen. So bleeding 7m every round which gives you 5 rounds of air time before you're dry if you're going full hard. You should also go after the commander first until he's crashed. He's got the same stats as the BG except lower, and you gain way more initiative off him so he'll give you a nice buffer to stay afloat with.<br /> <br /> And I even rolled it out just to see if there was anything I was missing. Keeping in mind here that dice are fickle and this is not by any means a guaranteed result. Also excuse the bad formatting<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Jon Battle<br /> DB 5<br /> BG 4<br /> CO 1<br /> <br /> i8 36m<br /> i7<br /> i4<br /> <br /> <br /> First attack, Death From Nowhere the commander. 7 to hit. Final damage 15 dice of damage for 5i damage. Enter Air Aura<br /> <br /> <br /> i19 32m<br /> i7<br /> i-1<br /> <br /> Battlegroup waits for orders<br /> <br /> i19<br /> i7<br /> i-1<br /> <br /> Commander rolls 8 dice and orders for 8 amazingly<br /> <br /> Battlegroup attacks, DB will resist with 4m ISOS. Rolling 21 dice for 10. Of the 6 dice 5 turn up successes<br /> <br /> i14 28m<br /> i5<br /> i-1<br /> ==================<br /> DB moves in to close and uses Soaring Zephyr Flight, reflexively moving 2 range bands straight up.<br /> <br /> Battlegroup aims<br /> <br /> Commander commands for 3 dice<br /> i14 23m<br /> i5<br /> i-1<br /> ====================<br /> i10 28m<br /> i5<br /> i-1<br /> <br /> Next turn DB drops to close and 10m full attacks, rolling 20 dice for 14. Then rolling 20 dice for a total of 15 damage. Battlegroup takes 9 damage filling out it's first size and checks for rout, rolling 6 dice and getting it with 5. Remaining 6 damage go into new health track, Battlegroup has 2 health levels left.<br /> <br /> i16 18m<br /> i5<br /> i-1<br /> <br /> <br /> Battlegroup attacks with 18 dice, DB defends with ISOS. Rolling 18 dice for 9, then rolling 5 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> i13 14m<br /> i7<br /> i-1<br /> <br /> Commander commands with 8 dice for 6 as he recovers from crash.<br /> ==================<br /> i9 19m<br /> i7<br /> i-1<br /> <br /> DB attacks again, this time with only Death from Nowhere. Rolling 14 dice for 9, and then 16 damage for only 4 but enough to kill the BG. Reflexive move to retreat to medium range.<br /> <br /> i15 15m<br /> i3<br /> <br /> Commander draws his bow.<br /> <br /> i15 15m<br /> i3<br /> ===============<br /> i11 20m<br /> i3<br /> DB moves to short and full attacks with combo. Rolling 20 dice for 7, and then 16 rolled damage for 8.<br /> <br /> i20 10m<br /> i-5<br /> <br /> Commander attacks, DB will not spend motes to defend. Rolling 11 dice for 7, then rolling 4 damage for 1<br /> <br /> i 19 10m<br /> i-3<br /> ===============<br /> i15 15m<br /> i-3<br /> <br /> DB attacks with Death from Nowhere, rolling 14 dice for 10, then 18 damage for 14 damage. Reflexively move to medium range.<br /> <br /> i29 11m<br /> i-3<br /> <br /> commander aims<br /> ===============<br /> DB chooses not to renew Soaring Zephyr Flight and drops down into Close range with the commander.<br /> i29 16m<br /> i-3<br /> <br /> DB Will decisive attack commander with 6m full excellency. Rolling 15 dice for 8 and hitting, and then 29 damage for 11 and killing. Victory DB, with 10 motes left in the tank.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> BUT that's not really ever going to happen more than once or twice, because you rarely fight alone <i>especially </i>as a DB, so where I think Soaring Zephyr Flight works there is basically how it worked there, except like this: Your hearth is fighting in the melee below you, and enemy archers are stuck with little to no response. Here's a side view of the range bands.<br /> <br /> ------O<br /> O-O<br /> <br /> You're in the one at the top, flying above your allies and enemies in melee at the bottom right. Enemy archers, if there are any, are in the bottom left. You're at medium range from them, so if they want to attack you they have to aim every other turn, and even then they're doing it at reduced accuracy, while the melee fighters mix it up underneath you. If there's anyone underneath that feels like they should shoot you to crash you and bring you back to earth, they need to drop whatever melee weapon they're holding, pick up their bow, and shoot you. So they're losing their Parry, which if they're dedicated frontline fighters is almost always better than their Evasion, often by a huge margin, and either giving up a turn to the Draw/Ready action, or flurrying it.<br /> <br /> You could do the same kind of thing from this position O O O, obviously, but that leaves you open to being disengaged into, which is a death sentence for archers. Thankfully though, Soaring Zephyr Flight can get you out of that situation. If you're doing the O O O style formation and get disengaged into, use SZF to escape way high up and then start the rain. You also don't always get to start there, sometimes you're stuck in the middle and need to disengage yourself pronto. If there's somewhere else with higher elevation above you, like trees or buildings, you can even use SZF and pay no initiative cost, just use it as an automatic disengage, use your reflexive move to get to that higher ground, and don't pay the initiative cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> Going through this has actually made me rethink SZF, I used to think its use in combat was marginal, or extremely situational, but abusing the movement and range mechanics can really make it useful. I imagine that in an actual melee where there's a bunch else going on and you're just up there pelting down shots it would be even more useful. You just have to make sure you're done with flying if you want to decisive attack. It helps that there's few things in the books with more than 4 defense, and 10 soak, and clearly 4 defense and 10 soak is not enough to stop the initiative trickle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With Sunder the Gold doing a thread on this and Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, I might also run a combat with a fire aspect that has that charm to see if it's as bad as we thought it was in practice too, if anyone has any suggestions about what they should fight. Something less powerful than a Solar with max in every stat, because that'll be over in one round like it always is, but more than a badass mortal. I'm also not sure what people's opinion of me kind of cheesing the Stamina effect of that charm. Technically if you ever plan on getting to Essence 5 you should have Stamina 5 to use that charm properly when you're there, buuuut if you're using it at Essence 3 just Stamina 3 is fine, and you've got hundreds of XP between Essence 3 and 5 to raise it with Dragon xp or regular xp, so I don't know if it's that awful to just say stamina 3.<br /> <br /> After I finish the turkey shoot battles anyway, which...tomorrow probably as I'm pretty ill right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T19:38:26-07:00","id":1341560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341548#post1341548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But every other turn they get to attack back. Why every other turn? Because you can dip in and out of range. Soaring Zephyr Flight starts you at medium range on the turn you use it. Then next turn you can drop to <b><u>close</u> </b>and fire, then they get to go and shoot. The next round starts and you fire and reflexively move back to medium range, they go but now you're back out of range. They also can't delay their action to attack you as you return to <b><u>Close</u> </b>range, you can only delay your action to a later tick in the same round, if the round ends and you didn't act then you don't go. So they're dealing about 3i damage to you every other round assuming they have a solid commander.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you mean Short range here instead of Close Range? If not I'm having trouble following how you fly away from Close to Medium range in a single turn every other turn.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T20:17:32-07:00","id":1341566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341560#post1341560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you mean Short range here instead of Close Range? If not I'm having trouble following how you fly away from Close to Medium range in a single turn every other turn.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's a typo, lol.<br /> <br /> Also I should point out that those conditions of a featureless bright field are the absolute worst for Dragonblooded archers. Between Sky Calming, Threshold Warding and their archery excellency effects they can easily fight in high winds, rain, midnight, all three at once and suffer zero penalties for any of it, where the horse archers would be suffering from a -5 to their attacks and maybe a -3 to defense and command rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 10-15-2019, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T15:57:42-07:00","id":1341725,"title":"","content":"Having read this thread I now want to run my Invincible Sword Princess, Shining Topaz (not fully built yet), against the local fae freehold. A Cataphract, a Loreli, and a size 5 army of hobgoblins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T16:04:44-07:00","id":1341727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341725#post1341725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having read this thread I now want to run my Invincible Sword Princess, Shining Topaz (not fully built yet), against the local fae freehold. A Cataphract, a Loreli, and a size 5 army of hobgoblins.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T20:22:57-07:00","id":1341768,"title":"","content":"Okay, late for Canadian Thanksgiving, but still early for the American one. Here's the turkey shoot. I added a little more story behind these, and also all three of these took as much time to run as just one DB vs Solar fight.<br /> <br /> First fight is Javen. He's a Solar wandering the woodland near Utahi satrapy. It's dangerous for his kind, but he's looking to maybe start a rebellion here, rallying the people as their new Great Hero. Unfortunately he's going to have to get past 3 of the most deadly predators in the whole West, Death Moa. Approaching him from the nearby woods he prepares for combat.<br /> <br /> Javen<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 4/4/3<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> Melee 3 daiklave specialty<br /> Awareness 4<br /> <br /> Daiklave 11 (Damage 16/5)<br /> Parry 5<br /> Soak 10/0 Mundane heavy armor<br /> <br /> Per: 13 Iph: 27 (33)<br /> <br /> <br /> -0/4x-1/6x-2/-4/I<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> Excellent Strike<br /> Fire and Stones Strike<br /> One Weapon two Blows<br /> Dipping Swallow Defense<br /> Bulwark Stance<br /> Hail Shattering Practice<br /> Call the Blade<br /> Summoning the Loyal Steel<br /> Ox-body Technique (x2)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Javen rolls join battle, spending 4m to enhance it, rolling 11 dice for 4, getting 7i<br /> <br /> Bird 1 rolls 5 dice for 3 getting 6i<br /> Bird 2 rolls 5 dice for 2 getting 5i<br /> Bird 3 rolls 5 dice for 2 getting 5i<br /> <br /> <br /> Javen 7i 13p 23ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird2 5i<br /> Bird3 5i<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> Javen knows these predatory birds have jaws that can snap bone with one bite, so he risks revealing his exalted nature this far from civilization, dropping Summoning the Loyal Steel and summoning his daiklave to his hand.<br /> <br /> Sweeping his daiklave towards Bird 2 he uses 3m Excellent Strike 3m Fire and Stones Strike, being cautious not to overextend his essence. Rolling 11 dice for 9, with one reroll netting nothing. Smashing the bird with 17 damage for 8, crashing the birb<br /> <br /> Javen 21i 7p 23ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird2 -3i<br /> Bird3 5i<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Bird 1 acts, attacking Javen, who will defend with 2m excellency. Rolling 8 dice against parry 6 and failing with 3<br /> <br /> Javen 21i 7p 21ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird2 -3i<br /> Bird3 5i<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Bird 3 snaps at Javen, who will defend with 2m Dipping Swallow and 2m Excellency. Rolling 8 dice against parry 6, getting 4 and missing.<br /> <br /> Javen 22i 7p 17ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird2 -3i<br /> Bird3 5i<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Bird 2 gives another sharp snap, Javen will defend with 2m DS and 2m Excellency again. Rolling 8 dice for 3 and missing<br /> <br /> Javen 23i 7p 13ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird2 -3i<br /> Bird3 5i<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> Javen 23i 7p 18ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird2 -3i<br /> Bird3 5i<br /> <br /> Javen strikes Bird 2 with a decisive attack, using 3m excellent strike and 2m excellency. Rolling 9 dice for a total of 7, and then 23 damage for 9, not enough to kill the bird but it's now going to flee.<br /> <br /> Javen 3i 2p 18ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird3 5i<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Bird 1 is going to strike Javen, who will defend with 2m excellency. Rolling 8 dice against parry 6 for 5, just barely missing.<br /> <br /> Javen 3i 2p 16ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird3 5i<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Bird 3 will do the same, who will defend with 5m bulwark stance. Rolling 8 dice against parry 5 for 6 with no 1s or 2s! Snapping Javen and forcing him back. Rolling 6 damage dice for 5, crashing Javen.<br /> <br /> Javen -2i 0p 13ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird3 16i<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> Javen -2i 0p 18ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird3 16i<br /> <br /> Bird 3 will go for the kill, spending a willpower and attacking Javen, who will defend with 4m excellency. Bird 3 rolls 8 dice with 3 autosuccesses against parry 7, getting 8 total! Rolling 16 damage for 7, putting Javen into his -2 health levels.<br /> <br /> Javen -2i 0p 18ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird3 3i<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Bird 1 is going to give a withering strike to Javen, who will defend with 4m excellency. Rolling 8 dice against parry 7 for 5 and missing.<br /> <br /> Javen -2i 0p 14ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird3 3i<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Javen strikes at Bird 3, with 3m Excellent Strike and 1m excellency. Rolling 10 dice for 8 with two 2s, giving another 2. Slamming his daiklave home for 15 damage, rolling 6. Initiative shift! Javen jumps to 10 initiative, then rolls Join Battle again rolling 7 for 5.<br /> <br /> Javen 15i 0p 10ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> Bird3 -3i<br /> <br /> Javan acts again immediately as per initiative shift, and decisive attacks Bird 3, using 3m Fire and Stones Strike and 1m excellency. Rolling 7 dice against parry 2 for 6, then rolling 18 damage for 8, forcing the bird to flee.<br /> <br /> Javen 3i 0p 6ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ===========<br /> Javen 3i 0p 11ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> <br /> Bird 1 will try to wither Javen, who defends with 4m excellency. Rolling 8 dice against parry 6 for 5.<br /> <br /> Javen 3i 0p 7ph <br /> Bird1 6i<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Javen strikes back with 3m excellent strike 1m fire and stones. Rolling 9 dice against parry 3 for a total of 6, and then 11 damage dice for only 4.<br /> <br /> Javen 8i 0p 3ph <br /> Bird1 2i<br /> <br /> Activating One Weapon Two Blows Javen strikes again, rolling 9 dice against parry 2 for 4, and then 10 damage f