d 2 -10i<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Bird 2 will wither, Vindral will 0m full defensive excellency, 1m 1i Blinding Spark. Rolling 3 dice against parry 6, failing with 0.<br /> <br /> Rolling 6 dice against difficulty 8, failing with 3<br /> <br /> Vindral 2i 3p 9ph<br /> Bird 2 -10i<br /> <br /> I'm actually going to call it here as an ST. With the perpetual blindness and full free excellency, this is only going to go on for several more turns and regenerate all of Vindral's motes, and that's not what combat is supposed to do. it's over.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well I had to call that early. Once the DB melee excellency gets online against a single foe, and especially combined with Blinding Spark Distraction and wound penalties, the only thing running the fight is going to do is let the DB regen all her motes. Still though, that was a pretty damn good fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I guess if you want to give a challenge to your players with death moa, maybe 2 times the number of moa as players? Like for 4 players 8 moa? I'm not sure if that's a great idea considering how hard they can gang up on one person once they're crashed though. If your group isn't heavily combat invested I might go for 1.5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, next I'll probably do something with Raging Fire Dragon Spirit. Each of those combats there took 5-8 rounds, which I have to say isn't my experience with the game, but maybe in smaller fights like this Raging Fire Dragon Spirit comes out and starts shining.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T20:37:24-07:00","id":1341770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1340907#post1340907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How easy do you find the reset condition to be?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Initially I expected it'd be a pretty tough condition to achieve, but a few things have made it easier: <br /> <br /> 1. Most fights involve at least one non-Exalt. Dragonblooded love to bring friends. Non-Exalts mean attacks without Overwhelming, and not buffed by excellencies and Charms (though relatively often Command dice are involved, evening it out a little). This makes it easier to soak hits outright. Would be even easier if heavy armor were an option, but sadly Single Point precludes that. <br /> <br /> 2. Even when Overwhelming gets into the mix, I read Iron Skin Concentration as allowing the user to treat up to Stamina points of Overwhelming damage as ordinary soakable damage. Even at a 2m cost, this often ends up being worthwhile when fighting Dynasts and the like. <br /> <br /> 3. God help them if Aegis of Invincible Might is triggered, somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T20:57:38-07:00","id":1341775,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I wonder if it might be better to go Supernal resistance then. The only thing is...I'm not running that. With only Essence 1 melee charms for offense, and a crazy amount of defensive charms that fight will take forever. I've already seen one infinite loop take place that way with Revolving Bow Discipline and Aegis of Invincible Might. That fight could take me literally days to run.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah... Aegis of Invincible Might and Spirit Gathering Temper might actually let you fight the entire Imperial Palace at once. With artifact fullplate that's like, what? 26 soak, boost to 34 or something with Diamond-Body Prana, and regenerate 10m every time anyone strikes you with a withering attack? I'm pretty sure that would do it. You could fight every DB in the entire wold at once with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 10-17-2019, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T06:29:24-07:00","id":1341844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341770#post1341770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Even when Overwhelming gets into the mix, I read Iron Skin Concentration as allowing the user to treat up to Stamina points of Overwhelming damage as ordinary soakable damage. Even at a 2m cost, this often ends up being worthwhile when fighting Dynasts and the like. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's not my reading of that Charm.<br /> <br /> It lets you apply &quot;Stamina <b>as soak</b> against unsoakable damage&quot;. Meaning you can't get below minimum damage (because you're still subject to the rules of Soak), but could Soak, for example, Azure Abacus Meditation.<br /> <br /> Aegis of Invincible Might works fine for negating minimum damage though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341775#post1341775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With artifact fullplate that's like, what? 26 soak, boost to 34 or something with Diamond-Body Prana</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't stack DBP with armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-17-2019, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T06:40:29-07:00","id":1341846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341768#post1341768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, late for Canadian Thanksgiving, but still early for the American one. Here's the turkey shoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thankful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T07:06:10-07:00","id":1341851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341768#post1341768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vindral -1i 11p 5ph<br /> Bird 1 13i<br /> Bird 2 5i<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Vindral deals 0 anima damage<br /> <br /> Vindral strikes back at Bird 1 with a chopping attack, </div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't Chopping attacks Perilous because they cost 1i?<br /> <br /> Great fight though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T07:17:49-07:00","id":1341853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naris counterattacks with 2m Unstoppable Beast Force Blow, and 4m excellency, rolling 12 dice with 2 autosuccesses</div> </div> </div> </div>Just checking, you know that the 2 auto-successes from the merit count as 4 charm dice?<br /> <br /> And also, since she's Dex 4 and Brawl 3, then in Death Moa form she rolls 8 dice (like a Death Moa) but counts as using 1 of her excellency cap.<br /> <br /> So she can only spend up to 3 motes for 11 dice if she doesn't stunt, or against a crashed target she can roll 8 dice and get 1 auto-success, with the potential to buy one more dice.<br /> <br /> If she does a Strength or Stamina-based 1pt stunt though, she can spend 3 motes to roll 13 dice with 2 auto-successes against a crashed target, or 7 motes to roll 17 dice against a non-crashed target.<br /> <br /> I may have made a mistake in reading your description (and I don't have the rules for Death Moa on hand, I'm just going by your explanation that they have a merit giving 2 auto-successes against crashed enemies), but that's how it looks to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T12:25:28-07:00","id":1341918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341851#post1341851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't Chopping attacks Perilous because they cost 1i?<br /> <br /> Great fight though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked and couldn\u2019t find anything to that effect. You can\u2019t crash yourself with a charm\u2019s initiative cost, but you explicitly can crash yourself with a disengage action for example. You can\u2019t launch decisive attacks, you can\u2019t use perilous charms, those are both explicit, but I couldn\u2019t find special attacks anywhere.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, if you can use chopping and piercing attacks while crashed, it makes them a lot better. Since you can use them when you\u2019re really low on initiative at the end of the round, and then next turn flip to going before all your enemies so that -1 defence never matters.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341853#post1341853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just checking, you know that the 2 auto-successes from the merit count as 4 charm dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I...I don\u2019t know Lunars so good... That was totally my bad. I haven\u2019t played any games with Lunars yet and I also haven\u2019t run a lot of combats with them either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 10-17-2019, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T14:26:12-07:00","id":1341944,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the way animal dice pools and merits interact with dice caps is something most of my Lunar players forget (we've had 11 sessions, though I guess most of them haven't fought in animal form more than once or twice), and are surprised when I remind them. It's certainly not just something that throws people who've never played Lunars.<br /> <br /> Sadly, the Lunar animal rules are supposed to be simple and easy, but in attempting to make them simple and easy the way dice pools are calculated actually ends up being really complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T20:30:44-07:00","id":1342003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341844#post1341844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not my reading of that Charm.<br /> <br /> It lets you apply &quot;Stamina <b>as soak</b> against unsoakable damage&quot;. Meaning you can't get below minimum damage (because you're still subject to the rules of Soak), but could Soak, for example, Azure Abacus Meditation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Digging into past answers from Mr. Vance, it appears that your read on it not applying to Overwhelming damage is on the money, though he does also admit that unsoakable damage like...barely ever comes up, which is why I figured I was in the clear with allowing that effect since it's otherwise kinda a mechanical orphan. Most of the time that Essence Gathering Temper is reset is from non-Artifact weapon attacks anyways, so it hasn't affected my game too, too much. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1341775#post1341775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... Aegis of Invincible Might and Spirit Gathering Temper might actually let you fight the entire Imperial Palace at once. With artifact fullplate that's like, what? 26 soak, boost to 34 or something with Diamond-Body Prana, and regenerate 10m every time anyone strikes you with a withering attack? I'm pretty sure that would do it. You could fight every DB in the entire wold at once with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of DBP not stacking with armor, yeah, if Aegis triggers it's about as bad as it seems (speaking from experience). Between that, Single Point, Thunderbolt Attack Prana, a bunch of powerful Melee charms, and Front-Line Warrior's Stamina with 4 Ox Bodies (i.e. get on average 10ish initiative as a Simple action once per day), the group's Dawn is...dirty. Makes for an interesting time designing fights. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T21:04:23-07:00","id":1342006,"title":"","content":"I can think of a few ways to get around it, but they all seem kind of equally dirty. Which sucks because he didn\u2019t buy the charm to never be able to use it.<br /> <br /> Like for one, it\u2019s perilous, so if nobody launches a damaging decisive attack against him while he\u2019s uncrashed he can never trigger it. Also locking him into a grapple and using the restrain option to prevent him from using offensive motes on his turn would end it. Or just the old standby of don\u2019t attack him, attack everyone else, even relatively unintelligent predators understand the concept of going after the soft weaker prey rather than the big metal encased thing. The grapple one though is the only one I\u2019d consider using all that often though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T21:28:10-07:00","id":1342008,"title":"","content":"DBs can roll 10 overwhelming with medium daiklaves thanks to Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite, even with Aegis of Invincible Might + Iron Kettle Body getting that down to 3 dice you are only resetting essence-gathering temper every 4-5th hit, and that assumes they let you trigger Aegis. If you actually build DBs to fight celestials they become pretty hard to take down when they have decent numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:36:02-07:00","id":1342294,"title":"","content":"I'm not really happy with this one. A Skycutter weilding DB vs a Cataphract. The matchup didn't feel proper, with a kind of boss-style enemy with lots of effects meant to handle multiple foes fighting one person uselessly, with huge soak and a bunch of other strange effects. I also didn't play the thrown part of this properly at all. Part of the power of thrown is that you get to pick the range band your enemy doesn't like. Has sword out? Use Hopping Firecracker to hop away, then attack and retreat until he either successfully rushes or pulls out the bow...then jump back into close and ruin his day there. I also made some big mistakes on the cataphract like not engaging right away with the giant army.<br /> <br /> I also went too far, I think, in trying to see if RFDS worked without building too hard for it. Instead of just trying to find a not-hyper-optimal way to do it, I went for the least optimal one, a fighting style with no counterattacks, no reflexive clashes, nothing like that. I built completely counter to what it wants and it shows. The only thing that I got out of this is that, against super high accuracy enemies, Shimmering Heat-Mirage Tactic actually is good. I couldn't figure out before if it was garbage or not, but unless I got insanely lucky, it's solid, and I thin a great complement to RFDS.<br /> <br /> Use it on your first turn to get into aura, then use RFDS on your second turn, and now you have 2e style Infinite Ability Mastery all over again, except balanced enough not to ruin the game, hopefully. I might even run something like this again, but not against a solo antagonist like the cataphract here. Too many of his abilities were useless and his stats were too high to make a good dynamic scene. Also next time I'll use something that actually works with it. If you were using Fire Melee with it's Blazing Interception counterattacks, Water Incites Fire to a Riot of Clouds bonus reflexive clashes, and Burning Pinnacle Strike extra attacks, you'd get your money back so much faster. That or Crane Style, just counterattack everything forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> Either way, I did all the work and I figure somebody might want to see if, if just for curiosity at this mess, so here it is. The backstory for this is Eragan, an outcaste DB wanderer, comes upon a ronin Cataphract seeking a master. Recognizing eachother as both kindred souls and rivals, the two decide to find out who is worthy the only way they know how.<br /> <br /> Eragan<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Erangan<br /> <br /> 5/3/3<br /> <br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> 5 Thrown with boomarang specialty<br /> 5 Dodge with specialty in light armor<br /> 5 Resistance<br /> 4 stealth<br /> 3 Athletics<br /> 3 awareness<br /> <br /> <br /> Red Jade Skycutter Crimson Horizon 14/15 (Damage 17/4) or 18 with rfds<br /> Evasion 5<br /> Soak/Hardness 5/4 With RFDS<br /> <br /> personal 14 peripheral 26<br /> <br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> Dodge<br /> Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Flickering Candle Meditation<br /> Hopping Firecracker Evasion<br /> Unassailable Body of Fire<br /> Ember Amid Smoke Misdirection<br /> <br /> Resistance<br /> Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit<br /> <br /> Stealth<br /> Distracting Breeze<br /> Vanishing Wind-Body<br /> Flowing Shadow Stance<br /> Shimmer Heat-Mirage<br /> <br /> Thrown<br /> Seeking Throw<br /> Invisibly Hidden Chakram<br /> Blinding Spark Throw<br /> Smoke Burst Eruption<br /> Exploding Weapon Technique<br /> Elusive Zephyr Strike<br /> Winter Fang Attack<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Eragan joins battle with 2m into a success and 8 dice for a total of 4 successes and 7i<br /> <br /> Pilaf joins battle with 11 dice for 5 successes and 8i<br /> <br /> Eragan 7i 14p 26ph 5wp<br /> Pilaf 8i 20m 7wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==========<br /> Pilaf uses 10m Marching Fever Dream Nightmare to summon a horde of nightmare soldiers. Rolling 12 dice plus a willpower and getting a total of 10 successes...for a size 5 battlegroup of soldiers. Rolled in with 6 dice for 1 success and 4i.<br /> <br /> Eragan 7i 14p 24ph 5wp<br /> Pilaf 8i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Eragan is gripped with fear as thousands of nightmare soldiers emerge from nothing before him, but slipping into shimmering illusion activates 4m 2i Shimmer Heat-Mirage Tactic.<br /> <br /> Eragan 5i 14p 20ph 5wp<br /> Pilaf 8i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Nightmares attack, swarming Eragan, who will defend with 3m Ember Amid Smoke Misdirection. Rolling 12 dice against Evasion 8 for only 6, showing 1s.<br /> <br /> Rolling 3 withering damage from EASM for one damage.<br /> <br /> Eragan 5i 14p 17ph 5wp<br /> Pilaf 8i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> Having missed by 2 Eragan activates 3m 2i Hopping Firecracker Evasion with 7m Unassailable Body of Fire. Blasting off from the gigantic army and setting them ablaze on the way out. Enhancing the attack roll with another 6m, rolling 11 dice and 3 autosuccesses against Parry 5 for exactly 5 and striking. Dealing 4 dice of lethal, plus an additional level due to decisive damage against battlegroups, for a total of 4 levels, the army is set ablaze. Anima level 3<br /> <br /> Eragan 3i 14p 1ph 5wp<br /> Pilaf 8i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan 3i 14p 6ph 5wp<br /> Pilaf 8i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> Pilaf orders the army of nightmares to attack, rolling 12 dice for 6 successes.<br /> <br /> Eragan 3i 14p 6ph 5wp<br /> Pilaf 8i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Army of nightmares takes 2L from the ongoing fire.<br /> <br /> Army of nightmares close back into range with Eragan and attack, rolling 18 dice, Eregan will defend with 3m Ember Amid Smoke. Rolling 18 dice against Evasion 8 and incrdibly getting only 5 successes, showing 1s.<br /> <br /> Rolling withering damage against the Nightmares, 3 dice for 1.<br /> <br /> Eragan 3i 14p 6ph 5wp<br /> Pilaf 8i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> 3 anima damage rolled nets only one<br /> <br /> Eregan activates 6m 1wp 1ahl Raging Fire Dragon Spirit.<br /> <br /> Eragan 3i 14p 0ph 4wp<br /> Pilaf 7i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan 2i 14p 5ph 4wp<br /> Pilaf 7i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> Wanting the crash bonuse Pilaf attacks Eragan with a withering strike, defending with EAS. Rolling 16 dice against an Evasion of 8, and getting 9, showing no 1s, but no 10s either. Then rolling 12 damage for 6, sending Eragan stumbling back into the crowd.<br /> <br /> Eragan -4i 14p 2ph 4wp<br /> Pilaf 19i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Army of nightmares takes another 2 levels from the ongoing fire<br /> <br /> The nightmares attack, Eragan trying desperately to keep from death here by using another 3m EAS. Rolling 12 dice against evasion 7 for only 3, showing 1s.<br /> <br /> Dealing 3 withering damage back to the group for 1 more level, reducing their magnitude to zero!<br /> <br /> Checking for route, rolling 4 willpower and making it with 2.<br /> <br /> Eragan 1i 13p 0ph 4wp<br /> Pilaf 19i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> 3 anima dice deal 2 withering damage.<br /> <br /> Eragan attempts a withering strike against Pilaf, trying to knock down his dangerous amount of initiative. Using a 3m full excellency and 2m Arcing Levinbolt Precision. Rolling 20 dice against parry 7 for 12, and then 11 damage for 8, hurling Crimson Horizion and bouncing it off the Cataphract's impressive breastplate.<br /> <br /> Eragan 10i 8p 0ph 4wp<br /> Pilaf 9i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan 9i 8p 5ph 4wp<br /> Pilaf 9i 20m 6wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> 3 anima damage deals 2 points<br /> <br /> In one motion snatching the skycutter back and spinning around to throw it again, with another 3m excellency 2m Arcing Levinbolt. Rolling 20 dice against Parry 6, Pilaf will spend a willpower to raise it to 7. Still getting 11 on the attack and punching through. Dealing another 9 damage, crashing Pilaf.<br /> <br /> Eragan 24i 8p 0ph 4wp<br /> Pilaf 0i 20m 5wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Pilaf needs to hit this next attack, so he goes all out with a command action, telling the army to Engage Eragan. Rolling 12 dice for 4.<br /> <br /> Eragan 24i 8p 0ph 4wp<br /> Pilaf 0i 20m 5wp<br /> Nightmares 4i<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Burning bonfire deals another 2 damage to the army.<br /> <br /> The nightmares surge forth and surround Eragan, this being their only chance with their initiative to properly engage. Eragan defends with 3m EAS and a willpower for a total evasion of 9. Rolling 15 dice they get...6, showing 1s.<br /> <br /> They take 3 withering from EAS, which deals 2 damage<br /> <br /> Eragan 24i 5p 0ph 3wp<br /> Pilaf 0i 20m 5wp<br /> Nightmares 1i<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan 23i 5p 5ph 3wp<br /> Pilaf 0i 20m 5wp<br /> Nightmares 1i<br /> <br /> 3 anima damage deals only 1<br /> <br /> Eragan will attempt a decisive strike against the Nightmares. Using 5m 1wp Exploding Weapon Technique, and 2m excellency. Rolling 14 dice against parry 5 for 7. Then rolling 26 damage for 8 levels, but with 4 9s and 10s, rolling another 5 for another two damage. Then because of how decisives work on battlegroups another 7 levels, for a total of 14.<br /> <br /> One magnitude immidiately fills and the group checks for rout, rolling 4 dice and getting it with 2. Then rolling another level fills and immidiately checks again, rolling 4 dice and failing with 1, the battlegroup disolves around Eragan into what it always was, only dreams.<br /> <br /> As Eragan depleted 2 levels of magnitude and got double initiative breaks, Eragan resets to 13i.<br /> <br /> Eragan 13i 3p 0ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf -1i 20m 5wp<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Pilaf, enraged by this, throws himself at Eragan, spending another willpower into a withering attack. Pilaf will defend with 3m EAS. Rolling 16 dice against Evasion 8, making it with a total of 12, still showing 1s.<br /> <br /> Rolling 15 damage for only 2.<br /> <br /> Eragan 11i 3p 0ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf 1i 20m 4wp<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan 10i 3p 5ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf 1i 20m 4wp<br /> <br /> 3 anima deals, thankfully, no damage.<br /> <br /> Not wanting to crash Pilaf the turn he recovers from crash, or the one after and miss out on initiative break, Eragan takes a full defense.<br /> <br /> Eragan 9i 3p 5ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf 1i 20m 4wp<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Pilaf isn't having it, and spending another willpower on a witering attack. Rolling 16 dice against Evasion 9 for only 6 total, the blade swinging wide and showing 1s.<br /> <br /> Eragan 9i 3p 5ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf 1i 20m 3wp<br /> <br /> Round 7<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan 8i 3p 10ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf 1i 20m 3wp<br /> <br /> 3 anima deals again no damage.<br /> <br /> Eragan hefts his boomarang and strikes Pilaf with an 3m excellency, 2m Levinbolt attack. Rolling 20 dice against Parry 7, grabbing 9. Then rolling 8 damage for 4.<br /> <br /> Eragan 18i 3p 5ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf -3i 20m 3wp<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Pilaf desperately tries to swing back, rolling 16 dice against EAS's Evasion 8, making it with 8 showing 1s, and rolling 11 damage for 4.<br /> <br /> Eragan 14i 3p 2ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf 1i 20m 3wp<br /> <br /> Round 8<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan 13i 3p 7ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf 1i 20m 3wp<br /> <br /> 3 anima deals 1 damage, re-crashing Pilaf for no bonus because of the recovery period.<br /> <br /> Eragan keeps hammering at it, the hard armor of the Fey creature difficult to penetrate. Rolling another attack with 3m excellency and 2m levinbolt. 20 dice gives 13 successes (6 10s, wow) and then 12 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Eragan 20i 3p 2ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf -6i 20m 3wp<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Pilaf again tries to wither his way back, and this time only a 2m excellency is brought up. Rolling 16 dice against Evasion 8 for only 7, and showing 1s.<br /> <br /> Eragan 20i 3p 0ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf -6i 20m 3wp<br /> <br /> Round 9<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan 19i 3p 5ph 1wp<br /> Pilaf -6i 20m 3wp<br /> <br /> 3 anima damage deals nothing<br /> <br /> Eragan will try to end this with a decisive strike. Using 5m 1wp Exploding Weapon Technique, and 3m excellency. Rolling 15 dice against Parry 7, and getting 10, hitting. Rolling 22 damage for 13, with 6 9s and 10s, rolling for one more damage. The monster isn't slain, but he's into his -2s.<br /> <br /> Eragan 3i 0p 0ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf -6i 20m 3wp<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> Pilaf goes in for an initiative shift, rolling 14 dice and an autosuccess from willpower, against evasion 7, getting it with 7, showing 1s. Dealing 11 damage for 5, initiative shift!<br /> <br /> Rolling 9 dice for join battle and getting 3, adding that to the 4 for a new 7i.<br /> <br /> Eragan -2i 0p 0ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf 7i 20m 2wp<br /> <br /> Attacking again, rolling 14 dice against Evasion 6 for 7, then 12 damage for 6<br /> <br /> Eragan -8i 0p 0ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf 14i 20m 2wp<br /> <br /> Round 10<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan -9i 0p 5ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf 14i 20m 2wp<br /> <br /> Pilaf attacks again, this time decisively, rolling 14 dice to hit, and doing so easily with 8, but showing 1s. Then rolling 14 damage for 7, putting Eragan into -2s!<br /> <br /> Eragan -8i 0p 5ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf 3i 20m 2wp<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> 3 anima damage deals 2<br /> <br /> Eragan attacks back, swinging wildly and hurtling his skycutter around to slam into the fey knight. Rolling 15 dice against parry 6, and missing with 5!<br /> <br /> Eragan -9i 0p 5ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf 1i 20m 2wp<br /> <br /> Round 11<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan -10i 0p 10ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf 1i 20m 2wp<br /> <br /> Pilaf, dodging the blow, slices another withering strike at the dragonblood, who will defend with 3m EAS. Rolling 14 dice against an evasion of 8 and getting only 3.<br /> <br /> Withering damage to Pilaf 3 dice for 3 successes, initiative shift again!<br /> <br /> Eragan rolls Join Battle, 6 dice for 6 successes, getting 9i.<br /> <br /> Eragan 9i 0p 7ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf -2i 20m 2wp<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> 3 anima damage deals 3 lethal levels<br /> <br /> Eragan withers Pilaf again with 3m excellency, 2m Levinbolt, rolling 18 dice against Parry 6, after Pilaf spends another WP, for 8, then rolling 8 damage for 4<br /> <br /> Eragan 13i 0p 2ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf -6i 20m 1wp<br /> <br /> Round 11<br /> ==========<br /> Eragan 12i 0p 7ph 0wp<br /> Pilaf -6i 20m 1wp<br /> <br /> 3 anima damage deals 1 lethal, finally killing Pilaf<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T04:15:46-07:00","id":1342325,"title":"","content":"BTW, what are p and ph in your resource-counting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T05:36:35-07:00","id":1342335,"title":"","content":"I was assuming \u201cpersonal\u201c and \u201cperipheral.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T06:26:58-07:00","id":1342337,"title":"","content":"Duh, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T17:17:21-07:00","id":1342607,"title":"","content":"This took way too fucking long.<br /> <br /> The Contestants:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6245\" target=\"_blank\">Shining Topaz</a> is fresh off her exaltation and is attacking the local fae freehold. The Freehold consists of 1 QC Cataphract, 1 QC Lorelei, and a S5 battlegroup of QC hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> I assume no stunts for the QCs, and only give Topaz stunt dice if I had one for her. I kinda ran out of steam in the end.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Fight:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Fresh off her Exaltation in a tournament, Shining Topaz has decided to take on the local fae freehold to rid her father\u2019s kingdom of the menace that is the fae. She bears the best mortal arms and armor, as befitting her position as the second in line to the throne. Unfortunately, by taking the fight to them, they benefit from their existing fortifications.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Join Battle:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz puts 10m into JB, rolling a total of 22 dice. Her anima goes to Burning. She gets nine sux, for 12i<br /> <br /> S5 Hobgoblins roll 6 dice for JB. They get 7 sux, for 10i.<br /> <br /> Cataphract rolls 11 dice for JB. They get 2 sux, for 5i.<br /> <br /> Lorelei uses Untouchable Performer Technique for 5m, rolling 13 dice for JB and attempting to inspire adoration in Topaz. Topaz spends 8m to raise her resolve to a total of 11, because she b