Battle 6<br /> <br /> Wrackstaff 14, +6 for 6m (Damage 15/4)<br /> Parry 6, +3 for 6m<br /> Soak/Hardness: 10/4<br /> <br /> Personal:13 Peripheral:26<br /> <br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon Vitality: 5m, Add to soak.<br /> <br /> Eyes of the Wood Dragon: 4m, add Perception to withering damage, and can make piercing attacks.<br /> <br /> Mind-Over-Body Meditation: 5m 1wp, Heal some damaged health levels.<br /> <br /> Soul-Marking Style: 3m 2i, Decisive attack marks the target making them easier to hit<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon Form: 10m, Gain temporary health levels.<br /> <br /> Spirit Wracking Method: Useless against non-spirits.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T05:21:31-07:00","id":1342692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1342647#post1342647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well here's the basics anyway. I don't think I forgot anything vital.<br /> <br /> Wood<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Strength 3<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 5<br /> Perception 5<br /> <br /> Join Battle 6<br /> <br /> Wrackstaff 14, +6 for 6m (Damage 15/4)<br /> Parry 6, +3 for 6m<br /> Soak/Hardness: 10/4<br /> <br /> Personal:13 Peripheral:26<br /> <br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon Vitality: 5m, Add to soak.<br /> <br /> Eyes of the Wood Dragon: 4m, add Perception to withering damage, and can make piercing attacks.<br /> <br /> Mind-Over-Body Meditation: 5m 1wp, Heal some damaged health levels.<br /> <br /> Soul-Marking Style: 3m 2i, Decisive attack marks the target making them easier to hit<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon Form: 10m, Gain temporary health levels.<br /> <br /> Spirit Wracking Method: Useless against non-spirits.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially the wood immaculate should have some archery? Any given attack would have to be archery or martial arts, but given the options to use a bow as a staff it seems somewhat intended.<br /> It potentially would matter a lot, since I think it would free them from suffering counter-attacks. Unless I'm missing something.<br /> Other thought on immaculate tactics - if all the monks spend a round aiming, they get mote regeneration and 3 non-charm dice, while my impression is the solar still spends their turn and 5m on Ri8DS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T06:18:57-07:00","id":1342702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1342692#post1342692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Potentially the wood immaculate should have some archery? Any given attack would have to be archery or martial arts, but given the options to use a bow as a staff it seems somewhat intended.<br /> It potentially would matter a lot, since I think it would free them from suffering counter-attacks. Unless I'm missing something.<br /> Other thought on immaculate tactics - if all the monks spend a round aiming, they get mote regeneration and 3 non-charm dice, while my impression is the solar still spends their turn and 5m on Ri8DS.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s true on archery, I\u2019m not sure how far I should go into each of them though to give backup abilities. It could keep them safe from counterattacks though. I should also have given them some ox bodies.<br /> <br /> The aiming thing is also a good tactic, in fact since Against the World drains 1i per turn you could theoretically wait that out forever. There\u2019s other things you can do too like keep firing shots until you pierce the Solars defence, and then just stop and wait for the initiative reset before resuming attacking. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s really appropriate though. Clearly Against the World and Ri8DS are meant to trigger multiple counterattacks in one turn and not just have enemies ignore you while you use it. It also doesn\u2019t work if the Solar has any allies, since they can protect the whole circle with War Lion Stance and the circle can just keep attacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T20:01:03-07:00","id":1342857,"title":"","content":"I have finished generating the <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6298\" target=\"_blank\">Air Immaculate</a>. Feel free to suggest anything that might help her win. I shall generate the Fire Immaculate next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T21:46:18-07:00","id":1342871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1342638#post1342638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I mean at that point why care about anything really? The Scarlet Empire bugging you? Go tear down the Imperial Palace, the Deliberative, and the Thosand Scales. Immaculate Order kind of getting on your nerves? Go knock over the Palace Sublime, that should make them think twice before scrounging up one of their little Wyld Hunts. Then maybe walk into Thorns completely casually and eradicate the presence of death from it, it's got a nice view, nice palace, could be a fun home to own.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. This post made me laugh way too loud at work.<br /> <br /> 2. It's a testament to 3e's ruleset, and the setting and vibe of the game itself, honestly, that this character that would be an absolute mechanical nightmare overshadowing every session in many other systems is instead (honestly) in some senses sort of a bit player in the -grand- grand scheme of my players' storyline. Like, he ensures whomever he's with isn't especially likely to be slain via battle or assassin, and he -equalizes- large conflicts Dynasty Warrior style, but he really can only be in one place at a time and he's not especially socially adept beyond having a high Resolve. The most recent thing he did that really swung things too much in the broader campaign was just...-equalize- two of Mask's key Abyssals in the River Province (particularly since he's got both Single Point and Edge of Morning Sunlight...they didn't have a good time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","user":"Zeesun","date":". 10-22-2019, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T22:19:52-07:00","id":1342877,"title":"","content":"Apologies, I've just been in actual 2e games where players have gone to the imperial palace with an unstable protoshinmaic vortex, told the deliberative &quot;you serve me now or the city will be destroyed.&quot; and when the dynasts refused they dropped it, Heavenly Guardien Defenced the explosion and swaggered off in his Kireeki class skyship that he built in a week. <br /> <br /> I think that was just before he broke into the loom of fate to boss around some pattern spiders into helping him out in a duel. I'm not sure my memory is a bit fuzzy that far back. <br /> <br /> Either way it's not a gameplay experience I'm super keen on repeating, which in my experience 3e does a good job of...mostly. Sometimes though I get a feeling uncomfortably close to that old 2e feel where the players just slap around Raksi because there's nothing she can do about it. She's an Essence 7 elder Lunar with her own nation, show a little respect at least...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T22:22:51-07:00","id":1342878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1342871#post1342871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(particularly since he's got both Single Point and Edge of Morning Sunlight...they didn't have a good time).</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait, can you use Edge of Morning Sunlight with Single Point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T05:08:44-07:00","id":1342920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1342878#post1342878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, can you use Edge of Morning Sunlight with Single Point?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Edge of Morning Sunlight doesn't say it can be used with other abilities. So no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T13:30:44-07:00","id":1343003,"title":"","content":"Hey, just found this thread, and I like it a lot. Respect to DrLoveMonkey particularly for starting the thread, and for all the contributors.<br /> <br /> Something I have struggled with--and I believe that this is pretty standard for Exalted games--is putting up challenging but balanced enemies for them to fight. (Socially, I can pretty much dominate if necessary.)<br /> <br /> If I put the group's characters on here, could someone help me out with this? In terms of composition, the group is two Solars (Investigation Supernal Twilight + Stealth Supernal Solar) and two Lunars (Chimeric Tyrant Lizard-Butterfly Changing Moon + Horse No Moon). Also, would people also offer advice--perhaps in another thread--as to how to best improve the characters with experience from the starting point given? Like, efficient Charm progression, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T14:12:11-07:00","id":1343008,"title":"","content":"In what way are you having trouble? Making fights hard enough, not making fights too hard, or both depending?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T14:35:44-07:00","id":1343014,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, 'making fights hard enough' due to my concern about accidentally TPKing the group through my own stupidity. (I have no issues TPKing my group through <i>their</i> stupidity.)<br /> <br /> It's not really an optimized group, and the combat quality varies, but none of them are <i>that </i>squishy. The Changing Moon and the Night are the two best combatants, but neither of them really would stack up against, well, maybe any Exalt shown in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T14:51:31-07:00","id":1343019,"title":"","content":"I find the &quot;once per story, instead of dying the PC can take a permanent crippling effect&quot; really useful for that. If I accidentally overcook the encounter, the PCs are just going to lose a hand or something. (That's why the Gorilla-totem has a snake arm instead of his original arm. The Full Moon's missing eye is his own fault, that's what happens when you try to solo a Wyld Hunt you lured to you after sending away all your allies.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T15:41:18-07:00","id":1343033,"title":"","content":"I guess. The issue there is with <i>permanent</i>. Most of my players would essentially equate this with death, with the same end result. Again, I don't have an issue punishing players when they screw up. I, frankly, don't think it's very fair to ask my players to accept permanent debilitations to their characters because I screwed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T15:53:26-07:00","id":1343035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343033#post1343033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess. The issue there is with <i>permanent</i>. Most of my players would essentially equate this with death, with the same end result. Again, I don't have an issue punishing players when they screw up. I, frankly, don't think it's very fair to ask my players to accept permanent debilitations to their characters because I screwed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Permanent is...not necessarily completely accurate here. In the rule at the end it reminds you that Exalted is a world of miracles, and gods, Exalted, artifacts, ect can be used to fix these things after the fact. Just don't make it totally trivial.<br /> <br /> The rule is on page 201 of the corebook if you haven't seen it yet. Having a buffer of 5 emergency health levels, and really you could easily houserule that last bracket to be 5-8 or more even, really helps. It puts so many layers of defense in for the players for dying. If an enemy is going to one shot them they need to build up the crazy amount of initiative needed to one-hit a player, keep it long enough to launch a decisive, and then don't mess up the damage roll, and have done it to a character that's already used his crippling injury for the story.<br /> <br /> If your player has 13 health levels the average decisive damage you need to one-shot him is 33i. If you're using the rule and saying only 5 damage can be negated it's 45i. There's basically no way to build that up in a single turn, so on the way up there some PC is going to knock down the enemy that's trying for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, try running more action scenes, not just combats, in a shorter period of time, but making them much easier. If your players are laying siege to a demon fortress with Octavian in them, instead of just letting them walk in there and roll Join Battle against Octavian, his Agata, his Infernal summoner and a pair of Blood Apes or something. Have a battle against outrider scouts that are trying to get away to warn the fortress, then one where they're outside at the gate facing a battlegroup of cultists and their leader, then maybe a chase scene or something where they leap through an ever changing and shifting fortress-maze that's trying to crush them, until finally they get to the throne room.<br /> <br /> That helps in a lot of ways. Firstly it can help you stealthily fine-tune things that you may have misjudged. So if after the battlegroup of cultists they're looking hurt and a bit out of motes, maybe tone down the maze, and drop the apes from the final fight. Secondly, it can help for the overall flow and grandiosity of Exalted antagonists and situations. The kinds of things that Solars fight are massive, entire nations, mile-high behemoths, stuff like that, so it makes it actually feel big. Thirdly, it helps make encounters <i>challenging </i>without making them <i>deadly</i>. If your big action section is focused on draining your PC's motes, willpower, and maybe dealing a point or two of health level damage, they're really going to feel the squeeze. They'll be rationing motes, trying to use tactics instead of just powering through everything, and maybe even consider retreating if they reach the last leg with nothing left.<br /> <br /> Lastly it just opens up the enemy variety a lot. There's still a bunch of enemies that are so weak you shouldn't really use them, all starting a fight with them is going to do is let your PCs regen motes, but the things they battle don't <i>need </i>to actually be able to win, they just need to force your players to spend 10m every round fighting them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T19:55:52-07:00","id":1343082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343003#post1343003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, just found this thread, and I like it a lot. Respect to DrLoveMonkey particularly for starting the thread, and for all the contributors.<br /> <br /> Something I have struggled with--and I believe that this is pretty standard for Exalted games--is putting up challenging but balanced enemies for them to fight. (Socially, I can pretty much dominate if necessary.)<br /> <br /> If I put the group's characters on here, could someone help me out with this? In terms of composition, the group is two Solars (Investigation Supernal Twilight + Stealth Supernal Solar) and two Lunars (Chimeric Tyrant Lizard-Butterfly Changing Moon + Horse No Moon). Also, would people also offer advice--perhaps in another thread--as to how to best improve the characters with experience from the starting point given? Like, efficient Charm progression, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey hey, I\u2019m always up for Lunar workshopping, can you post in another thread their basic builds and preferred tactics? <br /> <br /> Prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T20:00:52-07:00","id":1343083,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6299\" target=\"_blank\">Earth</a> and <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6300\" target=\"_blank\">Fire</a> Immaculate done. I gave the Fire Immaculate Steel Devil, because of compatible form weapons, but I'm not entirely sure if that's kosher for the purposes of the exercise. Dual Slaying Stance gives a passive +2 parry, which makes him one of the most likely opponents for Topaz to lose initiative too, what with the likelihood of missing the counterattack and losing initiative thereby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 10-22-2019, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T22:11:05-07:00","id":1343099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1342878#post1342878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, can you use Edge of Morning Sunlight with Single Point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that it's a Melee charm, normally, no. My Dawn's artifact reaper daiklave, however, has it as an Evocation, which he took.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T01:30:36-07:00","id":1343105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343083#post1343083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://&quot;https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6299&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Earth</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how valid it is to have both &quot;Attack&quot; and &quot;Defence&quot; as specialities on the same ability.<br /> <br /> <s>I'm REALLY not sure about an Immaculate monk with a Defining Intimacy to the Immaculate Faith. I realise there are Immaculates beyond the authority of the Realm, but still.</s> Oh right, Lookshy.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon Form probably means you're better off swapping the Strength and Stamina scores. I realise you lose OBT health levels but...<br /> <br /> Pain Tolerance is an insanely expensive Merit. But with the Earth Anima power and so many Ox-bodies you can really rack up the -0s. (5 health levels for +1 Charm Accuracy and +1 Withering Damage is pretty costly but you're going to struggle to hit this Solar and you're low on motes.)<br /> <br /> Finally, Evocations brother. Faith's Pillar and Fist of Titans are great. Investing in Deeb Charms over amazing Evocations is selling your Immaculate short.<br /> <br /> Finally, finally, I REALLY like Smash attacks. If you connect the Solar is going to take Flurry penalties. Good Infinite (Martial Arts) Mastery approximation with Earth Dragon Form. A Stone of the Ram's Horn would bring the cost of your Smashing attacks to a measly 1i. Coupled with Fist of Titans Accuracy bonus to Smashes (and waving the Defence cost) this is fantastic. Alternatively, Faith's Pillar eliminates the Initative cost entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-23-2019, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T02:24:59-07:00","id":1343107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343105#post1343105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how valid it is to have both &quot;Attack&quot; and &quot;Defence&quot; as specialities on the same ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not very valid, as it happens. When you take a specialty in one thing and its opposite, &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1332337#post1332337\">the Storyteller is allowed to glower dolefully at you until you change that</a>&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said the immaculate could simply have a single specialty in their weapon of choice and achieve the same result short of being disarmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 10-23-2019, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T03:01:39-07:00","id":1343109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan;n1343083[URL=&amp;quot;https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6300&amp;quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire[/URL] Immaculate</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly consider Dragon Soul Burst (accessed through the Glory Sphere) to bypass Hardness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T05:33:55-07:00","id":1343136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343105#post1343105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how valid it is to have both &quot;Attack&quot; and &quot;Defence&quot; as specialities on the same ability.<br /> <br /> <s>I'm REALLY not sure about an Immaculate monk with a Defining Intimacy to the Immaculate Faith. I realise there are Immaculates beyond the authority of the Realm, but still.</s> Oh right, Lookshy.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon Form probably means you're better off swapping the Strength and Stamina scores. I realise you lose OBT health levels but...<br /> <br /> Pain Tolerance is an insanely expensive Merit. But with the Earth Anima power and so many Ox-bodies you can really rack up the -0s. (5 health levels for +1 Charm Accuracy and +1 Withering Damage is pretty costly but you're going to struggle to hit this Solar and you're low on motes.)<br /> <br /> Finally, Evocations brother. Faith's Pillar and Fist of Titans are great. Investing in Deeb Charms over amazing Evocations is selling your Immaculate short.<br /> <br /> Finally, finally, I REALLY like Smash attacks. If you connect the Solar is going to take Flurry penalties. Good Infinite (Martial Arts) Mastery approximation with Earth Dragon Form. A Stone of the Ram's Horn would bring the cost of your Smashing attacks to a measly 1i. Coupled with Fist of Titans Accuracy bonus to Smashes (and waving the Defence cost) this is fantastic. Alternatively, Faith's Pillar eliminates the Initative cost entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have fixed the specialities, thank you. <br /> <br /> What books are Faith's Pillar and Fist of Titans' in? I think Fist is in Arms, but I also think it's not a Grand Goremaul, and thus not compatible with the style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T06:12:10-07:00","id":1343146,"title":"","content":"Faith's Pillar is in the Dragonblood book. It's an heirloom of House Mnemon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T06:21:13-07:00","id":1343148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343136#post1343136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have fixed the specialities, thank you. <br /> <br /> What books are Faith's Pillar and Fist of Titans' in? I think Fist is in Arms, but I also think it's not a Grand Goremaul, and thus not compatible with the style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arms of the Chosen page 28: Fist of Titans (White Jade Grand Goremaul, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> What Fire Has Wrought page 320: Faith\u2019s Pillar (White Jade Grand Goremaul, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T06:33:10-07:00","id":1343151,"title":"","content":"Johns suggestions are definitely good if you\u2019re making PC Dragonblooded, a couple of them might be a bit...excessive for running a fight like this. Mostly the hearthstones and evocations. Technically every artifact has evocations so they should have them and why not use them, but it just doesn\u2019t seem that fair for some reason. Though it\u2019s your choice of course.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re going to do it there\u2019s some other artifacts to look at, like the wood using Daring Venture, the air using Heaven Typoon, a few others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T06:43:42-07:00","id":1343152,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, is there a ratio for starting Solars vs Dragon Bloods? I imagine that a ratio of 2 average Dragon Bloods per starting Solar might be a fair fight but correct me if I am wrong (and I know there is lots of variation among exalted). The Solars have better Charms and the Dragon Bloods start with better toys I would imagine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T06:46:12-07:00","id":1343153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1342857#post1342857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have finished generating the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6298&amp;quot;]Air</a> Immaculate[/URL]. Feel free to suggest anything that might help her win. I shall generate the Fire Immaculate next.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stealth Charms might help synergize with ADS. Especially Shimmering Heat-Mirage Tactic if they can stay at Short throwing chakrams, and even just trying to establish stealth to burn Solar motes.<br /> <br /> Else, you have a bunch of Occult charms. Consider sorcery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T07:33:05-07:00","id":1343170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343152#post1343152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, is there a ratio for starting Solars vs Dragon Bloods? I imagine that a ratio of 2 average Dragon Bloods per starting Solar might be a fair fight but correct me if I am wrong (and I know there is lots of variation among exalted). The Solars have better Charms and the Dragon Bloods start with better toys I would imagine</div> </div> </div> </div>That very much depends on the makeup of the fighters in question. If you\u2019re talking a perfect circle with a loremaster Twilight, diplomat Eclipse, acrobat Night, high priest Zenith and swordsman Dawn, and they\u2019re fighting ten dedicated Wyld Hunt fighters then the Solars are going to die, or at least most of them are, probably.<br /> <br /> If the Dawn has Miracles charms and/or the Heaven Sword Flash deal, he could theoretically kill all ten DBs in round one of combat before they even act and save his whole circle, or at least survive until he\u2019s the last one standing and then maybe win. If he\u2019s got like 6 melee charms spread between effects like Glorious Solar Saber and Iron Raptor Technique and stuff, then no. A really combat focused DB at the start is easily a match or more for a non-combat focused Solar, and without reactor charms like Spirit Gathering Temper or Against the World the Dawn will eventually run out of motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T07:35:41-07:00","id":1343172,"title":"","content":"The solar in this fight should also probably pick up a Twice Strikes Lightning prism. It will let him use Hail Shattering to cancel up to 2 successes, and enhance Rising Sun Slash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T09:20:46-07:00","id":1343193,"title":"","content":"Good advice for the Wood Immaculate here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314291-help-me-design-the-invincible-sword-dynast?p=1314331#post1314331\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...31#post1314331</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T10:07:13-07:00","id":1343204,"title":"","content":"Looking at the rules, it seems that a Dawn Solar can let loose some devastating attacks and great defences, but this costs essence. Can I assume that if the Dragon Bloods can somehow survive the attacks and wait for the Solar to run out of Essence they would have the advantage and be able to defeat the Solar (broadly speaking)? Outnumbering the Solar helps since they can absorb some losses as well as all of them are taking initiative from the Solar, forcing it to initiative crash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T10:23:30-07:00","id":1343205,"title":"","content":"The key is in surviving those attacks, and reactor charms making that whole \u201crun out of motes\u201d thing take forever. A Solar can be lethal to a DB with 2 ox bodies from 20 initiative easily. So if you have 20i and activate Ready in Eight Directions Stance the DBs might just all kill themselves on you in a single round trying to land attacks. Or maybe like 3 or 4 out of five do, and then you\u2019ve just bought yourself a lot more time to deal with the last 1-2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T14:45:41-07:00","id":1343277,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> The purpose of the excersice is not to make optimal DBs. The purpose is to see if an optimally built dawn straight out of Chargen can defeat 5 generic immaculates. That's why I'm not sure how kosher giving the Fire Immaculate Steel Devil Style is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T20:49:35-07:00","id":1343340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343205#post1343205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key is in surviving those attacks, and reactor charms making that whole \u201crun out of motes\u201d thing take forever. A Solar can be lethal to a DB with 2 ox bodies from 20 initiative easily. So if you have 20i and activate Ready in Eight Directions Stance the DBs might just all kill themselves on you in a single round trying to land attacks. Or maybe like 3 or 4 out of five do, and then you\u2019ve just bought yourself a lot more time to deal with the last 1-2.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would it be better for the DBs to enter their Forms asap or try to get the reflexive? I don't want to run the DBs as dumb, just generic (as opposed to optimized).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T22:50:32-07:00","id":1343349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343340#post1343340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Would it be better for the DBs to enter their Forms asap or try to get the reflexive? I don't want to run the DBs as dumb, just generic (as opposed to optimized).</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the form. Fire Dragon only has one shot to activate reflexively, either you get it or you don't. With the Solar in heavy artifact plate the Air Dragon one will be next to impossible to activate, the Earth Dragon one could happen but it'd be a while and relies on being attacked by a low initiative Solar, so unlikely. Wood dragon can only be activated reflexively while healing halfway through the fight, and the water aspect...maybe if you can get enough initiative to beat the hardness (11+) then with standard Solar ox bodies you have a shot, if you can land the decisive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T02:39:21-07:00","id":1343550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343340#post1343340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be better for the DBs to enter their Forms asap or try to get the reflexive? I don't want to run the DBs as dumb, just generic (as opposed to optimized).</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that with some forms, you can be better off not activating them and having ~10 more motes to play with - Fire Dragon Form is tremendously useless against a Solar who can cancel onslaught at-will and has the pools and Charms to basically never ever miss you with a decisive, Wood Dragon Form is basically an extra Ox-Body attached to the ability to reset an objectively bad Charm, and Water Dragon Form is a not terribly impressive soak boost for 10m until your opponent gets wounded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T03:57:52-07:00","id":1343555,"title":"","content":"Fire Dragon might be useful if you can block one of the decisive counterattacks. A Solar has the pools and charms to never miss a decisive attack, but they don\u2019t have the motes even with stuff like Against the World to both full defence and full attack five times a round. If the Solar is using a full 9m defence against every attack five times a round, he probably doesn\u2019t have the motes even with Against the World and Essence Gathering Temper to fuel a full five attacks also. He\u2019ll probably just use 4m for Excellent Strike and Divine Executioner Stance, at which point he may still miss.<br /> <br /> Then again it\u2019s probably not worth the wasted turn and motes activating Fire Dragon anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T14:44:30-07:00","id":1343659,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6301\" target=\"_blank\">Water Immaculate</a> and <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6302\" target=\"_blank\">Wood Immaculate</a> done.<br /> <br /> I'll probably start rolling up the fight some time tomorrow. Don't know how long it'll take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T19:04:49-07:00","id":1343699,"title":"","content":"When Shining Topaz exalted, she exalted in front of a pair of DBs from Lookshy. When her father refused to disown her, Lookshy declared war with the goal of killing the Anathema that had inhabited Shining Topaz. Terek was in no way prepared to fight a war with Lookshy, and once their field force had made the river trip, the country folded in short order. Within months, the capital was under siege, after barely a week local adherents of the immaculate faith had thrown open the city gates.<br /> <br /> The five immaculate shikari of the wyld hunt manage to corner Topaz in the palace during the final stages of the assault.<br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> Note: I am assuming a 1pt stunt on everything Topaz does, every roll and every application of a static value.<br /> -<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Join Battle:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6392\" target=\"_blank\">Shining Topaz</a> spends 10m on Awareness Excellency, rolling 23 dice for 10 sux. She starts with 13i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6298\" target=\"_blank\">Nefvarin Vita</a> spends 5m on Precision Observation Method, adding 2 sux and 1 die. She rolls 9 dice for 2+2 sux. She starts with 7i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6299\" target=\"_blank\">Bounteous Pumice</a> spends 3m on Precision Observation Method, adding 1 sux and 1 die. He rolls 7 dice for 3+1 sux. He starts with 7i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6300\" target=\"_blank\">Yan Tu Ja </a>spends 5m on Precision Observation Method, adding 2 sux and 1 die. He rolls 11 dice for 3+2 sux. He starts with 8i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6301\" target=\"_blank\">Terasu Linwei</a> spends 5m on Precision Observation Method, adding 2 sux and 1 die. She rolls 11 dice for 4+2 sux. She starts with 9i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6302\" target=\"_blank\">Yushoto Nali</a> spends 5m on Precision Observation Method, adding 2 sux and 1 die. She rolls 9 dice for 4+2 sux. She starts with 9i.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (24/34m, 9/9wp, -0): 13i<br /> Terasu Linwei (29/34m, 7wp, -0): 9i<br /> Yushoto Nali (30/35m, 6/6wp, -0): 9i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (29/34m, 6/6wp, -0): 8i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (30/35m, 7/7wp, -0): 7i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (30/33m, 5/5wp, -0): 7i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 5m, 1wp on Fivefold Bulwark Stance. 5m are committed.<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei makes a withering attack. Linwei spends 3m on Become the Hammer, Shining Topaz spends 6m, 1wp on Against the World Stance (6m committed) and 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense and 2m on the melee excellency to raise her parry to 10. Linwei rolls 19 dice for 9 sux, missing. Topaz gains 2vm and 1i, putting her at 14i. Linwei enters Water Aura.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali makes a withering attack. Nali spends 4m on Eyes of the Wood Dragon and 1m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense and 2vm on the melee excellency to raise her parry to 10. Nali rolls 15 dice for 5 sux, missing. Topaz gains 6vm and 1i, putting her at 15i. Nali enters Wood Aura.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja spends 7m on Fire Dragon Form. 7m are committed and Ja enters Fire Aura.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita makes a withering attack. Vita spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense and 6vm on the melee excellency to raise her parry to 12. Vita rolls 22 dice for 17 sux, hitting with 6 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 12+6-14=5. Vita rolls 5 dice rerolling 6s and deals 2 withering damage. This puts Vita at 10i and Topaz at 13i. Vita enters Water Aura.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice commits 9m to Earth Dragon Form. He enters Earth Aura.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 2, +5m for all<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (17/23m, 0vm, 7/9wp, -0): 13i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (29/35m, 7/7wp, -0, Water): 10i<br /> Terasu Linwei (26/34m, 7wp, -0, Water): 9i<br /> Yushoto Nali (30/35m, 6/6wp, -0, Wood): 9i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (22/27m, 6/6wp, -0, Fire): 8i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (26/26m, 5/5wp, -0, Earth): 7i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz pays 1i for Against the World Stance, putting her at 12i.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 5m on Ready in Eight Directions.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita commits 8m to Air Dragon Form. She ends her Aura.<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei makes a withering attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1wp on Perfect Strike Discipline to raise her defense to 13. Linwei rolls 22 dice for 20 sux, hitting with 8 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> Topaz counterattacks. Topaz spends 3m on Excellent Strike and 1m on Divine Executioner\u2019s Stance, Linwei spends 6m in Become the Hammer to raise her parry to 9. Topaz rolls 19 dice for 13+1 sux and rerolls 1s for and additional 1 sux. She hits with 7 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 13+4 (divine executioner stance)=17. Topaz rolls 17 dice and deals 8 levels of lethal damage, raising Linwei\u2019s wound penalty to -2.<br /> <br /> Linwei\u2019s attack resolves. 12+8-14=6. Linwei rolls 6 dice rerolling 6s and deals 6 damage, putting her at 16i and Topaz at 7i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali makes a decisive attack. Nali spends 6m on Become the Hammer and 3m,2i on Soul Marking Style, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense and 6m on the Melee Excellency to raise her Parry to 12. Nali rolls 20 dice for 13 sux, Topaz spends 2m on Hail Shattering Practice to make her miss. Topaz gains 2vm and 1i, putting her at 8i. Nali loses 2i, putting her at 5i.<br /> <br /> Topaz counterattacks. She spends 1vm on Divine Executioner Stance, Nali spends 6m on Become the hammer to raise her defense to 10. Topaz rolls 17 dice for 5 sux, missing.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja makes a withering attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1vm on Dipping Swallow Defense and 2m om the Melee Excellency, raising her defense to 10. Ja rolls 22 dice for 9 sux, missing. Topaz gains 3vm and 1i, putting her at 9i.<br /> <br /> Topaz counterattacks. She spends 1vm on Divine Executioner Stance. She rolls 17 dice for 12 sux, hitting with 6 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 9+4(DES)=13. Topaz rolls 13 dice and deals 1 lethal damage. Yan Tu Ja\u2019s wound penalty remains at -0.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice makes a withering attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1vm on Dipping Swallow Defense and 2vm on the melee excellency raising her parry to 10. Pumice rolls 18 dice for 4 sux, missing. Topaz gains 7vm and 1i, putting her at 10i.<br /> <br /> Topaz counterattacks. She pays 1vm to Divine Executioner Stance, Pumice spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise his parry to 9. Topaz rolls 17 dice for 4 sux, missing. Topaz loses 2i, putting her at 8i.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 3, +5m for all<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei (26/34m, 7wp, -2, Water): 16i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (21/27m, 7/7wp, -0, Water): 10i<br /> Yushoto Nali (20/35m, 6/6wp, -0, Wood): 5i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (27/27m, 6/6wp, -0, Fire): 8i<br /> Shining Topaz (11/23m, 6vm, 6/9wp, -0): 8i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (19/26m, 5/5wp, -0, Earth): 7i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz\u2019s initiative resets to 4i, then she pays 1i to Against the World Stance, putting her at 3i.<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei makes a decisive attack. She pays 6m to Become the Hammer and 3m for drowning in blood technique, Topaz spends 1vm on Dipping Swallow Defense and 5vm and 3m on the melee excellency to raise her parry to 13. Linwei rolls 15 dice for 7 sux, missing. Topaz gains 7vm and 1i, putting her at 4i. Linwei loses 3i, putting her at 13i.<br /> <br /> Topaz counterattacks. She spends 1vm on Divine Executioner Stance, Linwei spends 6m on Become the hammer to raise her parry to 7. Topaz rolls 17 dice for 7 sux, hitting with 1 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 4+4(DES)=8. Topaz rolls 8 dice and deals 2 lethal damage. Terasu Linwei\u2019s wound penalty rises to -4.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita makes a withering attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1vm on Dipping Swallow Defense and 5vm and 1m on the melee excellency to raise her parry to 12. Vita rolls 22 dice for 14 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> Topaz counterattacks. Topax spends 1m on Divine Executioner Stance, Vita spends 6m on Become the hammer to raise her parry to 9. Topaz rolls 17 dice for 11 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 4+4 (DES)=8. Topaz rolls 8 dice and deals 2 lethal damage. Vita\u2019s wound penalty is increased to -1.<br /> <br /> Vita\u2019s attack resolves. 13+3-13=2. Vita rolls 3 Overwhelming Damage rerolling 6s and deals 1 withering damage. Putting her at 12i and Topaz at 3i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali makes a withering attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense and 2m on the melee excellency to raise her parry to 10. Nali rolls 20 dice for 4 sux. Topaz gains 1i and 7vm, putting her at 4i.<br /> <br /> Topaz counterattacks. She spends 1vm on Divine Executioner Stance, Nali spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise her parry to 10. Topaz attacks with 17 dice for 4 sux, missing. Topaz loses 2i, putting her at 2i.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja makes a withering attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1vm on Dipping Swallow Defense and 4vm on the melee excellency to raise her parry to 11. Ja rolls 22 dice for 13 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> Topaz counterattacks. She spends 1vm on Divine Executioner Stance. She rolls 17 dice for 9 sux, hitting with 2 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 2+4(DES)=6. Topaz rolls 6 dice and deals 1 lethal damage, raising Yan Tu Ja\u2019s wound penalty to -1.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja\u2019s attack resolves. 13+3-14=2. Ja rolls 4 Overwhelming rerolling 6s and deals 2 withering damage. Putting him at 11i and Topaz at 0i. Against the World Stance breaks and Yan Tu Ja gains 5i putting him at 16i.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice makes a decisive attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense raising her parry to 9. Pumice rolls 18 dice for 9 sux, Topaz spends 1m on Hail Shattering Practice making him miss. Topaz gains 1i, putting her at 1i.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a withering attack at Bounteous Pumice. She spends 1m on Divine Executioner Stance, he spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise his Parry to 9. Topaz rolls 19 dice for 6 sux, missing.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 4, +5m for all<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei (22/34m, 7wp, -4, Water): 16i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (14/27m, 7/7wp, -0, Water): 12i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (26/27m, 6/6wp, -0, Fire): 8i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (18/26m, 5/5wp, -0, Earth): 7i<br /> Yushoto Nali (13/35m, 6/6wp, -0, Wood): 5i<br /> Shining Topaz (9/29m, 0vm, 6/9wp, -0): 1i<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Shining Topaz resets to 4i.<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei makes a decisive attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 6m,1wp on Against the World Stance and 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense to raise her parry to 9. Linwei rolls 13 dice for 5 sux, missing. Topaz gains 1i and 5vm, putting her at 5i.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita makes a withering attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1vm on Dipping Swallow Defense and 4m on the melee excellency raising her parry to 11. Vita rolls 21 dice for 12 sux, Topaz spends 2m on Hail Shattering Practice, making Vita miss. Topaz gains 1i and 2vm, putting her at 6i.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja spends 2m on Unbearable Taunt Technique. He rolls 6 dice for 2 sux, failing to beat Topaz\u2019s resolve of 4.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice makes a withering attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1vm on Dipping Swallow Defense, raising her Parry to 9. Pumice rolls 18 dice for 11 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 18+3-14=7. Pumice rolls 7 dice rerolling 6s and deals 4 withering damage. Putting him at 12i and Topaz at 2i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali makes a withering attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1vm on Dipping Swallow Defense raising her parry to 9. Nali rolls 20 dice for 14 sux, hitting with 6 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 15+6-14=7. Nali rolls 7 dice rerolling 6s and deals 4 withering damage. Putting her at 10i, and putting Topaz at -2i. Against the World Stance shatters, and Nali gains 5i for landing a crashing Topaz, putting her at 15i.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a withering attack against Bounteous Pumice. Topaz spends 1wp to add a sux, Pumice spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise his parry to 9. Topaz rolls 15 dice for 7+1 sux, missing.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 5, +5m for all<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei (21/34m, 7wp, -4, Water): 16i<br /> Yushoto Nali (12/35m, 6/6wp, -0, Wood): 15i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (13/27m, 7/7wp, -0, Water): 10i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (27/27m, 6/6wp, -0, Fire): 8i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (11/26m, 5/5wp, -0, Earth): 7i<br /> Shining Topaz (5/29m, 5/9wp, -0): -2i<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei makes a decisive attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense, raising her parry to 9. Linwei rolls 13 dice for 4 sux, missing. Topaz gains 1i, putting her at -1i. Linwei loses 3i for missing, putting her at 13i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali makes a decisive attack. She pays 6m for Become the Hammer, Topaz pays 1m for Dipping Swallow Defense, raising her parry to 9. Nali rolls 7 dice for 11 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 15i. Nali rolls 15 dice rerolling 6s and deals 5 lethal damage. Topaz\u2019s wound penalty rises to -2. Nali resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita makes a decisive attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m for Dipping Swallow Defense raising her parry to 7. Vita rolls 16 dice for 9 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 10i. Vita rolls 10 dice rerolling 6s and deals 3 lethal damage. Vita resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja makes a decisive attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense raising her parry to 7. Ja rolls 17 dice for 3 sux, missing. He loses 2i, putting him at 6i.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice makes a decisive attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer and 3m on Force of the Mountain, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense to raise her parry to 7. Pumice rolls 17 dice for 9 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 7i. Pumice rolls 7 dice with double 10s and rerolling 6s, dealing 2 lethal damage. Topaz is dead.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Anathema killed, Lookshy withdraws having claimed victory. The Hearth of Immaculates congratulates themselves on a job well done. Although Terasu Linwei is close to death, none of them actually died.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> I did it tonight. Looking back, I think I may have made some mistakes, but I'm not sure it would change all that much. The Water Immaculate blew through a full excellency defense after I activated Ready in Eight Directions, and everything went to shit when I reset to 4i. Maybe I just got unlucky, and maybe I shouldn't have blown a full excellency on join battle, but the mote economy seemed pretty brutal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T02:19:56-07:00","id":1343738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343699#post1343699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did it tonight. Looking back, I think I may have made some mistakes, but I'm not sure it would change all that much. The Water Immaculate blew through a full excellency defense after I activated Ready in Eight Directions, and everything went to shit when I reset to 4i. Maybe I just got unlucky, and maybe I shouldn't have blown a full excellency on join battle, but the mote economy seemed pretty brutal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The dice seemed really against her that fight. But thanks for having the patience to play it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edite