nd Topaz at 2i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali makes a withering attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1vm on Dipping Swallow Defense raising her parry to 9. Nali rolls 20 dice for 14 sux, hitting with 6 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 15+6-14=7. Nali rolls 7 dice rerolling 6s and deals 4 withering damage. Putting her at 10i, and putting Topaz at -2i. Against the World Stance shatters, and Nali gains 5i for landing a crashing Topaz, putting her at 15i.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a withering attack against Bounteous Pumice. Topaz spends 1wp to add a sux, Pumice spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise his parry to 9. Topaz rolls 15 dice for 7+1 sux, missing.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 5, +5m for all<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei (21/34m, 7wp, -4, Water): 16i<br /> Yushoto Nali (12/35m, 6/6wp, -0, Wood): 15i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (13/27m, 7/7wp, -0, Water): 10i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (27/27m, 6/6wp, -0, Fire): 8i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (11/26m, 5/5wp, -0, Earth): 7i<br /> Shining Topaz (5/29m, 5/9wp, -0): -2i<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei makes a decisive attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense, raising her parry to 9. Linwei rolls 13 dice for 4 sux, missing. Topaz gains 1i, putting her at -1i. Linwei loses 3i for missing, putting her at 13i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali makes a decisive attack. She pays 6m for Become the Hammer, Topaz pays 1m for Dipping Swallow Defense, raising her parry to 9. Nali rolls 7 dice for 11 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 15i. Nali rolls 15 dice rerolling 6s and deals 5 lethal damage. Topaz\u2019s wound penalty rises to -2. Nali resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita makes a decisive attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m for Dipping Swallow Defense raising her parry to 7. Vita rolls 16 dice for 9 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 10i. Vita rolls 10 dice rerolling 6s and deals 3 lethal damage. Vita resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja makes a decisive attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense raising her parry to 7. Ja rolls 17 dice for 3 sux, missing. He loses 2i, putting him at 6i.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice makes a decisive attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer and 3m on Force of the Mountain, Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense to raise her parry to 7. Pumice rolls 17 dice for 9 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 7i. Pumice rolls 7 dice with double 10s and rerolling 6s, dealing 2 lethal damage. Topaz is dead.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Anathema killed, Lookshy withdraws having claimed victory. The Hearth of Immaculates congratulates themselves on a job well done. Although Terasu Linwei is close to death, none of them actually died.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> I did it tonight. Looking back, I think I may have made some mistakes, but I'm not sure it would change all that much. The Water Immaculate blew through a full excellency defense after I activated Ready in Eight Directions, and everything went to shit when I reset to 4i. Maybe I just got unlucky, and maybe I shouldn't have blown a full excellency on join battle, but the mote economy seemed pretty brutal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That goes to show you no amount of divine puisance can account for sheer bad luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T11:42:56-07:00","id":1343822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343791#post1343791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That goes to show you no amount of divine puisance can account for sheer bad luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if bad luck had that much to do with it. I also ran the fight and it ended up going like this.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Shining Topaz joins battle with 10m excellency, rolling 21 dice for 12, getting 15i<br /> Vita rolls 8 +4m for 2 sux, getting 3 total for 6i<br /> Yan rolls 10 dice +4m for 2 sux, getting 8 for 11i<br /> Pumice rolls 6 dice +2m for 1 sux, getting 3 for 6i<br /> Terasu rolls 10 dice +4m for 2 sux, getting 6 for 9i<br /> Yushoto rolls 8 dice +4m for 2 sux, getting 5 for 8i<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Topaz 15i 13p 17ph 9wp 0vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 22ph 7wp<br /> Yan 11i 9p 21ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 6i 11p 20ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 21ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 22ph 6wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> Topaz uses 5m 1wp Fivefold Bulwark Stance and 6m 1wp Against the World Stance<br /> <br /> Topaz 15i 13p 6ph 7wp 0vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 22ph 7wp<br /> Yan 11i 9p 21ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 6i 11p 20ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 21ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 22ph 6wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Yan attacks with 6m full excellency, 3m Searing Edge Attack, Topaz defends with 1m Dipping Swallow, 8m excellency. Yan rolls 21 dice against a defense of 12 for 16, unable to be hail shattered.<br /> <br /> Rolling 3 damage for 2, plus burning another 2i into nothing<br /> <br /> Topaz 11i 10p 0ph 7wp 0vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 22ph 7wp<br /> Yan 14i 9p 12ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 6i 11p 20ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 21ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 22ph 6wp<br /> -----------<br /> Teratsu attacks with 6m excellency, 5m Rippling Water Strike, Topax defends with 1m Dipping Swallow, 8m Full Excellency. Rolling 21 dice against parry 12 for 12 and hitting, but Topax pays 1m and Hail Shatters it, gaining 1i and 2m<br /> <br /> Topaz 12i 0p 0ph 7wp 2vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 22ph 7wp<br /> Yan 14i 9p 12ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 6i 11p 20ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 10ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 22ph 6wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Yushoto attacks with 6m excellency, 4m Eyes of the Wood Dragon. Topaz defends with 1m Dipping Swallow. Yushoto rolls 19 dice against defense of 8, rolling 7 and missing, granting Topaz 1i and 3m.<br /> <br /> Topaz 12i 0p 0ph 7wp 4vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 22ph 7wp<br /> Yan 14i 9p 12ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 6i 11p 20ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 10ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 12ph 6wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Vita attacks with 6m excellency, 5m Wind Dragon Speed. Topaz defends with 1m Dipping Swallow and 2m excellency. Rolling 21 dice against parry 9 for 9, Topaz Hail Shatters it for 1m, granting 1i and 2m.<br /> <br /> Vita will disengage with 2m excellency, rolling 13 dice against 6, for 5 against 4, disengaging to short range.<br /> <br /> Topaz 13i 0p 0ph 7wp 2vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 9ph 7wp<br /> Yan 14i 9p 12ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 6i 11p 20ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 10ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 12ph 6wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Pumice smashing attacks with 6m full excellency and 3m Force of the Mountain. Topaz will defend with 1m Dipping Swallow. Rolling 18 dice against defense 8, and getting 12. Then rolling 6 damage for 7.<br /> <br /> Topaz is now prone.<br /> <br /> Topaz 6i 0p 0ph 7wp 1vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 9ph 7wp<br /> Yan 14i 9p 12ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 14i 11p 11ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 10ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 12ph 6wp<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> Topaz 6i 0p 5ph 7wp 1vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 14ph 7wp<br /> Yan 14i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 14i 11p 16ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 15ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Yan will attack with 6m excellency, 3m Searing Edge Attack. Topaz will defend with 1m Dipping Swallow, 4m excellency. Rolling 21 dice against defense of 10, getting it with 11, topaz doesn't have the motes to Hail Shatter it.<br /> <br /> Yan rolls 3 dice for nothing, still burning 2i away.<br /> <br /> Topaz 4i 0p 0ph 7wp 1vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 14ph 7wp<br /> Yan 15i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 14i 11p 16ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 15ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Pumice rolls 6m excellency with 3m Force of the Mountain, Topaz defends with 1m Dipping Swallow. Pumice rolls 18 dice against defense of 8, getting 9 and hitting. Rolling 9 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Topaz 4i 0p 0ph 7wp 0vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 14ph 7wp<br /> Yan 15i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 14i 11p 7ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 9i 9p 15ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Terasu attacks with 6m full excellency, 5m Rippling Water Strike. Topaz has no motes left to defend. Rolling 21 dice against parry 0 for 14, rolling 17 damage for 8, crashing Topaz.<br /> <br /> Topaz -4i 0p 0ph 7wp 0vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 14ph 7wp<br /> Yan 15i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 14i 11p 7ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 23i 9p 4ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 8i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Yushoto makes a decisive attack with 2m excellency, 3m 2i Soul Marking Style, Topaz can not defend with motes. Rolling 13 dice against defense 0 and getting 9, then rolling 6 damage for only 1, but enough to trigger Soul Marking, all of Yushoto's attacks this scene will benefit from aiming.<br /> <br /> Topaz -4i 0p 0ph 7wp 0vm<br /> Vita 6i 9p 14ph 7wp<br /> Yan 15i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 14i 11p 7ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 23i 9p 4ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 3i 9p 14ph 6wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Vita withers with 2m excellency, Topaz can't spend any motes. Rolling 16 dice against defense 0 for 9, then 8 damage for nothing.<br /> <br /> Topaz -4i 0p 0ph 7wp 0vm<br /> Vita 7i 9p 14ph 7wp<br /> Yan 15i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 14i 11p 7ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 23i 9p 4ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 3i 9p 14ph 6wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Topaz flurries a rise from prone with a withering attack against Yushoto, using 1wp for Perfect Strike Discipline. Yushoto will defend with a 6m excellency. Rolling 3 dice to rise from prone and failing with only 1 success. Then rolling 17 dice against parry 10 for only 9, missing.<br /> <br /> Topaz -4i 0p 0ph 6wp 0vm<br /> Vita 7i 9p 14ph 7wp<br /> Yan 15i 9p 17ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 14i 11p 7ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 23i 9p 4ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 3i 9p 8ph 6wp<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> Topaz -4i 0p 5ph 6wp 0vm<br /> Vita 7i 9p 19ph 7wp<br /> Yan 15i 9p 23ph 6wp<br /> Pumice 14i 11p 12ph 5wp<br /> Terasu 23i 9p 9ph 7wp<br /> Yushoto 3i 9p 13ph 6wp<br /> <br /> Terasu decisive attacks with 6m excellency, and 3m Drowning In Blood. Topaz defends with 1m Dipping Swallow, 4m Excellency. Terasu rolls 17 dice against parry 10, getting 11 and hitting. Topaz has no motes left to hail shatter.<br /> <br /> Rolling 23 damage with double 10s, Terasu rolls 15 decisive damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will say this fight is over.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't quite seem to work the way I thought it would. Some attacks missed and granted motes, but just not enough to keep going, and once that big initiative swap happened, where Topaz went from going first to going last, and the DBs got 10 attacks in a row, including a successful smash attack, it's just too much. Topaz never even got to activate Ready in Eight Direction Stance.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure what I did wrong either. If I was more conservative on motes I could have lasted out longer, but more attacks would have hit, and the ones that did would have dealt more damage, and I would have gotten less reactor motes from Against the World because of it. It might be possible but I don't think it's just luck you need to worry about.<br /> <br /> I have to admit I'm surprised, but that's part of why I started this thread in the first place, to test out stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T13:47:11-07:00","id":1343855,"title":"","content":"I'm going to do it again, tweaking Topaz a bit. I'll pitch 2wp and Heavenly Guardian Defense for rearranged Physical Stats and picking up Essence Gathering Temper. But I'm fairly certain that she still won't win unless she gets lucky. Variance goes both ways, and losing initiative or health levels when the DBs get lucky hurts more than the motes when they get unlucky helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T14:07:25-07:00","id":1343860,"title":"","content":"What's the goal here? If it's just to test if a starting Solar can beat these five Deebs, I want in. If it's beating them specifically with this build, then carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T14:34:20-07:00","id":1343866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343860#post1343860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the goal here? If it's just to test if a starting Solar can beat these five Deebs, I want in. If it's beating them specifically with this build, then carry on.</div> </div> </div> </div>We kind of already know a starting solar can, with Heaven Sword Flash and TAP, but I was personally curious to see if a starting solar could kill 5 DBs and at the end still have all his motes with reactor charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T15:03:54-07:00","id":1343869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343860#post1343860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the goal here? If it's just to test if a starting Solar can beat these five Deebs, I want in. If it's beating them specifically with this build, then carry on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The goal is to run fights we find interesting. If you want to use the immaculates I made to see if a given starting solar build can beat them, feel free! I'd be happy to see the resulting fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T15:40:55-07:00","id":1343873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343866#post1343866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We kind of already know a starting solar can, with Heaven Sword Flash and TAP, but I was personally curious to see if a starting solar could kill 5 DBs and at the end still have all his motes with reactor charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How many times has this been run? Because I'm half sure it is dead easy to roll like shit on the attack roll and have all the DBs block the Heaven Sword Flash attack. And you really only have 1 shot to knock enough of them out to justify the expense before the beatdown we have seen happens.<br /> <br /> I'mma build Topaz like that and run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T15:47:01-07:00","id":1343874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343873#post1343873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many times has this been run? Because I'm half sure it is dead easy to roll like shit on the attack roll and have all the DBs block the Heaven Sword Flash attack. And you really only have 1 shot to knock enough of them out to justify the expense before the beatdown we have seen happens.<br /> <br /> I'mma build Topaz like that and run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s actually really really hard to roll badly on that attack. You give it a full excellency with Excellent Strike, Rising Sun Slash, and you only have to hit a defence of 9 or 10, and when you\u2019re rolling 23 dice, rerolling 1s and have such a good chance to activate Rising Sun Slash it happens well more than 50% of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T18:05:40-07:00","id":1343897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343874#post1343874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s actually really really hard to roll badly on that attack. You give it a full excellency with Excellent Strike, Rising Sun Slash, and you only have to hit a defence of 9 or 10, and when you\u2019re rolling 23 dice, rerolling 1s and have such a good chance to activate Rising Sun Slash it happens well more than 50% of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You cannot excellent strike and rising sun slash at the same time. Rising Sun Slash needs a full excellency, and Excellent Strike gives an auto-sux. Which means you'll be two motes short of the full excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T23:10:10-07:00","id":1343925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343897#post1343897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot excellent strike and rising sun slash at the same time. Rising Sun Slash needs a full excellency, and Excellent Strike gives an auto-sux. Which means you'll be two motes short of the full excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can at least do it as long as you either use Perfect Strike Discipline or simply pay the full mote cost anyway. If two effects give you dice and successes past your cap, you get to choose which of those you take, so I think you can overpay on the excellency and take the dice for using it in full. <br /> <br /> It's not super reliable anyway, all your targets need to be within one range band, and all at short range with you, and you can do that exactly once before you're tapped out, so if a second hearth then descends on you, you're toast. You can't just stand in the Palace Sublime mowing down circle after circle of immaculate masters.<br /> <br /> Plus, as far as I can tell, that's the only way to do that, so as long as every Dawn in the game isn't a supernal melee with HSF and TAP Wyld Hunts can still be challenging and if the Hunt are PCs against a lone Solar that Solar might even be a disappointing fight without backup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T11:37:46-07:00","id":1344030,"title":"","content":"I ran Heaven Sword Flash build of Topaz twice. <br /> <br /> Fight 1:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Join Battle<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6406\" target=\"_blank\">Shining Topaz</a> pays 5m for Sensory Acuity Prana and 10m for a full awareness excellency. She rolls 24 dice with double 9s for 23 sux. She starts with 26i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6406\" target=\"_blank\">Nefvarin Vita</a> pays 5m for Precision Observation Method to add 2 sux and 1 die to her roll. She rolls 9 dice for 5+2 sux, she starts with 10i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6299\" target=\"_blank\">Bounteous Pumice</a> spends 3m for Precision Observation Method to add 1 sux and 1 die to his roll. He rolls 7 dice for 2+2 sux, he starts with 7i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6300\" target=\"_blank\">Yan Tu Ja</a> spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 2 sux and 1 die to his roll. He rolls 11 dice for 5+2 sux, he starts with 10i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6301\" target=\"_blank\">Terasu Linwei</a> spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 2 sux and 1 die to her roll. She rolls 11 dice for 5+2 sux, she starts with 10i.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6302\" target=\"_blank\">Yushoto Nali</a> spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 2 sux and 1 die to her roll. She rolls 9 dice for 3+2 sux, she starts with 8i.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (26/36m, 6/6wp, -0): 23i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (30/35m, 7/7wp, -0): 10i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (29/34m, 6/6wp, -0): 10i<br /> Terasu Linwei (29/34m, 7/7wp, -0): 10i<br /> Yushoto Nali (30/35m, 6/6wp, -0): 8i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (28/33m, 5/5wp, -0): 7i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 6m, 1wp for Heaven Sword Flash, this is supplemented by 4m, 1wp for Thunderbolt Attack Prana and 1wp for Perfect Strike Discipline and 3m for Fire and Stones Strike. The Immaculates all spend 6m on Become the Hammer to raise their Parry by 3. Shining Topaz rolls 23 dice for 7 sux, missing all of them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to call it for the immaculate shikari here.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight 2:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Join Battle<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz pays 5m for Sensory Acuity Prana and 10m for a full awareness excellency. She rolls 24 dice with double 9s for 14 sux. She starts with 17i.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita pays 5m for Precision Observation Method to add 2 sux and 1 die to her roll. She rolls 9 dice for 5+2 sux, she starts with 10i.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice spends 3m for Precision Observation Method to add 1 sux and 1 die to his roll. He rolls 7 dice for 2+2 sux, he starts with 7i.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 2 sux and 1 die to his roll. He rolls 11 dice for 3+2 sux, he starts with 8i.<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 2 sux and 1 die to her roll. She rolls 11 dice for 4+2 sux, she starts with 9i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 2 sux and 1 die to her roll. She rolls 9 dice for 6+2 sux, she starts with 12i.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (26/36m, 6/6wp, -0): 17i<br /> Yushoto Nali (30/35m, 6/6wp, -0): 12i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (30/35m, 7/7wp, -0): 10i<br /> Terasu Linwei (29/34m, 7/7wp, -0): 8i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (29/34m, 6/6wp, -0): 7i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (28/33m, 5/5wp, -0): 7i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 6m, 1wp for Heaven Sword Flash, this is supplemented by 4m, 1wp for Thunderbolt Attack Prana and 1wp for Perfect Strike Discipline and 3m for Fire and Stones Strike. The Immaculates all spend 6m on Become the Hammer to raise their Parry by 3. Shining Topaz rolls 23 dice for 13 sux, hitting all of them with at least 4 threshold sux. Topaz declines to activate Rising Sun Slash<br /> <br /> Against Nali Topaz rolls 9+3=12 dice. She rolls 0 sux.<br /> <br /> Against Vita Topaz rolls 9+3=12 dice. She rolls 4 sux and inflicts 8 lethal damage, Raising Vita\u2019s wound penalty to -2.<br /> <br /> Against Linwei Topaz rolls 9+3=12 dice. She rolls 2 sux and inflicts 4 lethal damage, rising Linwei\u2019s wound penalty to -1.<br /> <br /> Against Ja Topaz rolls 9+3=12 dice. She rolls 4 sux and inflicts 8 lethal damage, raising Ja\u2019s wound penalty to -4.<br /> <br /> Against Pumice Topaz rolls 9+3=12 dice. She rolls 4 sux and inflicts 8 lethal damage, raising Pumice\u2019s wound penalty to -2.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz resets to 4i and pays 1m, 1wp, 3a for peony blossom attack. She makes a withering attack against Yan Tu Ja, spending 3m for Excellent Strike. Ja spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise his parry to 5. Topaz rolls 15 dice for 5+1 sux rerolling 2 dice for an additional 2 sux, hitting with 4 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 12+4-11=5. Topaz rolls 5 dice and deals 0 withering damage. She gains 1i for landing a withering attack, putting her at 5i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali makes a withering attack. Nali spends 6m on Become the Hammer and 4m on Eyes of the Wood Dragon, Topaz spends 5m on Bulwark Stance. Nali rolls 20 dice for 12 sux, hitting with 5 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 15+5+5-14-1. Nali rolls 10 dice and deals 6 withering damage. Putting Nali at 19i and Topaz at -1i. Nali gets +5i for crashing Topaz, putting her at 24i.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita makes a decisive attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer. She rolls 15 dice for 8 sux. Topaz spends 1m on Hail Shattering Practice to make her miss.<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei makes a withering attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer. She rolls 21 dice for 10 sux, hitting with 3 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 12+3-15=0. Linwei rolls 3 overwhelming dice and deals 2 withering damage. Putting her at 11i and Topaz at -3i. Linwei Enters Water Aura.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja spends 5m, 1wp to enter Dual Slaying Stance.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice makes a withering attack. He spends 6m on Become the Hammer and 3m on Force of the Mountain. He rolls 16 dice for 5 sux, missing. He enters Earth Aura.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 2 +5m for all.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali (19/35m, 6/6wp, -0, Wood): 24i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (23/35m, 7/7wp, -2, Water): 10i<br /> Terasu Linwei (22/34m, 7/7wp, -1, Water): 8i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (19/29m, 5/6wp, -4): 7i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (21/33m, 5/5wp, -2, Earth): 7i<br /> Shining Topaz (12/36m, 3/6wp, -0): -3i<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali makes a decisive attack. She spends 6m on Become the Hammer and 3m, 2i on Soul Marking Style, topaz spends 2m on the melee excellency raising her parry to 9. Nali rolls 17 dice for 14 sux, hitting with 6 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 22-1 (bulwark stance)=21. Yushoto Nali rolls 21 dice and deals 7 lethal damage. Topaz is dead.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not convinced that Heaven Sword Flash + Thunderbolt Attack Prana actually lets a starting Solar reliably survive 5 Immaculates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T11:59:16-07:00","id":1344036,"title":"","content":"To expand further: Assuming Fast Reflexes, 5 dots in Awareness and Wits, a specialty in Join Battle, and a full excellency + Sensory Acuity Prana, that still only gets you 13 sux on average. That means 16i.<br /> <br /> 16/2=8. 8+3 (fire and stones strike) is 11, and that's assuming you get 3 threshold sux on a 23 dice roll against Parries of 9 and 10.<br /> <br /> On average 11 dice will roll 4.4 sux. 4*2=8. 8 lethal isn't enough to kill an immaculate with even 1 ox body, and if they have more than 1 then it won't get to -4 wound penalty either. It won't even kill all of the QC immaculates in the core.<br /> <br /> Edit: Am I just missing something about the HSF+TAP build?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 10-27-2019, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T05:17:54-07:00","id":1344170,"title":"","content":"Hmm no your math checks out.<br /> <br /> Working backwards with TAP we need about 6 successes to kill a DB with two ox bodies, 6/.4=15. To get 15 dice we might need Dovine Executioner Stance for 4, Hungry Tiger for 3, which brings us to 8 base, which we can get from 16i. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s kind of right on the edge, so I guess reliable isn\u2019t exactly the way to phrase it, it\u2019s a coin flip. I think that might be the best you can get though without going to evocations for double 10s or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T14:21:51-07:00","id":1344256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344170#post1344170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm no your math checks out.<br /> <br /> Working backwards with TAP we need about 6 successes to kill a DB with two ox bodies, 6/.4=15. To get 15 dice we might need Dovine Executioner Stance for 4, Hungry Tiger for 3, which brings us to 8 base, which we can get from 16i.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s kind of right on the edge, so I guess reliable isn\u2019t exactly the way to phrase it, it\u2019s a coin flip. I think that might be the best you can get though without going to evocations for double 10s or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first idea was actually to cut the defensive suite to the bone to make room for Awakening Eye. But I think your idea might work better. Looking at Hungry Tiger Technique though makes me think Fire and Stones Strike might be superior, since that 2i will hurt for possibly minimal gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T14:46:39-07:00","id":1344262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344256#post1344256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My first idea was actually to cut the defensive suite to the bone to make room for Awakening Eye. But I think your idea might work better. Looking at Hungry Tiger Technique though makes me think Fire and Stones Strike might be superior, since that 2i will hurt for possibly minimal gain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I meant fire and stones, you can\u2019t even hungry tiger it needs a crashed target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:35:01-07:00","id":1344272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344262#post1344262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry I meant fire and stones, you can\u2019t even hungry tiger it needs a crashed target.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... An E1 solar doesn't have the motes for this. Not if they are in Heavy Artifact Armor. They'll be one mote short from adding 10 dice and 3m for Fire and Stones on the HSF attack.<br /> <br /> They need to spend 15m on Awareness Excellency+Sensory Acuity Prana. HSF+TAP is 10m. DES+FSS+Exellency= 10. And between Heavy Armor and DES, that's 12 already committed.<br /> <br /> That's 47m, starting solars only have 46 total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 10-28-2019, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:48:20-07:00","id":1344279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344272#post1344272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ... An E1 solar doesn't have the motes for this. Not if they are in Heavy Artifact Armor. They'll be one mote short from adding 10 dice and 3m for Fire and Stones on the HSF attack.<br /> <br /> They need to spend 15m on Awareness Excellency+Sensory Acuity Prana. HSF+TAP is 10m. DES+FSS+Exellency= 10. And between Heavy Armor and DES, that's 12 already committed.<br /> <br /> That's 47m, starting solars only have 46 total.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can get the full melee excellency from Perfect Strike Discipline, that saves them the motes to excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:50:37-07:00","id":1344282,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if that's actually kosher, mechanically.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to downgrade Topaz's armor to Medium when Running the scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 10-28-2019, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:56:15-07:00","id":1344284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344282#post1344282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if that's actually kosher, mechanically.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to downgrade Topaz's armor to Medium when Run the scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not, but it works either way. The kind of armor you're wearing actually doesn't even matter, either you kill all the DBs in the first attack or you die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T16:40:57-07:00","id":1344298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344284#post1344284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why not, but it works either way. The kind of armor you're wearing actually doesn't even matter, either you kill all the DBs in the first attack or you die.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I gave Bounteous Pumice 5 ox bodies at stamina 5. So... he's probably going to live. If it's one on one, there might be a chance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T16:56:09-07:00","id":1344300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344298#post1344298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I gave Bounteous Pumice 5 ox bodies at stamina 5. So... he's probably going to live. If it's one on one, there might be a chance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Jesus 5 at Stamina 5?<br /> <br /> Yeah that'll probably survive it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T18:15:13-07:00","id":1344312,"title":"","content":"When Shining Topaz exalted, she exalted in front of a pair of DBs from Lookshy. When her father refused to disown her, Lookshy declared war with the goal of killing the Anathema that had inhabited Shining Topaz. Terek was in no way prepared to fight a war with Lookshy, and once their field force had made the river trip, the country folded in short order. Within months, the capital was under siege, after barely a week local adherents of the immaculate faith had thrown open the city gates.<br /> <br /> The five immaculate shikari of the wyld hunt manage to corner Topaz in the palace during the final stages of the assault.<br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> Note: I am assuming a 1pt stunt on everything Topaz does, every roll and every application of a static value.<br /> -<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Join Battle<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6418\" target=\"_blank\">Shining Topaz</a> spends 5m on Sensory Acuity Prana and 10m on the Awareness Excellency. She rolls 24 dice for 16 sux, and starts with 19i.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 2 sux and 1 die to her roll. She rolls 9 dice for 4+2 sux, and starts with 9i.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice spends 3m on Precision Observation Method to add 3 dice to his roll. He rolls 9 dice for 2 sux, he starts with 5i.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 5 dice to his roll. He rolls 15 dice for 11 sux, he starts with 14i.<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 5 dice to her roll. She rolls 15 dice for 4 sux, she starts with 7i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali spends 5m on Precision Observation Method to add 5 dice to her roll. She rolls 13 dice for 4 sux, she starts with 7i.<br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (20/30m, 6/6wp, -0): 19i<br /> Yan Tu Ja (29/34m, 6/6wp, -0): 14i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (30/35m, 7/7wp, -0): 9i<br /> Terasu Linwei (29/34, 7/7wp, -0): 7i<br /> Yushoto Nali (30/35m, 6/6wp, -0): 7i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (30/33, 5/5wp, -0): 5i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 6m, 1wp on Heaven Sword Flash. She supplements this with 4m, 1wp for Thunderbolt Attack Prana, 1m for Divine Executioner Stance to add 4 dice, 6m melee excellency for 6 dice, 3m for Fire and Stones Strike, and 1wp for an automatic sux.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise his parry to 9.<br /> Nefvarin Vita spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise her parry to 9.<br /> Terasu Linwei spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise her parry to 9.<br /> Yushoto Nali spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise her parry to 10 and 5m on Wood Dragon Vitality to impose a -1 penalty to the damage roll if Topaz Hits.<br /> Bounteous Pumice spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise his parry to 9 and spends 5m, 1i on Stone Dragon\u2019s Skin to raise his hardness to 11.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz rolls 23 dice for 10+1 sux. She hits Ja, Vita, Linwei, and Pumice with 3 threshold sux, and hits Nali with 2 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> Against Ja. 10 (base)+4(DES)+3(FSS)=17. Topaz rolls 17 dice and deals 8 lethal damage, doubled to 16 by Thunderbolt Attack Prana. Ja is dead.<br /> <br /> Against Vita. 10 (base)+4(DES)+3(FSS)=17. Topaz rolls 17 dice and deals 9 lethal damage, doubled to 18 by Thunderbolt Attack Prana. Vita is dead.<br /> <br /> Against Linwei. 10 (base)+4(DES)+3(FSS)=17. Topaz rolls 17 dice and deals 8 lethal damage, doubled to 16 by Thunderbolt Attack Prana. Linwei is dead.<br /> <br /> Against Nali. 10 (base)+4(DES)+2(FSS)-1 (WDV)=15. Topaz rolls 15 dice and deals 6 damage, doubled to 12 by Thunderbolt Attack Prana. Nali is dead.<br /> <br /> Against Pumice. 10 (base)+4(DES)+3(FSS)=17. Topaz rolls 17 dice and deals 7 damage, doubled to 14 by Thunderbolt Attack Prana. Pumice lives with 7hl remaining, at wound penalty -2.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz resets to 4i.<br /> <br /> Pumice rolls a rout check against diff 2. He rolls 5 dice for 3 sux, passing.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice makes a smashing withering attack. He pays 6m for become the hammer and 3m for Force of the Mountain, Topaz pays 1wp for Perfect Strike Discipline to raise her parry to 13. Pumice rolls 16 dice for 8 sux, missing. Pumice enters Earth Aura<br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 2, +5m for all<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (5/30m, 2/6wp, -0): 4i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (15/33, 5/5wp, -2, Earth): 2i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz delays her action to clash with Bounteous Pumice.<br /> <br /> Topaz and Pumice Clash! Topaz makes a withering attack and spends 1m on Divine Executioner Stance and 3m on Excellent Strike, she also spends 1wp for an automatic sux. Pumice makes a withering attack and spends 6m on Become the Hammer and 3m on Force of the Mountain, he also spends 1wp for an automatic sux.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 19 dice for 9+2 sux and rerolls 1s for 0 additional sux. Total 11 sux.<br /> Pumice rolls 16 dice for 5+1 sux. Total 6 sux.<br /> Topaz wins with 6 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 12+6+4 (DES) -16=6. Topaz rolls 6 dice and deals 3+3(clash) withering damage. Putting her at 9i and Pumice at -4i. Topaz gains 5i for crashing Pumice, putting her at 14i.<br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 3, +5m for all<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (6/30m, 1/6wp, -0): 14i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (11/33, 4/5wp, -2, Earth): -4i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a decisive attack. She spends 1m on Divine Executioner Stance to add 4 dice, 3m on Excellent Strike, and 2m on Fire and Stones Strike. Pumice spends 6m on Become the Hammer to raise his parry to 5. Topaz rolls 19 dice for 15+1 sux, hitting with 12 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 14+4(DES)+2(FSS)=20. Topaz rolls 20 dice and deals 8 damage. Pumice is dead.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Her last foe dead on her blade, Shining Topaz collapses to her knees in exhaustion. She has killed five Princes of the Earth in less than a minute and is utterly spent, should any enemies find her in her exhausted state she would be easy pickings. Lucky it is for her, then, that it is not an enemy that finds her.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sister.&quot; Her brother says from an archway.<br /> <br /> Panting, Shining Topaz leverages herself to her feet. &quot;Gleaming Emerald, what news?&quot;<br /> <br /> Emerald grimaces, &quot;Father is dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> Topaz sways on her feet for a moment, processing her loss. Then the moment passes, and she falls to one knee. &quot;What are your orders my king?&quot;<br /> <br /> She feels her brothers hands on her shoulders, and looks up into his eyes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Topaz, you need to leave. As powerful as you are, you can only be in one place at a time. Terek cannot stand against Lookshy, and they only attack us because they are after you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Topaz swallows, and then nods in understanding. Her brother pulls her into a hug.<br /> <br /> &quot;I will need to denounce you for Terek's sake, but know that you are my sister and that I love you.&quot;<br /> <br /> King Gleaming Emerald of Terek released the Forsaken Anathema Shining Topaz.<br /> <br /> &quot;Goodbye brother. Keep Terek safe.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Take the tunnels sister. And stay safe yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> And so Shining Topaz, the Invincible Sword Princess fled Terek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 10-28-2019, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T18:43:42-07:00","id":1344316,"title":"","content":"Good fight! I think that's how it's usually going to go. Even if one of them survives, Solar vs DB one on one isn't much of a fight. Well, it can actually be really one sided for the DB, but not if it's a Dawn, which in this case it always will be.<br /> <br /> I think that settles it anyway, Heaven Sword Flash definitely lets you fight 5 DBs at once. Although I really hope this doesn't become like, a thing. Like if your Dawn isn't built for this she sucks because now your group is vulnerable to Dragonblooded attack, when otherwise they could be safely ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T19:11:04-07:00","id":1344324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344316#post1344316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good fight! I think that's how it's usually going to go. Even if one of them survives, Solar vs DB one on one isn't much of a fight. Well, it can actually be really one sided for the DB, but not if it's a Dawn, which in this case it always will be.<br /> <br /> I think that settles it anyway, Heaven Sword Flash definitely lets you fight 5 DBs at once. Although I really hope this doesn't become like, a thing. Like if your Dawn isn't built for this she sucks because now your group is vulnerable to Dragonblooded attack, when otherwise they could be safely ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, I'm willing to bet that even if one other had survived, even if at -4, Topaz would have been in big trouble. She just did not have the motes for onslaught negation.<br /> <br /> And the Wood Aspect would have survived if she'd had a third ox body, or topaz had rolled 5 damage instead of 6. and on average, that -4 would become -2 when the wood aspect pops mind over body meditiation.<br /> <br /> Topaz also got lucky in the JB roll. So I feel this kind of scenario is probably very vulnerable to swing from variance. <br /> <br /> If the Air Aspect had thrown as a backup and started at short range Topaz would also have gotten punk'd. <br /> <br /> <br /> This build is pretty mono-focused. It's built to do one thing, and while it probably does it more often than not, it feels very fragile. The scenario would need to be run more times to really get a feel for it, but my gut says its a fairly rickety structure.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I feel that in terms of party composition it's trash. In a party where there are other solars with even just excellent strike and dipping swallow defense, I think the 2x Victorious Wreath reactor build would be better in the vast majority of cases. Being mob'd by exalts while alone is just not a common scenario, and this build is monofocused on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T19:42:40-07:00","id":1344327,"title":"","content":"It is pretty focused, but I think it would still work really well in a group scenario. Just eliminating the entire enemy field in a single attack before any of your allies even have to spend motes is good. Especially if they want to save motes for other stuff later and don't want to waste them fighting. It's not like it does exactly this one thing and is totally useless in all other scenarios, it's really good otherwise. It's just solid, and it covers a lot of bases, if you grabbed 5FBS I'd say most bases.<br /> <br /> It is a pretty terrible NPC build though. Either you one-shot your whole PC circle without them having any way to avoid it, or you miss and this big battle that you've been building up to for months ends up being a laughable stomp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T04:13:56-07:00","id":1344381,"title":"","content":"Of course Topaz's anima banner is now at bonfire/iconic... So everyone is going to know about it so better hope the travel through the tunnels takes at least an hour or two...<br /> But a Solar that goes all out is magnificent monster, as they are kind of meant to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23598-quilligoth","name":"quilligoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T05:30:09-07:00","id":1344391,"title":"","content":"I totally respecced this from the ground up with Mela's Coil (for Wind Rider's Swiftness) and the Jewel of the Heroes Panoply... and rolled 6 successes for damage on the Earth Immaculate despite rolling 21 damage dice (18i+12 damage).<br /> <br /> I'd squeezed in Peony Blossom Attack to take care of anima, and Withered a whole 1i using motes from Foe Cleaving Focus. Then I called it because it was going to be a long, slow beat down.<br /> <br /> It clearly can be done, but I took 13 Melee Charms, spending 8BP on Charms to do it. And it was still swingy as a British politician.<br /> <br /> I absolutely think it's viable A While In The Sun. But I wouldn't build it as a normal starting character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T14:25:22-07:00","id":1344503,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> You said there was a supernal resistance build that might have a shot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T15:21:59-07:00","id":1344512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344503#post1344503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> You said there was a supernal resistance build that might have a shot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, with Aegis of Invincible Might and withering damage reducers, Essence Gathering Temper and Willpower Enhancing Spirit if you want as well.<br /> <br /> Once Aegis of Invincible Might is active you have well over 20 soak, maybe even over 30? So everyone's is only doing minimum damage to you at worst. At best they're dealing zero because Aegis lowers post soak damage by five, without saying if that lets it reduce damage below minimum or not. Then each time you get attacked and take no damage Essence Gathering Temper resets, and you can use that to get 10m per round in addition to your 5m regen.<br /> <br /> Then with 20 hardness, effectively infinite soak and ways to reduce damage after soaking it, so you just can't lose, which means that eventually you'll win.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I\u2019m also not going to ever run that. It might take actual days and involve a soul crushing amount of ineffectual attacks, and slow slow slow initiative build as he Solar keeps growing initiative and then spending it on charms and then building again before he makes even one decisive attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 10-29-2019, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T17:45:39-07:00","id":1344538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344324#post1344324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If the Air Aspect had thrown as a backup and started at short range Topaz would also have gotten punk'd.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Air Dragon is ranged out of the box. Smart play if you are coming in with your four buddies is to keep at range I'd imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T18:40:59-07:00","id":1344549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344538#post1344538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, Air Dragon is ranged out of the box. Smart play if you are coming in with your four buddies is to keep at range I'd imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I fluffed it as being inside the palace, and thus not actually taking place in a area big enough to have short range. But yeah, outside those circumstances, probably would want to keep at short range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T20:36:49-07:00","id":1344563,"title":"","content":"Most Wyld Hunts that I've played and played against don't just rush in and attack, they only get engaged like that if they get the anathema sprung on them. In my experience Wyld Hunts put together a huge amount of setup and planning to execute properly.<br /> <br /> In one memorable case the PCs were the Hunt, hunting a Solar near a town which was half hanging above a waterfall on an ancient spar of some First Age architecture. First they lead the Solar through their army, sending a large wave of heavy infantry and its exalted commander to wear him down. Then they lured him onto the spar, detonated explosives that completely knocked out the ground under his feet sending him tumbling hundreds of feet down onto jagged rocks, and then immediately detonating the other set which brought the entire spar crashing down on him. Then he leaped back up, but before he could engage them their friend in a Warstrider on a nearby hill started pelting him with arrows the size of ballista bolts. So he jumped into close quarters with the warstrider and destroyed it. Then, at last, he leaped back into the town to finish off the PCs, where they had another ambush of their allies waiting to take him down.<br /> <br /> They actually had more fallback positions and plans in place, assuming that ambush would fail and they'd have to either chase him down through the woods that they'd seeded with more surprises, or lure him down into the catacombs beneath the rest of the town, which they'd filled with deathtraps and soldiers. Thankfully it was not necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T21:17:09-07:00","id":1344573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344549#post1344549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I fluffed it as being inside the palace, and thus not actually taking place in a area big enough to have short range. But yeah, outside those circumstances, probably would want to keep at short range.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you interpret as short? I generally give even relatively small places a Short range that isn't in Close. Maybe not like a bedroom, but a bar or something would. A palace, depending on the room, could go either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T01:51:39-07:00","id":1344610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344512#post1344512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, with Aegis of Invincible Might and withering damage reducers, Essence Gathering Temper and Willpower Enhancing Spirit if you want as well.<br /> <br /> Once Aegis of Invincible Might is active you have well over 20 soak, maybe even over 30? So everyone's is only doing minimum damage to you at worst. At best they're dealing zero because Aegis lowers post soak damage by five, without saying if that lets it reduce damage below minimum or not. Then each time you get attacked and take no damage Essence Gathering Temper resets, and you can use that to get 10m per round in addition to your 5m regen.<br /> <br /> Then with 20 hardness, effectively infinite soak and ways to reduce damage after soaking it, so you just can't lose, which means that eventually you'll win.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I\u2019m also not going to ever run that. It might take actual days and involve a soul crushing amount of ineffectual attacks, and slow slow slow initiative build as he Solar keeps growing initiative and then spending it on charms and then building again before he makes even one decisive attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Against these five Immaculates? Yes.<br /> <br /> But a Dragon-Blooded with a Grand-Daiklave and Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite and Dragon-Graced Weapon has Overwhelming 12. So we're still looking at 7 dice minimum after Aegis. And you can't even activate Aegis until you take a Decisive attack, which isn't happening until the Deebs Wither enough Initiative... which they're not doing until you're mote tapped because of your Withering reducers.<br /> <br /> The Solar probably would win. But it's going to still be swingy until Aegis activates. And if the Deebs are built for it (12 OVR), the Aegis is still no sure thing. <br /> <br /> I'm tempted to try against these 5 Immaculates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T06:27:24-07:00","id":1344644,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s really only three options that the DBs have once Aegis activates. Run, deactivate Aegis by grappling the Solar and using the restrain action, or simply never launch a decisive attack unless the Solar is crashed, stopping them from ever activating aegis in the first place.<br /> <br /> Once it\u2019s active none of the Immaculates can raise their minimum damage above 5, except the Earth and even then only by 1, so they can\u2019t deal withering damage. The Solar also has 20 Hardness, so the DBs only chance is to land like 15 withering attacks in a row to generate 1i for each hit, and then launch a decisive attack that will just get Adamant Skinned anyway. Meanwhile the Solar is burning away through Essence Gathering Temper at a rate of maybe 2i per round, and with only Essence 1 melee charms that means he\u2019s probably just slowly creeping up initiative every round, but it doesn\u2019t matter because he\u2019s untouchable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T12:53:45-07:00","id":1344726,"title":"","content":"How does the Heaven Sword Flash character deal with a situation where the five Dragon-Blooded are spread out? Every fight I've seen showing off &quot;Chargen Solar kills entire Hearth via HFS&quot; seems to blindly assume five Immaculates so close they must be sharing a belt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T14:28:31-07:00","id":1344750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344726#post1344726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Heaven Sword Flash character deal with a situation where the five Dragon-Blooded are spread out? Every fight I've seen showing off &quot;Chargen Solar kills entire Hearth via HFS&quot; seems to blindly assume five Immaculates so close they must be sharing a belt.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to have Invincible Fury of the Dawn, so you still do pretty good if they're spread out -- but you're going to need the rest of your Circle to help because IFotD is WAY weaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T15:30:48-07:00","id":1344759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344573#post1344573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you interpret as short? I generally give even relatively small places a Short range that isn't in Close. Maybe not like a bedroom, but a bar or something would. A palace, depending on the room, could go either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Within 20 feet of her is close. Outside 20 ft is where short begins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 10-30-2019, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T17:15:35-07:00","id":1344779,"title":"","content":"&quot;Close&quot; doesn't seem like &quot;20 feet&quot; to me. Keep in mind that being within Close range of an opponent means you can't safely move away from them and thus necessitates a Disengage action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-30-2019, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T17:33:43-07:00","id":1344782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a character is at <b>close range</b>, he is in an opponent\u2019s face, close enough to easily attack with a hand-to-hand weapon such as a sword, spear, or his fists. <b>This doesn\u2019t mean that the characters are necessarily within arm\u2019s reach of each other at all times, but rather that they are able to</b> <b>close such a distance in moments</b>. If an opponent is within close range of a character, that character is embattled, and must use a disengage action if he wishes to move away from the opponent.<br /> <br /> When a character is at <b>short range</b>, he is outside of the immediate reach of an opponent wielding a hand-to-hand weapon, but <b>close enough that the opponent could reach him with a quick sprint</b> </div> </div> </div>As I see it, close range is within leaping distance, so no more than ~10ft. After all, you need to be able to Defend Other from anywhere within Close range, which is not gonna happen if you're 20ft away from your charge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T18:07:33-07:00","id":1344788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344782#post1344782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it, close range is within leaping distance, so no more than ~10ft. After all, you need to be able to Defend Other from anywhere within Close range, which is not gonna happen if you're 20ft away from your charge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah. I was going off the &quot;a knife wielder will win a gunfight if they start within 21ft of the gun wielder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T05:25:56-07:00","id":1344904,"title":"","content":"It's going to massively depend on the circumstances.<br /> <br /> Reflexive movement doesn't help this -- what is free movement as part of being at Close, what is &quot;a short sprint&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd say the maximum distance for Close can be anywhere from 2' to 20' depending on the circumstances. <br /> <br /> Flame weapons used to have a range of 45' and are now Short ranged. If we say Medium is ~50', that leaves a lot of leeway for how big Close and Short might be.<br /> <br /> Generally, I'd peg Close at ~10' (because D&amp;D), and Short being 10' to 50': but we're taught the average person can clear the average room in one second -- which squares with the 21' knife thing. You can close a twenty foot gap in a second (a Bolt is clearing 30' in a second) and an attack is three seconds.<br /> <br /> I certainly don't think it's unreasonable to say two people within 20' are Close, especially in the scenario described. I wouldn't be comfortable making Close range any bigger than that, but someone sitting on the back of a 15' Tyrant Lizard is still at Close range from foes on the ground. So it can't be MUCH smaller than 20'.<br /> <br /> But then, if the Deebs were PCs and wanted to have some at Short and some at Close, I'd allow that too. It's all about the narrative: and this is telling one heck of a story. The point is to be dynamic, not nickel-and-dime palace sizes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-31-2019, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T05:29:17-08:00","id":1345578,"title":"","content":"I am running the Aegis of Invincible Might fight. It is a slog. But from what I can tell currently, it's swingy and can go either way depending. Also, I built the guy wrong, I didn't realize you can use grappling to turn off Aegis until after I had built him, so I only gave him brawl 3 instead of brawl 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T01:38:24-08:00","id":1346401,"title":"","content":"Question. I've heard that solars can singlehandedly wipe out armies with a single shot from their bows. <br /> <br /> How? <br /> <br /> I'm looking at the 3e charms for archery, and so far, I've seen things that let you fire (Dexterity) times, or striking up to Essence x 3 targets. But nothing that is army-slaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T02:52:45-08:00","id":1346408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1345578#post1345578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am running the Aegis of Invincible Might fight. It is a slog. But from what I can tell currently, it's swingy and can go either way depending. Also, I built the guy wrong, I didn't realize you can use grappling to turn off Aegis until after I had built him, so I only gave him brawl 3 instead of brawl 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does grappling turn it off? Restrain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T03:37:35-08:00","id":1346412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346401#post1346401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. I've heard that solars can singlehandedly wipe out armies with a single shot from their bows. <br /> <br /> How? <br /> <br /> I'm looking at the 3e charms for archery, and so far, I've seen things that let you fire (Dexterity) times, or striking up to Essence x 3 targets. But nothing that is army-slaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you looked at the rules for battle groups?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T04:21:30-08:00","id":1346417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346408#post1346408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does grappling turn it off? Restrain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I THINK that works? It prevents the Solar from taking actions and therefore they can\u2019t spend those 8 offensive motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T05:02:53-08:00","id":1346427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346408#post1346408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does grappling turn it off? Restrain?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Aegis needs you to either make a decisive attack or spend 8m on offensive charms. So since Restrain stops you from taking actions on your turn, that stops you from doing offensive charms entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T12:36:54-08:00","id":1346542,"title":"","content":"Actually, Restrain isn't a perfect solution. It prevents actions <i>on their next turn</i>, not any action at all. Solars get a lot of out-of-turn offense. <br /> For example, Solar Counterattack is E1 and will handle the Restrain situation unless the DBs are meta-aware enough to hold their attacks until Aegis goes down. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T12:55:44-08:00","id":1346548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346542#post1346542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Restrain isn't a perfect solution. It prevents actions <i>on their next turn</i>, not any action at all. Solars get a lot of out-of-turn offense.<br /> For example, Solar Counterattack is E1 and will handle the Restrain situation unless the DBs are meta-aware enough to hold their attacks until Aegis goes down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't seem like the intent, to me.<br /> <br /> Characters can normally only act on their turns, after all. The restrain action is being written to handle the base rules, without trying to cover any and every possible Charm interaction.<br /> <br /> It's more plausible to me that those reflexive Charms were written with a blindspot in regards to interaction with the restrain action.<br /> <br /> <br /> But speaking of grappling and how terrifying it is, I've been looking for and failing to find any method for grappling my opponent that allows me to knock them prone at the same time. I either need to grapple an opponent who is already prone, using a smashing savaging attack (and few unarmed attacks have the Smash keyword), or slam them with a withering attack and grapple them a second time.<br /> <br /> Solar Brawl, Terrestrial Brawl, and even Mantis Style don't enable knocking an opponent down when I pin them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T13:29:57-08:00","id":1346560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346548#post1346548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But speaking of grappling and how terrifying it is, I've been looking for and failing to find any method for grappling my opponent that allows me to knock them prone at the same time. I either need to grapple an opponent who is already prone, using a smashing savaging attack (and few unarmed attacks have the Smash keyword), or slam them with a withering attack and grapple them a second time.<br /> <br /> Solar Brawl, Terrestrial Brawl, and even Mantis Style don't enable knocking an opponent down when I pin them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crashing Wave Throw + Lightning Strikes Twice should let you do that in a single tick. Technically you still have to grapple twice, but the second grapple is against DV 0, so it should be a cinch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T14:53:19-08:00","id":1346585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346560#post1346560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crashing Wave Throw + Lightning Strikes Twice should let you do that in a single tick. Technically you still have to grapple twice, but the second grapple is against DV 0, so it should be a cinch.</div> </div> </div> </div>All that to replicate the kind of flying tackle any mortal could perform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T15:16:29-08:00","id":1346589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346548#post1346548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But speaking of grappling and how terrifying it is, I've been looking for and failing to find any method for grappling my opponent that allows me to knock them prone at the same time. I either need to grapple an opponent who is already prone, using a smashing savaging attack (and few unarmed attacks have the Smash keyword), or slam them with a withering attack and grapple them a second time.<br /> <br /> Solar Brawl, Terrestrial Brawl, and even Mantis Style don't enable knocking an opponent down when I pin them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raging Tiger Pounce (Tiger Style) should suit your needs just fine. Reed Breaking Banda (Swaying Grass Dance Style) does the same thing just way worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T15:54:51-08:00","id":1346598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346585#post1346585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that to replicate the kind of flying tackle any mortal could perform.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you just want a mortal-level flying tackle then you can just do a Gambit that includes both a Grapple and a knock prone. It will be more expensive than a regular Grapple but it will get the job done without any Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T15:55:21-08:00","id":1346599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346548#post1346548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But speaking of grappling and how terrifying it is, I've been looking for and failing to find any method for grappling my opponent that allows me to knock them prone at the same time. I either need to grapple an opponent who is already prone, using a smashing savaging attack (and few unarmed attacks have the Smash keyword), or slam them with a withering attack and grapple them a second time.<br /> <br /> Solar Brawl, Terrestrial Brawl, and even Mantis Style don't enable knocking an opponent down when I pin them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Earth Dragon? It's a martial arts so it can do grappling, and it has smash attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T15:59:27-08:00","id":1346600,"title":"","content":"Earth Brawl also lets you make unarmed smash attacks. Earth melee Dragon Graced Weapon grants smash attacks to any melee weapon if it\u2019s already a grapple weapon, earth DGW adds grapple to a smash weapon. Those probably aren\u2019t what you mean though. Doing both with one attack certainly isn\u2019t unbalanceable, but it\u2019s pretty powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:03:14-08:00","id":1346601,"title":"","content":"Goddamnit. Most of the fight I've run so far is ineligible because I forgot you can't do grapple gambits with most weapons. I've seen RL people use swords and staffs and other weapons in grapples, so I just kinda blanked on that bit of rules interactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:06:21-08:00","id":1346603,"title":"","content":"You can initiate a grapple <i>while holding</i> a non-grappling weapon - after all, you've got another hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:07:12-08:00","id":1346604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346601#post1346601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goddamnit. Most of the fight I've run so far is ineligible because I forgot you can't do grapple gambits with most weapons. I've seen RL people use swords and staffs and other weapons in grapples, so I just kinda blanked on that bit of rules interactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are these guys all Immaculates? Because if they are everyone except the Fire aspect can just take a hand off their weapon and grapple with their free hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:10:13-08:00","id":1346606,"title":"","content":"Okay. Thank goodness. I can still keep going. I just need to give them all a specialty in grappling, because let me tell you those two dice matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:26:55-08:00","id":1346608,"title":"","content":"A specialty grants one die, not two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:32:47-08:00","id":1346610,"title":"","content":"For DBs it also boosts their excellency cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:33:47-08:00","id":1346611,"title":"","content":"So in my last session we had a great fight between my Dragon-Blooded and a Fair Folk Cataphract. It's a little cheaty in that the Cataphract NPC got, I think, one stunt bonus whilst Ganan got a stunt on pretty much every attack. But I kept notes, so enjoy. We did flub a little bit that we did anima flux at the bottom of the round instead of the top. Don't think it makes too much of a difference.<br /> <br /> Cynis Ganan - Starting Dragon-Blooded character:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Cynis Ganan<br /> Earth Aspect<br /> Righteous Warrior<br /> Heptagram<br /> <br /> Strength 5<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> Charisma 1<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Appearance 5<br /> <br /> Perception 1<br /> Intelligence 5<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> Earth Aspect Abilities (and Specialities) (6 BP)<br /> <br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Craft: Architecture 3 (Masonry)<br /> Integrity 4<br /> Resistance 3<br /> War 0<br /> <br /> Favoured Abilities (9 BP)<br /> <br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Brawl 1<br /> Earth Dragon Style 5 (Tetsubo)<br /> Lore: Heptagram education 5 (The Shogunate)<br /> Occult 5<br /> Performance 3<br /> <br /> Other Abilities<br /> <br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Melee 3<br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: High Realm) (3BP)<br /> <br /> Artifact 3 (Thunder\u2019s Crash Tetsubo (Fist of Titans))<br /> Martial Artist 4<br /> Pain Tolerance 4<br /> Well Bred 2<br /> (3 BP) Manse 3 (Stone of the Ram's Horn)<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Resources 3<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (Riverspeak)<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (Old Realm)<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> 1. Athletics: Effortlessly Rising Flame<br /> 2. Awareness: Precision Awareness Method<br /> 3. Brawl/Martial Arts: Become the Hammer<br /> 4. Integrity: Granite Curtain of Serenity<br /> 5. Performance: Audience Enthusing Display<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Melee: Elemental Sheath<br /> 2. Melee: Dragon Graced Weapon<br /> 3. Earth Dragon Style: Stone Dragon Skin<br /> 4. Earth Dragon Style: Force of the Mountain<br /> 5. Earth Dragon Style: Stillness of Stone Artemi<br /> 6. Earth Dragon Style: Unmoving Mountain Stance<br /> 7. Earth Dragon Style: Earth Dragon Form<br /> 8. Occult: Spirit Detecting Mirror<br /> 9. Occult: Spirit Grounding Shout<br /> 10. Occult: Secret Wind Revelation<br /> 11. Occult: Fivefold Resonance Stance<br /> 12. Occult: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> --. Control Spell: Invulnerable Skin of Bronze<br /> --. Shaping Ritual: Sevenfold Art Invocation<br /> 13. Resistance: Ox-body Technique<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> Free. Fist of Titans: Chambered Fist Charge<br /> 14. Fist of Titans: Mammoth Slam Quake<br /> 15. Fist of Titans: Unstoppable Hammering Blow<br /> <br /> Intimacies<br /> Defining Principle: The Dragon-Blooded are born to rule.<br /> Major Principle: The Immaculate Philosophy (Devout Belief)<br /> Major Principle: I am the mountain, strong and stable \u2013 I do not flee and I am unmoved by tears<br /> Minor Principle: Duty before pleasure<br /> Minor Principle: \u201cI like creating and repairing things.\u201d<br /> Minor Principle: The children are the foundation of the future<br /> Major Tie: Anathema (Loathing)<br /> Major Tie: Mnemon Alinos Danireya (Love)<br /> Major Tie: My Wife's House (Loyalty)<br /> Minor Tie: My children (Familial love)<br /> Minor Tie: Ragara Bhagwei (Respect)<br /> Minor Tie: House Cynis (Familial duty)<br /> Minor Tie: Amilar Shavok (&quot;I want to be sure he is dead&quot;)<br /> <br /> Evasion 3<br /> Parry 6 (+3, 6m)(With tetsubo or Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, else 5; +2, 4m)<br /> <br /> Soak 9 Hardness 8 (Invulnerable Skin of Bronze)<br /> (+5/0, Earth Dragon Form)<br /> (+3/+1, 5m/turn or Bonfire)<br /> <br /> Mobility Penalty -0<br /> Resist Poison: 4 dice<br /> <br /> Fist of Titans Smash Attacks (Earth Dragon Form): Accuracy 16 (14 Decisive)(+3, reroll 6s on damage, 3m), Damage 19 (+1/scene, 3m on summon; +5, 3m) (Overwhelming 5, 6 for 2m), Bashing, Smashing (-1i, no Defence penalty), Reaching, Two handed<br /> <br /> Javelin: Accuracy 9/8/7 (5 Decisive), Damage 14 (OVR 1), Lethal, Melee (Parry 5), Thrown (Medium)<br /> <br /> Join Battle 9 (+3 to result)(+3 successes, 6m)<br /> Rush 11 (+3 successes, 10s explode, 6m)<br /> Disengage 5<br /> <br /> Overwhelming Performance: 8 dice, +1 success and ignore multiple character penalty for 2m<br /> <br /> Resolve 5 (+2, ignore -1 from wounds, deprivation or poison, 4m)<br /> Guile 1<br /> <br /> Willpower 5<br /> Essence 2<br /> <br /> Personal motes 13<br /> Peripheral motes 31 (26, 5 committed)<br /> <br /> Health Track (3m/tick, ignore one point of penalties)<br /> -0 x1<br /> -1 x2<br /> -1 x4<br /> -3 x1<br /> Incap</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Eletha The Beautiful - Fair Folk Cataphract, Corebook page 534<br /> <br /> The Fight<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Eletha sighs contemptuously and quips about how the beautiful ones are always as dumb as rocks... and battle is enjoined. <br /> <br /> Ganan rolls a Full Excellency.<br /> <br /> Eletha: 8i 20m 7WP<br /> Ganan: 10i 13/20m 1a 5WP Invulnerable Skin of Bronze already active<br /> <br /> Short Range<br /> <br /> 1) As Ganan Reflexively pulls his tetsubo from a bolder (Dragon-Graced Weapon) and warily sizes up his foe with Chambered Fist Charge. <br /> <br /> Eletha reaches into the Dragon-Blooded's mind to pull forth a ravening mass of grotesques with Marching Fever Dream Nightmare. <br /> <br /> The grotesques take aim, slavering at the mouth ready to pounce.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 9i 13/20m 5WP 2a Earth Aura Aim bonus on Eletha<br /> Eletha: 8i 15m 6WP<br /> Minions: 9i Mag 9 Size 2 Aim bonus on Ganan<br /> <br /> 2) The grotesques await orders from their master. (7i)<br /> <br /> Ganan seizes the initative and charges Eletha, easily reaching him with an Essence backed Rush which flares his anima totemic before collapsing into a roaring sand storm. (Forfeiting his Aim bonus.)<br /> <br /> Eletha gives a howling shriek of mirth and sorrow, Commanding the grotesques to attack. (5 successes.)<br /> <br /> The grotesques have allowed the Dragon to charge into their maw, and on the signal from their master they converge with a gnashing of teeth (Aim and Command bonus, +8). As the blows rain down, Ganan shifts into Earth Dragon Form. I am the mountain. The blows slow the Dragon, blunting his offensive (-2i).<br /> <br /> Ganan: 7i 12/11m (3a, Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form for the rest of the fight)<br /> Eletha: 8i 20m 6WP<br /> Minions: 7i Mag 9 Size 2<br /> <br /> 3) Eletha orders his minions to stop playing with their food and bring him the Dragon-Blooded's pretty head. (5 successes.)<br /> <br /> The grotesques set about Ganan, but the Earth Master stands proud amongst the howling storm and their blows find no purchase.<br /> <br /> Ganan is the Hammer (3m) and strikes at Eletha with the Force of the Mountain (3m), putting all he has (1WP) into a Smashing (-1i) attack with his tetsubo -- determined to turn the tide against the fey. The blow connects, knocking the laughing Eletha to the ground (5i).<br /> <br /> Ganan: 12i 12/10m 4WP<br /> Eletha: 3i 20m 6WP Prone<br /> Minions: 7i Mag 9 Size 2<br /> <br /> 4) Ganan seeks to knock Eletha clear of the m\u00eal\u00e8e, Smashing (-1i) the prone fey clear of its minions (+2 dice from Become the Hammer, 2m; FotM, 3m). The mighty blow connects (9i), sending the fey flying as he Rushes after it. The blow Crashes the fey, ending its mocking laughter.<br /> <br /> The nightmares charge after Ganan and their fallen master and attempt again to slash and stab Ganan into submission, but they can find no gap in his defences.<br /> <br /> Eletha tries (1WP) to regain its footing whilst slashing at Ganan with its sword. Ganan does not allow this being of supernatural grace to rise, keeping Eletha down, even as the fey's whisper thin blade strikes at his leg, drawing a thin stream of blood (1i).<br /> <br /> The sandstorm of Ganan's anima batters the fey, driving them back. (1 damage each.)<br /> <br /> Ganan: 26i 12/10m 4WP<br /> Eletha: -4i 5WP Prone and Flurry penalty 1 damage<br /> Minions: 7i Mag 8 Size 2<br /> <br /> 5) The blow of the mountain (3m) is Decisive. The crushing blow would have killed any mere mortal, and bends the fey's neck to a sickening angle (10 damage).<br /> <br /> The grotes close in on all sides seeking to Engage (5i) the Earth Dragon, but Ganan will not be stopped, standing strong even as their blades and teeth bite at him (control roll lost, withering attack 1i).<br /> <br /> Eletha will not be denied (1WP) rising from prone like a puppet raised on tangled strings. Its unnaturally bent body moves in ways no human could, and it slashes at Ganan whilst he is distracted by the grotes (2i), drawing a howl of anguish and pain (Crashed, Initative Shift). Taking delight in this change of fortune, Eletha slashes again (2i).<br /> <br /> The sandstorm continues to lash the fey (-1i, 1 damage)<br /> <br /> Ganan: -2i 12/12m 4WP Crashed Engaged Onslaught-2<br /> Eletha: 10i 4WP 11 damage (-2)<br /> Minions: 5i Mag 7 Size 2<br /> <br /> 6) Eletha seizes Ganan (Grapple, lost control roll), hoisting him high into the air and Slamming him down into the ground. (Memo to self: remember Ganan has Charms specifically to stop this next time.)<br /> <br /> The grotes tear chunks out of the prone Ganan (1 damage). Rending him with wicked claws and curved blades.<br /> <br /> Surging with the power of Earth, Ganan rises from prone, the very stones themselves lifting him back into the fight (1WP) and lays into the nightmare army of grotesques, scattering them to the shadows and hidden places (Full Excellency+Force, 9m; 15i)<br /> <br /> Ganan: 15i 8/12m 3WP (Should Ganan have got a Crash bonus? Yes he should. I'm an idiot.)<br /> Eletha: 9i 4WP<br /> Minions: Ded<br /> <br /> 7) Hammering with the Force of the Mountain (6m), Ganan smashes Eletha prone (7i).<br /> <br /> The Cataphract rises like a marionette with one of its strings cut. Even mauled, it moves with a grace unmatched by any mortal solider and attacks again, but Ganan is blessed by the Dragons and he deflects the blow.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 22i 7/12m 3WP<br /> Eletha: 2i 4WP<br /> <br /> 8) Looking to end the fight, Ganan strikes another Decisive Smash (6m), but Eletha responds with Writhing Ego Inversion (7m). Ganan brings his weapon down, staving in the fae's chest, buckling its armor with a sickening crunch. The blow is devestating (6 damage), but the fey will not yield.<br /> <br /> No longer moving anything like a living thing, the body of Eletha the Broken pulls itself from the ground and pantomimes an attack, easily deflected by the Dragon.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 3i 6/12m -0 wound penalty<br /> Eletha: 2i 18m -4 wound penalty<br /> <br /> 9) Shifting with the flow of combat, Ganan sets one foot behind the other and braces himself against the fae's coming charge (Delay, -2i). Spinning like a demented puppet, Eletha charges and Ganan meets him head on (Clash, Force of the Mountain, Become the Hammer 6m). Tetsubo crashes past blade and Eletha comes crashing to the ground (12i, Crash). The puppet's last string is cut.<br /> <br /> The fae lord twists its head unnaturally to look up at Ganan, thick, white ichor pouring from every orifice in bloodly rivlets. The raging storm of Ganan's anima finally grinds down the last of the mighty Raksha's resistance (Incapacitated). The Eletha the Broken goes slack, its mighty form shattered. <br /> <br /> Ganan: 5/12m<br /> <br /> Ganan sheds a level of anima to banish his weapon (3m, 1a), clasps the half-dead creature in irons and Reya signals the retreat, swooping in to carry her husband and the unconscious Raksha back to Dovak.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 2/12m 2a 1 Lethal Damage (-0)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That was one of the best fights I've ever had in Exalted. It was so unbelievably tense, right up to the second Decisive. Round 6 opens with Ganan at -3 Defence Onslaught, -2 Defence Engaged, -1 Parry Prone, Crashed... then he Flurries, stands up and wipes out a practically undamaged Scale of battle-ready troops. Which dramatically turns the tide. I was on a knife edge the whole session. I really should have used Unmoving Mountain Stance on the Slam, but I completely spaced out.<br /> <br /> Anyone got a good foe for a combat focused Deeb? The Cataphract is a <i>supurb</i> opponent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-07-2019, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:39:24-08:00","id":1346612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346604#post1346604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are these guys all Immaculates? Because if they are everyone except the Fire aspect can just take a hand off their weapon and grapple with their free hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <b>never</b> need to Draw/Ready an Unarmed attack, and can deliver Unarmed attacks (with the Grappling tag) via &quot;kicks made with the character's [...] feet&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:44:51-08:00","id":1346615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346608#post1346608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A specialty grants one die, not two.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. But for DBs it means you can add another die with the excellency. Which is what I meant. Sorry if I was unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T19:09:04-08:00","id":1346634,"title":"","content":"Multi-quote function is fucked up and I'm impatient.<br /> <br /> <br /> Raging Tiger Pounce has to supplement an attack that causes damage; therefore, it cannot supplement a gambit.<br /> <br /> Stone Fist Strike and Rolling Boulder Blow are the same. Cannot supplement gambits.<br /> <br /> There is no Earth Dragon Style Charm that can supplement a gambit to cause knockdown.<br /> <br /> I'd already mentioned knocking the victim prone with a smashing savaging attack, which doesn't need any of those Charms if the grappler has a smashing weapon -- anything from a cestus to a grand goremaul would work.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea of making a custom gambit which works LIKE (or AS) a grapple gambit, but costs more Initiative AND renders you and your target prone, has some merit to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T19:33:31-08:00","id":1346640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346634#post1346634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multi-quote function is fucked up and I'm impatient.<br /> <br /> <br /> Raging Tiger Pounce has to supplement an attack that causes damage; therefore, it cannot supplement a gambit.<br /> <br /> Stone Fist Strike and Rolling Boulder Blow are the same. Cannot supplement gambits.<br /> <br /> There is no Earth Dragon Style Charm that can supplement a gambit to cause knockdown.<br /> <br /> I'd already mentioned knocking the victim prone with a smashing savaging attack, which doesn't need any of those Charms if the grappler has a smashing weapon -- anything from a cestus to a grand goremaul would work.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea of making a custom gambit which works LIKE (or AS) a grapple gambit, but costs more Initiative AND renders you and your target prone, has some merit to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Earth Dragon has Force of the Mountain, which gives unarmed attacks the smashing tag. Which means you can make a smashing grapple attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T04:42:11-08:00","id":1346696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346611#post1346611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in my last session we had a great fight between my Dragon-Blooded and a Fair Folk Cataphract. It's a little cheaty in that the Cataphract NPC got, I think, one stunt bonus whilst Ganan got a stunt on pretty much every attack. (...) The Cataphract is a <i>supurb</i> opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You, uhh, also seem to have forgotten about the most powerful Charm the cataphract has (Insidious Terror Mien). Between the ability to effectively ignore soak, a 16 dice/16 base damage attack, and 18 health levels on top of a respectable defensive suite, I don't think a properly played Cataphract is consistently beatable for any Dragon-Blood straight out of chargen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T04:59:43-08:00","id":1346698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13466#post13466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You, uhh, also seem to have forgotten about the most powerful Charm the cataphract has (Insidious Terror Mien). Between the ability to effectively ignore soak, a 16 dice/16 base damage attack, and 18 health levels on top of a respectable defensive suite, I don't think a properly played Cataphract is consistently beatable for any Dragon-Blood straight out of chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible, but hard. The fey has the stats of a focused exalt, but no excellencies, and one good soak enhancing and one great but conditional soak ignoring charm. In this case Ganan had an appropriate intimacy and could have ignored it. I wouldn't count on winning, if I had the option to not fight that battle with my character I'd take it, but I wouldn't resign myself to death either. I think with the right kind of character you stand a better chance than a coin flip. Like don't be an archer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T06:02:50-08:00","id":1346705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346696#post1346696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You, uhh, also seem to have forgotten about the most powerful Charm the cataphract has (Insidious Terror Mien). Between the ability to effectively ignore soak, a 16 dice/16 base damage attack, and 18 health levels on top of a respectable defensive suite, I don't think a properly played Cataphract is consistently beatable for any Dragon-Blood straight out of chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Characters with a Major or Defining Intimacy representing courage, valor, or a similar resilience to fear may pay a point of Willpower to become immune to this Charm for a scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cynis Ganan Major Principle: I am the mountain, strong and stable \u2013 I do not flee<br /> <br /> Things got absolutely nailbiting watching the Willpower points drop (&quot;SURELY that counts as a two-point stunt, right? Please? No? Okay...&quot;), but it wasn't forgotten. Certainly dropping Ganan's Soak from 17 to 8 would have been useful if he did run out of Willpower, but it's hardly &quot;ignoring&quot; soak.<br /> <br /> <br /> Writhing Ego Inversion could have got more use (Eletha went down with 4 WP still in the tank which should have been blown on resetting WEI). And the battlegroup should have Engaged more -- it's not like they're using the Initative for anything else.<br /> <br /> It's such a good fight, I wouldn't mind running it in the Arena against a more optimised Deeb (Ganan doesn't even have a maxed Join Battle pool -- he's built for combat but I could go harder) on a fairer ground (Ganan wasn't stunting defences, but <i>was</i> getting a free +2 dice on every attack -- it's not exactly perfect test conditions, it just came up in play as being a fight for the ages).<br /> <br /> It's absolutely not <i>consistently</i> beatable (Ganan did have a battlegroup and two more Dragon-Blooded sitting at Long range just in case), but apart from Ganan getting 15 successes on 20-something dice for the damage roll against the battlegroup in round 6, and Eletha failing to throw one success on five dice to stand up in round 4, the dice were pretty average all the way through.<br /> <br /> Now five Deebs against 5 Cataphracts would be interesting as the Cat is built to fight multiple opponents. And with Onslaught and Flurrying Command orders with attacks, I could see the Deebs getting picked on. (But Cataphract's also don't have Hardness, so I could see five elemental animas absolutely wrecking them... archery and orders might be the optimal play there?)<br /> <br /> Certainly the Cataphract is built to lead troops and probably shouldn't be the focus of a one-on-one duel.<br /> <br /> But darn, that was a good fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-07-2019, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T08:09:26-08:00","id":1346727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346705#post1346705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now five Deebs against 5 Cataphracts would be interesting as the Cat is built to fight multiple opponents. And with Onslaught and Flurrying Command orders with attacks, I could see the Deebs getting picked on. (But Cataphract's also don't have Hardness, so I could see five elemental animas absolutely wrecking them... archery and orders might be the optimal play there?)<br /> <br /> Certainly the Cataphract is built to lead troops and probably shouldn't be the focus of a one-on-one duel.<br /> <br /> But darn, that was a good fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a good fight, but you have the same takeaway as I did when I ran a 1-1 Cataphract fight. They\u2019re very clearly meant to be used alone or in pairs maybe against a group of PCs. I mean just look at Dreadful Fanged Maelstrom, that can easily smash two weaker defense characters and force their withdrawal. I also completely forgot engage actions exist, and they\u2019re very much the battlegroups response to a single powerful character. Worse yet I was using a guy in light armor with Raging Dragon, so his soak would have actually gone up if the Cataphract used his offensive charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T08:19:08-08:00","id":1346729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346640#post1346640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earth Dragon has Force of the Mountain, which gives unarmed attacks the smashing tag. Which means you can make a smashing grapple attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Is that from a later version of the backer documents?<br /> <br /> But it doesn't refute what I said about the smashing tag being incompatible with gambits.<br /> <br /> I will concede that succeeding at a grappling gambit and using a cestus, or Stone Fist Strike, or Rolling Boulder Blow, or (apparently) Force of the Mountain on an immediate savaging smashing attack (Raging Tiger Pounce wouldn't need the attack to be smashing) WOULD sufficiently model tackling an opponent to the ground with a clinch.<br /> <br /> And it wouldn't even require the attacker to go prone as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T08:36:40-08:00","id":1346736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346727#post1346727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a good fight, but you have the same takeaway as I did when I ran a 1-1 Cataphract fight. They\u2019re very clearly meant to be used alone or in pairs maybe against a group of PCs. I mean just look at Dreadful Fanged Maelstrom, that can easily smash two weaker defense characters and force their withdrawal. I also completely forgot engage actions exist, and they\u2019re very much the battlegroups response to a single powerful character. Worse yet I was using a guy in light armor with Raging Dragon, so his soak would have actually gone up if the Cataphract used his offensive charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to confess, when we were looking for this week's monster, I pushed for the Cataphract based on having read your fight and knowing it was totally &quot;doable&quot; so long as the dice didn't hate me. Wasn't really looking to break new ground with that one.<br /> <br /> I was sort of hoping you might have a similiar challenge in mind (but the next session is likely to be a gauntlet of lesser foes, then the session after that will see Ganan have spent some XP).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T08:43:20-08:00","id":1346739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346727#post1346727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also completely forgot engage actions exist, and they\u2019re very much the battlegroups response to a single powerful character.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a <i>RWBY</i> fan, I've recently been exploring how THIS is the thing that makes Grimm really dangerous.<br /> <br /> That is: Almost any Creature of Grimm has at least as much mass as (and frequently more than) a human being, and Grimm usually try to tackle and pin targets to the ground.<br /> <br /> This is why I've been asking about how to model that capability.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the Red Trailer, Ruby Rose made exterminating battle-groups of Beowolves look easy because she avoided all but one attack, and that attack only knocked her back rather than down. Since she consistently avoided getting knocked prone or grappled, she always retained her complete freedom of movement.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this was also helped by her ability to kill the closest Grimm in a single attack, and sometimes kill multiple Grimm with a single attack, thus denying them these individuals the ability to attack her at all. But that doesn't map very well to battle-groups.<br /> <br /> But in the Weiss Short, Weiss Schnee gives a similar performance until she slips up and shows us how quickly Ruby could have died. Even ignoring the exact mistakes leading up to it, as soon as one Beowolf grappled Weiss and bore her down to the ground, she became unable to dodge or retreat, and she could not have easily parried or struck back with her sword even if she hadn't been disarmed. She was seconds away from being dogpiled and savaged to death by the other Beowolves when her sister banished them all.<br /> <br /> I'm away from my book right now, so I can only vaguely recall that being &quot;engaged&quot; by a battle-group isn't as restrictive as being grappled by a single opponent.<br /> <br /> Also, calling it &quot;engaged&quot; was a silly idea, since it's not what the Disengage action is supposed to counter.<br /> <br /> It's as silly as not actually making more deliberate use of the &quot;embattled&quot; term that actually denotes the condition that the Disengage action is supposed to counter -- being caught at close-range by an opponent such that moving away is impossible without using a Disengage action. &quot;Embattled&quot; should have been called &quot;Engaged&quot; instead, and the term should actually be used in Charms designed to counter engagement.<br /> <br /> A battle-group's ability to grapple could have called &quot;embattle&quot; instead, or something like &quot;mobbing&quot;, &quot;grasping&quot;, &quot;pinning&quot;. Or just call it grappling.<br /> <br /> <br /> But in any case, the publicly available preview for Volume 7 continues to treat the Grimm this way: As long as our heroes mange to strike them first, the Grimm die instantly and the danger seems minimal. Our heroes rarely give the Grimm a chance to test their Parry or Evasion ratings.<br /> <br /> But repeatedly, other Grimm attack from a hero's blindside with a pounce intended to grapple and savage them. Twice, a hero is saved from this fate by an ally shooting the Grimm dead at the last second. Jaune counters being grappled by using his shield to bodily hold the Grimm at arm's length as he stabs it dead, but it takes so much of his effort that a second Grimm attacking from behind would have gotten him.<br /> <br /> The preview ends just as Blake is looking up in horror at a Grimm pouncing on her in slow-motion; the framing is clearly that this is an extremely vulnerable moment that could cause her real harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-07-2019, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:04:15-08:00","id":1346742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346729#post1346729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it wouldn't even require the attacker to go prone as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s also just awesomely powerful. You could definitely make a gambit that does both grapple and knockdown in one go, maybe a cost of 4-5?<br /> <br /> Having both conditions on you at once lowers your Evasion by 3, Parry by 2 and attacks by either 4 or 6. If they survive the grapple they also don\u2019t get to jump back up from prone either. I like the combo, it\u2019s awesome and also feels appropriate to being pinned on your face, as long as the cost fits I say go for it. It\u2019s just that grabbing and making a smash attack doesn\u2019t require any asking of the ST or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:38:41-08:00","id":1346752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346739#post1346739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a <i>RWBY</i> fan, I've recently been exploring how THIS is the thing that makes Grimm really dangerous.<br /> <br /> That is: Almost any Creature of Grimm has at least as much mass as (and frequently more than) a human being, and Grimm usually try to tackle and pin targets to the ground.<br /> <br /> This is why I've been asking about how to model that capability.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the Red Trailer, Ruby Rose made exterminating battle-groups of Beowolves look easy because she avoided all but one attack, and that attack only knocked her back rather than down. Since she consistently avoided getting knocked prone or grappled, she always retained her complete freedom of movement.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this was also helped by her ability to kill the closest Grimm in a single attack, and sometimes kill multiple Grimm with a single attack, thus denying them these individuals the ability to attack her at all. But that doesn't map very well to battle-groups.<br /> <br /> But in the Weiss Short, Weiss Schnee gives a similar performance until she slips up and shows us how quickly Ruby could have died. Even ignoring the exact mistakes leading up to it, as soon as one Beowolf grappled Weiss and bore her down to the ground, she became unable to dodge or retreat, and she could not have easily parried or struck back with her sword even if she hadn't been disarmed. She was seconds away from being dogpiled and savaged to death by the other Beowolves when her sister banished them all.<br /> <br /> I'm away from my book right now, so I can only vaguely recall that being &amp;quot;engaged&amp;quot; by a battle-group isn't as restrictive as being grappled by a single opponent.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>They can not restrain/drag targets, but being engaged prevents movement. Also Engage is actually insanely deadly. Firstly it auto succeeds to lock in the grapple, no initiative roll required. Next the control roll uses their highest combat stat, not their unarmed stat, so if they\u2019re melee focused they get to use melee to determine rounds of control, and also melee to make savaging attacks. <br /> <br /> Here\u2019s the silly part though, command actions add dice to ALL actions that battlegroup makes that turn. So if you u give them +7 dice for a command roll to engage, they get that to make the attack, determine rounds of control, and on their free savaging attack, which with the right weapons can be a smash or pierce or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:39:54-08:00","id":1346753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346736#post1346736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was sort of hoping you might have a similiar challenge in mind (but the next session is likely to be a gauntlet of lesser foes, then the session after that will see Ganan have spent some XP).</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what\u2019s a good single enemy that doesn\u2019t have a lot of charms focused on single combat, or what would be a better duelist antagonist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:46:03-08:00","id":1346756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346742#post1346742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s also just awesomely powerful. You could definitely make a gambit that does both grapple and knockdown in one go, maybe a cost of 4-5?<br /> <br /> Having both conditions on you at once lowers your Evasion by 3, Parry by 2 and attacks by either 4 or 6. If they survive the grapple they also don\u2019t get to jump back up from prone either. I like the combo, it\u2019s awesome and also feels appropriate to being pinned on your face, as long as the cost fits I say go for it. It\u2019s just that grabbing and making a smash attack doesn\u2019t require any asking of the ST or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every tackler will have a weapon with the smashing tag, and it shouldn't be necessary to have a cestus.<br /> <br /> Increasing the cost of the grappling gambit could be seen as substituting for the need (and cost) of using a cestus or hammer to make an immediate savaging attack count as smashing.<br /> <br /> And the idea is that this custom gambit WOULD require the attacker to go prone as well. NOT needing to go prone was a factor of using a normal grapple and then using the savaging attack itself to knock the target prone by whatever means.<br /> <br /> <br /> But however you pull it off, grabbing and making an immediate savaging smashing attack is indeed a powerful combo, and best of all it's completely legal within the base rules. It's an extremely natural, simple, and effective tactic that virtually any mob of enemies can and should instinctively employ.<br /> <br /> It's also another thing that Brawl boasts over various Martial Arts Styles. An Earth Dragon stylist can try this tactic to render an Anathema vulnerable to his Hearthmates, but Terrestrial Brawl is so much effective at it, whether with the Water or Earth elemental Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> The additional penalties to Evasion and Parry don't actually matter to the grappler, as savaging and throwing attacks count the victim's Defense as 0 to begin with and those values cannot go lower than that. Unless dice-adders can raise the 0 up into positive numbers; then I could see the penalties eating the dice-bonuses.<br /> <br /> But it definitely matters to the grappler's friends.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm away from my materials, so I forget if the Restrain action penalizes Defense against other characters or just prevents the victim from taking actions on their turn (or even outside of their turn, through Reflexive Charms).<br /> <br /> I don't think battle-groups can Restrain, though I imagine a battle-group might have a special trained ability, or being composed of beings with a magical or biological restraining ability, which would Restrain a victim so their commander could attack unhindered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-07-2019, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T10:10:36-08:00","id":1346760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346752#post1346752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can not restrain/drag targets, but being engaged prevents movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do characters within close range of battle-groups not become &quot;embattled&quot;, and thus can retreat without a Disengage action?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also Engage is actually insanely deadly. Firstly it auto succeeds to lock in the grapple, no initiative roll required. Next the control roll uses their highest combat stat, not their unarmed stat, so if they\u2019re melee focused they get to use melee to determine rounds of control </div> </div> </div>So a battle-group of javelin-throwers or stone-slingers could &quot;grapple / engage&quot; entirely with their Thrown rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and also melee to make savaging attacks. </div> </div> </div>Didn't Vance rule that characters could make Melee-savaging attacks in a grapple? Like shanking someone with a knife, or choking someone out with the haft of your goremaul that you're holding against their throat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T10:19:11-08:00","id":1346762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346756#post1346756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The additional penalties to Evasion and Parry don't actually matter to the grappler, as savaging and throwing attacks count the victim's Defense as 0 to begin with and those values cannot go lower than that. Unless dice-adders can raise the 0 up into positive numbers; then I could see the penalties eating the dice-bonuses.<br /> <br /> But it definitely matters to the grappler's friends.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm away from my materials, so I forget if the Restrain action penalizes Defense against other characters or just prevents the victim from taking actions on their turn (or even outside of their turn, through Reflexive Charms).<br /> <br /> I don't think battle-groups can Restrain, though I imagine a battle-group might have a special trained ability, or being composed of beings with a magical or biological restraining ability, which would Restrain a victim so their commander could attack unhindered.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we\u2019re talking a bit about a couple different things here separately. Battlegroups just can\u2019t restrain at all, so getting them into the position of knockdown+grapple+restrain would require a lot of changes and probably a special battlegroup or a charm or both. There\u2019s also knockdown while grappling and knockdown+restrain while grappling. <br /> <br /> I think if you wanted to do what the grims are doing they\u2019d probably just be engaging with maybe knockdown, because they\u2019re still doing damage, not just holding. I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s really possible to balance being able to Engage + knockdown + restrain + savage all at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T10:23:51-08:00","id":1346764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346760#post1346760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do characters within close range of battle-groups not become &amp;quot;embattled&amp;quot;, and thus can retreat without a Disengage action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but engage stops that. You oddly can\u2019t disengage from a battlegroup engaging you, you need to break their grapple first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346760#post1346760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a battle-group of javelin-throwers or stone-slingers could &amp;quot;grapple / engage&amp;quot; entirely with their Thrown rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the initial grapple roll to hit, yes. That roll doesn\u2019t care about overflow successes though, and still gets command dice and size/might bonuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346760#post1346760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Vance rule that characters could make Melee-savaging attacks in a grapple? Like shanking someone with a knife, or choking someone out with the haft of your goremaul that you're holding against their throat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t remember, but the book states a savage attack must be unarmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T10:30:02-08:00","id":1346768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346762#post1346762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we\u2019re talking a bit about a couple different things here separately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, sorry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Battlegroups just can\u2019t restrain at all, so getting them into the position of knockdown+grapple+restrain would require a lot of changes and probably a special battlegroup or a charm or both. There\u2019s also knockdown while grappling and knockdown+restrain while grappling. </div> </div> </div>I would definitely give a battle-group of beasts the ability to knock someone prone with at least the initial savaging attack following the grapple, to facilitate dogpiling and devouring people alive.<br /> <br /> No need to give Grimm a special restrain action, since that's not what they do, but battle-groups of other creatures...<br /> <br /> <br /> On that note, do you ever use Might? Or, when you use a battle-group of Blood Apes, do you just let the battle-group use the Blood Ape Charms?<br /> <br /> Rather than using Might to abstract the mixed abilities of a battle-group of Blood Apes and some other demons, I think I'd just have separate battle-groups for each different species of demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T10:33:52-08:00","id":1346769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346753#post1346753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like what\u2019s a good single enemy that doesn\u2019t have a lot of charms focused on single combat, or what would be a better duelist antagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either. Both. More the latter -- duelist antagonists are what I really want for the campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:27:00-08:00","id":1346789,"title":"","content":"Can a battlegroup grapple/engage only one character at a time? One character for each dot of size?<br /> <br /> Logically, there has to be some limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:29:48-08:00","id":1346790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346768#post1346768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, sorry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would definitely give a battle-group of beasts the ability to knock someone prone with at least the initial savaging attack following the grapple, to facilitate dogpiling and devouring people alive.<br /> <br /> No need to give Grimm a special restrain action, since that's not what they do, but battle-groups of other creatures...<br /> <br /> <br /> On that note, do you ever use Might? Or, when you use a battle-group of Blood Apes, do you just let the battle-group use the Blood Ape Charms?<br /> <br /> Rather than using Might to abstract the mixed abilities of a battle-group of Blood Apes and some other demons, I think I'd just have separate battle-groups for each different species of demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah a special merit for fey creatures that lets them pay a willpower as they Engage to also knockdown would be good. Or at least add the smashing keyword to their first attack, maybe with a benefit like reduced cost or penalty.<br /> <br /> I definitely use might and use charms for Battlegroup creatures at the same time. In my games a battlegroup of Bloodapes can do their gigantic howling roar, if ever you could field a battlegroup of terrestrial exalted they could use excellencies and basic charms that we can assume they all or even mostly have. I think that\u2019s both fair and RAW. A BG of 100 Bloodapes with Might 2 and charms is still like 1% as dangerous as 100 apes rolled into battle seperately anyway so the law of inverse ninja still holds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:34:05-08:00","id":1346791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346789#post1346789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a battlegroup grapple/engage only one character at a time? One character for each dot of size?<br /> <br /> Logically, there has to be some limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the limit is just \u201cHow many does your ST think is logical.\u201d A size 5 battlegroup is over 1,000 soldiers so, probably a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:34:50-08:00","id":1346792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346769#post1346769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either. Both. More the latter -- duelist antagonists are what I really want for the campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the corebook abyssal is pretty solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T12:02:29-08:00","id":1346806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346764#post1346764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but engage stops that. You oddly can\u2019t disengage from a battlegroup engaging you, you need to break their grapple first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but I remember that moving through a battlegroup counts as difficult terrain.<br /> <br /> A large enough battlegroup might fill multiple range bands, and if it can move so that a single character is a close range of the group's center, so the character is obviously surrounded on all sides, the character's ability to retreat could be slowed even if they avoid being engaged or knocked prone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can\u2019t remember, but the book states a savage attack must be unarmed. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's good, and Vance might have contradicted it.<br /> <br /> But I understand this might make savaging attacks more powerful than intended, especially with a Martial Arts Ability that can allow both grappling and weapon attacks, but usually such Styles have very limited grappling support or weapon attack support. Someone who double-dips into Brawl and Melee is arguably paying for the privilege.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T12:27:32-08:00","id":1346818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346806#post1346806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, but I remember that moving through a battlegroup counts as difficult terrain.<br /> <br /> A large enough battlegroup might fill multiple range bands, and if it can move so that a single character is a close range of the group's center, so the character is obviously surrounded on all sides, the character's ability to retreat could be slowed even if they avoid being engaged or knocked prone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just slowed, difficult terrain also imposes a dice penalty against all movement rolls, including rush and disengage actions. If you\u2019re fighting in the center of a size 5 battlegroup, not only do you need to take more movement actions to move through it, and pay initiative to do so, but you take a -3 penalty to disengage from any characters in the center. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346806#post1346806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's good, and Vance might have contradicted it.<br /> <br /> But I understand this might make savaging attacks more powerful than intended, especially with a Martial Arts Ability that can allow both grappling and weapon attacks, but usually such Styles have very limited grappling support or weapon attack support. Someone who double-dips into Brawl and Melee is arguably paying for the privilege.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but there\u2019s a lot of charms that make that maybe wonky. Hungry Tiger Technique either doubles overflow successes, or adds overflow successes to decisive damage, for example. If you double dip you should get some benefit, but that\u2019s probably too much. Especially since you always get a savage attack no matter what as long as you lock in the grapple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:05:24-08:00","id":1346826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346818#post1346818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just slowed, difficult terrain also imposes a dice penalty against all movement rolls, including rush and disengage actions. If you\u2019re fighting in the center of a size 5 battlegroup, not only do you need to take more movement actions to move through it, and pay initiative to do so, but you take a -3 penalty to disengage from any characters in the center.</div> </div> </div> </div>Penalties to movement actions could be important if the battlegroup is fighting together with an individual character ally, but otherwise the BG's individual character target doesn't need to disengage to retreat from the battlegroup, yes?<br /> <br /> What do you see as the minimum Size battlegroup that can cause an individual character such problems, and how easily could they do it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, but there\u2019s a lot of charms that make that maybe wonky. Hungry Tiger Technique either doubles overflow successes, or adds overflow successes to decisive damage, for example. If you double dip you should get some benefit, but that\u2019s probably too much. Especially since you always get a savage attack no matter what as long as you lock in the grapple. </div> </div> </div>Okay, but I see a &quot;compromise&quot; that follows the rules as written.<br /> <br /> Unarmed savaging attacks treat the victim's Defense as 0, not Melee attacks by the grappler. But the grappler's Melee-based savaging attacks DO get to exploit the victim's penalties to Parry or Evasion like any attack from a third party character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-07-2019, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T14:12:25-08:00","id":1346852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346826#post1346826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penalties to movement actions could be important if the battlegroup is fighting together with an individual character ally, but otherwise the BG's individual character target doesn't need to disengage to retreat from the battlegroup, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>No you need to disengage to move out of range of a battlegroup. Moving through it isn\u2019t disengaging because disengaging is moving from Close to Short range and moving through you stay at Close. Moving through also costs 1i per round in addition to counting as difficult terrain. Also battlegroups can spread, they don\u2019t have to be locked into tight formation. As long as the average distance between fighters is less than 10 yards, they\u2019re still considered a cohesive unit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346826#post1346826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you see as the minimum Size battlegroup that can cause an individual character such problems, and how easily could they do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Size one could do it easily. 6-7 people with 6 yard spacing between them fills a range band or most of a range band, and that\u2019s even before terrain concerns. Like six thugs in an alleyway or five walking statues in a ruined corridor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346826#post1346826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unarmed savaging attacks treat the victim's Defense as 0, not Melee attacks by the grappler. But the grappler's Melee-based savaging attacks DO get to exploit the victim's penalties to Parry or Evasion like any attack from a third party character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah I\u2019m pretty sure that\u2019s legit. You\u2019re not savaging them, you\u2019re just using a free hand or hands to hit them with your weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T14:28:50-08:00","id":1346855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346852#post1346852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No you need to disengage to move out of range of a battlegroup.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what you said earlier: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346764#post1346764\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...64#post1346764</a><br /> <br /> Unless we're miscommunicating. By &quot;retreat from the battlegroup&quot;, I meant moving from close range of the battle-group out to short range from it.<br /> <br /> If the battle-group isn't surrounding the character and imposing the &quot;difficult terrain&quot; penalty, the character can simply use a Move action without penalty or special cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Size one could do it easily. 6-7 people with 6 yard spacing between them fills a range band or most of a range band, and that\u2019s even before terrain concerns. Like six thugs in an alleyway or five walking statues in a ruined corridor. </div> </div> </div>So, a Size 1 group with enough room to spread out and no reason to be in a tight formation could effortlessly surround a single PC at close range, and impose the appropriate penalties.<br /> <br /> The PC cannot disengage, because they're not embattled by a singular important character. They can use a Move action, but it doesn't do anything immediately, because they need to take a second Move action on their next turn to finish retreating to short range... and the battlegroup could simply use its own Move action to enter close range and surround the PC again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fair to say that a Size 1 group dogpiling a single character by &quot;engaging&quot; them isn't spread out enough to fill the entire range band, but since the PC is engaged, they're actually rendered more immobile. Especially if the group knocks them prone as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T14:32:57-08:00","id":1346856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346855#post1346855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what you said earlier: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346764#post1346764\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...64#post1346764</a><br /> <br /> Unless we're miscommunicating. By &quot;retreat from the battlegroup&quot;, I meant moving from close range of the battle-group out to short range from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>DrLoveMonkey is saying Engage stops you Disengaging in that post. Which it does.<br /> <br /> You can be embattled with a battlegroup, and that stops you from using Reflexive Move to change range band relative to the battlegroup -- but you may move through the battlegroup, staying at close range to it. You need to Disengage to move away.<br /> <br /> If you are Engaged by a an Embattled battlegroup, you may not take a Disengage Action -- or any other Movement Action, including Reflexive Move to move through the battlegroup. (Further if you are Restrained you can't take any Actions, peroid: also no Disengaging.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-07-2019, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T14:51:19-08:00","id":1346859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346729#post1346729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Is that from a later version of the backer documents?<br /> <br /> But it doesn't refute what I said about the smashing tag being incompatible with gambits.<br /> <br /> I will concede that succeeding at a grappling gambit and using a cestus, or Stone Fist Strike, or Rolling Boulder Blow, or (apparently) Force of the Mountain on an immediate savaging smashing attack (Raging Tiger Pounce wouldn't need the attack to be smashing) WOULD sufficiently model tackling an opponent to the ground with a clinch.<br /> <br /> And it wouldn't even require the attacker to go prone as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see why the smashing tag would be incompatible? You do make an attack roll, and Force of the Mountain doesn't specify that it can't be made with a gambit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T14:57:40-08:00","id":1346862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346859#post1346859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why the smashing tag would be incompatible? You do make an attack roll, and Force of the Mountain doesn't specify that it can't be made with a gambit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could I knock someone prone with a disarming gambit then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:02:09-08:00","id":1346864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346855#post1346855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless we're miscommunicating.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are.<br /> <br /> When you're inside or right up against a battlegroup you're in Close range with them, and just like being in Close range with any enemy, you can't just move away freely. There's no just using your reflexive move to get away from a brawler when you're an archer, you need to take the Disengage action, where you roll your Dex + Dodge against their Dex + Athletics and pay some initiative to see if you can get away. Same holds true for battlegroups. If you're in a position where a battlegroup can hit you with their swords, and you want to move to a position where they can't, you need to Disengage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Engage is an action that can be taken by battlegroups that replaces the Grapple gambit, and also has essentially nothing to do with the Disengage action. It's just the shorthand word for &quot;Special battlegroup grapple.&quot; Instead of one character grabbing another by the arm, like a normal Grapple gambit, an Engage gambit has the battlegroup encircle the character with their weapons and totally blockade them. It acts very much like the Grapple gambit that regular individual characters can do though. One of the big things that it does is simply stop all movement. When you're the victim of a successful Engage action that a battlegroup takes against you, you can no longer move at all. You can't Disengage to get away from them, and you can't even reflexively move to get to another part of the battlegroup, you're stuck.<br /> <br /> In addition to that, they get to make their savaging attacks against you, just like a regular grappled target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:15:54-08:00","id":1346866,"title":"","content":"It may also be more helpful to place smaller battlegroups kind of between rangebands. Like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1 2 3 4<br /> OO|OO<br /> <br /> Where the battlegroup of guys is in between the middle two rangebands, and kind of filling into them slightly. That way moving from the second range band to the third takes 2 movement and initiative each time, and you need to disengage to move from the second rangeband to the first, or third to fourth. Then for larger ones you can do this.<br /> <br /> 1 2 3 4 5<br /> OO||||OO<br /> <br /> Where the third rangeband is entirely filled with the battlegroup, and slightly filtering into 2 and 4. Now you need to disengage from 2 to 1, or 4 to 5, and it takes 4 movement actions to move from 2 to 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:16:44-08:00","id":1346867,"title":"","content":"How does Disengaging and Rushing work within difficult terrain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:18:07-08:00","id":1346868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346867#post1346867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Disengaging and Rushing work within difficult terrain?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works exactly like normal, but if the ground between the two range bands is difficult terrain, you do it at a -3 penalty. Generally this will not be the case as you disengage from a battlegroup, unless the ground around you is already deep snow or a big crowd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:43:02-08:00","id":1346880,"title":"","content":"But basically, getting away from a battle-group can be really hard.<br /> <br /> First of all, you need to Disengage if they're at close range. If they're spread out enough to surround you, you suffer a -3 penalty to the disengage roll, while their countering roll is not inherently penalized in turn.<br /> <br /> If they Engage you, you cannot even try to Disengage until their rounds of control are exhausted.<br /> <br /> If they knock you prone, you cannot even try to Disengage until you rise from prone, which becomes a rolled action and counts as your movement action for the round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:59:11-08:00","id":1346885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346880#post1346880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But basically, getting away from a battle-group can be really hard.<br /> <br /> First of all, you need to Disengage if they're at close range. If they're spread out enough to surround you, you suffer a -3 penalty to the disengage roll, while their countering roll is not inherently penalized in turn.<br /> <br /> If they Engage you, you cannot even try to Disengage until their rounds of control are exhausted.<br /> <br /> If they knock you prone, you cannot even try to Disengage until you rise from prone, which becomes a rolled action and counts as your movement action for the round.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're on your own and actually inside a range band filled entirely with the group it's even worse than that. Moving between range bands that have the battlegroup in the interveneing space is difficult terrain, so takes you two movement actions to do. It's not difficult terrain for he battlegroup unless the ground is otherwise strewn with rocks or sticky mud. So you spend two rounds and 2i moving to a spot where you can try to disengage, and then they make a reflexive move to stick you right back in the middle.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: to illustrate, say we have this setup below, where range band 3 is totally filled with a battlegroup, and range bands 2 and 4 are both in Close range to the battlegroup.<br /> <br /> 1 2 3 4 5<br /> OO||||OO<br /> <br /> <br /> Now lets say your character is in range band 3, and wants to get away. Well, you can't disengage from the battlegroup from band 3, because even by moving a full range band you'd still be in Close range with them. So you need to get to band 2 or 4 first. You pick 4, but the battlegroup fills the entire area between 3 and 4, making it difficult terrain. So you make a reflexive move towards it, spending 1i to do so, but you don't actually move yet, you only move when you spend your next turn also moving towards it.<br /> <br /> So a turn goes by where you battle the army and they fight you, and then you use your reflexive move again to get to band 4. Next turn you can use Disengage to escape to band 5 and get away! Unfortunately, the battlegroup does this:<br /> <br /> 1 2 3 4 5<br /> OOO||||O<br /> <br /> Now they fill all of band 4, and you're right back where you started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 11-07-2019, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T16:46:00-08:00","id":1346892,"title":"","content":"So you make your second move the Disengage, so when they try to flumph back around you backpedaling ensues and you're at spot 5. <br /> <br /> But I don't agree with your geometry. I don't see anything that indicates that a BG is permitted to cheese the range system that way. I don't see any &quot;Close Minus One&quot; range band that says you have to move away a band to be just Close. <br /> The &quot;Surrounding and preventing retreat&quot; situation you describe sounds instead like an Engage gambit to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T16:59:40-08:00","id":1346896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346862#post1346862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could I knock someone prone with a disarming gambit then?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your using a thing with the smashing tag, I don't see why not? It would just cost an additional 2i.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T17:04:33-08:00","id":1346897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346892#post1346892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you make your second move the Disengage, so when they try to flumph back around you backpedaling ensues and you're at spot 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disengage is the action that you take when you want to move from close range to short range, and I don't think it lets you move more than one range band to do it? I guess RAW you just leap however far you have to in one action to get away. If that's the case then I guess it does work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346892#post1346892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't agree with your geometry. I don't see anything that indicates that a BG is permitted to cheese the range system that way. I don't see any &quot;Close Minus One&quot; range band that says you have to move away a band to be just Close.<br /> The &quot;Surrounding and preventing retreat&quot; situation you describe sounds instead like an Engage gambit to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...it's not really &quot;close minus one&quot;, it's just there's a bunch of range bands and they're ALL in close range with the battlegroup. The spanning 3 is just the minimum required for this, a battlegroup can span 4-5 range bands. On page 209 &quot;Two characters who are both within close range of a 500 battlegroup on opposite sides of it, for example, may well be at long range with regard to one another.&quot; battlegroups can cover a BIG area if they want to.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even have to be a regular shape either, they can completely fill a maze-like catacomb or man a network of defensive fortifications on a battlefield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T20:22:48-08:00","id":1346934,"title":"","content":"RAW, when you disengage, if the disengaged party attempts to move towards you, you reflexively move again to keep distance once. It is the same with Rush actions and people trying to move away after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T20:26:51-08:00","id":1346935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1346934#post1346934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, when you disengage, if the disengaged party attempts to move towards you, you reflexively move again to keep distance once. It is the same with Rush actions and people trying to move away after.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it\u2019s a bit of a weird territory with battlegroups because you can move away from them and still not be at short range. If you\u2019re in the middle of a massive army, and four range bands out in every direction are soldiers, what does disengaging even do?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying you can\u2019t get away, you could go vertically, surrender, just kill the army, magically teleport away, hide in the scenery by going to ground, convince them to let you go, there\u2019s lots of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T19:00:25-08:00","id":1348102,"title":"","content":"I ran a fight using a bunch of environmental penalties and giving stunt bonuses and stuff between a river dragon and 3 Dragonblooded who had a wide range of abilities. Their stats are below along with relevant charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Zorin, the dedicated warrior with a large artifact axe.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Water Aspect<br /> <br /> 3 Str<br /> 5 Dex<br /> 3 Sta<br /> <br /> 3 Percep<br /> 4 Wits<br /> <br /> 5 willpower<br /> <br /> 3 athletics<br /> 5 awareness<br /> 5 melee with grand grimcleaver specialty<br /> 5 dodge with specialty against aquatic foes<br /> <br /> Wavecleaver 12 (Damage 17/5)<br /> Evasion 6<br /> Soak 8/3 (Tidebreaker black jade breastplate)<br /> per:14 iph:26<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> Awareness Excellency<br /> Melee excellency<br /> Dodge excellency<br /> Burning Fury Wreath<br /> Flame Borne Interception<br /> Blinding Spark Distraction<br /> Crossfire Flash<br /> Elemental Sheath<br /> Dragon Graced Weapon<br /> Roaring River Slash<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ekart, the hard boiled investigator with fists of iron.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Fire Aspect<br /> <br /> 3 Str<br /> 3 Dex<br /> 3 Sta<br /> <br /> 5 Percep<br /> 3 Wits<br /> <br /> 7 willpower<br /> <br /> 3 athletics<br /> 5 awareness<br /> 5 brawl with specialty in purely unarmed<br /> <br /> <br /> Mitts 13 (Damage 10/1)<br /> Parry 5<br /> Soak 11/7 (Smokeshroud, red jade buff jacket)<br /> per:14 iph:30<br /> <br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> Awareness Excellency<br /> Brawl Excellency<br /> Pounding Surf Style<br /> Water Dragon's Coils<br /> Inescapable Whirlpool Hold<br /> Blade-Deflecting Palm<br /> Erupting Fury Barrage<br /> <br /> Cloud Piercing Focus<br /> Deep Listening Palm<br /> All Encomassing (all elements) sense<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And Taria, the sorcerer and socialite<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Earth Aspect<br /> <br /> 2 Str<br /> 3 Dex<br /> 3 Sta<br /> <br /> 3 Percep<br /> 2 Wits<br /> <br /> 5 willpower<br /> <br /> 3 awareness<br /> 5 archery with a powerbow specialty<br /> 5 dodge<br /> 5 presence<br /> <br /> Ascending Spire 14 (Damage 14/4)<br /> Evasion 5<br /> Soak 8/3 (Sandskin white jade chain shirt)<br /> per:14 iph:26<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> <br /> Archery excellency<br /> Dodge excellency<br /> Sky Calming Draw<br /> Death From Nowhere<br /> Earth's Judgement Awakened<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Then the actual fight itself!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The rain comes pouring down from a dark, late afternoon sky. The trio of dragonblooded walking along the river's shore, their rythmic footsteps punctuating the constant pattering of the raindrops on leaves and water. Something stirs in the water though. Ekart's honed senses from years of detective work tell him something is off.<br /> <br /> <br /> River Dragon rolls for stealth, stunting and, getting 1,3,8,8,8,10 for a total of 8.<br /> <br /> Zorin spends 4m into detection. Rolling 5 dice with 2 autosuccesses for only 3.<br /> <br /> Ekart spends 4m for 2 autosuccess, 1m for Cloud Piercing Focus, stunting. Rolling 11 dice with 2 autosuccesses, ignoring the weather penalties. Getting 12.<br /> <br /> Taria rolls 3 dice, getting 1 success.<br /> <br /> <br /> River<br /> Zorin 14per 22iph<br /> Ekart 14per 25iph<br /> Taria 14per 26iph<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> JOIN BATTLE!<br /> <br /> Noticing that it's been spotted the shape slips down further into the water, disappearing completely, but still very aware of its prey's location. Zorin notices Ekart snapping his fists into a ready stance and reaches for her grimcleaver.<br /> <br /> River Dragon stunts and spends a willpower, rolling 7 dice, getting a total of 5 for 8i<br /> Zorin spends 4m for 2 autosuccesses, stunting, rolling 11 dice for a total of 7 for 10i<br /> Ekart spends 4m for 2 autosuccesses, stunting, rolling 10 dice for a total of 10 for 13i<br /> Taria rolls 5 dice for 3 successes, gaining 8i<br /> <br /> <br /> River 8i<br /> Zorin 10i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 13i 14per 21iph 1a<br /> Taria 6i 14per 26iph<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ========<br /> Ekart keeps his eyes on where the dark form was in the water, shouting &quot;There! In the river!&quot;. The soggy ground and shallow water making it too difficult to approach, Ekart stays back and waits<br /> <br /> River 8i<br /> Zorin 10i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 13i 14per 21iph 1a<br /> Taria 6i 14per 26iph<br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Zorin prepares for combat, drawing her grimcleaver and swinging it low towards the river, eyes scanning for what Ekart saw.<br /> <br /> River 8i<br /> Zorin 10i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 13i 14per 21iph 1a<br /> Taria 6i 14per 26iph<br /> ---------<br /> <br /> The surface of the flowing water suddenly explodes with an enormous form, armored in thick scales that bulge out under the flex of powerful muscles. Opening its maw wide it lunges for Taria, an unexpected attack. She spends 4m to raise her evasion by 2 and ignore the environmental penalties. Rolling 10 dice and spending a willpower against 6 for a total of 11, hitting with the decisive.<br /> <br /> Rolling 8 damage dice for only a single point.<br /> <br /> River 3i<br /> Zorin 10i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 13i 14per 21iph 1a<br /> Taria 6i 14per 22iph<br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Taria attempts to disengage from the beast, spending 4m for 4 dice and ignoring penalties, and rolling 11 dice for a total of 6, the dragon trying to block her rolls 6 dice for 3 and she narrowly escapes.<br /> <br /> River 3i<br /> Zorin 10i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 13i 14per 21iph 1a<br /> Taria 6i 14per 18iph<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ========<br /> River 3i<br /> Zorin 10i 14per 23iph<br /> Ekart 13i 14per 26iph 1a<br /> Taria 6i 14per 23iph<br /> <br /> Ekart dashes forward and pulls his fist back, slamming it into the side of the dragon, spending 6m on the attack. Rolling 14 dice against parry 4 for 8. Rolling 13 damage for 4 lethal levels. Ekart enters Water aura.<br /> <br /> River 3i<br /> Zorin 10i 14per 23iph<br /> Ekart 3i 14per 20iph 2a<br /> Taria 6i 14per 23iph<br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Zorin takes up her grimcleaver and attempts a decisive attack, spending 3m to ignore 2 points of hardness with Burning Fury Wreath, and 2m on the excellency. Blade roaring with fire she rolls 12 dice for 5 and hitting! Then rolling 10 damage for 4, putting the dragon into his -1s. Zorin enters fire aura.<br /> <br /> River 3i<br /> Zorin 3i 14per 18iph 1a<br /> Ekart 3i 14per 20iph 2a<br /> Taria 6i 14per 23iph<br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Taria then launches a withering attack using 1m for excellency and 3m for Sky Calming Draw, ignoring all penalties. Rolling 15 dice with an autosuccess, and hitting with 10. Rolling 4 damage for 2<br /> <br /> River 1i<br /> Zorin 3i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 3i 14per 20iph 2a<br /> Taria 9i 14per 19iph<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> The river dragon snarls at the foes surrounding it, snapping jaws towards Ekart. Ekart will spend 4m to raise his defense to 6 with the penalties. Rolling 8 dice to attack and missing with 3.<br /> <br /> River 1i<br /> Zorin 3i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 3i 14per 20iph 2a<br /> Taria 9i 14per 19iph<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ========<br /> River 1i<br /> Zorin 3i 14per 23iph<br /> Ekart 3i 14per 25iph 2a<br /> Taria 9i 14per 24iph<br /> <br /> Taria makes another withering with the same combo, rolling 15 dice for 5 and hitting, rolling 4 damage for 5.<br /> <br /> River 1i<br /> Zorin 3i 14per 23iph<br /> Ekart 3i 14per 25iph 2a<br /> Taria 15i 14per 20iph<br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Zorin makes a withering attack, this time with a free 0m excellency. Rolling 12 dice for 7, and then 5 damage for 2<br /> <br /> River 1i<br /> Zorin 6i 14per 23iph<br /> Ekart 3i 14per 25iph 2a<br /> Taria 15i 14per 20iph<br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Ekart goes for a 2m Pounding Surf Style attack, rolling 12 dice for 7 and then three damage for 4!<br /> <br /> River 1i<br /> Zorin 6i 14per 23iph<br /> Ekart 8i 14per 23iph 2a<br /> Taria 15i 14per 20iph<br /> ---------<br /> <br /> The river dragon goes for Ekart again, spending a willpower on his attack. Ekart spends 4m in his defense to raise it to 6. Rolling 8 dice for a total of 3 the dragon misses.<br /> <br /> River 1i<br /> Zorin 6i 14per 23iph<br /> Ekart 8i 14per 23iph 2a<br /> Taria 15i 14per 20iph<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ========<br /> River 1i<br /> Zorin 6i 14per 26iph<br /> Ekart 8i 14per 28iph 2a<br /> Taria 15i 14per 25iph<br /> <br /> Taria makes a decisive attack with a 4m excellency and 3m Sky Calming. Taking one long sighted shot for the Beast's head she fires, rolling 13 dice for 7 total, hitting, and then 15 damage for 4, driving the River Dragon off.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That was better at least, everyone came out of that pretty well good except Taria has a little nick, which is definitely more than anyone would have gotten if the dragon had decided to try and wither right away that's for sure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T21:51:39-08:00","id":1348152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1348102#post1348102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran a fight using a bunch of environmental penalties and giving stunt bonuses and stuff between a river dragon and 3 Dragonblooded who had a wide range of abilities.<br /> <br /> [snip]<br /> <br /> That was better at least, everyone came out of that pretty well good except Taria has a little nick, which is definitely more than anyone would have gotten if the dragon had decided to try and wither right away that's for sure!</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! Thanks for running it - it reinforces the conclusion I've been coming to lately, that enemies should often be opening with decisives. However, I think I would have had the river dragon open with a grapple gambit. I know it's got Clamp Down, but since that requires 3 damage on the decisive to activate, I'd only count it as reliable if I had 10 or more initiative to roll. And since it's got a nice dice pool for grappling, <i>and</i> it's legendary size, and thus its control roll is unopposed unless the target has special charms, it's going to do pretty well. And it can then <i>immediately</i> do a roll for damage, either withering or decisive. I'd probably lead with a withering attack, hoping to get enough initiative in one turn to do a Death Roll next turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T22:11:02-08:00","id":1348155,"title":"","content":"That's a good point, it still wouldn't have gone off with only one success on that roll, but that was somewhat unlucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T19:48:06-08:00","id":1348599,"title":"","content":"I did another one with the characters pared down to Essence 2 and fighting against 3 boar-tusk crocodiles. I had the boar tusks spend willpower liberally and take advantage of onslaught penalties and their special abilities, and I'd say it actually went really well!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> A stiff breeze blows across the southern grasslands, sending waves through the innumerable blades of tall greenery. The three companions travel along a cleared road, unaware that stalking behind them are three of the savanna's greatest predators, and they're closing the distance.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ekart gains a sudden feeling that danger is close, activating All-Encompassing Earth Sense, feeling through the ground for concealed foes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ekart spends 3m on Earth Sense and 2m for a success. Rolling 10 dice for 7 total, successfully sensing the boar-tusks. The other two draw weapons as he cracks his knuckles. <br /> <br /> Zorin 14per 22iph<br /> Ekart 9per 25iph<br /> Taria 14per 26iph<br /> <br /> <br /> Croc1 rolls 7 dice, getting 7i<br /> Croc2 rolls 7 dice, getting 5i<br /> Croc3 rolls 7 dice, getting 5i<br /> Zorin rolls 9 dice and 4m for 2 sux, getting 11i<br /> Ekart rolls 8 dice and 4m for 2 sux, getting 7i<br /> Taria rolls 5 dice, getting 5i<br /> <br /> <br /> Croc1 7i<br /> Croc2 5i<br /> Croc3 5i<br /> Zorin 11i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 7i 9per 21iph<br /> Taria 5i 14per 26iph<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==========<br /> Zorin, unwilling to charge into the underbrush to battle enemies half blind, she will instead delay her action, preparing to clash.<br /> <br /> Croc1 7i<br /> Croc2 5i<br /> Croc3 5i<br /> Zorin 9i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 7i 9per 21iph<br /> Taria 5i 14per 26iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> One of the deadly predators charges out of the grass, loping towards Ekart and attempting to smash him to the ground. Ekart will defend by smashing that snout.<br /> <br /> <br /> Clashing Croc1 rolls 10 dice for 5, Ekart spends 6m on a full excellency, rolling 19 dice for 12. Rolling 4 damage for 3, which becomes 6 because of the clash, crashing the crocodile. Entering water aura.<br /> <br /> Croc1 -1i<br /> Croc2 5i<br /> Croc3 5i<br /> Zorin 9i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 19i 3per 21iph<br /> Taria 5i 14per 26iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Another beast, croc 2, comes bounding out from the foliage attempting the same maneuver against Ekart.<br /> <br /> Rolling 10 dice on the attack as well as spending a willpower, Ekart will defend with a 4m boost to his parry, for a total of 6 due to onslaught penalties. Croc a total of 8 and smashes Ekart to the ground.<br /> <br /> Rolling 5 damage for 2.<br /> <br /> Croc1 0i<br /> Croc2 6i<br /> Croc3 5i<br /> Zorin 9i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 17i 0per 20iph<br /> Taria 5i 14per 26iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Taria acts next, flurrying a disengage with an attack, adding 4m to excellency both. The crocs contest with 6 dice, getting 4 and 6 total. Taria rolls 9 dice for 6, and fails to get away.<br /> <br /> Next rolling the attack against croc 2, rolling 9 dice for 6 and hitting. Then rolling 4 damage for 1.<br /> <br /> Croc1 0i<br /> Croc2 5i<br /> Croc3 5i<br /> Zorin 9i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 17i 0per 20iph<br /> Taria 7i 14per 18iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Finally the last of the trio of crocs slinks out, keeping low to the ground and launching a decisive bite against Ekart, who will defend with a 6m excellency, totalling 5. The croc spends a willpower and rolls 8 dice, getting a total of 5, and hitting.<br /> <br /> Then rolling 10 damage for 4 lethal, putting him into his -1s.<br /> <br /> Croc1 0i<br /> Croc2 5i<br /> Croc3 3i<br /> Zorin 9i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 17i 0per 14iph 4L<br /> Taria 7i 14per 18iph<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ==========<br /> Croc1 0i<br /> Croc2 5i<br /> Croc3 3i<br /> Zorin 9i 14per 22iph<br /> Ekart 17i 0per 19iph 4L<br /> Taria 7i 14per 23iph<br /> <br /> Ekart will try to flurry a rise from prone with a grapple gambit. Spending a willpower and rolling 3 dice to rise from prone and stunting to roll 4 dice for a total of 3 and rising.<br /> <br /> Then using a 4m excellency, 5m Inescapable Whirlpool Hold Ekart attempts to grapple croc 1 by the tusks. Rolling 10 dice against a defense of 5 and getting 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 14 initiative to easily lock in the roll with a 9.<br /> <br /> The initiative cost is refunded by Whirlpool Hold and he now rolls to determine rounds, spending 6m on a full excellency. Rolling 14 dice against 10 and getting 11 successes with one rerolled 6, the croc gets 5, making for 6 additional rounds of control for Ekart.<br /> <br /> Ekart will then attempt a withering savage attack, spending 1m to excellency this, rolling 14 dice for 7, and then 4 damage for 3, with one rerolled 6.<br /> <br /> <br /> Croc1 -3i<br /> Croc2 5i<br /> Croc3 3i<br /> Zorin 9i 14per 22iph<br /> Ekart 21i 0per 4iph 4L<br /> Taria 7i 14per 23iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Zorin, getting fed up with these crocodiles picking on the easy prey takes her grimcleaver and makes a massive overhead chopping attack against croc 2. With a 6m excellency, rolling 18 dice against a parry of 5, making it with just 5. Then rolling up 7 damage for 5 and crashing him anyway!<br /> <br /> Croc1 -3i<br /> Croc2 0i<br /> Croc3 3i<br /> Zorin 20i 14per 16iph<br /> Ekart 21i 0per 4iph 4L<br /> Taria 7i 14per 23iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Taria attempts another escape flurry and attack, spending 6m on each. Rolling 12 dice against two pools of 6 and getting 5 against 3 and 2, escaping.<br /> <br /> Bounding back to short range Taria then unleashes a withering strike against croc3, rolling 17 dice for 6 against a parry of 5, and then rolling 4 damage for 2.<br /> <br /> Croc1 -3i<br /> Croc2 0i<br /> Croc3 1i<br /> Zorin 20i 14per 16iph<br /> Ekart 21i 0per 4iph 4L<br /> Taria 10i 14per 11iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Croc3 snuffles after Taria, but decides taking a chunk out of Ekart is a better option. Attacking with a withering bite using 8 dice against his parry of 2, rolling 4 and hitting, and then rolling 11 damage for 6, and peeling off 2 rounds of control.<br /> <br /> Croc1 -3i<br /> Croc2 0i<br /> Croc3 8i<br /> Zorin 20i 14per 16iph<br /> Ekart 15i 0per 4iph 4L<br /> Taria 10i 14per 11iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Croc2 tries to go after Zorin, who crashed him, going for a withering bite attack, snapping at her. Zorin will defend with a 1m excellency and 1m 1i Blinding Spark. Rolling 8 dice against parry 6 and missing with 2.<br /> <br /> Then rolling 8 dice against difficulty 6 for 5, and becoming blind.<br /> <br /> Croc1 -3i<br /> Croc2 0i<br /> Croc3 8i<br /> Zorin 19i 14per 13iph<br /> Ekart 15i 0per 4iph 4L<br /> Taria 10i 14per 11iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Croc1 will attempt to bite back against Ekart, trying to free itself from his grasp, biting him with a 8 dice attack. Rolling 6 against a defense of 1. Then rolling 14 damage for 6, and breaking the grapple.<br /> <br /> Croc1 3i<br /> Croc2 0i<br /> Croc3 8i<br /> Zorin 19i 14per 13iph<br /> Ekart 9i 0per 4iph 4L<br /> Taria 10i 14per 11iph<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ========<br /> Croc1 3i<br /> Croc2 0i<br /> Croc3 8i<br /> Zorin 19i 14per 18iph<br /> Ekart 9i 0per 9iph 4L<br /> Taria 10i 14per 16iph<br /> <br /> <br /> Zorin will try to decisive croc 2 with a 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite and a free 2 die excellency. Rolling 13 dice against a parry of 3 and getting it with 8. Then rolling 19 damage for 9, just shy of driving it off. <br /> <br /> Croc1 3i<br /> Croc2 0i<br /> Croc3 8i<br /> Zorin 3i 14per 15iph<br /> Ekart 9i 0per 4iph 4L<br /> Taria 10i 14per 11iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Daria decides to finish the job, firing a decisive strike at croc 2. Rolling 9 dice against a parry of 1, and getting it with 6, then 10 damage for 4, driving off croc 2 back into the brush with a shot straight to the eye.<br /> <br /> Croc1 3i<br /> Croc3 8i<br /> Zorin 3i 14per 15iph<br /> Ekart 9i 0per 9iph 4L<br /> Taria 3i 14per 11iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Next Ekart throws a few feints and then punches Croc3, spending 2m on the excellency. Rolling 14 dice against parry 5 and getting 10, and then 2 damage for one.<br /> <br /> Croc1 3i<br /> Croc3 7i<br /> Zorin 3i 14per 15iph<br /> Ekart 11i 0per 9iph 4L<br /> Taria 3i 14per 11iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Croc3 sees opportunity with Zorin and goes for a withering slam attack that's also a smash. Zorin defends with 4m excellency, 1m 1i Blinding Spark. Rolling 10 for 6 against parry of 8, missing, and then rolling 8 against difficulty 4 for only 1 and becoming blind.<br /> <br /> Croc1 3i<br /> Croc3 6i<br /> Zorin 2i 9per 15iph<br /> Ekart 11i 0per 9iph 4L<br /> Taria 3i 14per 11iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Croc 1 sees that same opportunity and goes for the same thing, Zorin defending in the same way, except with 6m excellency. This time the 10 dice against parry 8 turn up with 8 and actually hit! Rolling 6 damage for 2 and crashing Zorin!<br /> <br /> Croc1 11i<br /> Croc3 6i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 15iph<br /> Ekart 11i 0per 9iph 4L<br /> Taria 3i 14per 11iph<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ========<br /> <br /> Croc1 11i<br /> Croc3 6i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 20iph<br /> Ekart 11i 0per 14iph 4L<br /> Taria 3i 14per 16iph<br /> <br /> Ekart rolls no anima damage<br /> <br /> Ekart seizes the initiative and attacks croc1 before it can act, attempting a grapple with 4m excellency, 5m Inescapable Whirlpool Hold. Rolling 12 dice against parry 4 for 7.<br /> <br /> Rolling 11 dice for 5 and locking in the gambit at no cost.<br /> <br /> Then rolling for control rounds Ekart puts in a 5m excellency. Rolling 13 dice for 7, against 10 dice for 2, getting 5 additional rounds of control.<br /> <br /> Ekart says fuck that and throws the croc with a withering slam attack. Rolling 12 dice for only 2 to hit, and then 5 damage for only 1, but leaving the animal prone.<br /> <br /> Croc1 10i<br /> Croc3 6i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 20iph<br /> Ekart 13i 0per 0iph 4L<br /> Taria 3i 14per 16iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Croc1 now goes, on the ground, but going to attempt to rise from prone, rolling 6 dice for an amazing 8 and getting up.<br /> <br /> Croc1 10i<br /> Croc3 6i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 20iph<br /> Ekart 13i 0per 0iph 4L<br /> Taria 3i 14per 16iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Croc3 is going to go for a decisive bite against Zorin, who's prone and crashed. Zorin will defend with a 6m full excellency. Rolling 8 dice for 4 against a parry of 6 and missing with 4.<br /> <br /> Croc1 10i<br /> Croc3 4i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 14iph<br /> Ekart 13i 0per 0iph 4L<br /> Taria 3i 14per 16iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Taria is going to fire a withering few shots to harry croc 1, rolling 14 dice against parry 5 and getting it with 12, then rolling 8 damage for a great 7.<br /> <br /> Croc1 3i<br /> Croc3 4i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 14iph<br /> Ekart 13i 0per 0iph 4L<br /> Taria 11i 14per 16iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Zorin will attempt to flurry a rise from prone with an attack, rolling 8 to rise for 4 and making it.<br /> <br /> Then a withering strike on croc 3 with a 6m full excellency and a 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite. Rolling 15 dice for 4 against parry 5 and missing!<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ========<br /> <br /> Croc1 3i<br /> Croc3 4i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 19iph<br /> Ekart 13i 0per 5iph 4L<br /> Taria 11i 14per 21iph<br /> <br /> Ekart gives croc 1 another withering punch to the face with a 1m excellency, rolling 13 dice for only 3 and missing.<br /> <br /> Croc1 3i<br /> Croc3 4i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 19iph<br /> Ekart 13i 0per 4iph 4L<br /> Taria 11i 14per 21iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Taria attemps to crash croc1, rolling a 6m full excellency and 4m Death from Nowhere. Rolling 20 dice for 9 against parry 4, then 8 damage for 3 crashing Croc 1.<br /> <br /> Croc1 0i<br /> Croc3 4i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 19iph<br /> Ekart 13i 0per 4iph 4L<br /> Taria 20i 14per 11iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Croc3 is going to attempt a withering bite against Ekart, spending a willpower, snapping around as Ekart tries to block it with 4m. Rolling 8 dice against 6 for 6 and hitting. Rolling 9 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Croc1 0i<br /> Croc3 11i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 19iph<br /> Ekart 7i 0per 0iph 4L<br /> Taria 20i 14per 11iph<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Croc 1 now also rolls a bite against Ekart, and also spending a willpower. Rolling 8 dice for 3 and just hitting. Rolling 9 damage for 4.<br /> <br /> Croc1 5i<br /> Croc3 11i<br /> Zorin -1i 2per 19iph<br /> Ekart 3i 0per 0iph 4L<br /> Taria 20i 14per 11iph<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Zorin deals no anima damage<br /> <br /> Zorin is again going to use a 6m full excellency, and a 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite, slamming the axe down on croc3. Rolling 18 dice for 12, hitting by 7. Rolling 14 dice for 7 damage, pulling out of crash.<br /> <br /> Croc1 5i<br /> Croc3 4i<br /> Zorin 7i 2per 10iph<br /> Ekart 3i 0per 0iph 4L<br /> Taria 20i 14per 11iph<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> ========<br /> <br /> Croc1 5i<br /> Croc3 4i<br /> Zorin 7i 2per 15iph<br /> Ekart 3i 0per 5iph 4L<br /> Taria 20i 14per 16iph<br /> <br /> Taria is going to try a desperate finishing attack against Croc1, firing a decisive shot with a 6m full excellency. Rolling 15 dice for 5 and hitting, and then 20 damage for...10! Driving the croc off<br /> <br /> Croc1 5i<br /> Croc3 4i<br /> Zorin 7i 2per 15iph<br /> Ekart 3i 0per 5iph 4L<br /> Taria 20i 14per 10iph<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Having seen its fellows smashed into the ground, driven away and wounded the third croc will back away from the group slowly and then bound off. Clearly this prey was not so easy as it thought.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> By the end of that Ekart was wounded and totally spent, they'll definitely be a day or two recovering from this unless they have some exalted healing. They're also not so spent that they're not ready for another challenge though either. Definite success. I might have to plan a 4v4 boar tusks against my players for sometime this campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T20:27:24-08:00","id":1348605,"title":"","content":"I think animals spending willpower is in theme. Most animals only hunt once every several days and all animals value their own lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T17:56:23-08:00","id":1348762,"title":"","content":"Update, now that I realized Iron Kettle Body should reduce post soak, ie overwhelming, damage... well it went from the Resistance Supernal losing about 1 or 2 init a round to gaining 0 to 1i. I think it may actually be easier for the DBs if the resistance supernal has a bunch of mortal adds so they can build up initiative to keep him grappled constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T18:13:57-08:00","id":1348972,"title":"","content":"Here it is. I'm pretty sure I made a bunch of rule errors, and played pretty suboptimally from sheer exhaustion with the combat near the end. And suboptimally before that because there were just so many charms involved that I forgot Eyes of the Wood Dragon outright and most of the text on Iron Kettle Body (which got better the more I read it).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Join Battle<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6459\" target=\"_blank\">The Twelfth Servant of the Sunrise</a> spends 6m on the awareness excellency, he rolls 14 dice for 9 sux. He starts with 12i.<br /> <br /> Nefvarin Vita spends 5m on Precision Observation Method. She rolls 13 dice for 8 sux, she starts with 11i at short range.<br /> <br /> Bounteous Pumice spends 3m on Precision Observation Method. He rolls 9 dice for 7 sux, he starts at 10i.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja spends 5m on Precision Observation Method. He rolls 15 dice for 14 sux, and starts at 17i.<br /> <br /> Terasu Linwei spends 5m on Precision Observation Method. She rolls 15 dice for 5 sux, and starts with 8i.<br /> <br /> Yushoto Nali spends 5m on Precision Observation Method. She rolls 13 dice for 4 sux, and starts with 7i.<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja reflexively activates Fire Dragon Form for 7m.<br /> <br /> -<br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja (22/27m, 6/6wp, -0): 17i<br /> The Twelfth Servant of the Sunrise (29/35m, 6/6wp, s16, h10, -0): 12i<br /> Nefvarin Vita (30/35m, 7/7wp, -0): 11i<br /> Bounteous Pumice (30/33m, 5/5wp, -0): 10i<br /> Terasu Linwei (29/34m, 7/7wp, -0): 8i<br /> Yushoto Nali (30/35m, 6/6wp, -0) 7i<br /> <br /> <br /> Yan Tu Ja makes a decisive attack. He spends 6m on become the hammer, and 3m, 1wp on Perfect Blazing Blow. Servant spends 3m on Durability of Oak Meditation and 8m on Adamant Skin Technique. Ja rolls 17 dice, doubling 2 9s, for 11 sux. Hitting Servant with 5 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 17-2 (DoOM)-16 (AST) =-1. Ja rolls 0 dice and Servant takes zero damage. Aegis of Invincible Might activates. Ja\u2019s initiative resets to 3i and enters Fire Aura.<br /> <br /> Servant makes a withering attack against Yan Tu Ja. Servant spends 3m on Excellent Strike and 5m on the Melee Excellency, Ja spends 6m on