teous Pumice\u2019s anima flux inflicts 0 lethal damage on Servant. Pumice makes a decisive attack. Pumice spends 6m on Become the Hammer and 3m on Force of the Mountain, Servant spends 1wp to raise his Parry to 6. Pumice rolls 17 dice for 9 sux, hitting.<br /> <br /> 17i. Pumice rolls 17 dice, doubling 10s, and deals 15 lethal damage. The Twelfth Servant of the Sunrise is Dead.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thoughts:<br /> <br /> Iron Kettle Body on Supernal Resistance is a beating and a half.<br /> I'm not sure if going armorless and using Diamond Body Prana to render the wood aspect as useless as the air aspect is worth the on average worse soak, it may be.<br /> Piercing Attacks are fucking nasty against people who rely on armor for soak.<br /> Resistance Supernal Solar who is built better and has either more charms or some non-trivial adds would make a pretty good boss able to give a hearth of immaculates a run for their money.<br /> Air Dragon Style was mostly useless in this fight.<br /> Grappling can turn off Aegis, which gives the immaculates counterplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 11-16-2019, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T15:45:11-08:00","id":1349183,"title":"","content":"In the corebook, it says Dynasts consider Bears decent fights. So I'd like to see a fight between a dynast and a bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:21:47-08:00","id":1349229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349183#post1349183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the corebook, it says Dynasts consider Bears decent fights. So I'd like to see a fight between a dynast and a bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Dynast or mortal Dynast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:27:18-08:00","id":1349232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349229#post1349229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded Dynast or mortal Dynast?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> DB. The QC says Bears are a worthy challenge even for one of the Chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:35:38-08:00","id":1349259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349232#post1349232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DB. The QC says Bears are a worthy challenge even for one of the Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I did it with a wood aspect brawler and it was fairly one sided unfortunately. From a drama point of view the bear should definitely have opened with a decisive claw attack instead of a withering one, that would have at least left a bit of a wound. I didn't use anywhere close to a crazy optimized build, just to give the bear a chance.<br /> <br /> Wood Brawler<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 2 Strength<br /> 2 Dexterity<br /> 5 Stamina<br /> 3 Wits<br /> <br /> 3 Dodge (While weilding no weapons)<br /> 3 Brawl (While weilding no weapons)<br /> 3 Athletics<br /> 3 Awareness (Hunting)<br /> <br /> <br /> Join battle 7 (+2 successes)<br /> <br /> Fists 10 (+4) (Damage 9/1)<br /> Evasion 3 (+2)<br /> Soak/Hardness 10/4<br /> <br /> 5 movement<br /> Wood anima poison 2i/round, -1 penalty, 7 round duration<br /> <br /> Essence 13 per 27(31)iph<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> Awareness Excellency<br /> <br /> Brawl Excellency<br /> Pounding Surf Style<br /> Inescapable Whirlpool Hold<br /> Oakten Thew Exertion<br /> Entangling Roots Embrace<br /> <br /> Dodge excellency<br /> <br /> Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> Ox Body Technique x2<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Stalking through the woods, dismounted the brawler spots his quarry and charges fearlessly towards it, the great bear rising up on her hind legs to attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bear rolls 5 dice to join battle plus willpower for an amazing 9i<br /> Brawler spends 4m for 2 sux, and rolls 7 dice for 8i<br /> <br /> <br /> Bear 9i<br /> Brawler 8i 13per 23iph<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> =========<br /> <br /> The bear will attempt a withering claw strike against the brawler, who will defend with an 4m Impervious Skin of Stone. Rolling 12 dice for 3, hitting evasion of 3, and rolling 1 damage die for no damage, claws harmlessly sliding off the dragon's armor.<br /> <br /> Bear 9i<br /> Brawler 8i 13per 19iph<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> The dragon will strike back with a withering attack of his own, spending 4m into the excellency, and another 4 into Oaken Thew Exertion. Rolling 14 dice for 4, and then rolling 5 damage for only 1, entering Wood Aura.<br /> <br /> Bear 8i<br /> Brawler 10i 13per 11iph 1a<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =========<br /> Bear 8i<br /> Brawler 10i 13per 16iph 1a<br /> <br /> Now the dragon is going for a grapple, with a 4m excellency, 5m Entangling Roots Embrace, 5m Inexcapable Whirlpool Hold. The Bear will defend with a willpower. Rolling 10 dice for 8 and easily hitting.<br /> <br /> Rolling to lock it in with 10 dice, easily making it with 7.<br /> <br /> Now rolling for control, the DB spends 5m on Oakten Thew Exertion and spends a willpower, the bear will also spend a willpower. The Dragon getting rolling 10 and getting 6 to the bear's 9 dice for 3, three additional rounds of control.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next the Dragon will go for a withering savaging attack, spending another 5m on Oaken Thew Exertion. Rolling 10 dice for 4, and then rolling 9 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> At the end of the turn stealing 1i from Entangling Roots<br /> <br /> Bear 1i<br /> Brawler 15i 5per 0iph 3a<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> The bear attempts a withering bite attack, the wood dragon spending 4m for Invulnerable Skin of Stone. The bear rolls 8 dice against defense of 1, getting it with 3. Then rolling 2 damage for 3! Taking away 2 rounds of control.<br /> <br /> Bear 5i<br /> Brawler 12i 1per 0iph 3a<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> =========<br /> Bear 5i<br /> Brawler 12i 1per 5iph 3a<br /> <br /> The brawler will use his last round of control for a withering slam attack, rolling 10 dicce for 7 against defense 1, and then 5 damage for 4.<br /> <br /> Bear 1i<br /> Brawler 17i 1per 5iph 3a<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> The bear is now prone and will spend a turn rising, rolling 6 dice and making it with 2.<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> =========<br /> <br /> Bear 1i<br /> Brawler 17i 1per 10iph 3a<br /> <br /> The Brawler is going to go for a withering smack with his fists, spending 1m on the excellency and 4m on Oaken Thew Exertion. The bear will spend a willpower to defend. Rolling 11 dice for 4 and just barely hitting. Then rolling 4 damage for 5 and crashing the Bear.<br /> <br /> Bear -4i<br /> Brawler 28i 1per 5iph 3a<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> The bear will swipe back with a withering bite, the Dragon spending 4m for ISOS. Rolling 8 dice for zero successes and missing<br /> <br /> Bear -4i<br /> Brawler 28i 1per 1iph 3a<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> =========<br /> Bear -4i<br /> Brawler 28i 1per 6iph 3a<br /> <br /> Brawler deals 1L with his anima, and the bear must check against poison, rolling 8 dice against difficulty 7 for 4, getting 3 rounds of poison.<br /> <br /> <br /> Brawler will smack the bear with a decisive strike, spending 4m to excellency, bear will defend with a willpower. Rolling 10 dice for 6 and hitting, and then 28 dice, rerolling 6s for 12 damage, killing the bear outright.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> On the other hand that DB is SPENT at the end of the fight. With only 3 motes left.<br /> <br /> Actually, you know what, that was so easy to run, I'm going to run it again but what if the bear went for a decisive right away?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Stalking through the woods, dismounted the brawler spots his quarry and charges fearlessly towards it, the great bear rising up on her hind legs to attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bear rolls 5 dice to join battle plus willpower for an amazing 9i<br /> Brawler spends 4m for 2 sux, and rolls 7 dice for 8i<br /> <br /> <br /> Bear 9i<br /> Brawler 8i 13per 23iph<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> =========<br /> <br /> The bear is going to go for a decisive grapple attack, rolling 8 dice and a willpower. The brawler will defend with 4m to the dodge excellency. Rolling 8 dice for 8 successes, and hitting. Then rolling to lock it in, 9 initiative for 6 easily doing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then rounds of control, the DB will use 4m for 4 dice, rolling 10 against the bear's 9, getting 5 to 3.<br /> <br /> Still with this turn the bear will make a decisive bite attack, rolling 10 damage for 5 and putting the dragon into his last -1s.<br /> <br /> Bear 3i<br /> Brawler 8i 13per 19iph<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> The wood dragon is going to strike back with a withering punch, with a 4m excellency and 4m Oaken Thew Exertion. Rolling 13 dice for oinly 3, and then 4 damage for only 1.<br /> <br /> Bear 1i<br /> Brawler 10i 13per 10iph 1a<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =========<br /> Bear 1i<br /> Brawler 10i 13per 15iph 1a<br /> <br /> Hoping to put the bear into crash with the same move the brawler strikes again. This time getting 8 on 13 dice and dealing 10 damage, rolling it for 4, and then rerolling five of the 6s for an additional 1 damage, crashing the bear.<br /> <br /> Bear -4i<br /> Brawler 21i 13per 15iph 1a<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> The bear will try to bite his way back, with 8 dice and a willpower on the bite. Brawler will defend with 4m ISoS, rolling 4 successes to hit, and then 2 damage for nil.<br /> <br /> Bear -3i<br /> Brawler 21i 13per 11iph 1a<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> =========<br /> Bear -3i<br /> Brawler 21i 13per 16iph 1a<br /> <br /> The brawler is going to go for a decisive strike, with a 4m excellency, the bear will defend with a willpower. Rolling 9 dice for only 2 and missing.<br /> <br /> Bear -3i<br /> Brawler 18i 13per 10iph 1a<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Bear will attempt a withering claw strike this time, rolling 12 dice for 8, and then rolling 7 damage for 7, pulling out of crash.<br /> <br /> Bear 5i<br /> Brawler 11i 13per 10iph 1a<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> =========<br /> <br /> Bear 5i<br /> Brawler 11i 13per 15iph 1a<br /> <br /> The brawler is being more cautious this time, firing a precisve strike with his fist with only a 3m excellency behind it. Rolling 12 dice for 6 and hitting, and then 2 damage for 1<br /> <br /> Bear 4i<br /> Brawler 13i 13per 12iph 1a<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> The bear, gaining confidence will strike back with another claw, being defended with 4m ISOS. Rolling 12 dice for an unbelieveable 14, and then rolling 8 damage for 7!<br /> <br /> The bear will then activate Crushing Bear Hug, rolling the control roll with 8 bonus dice. The brawler will contest with a 5m Oaken Thews Exertion. The bear rolls 17 dice for 10 successes, and the DB rolls 9 dice for 6. The bear has 4 additional rounds of control.<br /> <br /> The bear will then make a withering bite attack, being defended by 4m ISOS. Rolling 8 dice for 1 success, and then 1 damage for 1.<br /> <br /> Bear 6i<br /> Brawler 12i 12per 0iph 2a<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> =========<br /> <br /> Bear 6i<br /> Brawler 12i 12per 0iph 2a<br /> <br /> <br /> Clawing at the bear, trying to pry it off him the brawler spends 3m to excellency, and then 5m into Oaken Thew Exertion, rolling 11 dice for 5, and then 6 damage for 2 thanks to rerolling 6s.<br /> <br /> Bear 4i<br /> Brawler 15i 4per 0iph 2a<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> The bear will then give another withering bite, defended with 4m ISOS. Rolling 8 dice for 4, and then 4 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Bear 11i<br /> Brawler 9i 0per 0iph 2a<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> =========<br /> Bear 11i<br /> Brawler 9i 0per 5iph 2a<br /> <br /> The bear will now give a decisive attack, rolling 11 damage for 7, and actually killing the dragonblood.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well the bear did actually win! So I guess sometimes it is dangerous for a DB to fight bears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T21:32:29-08:00","id":1349274,"title":"","content":"That bear got some really amazing rolls there. The early wound penalty seems to really have paid off even though it was just -1, on a starting DB that seems to have made a real difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T21:35:12-08:00","id":1349275,"title":"","content":"Yeah they really were some legendary rolls right at the end, when you're consistently getting more successes than you roll dice that can probably be chalked up to more luck than anything. I wouldn't necessarily consider a bear a good fight for a dragonblooded hunter if they were actually built like a PC. It could be a fight worth running, but he probably wouldn't be too worried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T04:56:38-08:00","id":1349543,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if the next fight I run should be Shining Topaz vs Resistance Supernal or something else.<br /> <br /> Thoughts guys? What would you lot like to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T12:32:29-08:00","id":1349649,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much for this thread!<br /> <br /> I would like to see any of the following: <br /> Ahlat vs Fakharu<br /> Ahlat vs Octavian<br /> Fakharu vs Octavian<br /> <br /> Or any of these against an E3 Solar Melee Dawn.<br /> <br /> Another one: how about Solar vs 3 Shikari, but now with Solar at Essence 5 and shamelessly combat-optimised?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:37:41-08:00","id":1349669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349649#post1349649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much for this thread!<br /> <br /> I would like to see any of the following: <br /> Ahlat vs Fakharu<br /> Ahlat vs Octavian<br /> Fakharu vs Octavian<br /> <br /> Or any of these against an E3 Solar Melee Dawn.<br /> <br /> Another one: how about Solar vs 3 Shikari, but now with Solar at Essence 5 and shamelessly combat-optimised?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ahlat vs Octavian was the fight to showcase the combat engine. Ahlat won, but Octavian was a tough customer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:57:14-08:00","id":1349677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349669#post1349669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahlat vs Octavian was the fight to showcase the combat engine. Ahlat won, but Octavian was a tough customer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I didn;t know it. However, I think that since the fight took place in 2014, we probably currently understand the system much better, o the fight may be also more instructive. But this is by no means a priority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:02:39-08:00","id":1349680,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind seeing Fakharu fight a group of low-xp Exalts. Or even Octavian, or whatever. Just anyone. Just want to see how good he is, basically, as I'm intending to use a buffed-up Fakharu as the final boss of this story arc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:06:57-08:00","id":1349683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349680#post1349680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't mind seeing Fakharu fight a group of low-xp Exalts. Or even Octavian, or whatever. Just anyone. Just want to see how good he is, basically, as I'm intending to use a buffed-up Fakharu as the final boss of this story arc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is particularly pertinent to you, how mean are you going to be when you play it? Basically are you playing to win using every tool he\u2019s got?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T15:41:36-08:00","id":1349709,"title":"","content":"I'll probably go for coolness rather than meanness.<br /> On the other hand, it'll be a buffed up Fakharu. Also, most of the PCs won't be fighting in the most efficient way, as they'll also be about the coolness, and some aren't combat characters.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't mind a lot about &quot;killing&quot; a few if it comes to it, as they can just take a permanent crippling injury and be knocked out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T18:10:54-08:00","id":1349743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349649#post1349649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one: how about Solar vs 3 Shikari, but now with Solar at Essence 5 and shamelessly combat-optimised?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is pretty easy. The DB's stats don't really matter, I just assumed pretty well max for everything, with a few relevant stats at the top. It's a Solar vs 4 DBs, a wood archer, a water brawler, a fire swordsman and an earth brawler.<br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Solar attack 14 (17 damage)<br /> Wood soak 10<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar using 15m to full excellency and Sensory Acuity Prana, Rolling 23 dice for 16, getting 19i<br /> <br /> Wood rolls in with a 4m for 2 success join battle, rolling 10 dice for a total of an impressive 14i.<br /> <br /> I'll roll the water/fire/earth DBs if it matters<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar 19i 26per 35iph 3a<br /> Wood 14i 36 motes<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar starts off the fight with 7m 1wp Heaven Sword Flash, 5m Fire and Stones Strike, 1m Divine Executioner Stance, 1wp Perfect Strike Discipline, 3m Excellent Strike, 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana and willpower. The DBs will defend with a full excellency and stunt with willpower.<br /> <br /> Rolling 23 dice against a max parry of 11 for 13, but with an added 1m Rising Sun Slash adding another 3, hitting by 5. Regaining 4 motes due to Foe-Cleaving Focus<br /> <br /> Solar 19i 9per 39iph 3a<br /> Wood 14i 36 motes<br /> <br /> Then rolling damage. Rolling 19 damage for 10, doubling for 20, all close ranged DBs are slain.<br /> <br /> Solar 6i 9per 39iph 3a<br /> Wood 14i 36 motes<br /> <br /> Solar uses his reflexive move to close into range with the wood aspect and withering with 1m 1wp 3a Peony Blossom Attack, with 1wp Perfect Strike Discipline, 5m Fire and Stones Strike, 3m Excellent Strike, and 1m Divine Executioner Stance. Wood will defend with a 6m full excellency and willpower.<br /> <br /> Rolling 24 dice against an evasion of 10 and getting 7, with a rising sun slash for 1m adding another 5 and hitting by 2. Getting 2m back from Foe-Cleaving Focus<br /> <br /> Solar 6i 0per 39iph<br /> Wood 14i 30 motes<br /> <br /> <br /> Rolling 18 damage for 9.<br /> <br /> Solar 16i 0per 39iph<br /> Wood 5i 30 motes<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar triggers 3m One Weapon Two Blows, throwing another 10m excellency, 5m Fire and Stones Strike, and 1m Divine Executioner Stance. Wood defends with 6m excellency and a willpower for 9 evasion. Rolling 24 dice for 7, rerolling 6 1s for 3, and without a Rising Sun Slash only hitting by 1. Rolling 17 damage for 8, crashing Wood<br /> <br /> Solar 30i 0per 20iph<br /> Wood -3i 24 motes<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar will now use 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn, with 1m Divine Executioner Strike, 3m Excellent Strike, 4m Fire and Stones Strike, 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana and 3m 2i Hungry Tiger Technique. Splitting his initiative 6/6/7/7/7<br /> <br /> The Wood will split her remaining essence into excellencies 6/6/4/4/4<br /> <br /> <br /> The Solar rolling 15 dice against evasion 7, hitting with 8. Rolling 12 damage for 3, doubling to 6.<br /> <br /> The Solar rolling 15 dice against evasion 6, hitting with 9. Rolling 16 damage for 4, doubling to 8.<br /> <br /> The Solar rolling 15 dice against evasion 4, rolling 5 and just hitting. Rolling 14 damage for 6, doubling to 12.<br /> <br /> The Solar rolling 15 dice against evasion 3, hitting with 9. Rolling 22 damage for 9, doubling to 18.<br /> <br /> The Solar rolling 15 dice against evasion 2, hitting with 6. Rolling 20 damage for 9, doubling to 18.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And with 62 health levels of damage to the Wood aspect I would say slain.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well that's it in a single round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T18:54:34-08:00","id":1349749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349743#post1349743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's it in a single round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again I bring up the point that every single Heaven Sword Flash fight makes the assumption that every single hearth of Dragonblooded walk around sharing a belt. Despite the fact that if Dawny Goldenpants is known to leap forward and slay everyone in sword's reach at once they'd space themselves out. It reeks of intellectual dishonesty to me, some sort of combat-example equivalent of a strawman. <br /> Can that Solar handle those foes, assuming instead that they're walking in a triangle such that each of the Dragonblooded is at Short range to the rest? I'm aware that the answer is probably &quot;Yes&quot;, but I think it'd be more intellectually honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T18:57:45-08:00","id":1349750,"title":"","content":"He\u2019s also blowing his entire supply of essence in a single combat turn as though he knew that this was a simulation, and he would cease existing the second it was over, not having to worry about the possibility of another fight two minutes down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T19:22:36-08:00","id":1349752,"title":"","content":"Eh, in my experience a circle of Dragonblooded is a fight worth blowing essence on when you are alone. The longer the fight drags on the harder it is for the Solar who while having better charms has much less collective mote. Hopefully your circle mates are on the other side of the fight or some place safe. Or a few easy fights to let you recover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T19:24:50-08:00","id":1349753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349749#post1349749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again I bring up the point that every single Heaven Sword Flash fight makes the assumption that every single hearth of Dragonblooded walk around sharing a belt. Despite the fact that if Dawny Goldenpants is known to leap forward and slay everyone in sword's reach at once they'd space themselves out. It reeks of intellectual dishonesty to me, some sort of combat-example equivalent of a strawman.<br /> Can that Solar handle those foes, assuming instead that they're walking in a triangle such that each of the Dragonblooded is at Short range to the rest? I'm aware that the answer is probably &quot;Yes&quot;, but I think it'd be more intellectually honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes but also how often do you, as PCs, ensure that you're always spaced out over three or four range bands? <i>Usually </i>you're going to be within at least one or two of eachother, and that's really all the crazy sword dervish needs. With One More Step he actually doesn't even need to be that close at the start of combat, he could even start the fight at long range and be close enough.<br /> <br /> Of course, the second half of that was pure flash. An Essence 5 Solar shamelessly optimized for combat with 50 motes left does not in any way need to blow the remaining motes and willpower into a fight against a single Essence 3 DB. That was just showing off by chaining Heaven Sword Flash into Peony Blossom Attack into One Weapon Two Blows into Peony Blossom Attack into Invincible Fury of the Dawn.<br /> <br /> In an actual game that would be probably not smart. Unless it was all a 3 die stunt leadup to an intimidation roll, daring anyone to come at you who just witnessed you slay 4 Exalted warriors before they could even place their hands on their weapons, delivered by your circlemate because you're flat out of juice to enhance that with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T19:55:58-08:00","id":1349759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349753#post1349753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yes but also how often do you, as PCs, ensure that you're always spaced out over three or four range bands? <i>Usually </i>you're going to be within at least one or two of eachother, and that's really all the crazy sword dervish needs. With One More Step he actually doesn't even need to be that close at the start of combat, he could even start the fight at long range and be close enough</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I don't understand this reply. Perhaps I miscommunicated, let me try again.<br /> My objection is that you deliberately set up the fight so that Heaven Sword Flash would apply to all foes. Despite the fact that negating Heaven Sword Flash is as trivial as not bunching together. Which seems to me to be a perfectly reasonable response to &quot;Dawny Goldpants is known to kill everyone in sword's reach of him when he hurtles into battle&quot;. I would expect any competent or intelligent foe, even mortal soldiers, to be going into that fight spread out enough that they were not all in one big Close Range pile waiting to be HSF'd into oblivion. The fact that every &quot;Dawns can solo a hearth!&quot; fight I've seen so far relies on &quot;Win initiative. Turn one, TAP into HSF will loads-o-motes, everyone dies&quot; which in turn relies on &quot;Every hearth of Dragonblooded maintain no distance between themselves&quot; strikes me as an indicator that assumptions are being made about the fight that result in an initial setup <i>heavily</i> weighted in the Solar's favor. <br /> I don't understand your reply because you're talking about multiple range bands. One is enough to prevent TAP HSF 1HK. And One Extra Step seems totally irrelevant unless we're totally missing each other's points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T20:52:25-08:00","id":1349769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349759#post1349759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, I don't understand this reply. Perhaps I miscommunicated, let me try again.<br /> My objection is that you deliberately set up the fight so that Heaven Sword Flash would apply to all foes. Despite the fact that negating Heaven Sword Flash is as trivial as not bunching together. Which seems to me to be a perfectly reasonable response to &quot;Dawny Goldpants is known to kill everyone in sword's reach of him when he hurtles into battle&quot;. I would expect any competent or intelligent foe, even mortal soldiers, to be going into that fight spread out enough that they were not all in one big Close Range pile waiting to be HSF'd into oblivion. The fact that every &quot;Dawns can solo a hearth!&quot; fight I've seen so far relies on &quot;Win initiative. Turn one, TAP into HSF will loads-o-motes, everyone dies&quot; which in turn relies on &quot;Every hearth of Dragonblooded maintain no distance between themselves&quot; strikes me as an indicator that assumptions are being made about the fight that result in an initial setup <i>heavily</i> weighted in the Solar's favor.<br /> I don't understand your reply because you're talking about multiple range bands. One is enough to prevent TAP HSF 1HK. And One Extra Step seems totally irrelevant unless we're totally missing each other's points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, what are the DBs doing that they're so far apart? If they're all in one room that's close range. If they're like <a href=\"https://www.unicorntrails.com/files/galleries/ride834_15187\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, that's close range. If they're like <a href=\"http://images5.fanpop.com/image/photos/31600000/The-Knights-of-the-Round-Table-2-arthur-and-gwen-31689592-498-283.gif\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, they're all in close range. They have to be starting the fight off both understanding that their opponent can do that, and expecting an attack, and in a place that's feasible to do so.<br /> <br /> Let me ask this though, how would you like the fight set up so that this doesn't feel intellectually dishonest?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T22:15:30-08:00","id":1349784,"title":"","content":"An ambush would work, you have 1 melee (The attacker, likely an opening grapple) and 1 archer, 1 tank, 1 throw. The Melee attempts to stealth and ambush, starting in stealth. The tank keeps attention and tries to resist being 1 shot. The archer lines up from medium range and the thrower from short. A Sidereal ally helped set this up with a bonus to stealth for everyone. This is the young dragonbloodeds only shot to stop the Solar as any hope of assistance is months away so they are taking every precaution to stop the Solar before they grow in power even more.<br /> <br /> How about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T22:15:35-08:00","id":1349785,"title":"","content":"Well, I\u2019m not the one raising the intellectual dishonesty claim, but I suspect the answer is something close to, \u201cif this Dawn Caste has done enough things to raise his Essence to 5, the largest empire in Creation should probably have gotten some intel about how he fights before bumping into him randomly, and formed up the team sent to hunt him down like a dog in such a way as to have the most advantage tactically long before coming near their target.\u201d<br /> <br /> But that wasn\u2019t the objection I raised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-20-2019, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T22:38:21-08:00","id":1349787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349784#post1349784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An ambush would work, you have 1 melee (The attacker, likely an opening grapple) and 1 archer, 1 tank, 1 throw. The Melee attempts to stealth and ambush, starting in stealth. The tank keeps attention and tries to resist being 1 shot. The archer lines up from medium range and the thrower from short. A Sidereal ally helped set this up with a bonus to stealth for everyone. This is the young dragonbloodeds only shot to stop the Solar as any hope of assistance is months away so they are taking every precaution to stop the Solar before they grow in power even more.<br /> <br /> How about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that wasn't really what was asked for. What Lanic said was an Essence 5 Dawn super combat optimized against 3 shikari. Getting ambushed with the aid of Sidereal astrology isn't really the same thing. I'm not sure the range thing is going to be that helpful though. Invincible Fury of the Dawn lets you reflexively move before each attack, ignoring disengaging even. Combined with TAP that lets you strike the archer with your first attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T00:10:54-08:00","id":1349793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349787#post1349787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that wasn't really what was asked for. What Lanic said was an Essence 5 Dawn super combat optimized against 3 shikari. Getting ambushed with the aid of Sidereal astrology isn't really the same thing. I'm not sure the range thing is going to be that helpful though. Invincible Fury of the Dawn lets you reflexively move before each attack, ignoring disengaging even. Combined with TAP that lets you strike the archer with your first attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>TheCountAlucard has it dead on. <br /> The point is, and I've gotten sick of trying to explain this, <i><b>why in the Sun's name are these example Dragonblooded always grouping up so they can be HSF'd</b></i>? Standing a dozen (or two, or three, or whatever constitutes Short at your table) paces apart when you're about to fight Goldenblade Killseverythingwithineightfeet is not an &quot;ambush&quot; and does not require &quot;Sidereal astrology&quot;, it requires feet and common sense. But apparently that requires Solar Lore or something, I guess. <br /> I'm actually so sick of this that I'm going to bow out of this conversation after this. If this post of mine resolves things, great. If not, it's not worth my time trying to make the point stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T02:22:40-08:00","id":1349818,"title":"","content":"But they weren't. It was four Deebs. Three of them were standing together, the forth was Short range behind them.<br /> <br /> You can run that exact fight again with them all at Short range, and the Solar still kills one, reflexive moves into the next one and kills them too then fights one-on-one with the last Deeb... or uses Iron Whirlwind Attack + TAP to kill the first one and drop the next two into -2s.<br /> <br /> You can run the fight with them all at Medium Range, and at Essence 5 with One More Step the Solar still kills 2/3 then 1v1s the remaining Deeb.<br /> <br /> Or at Long Range or further which is just the Solar TAP 1-hit-KOing the Deebs over three rounds.<br /> <br /> Have you, as a player, ever split the party so much that you have a combat where you all start at Long Range?<br /> <br /> I've had loads where two of us were at Close with a ranged character a rangeband behind us... and that's exactly what was run.<br /> <br /> I'll run the fight with the Deebs at Medium range if you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-20-2019, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T02:58:06-08:00","id":1349828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you, as a player, ever split the party so much that you have a combat where you all start at Long Range? </div> </div> </div> As an ST, I have. It was in my seafaring game; the PCs were each Captain of their own vessel, and they got blindsided by the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T03:53:01-08:00","id":1349833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349828#post1349828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As an ST, I have. It was in my seafaring game; the PCs were each Captain of their own vessel, and they got blindsided by the Wyld Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to put words in your mouth, but would you like me to run this as an NPC Solar ambushing three PC Deebs at long range from each other trying to force a TPK?<br /> <br /> Because that's kinda how your scenario reads to me.<br /> <br /> Your PCs weren't split up to long range as a tactic to avoid getting HSF'd. You arranged the PCs into a formation that made them easier to attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T05:05:21-08:00","id":1349841,"title":"","content":"They were the ones choosing to be on separate ships, and not crowd one another\u2019s vessels in the midst of a storm spawned by the Wyld, where a collision could prove disastrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T07:46:29-08:00","id":1349857,"title":"","content":"Ok, as promised Essence 5 Solar vs the 3 Corebook Shikari.<br /> <br /> The Immaculates close in on the Solar in a semi-circle. Fire is Medium away from Air, Air is Medium away from Earth -- all are Medium away from the Solar.<br /> <br /> Our Solar does not know Heaven Sword Flash, but is otherwise an optimized Essence 5 Solar. She wields a Diaklave and wears Artifact Light Armor. Let's say Silken Armor for argument's sake. No Evocations. No attunement bonuses. No Martial Arts. No Sorcery. No-one said &quot;Dawn Caste&quot;, so no Anima powers either. And if they've just hit Essence 5, they won't have any Essence 5 Charms yet either. No stunts. Corebook Charms only.<br /> <br /> So optimized, Essence 5 Solar with no Charms higher than Essence 4. Let's say it's a Craft Supernal Twilight who makes swords and practices with those swords three hours a day so when she meets an Immaculate, she can kill it. (But as I said, no anima powers.)<br /> <br /> As the Deebs want to flare, I've combined their motes into one big pool.<br /> <br /> Solar does not want to flare. She knows she'll probably have to, but tries to limit her exposure as much as possible.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Join Battle<br /> <br /> Solar uses Awakening Eye, rolls 22 dice for 16i (24/48m, 9w)<br /> Fires uses a full Excellency and Willpower 11i (40m, 4w)<br /> Earth follows suit 7i (42m, 6w)<br /> As does Air 10i (42, 5w)<br /> <br /> Are you sure you don't want me to call it here? Solar gets mote tapped, Deebs die. No? You sure? Ok...<br /> <br /> Round 1 - FIGHT<br /> <br /> Solar uses Thunderbolt Attack Prana (TAP), Perfect Strike Discipline (PSD) (24/48, 7w) to close with Air and launch a Decisive Attack.<br /> <br /> Air doesn't want to die so he maxes his Evasion with motes and Willpower (38m, 4w).<br /> <br /> Solar triggers Rising Sun Slash and Foe Cleaving Focus (RSS) (25/49m). 17 successes. That's a hit.<br /> <br /> 16i becomes 7 damage, becomes 14L. Air is dead.<br /> <br /> Solar Resets to 3i. Medium away from Fire and Earth.<br /> <br /> Fire and Earth enter their forms and close to Short of the Solar (Medium from each other).<br /> <br /> Solar 25/52m 7w 3i<br /> Earth 36m 6w 2a 7i<br /> Fire 33m 4w 2a 11i<br /> <br /> Round 2 - Fight Over<br /> <br /> Fire triggers Overwhelming Fire Magisty Stance (OFM) and Flash Fire Technique (23m 3a 13i) before closing to Close and Attacking with a full Excellency Grapple (Fire has the best Grapple pool of the Immaculates).<br /> <br /> Solar triggers Feverant Blow to Clash (lol), PSD, and spends the Willpower for OFM (25/51 4w).<br /> <br /> Fire rolls 10 successes on 14 dice (lol), but has one 1, which Solar using Hail Shattering Practice (HSP) on (25/50m).<br /> Solar rolls 10 successes on 21 dice, can't trigger RSS.<br /> <br /> Solar wins, 3i whiffs on Fire's Hardness. Solar resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Earth stays at Short (doesn't want to get HSFed) and triggers Earthshaker Attack (31m 5w).<br /> <br /> Solar doesn't want to fall down, so she blows 5m on the Athletics Excellency (I'm sure we could be more efficient here, I simply don't care) and she rolls 11 success (21/44m), easily not falling down.<br /> <br /> Earth then triggers the Decisive, Full Excellency, Willpower, Force of the Mountain (21m 4w).<br /> <br /> Solar's triggers Dippling Swallow Defence to remove Onslaught, and throws up a Full Excellency (16/48): Parry 12.<br /> <br /> Earth rolls (9+1) 10 successes, whiffing the Decisive (5i).<br /> <br /> Solar gets to play.<br /> <br /> Solar declares a Full Excellency and Fire and Stones Strike Withering Attack as she Flares Totemic (16/33 3a).<br /> Fire defends with a full Excellency and Willpower but Clash penalty for Parry 8 (13m 2w).<br /> <br /> Solar rolls 24 dice for 15 successes (no 9 so no RSS), hitting (4i).<br /> 24 damage - 10 soak + 5 FSS leads to 19 dice of damage = 10i<br /> <br /> Fire 3i.<br /> Solar goes to 14i.<br /> <br /> Solar triggers 1 Weapon, 2 Blows, Full Excellency, FSS to attack Fire with a second Withering attack (16/15m).<br /> Fire defends with Willpower and Flame Flicker Stance and Excellency for Parry 8 (7m 1w 2i).<br /> <br /> Solar hits with 10 successes (17i) and triggers RSS for 14 successes (18/15m),<br /> 18 dice of damage, 8i.<br /> <br /> Fire -6i<br /> Solar 27i<br /> <br /> Solar doesn't like being totemic. She uses Peony Blossom Attack to launch and Invincible Fury of the Dawn Iron Whirlwind Attack, declaring 5 attacks backed by a full FSS and TAP (32i, 16/11m 3w).<br /> <br /> Attack 1 is a Full Excellency (6/11m) vs Fire with 13i.<br /> Attacks 2-4 are 1i attacks, no Excellency vs Earth (thanks to movement from IFoTD).<br /> Attack 5 has 16i directed towards Earth with PSD (2w). Earth will defend with the usual (9m 2w).<br /> <br /> Attack 1<br /> Fire defends with Full Excellency and Willpower (1m 0w) for Parry 6.<br /> Solar hits with 6 successes on 21 dice, 13 dice of damage roll 7 successes, for 14L. Fire is dead.<br /> <br /> Attacks 2-4 are just stacking Onslaught.<br /> <br /> Attack 5<br /> Earth defences will Full Excellency + Willpower (15m 3w) for Parry 10.<br /> Solar rolls 21 dice for 9 successes. RSS (7/11m) converts that to 11. 17 dice of damage are rolled for 5 successes, 10L. Earth is on his -4.<br /> <br /> Solar resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Are you kidding me? Seriously. Are you freaking kidding me!<br /> <br /> Solar 12/11m 2w 3i<br /> Earth 20m 3w 3a 5i -4 Wound<br /> <br /> Round 3 - The round which should not be necessary<br /> <br /> Earth goes for a Full Excellency Wither (14m), 13 dice vs Parry 7, missing with only 2 successes.<br /> <br /> Solar uses Excellent Strike (ES) and a full FSS (8/7m) Wither vs a full defence and Unmoving Mountain Stance Parry 6 (5m 0w).<br /> Solar hits with 7 successes (4i). Doing 7i. CRASH.<br /> <br /> Solar 13/7m 2w 13i<br /> Earth 10m 0w -2i -4 Wound<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Solar uses ES (10/4m) vs Earth's Full Excellency Parry of 5.<br /> 8 successes hits.<br /> 13i does 6L, killing Earth.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And that's all she wrote folks. Solar wins without taking a single hit, nevermind damage. Deebs never once share a range-band, going all out on every single attack and defence and getting killed before they're tapped -- no HSF necessary. Solar walks away with a dim anima and 14 motes to spare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-20-2019, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T09:39:42-08:00","id":1349872,"title":"","content":"Yeah don\u2019t disrespect Essence 5 Solars. The QC Shikari are definitely less powerful than ones built with What Fire has Wrought, but as John says that Solar wasn\u2019t nearly as strong as you can get either. <br /> <br /> Of course with only 14 motes left she couldn\u2019t do that all AGAIN right away. Which makes me think of a good way you could run something like that in a DB game. Have the players make an entire other hearth that aren\u2019t their main characters, and have them go in first with the basic understanding that their battle is not to live, but to force the Solar to spend as much as they can. Then their actual PCs dive in immediately after and dogpile the exhausted Solar. It\u2019s a more satisfying session than either losing all your main characters, or just showing up and pushing over a drained enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T11:20:56-08:00","id":1349891,"title":"","content":"<i>THANK YOU</i>, JohnDoe244.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T13:09:54-08:00","id":1349903,"title":"","content":"First of all, thank you both for the fights. I indeed had no specific vision of the circumstances.<br /> <br /> If I might have one more suggestion, possibly time consuming, but also possibly rather fruitful: would any of you would like to run a fight where shameless melee Solar fights three to five (depending on how much is manageable), Dragon Blooded created according to What Fire Has Wrought who are fight capable at the level of player characters. For instance, they all have 11 in the relevant dicepools as player characters inevitably do, they all have Signature charms in the relevant abilities, they all have optimal weapon and armour etc. The Solar, on the other hand, is a Dawn caste, also allowed to take broad array of charms: a ton of Ox-Body Technique, some soak rising charms, Seven-Shadow Evasion, One More Step, maybe Single Point Style (which allows to apply melee charms to character's Initiative track, per developers' clarification) etc. Both side play to win: spending willpower, stunting etc. For definiteness, let's say that both sides know in advance who they're fighting, what the opponent is capable of etc.<br /> <br /> I know this sounds like an awful lot of work, but hopefully someone would be willing to do so (I am grateful in advance). Hopefully, this can be instructive to the rest of us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 11-20-2019, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T13:47:35-08:00","id":1349908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349903#post1349903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, thank you both for the fights. I indeed had no specific vision of the circumstances.<br /> <br /> If I might have one more suggestion, possibly time consuming, but also possibly rather fruitful: would any of you would like to run a fight where shameless melee Solar fights three to five (depending on how much is manageable), Dragon Blooded created according to What Fire Has Wrought who are fight capable at the level of player characters. For instance, they all have 11 in the relevant dicepools as player characters inevitably do, they all have Signature charms in the relevant abilities, they all have optimal weapon and armour etc. The Solar, on the other hand, is a Dawn caste, also allowed to take broad array of charms: a ton of Ox-Body Technique, some soak rising charms, Seven-Shadow Evasion, One More Step, maybe Single Point Style (which allows to apply melee charms to character's Initiative track, per developers' clarification) etc. Both side play to win: spending willpower, stunting etc. For definiteness, let's say that both sides know in advance who they're fighting, what the opponent is capable of etc.<br /> <br /> I know this sounds like an awful lot of work, but hopefully someone would be willing to do so (I am grateful in advance). Hopefully, this can be instructive to the rest of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the DBs also Essence 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:01:36-08:00","id":1349910,"title":"","content":"Mhm. That's a good question. I initially envisaged them as Essence 3, but already with a couple of charms under their belts. And with stats which plausibly could be taken by players.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if it turned out that this would make a difference, and a hearth of Essence 3 Dragon Blooded would perform differently when confronted with an elderish Solar than a hearth of Essence 5 Dragon Blooded, this would be something very interesting and desirable from balance perspective, so ideally it would be nice to compare both fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:15:37-08:00","id":1349914,"title":"","content":"If we\u2019re building the DBs like we\u2019re building the Solar that fight is totally unfeasible to run. The Solar would have like 32+ health levels and each DB would have about 29, for a total of 145 health levels. That\u2019s not counting the levels that you\u2019d save through things like Adamant Skin Technique and stuff. <br /> <br /> I think ultimately the Solar would win that, but you\u2019d be running the combat for days, and that\u2019s no exaggeration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:22:09-08:00","id":1349916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349872#post1349872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah don\u2019t disrespect Essence 5 Solars. The QC Shikari are definitely less powerful than ones built with What Fire has Wrought, but as John says that Solar wasn\u2019t nearly as strong as you can get either. <br /> <br /> Of course with only 14 motes left she couldn\u2019t do that all AGAIN right away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Challenge accepted.<br /> <br /> &quot;You didn't think it was going to be that easy did you?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Actually, for a second there. I kinda did.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Round 5<br /> <br /> Solar 15/4m 2w 3i<br /> <br /> Three new combatants Join Battle! Ninja smoke bombs detonate at Medium range and out jump:<br /> <br /> <br /> Fires uses a full Excellency and Willpower 10i (40m, 4w)<br /> Earth follows suit 8i (42m, 6w)<br /> As does Air 7i (42, 5w)<br /> <br /> Fire closes to Short, activates OFS and rolls to Rush - he goes all out (30m 3w 2a). Solar does not spend Essence. 5 successes to 10, Solar is Rushed.<br /> <br /> Earth enters Form and moves to Short (34m).<br /> <br /> Air stays at Medium and triggers Wrathful Winds Maneuver (36m 4i). Solar does not spend Essence: 6 successes on 11 dice. Whiff.<br /> <br /> Solar backs up -- Long to Air, Medium to Earth, Short to Fire. She uses Front-Line Warrior's Stamina (14/0m 17i).<br /> <br /> Solar 19/0m 2w 17i<br /> Fire 35m 3w 2a 10i<br /> Earth 38m 6w 1a Form 8i<br /> Air 41m 5w 1a 4i<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> Solar uses Surging Inner Fire (25/9m 2w 17i) and backs up again. Medium to Fire.<br /> <br /> Fire closes to Short and Rushes -- as before (31m 2w 2a). 5 successes to 6, the Rush fails (surprising).<br /> <br /> Earth isn't stupid and triggers full defence and moves up. Medium Range.<br /> <br /> Air enters Form (32m) and moves up. Long range.<br /> <br /> Solar 25/16m 2w 17i<br /> Fire 31m 2w 2a 10i<br /> Earth 38m 6w 1a Form 8i<br /> Air 34m 5w 2a Form 4i<br /> <br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> Fire uses Fire Flash Technique 27m.<br /> <br /> Solar closes from Short to Close with Fire. PSD FSS (25/9m 1w) Wither. Fire Full Excellency Willpower defends for Parry 10 (21m 1w 3a 10i). 12 successes, RSS 14 successes (25/5m). 8i.<br /> <br /> Solar 25i<br /> Fire 2i<br /> <br /> Earth closes to Short and and triggers Earthshaker Attack (33m 5w 2a Form 8i). Solars defends with 2m Excellency rolling 4 successes (25/3m).<br /> <br /> Earth goes all out on the Decisive (27m 4w 3a Form). Solar adds 3 Parry for 6m (22/0m). Earth rolls 9+1 successes, but is HS into a miss (21/0m). Earth down to (27m 4w 3a Form 6i).<br /> <br /> Air closes to Medium and Aims.<br /> <br /> Fire launches Fiery Blade Attack, full Excellency Decisive backed by Essence Igniting Strike (7m 0w 3a 2i). Solar defends with 8m Excellency and Dipping Swalllow (11/0m). 8 successes misses Parry 11. Solar gains a point of i (26i). For failing a Decisive, Fire Crashes himself (-5i). Solar gets Crash bonus (31i).<br /> <br /> Solar 17/0m 1w 31i<br /> Fire 12m 0w 3a -5i Close<br /> Earth 32m 4w 3a Form 6i Short<br /> Air 34m 5w 2a Form 4i Aim Medium<br /> <br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> Solar uses IFD ES FSS to make 5 Decisive attacks (6/0m 0w 36i).<br /> Attack 1, has 1i<br /> Attack 2, 1i<br /> Attack 3, 5i<br /> Attack 4, 28i<br /> Attack 5, 1i.<br /> <br /> Attack 1 vs Fire, Fire will use 6m to Defend. 7 successes vs Parry 9. Miss.<br /> Attack 2 vs Fire, Fire will not spend motes. 5 successes hits, no damage.<br /> Attack 3 vs Fire, will use 6m to defend (0m). 5 success misses Parry 7.<br /> Solar moves to Close with Earth<br /> Attack 4 vs Earth, 5m Excellency vs full defence (Parry 10, 26m 3w). 10 successes, RSS (2/0m), 13 successes. 31 dice, 17 damage, Earth is dead.<br /> Solar moves to Close with Air.<br /> Attack 5, no Essence spent, 2 successes vs Evasion 6.<br /> <br /> Solar resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Air will Withering Attack with Avenging Wind Strike (toward Fire) backed by Aim, Full Excellency, Breath Seizing Technique (BST) Willpower (29m 3w). Solar will not defend with Essence. Air rolls 21 dice +4 successes, 14 successes vs Parry 7. 6i Withered. 10i to -3i. Crash 15i.<br /> <br /> Fire will Wither, Solar will Dipping Swallow Defence (0/0m). 10 successes vs Parry 7. 0 damage for -4i.<br /> <br /> Solar 5/0m 0w -3i Breathless -1 Prone<br /> Air 34m 3w 3a 15i Medium<br /> Fire 5m 0w 3a -4i Close<br /> <br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> Anima 2L.<br /> <br /> Air moves to Short and launches a Decisive, full Excellency. Solar Dipping Swallow Defence's (3/0m). 8 successes, HS to 6 (1/0m). Miss. Air down to 12i.<br /> <br /> Solar will Flurry Rise from Prone with Wither. Rise is 7d for 3 sux, she's up. Attack is a fail.<br /> <br /> Fire will Wither -- 14 dice vs Parry 6, 4 successes fails.<br /> <br /> Air 33m 3w 3a 12i Short<br /> Solar 6/0m 0w 2L -3i Flurry Breathless<br /> Fire 6m 0w 3a -4i Close<br /> <br /> Round 10<br /> <br /> Anima 1L<br /> <br /> Air Aims.<br /> <br /> Solar Withers Fire, misses.<br /> <br /> Fire resets to Base Full Excellency Withers (0m) Solar, 7 successes, HS (5/0m). Misses.<br /> <br /> Air 33m 3w 3a 12i Short Aim<br /> Solar 10/0m 0w 3L -3i Breathless<br /> Fire 5m 0w 3a 3i Close<br /> <br /> Round 11<br /> <br /> Anima 1L<br /> <br /> Air Avenging Wind Strike (AWS), Full Excellency, Decisives Solar with WP (24m 1w 3a 12i). Solar spends 6m to boost Parry to 10 (4/0 0w 3L -3i). 20 successes hits, 8L. Solar in -1s. Air resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Fire Withers, 14d to Parry 5. Hits, 0i.<br /> <br /> Solar Resets to 3i and Withers Fire 12d vs Parry 6, 9 successes. 9i Withered. Crash.<br /> <br /> Solar 9/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds 17i<br /> Air 29m 1w 3a 3i<br /> Fire 10m 0w 3a -6i<br /> <br /> Round 12<br /> <br /> Anima whiffs.<br /> <br /> Solar will Decisive Excellent Strike 6m Excellency Fire (0/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds). Fire will full Excellency defend (4m 0w 3a -6i). 10 successes hits, 7L puts Fire on his -4. Solar resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Air full Excellency, BST, AWS (17m 0w 3a 3i), 8 successes hits Parry 6. 2i withered and knockback to Medium. 5i vs 1i.<br /> <br /> Fire pulls back to Medium and Full Defends.<br /> <br /> Solar 5/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds 1i Medium<br /> Air 17m 0w 3a 5i<br /> Fire 5m 0w 3a -4 Wounds -6i<br /> <br /> Round 13<br /> <br /> Air Aims.<br /> <br /> Solar moves to Short with Air, then takes One More Step to Close. ES Wither, Air boosts Evasion (15m 0w 3a 5i). 9 successes vs Evasion 7 (2/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds). 3i Withered 4i vs 2i.<br /> <br /> Fire closes and Withers. 5 successes vs Parry 6.<br /> <br /> Solar 7/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds 4i <br /> Air 22m 0w 3a 5i Aim<br /> Fire 10m 0w 3a -4 Wounds -6i<br /> <br /> Round 14<br /> <br /> Animas both whiff.<br /> <br /> Air full Excellency Withers (16m 0w 3a 5i), Solar will not defend with Essence. 12 successes vs Parry 6. 5i withered (16m 0w 3a 15i) -1i.<br /> <br /> Solar Excellency Withers (0/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds -1i) Air, Air full defends (14m 0w 3a 15i). 12 successes vs 7. 9i Withered (0/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds 8i) vs (14m 0w 3a 6i).<br /> <br /> Fire resets to 3i and Withers, full Excellency, hits 8 to 6. 0 damage, again (Fire 4m 0w 3a -4 Wounds 3i).<br /> <br /> Solar 5/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds 8i<br /> Air 19m 0w 3a 6i<br /> Fire 9m 0w 3a -4 Wounds 3i<br /> <br /> Round 15<br /> <br /> Anima whiffs.<br /> <br /> Solar Decisives Fire with a 2m Excellency and ES (0/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds 8i) and Fire full defends (3m 0w 3a -4 Wounds 3i) Parry 5. 5 successes, 3L. Dead. Solar resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Air full Excellency Withers (13m), 8 successes, 3i.<br /> <br /> Solar 5/0m 0w 12L -1 Wounds 0i<br /> Air 18m 0w 3a Form 9i<br /> <br /> Round 16<br /> <br /> 0 Anima damage<br /> <br /> Air Full Excellency Decisives (12m), Solar does not spend Essence. 10 successes hits, 3L. -2 wound penalty. Reset to 3i.<br /> <br /> Solar ES withers (2/0m), Air defends (10m). Misses 6 successes.<br /> <br /> Air 15m 0w 3a Form 3i<br /> Solar 7m 0w 15L -2 Wounds 0i<br /> <br /> Round 17<br /> <br /> Anima 1L<br /> <br /> Air full Excellency Withers (9m). 12 successes vs Parry 5. 8i (11i).<br /> <br /> Solar ES withers (4m). Full defence (7m). 10 successes vs Evasion 7. 4i Withered.<br /> <br /> Air 12m 0w 3a Form 7i<br /> Solar 9m 0w 16L -2 Wounds -4i<br /> <br /> Round 18<br /> <br /> Anima 2L<br /> <br /> Air full Excellency Decisives (6m), 10 successes hits, 1L. Reset to 3i<br /> <br /> Solar ES Withers (6m), Air defends (4m). Hits, 3i. CRASH. SHIFT 7 successes. 11i<br /> <br /> Solar ES 3m Excellency Decisive, Air defends (2m). Six successes vs Parry 6. 7L. Reset to 3i.<br /> <br /> Air 7m 0w 3a Form 0i 7L -2 Wounds<br /> Solar 5/0m 0w 3i 19L -2 Wounds<br /> <br /> Round 19<br /> <br /> Solar withers, Air defends (5m). 8 successes vs Evasion 5. 3i withered.<br /> <br /> Air withers (0m). 8 successes vs Parry 5. 7i withered. SHIFT. 9i.<br /> <br /> Solar 10/0m 0w -1i 19L -2 Wounds<br /> Air 5m 0w 3a Form 9i 7L -2 Wounds<br /> <br /> Round 20<br /> <br /> Anima 0 damage.<br /> <br /> Air full Decisives (0m), Solar Dipping Swallow Defence (8/0m). 8 successes vs Parry 7. HS (6/0m). Miss. 7i.<br /> <br /> Solar Withers. Miss.<br /> <br /> Solar 11/0m 0w -1i 19L -2 Wounds<br /> Air 5m 0w 3a Form 7i 7L -2 Wounds<br /> <br /> Round 21<br /> <br /> Anima 1L<br /> <br /> Air full Decisives (0m), Solar Dipping Swallow Defence (9/0m). 9 successes. HSP (6/0m). Miss 5i.<br /> <br /> Solar withers. 5 successes hits. 8i Withered. Crash. Shift. 17i.<br /> <br /> Solar Decisives ES excellency. 5 successes vs Evasion 4. 17i becomes 2L. Air is Incapacitated.<br /> <br /> -0x6 - Lethal<br /> -1x7 - Lethal<br /> -2x7 - Lethal<br /> -4x1 - Undamaged<br /> Incap - Undamaged</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Totally drained and at death's door, yet still at dim. Solar kills another 3 Shikari.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-20-2019, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:43:11-08:00","id":1349920,"title":"","content":"That's very instructive, thank you! By the way, I wouldn't expect that a fight in Exalted can take so long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349914#post1349914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we\u2019re building the DBs like we\u2019re building the Solar that fight is totally unfeasible to run. The Solar would have like 32+ health levels and each DB would have about 29, for a total of 145 health levels. That\u2019s not counting the levels that you\u2019d save through things like Adamant Skin Technique and stuff.<br /> <br /> I think ultimately the Solar would win that, but you\u2019d be running the combat for days, and that\u2019s no exaggeration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are right, so I would absolutely understand if no one is willing to run such a fight. Although, I could imagine that this scenario could happen at some table in a DB campaign. Personally, when I am a Storyteller, I usually eventually fully stat up main characters, and I expect that said Solar could be an arch-nemesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:54:56-08:00","id":1349926,"title":"","content":"Okay John, run it one more time with another three Shikari, officially challenging you to start out wounded with no motes or willpower and try to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T22:47:26-08:00","id":1349983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349920#post1349920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are right, so I would absolutely understand if no one is willing to run such a fight. Although, I could imagine that this scenario could happen at some table in a DB campaign. Personally, when I am a Storyteller, I usually eventually fully stat up main characters, and I expect that said Solar could be an arch-nemesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really know, necessarily, if that's something that should happen, even in a high essence DB game. For one thing even without managing the combat all on your own it would take hours, and hours, and slogging through everyone's massive soak and charms, and flipping through everything to see what you want to do. For another, even elder exalted often don't reach Essence 5. Mnemon is 5, Cathak Cainen is 5, Lilith is 6. They're all hundreds or even thousands of years old though, and excepting Usurpation survivors, Solars are in the 1-2 range being only a few years old.<br /> <br /> If you're running a high essence DB game, you'd have a way better time making the antagonists a circle of quick character Solars. Like the Wandering Deathknight in the corebook or Prince Resplendent in Adversaries of the Righteous. They can prove to be quite challenging without feeling almost impossible to run, and rather than having players getting frustrated flipping tables as all their attacks are being negated with Hail Shattering Practice and trying to whittle an enemy down through hundreds of motes the action will be a lot more dynamic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Something to keep in mind with all this is that any RPG system, and Exalted 3rd edition even more than most, is not a universal physics theory for the world the characters live in. It's not a system set in place where you set up all the pieces and hit the start button and everything falls into place as it should, logically as the setting presents it. The splatbook rules are designed to make player characters, who get special attention and focus in the story, not a glimpse at what those splats are <i>actually </i>like in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Some people don't like that, and to them I would say that the first thing they need to do then is start handing out only 1xp every 2-3 sessions to avoid the explosive and unrealistic growth of skill that their characters get over NPCs.<br /> <br /> Ideally the rules will help the game play out something like the stories are supposed to, while adding a fun tactical game element to it. You shouldn't be thinking &quot;What's a realistic scenario given the rules of the game, if I assume that Solar antagonists have access to all these charms and abilities.&quot; What you should be thinking is &quot;What's a fun way to portray a Solar that will not leave my players disappointed, and also not hate me and never want to play this game again.&quot;<br /> <br /> You could even make up charms that don't exist, and would be too powerful for normal Solars to have. Like a version of Circle of Bright Reaving that doesn't require you to incapacitate an enemy first, or cost initiative to use, but does cost a willpower. Normally, that wouldn't okay, but on your particular Solar who doesn't have 40 different charms to enhance that or chain into and out of it, that might be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T00:36:46-08:00","id":1349990,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't like to derail the thread, but let me just kindly disagree with you. If we plan to continue the discussion, maybe it could be placed in a separate thread?<br /> <br /> EDIT: That said, let me adress a couple of points. For disclaimer: I am not running a DB game, I am running a Solar game and idly musing about the system.<br /> <br /> I agree that fight at this scale would be difficult to run. However 90 percent of the difficulties would be already present in any other fight, since they have to do with players flipping through their charms. They either know it by heart or are already flipping (I have both species at my table). So the complexity doesn't seem really reduced. It's Essence 5 hearth versus any reliable opposition.<br /> <br /> Now, &quot;replace one archnemesis with a circle of weaker ones&quot; is not generically a good advice. This creates a completely different dynamics with completely different stories. I like archnemeses. I could imagine making a circle of enemies an archnemesis, but this would require a whole lot of story preparation. Each of them should be properly flashed out and have their own history with the players. That said, a single, nigh invincible archnemesis is a staple in the kind of stories that Exalted emulates. Moreover, I understand that in this edition Essence 5 means something different than in previous editions, but let's not exaggerate. It doesn't mean that we are not allowed to incorporate such beings in the stories we tell. I myself use some houserules that pumps things up slightly in the direction of second edition, but this scenario is reasonably canonical. Think of Mask of Winters if you like. He shouldn't be weaker than an Essence 5 Solar.<br /> <br /> So now, should the main villain be QC? <br /> <br /> I am personally not totally opposed to asymmetric game mechanics. However, I am not a great fan of QC as they are executed in Exalted. Replacing stats with dice pools doesn't really make preparations quicker (to me) and forces some arbitrary and barely consistent choices during the play. (E.g. what is exactly their armoured soak?) What is really time consuming is the choice of charms. And again, at this point I really prefer to simply pick some from the charmset, since I invest once in understanding it, than essentially make a whole new charmset each time I am coming up with the opposition.<br /> <br /> This has also a side advantage: when there are more participants to the combat, I let them be run by players whose characters are absent in the scene. Creating them by the book make them easier to run.<br /> <br /> What is more, I personally feel that whenever I prepare my NPCs like PCs I am forced to actually leave them with some weakness to exploit. For example, it turns out that they are very bad against stealth. When I'm making generic QC, I am somewhat lazy and all their capabilities end up rather generic.<br /> <br /> Now, I understand that some people like asymmetric mechanics, but I also don't like it on a personal level. It's ok in a very focused and light games, like PBTA, but in heavier more classical game, when I want to make the opposition stronger than individual players, it feels like cheating. Especially that my players also tend to ask whether some particular feat is something they can achieve and I know that at some point it would get frustrating if the answer is consistently &quot;no.&quot;<br /> <br /> As I said, I understand that the fight I asked for is a whole lot of work, but I think it's doable. My players fought with regular characters and it was longish but in a pleasant way, It felt like a multi-episode fight in shonen anime, exactly as it should. They told me, they found it very satisfying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 11-21-2019, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T01:49:05-08:00","id":1349993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349926#post1349926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay John, run it one more time with another three Shikari, officially challenging you to start out wounded with no motes or willpower and try to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Utterly spent, the Twilight with no name sheathes her diaklave. Turns away and... poof ninja smoke!<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you guys come off an assembly line or something?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Round 22<br /> <br /> Solar 0/0m 0w 3i -2 Wound Penalty 20L<br /> <br /> Three new combatants Join Battle! Ninja smoke bombs detonate at Medium range and out jump:<br /> <br /> <br /> Fires uses a full Excellency and Willpower 10i (40m, 4w)<br /> Earth follows suit 7i (42m, 6w)<br /> As does Air 8i (42, 5w)<br /> <br /> Fire closes to Short, activates OFS and rolls to Rush - he goes all out (30m 3w 2a). 8 successes to 2, Solar is Rushed.<br /> <br /> Air moves to Short and launches a Decisive, full Excellency, AWS with Willpower (33m 3w 1a). 12 successes, hits. 3L. Solar is dead.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well it was quick at least.<br /> <br /> Do note, I didn't use any &quot;prep&quot; or committed Charms. With time to buff... I think it's winnable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-21-2019, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T05:37:06-08:00","id":1350001,"title":"","content":"So clearly the winning strategy for middling Essence Dragon-Blooded knowingly facing an Essence 5 combat-optimized Solar is to unleash a dormant behemoth or two, or some other nasty thing that takes a lot of oomph to trounce, to wear him down, and then jump his ass before he can recover.<br /> <br /> I mean, that\u2019s not surprising - that\u2019s how Bane took down Batman. By turning loose pretty much the entire rogues gallery at once, and letting Bruce wear himself out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-21-2019, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T07:27:55-08:00","id":1350010,"title":"","content":"(I mean, heck, even if I was an Essence 5 Solar myself, I'd be hesitant to face down another Essence 5 combat-optimized Solar without leveraging every advantage possible before the fight began.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T09:17:43-08:00","id":1350025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350010#post1350010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I mean, heck, even if I was an Essence 5 Solar myself, I'd be hesitant to face down another Essence 5 combat-optimized Solar without leveraging every advantage possible before the fight began.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... at Essence 5 &quot;combat optimized&quot; means you summoned Lieger and a battle group of Octavians to act as your personal bodyguard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:15:33-08:00","id":1350040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349990#post1349990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is more, I personally feel that whenever I prepare my NPCs like PCs I am forced to actually leave them with some weakness to exploit. For example, it turns out that they are very bad against stealth. When I'm making generic QC, I am somewhat lazy and all their capabilities end up rather generic.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we\u2019re talking about a supremely optimized very high Essence Solar this will not really be the case. Solars, by design, have a near perfect response to anything. Stealth would be a non-issue with charms like Awakening Eye, Inner Eye Focus and Surprise Anticipation Method. Poisons and diseases are completely stopped by Immunity to Everything Technique, environmental penalties and dangers are canceled by Element Resisting Prana. <br /> <br /> What might even be worse though is that as soon as combat starts the Solar is probably just going to kill two characters before they even get to act. Tactically it\u2019s one of the best options, cutting your opposition by 40% right off the hop, but it really sucks for those players to be left out of the biggest most epic scene in the campaign and lose their characters right at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T11:43:07-08:00","id":1350072,"title":"","content":"First of all, I would once more like to thank you for the wonderful and instructive thread. I fully agree that taken your opinions on how NPCs should be statted (namely, asymmetrically), it would not make sense for you to run the proposed fight. Moreover, I think that this particular discussion is really mostly a matter of taste: I do think that there are bad design choices, but I also think that &quot;asymmetric&quot; vs &quot;symmetric&quot; approach is really not one of them. Thankfully, Exalted is compatible with both approaches, so I'm just trying to just sketch where I am coming from and why I prefer to use the symmetric one. I understand that my initial request for simulation makes little sense under your assumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350040#post1350040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we\u2019re talking about a supremely optimized very high Essence Solar this will not really be the case. Solars, by design, have a near perfect response to anything. Stealth would be a non-issue with charms like Awakening Eye, Inner Eye Focus and Surprise Anticipation Method. Poisons and diseases are completely stopped by Immunity to Everything Technique, environmental penalties and dangers are canceled by Element Resisting Prana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is technically true, but given the general reasons why I prefer to have NPCs statted just the regular way it would be strange to me not t it in the case of the hypothetical main opponent. Essence 5 Solar isn't and shouldn't be a point where regular mechanics breaks and we have to use only fiat-level solutions.<br /> <br /> Just a side note: I think that it really fits the theme of Exalted if beings within the system are organised in tiers such that beings from higher tiers completely dominate the ones from the lower. When I was asking on this very forum whether I should play third edition, I was warned that flattening the tiers was explicitly one of the goals, but reassured that between many interactions and synergies in the rules, Essence 1 and Essence 5 feel like really different tiers. I decided to play carefully houseruled 3e, to retain a bit of 2e feel and we are very satisfied with it.<br /> <br /> Now, when you are writing essentially that Exalted doesn't really work good at Essence 5 (not here, but this is the general point of the argument) precisely because it creates tiers just saddens me, so my posts may seem somewhat emotional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350040#post1350040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What might even be worse though is that as soon as combat starts the Solar is probably just going to kill two characters before they even get to act. Tactically it\u2019s one of the best options, cutting your opposition by 40% right off the hop, but it really sucks for those players to be left out of the biggest most epic scene in the campaign and lose their characters right at the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but I am not sure whether this is really relevant in the discussion. Alpha strike is also a tenable strategy when your hearth fights QC Octavian. It's a difficult problem how to handle character death in a way that makes everyone cool, but this is really mostly up to Storyteller's skills (plus some safety net: crippling injuries, the fact that rules are intentionally vague on when you die...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 11-21-2019, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T12:35:11-08:00","id":1350083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350072#post1350072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is technically true, but given the general reasons why I prefer to have NPCs statted just the regular way it would be strange to me not t it in the case of the hypothetical main opponent. Essence 5 Solar isn't and shouldn't be a point where regular mechanics breaks and we have to use only fiat-level solutions. <br /> <br /> Just a side note: I think that it really fits the theme of Exalted if beings within the system are organised in tiers such that beings from higher tiers completely dominate the ones from the lower. When I was asking on this very forum whether I should play third edition, I was warned that flattening the tiers was explicitly one of the goals, but reassured that between many interactions and synergies in the rules, Essence 1 and Essence 5 feel like really different tiers. I decided to play carefully houseruled 3e, to retain a bit of 2e feel and we are very satisfied with it.<br /> <br /> Now, when you are writing essentially that Exalted doesn't really work good at Essence 5 (not here, but this is the general point of the argument) precisely because it creates tiers just saddens me, so my posts may seem somewhat emotional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted third edition can work with Essence 5, but if you\u2019re trying to break it you absolutely can. It\u2019s the most shaky with Solars, but even Dragonblooded can to a certain extent. Actual characters tend to be much less so than theorized characters, because actual characters will take suboptimal choices, and pick up charms because they\u2019re cool even if they\u2019re not powerful, and also just not be so mono focused. You can make an Essence 5 Solar that isn\u2019t immune to every form of danger, it\u2019s just that you can also make one who is if you really try. Well, almost anyway, there is an amount of opposition where any Solar will eventually run out of essence and luck.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m really and honestly curious about your statement that it fits the exalted themes for beings of higher tier to be untouchable to those beneath them. The history of Creation is full of things rising up above their abilities to punch things above them. The Exalted overthrew the primordials, the Dragonblooded overthrew the Solars, the Lunars, Sidereals and Dragonblooded saved a plague ravaged Creation from an invasion lead by an Ishvara. <br /> <br /> I really don\u2019t mean to criticize, I just don\u2019t see the same thing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350072#post1350072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but I am not sure whether this is really relevant in the discussion. Alpha strike is also a tenable strategy when your hearth fights QC Octavian. It's a difficult problem how to handle character death in a way that makes everyone cool, but this is really mostly up to Storyteller's skills (plus some safety net: crippling injuries, the fact that rules are intentionally vague on when you die...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Octavian can alpha strike with his starting initiative in some pretty impressive ways, but it\u2019s not quite the same thing as what an E5 Solar can do. Octavian\u2019s best option to knock out a character right away is Crimson Spray Blur, which doubles the damage on his decisive attack unless the victim cancels the damage with the crippling option, otherwise he has no decisive damage adders. So you get smacked, and with his join battle take maybe 8 lethal damage on a good roll, which doubled is enough to kill you, but you have the option to instead cancel 5 levels with a crippling, and thus take only 3 damage. A Solar can activate a huge charm combo and even if they\u2019re spread out paste 2-3 enemies with more than 5 dams he to spare, which prevents accepting a crippling injury to avoid damage. <br /> <br /> The difference with the Solar is there\u2019s no counter play, no other options. You just max your defense and cross your fingers he flubs the roll, which he\u2019s unlikely to do. Which is why I think Octavian is solid encounter design but a maxed out mega Solar isn\u2019t really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:27:50-08:00","id":1350103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350083#post1350083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m really and honestly curious about your statement that it fits the exalted themes for beings of higher tier to be untouchable to those beneath them. The history of Creation is full of things rising up above their abilities to punch things above them. The Exalted overthrew the primordials, the Dragonblooded overthrew the Solars, the Lunars, Sidereals and Dragonblooded saved a plague ravaged Creation from an invasion lead by an Ishvara.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're reading too much into what I wrote. By &quot;dominating&quot; I didn't mean literally &quot;untouchable&quot;, but rather simply &quot;much, much, much&quot; more powerful. The tiers can and should overlap, you should be able to scale them in the course of the campaign.<br /> <br /> I agree that Creation is full of stories of punching above your weight class. By saying that tiers fit the themes I didn't mean anything deep, like in the sense that bearing consequences of power fits the themes. I simply meant that this is not quasi-realistic low-key setting when we are dealing with fundamentally intimate conflicts (though these can find their place). The Creation with its surroundings is a place with a number of beings of unbelievable power and for each of them, there is still something above. There are bandits and mortal sifus of martial arts, and Dragon Blooded, and Sideral ninjas, and actual dragons, and first-age behemots, and even bigger, kilometres-ranging dragons, and primordial-world-in-themselves-cosmic-horror-dragons. It's just big and populated. The ladder could stop at any of these points with no inevitable harm to the setting. Of course, this is hard to manage if you want your role-playing game to run like a well-designed board game which third-edition partially tries to achieve.<br /> <br /> I definitely don't need it myself, not all the time. I don't like DnD 5e precisely for sacrificing too much for this kind of benefit, I never viewed elders in Vampire a major problem, I loved cosmic-level ambitions of Mage, so now I consciously ignore some changes of Exalted 3e, especially concerning Essence 6+, (although I use 90-95% of it). When I want to tell intimate stories, I prefer much lighter systems which totally do not interfere with the story..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:40:38-08:00","id":1350108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349903#post1349903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, thank you both for the fights. I indeed had no specific vision of the circumstances.<br /> <br /> If I might have one more suggestion, possibly time consuming, but also possibly rather fruitful: would any of you would like to run a fight where shameless melee Solar fights three to five (depending on how much is manageable), Dragon Blooded created according to What Fire Has Wrought who are fight capable at the level of player characters. For instance, they all have 11 in the relevant dicepools as player characters inevitably do, they all have Signature charms in the relevant abilities, they all have optimal weapon and armour etc. The Solar, on the other hand, is a Dawn caste, also allowed to take broad array of charms: a ton of Ox-Body Technique, some soak rising charms, Seven-Shadow Evasion, One More Step, maybe Single Point Style (which allows to apply melee charms to character's Initiative track, per developers' clarification) etc. Both side play to win: spending willpower, stunting etc. For definiteness, let's say that both sides know in advance who they're fighting, what the opponent is capable of etc.<br /> <br /> I know this sounds like an awful lot of work, but hopefully someone would be willing to do so (I am grateful in advance). Hopefully, this can be instructive to the rest of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious Assumptions... I have yet to see a Player character start at 11 Dice (as PC's inevitably do)... Not even as a Dawn Cast do I have that.as a base, nor optimal armor, weapon, etc. Nor do I have ANY Stat at a 5...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 11-21-2019, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T14:53:28-08:00","id":1350132,"title":"","content":"In my current Lunar game, one PC out of 6 did. Their attack pools (not counting accuracy from weapons) are 11, 8, 8, 7, 6, 6 I think.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> I play a 475xp game. Despite their enormous numbers of charms (I'm talking like 50), the characters still have weaknesses. They're all decent at combat, but most are not actually good at combat for an Essence 5 character, because their specialties are in other areas (preaching, spying, etc). And even the Dawn, who is ridiculously tough (Supernal Resistance) and amazing at War (I think he has 20 War charms), doesn't have great mental defences, and he's pretty slow. And he doesn't have good ranged attacks. He's virtually unkillable, but when I fought him I just... ran away. Because he's sloooow. And another character managed to throw him off the side of a ship (even with Brawl 5, he's not amazing at grappling because he's invested in Resistance and Melee) and sail away.<br /> There's just so much to potentially get, there's always areas you're weak in. Yes, a Solar can completely dominate one Ability, but if you take 15 charms to do so, then at Essence 5 you can completely dominate... 3 abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-21-2019, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T22:53:40-08:00","id":1350191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350103#post1350103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're reading too much into what I wrote. By &quot;dominating&quot; I didn't mean literally &quot;untouchable&quot;, but rather simply &quot;much, much, much&quot; more powerful. The tiers can and should overlap, you should be able to scale them in the course of the campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I think I see what you mean now.<br /> <br /> <br /> I did one fight with a E5 max Solar against some middling Essence 3 DBs, it turned out like this.<br /> <br /> Combatants<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Air<br /> 3/5/3<br /> 3 wits<br /> <br /> Boomarang 16 (+6) (Damage 15/4)<br /> Evasion 6 (+3)<br /> Soak/Hardness 8/4<br /> 40m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Earth<br /> 5/3/5<br /> 3 wits<br /> <br /> Tetsubo 10 (+6) (Damage 19/5)<br /> Parry 5 (+3)<br /> Soak/Hardness 16/10<br /> 38m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Fire<br /> 5/5/3<br /> 4 wits<br /> <br /> Twinblades 16 (+6) (Damage 15/4)<br /> Parry 6 (+3)<br /> Soak/Hardness 11/7<br /> 39m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Water<br /> 5/3/3<br /> 3 wits<br /> <br /> Smashfists 14 (+6) (Damage 15/3)<br /> Parry 5 (+3)<br /> Soak/Hardness 11/7<br /> 39m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Wood<br /> 3/3/5<br /> 3 Wits<br /> <br /> Powerbow 14 (+6) (Damage 15/4)<br /> Evasion 5 (+3)<br /> Soak/Hardness 10/4<br /> 40m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> All of whom have most charms applicable to their abilities. They all have 3 ox-bodies except the Earth who has 5.<br /> <br /> The Solar not only has max stats but also the fast reflexes merit.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Join Battle!<br /> <br /> Solar starts with 5m 1wp Awakening Eye with 5m Sensory Acuity Prana and 4m Inner Eye Focus. Stunting for 24 dice, getting a lot of 9s and two 10s, and making for 25 successes. Then rerolling 2 failures due to the two 10s and getting another 3 successes. Then using Inner Eye Focus, rolling 5 dice for only one success, and none after that. Solar starts with 31i<br /> <br /> <br /> Each DB spends 4m for 2 autosuccesses and ends up with this:<br /> <br /> Air 6i<br /> Earth 6i<br /> Fire 10i<br /> Water 14i<br /> Wood 7i<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar 31i 61m 9wp<br /> Air 6i 36m 5wp<br /> Earth 6i 34m 5wp<br /> Fire 10i 35m 5wp<br /> Water 14i 35m 5wp<br /> Wood 7i 36m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==========<br /> <br /> The Solar is going to activate 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn, enhanced by 1m Divine Executioner Stance, 5m Fire and Stones Strike, 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana, 3m Excellent Strike, and 1m 1i Gleaming Sever. Dividing up initiative as 7/7/7/7/7.<br /> <br /> <br /> First attack the Solar will spend 2m to full excellency. Earth will use 10m 1wp Weapon Breaking Defense Technique to try to clash, spending 6m to excellency. The Solar rolls 19 dice for 11, then triggering 1m Rising Sun Slash for 17, and regaining +3 motes from 3 10s.<br /> <br /> The earth rolls 15 dice for 11, failing by 6. Solar rolls 16 damage for 7, doubling to 14.<br /> <br /> Second attack also into Earth, also spending 2m to enhance. Earth will spend 6m to raise parry to 5. Solar rolls 19 dice and gets 14. rolling 16 damage for 8, doubling to 16, Earth is slain<br /> <br /> Third attack going over to the Air aspect, who will spend 6m to raise defense, Solar will spend 2m to full excellency. Rolling 19 dice for 12, using 1m to Rising Sun Slash, and getting another 2, with no motes back. Rolling 14 damage for 7, doubling to 14 and slaying Air.<br /> <br /> Fourth attack going to Wood, who will spend 6m to defend, Solar spending 2 to full excellency. Rolling 19 dice for 16, using Rising Sun Slash to get back +5m. Rolling 16 damage for 10, doubling to 20, slaying wood.<br /> <br /> Fifth attack goes to Water, who will spend 6m to defend, Solar spending 2m to full excellency. rolling 19 dice for 16 with no rising sun slash, then 16 damage for 6, doubling to 12, putting water into -4 health levels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Solar 6i 32m 7wp<br /> Fire 10i 35m 5wp<br /> Water 14i 29m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar will spend 1m 1wp on Peony Blossom Attack and 1m Divine Executioner Stance, to strike Water, who will spend 6m to raise parry. Rolling 15 dice for 6 and hitting, then 10 damage for 2, killing Water.<br /> <br /> Solar 6i 30m 6wp<br /> Fire 10i 35m 5wp<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> Fire will attack with a witering strike, 6m to enhance, 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite. Solar will defend with 10m full excellency. Fire rolling 22 dice for 12 and hitting, but is hail shattered down to a miss<br /> <br /> Solar 6i 19m 6wp<br /> Fire 10i 26m 4wp<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ==========<br /> Solar 6i 24m 6wp<br /> Fire 10i 26m 4wp<br /> <br /> Fire will attempt another wither, exactly the same as before, spending a willpower, getting 14 and being hail shattered down to a miss.<br /> <br /> Solar 6i 10m 6wp<br /> Fire 10i 17m 2wp<br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Solar strikes with a 1m Divine Executioner Stance, 3m Excellent Strike. Fire will respond with a 4m 3i Fire Incites Water to a Riot of Clouds, 5m Crossfire Flash, 6m excellency. Solar rolls 18 dice for 8, no sun slash.<br /> <br /> DB rolls 27 dice for 18, hitting by 8. Rolling 7 damage for 4.<br /> <br /> Solar 2i 6m 6wp<br /> Fire 10i 1m 2wp<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ==========<br /> Solar 2i 11m 6wp<br /> Fire 10i 6m 2wp<br /> <br /> Fire will attempt another wither with 6m. Solar will defend with 6m Iron Kettle Body. DB rolls 22 dice for 14, hitting by 7 with two 1s. Rolling 3 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Solar 1i 5m 6wp<br /> Fire 12i 0m 2wp<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Solar strikes with 1m Divine Executioner Stance, rolling 17 dice and hitting with 6. Rolling 10 damage for 4. Solar uses 1i Essence Gathering Temper<br /> <br /> Solar 6i 12m 6wp<br /> Fire 8i 0m 2wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ==========<br /> Solar 6i 17m 6wp<br /> Fire 8i 5m 2wp<br /> <br /> Fire will attempt another wither with 5m. Solar will spend 6m to defend with Iron Kettle Body. Fire rolls 21 dice for 11, hitting by 4, rolling 2 damage for nothing.<br /> <br /> Solar 7i 11m 6wp<br /> Fire 7i 0m 2wp<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Solar will wither with 1m Divine Excecutioner Stance. Rolling 17 dice for 6, then rolling 10 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Solar 11i 10m 6wp<br /> Fire 4i 0m 2wp<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ==========<br /> Solar 11i 15m 6wp<br /> Fire 4i 5m 2wp<br /> <br /> Solar will spend 1m on DES and attack. Getting 9 successes, and rolling 14 damage for 4, crashing Fire.<br /> <br /> Solar 21i 8m 6wp<br /> Fire 0i 0m 2wp<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> Fire will try a 5m wither against the Solar, who will not defend. Rolling 21 dice for 10, and being hail shattered to a miss.<br /> <br /> Solar 21i 4m 6wp<br /> Fire 0i 0m 2wp<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ==========<br /> Solar 21i 9m 6wp<br /> Fire 0i 5m 2wp<br /> <br /> Solar will use 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn with 1m Divine Executioner Stance. Fire will defend with 4m on the first attack. Dividign damage up 5/5/5/5/6<br /> <br /> <br /> Rolling 15 dice for 7 and missing.<br /> <br /> Rolling 15 dice for 5 and hitting. Rolling 9 damage for 4<br /> <br /> Rolling 15 dice for 10 and hitting. Rolling 9 damage for 4<br /> <br /> Rolling 15 dice for 6 and hitting. Rolling 6 damage for 5<br /> <br /> Rollign 15 dice for 10 and hitting. Rolling 9 damage for 4, killing Fire.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it's definitely possible, with a really focused Solar to beat an entire hearth of 5 DBs at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T00:24:53-08:00","id":1350199,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much. It was especially instructive to see how different the dynamic of the fight became after the first round when everyone was short on motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T00:38:33-08:00","id":1350200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350199#post1350199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much. It was especially instructive to see how different the dynamic of the fight became after the first round when everyone was short on motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so you can imagine if the DBs were all built like the Solar and had 30 health levels, especially if they got unlucky and missed an attack or two. It would turn into a very conservative fight where the Solar has to creep slowly up to huge initiative while staying mote positive every turn so he can do that again. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s also very specific. This isn\u2019t a thing that Solars do, it\u2019s a thing really particular solars can do. If I tried to run that fight without Iron Whirlwind and Divine Executioner Stance it would be radically different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T10:12:18-08:00","id":1350254,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m actually not sure how you would make this fight a good campaign conclusion. It\u2019s obviously bad design to ask all the players to roll a d10 and the people with the lowest three numbers rip up their character sheets and go grab a pizza while thinking up characters for the next game. On the other hand if the Solar doesn\u2019t knock out at least a couple of Terrestrials in the first round the weight of attacks is going to be a pretty heavy drain, and between Iron Kettle Body and Hail Shattering Practice there\u2019s going to be a lot of swinging and missing, or swinging and doing nothing. Hail Shattering in particular is going to make it a really bad idea to attach many charms to a single attack, so the DBs are probably going to end up using excellencies and nothing else.<br /> <br /> On the flip side of that the Solar just can\u2019t afford to make big attacks either. Not because they\u2019d be ineffective but just because he can\u2019t afford to go all out chaining 1W1B into Peony Blossom into 1W2B and stay afloat with motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T10:33:42-08:00","id":1350257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350254#post1350254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m actually not sure how you would make this fight a good campaign conclusion. It\u2019s obviously bad design to ask all the players to roll a d10 and the people with the lowest three numbers rip up their character sheets and go grab a pizza while thinking up characters for the next game. On the other hand if the Solar doesn\u2019t knock out at least a couple of Terrestrials in the first round the weight of attacks is going to be a pretty heavy drain, and between Iron Kettle Body and Hail Shattering Practice there\u2019s going to be a lot of swinging and missing, or swinging and doing nothing. Hail Shattering in particular is going to make it a really bad idea to attach many charms to a single attack, so the DBs are probably going to end up using excellencies and nothing else.<br /> <br /> On the flip side of that the Solar just can\u2019t afford to make big attacks either. Not because they\u2019d be ineffective but just because he can\u2019t afford to go all out chaining 1W1B into Peony Blossom into 1W2B and stay afloat with motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a gimmick could help? Say 2 of the DBs lead the charge with a Warstrider each and force the Solar to spend themselves to 1-shot both Warstriders, knocking their pilots unconscious or locking them within the mech. So in that scenario there are still sacrifical goats but they don't need to die permanently.<br /> <br /> For the remaining 3v1 the ST could choose to play the Solar too aggressively for the motes they have left, making the Solar still a dangerous threat but ensuring they will run out of steam eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T12:31:32-08:00","id":1350288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1350257#post1350257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe a gimmick could help? Say 2 of the DBs lead the charge with a Warstrider each and force the Solar to spend themselves to 1-shot both Warstriders, knocking their pilots unconscious or locking them within the mech. So in that scenario there are still sacrifical goats but they don't need to die permanently.<br /> <br /> For the remaining 3v1 the ST could choose to play the Solar too aggressively for the motes they have left, making the Solar still a dangerous threat but ensuring they will run out of steam eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that might work, destroying the warstrider fits first would be a tactical mistake, but you could maybe make that more likely through some story point, or just powerful social influence. <br /> <br /> Normally with really powerful singular enemies these problems don\u2019t exist. The enemies that can boost their defense high don\u2019t also have cheap penalty negators, if they have any at all, and the ones that do are usually legendary size things that have a resting defense of no more than 5-6. So you get to use all your really cool charms without wasting them. On offence they might have some multi-target or alpha strike abilities but lack the ability to really boost them to levels that are nearly impossible to defend against, so you can protect yourself if you need to, but don\u2019t necessarily lose right away if you can\u2019t, you can adapt.<br /> <br /> With Solar antagonists, especiallynones built out of the corebook, it\u2019s pretty clear that they\u2019re made to fight monsters, not be them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T12:28:09-08:00","id":1350489,"title":"","content":"And now I want to see a fight between Shining Topaz and two DBs in warstriders.<br /> <br /> I'll probably run it myself later, but it should be interesting. I'll probably use two of the Arms striders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T15:54:47-08:00","id":1350716,"title":"","content":"I am taking ideas for how to build the Warstriders. Should I do them as Quick Characters? As fully tool'ed out DBs built from the book? I'm thinking they should be E3 and have the signature charm of their aspect for their attack ability. Which will probably be Melee, although it might be brawl, I'm undecided.<br /> <br /> Edit: Two E3 DBs, built from the book. One having all Melee Charms up to E3, with the water signature and all valid evocations from All Conquering Colossus. One having all Brawl Charms up to E3, with the wood signature and all valid evocations from Crusading Spear of the Depths.<br /> <br /> Edit2: Crusading Spear of the Depths doesn't really seem all that well suited for a brawler, but neither do any of the others except Karvara, which DBs can't use, so I guess I'll make due.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 11-27-2019, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T17:40:20-08:00","id":1355298,"title":"","content":"I wanted to see a little fight with Buck Ogres for myself so I ran one, I figured that work might as well not go to waste so I'll post it here. I was trying to see if Buck-Ogres had enough oomph to actually be a drain on motes, or if fighting them would actually give the party more with regen than they spent on attack and defense. To that end I didn't want the PCs to just blow 50 motes and 3 willpower on turn one and win, which they could have easily done, because that's an unrealistic amount of effort for combatants who are expecting maybe to fight something else later, so I used motes sparingly.<br /> <br /> I feel like I might have misplayed the ogres a bit, their ability to spend a willpower for two attacks is really good. I honestly wasn't expecting them to live past turn 3 anyway, so that's why I blew all the willpower right away.<br /> <br /> Anyway<br /> <br /> Combatants<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Darius<br /> <br /> Join Battle 10 +10<br /> Short Daiklaves 16 +10 (Damage 13/3)<br /> Parry 6<br /> Soak 14/10<br /> <br /> <br /> Excellent Strike<br /> Fire and Stones Strike<br /> One Weapon Two Blows<br /> Peony Blossom Technique<br /> Dipping Swallow Defense<br /> Rising Sun Slash<br /> Hungry Tiger Technique<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Twila<br /> <br /> Join Battle 8 +8<br /> Chakram 14 +8 (Damage 13/3)<br /> Evasion 5<br /> Soak 8/3<br /> <br /> <br /> Precision of the Striking Raptor<br /> Steel Storm Descending<br /> Flashing Draw Mastery<br /> <br /> Reed in the Wind<br /> Shadow Over Water<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Combat<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Ogre1 starts with 8i<br /> Ogre2 starts with 7i<br /> Darius spends 5m on Join Battle and starts with 13i<br /> Twila spends 5m on Jon Battle with Flashing Draw Mastery and starts with 10i<br /> <br /> <br /> Ogre1 8i<br /> Ogre2 7i<br /> Darius 13i 35m 5wp<br /> Twila 10i 35m 5wp<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> =============<br /> <br /> Darius attacks ogre 1 with a withering strike, using 3m Excellent Strike and 3m Fire and Stones Strike. Rolling 16 dice for 8 and hitting by 3, then rolling 6 damage for 4<br /> <br /> Ogre1 4i<br /> Ogre2 7i<br /> Darius 18i 29m 5wp<br /> Twila 10i 35m 5wp<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Twila attacks Ogre1 with a decisive strike, using 2m Steel Storm Descending, hitting and dealing 4 lethal<br /> <br /> Ogre1 4i 4L (-1)<br /> Ogre2 7i<br /> Darius 18i 29m 5wp<br /> Twila 3i 33m 5wp<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Ogre 2 makes a 3WP super flurry, attacking with Axe into Darius, Antlers into Twila, and spending a willpower on both.<br /> <br /> The axe blow goes wide with only 5 successes.<br /> <br /> The antlers just barely hit with 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 8 damage for 3 and crashing Twila<br /> <br /> Ogre1 4i 4L (-1) 5wp<br /> Ogre2 16i 2wp<br /> Darius 18i 29m 5wp<br /> Twila 0i 33m 5wp<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Ogre 1 pulls the same trick, but reversed, axe into Twila and antlers into Darius. This time Twila will use 2m Shadow Over Water and 4m to excellency. Darius will defend with 2m dipping swallow.<br /> <br /> The axe goes wide on Twila, and the antlers likewise on Darius, missing by 1.<br /> <br /> Ogre1 4i 4L (-1) 2wp<br /> Ogre2 16i 2wp<br /> Darius 18i 27m 5wp<br /> Twila 0i 27m 5wp<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =============<br /> <br /> Ogre1 4i 4L (-1) 2wp<br /> Ogre2 16i 2wp<br /> Darius 18i 32m 5wp<br /> Twila 0i 32m 5wp<br /> <br /> Darius is going to try and finish off Ogre1 with a 3m Fire and Stones Strike and 5m excellency, Ogre1 will defend with a willpower. Rolling 16 dice for 10 and hitting. Then rolling 21 damage for 6, putting Ogre1 into his last -2.<br /> <br /> Ogre1 4i 10L (-2) 1wp<br /> Ogre2 16i 2wp<br /> Darius 3i 32m 5wp<br /> Twila 0i 32m 5wp<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Ogre2 is going to spend a willpower to flurry, and decisive antler Twila with a willpower, and then withering axe Darius. Twila will spend 2m on Shadow Over Water and 6m on the excellency. Darius will spend 2m on Dipping Swallow.<br /> <br /> Rolling 8 dice for 2 and missing the decisive, and then rolling 7 and missing the withering as well.<br /> <br /> Ogre1 4i 10L (-2) 1wp<br /> Ogre2 13i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 30m 5wp<br /> Twila 0i 24m 5wp<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Ogre 1 will spend a willpower and flurry two attacks, a withering axe into darius and a withering axe into twila. Darius will defend with 2m Dipping Swallow and Twila with 2m Shadow over Water.<br /> <br /> Rolling 5 dice into Darius, missing.<br /> <br /> Then rolling 6 dice into Twila for 2 and missing again.<br /> <br /> Ogre1 4i 10L (-2) 0wp<br /> Ogre2 13i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 28m 5wp<br /> Twila 0i 22m 5wp<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Twila makes a withering attack against ogre1 with 1m Precision of the Striking Raptor. Rolling 14 dice for 12, and then 8 damage for only 2.<br /> <br /> Ogre1 2i 10L (-2) 0wp<br /> Ogre2 13i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 28m 5wp<br /> Twila 3i 21m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> =============<br /> <br /> Ogre1 2i 10L (-2) 0wp<br /> Ogre2 13i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 33m 5wp<br /> Twila 3i 26m 5wp<br /> <br /> Ogre 2 will try for a decisive gore against twila, who will defend with 4m excellency. Rolling 8 dice for 7 and just barely hitting. Rolling 13 damage for 10 with Gore.<br /> <br /> Ogre1 2i 10L (-2) 0wp<br /> Ogre2 3i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 33m 5wp<br /> Twila 3i 22m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Darius will make a withering attack against Ogre 1 with a 3m excellent strike and 3m Fire and Stones Strike. Rolling 16 dice for 7, dealing 2 damage and crashing ogre 1.<br /> <br /> Ogre1 0i 10L (-2) 0wp<br /> Ogre2 3i 0wp<br /> Darius 11i 27m 5wp<br /> Twila 3i 22m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Twila will wither Ogre2 with 1m Striking Raptor and 4m excellency, Rolling 16 dice for 11, and then rolling 7 damage for only 1.<br /> <br /> Ogre1 0i 10L (-2) 0wp<br /> Ogre2 2i 0wp<br /> Darius 11i 27m 5wp<br /> Twila 5i 17m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Ogre 1 will try a withering antler attack on Darius, who will defend with 2m. Rolling 5 the ogre misses.<br /> <br /> Ogre1 0i 10L (-2) 0wp<br /> Ogre2 3i 0wp<br /> Darius 11i 25m 5wp<br /> Twila 3i 17m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> =============<br /> <br /> Ogre1 0i 10L (-2) 0wp<br /> Ogre2 2i 0wp<br /> Darius 11i 30m 5wp<br /> Twila 5i 22m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> Darius will finish off Ogre1 with 3m Excellent Strike, rolling 11 dice for 6 and hitting, then 11 damage for 6 and killing Ogre1<br /> <br /> Ogre2 2i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 27m 5wp<br /> Twila 5i 22m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Twila will try the same maneuver attacking with 16 dice for 8, then 4 damage for nothing<br /> <br /> Ogre2 2i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 27m 5wp<br /> Twila 6i 17m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Ogre2 will withering axe strike Twila, who will defend with 2m Shadow Over Water and 2m excellency, the ogre just barely misses with 6.<br /> <br /> Ogre2 2i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 27m 5wp<br /> Twila 6i 13m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> =============<br /> <br /> Ogre2 2i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 32m 5wp<br /> Twila 6i 18m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> Twila will just make an unenhanced attack, rolling 12 dice and hitting with 7, then dealing 2 damage and crashing Ogre2.<br /> <br /> Ogre2 0i 0wp<br /> Darius 3i 32m 5wp<br /> Twila 14i 18m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Darius will attack with 3m excellent strike, 3m Fire and Stones. Rolling 16 dice for 5 and just hitting. Then rolling 3 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Ogre2 -3i 0wp<br /> Darius 7i 26m 5wp<br /> Twila 14i 18m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Ogre2 takes an antler swing at twila, who will defend with 2m Shadow Over Water and 2m excellency. Rolling 8 dice for 3 and missing.<br /> <br /> Ogre2 -3i 0wp<br /> Darius 7i 26m 5wp<br /> Twila 14i 14m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> =============<br /> Ogre2 -3i 0wp<br /> Darius 7i 31m 5wp<br /> Twila 14i 19m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> Twila will make a decisive attack, with 1m Striking Raptor and 4m excellency. Rolling 13 dice and hitting with 5, then rolling 14i for 6 damage.<br /> <br /> Ogre2 -3i 0wp 6L (-1)<br /> Darius 7i 31m 5wp<br /> Twila 3i 14m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Darius will decisive attack with 3m Fire and Stones and 6m full excellency. Hitting and then rolling 10 damage for 5, ending the fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Darius 7i 22m 5wp<br /> Twila 3i 14m 5wp 10L (-2)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So being down on average more than 20 motes each and a big chunk of health levels the ogres did surprisingly well. Of course they weren't facing optimized combatants, but not everyone in a group will be sporting that kind of punch anyway. If I fought 4 PCs against 4 of them, and had one of the ogres maybe as an ogre champion with a bonus 2 dice to attack and parry, that might work out.<br /> <br /> The ogres have really crappy accuracy on average, but with 13 soak and 5 parry they're actually reasonably tough. If you don't spend anything on attack you're going to be a while whittling them down. Also just the factor of luck, if they're all making 2 attacks every round some of them are going to get lucky, but you don't know which ones those are until you've already spent your motes on defense.<br /> <br /> It could just be a fluke, of course, the Ogres got pretty lucky, and the Solars were somewhat badly suited for fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T19:50:22-08:00","id":1355323,"title":"","content":"As far as my Solar vs Warstriders, The Invincible Sword Princes was winning. It was taking a long fucking time, but the -4 penalty to hit human sized things is a beating. Having to aim every other turn to offset it just gives her too much time to regen motes, and if they didn't then they had basically no chance of actually hitting her. I don't know if other signatures would have helped, but I doubt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T20:07:45-08:00","id":1355329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1355323#post1355323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as my Solar vs Warstriders, The Invincible Sword Princes was winning. It was taking a long fucking time, but the -4 penalty to hit human sized things is a beating. Having to aim every other turn to offset it just gives her too much time to regen motes, and if they didn't then they had basically no chance of actually hitting her. I don't know if other signatures would have helped, but I doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any of the signature charms really help. Solars that have really high defenses have a really easy time fighting almost anything that isn't a huge number of super high accuracy attacks. Of course that kind of character is a warrior who is legendary even among the ranks of the Dawn caste, so if they could be easily beaten without any kind of special tactics than pretty much anyone could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T09:05:10-08:00","id":1355416,"title":"","content":"1e's Creatures of the Wyld introduced the stats for claw striders, and made the claim that a pack of them could take down even a tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat I'm curious about is, about how many claw striders would be necessary to do that in 3e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T09:26:30-08:00","id":1355426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1355416#post1355416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e's Creatures of the Wyld introduced the stats for claw striders, and made the claim that a pack of them could take down even a tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat I'm curious about is, about how many claw striders would be necessary to do that in 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>With no charms I could do that tonight easy. Since it just says \u201ccould\u201d take down a T-Lizard, would you say it\u2019s fair if they attack from downwind and tall grass? If they can I bet four could do it, although they\u2019d take some losses for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T09:30:13-08:00","id":1355427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1355426#post1355426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With no charms I could do that tonight easy. Since it just says \u201ccould\u201d take down a T-Lizard, would you say it\u2019s fair if they attack from downwind and tall grass? If they can I bet four could do it, although they\u2019d take some losses for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T17:38:30-08:00","id":1355528,"title":"","content":"Well here it is, it actually went pretty well for the claw striders, but one's only alive by the grace of the dice gods, and had it died early the fight would have gone very differently and been a lot longer, if not a victory for the lizard.<br /> <br /> Combat<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Pre-battle the claw striders all roll for stealth, getting 3,4,3,3 respectively. The Tyrant lizard rolls a sight based perception check with -2 due to tall grass, getting nothing and missing the striders.<br /> <br /> <br /> All 4 claw striders will spend a willpower on join battle, and so will the Lizard, and also 2 die stunt.<br /> <br /> Claw1 10i 4wp<br /> Claw2 5i 4wp<br /> Claw3 4i 4wp<br /> Claw4 8i 4wp<br /> Lizard 8i 4wp<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ============<br /> <br /> Claw 1 will leap into Close from the brush and attack with a withering bite attack, rolling 11 dice and hitting with 4, then rolling 1 damage for nothing.<br /> <br /> Claw1 11i 4wp<br /> Claw2 5i 4wp<br /> Claw3 4i 4wp<br /> Claw4 8i 4wp<br /> Lizard 8i 4wp<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 4 will leap forward and clash with Lizard using a claw, the lizard will respond with a smashing slam. lizard rolling 12 dice to to the Claw's 15, and getting 8 to 9, just losing.<br /> <br /> The strider rolls only one damage die for nothing again, but then deal 2 damage due to clash.<br /> <br /> Claw1 11i 4wp<br /> Claw2 5i 4wp<br /> Claw3 4i 4wp<br /> Claw4 11i 4wp<br /> Lizard 4i 4wp<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Claw 2 is going to rush in and attack with a withering bite, rolling 11 dice for 11. Then rolling 6 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Claw1 11i 4wp<br /> Claw2 9i 4wp<br /> Claw3 4i 4wp<br /> Claw4 11i 4wp<br /> Lizard 1i 4wp<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 3 runs up and snaps at the lizard as well. Rolling 11 dice for 9 and then rolling 5 damage for 2<br /> <br /> Claw1 11i 4wp<br /> Claw2 9i 4wp<br /> Claw3 7i 4wp<br /> Claw4 11i 4wp<br /> Lizard 1i 4wp<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ============<br /> <br /> Claw 1 attacks with a decisive strike, spending a willpower to add 3 damage to it. Rolling 12 dice for 10 and hitting. Then rolling 14 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 9i 4wp<br /> Claw3 7i 4wp<br /> Claw4 11i 4wp<br /> Lizard 1i 4wp 6L (-1)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 4 does the exact same, digging into the Tyrant Lizard, rolling 12 dice for 7 and hitting. Then rolling 14 damage for a sad 2.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 9i 4wp<br /> Claw3 7i 4wp<br /> Claw4 3i 3wp<br /> Lizard 1i 4wp 8L (-1)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 2 hops on top and digs in with a decisive claw, spending a willpower to add damage. Hitting with 7, and then rolling 12 damage for another 2.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 3i 3wp<br /> Claw3 7i 4wp<br /> Claw4 3i 3wp<br /> Lizard 1i 4wp 10L (-1)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 3 dives in going for the throat with the same trick, 12 dice netting 10 successes, and 10 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 3i 3wp<br /> Claw3 3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 3i 3wp<br /> Lizard 1i 4wp 13L (-2)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> The lizard, having had quite enough of this, makes a withering bite against Claw 4, spending a willpower to attack and rolling 9 dice for 5, hitting by 1, and then 10 damage for 5, crashing Claw 4 and regaining a willpower.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 3i 3wp<br /> Claw3 3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 -2i 3wp<br /> Lizard 7i 4wp 13L (-2)<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ============<br /> <br /> Lizard will now make a decisive bite using Ferocious Bite on claw4, spending a willpower to hit. Claw4 will spend one to defend. Rolling 6 against 5 and hitting, and then 17 decisive damage for only 3.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 3i 3wp<br /> Claw3 3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 -2i 2wp 3L (-1)<br /> Lizard 5i 3wp 13L (-2)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Claw 1 will rip and tear, making a decisive attack and spending a willpower for +3 damage, rolling 12 dice for 9 and hitting, then 6 damage for 2.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 2wp<br /> Claw2 3i 3wp<br /> Claw3 3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 -2i 2wp 3L (-1)<br /> Lizard 5i 3wp 15L (-2)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 2 rip and tear, getting 11 and then 3 damage.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 2wp<br /> Claw2 3i 2wp<br /> Claw3 3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 -2i 2wp 3L (-1)<br /> Lizard 5i 3wp 19L (-4)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 3 rip and tear, getting 12 and then 3 damage.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 2wp<br /> Claw2 3i 2wp<br /> Claw3 3i 2wp<br /> Claw4 -2i 2wp 3L (-1)<br /> Lizard 5i 3wp 21L (-4)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 4 makes a withering bite, rolling 7 dice for 7 total, and then rolling 2 damage for 1.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 2wp<br /> Claw2 3i 2wp<br /> Claw3 3i 2wp<br /> Claw4 0i 2wp 3L (-1)<br /> Lizard 5i 3wp 21L (-4)<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ============<br /> <br /> Tyrant lizard will attempt a slam attack against Claw 3, spending a willpower on the attack, Claw3 will spend one on defense as well. Rolling 8 dice for 5, and just hitting. Rolling 7 damage for 5.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 2wp<br /> Claw2 3i 2wp<br /> Claw3 -2i 1wp<br /> Claw4 0i 2wp 3L (-1)<br /> Lizard 11i 3wp 21L (-4)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 1 getting desperate to take down the beast as its packmates are being systematically thrown to the ground it spends a willpower to rip and tear, hitting and dealing 2 damage.<br /> <br /> Claw1 3i 1wp<br /> Claw2 3i 2wp<br /> Claw3 -2i 1wp<br /> Claw4 0i 2wp 3L (-1)<br /> Lizard 11i 3wp 23L (-4)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Claw 2 will do the same, hitting and dealing another 2 damage, killing the lizard with all of their might expended.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T18:05:00-08:00","id":1355539,"title":"","content":"So what you\u2019re saying is, they could hypothetically do it, but engaging one with less-than-overwhelming numbers is not a good long-term survival strategy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T18:25:56-08:00","id":1355544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1355539#post1355539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you\u2019re saying is, they could hypothetically do it, but engaging one with less-than-overwhelming numbers is not a good long-term survival strategy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and even then it's dangerous. A pack of 4 claw striders should only ever even consider it if they're starving. If the one strider had died, the other 3 wouldn't have been able to penetrate the lizard's hardness with their pack tactics trick, and then they're really screwed because they have a seriously hard time dealing withering damage to it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As an addition, four claw striders is kind of a large hunting party if we're considering them to act like lion hunting groups, but it could be upwards of six or seven easily. If you want to play out the end scene from Jurassic Park with just two striders, you'll find a very similar thing happens mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 12-17-2019, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T02:57:20-08:00","id":1355808,"title":"","content":"I've noticed trend in this thread and 3e lore in general is that a bunch of medium threats can kill a solitary big threat pretty reliably (although at great cost)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T05:39:12-08:00","id":1355814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1355808#post1355808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed trend in this thread and 3e lore in general is that a bunch of medium threats can kill a solitary big threat pretty reliably (although at great cost)</div> </div> </div> </div>I also have two unfinished and unpublished fights, one against Fakharu and one against Octavian, and they also went the same way. Even with Fakharu starting at range and breathing poison on all three exalts facing him he still wasn\u2019t doing well by turn 5. He\u2019d wither somebody and then the simple overwhelming damage from three artifact weapons would take it all away again. <br /> <br /> They might be scary if there was only one or two people with artifact weapons and armor in the group, but otherwise not really. Thankfully there\u2019s almost no powerful enemies in Exalted that aren\u2019t also the leaders of other powerful things. Fakharu should have elemental backup, Octavian should have a host of demonic allies, ect.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Which might be a good thing. If a small group of people who aren\u2019t THAT combat focused want to fight Octavian they can, and the ST just has to bend things a bit so that they\u2019re facing him alone. If a group that has everyone with combat abilities at 5 and artifact weapons, then the ST can bring on the size 3 battlegroup of Blood apes, Octavians special Agata, and a demon-blooded akuma champion or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 12-19-2019, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T12:27:16-08:00","id":1366609,"title":"","content":"Ma-Ha-Sachi vs Five Starting Solars:<br /> <br /> Solars:<br /> <br /> Dawn: <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/6245\" target=\"_blank\">Shining Topaz</a><br /> Zenith: Karal Fire Orchid, Tomb of Dreams Stats<br /> Twilight: Iay Sela-Amu, Tomb of Dreams Stats<br /> Night: Faka Kun, Tomb of Dreams Stats<br /> Eclipse: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768056-is-appearance-kind-of-rubbish-or-am-i-missing-something/page10\">Modest Desert Mouse</a><br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Sachi: Kickstarter Lunars Stats<br /> Wolf Bodyguards: Size 2, Magnitude 10, Elite Bodyguards, Elite Drill, Might 1, Defense 8, Soak 12, Bow 14 at Short 13/1<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Combatants start at Long Range to give Ma-Ha-Sachi\u2019s archers a fighting chance.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 10ph (13/23m) and Willpower (4), for 13+1 successes 17i<br /> Karal: Spends 7ph (13/26m) and Willpower (5) for 8+1 successes 12i<br /> Iay: Spends 4ph (13/29m) and Willpower (6) for 5+1 successes 9i 4sm<br /> Faka: Spends 8ph (13/25m) and Willpower (5) for 8+1 successes 12i<br /> Mouse: Spends 8ph (13/10m) and Willpower (4) for 9+1 successes 13i<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi: 21 dice for 10ph (21/34m) plus Willpower (9) for 13i (Hybrid Body Transformation is active)<br /> Guard: 7i<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> Topaz closes to Medium<br /> Mouse closes to Medium<br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi uses uses Invincible Beast-Warrior Empowerment (21/19m, 3a, 8WP, 12i)<br /> Karal closes to Medium<br /> Faka closes to Medium<br /> Iay closes to Medium<br /> Guard Aims<br /> <br /> Round 2 \u2013 5m regen on all<br /> <br /> Topaz closes to Short and Rushes Ma-Ha-Suchi. Ma rolls 16 dice (21/17m) for 4 successes to Topaz\u2019s 10 (13/22m) 5 successes, and against the odds, Ma is Rushed.<br /> <br /> Mouse closes to Short and unleashes a Kiai! Targetting the Elder she backs her blast with Essence (13/0m) and Willpower (3) who attempts to Parry (21/7m). Mouse rolls 11+1 successes, scraping a hit, which is Soaked down to minimum damage. Mouse 15i. Ma 11i. Mouse also sings a song of woe Inspiring Ma with a Minor Intimacy of Fear and a second Intimacy of Love for Mouse: she uses a 1m Excellency for +1 die and Threefold Magnetic Ardor for +2 successes (9/0m). Ma can\u2019t very well raise up a Lunar Realm if he\u2019s dead, so applies his Defining Intimacy for +4 Resolve, taking him to 9 and giving Mouse 2 non-charm dice. Mouse rolls 11 successes Instilling both Intimacies, but Ma quashes them both with Willpower (6).<br /> <br /> Karal closes to Short.<br /> <br /> Faka closes to Short and launches a Full Excellency Withering Knife throw on the battlegroup, rolling 25 dice vs Defense 9... and missing.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi Commands his Battle Group to rain arrows on the Solars, rolling 21 dice (18/0m) and Spending Willpower (5) and using Raiton Banquet Assault to add to damage (16/0m, 4WP, 10i). He rolls 14+1 successes. Ouch.<br /> <br /> Iay Shapes Sorcery with a Full Excellency (13/25m) and gathers 9sm, plus 3sm from his nightmares. He spends 1WP and casts Death of Obsidian Butterflies, targetting the Battle Group (to avoid hitting his allies in the back) with a full Excellency (13/16m) for 9 successes vs Parry 5. 4 Magnitude damage.<br /> <br /> The Bear Guard fire arrows with Willpower (3). 11+3 dice gets 5 successes +1+3+15= 24 successes. All the Solars are hit. (10+Threshold Successes-Soak) dice +18 successes in Initiative damage. Yikes.<br /> <br /> Topaz: Dipping Swallow (13/20m), Excellency (13/10m), Hail Shattering Practice (13/9m) is hit by 11, Soaks 10 and takes 20 Initiative damage, CRASHED at -3i.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And I\u2019m going to stop there\u2026<br /> <br /> Yup. Ma-Ha-Suchi with archers is an absolute beast.<br /> <br /> Five Starting Level Solars can ABSOLUTELY beat him hands down, no doubt. But they have to be five Solars that are custom built to take him down.<br /> <br /> Five normal Solars, even accounting for a relatively powerful Dawn build are going to die.<br /> <br /> Still at the end of Round 2, Ma-Ha-Suchi has burned half his Willpower and is down from 74m to 16m... and he's Rushed. But then the Solars are Crashed and about to take Decisive Battle Group Damage.<br /> <br /> Respect your (Lunar) Elders kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-09-2020, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T16:56:39-08:00","id":1366658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1366609#post1366609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I\u2019m going to stop there\u2026<br /> <br /> Yup. Ma-Ha-Suchi with archers is an absolute beast.<br /> <br /> Five Starting Level Solars can ABSOLUTELY beat him hands down, no doubt. But they have to be five Solars that are custom built to take him down.<br /> <br /> Five normal Solars, even accounting for a relatively powerful Dawn build are going to die.<br /> <br /> Still at the end of Round 2, Ma-Ha-Suchi has burned half his Willpower and is down from 74m to 16m... and he's Rushed. But then the Solars are Crashed and about to take Decisive Battle Group Damage.<br /> <br /> Respect your (Lunar) Elders kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I've noticed in my game is that Commanding a battlegroup is particularly effective in a multiple Exalts vs. multiple Exalts fight. This is because it lets you make multiple Exalt-quality attacks using only 1 Exalt action plus 1 battlegroup action. (We made a tactical error in a recent fight where we prioritized other targets, when we should have attacked the battlegroup to break up this combo.) It's certainly thematic for a big boss, who is usually a leader type, to usually fight off the party by commanding the troops, although it does seem sad that they won't get to use their other sweet charms as much in this type of battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T01:27:04-08:00","id":1366712,"title":"","content":"Volfer vs Ragara Smash<br /> <br /> Volfer: Tomb of Dreams statline<br /> Ragara Smash: Starting level Dynast, statline below:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragara Smash<br /> Earth Aspect<br /> Righteous Warrior<br /> Heptagram<br /> <br /> Strength 5<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> Charisma 1<br /> Manipulation 5<br /> Appearance 1<br /> <br /> Perception 1<br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> Earth Aspect Abilities (and Specialities) (4 BP)<br /> <br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Craft: Weapons 1 (Javelins)<br /> Integrity 5<br /> Resistance 3<br /> War 1<br /> <br /> Favored Abilities (8 BP)<br /> <br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Brawl 1<br /> Earth Dragon Style 5 (Armed)<br /> Lore: Heptagram education 5 (The Shogunate)<br /> Occult 5<br /> Melee 3<br /> <br /> Other Abilities<br /> <br /> Linguistics 1<br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: High Realm) (6BP)<br /> <br /> Artifact 3 (Fist of Titans)<br /> Artifact 5 (Mela's Coil)<br /> Martial Artist 4<br /> Pain Tolerance 4<br /> (3 BP) Manse 3 (Stone of the Ram's Horn)<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Resources 3<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (Riverspeak)<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (Old Realm)<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> 1. Athletics: Effortlessly Rising Flame<br /> 2. Awareness: Precision Awareness Method<br /> 3. Brawl/Martial Arts: Become the Hammer<br /> 4. Integrity: Granite Curtain of Serenity<br /> 5. Resistance: Purifying Blood Ascendancy<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Melee: Elemental Sheath<br /> 2. Melee: Dragon Graced Weapon<br /> 3. Earth Dragon Style: Stone Dragon Skin<br /> 4. Earth Dragon Style: Force of the Mountain<br /> 5. Earth Dragon Style: Stillness of Stone Artemi<br /> 6. Earth Dragon Style: Unmoving Mountain Stance<br /> 7. Earth Dragon Style: Earth Dragon Form<br /> 8. Occult: Spirit Detecting Mirror<br /> 9. Occult: Spirit Grounding Shout<br /> 10. Occult: Secret Wind Revelation<br /> 11. Occult: Fivefold Resonance Stance<br /> 12. Occult: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> --. Control Spell: Invulnerable Skin of Bronze<br /> --. Shaping Ritual: Sevenfold Art Invocation<br /> 13. Resistance: Ox-body Technique<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> Free. Fist of Titans: Chambered Fist Charge<br /> 14. Fist of Titans: Mammoth Slam Quake<br /> 15. Fist of Titans: Unstoppable Hammering Blow<br /> <br /> Intimacies<br /> Defining Principle: The Dragon-Blooded are born to rule.<br /> Major Principle: The Immaculate Philosophy (Devout Belief)<br /> Major Principle: I am the mountain, strong and stable \u2013 I do not flee and I am unmoved by tears<br /> Minor Principle: Duty before pleasure<br /> Minor Principle: \u201cI like creating and repairing things.\u201d<br /> Defining Tie: House Ragara<br /> Major Tie: Anathema (Loathing)<br /> <br /> Evasion 3<br /> Parry 6 (+3, 6m)(With tetsubo or Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, else 5; +2, 4m)<br /> <br /> Soak 18 Hardness 10 (Mela's Coil + Invulnerable Skin of Bronze)<br /> (+5/0, Earth Dragon Form)<br /> (+3/+1, 5m/turn or Bonfire)<br /> <br /> Mobility Penalty -0<br /> Resist Poison: 4 dice (2m: +1 success and reroll 6s)<br /> <br /> Fist of Titans Smash Attacks (Earth Dragon Form): Accuracy 16 (14 Decisive)(+3, reroll 6s on damage, 3m), Damage 19 (+1/scene, 3m on summon; +5, 3m) (Overwhelming 5, 6 for 2m), Bashing, Smashing (-1i, no Defence penalty), Reaching, Two handed<br /> <br /> Javelin: Accuracy 9/8/7 (5 Decisive), Damage 14 (OVR 1), Lethal, Melee (Parry 5), Thrown (Medium)<br /> <br /> Join Battle 11 (+3 to result)(+3 successes, 6m)<br /> Rush 11 (+3 successes, 10s explode, 6m)<br /> Disengage 5<br /> <br /> Resolve 4 (+2, ignore -1 from wounds, deprivation or poison, 4m)<br /> Guile 3<br /> <br /> Willpower 5<br /> Essence 2<br /> <br /> Personal motes 13<br /> Peripheral motes 31 (20, 11 committed)<br /> <br /> Health Track (3m/tick, ignore one point of penalties)<br /> -0 x1<br /> -1 x2<br /> -1 x4<br /> -3 x1<br /> Incap</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Fight<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Join Battle</b>:<br /> <br /> Medium Range<br /> <br /> Volfer Join Battle: 12 dice for 6m +1 Willpower. Result of 10i. (7m Personal/33m Peripheral, 5WP)<br /> Smash Join Battle: 17 dice for 6m +1 Willpower. Result 17i. (13/14m, 1a, 4WP)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b>:<br /> <br /> Smash enters Eath Dragon Form and draws her tetsubo from a nearby rock with Dragon Graced Weapon (13/2m, 3a). Her anima flares totemic.<br /> <br /> Volfer moves to Short and kicks of Thunderclap Rush (3/33m). Volfer closes to Close and attacks with an Unclashable attack: 16 dice, 2 automatic successes, rerolling 1s and with 5 post-soak extra damage (0/22m, 4WP). Smasher boosts her Parry to 9 (9/0m), and with 7 successes Volfer misses.<br /> <br /> Smash (13/1m, 3a, Earth Aura, 4WP) 17i<br /> Volfer (0/27m, 2a, 4WP) 10i<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b>:<br /> <br /> Essence backed anima flux (12/0m) withers 1i from Volfer and knocks him Prone.<br /> <br /> Smash launches a Withering Smash, backed by Willpower, Become the Hammer and Force of the Mountain (6/0m, 3WP, 16i). Volfer defends with a Full Excellency and Durability of Oak Meditation with Willpower (0/16m, 3a, 3WP, Parry 9). Smash rolls 8+1 successes and Smashes Volfer out to Short range. Volfer uses Spirit Strengthens the Skin (0/12m) and Soaks 13, leaving 12 dice of rolled damage (rerolling 6s), 6i. Volfer 3i. Smash 23i. Smash Reflexively moves to Close.<br /> <br /> Volfer Flurries Rise from Prone (2WP) with an Attack. He handily rolls the 1 success he needs to stand up, then rolls an Excellent Strike (0/9m) with Excellency (0/3m) and Fire and Stones Strike (0/0m) and Willpower (1WP). Smash uses a 4m Excellency Willpower Parry (2/0m 2WP, Parry 9). Volfer rolls 7+2 successes, hitting. He's Soaked down to Minimum+Fire and Stones Strike Damage (4 dice), and rolls 3i. Volfer 7i. Smash 20i.<br /> <br /> Smash: (2/5m, 2WP, 3a, Earth Aura) 20i<br /> Volfer: (0/5m, 1WP, 3a) 7i<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b>:<br /> <br /> Anima flux withers Volfer again to 6i.<br /> <br /> Smash delays to Clash (18i).<br /> <br /> Volfer attacks -- CLASH.<br /> <br /> Smash uses Become the Hammer and Force of the Mountain and Willpower on a Smash attack (1/0m 1WP 17i). 18 dice + 1 success. 12 successes.<br /> Volfer uses Excellent Melee and a 2m Excellency with Willpower (0/0m 0WP). 10 dice, rerolling 1s + 2 successes. 10 successes.<br /> <br /> Volfer is Smashed Prone and takes 20 dice of Withering damage, re-rolling 6s. 7i+3i, Crashes Volfer.<br /> <br /> Smash: (1/5m, 1WP, 3a, Earth Aura) 33i<br /> Volfer: (0/5m, 0WP, 3a, CRASHED, Prone) -3i<br /> <br /> <b>Round 4</b>:<br /> <br /> Anima flux does nothing.<br /> <br /> Smash uses Become the Hammer on a Decisive attack with Willpower (5 Dex+5 MA+1 Speciality+3 Earth Dragon Form+3 Become the hammer=17 dice to hit +1 success, 0/3m). Volfer (Parry 5-2-1=2) uses a 4m Excellency to reach Parry 4. Smash rolls 4+1 successes (YIKES) and hits the Prone Volfer and rolls 33i of damage for 14B, which takes Volfer out of the fight.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wow... I cannot believe that it took four rounds for a starting Deeb to beat Volfer. That's basically twice as long as it takes an Essence 3 Deeb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-12-2020, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T11:37:37-08:00","id":1367046,"title":"","content":"So, Gotta Ask... In the Ma Ha Suchi Fight, it looks like the Bear Guard are firing off an Arrow Attack but where are they getting an automatic 15 successes from? Is not the 15 Successes that Ma Ha Suchi gave them a DICE bonus to their Attack, NOT an Automatic 15 Successes? THAT changes the entire battle completely.<br /> <br /> Maybe I am just misreading something... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T11:54:18-08:00","id":1367051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367046#post1367046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Gotta Ask... In the Ma Ha Suchi Fight, it looks like the Bear Guard are firing off an Arrow Attack but where are they getting an automatic 15 successes from? Is not the 15 Successes that Ma Ha Suchi gave them a DICE bonus to their Attack, NOT an Automatic 15 Successes? THAT changes the entire battle completely.<br /> <br /> Maybe I am just misreading something... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Invincible Beast-Warrior Empowerment is absolutely insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T12:02:02-08:00","id":1367053,"title":"","content":"But are the troops not gaining the 15 Dice to aid the attack, rather than straight successes? Does <i><b>Invincible Beat-Warrior Empowerment</b></i> actually transform those command dice to successes? Sorry, I do not have access to the Lunar Book as of yet (missed the Kickstarter, sadly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T12:15:48-08:00","id":1367057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367053#post1367053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are the troops not gaining the 15 Dice to aid the attack, rather than straight successes? Does <i><b>Invincible Beat-Warrior Empowerment</b></i> actually transform those command dice to successes? Sorry, I do not have access to the Lunar Book as of yet (missed the Kickstarter, sadly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it does more than that, it converts dice added by Might, Size, command rolls, and Drill to automatic successes, and also gives Essence dice to route checks. If they have perfect morale it adds +1 might instead of the rout bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T12:17:37-08:00","id":1367058,"title":"","content":"WOW... that is pretty amazing indeed... cannot wait for Fangs to hit publication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T13:02:01-08:00","id":1367072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367058#post1367058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WOW... that is pretty amazing indeed... cannot wait for Fangs to hit publication.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also beastmen are might 1 by default, so that\u2019s even more helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T13:13:01-08:00","id":1367075,"title":"","content":"Indeed... Thanks for the information <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T17:23:16-08:00","id":1367127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1366712#post1366712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Volfer vs Ragara Smash<br /> <br /> Volfer: Tomb of Dreams statline<br /> Ragara Smash: Starting level Dynast, statline below:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragara Smash<br /> Earth Aspect<br /> Righteous Warrior<br /> Heptagram<br /> <br /> Strength 5<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> Charisma 1<br /> Manipulation 5<br /> Appearance 1<br /> <br /> Perception 1<br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> Earth Aspect Abilities (and Specialities) (4 BP)<br /> <br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Craft: Weapons 1 (Javelins)<br /> Integrity 5<br /> Resistance 3<br /> War 1<br /> <br /> Favored Abilities (8 BP)<br /> <br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Brawl 1<br /> Earth Dragon Style 5 (Armed)<br /> Lore: Heptagram education 5 (The Shogunate)<br /> Occult 5<br /> Melee 3<br /> <br /> Other Abilities<br /> <br /> Linguistics 1<br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: High Realm) (6BP)<br /> <br /> Artifact 3 (Fist of Titans)<br /> Artifact 5 (Mela's Coil)<br /> Martial Artist 4<br /> Pain Tolerance 4<br /> (3 BP) Manse 3 (Stone of the Ram's Horn)<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Resources 3<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (Riverspeak)<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (Old Realm)<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> 1. Athletics: Effortlessly Rising Flame<br /> 2. Awareness: Precision Awareness Method<br /> 3. Brawl/Martial Arts: Become the Hammer<br /> 4. Integrity: Granite Curtain of Serenity<br /> 5. Performance: Audience Enthusing Display<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Melee: Elemental Sheath<br /> 2. Melee: Dragon Graced Weapon<br /> 3. Earth Dragon Style: Stone Dragon Skin<br /> 4. Earth Dragon Style: Force of the Mountain<br /> 5. Earth Dragon Style: Stillness of Stone Artemi<br /> 6. Earth Dragon Style: Unmoving Mountain Stance<br /> 7. Earth Dragon Style: Earth Dragon Form<br /> 8. Occult: Spirit Detecting Mirror<br /> 9. Occult: Spirit Grounding Shout<br /> 10. Occult: Secret Wind Revelation<br /> 11. Occult: Fivefold Resonance Stance<br /> 12. Occult: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> --. Control Spell: Invulnerable Skin of Bronze<br /> --. Shaping Ritual: Sevenfold Art Invocation<br /> 13. Resistance: Ox-body Technique<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> Free. Fist of Titans: Chambered Fist Charge<br /> 14. Fist of Titans: Mammoth Slam Quake<br /> 15. Fist of Titans: Unstoppable Hammering Blow<br /> <br /> Intimacies<br /> Defining Principle: The Dragon-Blooded are born to rule.<br /> Major Principle: The Immaculate Philosophy (Devout Belief)<br /> Major Principle: I am the mountain, strong and stable \u2013 I do not flee and I am unmoved by tears<br /> Minor Principle: Duty before pleasure<br /> Minor Principle: \u201cI like creating and repairing things.\u201d<br /> Defining Tie: House Ragara<br /> Major Tie: Anathema (Loathing)<br /> <br /> Evasion 3<br /> Parry 6 (+3, 6m)(With tetsubo or Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, else 5; +2, 4m)<br /> <br /> Soak 18 Hardness 10 (Mela's Coil + Invulnerable Skin of Bronze)<br /> (+5/0, Earth Dragon Form)<br /> (+3/+1, 5m/turn or Bonfire)<br /> <br /> Mobility Penalty -0<br /> Resist Poison: 4 dice<br /> <br /> Fist of Titans Smash Attacks (Earth Dragon Form): Accuracy 16 (14 Decisive)(+3, reroll 6s on damage, 3m), Damage 19 (+1/scene, 3m on summon; +5, 3m) (Overwhelming 5, 6 for 2m), Bashing, Smashing (-1i, no Defence penalty), Reaching, Two handed<br /> <br /> Javelin: Accuracy 9/8/7 (5 Decisive), Damage 14 (OVR 1), Lethal, Melee (Parry 5), Thrown (Medium)<br /> <br /> Join Battle 11 (+3 to result)(+3 successes, 6m)<br /> Rush 11 (+3 successes, 10s explode, 6m)<br /> Disengage 5<br /> <br /> Resolve 4 (+2, ignore -1 from wounds, deprivation or poison, 4m)<br /> Guile 3<br /> <br /> Willpower 5<br /> Essence 2<br /> <br /> Personal motes 13<br /> Peripheral motes 31 (20, 11 committed)<br /> <br /> Health Track (3m/tick, ignore one point of penalties)<br /> -0 x1<br /> -1 x2<br /> -1 x4<br /> -3 x1<br /> Incap</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Fight<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Join Battle</b>:<br /> <br /> Medium Range<br /> <br /> Volfer Join Battle: 12 dice for 6m +1 Willpower. Result of 10i. (7m Personal/33m Peripheral, 5WP)<br /> Smash Join Battle: 17 dice for 6m +1 Willpower. Result 17i. (13/14m, 1a, 4WP)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b>:<br /> <br /> Smash enters Eath Dragon Form and draws her tetsubo from a nearby rock with Dragon Graced Weapon (13/2m, 3a). Her anima flares totemic.<br /> <br /> Volfer moves to Short and kicks of Thunderclap Rush (3/33m). Volfer closes to Close and attacks with an Unclashable attack: 16 dice, 2 automatic successes, rerolling 1s and with 5 post-soak extra damage (0/22m, 4WP). Smasher boosts her Parry to 9 (9/0m), and with 7 successes Volfer misses.<br /> <br /> Smash (13/1m, 3a, Earth Aura, 4WP) 17i<br /> Volfer (0/27m, 2a, 4WP) 10i<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b>:<br /> <br /> Essence backed anima flux (12/0m) withers 1i from Volfer and knocks him Prone.<br /> <br /> Smash launches a Withering Smash, backed by Willpower, Become the Hammer and Force of the Mountain (6/0m, 3WP, 16i). Volfer defends with a Full Excellency and Durability of Oak Meditation with Willpower (0/16m, 3a, 3WP, Parry 9). Smash rolls 8+1 successes and Smashes Volfer out to Short range. Volfer uses Spirit Strengthens the Skin (0/12m) and Soaks 13, leaving 12 dice of rolled damage (rerolling 6s), 6i. Volfer 3i. Smash 23i. Smash Reflexively moves to Close.<br /> <br /> Volfer Flurries Rise from Prone (2WP) with an Attack. He handily rolls the 1 success he needs to stand up, then rolls an Excellent Strike (0/9m) with Excellency (0/3m) and Fire and Stones Strike (0/0m) and Willpower (1WP). Smash uses a 4m Excellency Willpower Parry (2/0m 2WP, Parry 9). Volfer rolls 7+2 successes, hitting. He's Soaked down to Minimum+Fire and Stones Strike Damage (4 dice), and rolls 3i. Volfer 7i. Smash 20i.<br /> <br /> Smash: (2/5m, 2WP, 3a, Earth Aura) 20i<br /> Volfer: (0/5m, 1WP, 3a) 7i<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b>:<br /> <br /> Anima flux withers Volfer again to 6i.<br /> <br /> Smash delays to Clash (18i).<br /> <br /> Volfer attacks -- CLASH.<br /> <br /> Smash uses Become the Hammer and Force of the Mountain and Willpower on a Smash attack (1/0m 1WP 17i). 18 dice + 1 success. 12 successes.<br /> Volfer uses Excellent Melee and a 2m Excellency with Willpower (0/0m 0WP). 10 dice, rerolling 1s + 2 successes. 10 successes.<br /> <br /> Volfer is Smashed Prone and takes 20 dice of Withering damage, re-rolling 6s. 7i+3i, Crashes Volfer.<br /> <br /> Smash: (1/5m, 1WP, 3a, Earth Aura) 33i<br /> Volfer: (0/5m, 0WP, 3a, CRASHED, Prone) -3i<br /> <br /> <b>Round 4</b>:<br /> <br /> Anima flux does nothing.<br /> <br /> Smash uses Become the Hammer on a Decisive attack with Willpower (5 Dex+5 MA+1 Speciality+3 Earth Dragon Form+3 Become the hammer=17 dice to hit +1 success, 0/3m). Volfer (Parry 5-2-1=2) uses a 4m Excellency to reach Parry 4. Smash rolls 4+1 successes (YIKES) and hits the Prone Volfer and rolls 33i of damage for 14B, which takes Volfer out of the fight.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wow... I cannot believe that it took four rounds for a starting Deeb to beat Volfer. That's basically twice as long as it takes an Essence 3 Deeb.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I don't have Volfer's stats on hand, but just generally speaking why did he do so poorly in this fight? An E1 Dawn should have no problem chewing through an E1 Deeb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T17:41:56-08:00","id":1367131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367127#post1367127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I don't have Volfer's stats on hand, but just generally speaking why did he do so poorly in this fight? An E1 Dawn should have no problem chewing through an E1 Deeb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Volfer is solid, but Ragara Smash is utterly optimized with min/max'd stats, sorcery, and some of the best artifacts in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically it's pitting an average Solar warrior at Essence 1 against one off the greatest Essence 2 Dragonblooded alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-11-2020, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T18:10:53-08:00","id":1367134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367127#post1367127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I don't have Volfer's stats on hand, but just generally speaking why did he do so poorly in this fight? An E1 Dawn should have no problem chewing through an E1 Deeb.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't help that Volfer's made a bunch of glaringly bad optimization decisions. His most important Physical Attribute is his lowest. He has no charms to help him not get hit, and nothing to deal with Overwhelming so every hit hurts. On that note, his Soak is laughable for a dedicated combatant so every hit really hurts. He has no ESS2+ Charms. The list could be extended. <br /> I wouldn't call him average, he's a pretty iffy Dawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T18:25:08-08:00","id":1367135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367134#post1367134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't help that Volfer's made a bunch of glaringly bad optimization decisions. His most important Physical Attribute is his lowest. He has no charms to help him not get hit, and nothing to deal with Overwhelming so every hit hurts. On that note, his Soak is laughable for a dedicated combatant so every hit really hurts. He has no ESS2+ Charms. The list could be extended.<br /> I wouldn't call him average, he's a pretty iffy Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not taking advantage of Supernal isn't good, but his attribute choices and lack of ability to deal with Overwhelming is fine. His soak could be better, 11 in heavy armor, but then he's got a -2 mobility penalty, so his Disengage pool goes down to 3, and rushes down to 2. He looks like garbage compared to other Dawn PCs but he's fine. Mirror Flag is a BAD Dawn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T18:30:22-08:00","id":1367136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367135#post1367135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not taking advantage of Supernal isn't good, but his attribute choices and lack of ability to deal with Overwhelming is fine. His soak could be better, 11 in heavy armor, but then he's got a -2 mobility penalty, so his Disengage pool goes down to 3, and rushes down to 2. He looks like garbage compared to other Dawn PCs but he's fine. Mirror Flag is a BAD Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm missing something, Mirror Flag isn't a Dawn. So I must be missing something, what is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","user":"vwllss trnt prncss","date":". 02-11-2020, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T18:35:16-08:00","id":1367138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367136#post1367136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I'm missing something, Mirror Flag isn't a Dawn. So what <i>am</i> I missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if somebody showed up at my table with a Dawn that looked like Mirror Flag, they would have made a really bad Dawn. If I don't know the person is up to something deliberate with the character I might give them a side conversation about how to design characters to do specific things, and let them redesign it for session 2. Give Volfer the rest of his chargen charms and merits and he'll do just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T18:44:31-08:00","id":1367140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367127#post1367127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't have Volfer's stats on hand, but just generally speaking why did he do so poorly in this fight? An E1 Dawn should have no problem chewing through an E1 Deeb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Volfer's missing about a third of his Charms in the Tomb of Dreams adventure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T19:03:37-08:00","id":1367145,"title":"","content":"I like to think of Volfer as a... 5 on the scale of Exalt Chargen prowess.<br /> <br /> Is 5 awful? No. 5 can fight off armies and handily take on rated 5 Deebs and whatnot.<br /> <br /> However ... the scale goes to 20. 20 ish is about where Ragara Smash is operating.<br /> <br /> Now I'm reasonably confident to say that any Chargen Celestial at 20 can probably beat Ragara Smash like 70-80% of the time, with the remainder being dice luck.<br /> <br /> How do I know this? Well, JohnDoe pitted one of my optimized chargen creations (ish, Death Kitty could be more optimal for combat, she runs about a 15-17) against Ragara Smash's older Ess 3 brother (which is the one that pancaked Volfer in 2 rounds) and she won (barely, but as I said, she's not as optimal as I could make her).<br /> <br /> The fact that even at the top of the scale (Dawns) there is so much granularity and room for jostling for Best Combatant Crown is heartening to me, in a weird way.<br /> <br /> It probably speaks to the leering munchkin that lairs in my optimizer's brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-11-2020, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T19:13:00-08:00","id":1367146,"title":"","content":"Side question. What is Tomb of Dreams? Sounds like a prepublished adventure. Where can i get it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T19:28:06-08:00","id":1367151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367146#post1367146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side question. What is Tomb of Dreams? Sounds like a prepublished adventure. Where can i get it?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/208891/Tomb-of-Dreams-an-Exalted-3rd-Edition-Jumpstart\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/208891.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/208891/Tomb-of-Dreams-an-Exalted-3rd-Edition-Jumpstart\" target=\"_blank\"> Tomb of Dreams an Exalted 3rd Edition Jumpstart - Onyx Path Publishing | Exalted 3rd Edition | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/208891/Tomb-of-Dreams-an-Exalted-3rd-Edition-Jumpstart\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/208891/Tomb-of-Dreams-an-Exalted-3rd-Edition-Jumpstart </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Tomb of Dreams an Exalted 3rd Edition Jumpstart - Once, in the time before the gods forgot their names, when the world was flat and floated on a sea of chaos, there was a </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T20:28:33-08:00","id":1367154,"title":"","content":"If <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> or <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> are taking requests, I'd love to settle an old forum debate: Dawn Single Point vs Dawn Melee. Either from chargen or at E3, really the parameters are up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T21:34:11-08:00","id":1367161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367154#post1367154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> or <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> are taking requests, I'd love to settle an old forum debate: Dawn Single Point vs Dawn Melee. Either from chargen or at E3, really the parameters are up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we putting any kind of limit on other charms outside of the combat styles? Like can they both grab Thunderbolt Attack Prana? Also can the Single Point guy grab Melee or other MA charms? And lastly is there a number of charms restriction or just as many as each wants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T22:13:28-08:00","id":1367164,"title":"","content":"Let's say Chargen and they can both have 15 charms to spend in Dodge, Resistance, Athletics and Awareness and their combat ability. SP can't dip into Melee and vice versa, neither can dip into Thrown/Archery/Brawl or other MAs. <br /> <br /> As for merits and artifacts i leave that up to you to decide if its worth adding, as long as each side gets equal access it should be fine.<br /> <br /> Edit: sorcery is allowed (probably just for ISoB)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 02-12-2020, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T02:27:59-08:00","id":1367181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367145#post1367145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think of Volfer as a... 5 on the scale of Exalt Chargen prowess.<br /> <br /> Is 5 awful? No. 5 can fight off armies and handily take on rated 5 Deebs and whatnot.<br /> <br /> However ... the scale goes to 20. 20 ish is about where Ragara Smash is operating.<br /> <br /> Now I'm reasonably confident to say that any Chargen Celestial at 20 can probably beat Ragara Smash like 70-80% of the time, with the remainder being dice luck.<br /> <br /> How do I know this? Well, JohnDoe pitted one of my optimized chargen creations (ish, Death Kitty could be more optimal for combat, she runs about a 15-17) against Ragara Smash's older Ess 3 brother (which is the one that pancaked Volfer in 2 rounds) and she won (barely, but as I said, she's not as optimal as I could make her).<br /> <br /> The fact that even at the top of the scale (Dawns) there is so much granularity and room for jostling for Best Combatant Crown is heartening to me, in a weird way.<br /> <br /> It probably speaks to the leering munchkin that lairs in my optimizer's brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record (because it's important for the next fight) Death Kitty is the closest thing I've ever seen to a perfect character. It's not completely combat optimized (I'd give her a solid 17/20 for combat)... But she's not meant to be combat optimized. She's got Omni-applicable Excllencies! She can fit into any Exalted Campaign, no matter the tone and do well.<br /> <br /> Ragara Smash and The Invincible are not meant as player characters. They're thought exercises. They would be utterly unplayable in a real game (which is why Cynis Ganan, my actual character, is significantly less tough than Ragara Smash). Even in the one field they're &quot;good&quot; at, they're unplayable. Against most combatants they're too powerful, meaning no drama and great difficulty balancing encounters against the rest of the party. Against dedicated combatants (like Octavian) they're not nearly powerful enough (even highly mobile archers would be a problem for them). Heck, even the Corebook Essence 2 Deathknight can wipe the floor with Smash (if mounted, and wins more often than not against Invi I'd suspect). You would not have fun playing these characters in a real game.<br /> <br /> (Volfer also has probably the worst possible array for a Physical Primary character. I'd rather play a 5/1/5 than be lumbered with Volfer's statline.)<br /> <br /> So on to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a>'s request... sure I <i>can</i> do that if you really want me to.<br /> <br /> Are you sure you wouldn't rather me test out characters more like Death Kitty -- ones you could reasonably expect to be able to use in a game?<br /> Or characters more like Ragara Smash -- utterly optimized to kill things?<br /> <br /> And do you just want them to fight each other, or would you like to see how well each does against a &quot;typical&quot; opponent (like Volfer) as well?<br /> <br /> Because unless my math is <i>way</i> off:<br /> <br /> Supernal Melee will wreck Single Point.<br /> Single Point will be much better against anything of Volfer's power level or below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T02:44:27-08:00","id":1367182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367181#post1367181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So on to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a>'s request... sure I <i>can</i> do that if you really want me to.<br /> <br /> Are you sure you wouldn't rather me test out characters more like Death Kitty -- ones you could reasonably expect to be able to use in a game?<br /> Or characters more like Ragara Smash -- utterly optimized to kill things?<br /> <br /> And do you just want them to fight each other, or would you like to see how well each does against a &quot;typical&quot; opponent (like Volfer) as well?<br /> <br /> Because unless my math is <i>way</i> off:<br /> <br /> Supernal Melee will wreck Single Point.<br /> Single Point will be much better against anything of Volfer's power level or below.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, thank you for your post and your hard work. Second, I would like to see the fight of Melee vs SP, because it's been a lengthy debate with many people convinced that both sides are certainly going to win, there are many posts on this very forum about how OP Single Point is and equally many saying Melee is better. I would like to see it play out with my own eyes. If you would like to run a second battle, Melee vs Somebody and SP vs Somebody and see how the benchmark against a known quantity, that would also be great. <br /> <br /> Also, before the dice come out, why do you believe Melee will do much better? I'm curious to know your reasoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T04:20:25-08:00","id":1367193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367182#post1367182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Firstly, thank you for your post and your hard work. Second, I would like to see the fight of Melee vs SP, because it's been a lengthy debate with many people convinced that both sides are certainly going to win, there are many posts on this very forum about how OP Single Point is and equally many saying Melee is better. I would like to see it play out with my own eyes. If you would like to run a second battle, Melee vs Somebody and SP vs Somebody and see how the benchmark against a known quantity, that would also be great. <br /> <br /> Also, before the dice come out, why do you believe Melee will do much better? I'm curious to know your reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Single Point is hella broken mega powerful. More so than Solar Melee. But...<br /> <br /> It's like the fight between Ahalt and Octavian. Ahlat is clearly more powerful, but he specializes in making one, unstoppable nuke attack whilst Octavian specializes in utterly wrecking anything that uses one unstoppable nuke attack.<br /> <br /> Single Point has Onslaught reflection. Insanely powerful. Melee ignores Onslaught.<br /> Single Point has two Initative tracks. Melee has multiple attacks.<br /> Single Point has various mega-attacks. Melee has cap-breaker defenses.<br /> Single Point has an unblockable, unparryable attack. Solar Melee has Heavenly Guardian Defense.<br /> <br /> Against a regular opponent, piling your onslaught penality onto them, then hitting them with two damage boosted attacks each round, stacking even more onslaught, before hitting them with the Single Point capstone is... massively broken.<br /> <br /> But Solar Melee just goes &quot;lolno&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Also: &quot;hard work&quot;, heh. You're Welcome and Thank You.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-12-2020, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T04:50:31-08:00","id":1367196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367181#post1367181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record (because it's important for the next fight) Death Kitty is the closest thing I've ever seen to a perfect character. It's not completely combat optimized (I'd give her a solid 17/20 for combat)... But she's not meant to be combat optimized. She's got Omni-applicable Excllencies! She can fit into any Exalted Campaign, no matter the tone and do well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lion's share of the credit should go to my fellow forumites who worked tirelessly in the optimization mines to perfect her, but indeed thank you very much for the kind words. Its always nice to see a particular build do well in practice as well as in theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T10:20:11-08:00","id":1367254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367193#post1367193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Solar Melee just goes &amp;quot;lolno&amp;quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I agree with that. Solar Melee just has ways of sitting down almost all of SPs stuff, but the reverse isn\u2019t true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T14:06:30-08:00","id":1367301,"title":"","content":"21 dice rerolling 1s adding 2 successes averages 13 successes<br /> 19 dice adding 3 successes minus 1 averages 11 successes...<br /> <br /> So close...<br /> <br /> (I've just made the characters and rolled Join Battle. It occured to me that if Single Point went all in, he could launch a 37i+1 Decisive with double tens and one double nine on his first turn. But it missed, so now I called a do over, because statistically speaking it will miss and is therefore a bad strategy. Still. Very nearly got away with a one turn combat there.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T14:14:35-08:00","id":1367302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367301#post1367301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">21 dice rerolling 1s adding 2 successes averages 13 successes<br /> 19 dice adding 3 successes minus 1 averages 11 successes...<br /> <br /> So close...<br /> <br /> (I've just made the characters and rolled Join Battle. It occured to me that if Single Point went all in, he could launch a 37i+1 Decisive with double tens and one double nine on his first turn. But it missed, so now I called a do over, because statistically speaking it will miss and is therefore a bad strategy. Still. Very nearly got away with a one turn combat there.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It still might be the best strategy, if the chance of winning the all-or-nothing is better than the chance of winning the long way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T14:20:12-08:00","id":1367305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367302#post1367302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still might be the best strategy, if the chance of winning the all-or-nothing is better than the chance of winning the long way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm playing the fight out because I hate myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T15:09:23-08:00","id":1367317,"title":"","content":"By the way, I think it might be worth trying a variant, were you are allowed to take both Single Point and Melee charms (sticking to 15 charms limit), since per Developers' clarification, while in Single Point form, you are allowed to make your regular attacks with Melee (while your sword's attacks must always be made with Martial Arts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T18:25:29-08:00","id":1367348,"title":"","content":"So I tried running Volfer against two blood apes. I brought him up to chargen levels by giving him his signature daiklave, a specialty in it, and some other Essence 1 charms, Dipping Swallow, Solar Counterattack and another Ox-Body. This was the result.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Volfer spends 6m for 6 dice on Join battle, rolling 10i<br /> BA1 gets 6i<br /> BA2 gets 4i<br /> <br /> volfer has 35 motes left<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> <br /> Volfer will attempt a withering strike against BA1, spending 3m for Excellent Strike, and 5m for Fire and Stones Strike. Volfer rolls 12 dice for 8 total successes. Then rolling 19 damage for 12, brutally crashing BA1.<br /> <br /> Volfer 23i 27m<br /> BA1 -6i<br /> BA2 4i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Bloodape 2 will use Principle of Motion to make two withering attacks against Volfer, who will use Durability of Oak meditation for 3m.<br /> <br /> First attack with 11 dice misses with only 4.<br /> <br /> Second attack with 11 dice also misses with an even worse 3.<br /> <br /> Volfer 23i 24m<br /> BA1 -6i<br /> BA2 4i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Bloodape 1 will attempt the same with 2 withering attacks. On the first one though Volfer will spend 3m on Solar Countarattack, 3m on Excellent Strike, 3m on Fire and Stones Strike and 4m on his excellency.<br /> <br /> Rolling 13 dice for 7 total and striking the ape. Then rolling 26 decisive damage for 11, killing the ape outright.<br /> <br /> Volfer 4i 11m<br /> BA2 4i<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> Volfer 4i 16m<br /> BA2 4i<br /> <br /> BA2 and Volfer clash! BA2 using Principle of Motion, and Volfer using 3m Excellent Strike, 5m Fire and Stones Strike, and 4m Excellency.<br /> <br /> Blood Ape rolls an impressive 10 on 11 dice, and Volfer gets only 7 with 16 dice!<br /> <br /> BA2 rolls 11 damage, getting a sad 1 and failing to even crash the Dawn.<br /> <br /> Volfer 2i 4m<br /> BA2 7i<br /> <br /> BA2 still has another attack though, and will use it. Volfer this time defending with a 2m Peony Blossom and 2m excellency, the last of his motes. Rolling 11 dice for an amazing 10 AGAIN! And rolling 10 damage for 4, crashing Volfer.<br /> <br /> Volfer -2i 0m<br /> BA2 15i<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> <br /> Volfer -2i 5m<br /> BA2 15i<br /> <br /> The ape will use Principle of Motion to wither, and Volfer will Dipping Swallow each.<br /> <br /> Rolling 11 dice the ape misses with just 3.<br /> <br /> Volfer -1i 3m<br /> BA2 15i<br /> <br /> Then rolling his decisive with 11 dice, hitting with 7. Then rolling 9 dice for 5 damage.<br /> <br /> Volfer -6i 1m<br /> BA2 21i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Volfer will attempt to wither back, rolling 12 dice and missing with only 2.<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ===========<br /> Volfer -6i 6m<br /> BA2 21i<br /> <br /> Bloodape makes another two withering attacks, this time Volfer defends with Durability of Oak.<br /> <br /> First attack misses with 3, second misses with 5<br /> <br /> Volfer -6i 3m<br /> BA2 21i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Volfer will attempt to wither back, rolling 12 dice and hitting with 7. Rolling 13 dice for 8 damage, pulling out of crash.<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ===========<br /> Volfer 3i 8m<br /> BA2 13i<br /> <br /> Bloodape uses his final willpower point for another two withering, Volfer will again use 3m Durability of Oak. First one hits with 6, rolling 7 damage for 4, crashing Volfer again.<br /> <br /> Second one misses with only 4<br /> <br /> Volfer -1i 5m<br /> BA2 18i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Volfer will attempt to wither back, rolling 12 dice and hitting with 7. Rolling 13 dice for 8 damage, pulling out of crash, again.<br /> <br /> Volfer 8i 5m<br /> BA2 10i<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> ===========<br /> Volfer 8i 10m<br /> BA2 10i<br /> <br /> Bloodape will use a 4m Brutal Ape Pounce, Volfer will not spend motes to defend. Ape rolls 4 successes and misses.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Volfer will attack back with a withering strike, rolling 12 dice for 6 and hitting, then rolling 12 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Volfer 12i 10m<br /> BA2 7i<br /> <br /> Volfer will spend 3m to use One Weapon Two Blows, giving another withering attack, rolling 12 dice and getting it with 4. Then rolling 11 damage for 7, crashing the ape.<br /> <br /> Volfer 25i 7m<br /> BA2 0i<br /> <br /> Round 7<br /> ===========<br /> Volfer 25i 12m<br /> BA2 0i<br /> <br /> Volfer tries to finish this with a 3m Fire and Stones Strike and a 3m Excellent Strike. Rolling 12 dice for 6 and hitting, then rolling 28 decisive damage for 11, slaying the ape.<br /> <br /> Volfer 4i 6m<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> In spite of getting pretty unlucky a lot of the time, Volfer had this solidly in the bag. If I was actually running this in a game I would have had the ape decisive when he got 15 initiative. I actually ran it that way at first, but then he only dealt 6L, and then got Initiative Shifted on and well...that's that. So instead of playing like it would be in a game I was playing to win, only launching a decisive when I had the roughly 50i required to stand a good shot at one-shotting Volfer. Unfortunately the willpower dried up, and without Principle of Motion the ape is basically worse than Volfer in every way, without even counting his charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> You COULD make a Dawn that kills both those apes in one turn using Invincible Fury of the Dawn and some other stuff, but in this case they might actually be worse off doing it. It's not like Volfer spent any willpower here, and he won with 6m left to spare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:32:02-08:00","id":1367438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367317#post1367317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I think it might be worth trying a variant, were you are allowed to take both Single Point and Melee charms (sticking to 15 charms limit), since per Developers' clarification, while in Single Point form, you are allowed to make your regular attacks with Melee (while your sword's attacks must always be made with Martial Arts).</div> </div> </div> </div>The power play is probably to attack with Single Point and defend with Melee, I guess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T14:02:58-08:00","id":1367598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1342638#post1342638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I mean at that point why care about anything really? The Scarlet Empire bugging you? Go tear down the Imperial Palace, the Deliberative, and the Thosand Scales. Immaculate Order kind of getting on your nerves? Go knock over the Palace Sublime, that should make them think twice before scrounging up one of their little Wyld Hunts. Then maybe walk into Thorns completely casually and eradicate the presence of death from it, it's got a nice view, nice palace, could be a fun home to own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just catching up with this thread. But I recall a discussion about a flying archer being lethal (eventually) to these types. Surely someone with wings lives in one of these setting-important places?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T14:11:11-08:00","id":1367602,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Melee vs Single Point</b></u><br /> <br /> Standard white-room conditions. Honorable fight with no poisoned throwing knives, no tyrant lizard mounts (reaper daiklaves don't have Reach, but grand daiklaves do...), no turning into a shadow or other shennanigans. Win or lose based on Melee/Single Point Charms, not Atheletics Charms or the such like. One point stunt on everything important (included in statlines). Fighting to the death.<br /> <br /> Two &quot;save points&quot; where we pick up and replay the fight using alternate strategies.<br /> <br /> Melee wins by a much larger margin than I thought they would.<br /> <br /> <br /> Melee:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Cutting Edge of the Melee<br /> Dawn Caste<br /> Immovable Swordswoman (she/her - Melee)<br /> <br /> Strength 5<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> Charisma 1<br /> Manipulation 5<br /> Appearance 1<br /> <br /> Perception 3<br /> Intelligence 1<br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> Dawn Caste Abilities (and Specialities) (8 BP)<br /> <br /> <b>Melee 5 (Swords)</b><br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Dodge 5 (Armored)<br /> Resistance 5<br /> Thrown 1<br /> <br /> Favored Abilities (2 BP)<br /> <br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Integrity 3<br /> Occult 3<br /> Sail 3<br /> War 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: Riverspeak) (3BP)<br /> <br /> Artifact 5 (Mela's Coil)<br /> Artifact 5 (Gorgon)<br /> Fast Reflexes 3<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Melee: Excellent Strike<br /> 2. Melee: One Weapon, Two Blows<br /> 3. Melee: Peony Blossom Technique<br /> 4. Melee: Dipping Swallow Defense<br /> 5. Melee: Bulwark Stance<br /> 6. Melee: Five-Fold Bulwark Stance<br /> 7. Melee: Hail Shattering Practice<br /> 8. Melee: Iron Whirlwind Attack<br /> 9. Melee: Invincible Fury of the Dawn<br /> 10. Melee: Perfect Strike Discipline<br /> 11. Melee: Fervent Blow<br /> 12. Resistance:Ox-body Technique<br /> 13. Resistance: Ox-body Technique x2<br /> 14. Awareness: Sensory Acuity Prana<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> 15. Mela's Coil: Wind Rider's Swiftness<br /> <br /> Intimacies<br /> Defining Principle: I live by the sword<br /> Major Principle: The Realm Must Fall<br /> Major Tie: The Undead (Loathing)<br /> Minor Tie: My Circle (Loyalty)<br /> <br /> Evasion 7<br /> Parry 8<br /> <br /> Gorgon: Accuracy 16 (13 Decisive), Damage 17 (OVR 5), Lethal<br /> <br /> Soak 12 Hardness 10<br /> Mobility Penalty -0<br /> Resist Poison: 6 dice<br /> <br /> Join Battle 14<br /> Rush 13<br /> Disengage 12<br /> <br /> Resolve 5<br /> Guile 4<br /> <br /> Willpower 6 (2BP)<br /> Essence 1<br /> <br /> Personal motes 13<br /> Peripheral motes 33 (11 Committed, 22 Available)<br /> <br /> Health Track<br /> -0 x1<br /> -1 x4<br /> -2 x4<br /> -4 x1<br /> Incap</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Martial Arts:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Bleeding Point of All The Martial Arts<br /> Dawn Caste<br /> Unstoppable Martial Arts Master (him/he - Point)<br /> <br /> Strength 5<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> Charisma 1<br /> Manipulation 5<br /> Appearance 1<br /> <br /> Perception 3<br /> Intelligence 1<br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> Dawn Caste Abilities (and Specialities) (8 BP)<br /> <br /> <b>Martial Arts: Single Point Shining Into the Void 5 (Shining Ice Mirror)</b><br /> Brawl 3<br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Dodge 5 (Armored)<br /> Resistance 5<br /> Thrown 0<br /> <br /> Favored Abilities (2 BP)<br /> <br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Integrity 3<br /> Occult 3<br /> Sail 1<br /> War 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: Riverspeak) (3BP)<br /> <br /> Artifact 3 (Shining Ice Mirror)<br /> Artifact 3 (Medium Armor)<br /> Fast Reflexes 3<br /> Martial Artist 4<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Single Point: Cutting Light Concentration<br /> 2. Single Point: Shining Starfall Execution<br /> 3. Single Point: Single Point Shining Into The Void Form<br /> 4. Single Point: Fatal Stroke Flash<br /> 5. Single Point: Liquid Steel Flow<br /> 6. Single Point: Horizon-Swallowed Star Flash<br /> 7. Single Point: Void Slicing Wind<br /> 8. Single Point: Six-Demon Scabbard Binding<br /> 9. Single Point: Blinding Nova Flare<br /> 10. Awareness: Sensory Acuity Prana<br /> 11. Awareness: Keen Sight Technique<br /> 12. Awareness: Keen Hearing and Touch Technique<br /> 13. Awareness: Awakening Eye<br /> 14. Resistance:Ox-body Technique<br /> 15. Resistance: Ox-body Technique x2<br /> <br /> Intimacies<br /> Defining Principle: I live by the sword<br /> Major Principle: The Realm Must Fall<br /> Major Tie: The Undead (Loathing)<br /> Minor Tie: My Circle (Loyalty)<br /> <br /> Evasion 6<br /> Parry 8<br /> <br /> Shining Ice Mirror: Accuracy 16 (13 Decisive), Damage 17 (OVR 5), Lethal<br /> <br /> Soak 9 Hardness 7<br /> Mobility Penalty -1<br /> Resist Poison: 6 dice<br /> <br /> Join Battle 14<br /> Rush 12<br /> Disengage 11<br /> <br /> Resolve 5<br /> Guile 4<br /> <br /> Willpower 6 (2BP)<br /> Essence 1<br /> <br /> Personal motes 13<br /> Peripheral motes 33 (12 Committed, 21 Available)<br /> <br /> Health Track<br /> -0 x1<br /> -1 x4<br /> -2 x4<br /> -4 x1<br /> Incap</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Fight:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Join Battle</b><br /> <br /> Point: Awakening Eye, 2m Awareness Excellency, Sensory Acuity Prana, Willpower (11/10m 4WP 2a) 21i<br /> Melee: Full Awareness Excellency, Sensory Acuity Prana, Rouses Gorgon to Slitted, Willpower (13/7m, 4WP 3a) 13i<br /> <br /> Medium Range<br /> <br /> *First Save Point*<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 21i: Point opens with Void Slicing Wind, backed with a full Martial Arts Excellency, Fatal Stroke Flash, Shining Starfall Execution, and Willpower (2/0m, 1WP).<br /> Melee responds with Fervent Blow to Clash, and backs it with Perfect Strike Discipline, Excellent Strike, Bulwark Stance and Willpower (4/7m 2WP).<br /> <br /> *Save Point Two*<br /> <br /> Point rolls 14 successes and Melee rolls 16.<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 13i of Lethal Damage and adds one automatic level for 3L, dropping Point into his minus 1s, then she resets to 4i. Gorgon stays Slitted.<br /> Point moves to Short range behind Melee, drops to 13i, then loses 3i for failing to land a Decisive attack, takes one Onslaught penalty to defense and 2 Clash penalty (on top of the -1 Wound Penalty).<br /> <br /> 4i: Melee Reflexively moves to Close and makes an Excellent Strike, Withering (1/7m).<br /> Point, knowing what's coming, defends with a 2m Excellency and Willpower (0/0m 0WP) for Parry 6.<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 6 successes, hitting, and 8 dice of damage for 6+1i.<br /> <br /> Melee rises to 12i, Point drops to 3i. Point takes another point of Onslaught.<br /> <br /> Melee then triggers One Weapon, Two Blows (0/5m) for a second Withering attack.<br /> Point defends with Parry 3.<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 7 successes, hitting with a threshold of 4, rising to 13i.<br /> Melee rolls 12 dice of damage for 6i.<br /> <br /> Melee rises to 19i. Point drops to -3i, Crash. Melee rises to 24i.<br /> <br /> Melee: 24i (0/10m, 2WP, 3a)<br /> Point: -3i (0/5m, 0WP, 3a) CRASH -1 Wound Penalty, -3 Onslaught, -2 Clash<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> 24i: Melee opens with a Withering attack.<br /> Point defends on Parry 1.<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 11 successes, hitting with a threshold of 10, rising to 25i.<br /> Melee rolls 18 dice of damage for 11i. Melee rises to 36i. Point falls to -14i.<br /> <br /> Melee triggers Peony Blossom Technique (0/9m, 1WP, 0a) and Invincible Fury of the Dawn (0/4m, 0WP), declaring 5 Decisive attacks backed by Excellent Strike (0/1m), each with 8i and 9i in the last attack.<br /> Point declares a 4m Excellency to defend against the first attack on Parry 2. Remaining attacks resolve against Parry 0.<br /> <br /> First attack hits for 4L (7L).<br /> Second attack hits for 2L (9L).<br /> Third attack hits for 1L (10L).<br /> Forth attack hits for 3L (13L), killing Point.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Melee wins decisively in Round 2: Point fails to land even a single blow.<br /> <br /> Replay from Second Save Point.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Point rolls 13 successes and Melee rolls 11. (Statistically improbable, but not impossible.) Point wins the Clash.<br /> <br /> Point rolls 37i in Lethal damage with double-10s and one double-9, then adds an automatic level of lethal damage, for 18L, reduced to 17L by Bulwark Stance.<br /> <br /> Melee is dead.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Single Point wins in Round 1, cutting Melee down in a single blow.<br /> <br /> Replay from Save Point One.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Point wins Join Battle and Reflexively enters Single Point Form (11/0m, 3a).<br /> <br /> Sword is rolled into battle on 9i.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 23i: Point Aims at Melee (Parry 10, +3 dice to next attack).<br /> 13i: Melee activates Wind-Rider Swiftness (8/7m) to move to Short and Rush Point (9 successes to 2, Point is Rushed). Melee activates Five-Fold Bulwark Stance (3/7m, 3WP).<br /> 9i: Sword does nothing.<br /> <br /> Short Range<br /> <br /> Point: 23i (11/5m, 4WP, 3a) Single Point Form<br /> Sword: 9i<br /> Melee: 13i (3/12m, 3WP, 3a) Five-Fold Bulwark Stance<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> 23i, Point drops to Parry 8: Point Reflexively moves to Close (losing his Aim bonus) and makes a Withering attack with Liquid Steel Flow and an 8m Excellency with Willpower (3/0m, 3WP).<br /> Melee Clashes with Fervent Blow, Excellent Strike, and an 8m Excellency with Willpower (0/11m, 1WP).<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 13 successes. Points rolls 9 successes. Point drops to Parry 5.<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 13+5i+1 in Lethal damage for 8L. Point is in -2 Wound Penalty (Parry 3). Melee resets to 4i.<br /> <br /> 9i: Sword attacks Melee, Withering with a 3m Excellency and Willpower (0/0, 2WP).<br /> Melee defends with Five-Fold Bulwark Stance (Parry 8) and Dipping Swallow Stance (0/10m, Parry 9).<br /> <br /> Sword rolls 17 dice for 6 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> 4i: Melee attacks Sword, Withering.<br /> Sword defends with Willlpower (1WP) on Parrry 4.<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 9 successes on 16 dice, hitting with a threshold of 5. Melee rises to 5i.<br /> Melee rolls 13 dice of damage for 7i. Melee rises to 12i. Sword falls to 2i (Parry 2).<br /> <br /> Melee activates One Weapon, Two Blows (0/7m) and attacks Sword, Withering.<br /> Sword defends with Willpower (0WP) on Parry 3.<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 8 successes on 16 dice, hitting with a threshold of 5. Melee rises to 13i.<br /> Melee rolls 13 dice of damage for 3i. Melee rises to 16i. Sword falls to -1i, Crash. Melee rises to 21i.<br /> <br /> Point: 23i (0/5m, 0WP, 3a) Single Point Form<br /> Sword: -1i Crashed Awaiting Reset<br /> Melee: 21i (0/12m, 1WP, 3a) Five-Fold Bulwark Stance<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> 23i: Point resets defence to Parry 6. Point attacks with Liquid Steel Flow (0/0m).<br /> Melee defends with Dipping Swallow Stance (0/11m, Parry 9).<br /> <br /> Point rolls 16 dice against Parry 9 for 9 successes.<br /> Melee uses Hail-Shattering Practice (0/10m) and Point misses.<br /> <br /> 21i: Melee uses Excellent Strike (0/7m) to Wither Point.<br /> Point defends on Parry 6.<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 11 successes, hitting with a threshold of 5, rising to 22i.<br /> Melee rolls 13 dice of damage, for 9i. Melee rises to 31i. Point falls to 13i.<br /> <br /> I remember that Point actually only has three health levels left and I should have used Peony Blossom Technique last turn and that I am, in fact, an idiot.<br /> I also remember that Gorgon is supposed to be adding a success to damage rolls.<br /> <br /> Melee uses One Weapon, Two Blows (0/4m), to launch a Decisive attack.<br /> Point defends on Parry 5.<br /> <br /> Melee rolls 9 successes to hit, and 12L.<br /> <br /> Point is dead. Again.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Melee wins decisively in Round 3.<br /> <br /> That's 2/3 wins for Melee, and Single Point only won that one on an incredibly lucky dice roll.<br /> <br /> If I were Supernal Melee, I wouldn't want to fight a Single Point Supernal. Ever. For any reason. But if I did, I'd probably win 75% of the time.<br /> <br /> Single Point could do better with more Atheltics Charms and fewer Single Point Charms.<br /> <br /> Imagine, if you will, using Foe Vaulting Method and Thunderbolt Attack Prana to make a Suprise Attack with Double Damage. With Strength Increasing Exercise for +1 damage.<br /> <br /> But at that point is it really Single Point vs Melee, or Melee vs Athletics?<br /> <br /> (Melee, of course, could also benefit from any of these Essence 1 Charms. It's just that you wouldn't want to give up any of the Melee Charms in this build to buy them. If anything you really want to drop an Ox-Body for Fire and Stones Strike.)<br /> <br /> I have no interest in running a mix of Single Point and Melee at this juncture. But I will run Melee and Point against Volfer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-17-2020, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:19:02-08:00","id":1367628,"title":"","content":"How do both fighters have a resting Parry of 8? 5 ability 5 attribute 1 speciality is Parry 6, and a Medium weapon is +1 to parry 7. Where's the last point of parry<br /> <br /> Edit: posted too soon. <br /> <br /> Excellent work. It looks like the conventional wisdom is true- if SP can't splat melee on the first shot it can't win.<br /> <br /> Fervant Blow was a lot more useful than I thought it was, and Im surprised FaSS wasn't picked","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 02-13-2020, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:20:56-08:00","id":1367629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367628#post1367628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do both fighters have a resting Parry of 8? 5 ability 5 attribute 1 speciality is Parry 6, and a Medium weapon is +1 to parry 7. Where's the last point of parry?</div> </div> </div> </div>One point stunt.<br /> <br /> It's also +2 Accuracy dice (most noticeable on their 13 dice Decisives).<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> FaSS is amazing and it wasn't picked as a complete oversight. I thought I'd picked it. But 15 Charms is a tight restriction.<br /> <br /> Anything that lets you Clash Reflexively is amazing. Single Point lets you Clash Reflexively for 8m 1WP. Fervent Blow lets you Clash for 1m 1WP. It's one of the best Charms in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-14-2020, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T16:38:21-08:00","id":1367643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367598#post1367598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just catching up with this thread. But I recall a discussion about a flying archer being lethal (eventually) to these types. Surely someone with wings lives in one of these setting-important places?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible, but not if the Solar has Bonfire Anima Wings or something of the like. The only thing that can take them down is a concentrated effort of massively powerful exalt-level characters, or possibly a legendary general leading an elite and massive army using an Engage action, if you could get them to live long enough.<br /> <br /> That or if they decide to fight something like The Unconqured Sun or someone similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:03:31-08:00","id":1367860,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Point Vs Volfer</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> As established, Point can open with a nova strike that rolls an average of 12 successes. Volfer doesn't have Fervent Blow, so can't Reflexively Clash, has a lower Join Battle than Melee, so will take more damage, and with a Parry 5 + Full Excellency + Willpower (and no cap-breaking Hail-Shattering Strike), Volfer will therefore be hit by Point's nova strike 84% of the time.<br /> <br /> Playing out &quot;can Point beat Volfer&quot; is obviously a waste of time. Approximately 80% of the time, Point will chunk Volfer in one round before he even gets the chance to strike back.<br /> <br /> &quot;But John, you've completely Worfed Volfer and we no longer care!&quot;<br /> <br /> Sheesh, tough crowd.<br /> <br /> Ragara Smash ALSO does not have a Reflexive Clash, and has the same max parry as Volfer. Meaning Smash gets hit and chunked in one round by Point as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;Boo! Terrestrials aren't real Exalted!&quot;<br /> <br /> Wow. Harsh.<br /> <br /> The Knight of Bone and Ivory (one of the best Lunar defensive builds in the game) has Dodge 6. Full Excellency takes them to 8. Stunting Excellency 12. The Knight gets hit by Point 62% of the time on an opening nova strike. The Knight <i>might </i>survive a 38i attack with double-10s and 1 double-9. But it's going to <i>hurt.</i><br /> <br /> Single Point Supernals are scary, ok?<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> I still want to fight Point vs Volfer though.<br /> <br /> Let's make things interesting.<br /> <br /> Volfer has made a demonic pact, and now all his weapons are coated in Yozi Venom. Immaculates are growing suspicious and are closing in. Whilst Volfer will stop at nothing to defeat Point, Point doesn't want to face a Wyld Hunt and therefore must complete the entire fight without flaring his anima. At all. And knowing he must conserve strength, let's say Point can only use half his Willpower pool. Be nice if he can finish with some motes too...<br /> <br /> The Fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Medium Range<br /> <br /> Volfer throws a Full Excellency into Join Battle (13/27m, 1a) for 9i.<br /> Point uses Awakening Eye (8/21m, 5WP) for 12i.<br /> <br /> On winning join battle, Point reflexively activates Single Point Shining Into the Void Form (0/19m) and rolls his sword into battle on 7i.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 12i: Point moves to Short range and Aims.<br /> <br /> 9i: Volfer uses Thunderclap Rush, Excellent Strike, Fire and Stones Strike and a 6m Excellency with Willpower to close to Close and make an (unClashable) Withering attack as his anima goes totemic (13/15m, 5WP, 3a).<br /> Point Parries on 10, and Volfer misses.<br /> <br /> 7i: Sword Withers Volfer with Point's Aim bonus.<br /> Volfer defends with a Full Excellency (13/7m) and Sword misses (by a single success).<br /> <br /> Point: 12i (3/21m, 5WP) Single Point Form<br /> Volfer: 9i (13/12m, 5WP, 3a) -1 Onslaught<br /> Sword: 7i<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> 12i: Point uses a 2m Excellency, Willpower and Liquid Steel Flow to Wither Volfer (0/17m, 3WP).<br /> Volfer defends with a Full Excellency and Willpower (13/4m, 4WP), minus 1 Onslaught.<br /> Point hits (threshold 0) and spends Willpower to extend the duration of Liquid Steel Flow (4WP). 13i.<br /> Volfer boosts Soak using Spirit Strengthens the Skin (13/0m), and Point rolls 3 damage. 16i/6i.<br /> <br /> 7i: Sword Withers with a 4m Excellency (0/13m).<br /> Volfer Parries with a Full Excellency and Willpower (5/0m, 3WP), -2 Onslaught.<br /> Sword hits (threshold 3), 8i.<br /> Volfer boosts Soak using Spirit Strengthens the Skin (1/0m), and Sword rolls 5 damage. 13i/1i.<br /> <br /> 1i: Without enough motes to reasonably stand a chance of hittting, Volfer Aims.<br /> <br /> Point: 16i (1/17m, 3WP) Single Point Form, Liquid Steel Flow<br /> Sword: 13i<br /> Volfer: 1i (1/5m, 3WP) Aim<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> 16i: Point Withers with a 4m Excellency (1/13m).<br /> Volfer defends with a 6m Excellency and Willpower (0/0m, 2WP).<br /> Point hits (threshold 3), 17i.<br /> 6 damage. 23i/-5i.<br /> Volfer is Crashed. 28i.<br /> <br /> 13i: Sword Wither's Volfer.<br /> Volfer Parries backed with Willpower (1WP).<br /> Sword misses.<br /> <br /> -5i: Volfer Withers Sword with Aim and Willpower (0WP).<br /> Sword Parries on 8, Volfer rolls 9(!!!) successes, and hits with a threshold of 1. -4i.<br /> Volfer's damage is Soaked down to Overwhelming. 1 damage. -3i/12i.<br /> <br /> Point: 28i (2/17mm 3WP) Single Point Form, Liquid Steel Flow<br /> Sword: 12i<br /> Volfer: -3i (0/5m, 0WP)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 4</b><br /> <br /> 28i: Point launches a 4m Excellency Decisive backed by Fatal Stroke Flash (2/12m -- Willpower cost waived, ending Liquid Steel Flow).<br /> Volfer defends with a 4m Parry (0/1m)<br /> Point hits with a Threshold of 3 (not that this matters).<br /> <br /> Point rolls 53 dice of lethal damage with 1 double 9 and 3 automatic levels of damage.<br /> <br /> Point deals 30 levels of Lethal damage, enough to kill Volfer twice over, and then resets to 3i.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And there you have it. Point chunks Volfer with 14 motes to spare, without flaring a single level of anima, with half his Willpower remaining (and 12i left on his sword) in only 4 rounds.<br /> <br /> Single Point is an absolute beast-mode martial art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-14-2020, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:55:17-08:00","id":1367874,"title":"","content":"That makes me wonder, since I've never seen it, how scary is a DB with Single Point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:24:57-08:00","id":1367890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367874#post1367874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes me wonder, since I've never seen it, how scary is a DB with Single Point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never used it, but theory crafting I <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330227#post1330227\">honestly don't think it works</a> without Mastery.<br /> <br /> That said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24836_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24836\" data-vbnamecard=\"24836\">Timbo</a> has actually played it so... I'd love to hear that I'm wrong?<br /> <br /> Gathering Light Concentration: Needs a successful Parry. Mastery means you just need to Parry one attack against you before your DV refreshes to use it, but without Mastery it's a pretty unusable Charm IMO. But it is a cap-breaker, and Single Point relies on Decisives. <i>And </i>Deebs don't get a lot of Onslaught negation. So... not completely useless: 4/10. (7/10 with Mastery.)<br /> <br /> Shining Starfall Execution: Without mastery, 6m for +5 damage Decisive-only is &quot;ok&quot; (by contrast Mela's Coil gives +5 damage, Uniform, for 5m and gives you a Reflexive Rush to boot). 6/10. (8/10 with Mastery.)<br /> <br /> Form: Terrestrial - Commit 10m: each round lose 1i unless you spend 1WP. If you spend 1WP, make an extra attack but lose 1i if that attack misses. Yikes. 1/10. (9/10 with Mastery.)<br /> <br /> Fatal Flash Stroke: Terrestrial - You May Not Use This Charm. 0/10. (10/10 with Mastery.)<br /> <br /> Liquid Steel Flow: Terrestrial - 5m for +5 Withering damage or +6 Decisive damage. Yeah that's still pretty good. Not great. 7/10. (10/10 with Mastery.)<br /> <br /> Void-Slicing Wind: Terrestrial - &quot;2m&quot; 1WP Make a Melee attack from Medium range, Decisive-only. Still ok. 7/10. (7.5/10 without Terrestrial, very situational)<br /> <br /> Horizon-Swallowed Star Flash: Terrestrial - Decisive Clash with bonus damage by giving up attack option. Very expensive for what it does. Within reach of a starting character though... 5/10. (8/10 with Mastery.)<br /> <br /> Six-Demon Scabbard Binding: Terrestrial - defend against hostile magic with a Dex+Martial Arts roll that resets you to Base Initiative. This could be worse. It could be better. But it could be worse. 5/10. (9/10 with Mastery.)<br /> <br /> Blinding Nova Flare: &quot;Terrestrial - When Form Charm is active and you choose to spend WP, apply a -2 to your opponents defense for 2i instead of making an extra attack (and do not lose 1i). If you succeed in a Difficulty 5 Gambit, apply an additional -1 per success to a maximum total penality of -7. 1/scene.&quot; Combined with +9 Decisive damage from Liquid Steel Flow and Shining Starfall Execution... 2i 1WP for +2 non-Charm successes is a solid 7/10. (10/10 with Mastery.)<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> My curiosity is peaked enough to try it though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-14-2020, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:00:32-08:00","id":1367901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367890#post1367890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My curiosity is peaked enough to try it though...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd do it myself but I don't know SP well enough. I'm also not sure if it's okay to supplement with base DB charms or not, or if that even matters if there's any good ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T21:00:57-08:00","id":1367969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367890#post1367890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fatal Flash Stroke: Terrestrial - You May Not Use This Charm. 0/10. (10/10 with Mastery.)</div> </div> </div> </div>...why? Vance clarified that an attacker who was already below your initiative can still fall below your initiative after a parry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T23:25:18-08:00","id":1367997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367969#post1367969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...why? Vance clarified that an attacker who was already below your initiative can still fall below your initiative after a parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I missed that. Thanks for the correction.<br /> <br /> (I thought they had to start above your Initative, then miss with a Decisive, then you could attack them for +2 damage (more if your allies could Wither them before your turn).)<br /> <br /> If it's just vs any opponent with a lower Initative who misses a Decisive then 5/10 if the ST is like you (having NPCs open with Decisives) and 3/10 otherwise.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are definitely going to need non-SPSITV charms. Made me think what the optimal Solar SO Charms are:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">1-4. Awareness: Awakening Eye<br /> 6-8. Athletics: Foe Vaulting Method<br /> 9-10. Athletics: Thunderbolt Attack Prana<br /> 11. Melee: Dipping Swallow Defense<br /> 12. Occult: Invulnerable Skin of Bronze<br /> 13-14. Resistance: \u00d73 Ox-bodies<br /> 15. Single Point: Shining Starfall Execution<br /> <br /> Mental Primary (5/1/5), Physical Secondary (3/5/1). <br /> <br /> Open with Sensory Acuity Prana and Awakening Eye. Win Join Battle.<br /> <br /> Decisive attack with Thunderbolt Attack Prana, Foe Vaulting Method and Shining Starfall Execution.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-15-2020, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T23:41:14-08:00","id":1368001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367997#post1367997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I missed that. Thanks for the correction.<br /> <br /> (I thought they had to start above your Initative, then miss with a Decisive, then you could attack them for +2 damage (more if your allies could Wither them before your turn).)<br /> <br /> If it's just vs any opponent with a lower Initative who misses a Decisive then 5/10 if the ST is like you (having NPCs open with Decisives) and 3/10 otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says the triggering attack has to be decisive? Maybe they attack you with a withering, trying to get out of crash, you parry, and their initiative falls below yours at the value of minus three or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T05:29:44-08:00","id":1368023,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1225902#post1225902\">Vance disagrees with you.</a><br /> <br /> The enemy has to <i>lose</i> Initiative as a result of their attack (spent Initiative doesn't count).<br /> Their final score has to be lower than your score.<br /> And you must successfully Parry.<br /> <br /> Absent other Charms, that means they must fail a Decisive attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-15-2020, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T05:52:48-08:00","id":1368026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368023#post1368023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1225902#post1225902\">Vance disagrees with you.</a><br /> <br /> The enemy has to lose Initiative as a result of their attack.<br /> Their final score has to be lower than your score.<br /> And you must successfully Parry.<br /> <br /> Absent other Charms, that means they must fail a Decisive attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh, okay, so they must lose some. I was assuming &quot;fall&quot; was colourful language for &quot;ends up&quot;. That could be literally useless then depending on your ST. Your ST might just decide that they will never, ever launch a decisive attack against you unless they're 3+ initiative over your character. Aegis of Unstoppable Might has the same problem, if NPCs never decsisive you when you're not crashed you will never get to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T11:12:07-08:00","id":1368070,"title":"","content":"Single Point Deeb (no stunts this fight):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Burano Zena<br /> Water Aspect<br /> Dragon Princess<br /> <br /> Strength 5<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> Charisma 5<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Appearance 1<br /> <br /> Perception 3<br /> Intelligence 1<br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> Water Aspect Abilities (and Specialities)<br /> <br /> Brawl 1<br /> Martial Arts: Water Dragon Style 5<br /> Martial Arts: Single Point Shining Into the Void 5 (Stormcaller)<br /> Bureaucracy 0<br /> Investigation 0<br /> Larceny 1<br /> Sail 1<br /> <br /> Favoured Abilities<br /> <br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Dodge 5 (Armored)<br /> Occult 5<br /> Resistance 5 (Sword-in-hand)<br /> <br /> Other Abilities<br /> Integrity 3 (The Pure Way)<br /> Linguistics 1<br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: Rivertongue)<br /> <br /> Artifact 5 (Stormcaller)<br /> Artifact 3 (Medium Armor - Enchanted Leathers)<br /> Cult 3<br /> Martial Artist 4<br /> (Dragon Caste Freebie) Language (Dragon-tongue)<br /> (Dragon Caste Freebie) Language (Old Realm)<br /> (Dragon Caste Freebie) Resources 3<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> 1. Athletics: Effortlessly Rising Flame<br /> 2. Awareness: Precision Awareness Method<br /> 3. Brawl/MA: Become the Hammer<br /> 4. Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> 5. Resistance: Purifying Blood Ascendancy<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Athletics: Soaring Leap Technique<br /> 2. Water Dragon Style: Flowing Water Defense<br /> 3. Water Dragon Style: Rippling Water Strike<br /> 4. Water Dragon Style: Drowning-In-Blood Technique<br /> 5. Water Dragon Style: Water Dragon Form<br /> 6. Single Point: Cutting Light Concentration<br /> 7. Single Point: Shining Starfall Execution<br /> 8. Single Point: Single Point Shining Into The Void Form<br /> 9. Single Point: Fatal Stroke Flash<br /> 10. Single Point: Liquid Steel Flow<br /> 11. Single Point: Void Slicing Wind<br /> 12. Resistance: Oxbody Technique<br /> 13. Resistance: Oxbody Technique x2<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> 14. Stormcaller: Fulminating Edge Flash<br /> 15. Stormcaller: Storm Binding<br /> <br /> Intimacies<br /> <br /> Defining Principle: I am a student of cutting<br /> Defining Principle: Demons must be controlled<br /> Major Principle: The Pure Way (Loyal Adherence)<br /> Defining Tie: Clan Benaro (Loyalty)<br /> Major Tie: The people of Prasad (Nobless Oblige)<br /> Minor Tie: Anathema (Disgust)<br /> <br /> Evasion 6<br /> Parry 7<br /> Soak 9 Hardness 7<br /> Mobility Penalty -0<br /> <br /> Stormcaller Attacks: Accuracy 14 (11 Decisive), Damage 15 (Overwhelming 5), Lethal, Stormy<br /> <br /> Chakram Attacks: Accuracy 9/8/7 (5 Decisive), 10 Damage (OVR 1), Lethal, Cutting, Mounted<br /> <br /> Join Battle 11 (+3 to result)<br /> Rush 11<br /> Disengage 11<br /> <br /> Resolve 5 (6)<br /> Guile 1<br /> <br /> Willpower 6<br /> Essence 2<br /> <br /> Personal motes 13<br /> Peripheral motes 31 (22, 9 committed)<br /> <br /> Health Track<br /> -0 x1<br /> -1 x2<br /> -2 x6<br /> -4 x1<br /> Incap<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Zena, Dragon-Princess vs Volfer, Tomb of Dreams<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Medium Range<br /> <br /> Volfer rolls 12 dice to join battle with Willpower (13/27m, 5WP, 1a) for 8i, sword in hand.<br /> Zena rolls 11 dice to join battle with +3 successes (13/16m, 2a) for 9i, and draws Stormcaller (Storm Intensity 0).<br /> Zena reflexively enters Single Point Form and rolls Sword into battle on 10i (13/6m, 3a).<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 10i. Zena spends Cult to attack twice.<br /> <br /> Zena uses Void Slicing Wind to close to Close and launch a Decisive backed by Shining Starfall Execution and a 2m Become the Hammer and Willpower (0/5m, Cult expended).<br /> Volfer defends with a Full Excellency, and Willpower (13/19m, 2a, 4WP) for Parry 10.<br /> Zena rolls 7+3 successes on 13 dice, hitting for 4L, putting Volfer in his -1s. Sword resets to 3i. Storm intensity rises to 1.<br /> Zena enters Water Aura.<br /> <br /> 9i. Zena Withers Volfer with a 1m Become the Hammer (0/4m).<br /> Volfer defends with a Full Excellency, Parry 8 (13/11m, 3a).<br /> Zena rolls 7 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> 8i. Volfer Withers Zena with a 6m Excellency, Excellent Strike, Fire and Stones Strike, Willpower (0/10m, 3WP) for 15d+2.<br /> Zena defends with a 4m Excellency and Willpower (0/0m, 5WP), Parry 9.<br /> Volfer rolls 10+2 successes, hitting (9i) for 7i. Zena 2i, Volfer 17i.<br /> <br /> Volfer uses One Weapon, Two Blows (0/7m) to Willpower, Excellent Strike, Fire and Stones Strike against Sword (0/0m, 2WP) 9d+2.<br /> Zena defends with Willpower (4WP) for Parry 7.<br /> Volfer rolls 6+2 success, hitting (18i). Volfer rolls 4+4 dice of damage for 3i. Crashing Sword, knocking Zena out of Form. 26i.<br /> <br /> Sword: Crashed<br /> Zena: 2i (0/5m, 4WP, 3a) Water Aura -2 Onslaught<br /> Volfer: 26i (0/5m, 2WP, 3a) 4L (-1)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> Zena's anima deals 0 damage.<br /> <br /> 26i. Volfer launches an Excellent Strike, 2m Excellency, Willpower Decisive (0/0m, 1WP) for 9d+2<br /> Zena defends with a 4m Excellency and Willpower (0/1m, 3WP), Parry 8.<br /> Volfer rolls 6+2 successes, hitting.<br /> Volfer rolls 26i in damage for 12L.<br /> <br /> Zena is dead.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ouch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T11:27:40-08:00","id":1368075,"title":"","content":"Yeah that doesn't look good. What if you used your action to Aim or Full Defense while attacking with the sword? You're not spending a willpower each turn to double attack but you are getting two actions, both of which are normally not able to be flurried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T11:37:16-08:00","id":1368078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368075#post1368075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that doesn't look good. What if you used your action to Aim or Full Defense while attacking with the sword? You're not spending a willpower each turn to double attack but you are getting two actions, both of which are normally not able to be flurried.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was Zena can expend Aura to ignore the Terrestrial keyword literally every round after the first.<br /> <br /> She just didn't survive until the second round and died with Willpower to spare.<br /> <br /> Was a pretty unlucky nova strike though. 2 successes on 13 dice with rerolled 6s is wildly improbably low. 98% of rolls should be better than that. An average roll would have been 7+2L which should have set Volfer firmly in his -2s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-15-2020, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T11:41:18-08:00","id":1368081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368078#post1368078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea was Zena can expend Aura to ignore the Terrestrial keyword literally every round after the first.<br /> <br /> She just didn't survive until the second round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so why start off with the killshot if the goal is to come online in round 2? Rather than ensure that Volfer gets 2 rounds in a row by initiative swapping? Using the Immaculate style to get the full bonus from the form seems like a pretty good strategy there actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T12:17:30-08:00","id":1368090,"title":"","content":"I wonder if this doesn't point to a more general distinction actually. Solars, or dawns particularly, often have the power to boost decisive damage so much that they can afford to just end combats in round 1 before their enemy acts. So doing a big nova alpha Strike works. Dragonblooded might have to engage with the system more.<br /> <br /> That's certainly been the case in the 3 on one fights anyway. Solar ends them in round one, if he doesn't the Dzbs do not likewise have the power to just end the Solar on their turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T13:35:30-08:00","id":1368113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368081#post1368081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, so why start off with the killshot if the goal is to come online in round 2? Rather than ensure that Volfer gets 2 rounds in a row by initiative swapping? Using the Immaculate style to get the full bonus from the form seems like a pretty good strategy there actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thunderclap Rush.<br /> <br /> If Volfer gets to open with a nova, Zena won't recover. If Zena can put Volfer into -2s, then pile two attacks each round that should swing it. At least, that was the plan.<br /> <br /> Let's try that again, using a full defense instead of a nova strike (with +2 Defense, Volfer will have a hard time landing a Decisive so that might just work).<br /> <br /> Zena vs Volfer<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Zena spends 6m and 1 Cult to add four successes to her 11d Join Battle for 13i (13/16m, 1a). She draws Stormcaller, Intensity 0.<br /> Volfer rolls 12d+1 for 6m 1WP (13/27m, 5WP, 1a) for 9i.<br /> Zena wins join battle and rolls Sword into combat at 12i (13/6m, 3a)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 13i. Zena moves to Short and Full Defends (11i), she spends 1m to stay dry in the rain (13/5m).<br /> 12i. Sword falls to 11i.<br /> Zena enters Water Aura.<br /> <br /> 9i. Volfer moves to Close and Withers Sword with a 6m Excellency, Excellent Strike, 5m Fire and Stones Strike with Willpower (13/14m, 4WP, 3a) 14d+2.<br /> Zena defends with Cult and a 4m Excellency, Parry 12 (13/2m, 6+1WP, 3a).<br /> Volfer rolls 7 successes, missing.<br /> Zena uses Gathering Light Concentration to reverse Onslaught (12/0m).<br /> <br /> Zena: 13i (12/5m, 6+1WP, 3a) Water Aura<br /> Sword: 11i<br /> Volfer: 9i (13/19m, 4WP, 3a), -1 Onslaught<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> Zena's anima wither's Volfer for 1i.<br /> <br /> 11i. Sword expends Water Aura to ignore the Terreistral Keyword this tick.<br /> Zena Withers Volfer with Become the Hammer, Cult and Liquid Steel Flow (5/0m, 6WP, 3a).<br /> Volfer Parries with Excellency and Willpower, Parry 9 (13/11m, 3WP, 3a).<br /> Zena rolls 14 successes, hitting threshold 5. She spends Willpower to extend the duration of Liquid Steel Flow (5WP). 12i.<br /> Zena rolls 18 damage, reroll 6s, for 12i. Sword rises to 24i. Volfer falls to -4i, Crash. Sword rises to 29i<br /> <br /> Zena withers Volfer with 4m Become the Hammer and Willpower (1/0m, 4WP, 3a)<br /> Volfer Parries with Excellency and Willpower, Parry 8 (13/3m, 2WP, 3a).<br /> Zena rolls 6 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> Zena enters Water Aura.<br /> <br /> -4i. Volfer Withers Zena with a 6m Excellency, Excellent Strike, 5m Fire and Stones Strike with Willpower (2/0m, 1WP, 3a)<br /> Zena defends on Parry 7.<br /> Volfer rolls 8 successes, hitting. -3i.<br /> Volfer rolls 11 dice of damage for 6i. Volfer 3i. Zena 7i.<br /> <br /> Sword: 29i<br /> Zena: 7i (1/5m, 4WP, 3a) Water Aura<br /> Volfer: 3i (2/5m, 1WP, 3a)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> Zena's anima has no effect.<br /> <br /> 29i: Sword delays to 7i. 27i.<br /> <br /> 7i. Zena expends Water Aura to ignore the Terreistral Keyword this tick.<br /> Zena Withers Volfer with Willpower (1/5m, 3WP, 3a).<br /> Volfer defends on Parry 5.<br /> Zena hits with 6 successes (8i) and withers 6i (14i/-3i).<br /> <br /> Sword Decisives Volfer with a full excellency and Willpower (0/0m, 2WP, 3a).<br /> Volfer defends with Willpower and a 6m Excellency for Parry 8 (1/0m, 0WP, 3a).<br /> Sword rolls 11 successes, hitting.<br /> 3 dice are converted to levels (ending Liquid Steel Flow), and 24i is rolled as damage, re-rolling 6s, for 8L, putting Volfer in his -2s.<br /> Sword resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Zena enters Water Aura.<br /> <br /> 3i. Volfer Withers Sword.<br /> Sword defends with Willpower (1WP) for Parry 8.<br /> Volfer rolls 4 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> Zena: 14i (0/5m, 1WP, 3a) Water Aura<br /> Sword: 3i<br /> Volfer: 3i (1/5m, 0WP, 3a) -2 Wound Penalty (8L)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 4</b><br /> <br /> Zena's anima has no effect.<br /> <br /> 14i. Zena Withers Volfer.<br /> Volfer defends on Parry 3.<br /> Zena rolls 6 successes on 14 dice, hitting with a threshold of 3. 15i.<br /> Zena rolls 9 dice of damage, rerolling 6s, for 5i. Zena 20i. Volfer -2i, Crash. Zena 25i.<br /> <br /> 3i. Zena expends Water Aura.<br /> Sword Withers Volfer.<br /> Volfer defends with Parry 4.<br /> Sword rolls 7 successes on 14 dice, hitting with a threshold of 5.<br /> Sword rolls 13 dice of damage, rerolling 6s, for 6i. Sword rises to 10i. Volfer falls to -8i.<br /> <br /> -8i. Volfer Withers Sword with Excellent Strike and a 3m Excellency (0/0m)<br /> Sword defends on Parry 7.<br /> Volfer rolls 6+1 successes, hitting. -7i.<br /> Volfer rolls 6 dice of damge for 4i. Sword falls 6i. Volfer rises to -3i.<br /> <br /> Zena: 25i (0/10m, 1WP, 3a) Water Aura<br /> Sword: 6i<br /> Volfer: -3i (0/5m, 0WP, 3a) -2 Wound Penalty (8L)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 5</b><br /> <br /> Zena's anima has no effect.<br /> <br /> 25i: Zena launches a 6m Become the Hammer Decisive with Willpower (0/4m, 0WP, 3a) for 17d+1.<br /> Volfer defends with a 4m Excellency, Parry 5.<br /> Zena rolls 7+1 successes, hitting.<br /> Zena rolls 25i rerolling 6s for 11L. 19L total.<br /> <br /> Volfer is dead.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Zena beats Volfer in 5 rounds.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that was a much better strategy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-16-2020, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T15:16:42-08:00","id":1368146,"title":"","content":"Man they run out of resources fast. Using the immaculate ability to extend Liquid Steel Flow to one scene though is galaxy brain level though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T16:13:51-08:00","id":1368163,"title":"","content":"I wonder if I shouldn't run some more arena fights that are less white room. Like for example somebody with Air Dragon or Monkey Leap fighting in the middle of a swamp where disengaging buys you at least two free rounds, but I feel like they'd either end up really one sided if their opponent didn't have a charm to counter it like Thunderbolt Attack Prana, or pointless in the reverse of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T16:54:00-08:00","id":1368171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368163#post1368163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if I shouldn't run some more arena fights that are less white room. Like for example somebody with Air Dragon or Monkey Leap fighting in the middle of a swamp where disengaging buys you at least two free rounds, but I feel like they'd either end up really one sided if their opponent didn't have a charm to counter it like Thunderbolt Attack Prana, or pointless in the reverse of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some other thoughts - maybe one of them will inspire you:<br /> <br /> Fights where one character is trying to protect a noncombat and the other is trying to kill them. (But this might end up as pretty easy with the right defend other-enhancing charms or an alpha strike and pretty hard without it)<br /> <br /> Fights where one character is trying to get past another (but this might end up as an exercise in rush vs. disengage or an alpha strike)<br /> <br /> Fights where the weaker character is just trying to survive a certain number of rounds to be rescued<br /> <br /> Relatedly, fights where a sorcerer with Travel Without Distance is trying to gather enough sorcerous motes to teleport away while surviving a powerful onslaught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T01:25:57-08:00","id":1368243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368163#post1368163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if I shouldn't run some more arena fights that are less white room. Like for example somebody with Air Dragon or Monkey Leap fighting in the middle of a swamp where disengaging buys you at least two free rounds, but I feel like they'd either end up really one sided if their opponent didn't have a charm to counter it like Thunderbolt Attack Prana, or pointless in the reverse of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>These fights work great in play (and in fiction, like the Wizard's Duel from Princess Bride), but less so in a one-off.<br /> <br /> Either the fighters are both built for it, or they aren't.<br /> <br /> It is good for test builds though. Like if you want to put a character that you want to use in play through their paces, you could post them here and we'd all put them through a ringer.<br /> <br /> It'd have to be characters intended for play though: less Ragara Smash, more Death Kitty.<br /> <br /> But Zena the Single Point DB is a pretty good NPC for such a challenge -- how well do you fight in a demonic thunderstorm?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368146#post1368146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man they run out of resources fast. Using the immaculate ability to extend Liquid Steel Flow to one scene though is galaxy brain level though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could play conservatively -- Volfer trying not to flare, Zena saving motes (until she reveals she's not left handed). But I feel that an Exalted level threat is one you go all in on.<br /> <br /> If conserving motes, my money is firmly on Zena winning -- her base stats are higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-16-2020, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T03:38:19-08:00","id":1368276,"title":"","content":"My take away from the last two pages is that Volfer sucks. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> , what does this mean?<br /> <i>13i. Zena moves to Short and Full Defends, <b>she spends 1m to stay dry in the rain</b> (13/5m).</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T05:43:50-08:00","id":1368286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368276#post1368276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take away from the last two pages is that Volfer sucks. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> , what does this mean?<br /> <i>13i. Zena moves to Short and Full Defends, <b>she spends 1m to stay dry in the rain</b> (13/5m).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Drawing Stormcaller starts a rainstorm.<br /> Water Aspect DBs can spend 1m to perform a minor manipulation of water -- like staying dry in a rainstorm -- as an Anima power.<br /> If a DB only spends motes on their Anima on their turn, they enter an Aura state that matches their Aspect.<br /> Zena can expend her Water Aura to ignore the Terrestrial keyword on her Martial Arts Charms for one Tick because she knows Water Dragon Form.<br /> <br /> And Volfer... is a standard published NPC.<br /> <br /> Pick literally any published Essence 1 NPC. Volfer will amost certainly trounce them (maybe not Faka Kun). There's a reason I use the signature Dawn for benchmarking, but I'm happy to switch to the Young Dynast or a Blood Ape or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-16-2020, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T05:52:31-08:00","id":1368289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368286#post1368286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drawing Stormcaller starts a rainstorm.<br /> Water Aspect DBs can spend 1m to perform a minor manipulation of water -- like staying dry in a rainstorm -- as an Anima power.<br /> If a DB only spends motes on their Anima on their turn, they enter an Aura state that matches their Aspect.<br /> Zena can expend her Water Aura to ignore the Terrestrial keyword on her Martial Arts Charms for one Tick because she knows Water Dragon Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do people think of these things holy shit. Then again I don't really care about DBs so thats on me for not knowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T06:14:08-08:00","id":1368291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368289#post1368289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do people think of these things holy shit. Then again I don't really care about DBs so thats on me for not knowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been accused in the past of using edge case mechanics in Exalted to give the characters I make an advantage that people who don't study the rules won't get.<br /> <br /> What my naysayers don't understand is Exalted is explicitly a system that Rewards System Mastery and is full of such edge cases, such that building a character around them (including the Character Creation bp game) is at least 50% more effective (in my estimation) at what you aim towards than just picking &quot;cool stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, just try explaining this to people who want to play Fashion-xalted. I'm sure once Essence is out, their pique will be sated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-16-2020, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T19:30:24-08:00","id":1368449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368276#post1368276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take away from the last two pages is that Volfer sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Volfer is suboptimal, but that doesn't make him suck. If you bring him up to chargen levels of charms and merits and stuff he can kill pretty much anything in Creation, and that's just being an average Dawn. Zena is not an average Dynast, she's like the deadly prodigy that's been the top 1% of all her combat classes her whole life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T21:35:01-08:00","id":1368458,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Opening everyone uses a full excellency, except BBEG, Dawn and Night, who use Awakening Eye<br /> <br /> <br /> BBEG 13i 70m 9wp<br /> Dawn 12i 35m 9wp<br /> Night 12i 40m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 35m 5wp<br /> Twilight 17i 35m 5wp<br /> Eclipse 15i 35m 5wp<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==============<br /> BBEG reflexively uses Steel Faster than Thought 3 times, spending 20m, 6i, 2wp.<br /> <br /> BBEG 7i 50m 7wp<br /> BBEG2 14i<br /> BBEG3 11i<br /> BBEG4 11i<br /> Dawn 12i 35m 9wp<br /> Night 12i 40m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 35m 5wp<br /> Twilight 17i 35m 5wp<br /> Eclipse 15i 35m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Twilight starts things off trying to wither BBEG down using a 3m Excellent Strike, 8m Full Excellency and 3m Fire and Stones strike, and a willpower. BBEG defends with a 5m Bulwark Stance and 6m Iron Kettle Body.<br /> <br /> 24+1 dice are rolled against a defense of 8. Rolling 14 with six 1s, and those becoming another 3 successes for a total of 17. BBEG will use Spirit Strengthen's the Skin to raise soak by 5 for 5m, and spend 1i to use Essence Gathering Temper.<br /> <br /> Rolling 7 damage Twilight deals 5.<br /> <br /> BBEG 1i 44m 7wp<br /> BBEG2 14i<br /> BBEG3 11i<br /> BBEG4 11i<br /> Dawn 12i 35m 9wp<br /> Night 12i 40m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 35m 5wp<br /> Twilight 23i 21m 4wp<br /> Eclipse 15i 35m 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Twilight will activate 1m 1wp Peony Blossom attack to do the same withering to BBEG2.<br /> <br /> Rolling 24+1 dice for 14 with two 1s, rolling no extra help. BBEG will spend 3m to soak it down to 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 5 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> BBEG 1i 44m 7wp<br /> BBEG2 11i<br /> BBEG3 11i<br /> BBEG4 11i<br /> Dawn 12i 35m 9wp<br /> Night 12i 40m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 35m 5wp<br /> Twilight 27i 6m 2wp<br /> Eclipse 15i 35m 5wp<br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> Eclipse acts, withering BBEG with 1m Ferocious Jab, 10m full excellency and willpower.<br /> <br /> Rolling 28 dice against a defense of 8 for 19 total. BBEG will reduce the damage by 5 for 5m.<br /> <br /> Eclipse rolls 7 dice for 3, crashing BBEG.<br /> <br /> BBEG -2i 39m 7wp<br /> BBEG2 11i<br /> BBEG3 11i<br /> BBEG4 11i<br /> Dawn 12i 35m 9wp<br /> Night 12i 40m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 35m 5wp<br /> Twilight 27i 6m 2wp<br /> Eclipse 19i 24m 4wp<br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> Dawn goes, and activates 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn. Supplementing with 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana, 1m Divine Executioner Strike, 3m Excellent Strike, 1m 1i Gleaming Sever, and 3m Fire and Stones Strike. Fueling each attack with an additional 2m for a full excellency.<br /> <br /> BBEG will use 3m Durability of Oak.<br /> <br /> Dividing Damage thusly: 9/9/9/9/10<br /> <br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 15, rerolling two 1s for 17. Then rolling 10 damage for 2, doubling to 4.<br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 10, rerolling three 1s for 11. Then rolling 10 damage for 2, doubling to 4.<br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 9, rerolling one 1s for 11. Then rolling 10 damage for 4, doubling to 8.<br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 10, rerolling two 1s for 11. Then rolling 10 damage for 4, doubling to 8.<br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 11, rerolling two 1s for 11. Then rolling 11 damage for 4, doubling to 8.<br /> <br /> <br /> BBEG -2i 36m 7wp Damage: 32L<br /> BBEG2 11i<br /> BBEG3 11i<br /> BBEG4 11i<br /> Dawn 5i 11m 7wp<br /> Night 12i 40m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 35m 5wp<br /> Twilight 27i 6m 2wp<br /> Eclipse 19i 24m 4wp<br /> <br /> Dawn uses 1m 1wp to Peony Blossom Technique BBEG2 with a Withering Strike. Also using a 3m Excellent Strike and 1m Divine Executioner Stance. Rolling 20+1 dice against a parry of 8 for 14 total. BBEG will spend 2m to lower the damage by 2.<br /> <br /> Dawn rolls 5 for 2 damage.<br /> <br /> BBEG -2i 34m 7wp Damage: 32L<br /> BBEG2 9i<br /> BBEG3 11i<br /> BBEG4 11i<br /> Dawn 8i 6m 7wp<br /> Night 12i 40m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 35m 5wp<br /> Twilight 27i 6m 2wp<br /> Eclipse 19i 24m 4wp<br /> -------------------<br /> Night Withers BBEG2 using 3m Excellent Strike, 5m Fire and Stones Strike, and 8m full excellency. Rolling 24+1 dice against a parry of 8 for 13, rerolling 4 1s for 15. BBEG pays 3m to lower it to 5 damage.<br /> <br /> Rolling 5 for 2<br /> <br /> BBEG -2i 31m 7wp Damage: 32L<br /> BBEG2 7i<br /> BBEG3 11i<br /> BBEG4 11i<br /> Dawn 8i 6m 7wp<br /> Night 15i 24m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 35m 5wp<br /> Twilight 27i 6m 2wp<br /> Eclipse 19i 24m 4wp<br /> -------------------<br /> Zenith orders the Tyrant Lizard into battle with 4m Familiar Honing Instruction, 3m Ambush Predator Style, relfexively activating 15m 1wp Deadly Predator Method. Rolling in the Tyrant Lizard using 16 dice, cascading due to Ambush Predator Style for 15i.<br /> <br /> <br /> BBEG -2i 31m 7wp Damage: 32L<br /> BBEG2 7i<br /> BBEG3 11i<br /> BBEG4 11i<br /> Dawn 8i 6m 7wp<br /> Night 15i 24m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 13m 4wp<br /> Twilight 27i 6m 2wp<br /> Eclipse 19i 24m 4wp<br /> Tyrant Lizard 15i<br /> <br /> Tyrant Lizard acts immidiately, Zenith orders it to Decisive Bite, it will spend a willpower. BBEG will defend with 3m Durability of Oak.<br /> <br /> Rolling 14+3 the lizard will miss with only 7 the decisive attack.<br /> -------------------<br /> BBEG 3 goes, using 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn, augmented by 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana, 1m Divine Executioner Strike, 1m 1i Gleaming Sever, 3m Excellent Strike, 5m Fire and Stones Strike. Using 2m on each attack to bring it up to full excellency.<br /> <br /> Dividing damage up thusly: 8/8/8/8/8<br /> <br /> <br /> Rolling 17+2 dice against defense of 8 for 9, rerolling two 1s for 9. The one bonus damage is unable to overcome hardness, but Gleaming Sever rolls one anyway for 1.<br /> <br /> Rolling 17+2 dice against defense of 7 for 10, rerolling two 1s for 11. Then rolling 11 decisive for 4 which becomes 8.<br /> <br /> Rolling 17+2 dice against defense of 6 for 10, rerolling one 1s for 10. Then rolling 12 decisive for 6 which becomes 12, killing the Dawn.<br /> <br /> Rolling 17+2 dice against defense of 8 for 11, rerolling three 1s for 11. Then rolling 12 decisive for 4 which becomes 8, on the twilight.<br /> <br /> Rolling 17+2 dice against defense of 7 for 9, rerolling two 1s for 12. Then rolling 13 decisive for 4 which becomes 8, killing the twilight.<br /> <br /> <br /> BBEG -2i 2m 5wp Damage: 32L<br /> BBEG2 6i<br /> BBEG3 6i<br /> BBEG4 6i<br /> Night 15i 24m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 13m 4wp<br /> Eclipse 19i 24m 4wp<br /> Tyrant Lizard 15i<br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> BBEG 4 rolls a withering attack against Eclipse, rolling 14 dice against a defense of 7, getting it with 9, then rolling 5 damage for 2<br /> <br /> BBEG -2i 2m 5wp Damage: 32L<br /> BBEG2 6i<br /> BBEG3 6i<br /> BBEG4 9i<br /> Night 15i 24m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 13m 4wp<br /> Eclipse 17i 24m 4wp<br /> Tyrant Lizard 15i<br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> BBEG 2 rolls a withering attack against Eclipse, rolling 14 dice against a defense of 6, getting it with 6, then rolling 5 damage for 2<br /> <br /> BBEG -2i 2m 5wp Damage: 32L<br /> BBEG2 9i<br /> BBEG3 6i<br /> BBEG4 9i<br /> Night 15i 24m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 13m 4wp<br /> Eclipse 15i 24m 4wp<br /> Tyrant Lizard 15i<br /> -------------------<br /> BBEG rolls a withering attack against Eclipse, who will defend with 2m Dipping Swallow. Hitting with 8 and rolling 5 damage for 2, not quite pulling out of crash.<br /> <br /> BBEG 0i 2m 5wp Damage: 32L<br /> BBEG2 9i<br /> BBEG3 6i<br /> BBEG4 9i<br /> Night 15i 24m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 13m 4wp<br /> Eclipse 13i 24m 4wp<br /> Tyrant Lizard 15i<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ============================<br /> BBEG 0i 7m 5wp Damage: 32L<br /> BBEG2 9i<br /> BBEG3 6i<br /> BBEG4 9i<br /> Night 15i 29m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 18m 4wp<br /> Eclipse 13i 29m 4wp<br /> Tyrant Lizard 15i<br /> <br /> Night will launch a decisive attack on BBEG with 3m Excellent Strike, 3m Fire and Stones Strike, 8m Full Excellency. BBEG will defend with 2m Dipping Swallow.<br /> <br /> Night rolls 21+1 dice against parry 8, getting it with 13 after rerolls. Then rolling 18 decisive damage for 5<br /> <br /> BBEG 0i 5m 5wp Damage: 37L<br /> BBEG2 9i<br /> BBEG3 6i<br /> BBEG4 9i<br /> Night 15i 29m 9wp<br /> Zenith 12i 18m 4wp<br /> Eclipse 13i 29m 4wp<br /> Tyrant Lizard 15i<br /> -------------------<br /> Tyrant Lizard waits for the zenith order.<br /> ------------------<br /> Eclipse will decisive BBEG, using a 10m full excellency, 1m ferocious jab. BBEG will defend with 2m dipping swallow. Rolling 23 dice against parry 8 for 12 and hitting, then rolling 14 damage for 4, killing BBEG.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I had to make up some stuff on the fly, like letting the BBEG launch decisive attacks even while crashed and giving him 40 health levels but this is how it turned out. Due to the magic of Solar melee two Solars died before BBEG ran out of motes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T21:43:29-08:00","id":1368460,"title":"","content":"Also Divine Executioner Stance is probably dumb on the level of Thunderbolt Attack Prana. 1m for +4 to attack and damage, combo-able with IFotD should probably not be in the game.<br /> <br /> I also realize two other things, the multi initiative track is both not nearly enough and way too good. Not nearly enough because you\u2019re still losing to that Dawn alpha strike, but also way too good because you\u2019re basically making one Essence 5 Solar into five Essence 5 Solars. So all the defensive charms and stuff they use apply to all tracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-17-2020, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:32:33-08:00","id":1368478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368458#post1368458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dawn goes, and activates 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn. Supplementing with 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana, 1m Divine Executioner Strike, 3m Excellent Strike, 1m 1i Gleaming Sever, and 3m Fire and Stones Strike. Fueling each attack with an additional 2m for a full excellency.<br /> <br /> BBEG will use 3m Durability of Oak.<br /> <br /> Dividing Damage thusly: 9/9/9/9/10<br /> <br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 15, rerolling two 1s for 17. Then rolling 10 damage for 2, doubling to 4.<br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 10, rerolling three 1s for 11. Then rolling 10 damage for 2, doubling to 4.<br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 9, rerolling one 1s for 11. Then rolling 10 damage for 4, doubling to 8.<br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 10, rerolling two 1s for 11. Then rolling 10 damage for 4, doubling to 8.<br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice against defense of 8 for 11, rerolling two 1s for 11. Then rolling 11 damage for 4, doubling to 8.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure this is not rules-legal. TAP enhances an attack made against an opponent at another range band. You move into close on the first attack, dealing double damage, then it does nothing on the rest of the flurry because the target is in the same range band you occupy.<br /> <br /> (If you had two opponents in two different range bands, you could use the reflexive movement granted by Invincible Fury of the Dawn to zig-zag between them and do double damage against each.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:38:46-08:00","id":1368480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368478#post1368478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure this is not rules-legal. TAP enhances an attack made against an opponent at another range band. You move into close on the first attack, dealing double damage, then it does nothing on the rest of the flurry because the target is in the same range band you occupy.<br /> <br /> (If you had two opponents in two different range bands, you could use the reflexive movement granted by Invincible Fury of the Dawn to zig-zag between them and do double damage against each.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Invincible Fury of the Dawn gives you a reflexive, uncontested movement before or after every attack. Retreat out to Short and then TAP back in to close every time. I advocate for TAP to be a simple charm.<br /> <br /> It's also a debatably inaccurate reading of TAP anyway. It seems to imply that you can use it without moving if you want to, but either way the rules allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-17-2020, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:58:24-08:00","id":1368483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368480#post1368480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Invincible Fury of the Dawn gives you a reflexive, uncontested movement before or after every attack. Retreat out to Short and then TAP back in to close every time. I advocate for TAP to be a simple charm.<br /> <br /> It's also a debatably inaccurate reading of TAP anyway. It seems to imply that you can use it without moving if you want to, but either way the rules allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The language seems fairly unambiguous to me?<br /> <br /> IFoD says &quot;[the Solar] may move a single range band <b>to make </b>each attack&quot;, implying you don't get to move unless that move enables you to make the attack you want to make, and TAP says it &quot;supplements a nonranged attack which can be made against aerial targets up to short range, or ground targets <b>at another range band</b>&quot;.<br /> <br /> The system has enough ambiguity that you <i>can </i>interpret the Charms as more powerful than the strictest RAW reading would imply, but why would you want to, when all it does is cause more balance concerns?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T01:02:48-08:00","id":1368484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368483#post1368483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The language seems fairly unambiguous to me?<br /> <br /> IFoD says &quot;[the Solar] may move a single range band <b>to make </b>each attack&quot;, implying you don't get to move unless that move enables you to make the attack you want to make, and TAP says it &quot;supplements a nonranged attack which can be made against aerial targets up to short range, or ground targets <b>at another range band</b>&quot;.<br /> <br /> The system has enough ambiguity that you <i>can </i>interpret the Charms as more powerful than the strictest RAW reading would imply, but why would you want to, when all it does is cause more balance concerns?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems unambiguous to me too, but the other way around. <br /> Thanks, natural language!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T01:26:47-08:00","id":1368487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368483#post1368483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The language seems fairly unambiguous to me?<br /> <br /> IFoD says &amp;quot;[the Solar] may move a single range band <b>to make </b>each attack&amp;quot;, implying you don't get to move unless that move enables you to make the attack you want to make, and TAP says it &amp;quot;supplements a nonranged attack which can be made against aerial targets up to short range, or ground targets <b>at another range band</b>&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> The system has enough ambiguity that you <i>can </i>interpret the Charms as more powerful than the strictest RAW reading would imply, but why would you want to, when all it does is cause more balance concerns?</div> </div> </div> </div>But moving does enable you to make the attack you want to make. You want to use TAP but can't from where you are, so you've got to move out to jump back in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T01:32:57-08:00","id":1368490,"title":"","content":"Actually you may be right. TAP counts as your movement action for the round if you use it to move a range band, so it may be that you can\u2019t use it more than once per round?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T01:47:08-08:00","id":1368491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368490#post1368490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually you may be right. TAP counts as your movement action for the round if you use it to move a range band, so it may be that you can\u2019t use it more than once per round?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a valid reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T06:21:02-08:00","id":1368520,"title":"","content":"First of all: thank you! I really appreciate it. Have a good luck with the midterm! (Or may your students have it, depending on what's your role.)<br /> <br /> Second, I'll have to change the wording of Steel Faster than Thought. My intent was that you are not crashed as long as you have some tracks open. When one track would go into negative it simply disappears and has to be reopen using Initiative (so there is no difference in how &quot;Track 0&quot; and the rest of tracks work).<br /> <br /> The third thing is that this fight really revealed to me how powerful is Solar alpha-strike. It seems that Solars have much better offensive alpha strike than the ways to prevent it. The only charm I know that is really good against alpha strikes is that one in Occult which lets you survive incapacitation, combined with the Resistance charm reflexively creating health levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T09:55:09-08:00","id":1368553,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1368551#post1368551\">Well, the devs have spoken.</a> The movement in Thunderbolt Attack Prana <i>is not</i> optional.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-17-2020, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T10:06:07-08:00","id":1368560,"title":"","content":"It's a very powerful charm, so that seems fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T10:06:11-08:00","id":1368561,"title":"","content":"But if you are at melee range with someone and wishes to attack someone at short range with TAP you dont need to disengage right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T10:10:08-08:00","id":1368562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368561#post1368561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you are at melee range with someone and wishes to attack someone at short range with TAP you dont need to disengage right?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1316114#post1316114\">Correct.</a><br /> <br /> Charms which move you, move you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1103570#post1103570\">Additional referrence.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1091357#post1091357\">Additional additional referrence.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-17-2020, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T11:11:32-08:00","id":1368583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368520#post1368520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all: thank you! I really appreciate it. Have a good luck with the midterm! (Or may your students have it, depending on what's your role.)<br /> <br /> Second, I'll have to change the wording of Steel Faster than Thought. My intent was that you are not crashed as long as you have some tracks open. When one track would go into negative it simply disappears and has to be reopen using Initiative (so there is no difference in how &quot;Track 0&quot; and the rest of tracks work).<br /> <br /> The third thing is that this fight really revealed to me how powerful is Solar alpha-strike. It seems that Solars have much better offensive alpha strike than the ways to prevent it. The only charm I know that is really good against alpha strikes is that one in Occult which lets you survive incapacitation, combined with the Resistance charm reflexively creating health levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're also probably going to want to find some way of dealing with the fact that whenever the BBEG activates a scene-long or turn-long charm it affects every initiative track. So for example Fivefold Bulwark Stance, or Aegis of Invincible Might, or even like Iron Kettle Body or something.<br /> <br /> Already enemies with high defense, penalty negators, damage mitigation and high soak are a really annoying thing to fight. The last thing you need is to make that one enemy into four. The simple fact of it is even if it's balanced it's just not fun.<br /> <br /> I might look to something like the actual published boss monster the Volcanic Earthwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T11:35:46-08:00","id":1368592,"title":"","content":"Is there already a good fight in this thread that demonstrates how well Legendary Size helps in the whole single opponent discussion? I've been keeping up with the thread off and on for awhile, but it has been quite some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T11:39:08-08:00","id":1368594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368592#post1368592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there already a good fight in this thread that demonstrates how well Legendary Size helps in the whole single opponent discussion? I've been keeping up with the thread off and on for awhile, but it has been quite some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you have in mind?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena/page34\">We had a Legendary Size Tyrant Lizard vs 4 Claw Striders.</a> The Striders won.<br /> <br /> We also had <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena/page5\">a Dragon-Blooded</a> vs Tyrant Lizard. Deeb won.<br /> <br /> You want Warstrider fights? Essence 5 Solar with Legendary Size fights? Or what? What's the ask here?<br /> <br /> In general:<br /> 1. Multiple little things beat one big thing.<br /> 2. Being big is no substitute for kewl powaz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-17-2020, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T13:13:52-08:00","id":1368624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368594#post1368594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you have in mind?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena/page34\">We had a Legendary Size Tyrant Lizard vs 4 Claw Striders.</a> The Striders won.<br /> <br /> We also had <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena/page5\">a Dragon-Blooded</a> vs Tyrant Lizard. Deeb won.<br /> <br /> You want Warstrider fights? Essence 5 Solar with Legendary Size fights? Or what? What's the ask here?<br /> <br /> In general:<br /> 1. Multiple little things beat one big thing.<br /> 2. Being big is no substitute for kewl powaz.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, that just about answers that, and I just realized from catching up on the 5 on 1 thread that the BBEG that the good Dr was running was Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> Although now that you mention it, kinda surprised that there hasn't been a Warstrider Fight yet.<br /> <br /> I would never be so gauche as to ask for a fight, but if the idea piques your interest, I wouldn't mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T13:31:02-08:00","id":1368631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368624#post1368624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, that just about answers that, and I just realized from catching up on the 5 on 1 thread that the BBEG that the good Dr was running was Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> Although now that you mention it, kinda surprised that there hasn't been a Warstrider Fight yet.<br /> <br /> I would never be so gauche as to ask for a fight, but if the idea piques your interest, I wouldn't mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legendary size definitely helps a lot. A legendary size creature with a lot of soak is next to impossible to crash, the built in onslaught penalty negation is a saviour, and the cap on decisive damage makes decisive gains it hard. The next fight I Run might be against Mahicara just to show the difference between one big Exalted enemy and an actual boss monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T17:21:58-08:00","id":1368643,"title":"","content":"Hmm, could High Ess Lunar Elder who actually uses Legendary Size (as opposed to the LFATG Elders) but everything according to the rules actually be a credible boss fight for a Solar Circle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T17:28:03-08:00","id":1368646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368643#post1368643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, could High Ess Lunar Elder who actually uses Legendary Size (as opposed to the LFATG Elders) but everything according to the rules actually be a credible boss fight for a Solar Circle?</div> </div> </div> </div>This came up in the other thread but &quot;A circle of Solars&quot; is way, way way too broad to make any kind of statement about. A Legendary Size Lunar Elder could either destroy them in a handful of turns, maybe even 1-2, or get beaten down by them just as quickly. It's entirely possible for a circle to include two Dawns, and every non-Dawn to take every possible combat advantage first, and then whatever their caste specialty is second....or the Dawn could be super well rounded and everyone else dipping 1-3 dots into combat abilities if that.<br /> <br /> Allow me to illustrate, just to make it super clear. Could you fight<a href=\"https://otterlover58.files.wordpress.com/2015/03/old_women.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> five people</a> at once? That's <a href=\"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/i/pix/2013/04/16/article-0-19519999000005DC-893_634x419.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">five people</a> at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-17-2020, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T17:46:36-08:00","id":1368651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368646#post1368646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This came up in the other thread but &amp;quot;A circle of Solars&amp;quot; is way, way way too broad to make any kind of statement about. A Legendary Size Lunar Elder could either destroy them in a handful of turns, maybe even 1-2, or get beaten down by them just as quickly. It's entirely possible for a circle to include two Dawns, and every non-Dawn to take every possible combat advantage first, and then whatever their caste specialty is second....or the Dawn could be super well rounded and everyone else dipping 1-3 dots into combat abilities if that.<br /> <br /> Allow me to illustrate, just to make it super clear. Could you fight<a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://otterlover58.files.wordpress.com/2015/03/old_women.jpg&amp;quot;]</a> five people[/URL] at once? That's <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.dailymail.co.uk/i/pix/2013/04/16/article-0-19519999000005DC-893_634x419.jpg&amp;quot;]five</a> people[/URL] at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those grandmas look tough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T17:54:35-08:00","id":1368652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368651#post1368651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those grandmas look tough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wha? Yeah they're the hard fight, what did you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T05:10:08-08:00","id":1368714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368291#post1368291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been accused in the past of using edge case mechanics in Exalted to give the characters I make an advantage that people who don't study the rules won't get.<br /> <br /> What my naysayers don't understand is Exalted is explicitly a system that Rewards System Mastery and is full of such edge cases, such that building a character around them (including the Character Creation bp game) is at least 50% more effective (in my estimation) at what you aim towards than just picking &quot;cool stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, just try explaining this to people who want to play Fashion-xalted. I'm sure once Essence is out, their pique will be sated.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Okay, so this post got flagged so I'm going to take this opertunity to nip something in the bud and establish a precident.<br /> <br /> The last line is pretty condescending towards people who are excited about Exalted: Essence and might be crossing into edition war territory if we had some solid previews. Right now it's a grey area due to the lack of a preview, but could everyone please keep that in mind going forward?<br /> <br /> Thanks. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T06:11:28-08:00","id":1368727,"title":"","content":"Upon further inspection of Mahicara, I might have to go over how I statted up this Solar circle before they fight. This Solar circle is all dedicated towards combat, but Mahicara has a bunch of ways around that. If the Dawn uses IFotD on its torso he\u2019s probably just going to end up killing everyone including himself. Also with everyone in heavy armor and not investing much into dodge because of that the shockwave from the fist and stomp attacks is basically going to hit everyone every time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T16:16:27-08:00","id":1369045,"title":"","content":"I tried again with Mahicara. So they have stats that look something like this<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Fists 16 Accuracy 13/3 damage<br /> Swords 14 Accuracy 17/5 damage, 15 for non-dedicated combatants<br /> <br /> Motepools 45<br /> <br /> Soak 16/10, 14 for non-dedicated combatants<br /> <br /> Everyone has:<br /> <br /> Physical Stats 3/5/3, except the Night and Dawn who have 5/5/5<br /> <br /> <br /> 5 Awareness (Applicable specialty)<br /> 5 Brawl/Melee (Applicable specialty)<br /> 3 Athletics<br /> 3 Dodge (Applicable specialty)<br /> 3 Resistance (Dawn and Night have 5)<br /> <br /> <br /> Roughly 10 combat charms each, except the Dawn who has closer to 20<br /> <br /> <br /> -0x1<br /> -1x5<br /> -2x8<br /> -4<br /> I<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And the fight went like this<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Opening everyone uses a full excellency, Dawn and Night, who use Awakening Eye<br /> <br /> <br /> Mahicara 8i 90m 8wp<br /> Dawn 10i 40m 9wp<br /> Night 10i 40m 9wp<br /> Zenith 11i 35m 5wp<br /> Twilight 16i 35m 5wp<br /> Eclipse 8i 35m 5wp<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> Twilight will attack Mahicara's arm with a decisive attack, spending 3m Excellent Strike, 3m Fire and Stones Strike, and 8m Excellency. Rolling 21+1 dice for a total of 9 and hitting. Then rolling 19i for 7L, but capped at 6 due to Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> Molten Core activates, all spend until they have 10 dice to resist<br /> <br /> Dawn rolls 5 and passes<br /> Night rolls 5 and passes<br /> Zenith rolls 7 and passes<br /> Twilight rolls 4 and passes<br /> Eclipse rolls 1 and fails, and takes 2 L damage<br /> <br /> Mahicara 8i 90m 8wp 6L to left arm<br /> Dawn 10i 38m 9wp<br /> Night 10i 38m 9wp<br /> Zenith 11i 31m 5wp<br /> Twilight 3i 17m 5wp<br /> Eclipse 8i 31m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Zenith orders the Tyrant Lizard into battle with 4m Familiar Honing Instruction, 3m Ambush Predator Style, relfexively activating 15m 1wp Deadly Predator Method. Rolling in the Tyrant Lizard using 16 dice, cascading due to Ambush Predator Style for 17i.<br /> <br /> T-Lizard goes right away and attempts a decisive Ferocious Bite to the left arm. Rolling 11+2 