0m 5wp 6L(-1s) 7 rounds of control<br /> Twilight 6i 1m 5wp 5L(-1s)<br /> Eclipse 3i 0m 5wp 6L(-1s) 10 rounds of control<br /> T-Lizard -12i 9L(-1s)<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ===========<br /> Mahicara 28i 79m 6wp (Destroyed left arm+7/Destroyed left leg+2)<br /> Dawn 4i 6m 9wp 5L(-1s)<br /> Night 8i 11m 9wp 6L(-1s)<br /> Zenith 12i 5m 5wp 6L(-1s) 7 rounds of control<br /> Twilight 6i 6m 5wp 5L(-1s)<br /> Eclipse 3i 5m 5wp 6L(-1s) 10 rounds of control<br /> T-Lizard -12i 9L(-1s)<br /> <br /> <br /> Mahicara reactivates Unleashing the Flow for 9m 2i<br /> <br /> <br /> Everyone tests against Unleashing the Flow, Everybody spends what they can to up their resistance roll.<br /> <br /> Dawn rolls 7 and passes<br /> Night rolls 8 and passes<br /> Zenith rolls 3 and fails, taking 1L<br /> Twilight rolls 6 and passes<br /> Eclipse rolls 6 and passes<br /> T-Lizard rolls 5 and passes<br /> <br /> Mahicara 26i 70m 6wp (Destroyed left arm+7/Destroyed left leg+2)<br /> Dawn 4i 0m 9wp 5L(-1s)<br /> Night 8i 5m 9wp 6L(-1s)<br /> Zenith 12i 0m 5wp 7L(-2s) 7 rounds of control<br /> Twilight 6i 0m 5wp 5L(-1s)<br /> Eclipse 3i 0m 5wp 6L(-1s) 10 rounds of control<br /> T-Lizard -12i 9L(-1s)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> After that I've just decided not to keep running it. I'm not even really 100% sure who's eventually going to win that but it looks to me like Mahicara might actually take it. I was kind of stuck here. Do I keep boosting the resistance rolls to resist the magma, and blow out all my motes? Or do I just keep letting myself take a ton of lethal damage and keep my motes for attacking?<br /> <br /> I also stopped there because I wasn't sure how to rule multiple grapples, especially reflexive ones. Do you get to take an action to savage when you initiate a reflexive grapple? The rules say on every turn, including one you initiate you MUST choose one of those options? Also can a character grapple multiple opponents without a charm? Does it even matter because Mahicara is a fucking MILE tall, and has plenty of fissures in its skin to spare?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T14:34:28-08:00","id":1369205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369045#post1369045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also stopped there because I wasn't sure how to rule multiple grapples, especially reflexive ones. Do you get to take an action to savage when you initiate a reflexive grapple?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so; it's part of the grapple. However, in this case, maybe the environmental damage is instead? I'd probably rule that they are restrained instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also can a character grapple multiple opponents without a charm? Does it even matter because Mahicara is a fucking MILE tall, and has plenty of fissures in its skin to spare? </div> </div> </div>You can't, because there are some charms and merits that allow you to do so, which Mahicara doesn't have. But it does make sense that it could fit multiple people in its fissures.<br /> <br /> It looks to me like the main issue in that fight was all the environmental damage. So I'm guessing (and not asking you to run this!) that long-range archery builds and people with survival charms for resisting environmental damage are the way to go when fighting this thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a different subject; as you guys run a lot of complicated fights, can I ask your advice? Tomorrow, I'm going to write up 6 Solar NPCs for Sunday's game; a Dawn barbarian general, a Zenith sorceress who uses the armour spell, an athletic Night with a sword (but his combat charms are mostly Night stuff), a Twilight with Archery and a demonic gun-thing, a Dawn with a magic throwing hammer (am I remembering right that artefact thrown weapons fly back to you?) who uses Thrown and Melee, and an Eclipse doctor/shaman. They're very mixed in combat ability.<br /> <br /> Anyway, running six NPCs is very complicated. Especially as there's likely to be other NPCs in the fight (the PCs can choose to side with the Solars against some Dragonblood and the Elemental Dragon of Air, or they can side with Mela and the Dragonblood against the Solars).<br /> So I want to keep them pretty simple to run.<br /> I'm thinking mostly ox-bodies for defence, so I don't have to keep track of charms, but also the Pain Resistance merit, and maybe give the Melee-ists an overwhelming negator so I don't have to remember that penalty either. And avoid dice tricks.<br /> Any advice?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T14:53:50-08:00","id":1369208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369205#post1369205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks to me like the main issue in that fight was all the environmental damage. So I'm guessing (and not asking you to run this!) that long-range archery builds and people with survival charms for resisting environmental damage are the way to go when fighting this thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the survival/resistance charms to resist the environmental damage is a must either way. Long range archery builds might be a way to go, especially if you can't get those charms, but the combat is going to be pretty slow. Solars have some ways to reflexively aim, but they cost a Willpower to use, and if you ever run out of willpower Mahicara gets a chance to catch up, which it's not awful at. It's a small thing but if you're out of motes to oppose it it automatically succeeds at Rushes, but even one excellency mote will negate that. It's definitely not invincible, but trying to take it on without Warstriders and without preparing specifically for fighting it is going to be really hard.<br /> <br /> Supposedly Dragonblooded can beat it, but I don't see it unless everyone has Earth Protection Technique active, with good Stamina and Resistance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369205#post1369205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Run them as QCs first of all, so make no distinctions between withering/decisive attacks, or worry about their specific stats. They're more straightforward to run that way and also more dangerous in spite of lacking charms. Then for the charms they do get pick a couple of the more powerful ones without worrying about their prerequisites, and maybe even boost their strength a bit. Like if they're Solars maybe give them Fire and Stones Strike, Hungry Tiger Technique, Peony Blossom Technique and Bulwark Stance or something.<br /> <br /> Also if it's two massive groups fighting maybe make an assessment and pair off some to fight in the background. If it's Mela, 8 Dragonblooded and the 5 PCs vs 6 Solars, maybe make it so that it's just the PCs and Mela vs 4 of the Solars with the DBs and the other two being assumed to be fighting in the background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T15:02:11-08:00","id":1369210,"title":"","content":"Thrown Artifact weapons (like Skycutters) return to you. They usually may not be used in Melee.<br /> <br /> Melee Artifact weapons (like longfangs) do not return to you. Usually -- you may have Charms like Call the Blade or Evocations which do cause the weapon to return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T15:23:21-08:00","id":1369215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369208#post1369208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if it's two massive groups fighting maybe make an assessment and pair off some to fight in the background. If it's Mela, 8 Dragonblooded and the 5 PCs vs 6 Solars, maybe make it so that it's just the PCs and Mela vs 4 of the Solars with the DBs and the other two being assumed to be fighting in the background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely, I do intend to do that. But I'm not sure what the PCs are going to do. So I want to be ready whatever.<br /> (They're going to try and negotiate first. Negotiating between the Bull of the North and House Tepet Dragonblood probably isn't going to be easy... but you never know, maybe there won't be any fighting!)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T15:33:47-08:00","id":1369218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369208#post1369208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supposedly Dragonblooded can beat [Mahicara], but I don't see it unless everyone has Earth Protection Technique active, with good Stamina and Resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you're running DBs against Mahicara I cannot recommend Sekhem enough, as this is basically what the artifact was designed for. It's an amazing Jade Artifact which directly counters Mahicara in multiple ways (it's ranged, it deals extra damage to fire creatures, and it deals aggravated damage that keeps Mahicara from regenerating mid-fight). Plus the fight against Mahicara is the most epic way to unlock Sekhem's final Evocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 02-20-2020, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T15:54:52-08:00","id":1369224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369205#post1369205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't, because there are some charms and merits that allow you to do so, which Mahicara doesn't have. But it does make sense that it could fit multiple people in its fissures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a perfect example where Storyteller's rule should be applied. If the rules don't make sense in the narrative context, the rules are wrong, the story is right. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T02:02:31-08:00","id":1369307,"title":"","content":"so not to be that guy but uh, what's a Mahicara?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T02:09:43-08:00","id":1369308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369205#post1369205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different subject; as you guys run a lot of complicated fights, can I ask your advice? Tomorrow, I'm going to write up 6 Solar NPCs for Sunday's game; a Dawn barbarian general, a Zenith sorceress who uses the armour spell, an athletic Night with a sword (but his combat charms are mostly Night stuff), a Twilight with Archery and a demonic gun-thing, a Dawn with a magic throwing hammer (am I remembering right that artefact thrown weapons fly back to you?) who uses Thrown and Melee, and an Eclipse doctor/shaman. They're very mixed in combat ability.<br /> <br /> Anyway, running six NPCs is very complicated. Especially as there's likely to be other NPCs in the fight (the PCs can choose to side with the Solars against some Dragonblood and the Elemental Dragon of Air, or they can side with Mela and the Dragonblood against the Solars).<br /> So I want to keep them pretty simple to run.<br /> I'm thinking mostly ox-bodies for defence, so I don't have to keep track of charms, but also the Pain Resistance merit, and maybe give the Melee-ists an overwhelming negator so I don't have to remember that penalty either. And avoid dice tricks.<br /> Any advice?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh boy oh boy this kind of situation is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360253-quicker-quick-characters\">literally why I made a thing</a>.<br /> <br /> The process:<br /> - determine each character's post-attunement mote pools<br /> - divide by 10, note the result as an Effort pool<br /> - add any leftover motes to their Join Battle pool as excellency dice<br /> - for each area of competence, choose a pool from the following: competent - 5 dice, expert - 7 dice, exceptional - 9 dice, legendary - 11 dice<br /> - calculate withering and decisive attack pools plus defenses<br /> - make up three Stances, each worth an expenditure of 5m<br /> - give them a Charm combo for withering attacks, another for decisives, and a third for defense, each worth 10m 1wp chunks. For each 10m 1wp, they cost 1 Effort.<br /> <br /> If you tell me more about what level of combat ability you imagined them being at, I might even write them up for you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T03:20:16-08:00","id":1369315,"title":"","content":"Thanks, but it's okay, I'll write them up. Too many weird specific details that are specific to this game. Nice of you to offer though, but I'm off work until next Thursday, so it'll give me something to do.<br /> <br /> Tbh, I'm not worried about dice pools per-se, I'll probably give a lot of them the same, and I tend to only do about 4-5 dice pools that come up a lot, then any minor random dice pools they need pull out a number that seems fair.<br /> It's more keeping track of various charm effects, penalties, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369307#post1369307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so not to be that guy but uh, what's a Mahicara?</div> </div> </div> </div>A behemoth from Hundred Devils Night Parade. It's like a mile high, made of lava, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T05:57:31-08:00","id":1369346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369307#post1369307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so not to be that guy but uh, what's a Mahicara?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/C8MzC70\" target=\"_blank\">Mahicara</a> the Volcanic Earthwalker lives to travel between the Elemental Poles endlessly. If some insignificant human settlement like say, Nexus or Wu-Jian happens to be on the most direct path between 2 Poles, well, that's on them, maybe they'll build somewhere more sensible next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T06:57:26-08:00","id":1369356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1369346#post1369346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://&quot;https://imgur.com/a/C8MzC70&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Mahicara</a> the Volcanic Earthwalker lives to travel between the Elemental Poles endlessly. If some insignificant human settlement like say, Nexus or Wu-Jian happens to be on the most direct path between 2 Poles, well, that's on them, maybe they'll build somewhere more sensible next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also worth noting that particular piece of art way undersells the size of Mahicara. It\u2019s either a perspective shot with the human way in the foreground, or just inaccurate drawing. If Mahicara were as close to somebody as it appears there it\u2019d be 20-30 times taller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T09:18:39-08:00","id":1370582,"title":"","content":"A very random blast from the past this, apologies if it breaks up the flow of the thread. I really enjoyed aluminiumtrioxid\u2019s sequence of Immaculates fighting Blood Apes as a means of getting to know the various styles (thanks for running those!).<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think Wood Dragon was ever done (possibly for good reason as you\u2019ll see below), and this <i>appalled</i> my entitled sense of completeness, so with some free time I\u2019ve finally taken the liberty of doing it myself. I\u2019m much less practised and proficient at writing these up as concisely/interestingly as I\u2019ve seen aluminiumtrioxid, DrLoveMonkey and JohnDoe244 et al do it, so apologies for wordiness/showing my workings...<br /> <br /> Wood Aspect Immaculate<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3 | Perception 5, Wits 3<br /> Abilities: Wood Dragon 5, Athletics 4, Awareness 4<br /> Mundane light armour, mundane long bow/staff<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> Wood Dragon: Wood Dragon Vitality, Eyes of the Wood Dragon, Mind-Over-Body Meditation, Soul-Marking Style, Wood Dragon Form, Spirit-Wracking Method<br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> Awareness: Precision Observation Method<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique x 2<br /> <br /> Vanilla spread here, with the one exception being pushing perception to 5 to max out Eyes of the Wood Dragon, which will be doing the majority of the lifting in this fight (even if piercing is useless here) along with the Excellency. It means having wits at 3 (and intelligence at 1) so join battle suffers, but that can be mitigated with motes and willpower (and intelligence 1 on a perceptive but not especially quick-witted monk doesn't seem that outrageous...).<br /> <br /> Most of the Wood Dragon charms sadly aren't very useful fighting solo against two Blood Apes. Foregoing an attack to heal (maybe) three health levels with Mind-Over-Body Meditation seems an easy way to commit suicide by Principle of Motion \u2013 this also means reflexively activating the form charm isn't going to happen. It\u2019s probably not worth the motes in any case.<br /> <br /> Soul-Marking Style makes some sense as part of a risky alpha strike (win JB, put an ape into -2s and inflict a crippling injury and gain an aiming bonus) but it's a no go realistically \u2013 sitting with 3i and facing 8 attacks before going again is, well, not great, even if you don\u2019t screw up the damage roll. Spirit-Wracking Method also doesn't look great fighting solo, when building an initiative buffer quickly is key to survival. They both look like charms for when you're fighting something BIG and dangerous with lots of health levels alongside allies, where wound penalties are compounded because they benefit everyone over lots of rounds.<br /> <br /> I toyed with ditching Spirit-Wracking Method and maybe an Ox-Body to buy some archery charms and take advantage of Wood Dragon's long bow/staff combo, but decided against it as the scenario has everyone starting at short range and all abilities other than MA at 4 - I'd either end up playing keep away and not using the Wood Dragon charms I\u2019m supposed to be testing or wasting the archery charms entirely because my dice pools are better if I just wade in. I could have taken advantage of WD's form weapon and picked some complementary Golden Janissary charms, but that's a cop out. We're supposed to be road testing Wood Dragon after all...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">JOIN BATTLE<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon buys two successes with the Excellency (4m) and spends a point of willpower to supplement their 9 dice, yielding 4 further successes for a total of 7.<br /> WD: 10i (13p/27ph, 4wp)<br /> <br /> Blood Ape 1: Rolls 6 dice for 7 successes. Crap.<br /> Ape 1: 10i<br /> <br /> Blood Ape 2: Rolls 6 dice for 3 successes.<br /> Ape 2: 6i<br /> <br /> TURN 1<br /> WD: 10i (13p/27ph, 4wp), Ape 1: 10i, Ape 2: 6i<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon and Ape 1 act on the same tick. Ape 1 doesn\u2019t fancy his chances of winning a clash against a stunted, full Excellency attack, so delays his action.<br /> Ape 1: 8i<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon moves into close range and makes a maxed out withering attack on Ape 2, hoping for a crash. Dexterity 5 + Wood Dragon 5 + Accuracy 2 + Stunt 2 + Excellency 5 (5m) + Eyes of the Wood Dragon (4m) = 19 dice. Results in just 8 successes, but anima rises to glowing.<br /> <br /> Ape 2 has parry of 4, thus 4 threshold successes + 9 (staff) + 3 (strength) + 5 (Eyes of the Wood Dragon) = 21 raw damage. 7 soak leaves 14 dice, resulting in an underwhelming 4 successes and one uncrashed ape.<br /> <br /> WD: 15i (13p/18ph, 4wp), Ape 2: 2i<br /> <br /> Ape 2 uses Principle of Motion, making two withering attacks.<br /> <br /> First attack: Wood Dragon has a parry of 7 (Defence 5 + 1 (Medium Weapon) + 1 (Stunt)). Ape 2 rolls 11 dice, 5 successes, attack misses.<br /> <br /> Second attack: Wood Dragon has a parry of 6. Ape 2 rolls 11 dice, 3 successes, attack misses.<br /> <br /> Ape 1 uses Principle of Motion, making one withering attack before attempting a grapple.<br /> <br /> First attack: Wood Dragon uses 4m Excellency, parry of 7. Ape 1 rolls 11 dice, 6 successes, attack misses.<br /> WD: 15i (13p/14ph, 4wp)<br /> <br /> Grapple: Wood Dragon really, really does not want to get grappled so uses 4m Excellency plus willpower for a parry of 7. Ape 1 rolls 8 dice plus willpower for 6 successes, attack misses.<br /> WD: 15i (13p/10ph, 3wp) and in wood aura, Ape 1: 6i<br /> <br /> TURN 2<br /> <br /> Mote regen<br /> WD: 15i (13p/15ph, 3wp), Ape 1 6i, Ape 2 2i<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon withers Ape 2 with 1m Excellency + Eyes of the Wood Dragon. 15 dice for 7 successes, anima rises to burning.<br /> <br /> 20 raw damage - 7 soak = 13 dice for 7 successes. Ape 2 is crashed at -5i, Wood Dragon smugly sitting at 28i (13p/10ph, 3wp).<br /> <br /> Ape 1 uses Principle of Motion, making two withering attacks.<br /> <br /> First attack: Ape 1 rolls 11 dice against Wood Dragon's parry of 7, gets 5 successes, attack misses.<br /> <br /> Second attack: Wood Dragon uses 2m Excellency, parry 7. Ape 1 rolls 11 dice, 7 successes, attack hits. 15 dice - (Soak of 3 (Stamina) + 5 (Armour)) = 7 dice rolled, resulting in 3 damage.<br /> WD: 25i (13p/8ph, 3wp), Ape 1: 10i<br /> <br /> Ape 2 uses Principle of Motion, making two withering attacks, the second backed up by willpower as, looking at Wood Dragon\u2019s initiative, he suspects he\u2019s not long for this world and wants to take full advantage of the onslaught penalty before he goes down.<br /> <br /> First attack: Wood Dragon uses 4m Excellency, parry 7. Ape 2 rolls 11 dice, 6 successes, attack misses.<br /> WD: 25i (13p/4ph, 3wp)<br /> <br /> Second attack: Wood Dragon uses 1 willpower and Wood Dragon Vitality (5m), parry 5. Ape 2 rolls 11 dice, 10 successes (including willpower), attack hits. Anima rises to bonfire.<br /> <br /> 5 threshold successes + 15 - (Soak of 3 (Stamina) + 5 (Armour) + 7 (Wood Dragon Vitality)) = 5 dice rolled, resulting in 3 damage. Ape just fails to climb out of crash. WD: 22i (12p/0ph, 2wp), Ape 2 -1i<br /> <br /> TURN 3<br /> <br /> Mote regen, anima deals 1 HL of damage to Ape 2, no damage to Ape 1.<br /> WD: 22i (12p/5ph, 2wp), Ape 1 10i, Ape 2 -1i<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon makes a decisive attack against Ape 2. Dexterity 5 + Martial Arts 5 + Stunt 2 + Excellency 2 (2m) = 14 dice. Ape 2 defends with willpower for a parry of 5. Result is 6 successes. 22 dice of damage results in 9 health levels, Ape 2 is out of the fight.<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon resets to 3i (12p/3ph, 2wp)<br /> <br /> Ape 1 uses Principle of Motion, making two withering attacks.<br /> <br /> First attack: Ape 1 rolls 11 dice against Wood Dragon's parry of 7, gets 5 successes, attack misses.<br /> <br /> Second attack: Wood Dragon uses 2m Excellency, parry 7. Ape 1 rolls 11 dice, 7 successes, attack hits. 7 dice after soak results in just 2 damage, flukily avoiding crash.<br /> WD: 1i (12p/1ph, 2wp), Ape 1: 13i<br /> <br /> TURN 4<br /> <br /> Mote regen, anima withers 1 initiative from Ape 1<br /> WD: 1i (12p/6ph, 2wp), Ape 1: 12i<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon is very close to crash, so will be upping their standard parry to 8 from their \u2018usual\u2019 7 this turn to play it safe.<br /> <br /> Ape 1 uses Principle of Motion, making one withering attack followed by one decisive attack in an attempt to inflict a wound penalty before WD\u2019s attack withers away all his initiative.<br /> <br /> First attack: Wood Dragon uses 2m Excellency, parry 8. Ape 1 rolls 11 dice, 5 successes, attack misses.<br /> WD: 1i (12p/4ph, 2wp)<br /> <br /> Second attack: Wood Dragon uses 4m Excellency, parry 8. Ape 1 rolls 11 dice, 6 successes, attack misses.<br /> WD: 1i (12p/0ph, 2wp), Ape 1: 9i<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon withers Ape 1 with 1m Excellency + Eyes of the Wood Dragon (4m). 15 dice yields 8 successes against Parry 4, hitting comfortably. 21 raw damage gives 14 dice, 7 damage.<br /> WD: 9i (7p/0ph, 2wp), Ape 1: 2i<br /> <br /> TURN 5<br /> <br /> Mote regen, anima does nothing.<br /> WD: 9i (12p/0ph, 2wp), Ape 1: 2i<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon withers Ape 1 with (again) 1m Excellency and Eyes of the Wood Dragon. 15 dice yields 5 successes against Parry 4. 18 raw damage gives 11 dice, 6 damage. Ape 1 is crashed at -4i, Wood Dragon 21i (7p/0ph, 2wp).<br /> <br /> Ape 1 is out of willpower, so uses Brutal Ape Pounce.<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon uses 2m Excellency, parry 8. Ape 1 rolls 11 dice, 3 successes, attack misses.<br /> WD: 21i (5p/0ph, 2wp)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> TURN 6<br /> <br /> Mote regen, anima inflicts 1HL on Ape 1<br /> WD: 21i (10p/0ph, 2wp), Ape 1: -4i<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon makes a decisive attack against Ape 2, using a 3m Excellency. 6 successes from 15 dice against Parry 4 proves enough as 8 health levels of damage follow. Fight over.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Notes<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">- WD only used three charms during the fight, and one of those only once. Might re-run it one idle day using the alpha strike approach or the archery approach mooted above to see if they are more interesting. It's probably why it wasn't run in the first place...<br /> <br /> - Eyes of the Wood Dragon with Perception 5 is pretty sweet.<br /> <br /> - I still think Wood Dragon works best/most interestingly as part of a group fighting a single, powerful spirit. Say, with an Earth Aspect wading in and an air aspect withering away to keep the spirit honest, allowing Wood Dragon to not worry about hoarding loads of initiative himself and just dip in and out of the fight, inflicting crippling injuries and stripping away health levels with Spirit-Wracking Method. Basically being the wild card weirdo of the group.<br /> <br /> - Might be my perception bias, but at this lower tier power level, medium weapons seem good \u2013 arguably the best thing about WD in this fight. +1 to your parry is massive in terms of saving you motes you\u2019d otherwise have to pump into your defence. When you start facing tougher opponents then the accuracy and clashing bonus of paired light weapons is what I\u2019d favour for DBs, but at this weight class a parry of 7 with a stunt is great.<br /> <br /> - Blood Apes probably need stunts to be dangerous to combat DBs unless there are three or more of them (then motes would start getting tight). That said, WD never had one of those disaster rolls where everything goes wrong \u2013 he got lucky in turn 3 and otherwise rolled pretty well, which was all he needed to do as the apes only ever got one above average roll in.<br /> <br /> - Shattering Roar seems too inaccurate to bother with?<br /> <br /> - I\u2019ve barely played 3e due to minimal free time, so don\u2019t think I\u2019ve got the best handle on the way to run opponents \u2013 I remember an interesting discussion on this thread about whether launching alpha strike decisives with single figure-to-teens initiative with the intent to wound early on is the way to go. Maybe I should have gone with a decisive-to-wound from Ape 1 in Turn 2\u2026</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>I\u2019ll pipe down now and return you to your regularly scheduled programming\u2026</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 02-27-2020, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T12:37:08-08:00","id":1370624,"title":"","content":"Wood Dragon definitely did way better than I thought it would.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370582#post1370582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Might be my perception bias, but at this lower tier power level, medium weapons seem good \u2013 arguably the best thing about WD in this fight. +1 to your parry is massive in terms of saving you motes you\u2019d otherwise have to pump into your defence. When you start facing tougher opponents then the accuracy and clashing bonus of paired light weapons is what I\u2019d favour for DBs, but at this weight class a parry of 7 with a stunt is great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having max parry is definitely good, but I wouldn't necessarily call this a lower power tier. By the end of that fight the dedicated Immaculate fighter had 10m and 2wp left, if they had to fight another two bloodapes right away they'd be in some real trouble.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also relying on clash bonuses for defense isn't that easy.<ul><li>If your opponent ever gets ahead of you in initiative you need to rely on reflexive clash charms, most of which are decisive so you're actually not any better off on average compared to your parry.</li> <li>You need to keep bleeding 2i every turn to delay to clash, which can add up.</li> <li>If you're facing multiple opponents or opponents with multiple attack charms you need to use a lot of those reflexive clash charms, most of which cost a willpower at least.</li> <li>Using your attack to clash every turn means you can't take advantage of your allies setting up onslaught penalties. Even if they're sitting at 0 Defense due to the pouring of attacks, they still get their full attack pool to clash you with.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370582#post1370582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Blood Apes probably need stunts to be dangerous to combat DBs unless there are three or more of them (then motes would start getting tight). That said, WD never had one of those disaster rolls where everything goes wrong \u2013 he got lucky in turn 3 and otherwise rolled pretty well, which was all he needed to do as the apes only ever got one above average roll in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as an ST I've started stunting a lot more with my NPCs, even two and three point stunts. Exalted already heavily favours the PCs in a lot of ways, they really don't need to be the only people in the world getting stunt bonuses. That's not a house rule either, NPCs are <i>supposed </i>to stunt. Storm Mothers have an attack that only resets on a 2/3 point stunt, same with Fakharu, NPC Lunars, ect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370582#post1370582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Shattering Roar seems too inaccurate to bother with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the game is designed with the idea that some players might have a defense of 2-3. In my experience this is not the case, usually people have 6, some have 7, others have 5, almost never do they have as little as 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370582#post1370582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- I\u2019ve barely played 3e due to minimal free time, so don\u2019t think I\u2019ve got the best handle on the way to run opponents \u2013 I remember an interesting discussion on this thread about whether launching alpha strike decisives with single figure-to-teens initiative with the intent to wound early on is the way to go. Maybe I should have gone with a decisive-to-wound from Ape 1 in Turn 2\u2026[/spoiler]</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were looking to see if the bloodapes could win, don't do that, usually. In this case the apes missed by just 1 success so many times it might actually have been worth it to knock that defense down by 1, but usually opening yourself up to be crashed badly isn't worth it.<br /> <br /> <br /> The reason you should open up or launch early decisives is to wound the players. For example, this might be an adventure arc with some beats I'm expecting:<br /> <br /> <br /> The players have heard that their ancestor/former-exaltation/ancient-ghost-friend has hidden something they need in the depths of an unbreached first age tomb. They reach the edge of the tomb late at night so they decide to camp and head in first thing the next morning. Let's say there's some kind of time pressure urging them forth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Scene 1 Dawn of Claws</u></b></span><br /> <br /> Just as the sky begins to lighten in the pre-dawn, a hunting pack of seven claw striders creep through the thick, dark foliage in an attempt to ambush. Those on watch take a -3 penalty to awareness rolls due to the dark and the terrain. The ambush happens, the PCs defeat it and move on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Scene 2 Living Lock</span></u></b><br /> <br /> The lock on this first age tomb is actually a bound spirit. The door can either be smashed open with a Strength 10+ difficulty 15 roll, or by convincing the spirit to open the door. The spirit has a defining principle to protect that which is locked within it, a major tie of loyalty to the person who bid it guard this place, and a minor tie of love towards the fellow spirits that inhabit this place and often keep it company from their side of the door. Guile 4, Resolve 5, maybe some enhancing charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Scene 3 Stone Guardians</u></b></span><br /> <br /> Once through the door, by whatever means, mindless walking statue guardians come to life, flooding the massive open foyer. The spirit unable to dissuade them if they entered legitimately. Treat them as a size 2 battlegroup of Walking Statues with elite drill, might 1, and a two-headed commander. Give the commander a merit that allows it to flurry an attack action with a command action, taking no defense penalty and only a -1 penalty to both actions and also gains +2 dice to command actions. .<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Scene 4 Hall of Barred Doors</span></u></b><br /> <br /> After that battle they move into a hallway with doors shut and sealed along both walls, and no door at the end of the hallway. Some of these doors have been shut with dangerous things behind them, others lead further into the tomb. A (Perception + Investigation) roll, difficulty 3 reveals that hidden above each door is a symbol, raise difficulty to 4 without proper lighting. Furthermore an (Intelligence + Linguistics) roll, difficulty 4 determines this to be some kind of code written by the builders to determine which door is which. With that they can pick the door to go down.<br /> <br /> All doors are locked, opening them requires a (Dexterity + Larceny) roll of difficulty 3, the correct door to take down is difficulty 4. The trap doors contain one of two things. One is a poisonous cloud, environmental hazard difficulty 5, damage 3L. The other is the screams of fallen foes, treat it as an inspire roll to instill fear in the characters using 13 dice. If the PC already suffers from an emotion of fear, treat it as an instill roll to introduce or raise an intimacy of fear for this place.<br /> <br /> If they pick a door at random roll a d10, on a 10 they pick correctly, on a 1-5 they pick a poison door, 6-9 a door of screams.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Scene 5 Pit of Webs</u></b></span><br /> <br /> As they descend the spiral staircase down they notice that it ends, broken sharply, and continues down at as a drop. Any who wish to drop down a range band my do so, either with charms, accepting the falling damage, or using some kind of equipment like rope lines and pitons to descend. Once they're all down a successful (Perception + Awareness) difficulty 3 reveals that the ground is covered in spider webs. Moving on to them triggers the Anuhle's Tread-Spinning Snare, initiating combat as a group of six massive demonic spiders crawl from cracks in the walls, ceiling and floor. The terrain is uneven, broken rocks and covered in spiderwebs, all non-Anhule take a -3 penalty to physical actions.<br /> <br /> After the players dispatch the demon spiders, or if they look around during combat, they may notice a door overwebbed with Anuhle webs with a (Perception + Investigation or Awareness) roll difficulty 3. Cutting away the demon silk requires a feat of demolition strength 5 difficulty 6.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Scene 6 Door of Spiteful Locks</u></b></span><br /> <br /> The final door to the tomb. On it there are three locks, difficulty 4, 5 and 6 to open. Upon opening the difficulty 4 lock a spirit will materialize, bound as one of the final protectors of this place. It has stats similar to a fair folk Lorelei, and desperately tries to dissuade the characters from continuing. It must either be slain, ignored, or convinced to allow the party to pass.<br /> <br /> Upon opening the difficulty 5 lock plugs break open and begin to flood the room with an acid bath as the exit slams shut. It may be stopped by breaking open the exit door Difficulty 10 Strength 5+ Feat of Strength<br /> <br /> Upon opening the Difficulty 6 lock, nothing appears to happen except the door opens, revealing a stair upwards and out off the acid bath. It also, however, exposes all present to a disease. Use the stats of Plague.<br /> <br /> The locks may be opened without triggering their effects at +3 difficulty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Scene 7 Victory!</u></b></span><br /> <br /> Here whatever treasures or knowledge or whatever that the players sought is there, along with means to deactivate the acid bath and leave the way they came. Hopefully in time to meet whatever time pressure was on them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, if that's the session of getting through that first age tomb, you can see that the Claw Strider attack right at the beginning is just the start of it. If those claw striders attack it's probably going to cost the party some motes to defend themselves. If those striders land decisive attacks though, those are wounds that are probably going to last for the whole day. Now you're fighting the walking statue battlegroup at -1 wound penalty. Then you take more damage from the poison door, and now you're fighting the Anuhle at -2. Finally when you achieve victory not only are you totally drained on motes, but also kind of beat up...which I think makes for more exciting and dramatic action.<br /> <br /> Also anyone who bought medicine charms that help people recover wounds, or resistance charms that help them heal faster don't feel totally useless because the world they live in can't scratch them anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T14:13:19-08:00","id":1370644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe the game is designed with the idea that some players might have a defense of 2-3. In my experience this is not the case, usually people have 6, some have 7, others have 5, almost never do they have as little as 4. </div> </div> </div>I started our Campaign with a Dawn that had an Evasion of 3... so it does indeed happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 02-26-2020, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T14:21:01-08:00","id":1370647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370624#post1370624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the game is designed with the idea that some players might have a defense of 2-3. In my experience this is not the case, usually people have 6, some have 7, others have 5, almost never do they have as little as 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like the game was designed for a completely different chargen mechanism, then they went and changed things so everyone would have half a dozen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T14:33:58-08:00","id":1370652,"title":"","content":"I do not think that this is the case... Going back to my Dawn Cast... He has no Stat at greater than 4 (and only 3 of those) and only Martial Arts at a 5 (two Martial Arts). Everything else is 4 or less with a LOT of 3's, both in Attributes and abilities. It is generally the Players, more often than not, that choose to maximize the dots as efficiently as possible, to make character advancement cheaper, that are the actual cause of the issue you describe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T14:39:12-08:00","id":1370654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370644#post1370644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started our Campaign with a Dawn that had an Evasion of 3... so it does indeed happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen it. In fact my last two Solar characters deliberately had defence scores of 2 to start out and I had an absolute blast. Combats felt more engaging, there was rising and falling initiatives, I used different tactics, good stuff. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370647#post1370647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like the game was designed for a completely different chargen mechanism, then they went and changed things so everyone would have half a dozen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... the thing is you CAN make characters like that. The published Solar circle has a few. The Dawn has a parry of 5-6, the Zenith of 5, but the Twilight and Eclipse only have 2-3 and they\u2019re all made legit with the chargen rules. Barring specialties, and a couple charms and a couple bonus points. Awareness is another one, no foe will ever successfully ambus a party of PCs with everyone sporting awareness 5. Which puts a lot of antagonists in bad positions.<br /> <br /> Not impossible ones, I think the rough little example adventure adventure I just made up makes okay use of what\u2019s there, but there\u2019s just a lot of stuff that\u2019s nearly useless. Which is sad, foes like the basilisk or the scorpion-man are really cool, but they\u2019ll never really be useful.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re all consistent with eachother at least, ta just such a waste to give them cool powers and fluff only to have them sit on the shelf gathering dust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T14:42:36-08:00","id":1370656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370652#post1370652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that this is the case... Going back to my Dawn Cast... He has no Stat at greater than 4 (and only 3 of those) and only Martial Arts at a 5 (two Martial Arts). Everything else is 4 or less with a LOT of 3's, both in Attributes and abilities. It is generally the Players, more often than not, that choose to maximize the dots as efficiently as possible, to make character advancement cheaper, that are the actual cause of the issue you describe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s hard to tell them no though. I mean, they can make a powerful character, or choose to make a weak one deliberately, it\u2019s really hard to resist doing the former.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also made worse by STs giving PCs stunt bonuses but not NPCs. When your players are already min-maxing stats, giving them 1-3 bonus successes on top of that really doesn\u2019t help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T14:50:04-08:00","id":1370659,"title":"","content":"This is true, for the most part - after all, we do not want to tell players that they cannot play what they want to play, but the system seems to be structured for those characters that are not totally optimized bad-asses... which I do appreciate, since I far prefer a more non-optimized approach, because that allows the GM to actually have non-optimized opponents in play, rather than having to push the optimization arms race ever upward, as I have seen some do in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T15:33:29-08:00","id":1370667,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not so sure that the system is structured like that. Just look at the charms. There\u2019s 48 melee charms and a grand total of 12 that don\u2019t require at least melee 4. It\u2019s also just so easy to max out your characters combat ability. You\u2019re not sacrificing much else..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T23:54:52-08:00","id":1370708,"title":"","content":"And, again, it's intentional Exalted design.<br /> <br /> You are playing the beings who cast down the creators of the universe. You are thrust into a broken world that hates you. You are hunted by a world spanning empire and thousand year old martial arts masters.<br /> <br /> You are supposed to be excellent in all things and unsurpassed in your area of focus (as 1st edition phrased it).<br /> <br /> A mortal brigand with a rusty blade is not supposed to challenge you.<br /> <br /> You're supposed to have encounters like DrLoveMonkey described over-leaf. And you're supposed to win.<br /> <br /> If you want tense, life and death combat against demons then play heroic mortals.<br /> If you want to be pushed to the limit by the foes in the Corebook then play Dragon-Blooded.<br /> If you want to walk the edges of Creation, testing your limits then that's what Lunars are for.<br /> <br /> Solars are for playing the returning god kings who change the world in their wake.<br /> <br /> Complaining that a Solar has Parry 7 is like complaining that The Terminator is too difficult for Sarah Connor to beat and that it should be vulnerable to pepper spray and a tazer.<br /> <br /> Your bookish Twilight does not have to be a Parry 7 combat monster. Your bookish Twilight can be a Defense 2 non-combatant. But you don't have to be a Dawn Caste to be a capable warrior.<br /> <br /> The Corebook explicitly tells you that it's ok to take 5s. The sample characters (like Volfer) have 5s. Starting Charms (Essence 1) require 5s.<br /> <br /> There are three Circles of Demons. Blood Apes are literally the weakest. Blood Apes are the low tier bodyguards summoned ny the very weakest of Exalted sorcerers (because they're just powerful enough to be useful but not oowerful enough to be a threat). Of course your combat focused Exalt can beat them. Forget the Third Circle, go fight Mara with your Immaculate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-27-2020, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T01:00:06-08:00","id":1370712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, again, it's intentional Exalted design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wish they went one way or the other with it. Either make the Exalted warriors nearly invincible, but if you decide to focus your character elsewhere it's not so easy to trivialize so many opponents OR stop printing so many friggin cool antagonists with like, 7-8 die attacks. Ghostfisher, fucking so god damn cool. A creature with Legendary Size that hides in wait, using a creepy ghostly lure to get people close so it can eat them...8 dice to it's highest accuracy attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> 'cause sometimes it feels like<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> System: &quot;Man check out this awesome antagonist steel beast that can devour metal and want to swallow daiklaves!&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Wow that sounds awesome.&quot;<br /> System: &quot;Yeah it's got an 8 die attack with 10 damage. The Exalted are so mighty they care not for this manner of beast.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Right got it, that makes sense.&quot;<br /> <br /> System: &quot;How about this thing, it's a scorpion beastman from a nation of scorpion-folk, and he's waging a one-man war against outsiders. He's got all these merits representing his mutations and coolness.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Okay sweet. Maybe I could use him to-&quot;<br /> System: &quot;Oh you won't be using him. He's got a 10 die attack with 6 damage as his best offense. How badass are the Exalted that this guy is meaningless to them eh?&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Yeah, badass I guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> System: &quot;You ever hear of a Haloed Husk before?&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Can't say I have.&quot;<br /> System: &quot;It's a hallow shell of a once living creature, animated by chaos. It's very soul set ablaze and light pouring from every orifice.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Mhm.&quot;<br /> System: &quot;They slink through the world, stealing light from natural sources, the only thing that feeds them, and they need much of it.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;That's pretty cool actually...&quot;<br /> System: &quot;In the cold north, stealing fires is deadly, and they love to devour Exalted anima banners when they can.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Exalted you say? Like my PCs?&quot;<br /> System: &quot;Haha, no, 6-7 die attack, Evasion 2, Soak 3. Are you such a fool to think that the mighty Exalted would ever be concerned with such a trivial thing?&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;I guess not.&quot;<br /> System: &quot;Now have you heard of the deadly Cockatrice..&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Fuck off.&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not actually THAT spiteful, and I've found some ways to use antagonists that I previously haven't had a use for, mostly be increasing numbers drastically and changing some tactics but...a lot still not really useful. A lot of them aren't even that useful in a <i>mortals </i>game, since it's not like you need to be an exalt to get 7 Parry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T01:15:56-08:00","id":1370713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370624#post1370624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loadsa great stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>So fast... cool complete adventure... how? How? It takes me like a week to do/plan anything in this game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T01:57:32-08:00","id":1370722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370713#post1370713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So fast... cool complete adventure... how? How? It takes me like a week to do/plan anything in this game...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I am a veteran Storyteller at this point. For that adventure though I use cobbled together some ideas I had previously, along with just noodling around the systems chapter a bit. I want combat and social influence to be big parts because they're big parts of the system, environmental damage is always good because it's hard to resist and causes direct damage, same with disease. Also don't be afraid to make up your own stuff like the two headed statue commander. Browse through the corebook and see acid bath and go &quot;sure, there's an acid bath now.&quot; Then just keep going adding more and more.<br /> <br /> One single challenge will never, ever, actually challenge your PCs, you need to just keep going. Especially out of combat, with no 5m/round drip every full excellency is really felt. I was debating adding another really short scene of a long, wide hallway with a low ceiling and no floor, just a 500 foot drop to spikes or something. Ceiling too low to monkey leap, find some other way across. Alternatively rather than a pit a grid of flamethrower triggering plates that could be destroyed, figured out, or dismantled.<br /> <br /> Also remember that absent charms even Solars are basically human. You actually can use DnD style challenges a lot of the time. Like that drop into the pit of webs onto uneven broken stone. You fall 30 feet onto that and you don't get to walk away without a scratch just because you're awesome. <br /> <br /> Don't forget about environmental penalties either. Exalted is an epic world with extreme environments and climates. Towering frozen waterfalls and thick weed-choked bogs. Some people will buy charms to ignore those penalties, they didn't buy them to never use them. It's also a good way of leeching motes out of se that don't have them, that helps leeching health levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T07:47:27-08:00","id":1370758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, again, it's intentional Exalted design.<br /> <br /> You are playing the beings who cast down the creators of the universe. You are thrust into a broken world that hates you. You are hunted by a world spanning empire and thousand year old martial arts masters.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that you are not casting down the Creators of the Universe at Essence 1... You can definitely be a badass, but you are absolutely <i><b>not</b></i> the Ultimate Badass at Essence 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T08:01:57-08:00","id":1370761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are playing the beings who cast down the creators of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are playing <i>the reincarnations</i> of the beings who <i>collectively</i> cast down <i>some</i> of the creators of the universe, and convinced the others to surrender, with the support of gods, elementals, at least two traitor-Primordials, and the Dragon Kings and Mountain Folk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mortal brigand with a rusty blade is not supposed to challenge you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the scenario really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're supposed to have encounters like DrLoveMonkey described over-leaf. And you're supposed to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's more that you're supposed to be <i>able</i> to win; people shouldn't count you out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want tense, life and death combat against demons then play heroic mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or play Exalts who aren't combat-optimized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to be pushed to the limit by the foes in the Corebook then play Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Solars who aren't combat-optimized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to walk the edges of Creation, testing your limits then that's what Lunars are for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dispute that this is &quot;what Lunars are for.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are for playing the returning god kings who change the world in their wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but they've been usurped before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370708#post1370708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Complaining that a Solar has Parry 7 is like complaining that The Terminator is too difficult for Sarah Connor to beat and that it should be vulnerable to pepper spray and a tazer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the Terminator is made of metal all the time, and doesn't become vulnerable flesh when he runs out of Essence; god-kings, on the other hand, can be worn down, as you yourself demonstrated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370758#post1370758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that you are not casting down the Creators of the Universe at Essence 1...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not by yourself, no, but Ghost-Eating Technique <i>is</i> an Essence 1 Charm. If Invisible Horse Princess had been part of the forces fighting the Primordials, she might well have been able to strike the killing blow on one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T09:19:10-08:00","id":1370777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370761#post1370761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are playing <i>the reincarnations</i> of the beings who <i>collectively</i> cast down <i>some</i> of the creators of the universe, and convinced the others to surrender, with the support of gods, elementals, at least two traitor-Primordials, and the Dragon Kings and Mountain Folk.<br /> <br /> Depends on the scenario really.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's more that you're supposed to be <i>able</i> to win; people shouldn't count you out.<br /> <br /> Or play Exalts who aren't combat-optimized.<br /> <br /> Or Solars who aren't combat-optimized.<br /> <br /> I dispute that this is &amp;quot;what Lunars are for.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Sure, but they've been usurped before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you've deliberately missed off the part of my argument where I say pretty much this. But ok.<br /> <br /> My point is that the theme of Solars is excellence, Solars are excellent, and a Solar who focuses on being excellent at combat will be excellent at combat.<br /> <br /> Embrace the awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370761#post1370761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the Terminator is made of metal all the time, and doesn't become vulnerable flesh when he runs out of Essence; god-kings, on the other hand, can be worn down, as you yourself demonstrated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with no motes they still have Parry 7.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370758#post1370758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that you are not casting down the Creators of the Universe at Essence 1... You can definitely be a badass, but you are absolutely <i><b>not</b></i> the Ultimate Badass at Essence 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a 2-ism but a freshly Exalted Solar forced a Primordial to flee.<br /> <br /> As a 3-ism the entire War was fought between Essence 1-5.<br /> <br /> Embrace the awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T10:19:34-08:00","id":1370790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370777#post1370777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with no motes they still have Parry 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does mean that powerful mortals also have a resting parry of 7. They don't have charms to compensate for being swarmed and onslaught penalties and stuff, but that still leaves a lot of otherwise supposedly powerful beasts in a position where they can't do much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T10:37:51-08:00","id":1370792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370790#post1370790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That does mean that powerful mortals also have a resting parry of 7. They don't have charms to compensate for being swarmed and onslaught penalties and stuff, but that still leaves a lot of otherwise supposedly powerful beasts in a position where they can't do much.</div> </div> </div> </div>You saw the fight between The Mountain and Prince Oberyn, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T10:45:58-08:00","id":1370793,"title":"","content":"The issue is that it is trivially easy to get a resting parry of 6, and not very difficult to get a resting parry of 7. The resources invested in boosting your parry to 6-7 give you a huge return on investment beyond anything else you can buy at chargen. Sure, you can say &quot;don't play optimized characters&quot; but how about expecting the system to work when people follow basic incentives? DrLoveMonkey's post about the printed antagonists is right, they are just laughably weak next to any remotely well designed character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T10:55:27-08:00","id":1370795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370793#post1370793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that it is trivially easy to get a resting parry of 6, and not very difficult to get a resting parry of 7. The resources invested in boosting your parry to 6-7 give you a huge return on investment beyond anything else you can buy at chargen. Sure, you can say &quot;don't play optimized characters&quot; but how about expecting the system to work when people follow basic incentives? DrLoveMonkey's post about the printed antagonists is right, they are just laughably weak next to any remotely well designed character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like we're going off-piest now.<br /> <br /> If I make a character designed to be the best combatant in the world, it's because I want to tell a story about the best combatant in the world.<br /> <br /> Exalted supports this.<br /> <br /> Exalted, further, explicitly tells you that 3 dots is the level of a skilled professional -- a real stand-out of exceptional talent.<br /> <br /> And the static difficulties support this.<br /> <br /> Your Parry 7 mortal absolutely cannot beat Octavian. They can beat a Blood Ape, <i>maybe</i>. They can't best two Blood Apes at once: and as First Circle Demons, Blood Apes are literally the weakest demons in the game.<br /> <br /> You can play an optimized Scholar who also just happens to be the <i>greatest swordsman in the world</i>. That's Raptors in an F-16 awesome. That's Exalted.<br /> <br /> But you are still playing <i>literally the greatest swordsman in the world</i>.<br /> <br /> If you feel that lacks narrative weight then that's not a system problem -- that's on you and your ST.<br /> <br /> Mortal NPCs aren't running round with Parry 7. Most Exalted NPCs aren't built that way. The average encounter isn't with foes who are the best in the world at what they do, so if you make a character who IS the best in the world then you will (usually) win. That's system working as intended. Oblivion style &quot;bandits in Daedric armor&quot; would be deeply unsatisfying for me. In Exalted, if you optimize yourself for combat, you should be an unstoppable terror in combat.<br /> <br /> And if you don't want to be an optimized, unstoppable terror in combat, then don't play <i>literally the greatest combatant in the world</i>.<br /> <br /> It's like playing an Epic Level D&amp;D game and complaining that the only monsters in the MM that can challenge you are CR20+ which means you'll never get to fight a harpy or a wyvnn. The CR1-19 monsters are for level 1-19 characters: they're not for you. If you want to turn up and one-shot them with your awesomeness then so much the better. You are awesome, lean into it. Describe the fantastic abilities which make these beasts unstoppable to mortals then roll right over them. But recognise that most people are not the greatest swordsman in the world.<br /> <br /> If the ask is &quot;more behemoths, more elemental dragons, more 2/3 Circle Demons, more elders&quot;, then I'm down with that.<br /> <br /> But if I'm in the top 1%, I don't want to play DBZ -- I want to play One Punch Man","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-27-2020, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T12:21:35-08:00","id":1370815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370792#post1370792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You saw the fight between The Mountain and Prince Oberyn, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but the Mountain did, eventually, hit Oberyn. Ghostfishers have pretty powerful attacks, but against somebody with 7 parry in heavy armor, they're not so hot. They've got less than a 10% chance to hit, and if they do land a hit, maybe 8-9 dice of post-soak withering damage? They're the undead equivalent of a sandworm from Dune and it falls flat against mortal characters.<br /> <br /> A lot don't even have the Ghostfisher's epic damage either. A Steel Eater only has 10 damage on its 8-die attack, which against mundane heavy armor just plinks off.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the one hand, agreed, it's cool that in the world of Exalted even mortal heroes can be epic enough to face those kinds of challenges. As a Storyteller though it can be grating when literally everyone in the party is also the greatest swordsman in the world in addition to anything else they might be. They're the greatest swordsman in the world <i>and </i>only spent 20% of their chargen resources to do it. It's such a no-brainer that everyone does it.<br /> <br /> Which is workable. It wouldn't be my favourite way of going about things, but it is workable. If that's the case though, stop wasting my time giving me a hundred cool enemies that I can't use. We might as well publish a book of ants. One hundred and fifty pages of ants, detailing their colonies, how Creation ants differ from ants on Earth, regional ants, the structure of their homes, etc. We are not playing a game of insects. I can not use that information.<br /> <br /> It's not like it's every beast anyway. A pack of claw striders with their 12 dice + 3 automatic successes attacks are dangerous to basically anyone not spending motes. There's just waaaay too many enemies that aren't clawstriders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370795#post1370795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if I'm in the top 1%, I don't want to play DBZ -- I want to play One Punch Man</div> </div> </div> </div>Whaaaa? Do you mean <a href=\"https://youtu.be/1hAN_s9Iz-s?t=105\" target=\"_blank\">this DBZ</a>? Or <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pRHwEIjDk7Q?t=36\" target=\"_blank\">this DBZ</a>? Also I <i>love </i>One Punch Man, but having a full circle of Saitamas isn't a good thing for Exalted, and Saitama doesn't really work like Solars work anyway. There are other settings and other systems that can do that, like Nobilis or Godsent from the World of Legacy.<br /> <br /> All Might from My Hero Academia is a lot closer if you're going to make a comparison. During the series he takes on a mindless killer enemy who's been expertly engineered from the ground up by people who intimately know All Might's powers to specifically counter his strengths and exploit his weaknesses. All Might thrashes him in less than three minutes by just punching even more. After that though, he's basically spent, he's bluffing in threatening the remaining villains to surrender. Thankfully a cadre of professional heroes arrive as support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:50:31-08:00","id":1370842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370795#post1370795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if I'm in the top 1%, I don't want to play DBZ -- I want to play One Punch Man</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Do you want to replicate Saitama's experience of becoming totally bored and disillusioned in fighting since he effortlessly overcomes every foe without fail? Because playing the One Punch Man in a system like Exalted 3e would be so horrendously boring. I know this because I've done it.<br /> <br /> I played a Brawl Supernal Dawn Caste named Simurgh, with the intention of making him the strongest warrior in the Empire of Prasad. I figured 'hell yeah, I'm gonna be a big badass dude who has bombastic awesome fights with powerful Dragonblooded and behemoths and giant godlings and takes on armies with nothing but his bare hands.'<br /> <br /> The reality was a series of ultimately identical battles that each ended in 2 rounds. Round 1: Simurgh wins Initiative with Awakening Eye and Crashes his opponent. In return, his opponent swipes back for paltry Withering Damage. Round 2: Simurgh makes a decisive attack and defeats his enemy. Rinse and repeat for 11 sessions.<br /> <br /> I found no enjoyment in this. Simurgh's obscene strength had no meaning. He could punch a dude through the air over 10 city blocks, but he's no better at say, running, than a normal person. He's a kaiju of dice tricks and combat math that nothing in the world can stand up to, and that got boring, fast. He's not even optimized particularly well: I chose Incarnated Fury Attack in character generation and forgot to take Falling Hammer Strike until session 10.<br /> <br /> I figured that, by investing so heavily into combat charms, I'd be signing up for big cool anime fights with fun back and forth and shifting advantage, but that couldn't be further from the truth. In my experience combat with Simurgh became less and less interesting the more I invested into it. This seems like a fault with the system to me.<br /> <br /> Though, this is all anecdotal. It could be that I wasn't seeking out the <i>right </i>enemies or something like that, but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T14:06:31-08:00","id":1370845,"title":"","content":"Exigent Exalted of Tenachel, the God of Ennui.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370842#post1370842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, this is all anecdotal. It could be that I wasn't seeking out the <i>right </i>enemies or something like that, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>There could have been things that made for more interesting fights, but they'd only be in combination with other things. Other fights, other challenges, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T14:46:59-08:00","id":1370855,"title":"","content":"I know most STs pretty much do this themselves anyway, but I always thought adopting the Final Fantasy 'same enemy but in a different colour with a few new tricks' approach on published antagonists would be great if the devs could make it work (greedy, I know).<br /> <br /> Have, I dunno, the basic stat line, one for err... 'elites' with a couple of bonuses to key stats and one new/tweaked charm, and one for 'champions' with a couple of further bonuses and another new trick.<br /> <br /> Bloop Apes, for a 'current' example - if you make... call 'em Berserkers instead of elites?... have a couple more dice plus Brutal Ape Pounce as a supplemental charm they'd be much scarier to PCs short of your optimised death machines, two withering attacks a turn that can knock you prone...?<br /> <br /> Probably stipulate that unless the ST says otherwise summon spells only produce the baseline demon to avoid shenanigans though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T14:53:22-08:00","id":1370858,"title":"","content":"That might work for Essence actually, yeah.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T16:05:47-08:00","id":1370873,"title":"","content":"For Exalted combat I'd take Jojo's Bizarre Adventure over Dragonball Z or One Punch Man.<br /> Obviously, downplay the aspect where the main characters are constantly railroaded into antagonists waiting for them with the perfect set-up to use their one weird trick to devastating effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T19:39:31-08:00","id":1370914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370855#post1370855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have, I dunno, the basic stat line, one for err... 'elites' with a couple of bonuses to key stats and one new/tweaked charm, and one for 'champions' with a couple of further bonuses and another new trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the demon antagonist chapters of earlier editions did a pretty good job of this, but with the typical Exalted full-flavor fluff. Florivet isn't listed as Florivet - instead he's Florivet, The Whim of the Wind, Demon of the Second Circle, The Reflective Soul of the End of All Wisdom (Orabilis). Your circle trounced Florivet? Now Orabilis wants to play...<br /> <br /> Similarly, in 3rd edition, any enemy with 8 dice attacks can find themselves in a size 3 battlegroup and a commander throwing 3 success commands for another 3 dice, and, wham, now you've got 14 dice to toss at those Parry 7 PCs (with 3 more damage to their listed attack). <br /> <br /> I know it's silly to have literal armies for every challenge the PCs want to combat - but the ones at lesser powers you can let your combat monster circle auto-win (with appropriate social penalties for tyranny).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T19:48:22-08:00","id":1370915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370914#post1370914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, in 3rd edition, any enemy with 8 dice attacks can find themselves in a size 3 battlegroup and a commander throwing 3 success commands for another 3 dice, and, wham, now you've got 14 dice to toss at those Parry 7 PCs (with 3 more damage to their listed attack).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but here's the thing, some of them are really not guys that end up in battlegroups. Like, do you have a battlegroup of cockatrice, with a cockatrice commander? Or a battlegroup of Legendary sized ghostfishers? Probably not right? Zombies are not actually that bad, because in spite of their stupidly bad statline fielding a size 5 battlegroup of them is almost expected.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also want to say for clarity that I think bloodapes are fine. If your immaclate monk had to spend 30 motes and 3 willpower fighting a pair of bloodapes, that's not a sustainable win. Bloodapes are not only reasonably dangerous, but absolutely show up in large groups as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T19:59:16-08:00","id":1370917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370873#post1370873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Exalted combat I'd take Jojo's Bizarre Adventure over Dragonball Z or One Punch Man.<br /> Obviously, downplay the aspect where the main characters are constantly railroaded into antagonists waiting for them with the perfect set-up to use their one weird trick to devastating effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hamon == Essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:00:20-08:00","id":1370918,"title":"","content":"I could see the Fair Folk charming/conjuring a battlegroup of cockatrice. Similarly, a noble court of Raksha could have a dozen behemoths of legendary size at the heel of the beastmaster among them. Or a Labyrinth encounter of similar lethality and many massive ghost-beasts.<br /> <br /> I admit you're not going to walk into Wu-Jian and see them tied next to the horses at the watering-trough, but the Creation-centric stories rely on Dragon-Blooded and spirits to bring the status-quo muscle against our PC change agents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:14:20-08:00","id":1370923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370917#post1370917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hamon == Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the introduction of Stands but Part 4 is by far my favourite thus far because it shook up the formula I described above, which really wore on me in Part 3. I also disliked Jotaro Kujo as a protagonist and the everpresent Jojo memes spoilt sooo much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:44:03-08:00","id":1370928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370918#post1370918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see the Fair Folk charming/conjuring a battlegroup of cockatrice. Similarly, a noble court of Raksha could have a dozen behemoths of legendary size at the heel of the beastmaster among them. Or a Labyrinth encounter of similar lethality and many massive ghost-beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's possible, but they're just really not written like that. They have a bunch of merits and abilities and stuff that make them really not written like they're supposed to be battlegrouped. Like the cockatrice can grapple multiple people at once, the ghostfisher can swallow foes that it grapples, stuff like that. I know what they're <i>supposed </i>to be. They're just supposed to be battling people who don't have &quot;Also as awesome a fighter as Cu Chulainn.&quot; tacked on to their concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T01:27:54-08:00","id":1370949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370793#post1370793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that it is trivially easy to get a resting parry of 6, and not very difficult to get a resting parry of 7. The resources invested in boosting your parry to 6-7 give you a huge return on investment beyond anything else you can buy at chargen. Sure, you can say &quot;don't play optimized characters&quot; but how about expecting the system to work when people follow basic incentives? DrLoveMonkey's post about the printed antagonists is right, they are just laughably weak next to any remotely well designed character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In this situation, a reasonable person might conclude that it's the chargen incentives that are wrong, not <i>literally the rest of the entire game</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T01:35:53-08:00","id":1370950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370949#post1370949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In this situation, a reasonable person might conclude that it's the chargen incentives that are wrong, not <i>literally the rest of the entire game</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this.<br /> I run a Lunars only game. Base Defences are 3-5. They just don't have the same incentives to optimise as Solars (and Fire Aspects).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T02:02:19-08:00","id":1370955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370923#post1370923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the introduction of Stands but Part 4 is by far my favourite thus far because it shook up the formula I described above, which really wore on me in Part 3. I also disliked Jotaro Kujo as a protagonist and the everpresent Jojo memes spoilt sooo much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally don't want to start an argument on this topic but Joseph is the best Jojo and anyone that thinks otherwise is <i>literally </i>a nazi (or a communist chose your side I'm actually not that virulent).<br /> <br /> About the current obviously less interesting topic of the discussion : There's a difficulty to approach chargen that I believe is linked to our historical perception of RPG that is usually the character belong to the player and the world to the ST. We've gone pretty far away from it now in a lot of games, but everyone at a table doesn't have the same mentality.<br /> <br /> For example : Almost no one would be shocked if I told a player &quot;No I don't want you starting with 4 or 5 in Ressources because I'd be interested to see you acquire it in game&quot; (I mean some people will not agree with it but I think they can <i>understand </i>the idea) because these are merits and usually merits have an effect on the game world so you expect storyteller approval, and I believe it's only one among many reasons which makes it an acceptable (if not always consensual) decision.<br /> But I believe, if I told a player &quot;No you can't go to 4-5 Melee because I'd be interested to see you acquire in game&quot; there'd be a very different reactions from the players (including mine) because abilities and attributes are usually more in the player territory.<br /> <br /> So when people with different mindset are playing together (for example, a more JohnDoesque approach of &quot;let everyone pick what they want and have fun with it&quot; and a more Chaussesque approach of &quot;Well I have this kind of story in mind where I like character progression so you can have only one ability at 5 and Supernals are capped at Essence +1&quot;), we have this situation where everyone is at the same table but no one is playing the same game.<br /> <br /> And I believe that as DrLoveMonkey noted, it is then extremely difficult for the developers to account for all these different kind of players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 02-28-2020, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T02:26:06-08:00","id":1370962,"title":"","content":"Polite Sage. I've spoilered my arguments here because I don't want to derail the thread.<br /> <br /> No offense is intended in my arguments: play the way which is fun for you. My opinion is simply my opinion: I'm not a writer or a dev or anyone of importance to the game-line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370815#post1370815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whaaaa? Do you mean DBZ? Or <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pRHwEIjDk7Q?t=36\" target=\"_blank\">this DBZ</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's deconstruct this.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In his first appearance, Goku (who has been sent to conquer the entire planet Earth single-handed) is shot at, point-blank, by a woman with an Uzi. He doesn't lose that fight.<br /> He then meets Earth's greastest martial arts master, who is barely able to match him and trains to a greater level of power.<br /> <br /> That's Exalted to me.<br /> <br /> Then an alien of vastly greater power shows up, and Goku defeats them.<br /> Then an alien of vastly greater power still shows up, and Goku defeats them and in so doing becomes more powerful.<br /> <br /> Then we jump the shark and have two aliens, the more powerful of which is able to destroy a planet but both of which are more powerful than a god, show up. Goku unlocks a new level of power to beat them both.<br /> <br /> Then they fight the head of an evil galatic empire and Goku unlocks an ancient power of legend, becoming even more powerful.<br /> <br /> That's Exalted 2E -- the race to Essence 6 (ancient power of legend) so you can play &quot;the real game&quot;. This is not desirable to me and I'm glad 3E scrapped it.<br /> <br /> Then, seeing how powerful they are, someone builds a biological robot using their DNA and we get a <u><i>time travel</i></u> plot to unlock a level of power above the power of ancient legend.<br /> Then an ancient god-killer is unleashed, and we get fusion and a level of power above the level of power which is ascendend beyond the level of power of ancient legend.<br /> <br /> How are you thinking this is a good model for Exalted?<br /> <br /> Then a new class of god is unleashed who absolutely shrugs off <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xfgbt9QXZmY\" target=\"_blank\">the level of power above the level of power above the ancient power of legend used to defeat a galaxy spanning empire</a>.<br /> <br /> So a new level of power is unlocked.<br /> Then one above that.<br /> Then one above that.<br /> <br /> Six powerlevels ago, we were fighting beings more powerful than gods who could wipe out entire planets.<br /> <br /> Then we get to Broly and video clip. Where the &quot;Super Saiyan God Super Saiyan Ko-Ken x100&quot; is not powerful enough, so we get a &quot;Super Saiyan God Super Saiyan Fusion Ko-ken x100&quot; vs the new threat.<br /> <br /> DBZ is a constant arms race between the protagonists and the world. The game starts with the fate of the Earth in the balance (before Goku even unlocks the power of legend, they literally blow up the freakin' moon) and things just escalate from there!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't want to play a game where no matter how powerful I get, the enemies just magically level up alongside me and every fight is a constant struggle as the stakes get higher and higher until I'm defending the multi-verse.<br /> <br /> I want to play a game where if I'm the most powerful warrior in the world, then I am the most powerful warrior in the world. 3E lets me do that, and I'm very happy with 3E.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370815#post1370815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Might from My Hero Academia is a lot closer if you're going to make a comparison. During the series he takes on a mindless killer enemy who's been expertly engineered from the ground up by people who intimately know All Might's powers to specifically counter his strengths and exploit his weaknesses. All Might thrashes him in less than three minutes by just punching even more. After that though, he's basically spent, he's bluffing in threatening the remaining villains to surrender. Thankfully a cadre of professional heroes arrive as support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370842#post1370842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. Do you want to replicate Saitama's experience of becoming totally bored and disillusioned in fighting since he effortlessly overcomes every foe without fail?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> I explicitly want this.<br /> <br /> Sage:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If you don't want this, don't play Saitama.<br /> <br /> E3 shows you how to build a Dawn caste in Volfer. Volfer can take on any of the Essence 1 corebook enemies 1-on-1. Bring him up to the level of a starting character and he can take on most of the Essence 2 enemies. Volfer is a very solid Genus -- he's an unbelievably powerful warrior. S-class hero.<br /> <br /> You can build a powerful Solar Brawler like Volfer/Genus and be a powerful warrior who is still challenged. And you can invest your left-over charms into doing something cool (like Craft or Sail or Presence).<br /> <br /> E3 allows this. Look at the enemies in the Corebook. Look at the static difficulties. You don't have to go all-in to be a formiddable warrior. 3 Dexterity, 4 Brawl and artifact Smashfists makes you the greatest Brawler in Prasad after 3-4 Charms. Enjoy your epic fights. The drama is now about whether you find a foe who can beat you.<br /> <br /> <i>But... </i>if you want to start at the top, you can Supernal Brawl, go Dex 5/Brawl 5, spend 8 of your starting Charms on Brawl and be Saitama. <i>If you want to. </i>The drama is now about what you do in a world where nothing* can beat you.<br /> <br /> [*Only, you know, Ligier and the Unconquered Sun exist if the story really requires that you eat a beat-down. And Octavian and Ma-Ha-Suchi can probably take you down too. But you're super-good at fighting the Wandering Deathknight or a pair of Blood Apes or Fog Sharks.]<br /> <br /> The beauty of Exalted to me is that you are not a level 1 peasant. You are the champions of the gods who are <i>actually good</i> at what you choose to be good at. Not &quot;you will be good at this in six months after you've leveled up twice&quot;. Not &quot;you're good, but every NPC is actually better&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't like playing a character who is the best in the world, even though the system explicity shows me how to create a character who is merely above average because I want the characters in Exalted to be weaker&quot; is a complaint which <i>completely misses </i>the point of Exalted: no-one is forcing you to min-max combat over creating an organic character like the example in the Corebook character creation guide. And &quot;I want to optimize my character but still suck because the game is more fun when you fail but I don't want to be suboptimal&quot; is a viewpoint which is perfectly suited to Call of Cthulu or Paranoia (two games which I absolutely <i>adore -- </i>I love being the under-dog against impossible odds): it's not a bad viewpoint, it's not a wrong viewpoint, and if house-ruling Exalted that way makes it more fun for you then enjoy yourself. But it is not, and it never has been, the default viewpoint for <i>Exalted</i>.<br /> <br /> There is not a version of Exalted where a Griffen or a Zombie or a Blood Ape is a meaningful threat to a combat optimized starting Solar.<br /> There is not a version of Exalted where you <i>cannot </i>build a Solar <i>who is </i>meaningfully threatened by these foes <i>if that's what you want.</i><br /> There is not a version of Exalted which does not have a character creation example, and in that example the character is never combat optimized but an organically grown character.<br /> <br /> You've gone out of your way to ignore all the advice in the Corebook and push the game to its utmost limits, found that it still explicitly fits within the lore and mythos of the game world, and that in setting out to create an unstoppable warrior you've succeeded in creating an unstoppable warrior. I am sorry that this disappoints you, and I understand why you're frustrated -- if you tried to do this in D&amp;D for example, you wouldn't have succeeded and would be still able to enjoy the thrill of challenge. I get why you're disappointed: RPGs don't usually let you do this, and it wasn't an unreasonable expectation to think Exalted wouldn't let you do this. But Exalted is <i>explicitly</i> different from other RPGs in that it lets you succeed. That's a feature, not a bug: it is, in fact, the core-selling point of the game.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-28-2020, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T02:50:13-08:00","id":1370964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370955#post1370955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when people with different mindset are playing together (for example, a more JohnDoesque approach of &quot;let everyone pick what they want and have fun with it&quot; and a more Chaussesque approach of &quot;Well I have this kind of story in mind where I like character progression so you can have only one ability at 5 and Supernals are capped at Essence +1&quot;), we have this situation where everyone is at the same table but no one is playing the same game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to nitpick this:<br /> <br /> I am a firm believer in the Session 0.<br /> <br /> In my current 3E game, I gathered the players and explained that I'd like to run a Dragon-Blooded game, set in the Threshold where the PCs gather personal and political power, fight monsters and unearth a conspiracy which will indirectly affect the out-come of the impending Realm Civil War.<br /> <br /> The only player who was interested said they weren't particularly interested in combat, but wanted to play a Dragon-Blooded game where they would have the oppertunity to build their own Great House, and that they wouldn't mind helping to run NPCs in combat scenes so they could learn the system (having never played 3E) but didn't want to have to overly design their own character to stay alive. We discussed what themes we might be exploring and the level of adult content. I said that the plot I had in mind would work best with House Mnemon or Ragara (knowing full well that my player had only ever been interested in playing Ledaal or Nellens in the past), and they decided that House Mnemon suited the Dynasty building theme they wanted to riff-off, which meant I shifted the location of the game south a ways to tie in with Mnemon activity in Jiara. We disucssed the trait restrictions placed on Dynasts in 1st and 2nd edition (lots of minimum dot requirements in ancillary abilities in editions past), and that I had no expectation of reviving those as minimums but that I would be using them to inform how Dynastic society might work (so you're free not to take dots in Ride, but the other characters <i>will expect</i> that you are able to Ride). When Player 3 wanted to join in with a Solar, we didn't just say &quot;let everyone pick what they want&quot;, but we bargained them down to an Outcaste with an Oricalcum bow (and a Legendary Sized dinosaur mount).<br /> <br /> Role Playing is a communal experience. In my other games, I'm playing a Pilot (because our old pilot deserted and left us with no-one to fly the ship) and a Corpse (because no-one else wanted to be a Rogue in a game about <i>Dungeon Crawling</i>). It's important that you work together to tell a coherent story.<br /> <br /> So if one player turned up with a combat optimized Warstrider Pilot and another turned up without any combat abilities at all... I'd have to have a serious sit-down talk with them about what their expectations were and what compromises needed to be made to make the game work.<br /> <br /> But, <i><u><b>importantly</b></u>,</i> I think the system <i>should support </i>a combat optimized Warstrider Pilot and a complete Pacifist. I think saying &quot;this disparity is too difficult to manage and the game shouldn't support it&quot; is not the right way of addressing the issue. And I think you <i>could </i>run a fun game with a combat optimized character and a pacifist (although I personally would rather avoid the head-ache if possible).<br /> <br /> I don't like games where the ST dictates &quot;I want a game where this happens so I'm nerfing you to Melee 3&quot; (bad memories of the WW RPG chat right there).<br /> I do like games where all the players, including the ST, work together to make a communal experience (which might involve <i>agreeing </i>that no-one goes above Melee 3).<br /> <br /> (And if you're playing a Chaussesque game, I'm happy to give advice based on your house-rules. But if you don't explicity tell me what your house-rules are, then I'm going to assume you're playing the default setting, rules as written -- I'm not going to try to guess your house-rules.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-28-2020, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T04:34:51-08:00","id":1370977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370964#post1370964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to nitpick this:<br /> <br /> I am a firm believer in the Session 0.<br /> <br /> In my current 3E game, I gathered the players and explained that I'd like to run a Dragon-Blooded game, set in the Threshold where the PCs gather personal and political power, fight monsters and unearth a conspiracy which will indirectly affect the out-come of the impending Realm Civil War.<br /> <br /> The only player who was interested said they weren't particularly interested in combat, but wanted to play a Dragon-Blooded game where they would have the oppertunity to build their own Great House, and that they wouldn't mind helping to run NPCs in combat scenes so they could learn the system (having never played 3E) but didn't want to have to overly design their own character to stay alive. We discussed what themes we might be exploring and the level of adult content. I said that the plot I had in mind would work best with House Mnemon or Ragara (knowing full well that my player had only ever been interested in playing Ledaal or Nellens in the past), and they decided that House Mnemon suited the Dynasty building theme they wanted to riff-off, which meant I shifted the location of the game south a ways to tie in with Mnemon activity in Jiara. We disucssed the trait restrictions placed on Dynasts in 1st and 2nd edition (lots of minimum dot requirements in ancillary abilities in editions past), and that I had no expectation of reviving those as minimums but that I would be using them to inform how Dynastic society might work (so you're free not to take dots in Ride, but the other characters <i>will expect</i> that you are able to Ride). When Player 3 wanted to join in with a Solar, we didn't just say &quot;let everyone pick what they want&quot;, but we bargained them down to an Outcaste with an Oricalcum bow (and a Legendary Sized dinosaur mount).<br /> <br /> Role Playing is a communal experience. In my other games, I'm playing a Pilot (because our old pilot deserted and left us with no-one to fly the ship) and a Corpse (because no-one else wanted to be a Rogue in a game about <i>Dungeon Crawling</i>). It's important that you work together to tell a coherent story.<br /> <br /> So if one player turned up with a combat optimized Warstrider Pilot and another turned up without any combat abilities at all... I'd have to have a serious sit-down talk with them about what their expectations were and what compromises needed to be made to make the game work.<br /> <br /> But, <i><u><b>importantly</b></u>,</i> I think the system <i>should support </i>a combat optimized Warstrider Pilot and a complete Pacifist. I think saying &quot;this disparity is too difficult to manage and the game shouldn't support it&quot; is not the right way of addressing the issue. And I think you <i>could </i>run a fun game with a combat optimized character and a pacifist (although I personally would rather avoid the head-ache if possible).<br /> <br /> I don't like games where the ST dictates &quot;I want a game where this happens so I'm nerfing you to Melee 3&quot; (bad memories of the WW RPG chat right there).<br /> I do like games where all the players, including the ST, work together to make a communal experience (which might involve <i>agreeing </i>that no-one goes above Melee 3).<br /> <br /> (And if you're playing a Chaussesque game, I'm happy to give advice based on your house-rules. But if you don't explicity tell me what your house-rules are, then I'm going to assume you're playing the default setting, rules as written -- I'm not going to try to guess your house-rules.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I overall agree with you, but as I said not everyone is on the same page about agreeing to the story ahead, having limitations published official content, etc ... so it's not always this simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T05:07:47-08:00","id":1370983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370955#post1370955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally don't want to start an argument on this topic but Joseph is the best Jojo and anyone that thinks otherwise is <i>literally </i>a nazi (or a communist chose your side I'm actually not that virulent).</div> </div> </div> </div> He's my favourite too. I just prefer how the Stands were employed in Part 4 over the struggle against the Aztec Gods of Fitness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T05:17:01-08:00","id":1370984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370983#post1370983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> He's my favourite too. I just prefer how the Stands were employed in Part 4 over the struggle against the Aztec Gods of Fitness.</div> </div> </div> </div>We may have found common ground. I think Part 5 is even better than part 4 in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:16:43-08:00","id":1371000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370915#post1370915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also want to say for clarity that I think bloodapes are fine. If your immaclate monk had to spend 30 motes and 3 willpower fighting a pair of bloodapes, that's not a sustainable win. Bloodapes are not only reasonably dangerous, but absolutely show up in large groups as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've realised I screwed up in the WD fight anyway in that I forgot the 3i cost for a grapple gambit on top of the -2i for missing a decisive at 1-10i anyway. Apologies all.<br /> <br /> On a related note, it prompted me to quickly run the fight giving the Blood Apes stunts as most STs would (was following the precedent of the other fights previously) and it wasn't pretty \u2013 the first round grapple came off. Cue one dead Immaculate. So yeah, there's that...<br /> <br /> Would a 'Cockatrice and a 're-skinned' Wyld-Maddened Cockatrice' make more sense? Something that's not such an in-game institution? All I'm thinking is of a few notes giving STs the option of 'if your game starts at 11 [AKA the party of super swordy Dawn and his parry 7 Zenith BFF], here's how you could tweak this awesome creature to make it more dangerous'.<br /> <br /> Appreciate that unless it's simply 'add MAWOre dice' that's more work for massively busy devs and totally get John Doe's points about not wanting the world to scale artificially because an Exalted is supposed to be objectively awesome at what they're good at. Just musing on a way to make life easier for STs to come up with an adventure tailored to their group's expectations/abilities really.<br /> <br /> But I guess that's what session 0 does in effect...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:26:33-08:00","id":1371004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370962#post1370962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oYou've gone out of your way to ignore all the advice in the Corebook and push the game to its utmost limits, found that it still explicitly fits within the lore and mythos of the game world, and that in setting out to create an unstoppable warrior you've succeeded in creating an unstoppable warrior. I am sorry that this disappoints you, and I understand why you're frustrated -- if you tried to do this in D&amp;D for example, you wouldn't have succeeded and would be still able to enjoy the thrill of challenge. I get why you're disappointed: RPGs don't usually let you do this, and it wasn't an unreasonable expectation to think Exalted wouldn't let you do this. But Exalted is <i>explicitly</i> different from other RPGs in that it lets you succeed. That's a feature, not a bug: it is, in fact, the core-selling point of the game.[/spoiler]</div> </div> </div> </div>I do also like that if you really focus hard you can become somebody that has some real weight in the setting, I just don\u2019t like how easy it is to incidentally tack that on to another character concept. You\u2019re the greatest loremaster in a generation, maybe several generations, whos sorcery and knowledge bend the world, who\u2019s discovered hidden meanings and lost secrets that it was thought could never be recovered. And also you\u2019re a combat 