d that isn\u2019t bloodapes.</div> </div> </div> </div>[New Shard Brainstorming] The world is actually a Blood-Ape PEACH","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T08:27:03-08:00","id":1371021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371004#post1371004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do also like that if you really focus hard you can become somebody that has some real weight in the setting, I just don\u2019t like how easy it is to incidentally tack that on to another character concept. You\u2019re the greatest loremaster in a generation, maybe several generations, whos sorcery and knowledge bend the world, who\u2019s discovered hidden meanings and lost secrets that it was thought could never be recovered. And also you\u2019re a combat god, and so is everyone else in the circle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> XP-based character creation mostly solves this issue I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T08:31:04-08:00","id":1371022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371004#post1371004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do also like that if you really focus hard you can become somebody that has some real weight in the setting, I just don\u2019t like how easy it is to incidentally tack that on to another character concept. You\u2019re the greatest loremaster in a generation, maybe several generations, whos sorcery and knowledge bend the world, who\u2019s discovered hidden meanings and lost secrets that it was thought could never be recovered. And also you\u2019re a combat god, and so is everyone else in the circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear what you're saying and I respect your point of view.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, you are correct: you get enough dots on the page to do this.<br /> <br /> But to fall on the old, &quot;roll-playing&quot; trope... can you? Should you? Do you?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If the Session 0 expectation is that everyone is &quot;also one of the fierciest combatants in existence, just because&quot;, then I think it's a good thing that Exalted supports this. You can be great at combat AND great at something else which is interesting. Many games make you choose (like the Careers in Edge of the Empire), and these sorts of players don't choose the &quot;something interesting&quot;. But if you do that, then you're playing Saitama. You're playing the 2E game of &quot;you succeed, these are the unforseen concequences&quot;. I loved 2E, I'd happily play that game. This is my default Exalted expectation, to be honest.<br /> <br /> Or, you don't. You don't need to take Dexterity 5, Melee 5, Specailty in Swords, Awareness 5, Specialty in Join Battle. It's <i>completely </i>unneccessary. The game I'm STing has nearly hit Essence 3 on Dexterity 3, Melee 3, Awareness 2 (granted she's raised that with Dragon Experience) and no Excellency. Danireya has faced down a Nephwrack and a Second Circle Demon (socially) and beaten a bear to death in melee. No-one is forcing you to become a combat god. Even the combat focused characters, like Isthus (a &quot;properly terrifying Exalted Assassin&quot;) and Volfer (the <i>signature</i> Dawn caste) are not built 5/5+1.<br /> <br /> You're making a rod for your own back.<br /> <br /> No-one is telling you to make your loremaster a combat god.<br /> <br /> Character Creation begins on Page 120: &quot;Before you begin, ask your Storyteller about her plans&quot;. Step 1 of character creation is to come up with a heroic concept for your character, then you assign dots to match that concept. I freely concede that mechanically, it's easy to bolt &quot;combat god&quot; onto a concept when talking about assigning dots. But when actually following the character creation rules, step by step for an actual game? I think you have to go seriously out of your way and into min-max territory to do this.<br /> <br /> And I get how an inexperienced group might over-shoot: in Mutants and Masterminds you have to build to hit the absolute limit of your combat ability, because that's where the game is balanced (same for Pathfinder 1 and most versions of D&amp;D). If you're used to having to optimize to stay alive, then you're going to overshoot in 3E -- and playing past editions of Exalted isn't much help with that. And the lack of a Storytelling chapter does not help.<br /> <br /> But you're going out of your way to create a problem. You can't even get to Melee 5 without spending bonus points. If your bookish loremaster is already a renowned swordsman well above the level of a trained soldier (Melee 3)... then follow the rules of the game: speak to your ST, respect your character concept and don't spend bonus points to make them the greatest swordsman in the world. Going out of your way to find a heroic archtype to justify why your bookish loremaster is also an unstoppable swordsman is hard.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T09:14:25-08:00","id":1371030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/