=1371022#post1371022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hear what you're saying and I respect your point of view.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, you are correct: you get enough dots on the page to do this.<br /> <br /> But to fall on the old, &amp;quot;roll-playing&amp;quot; trope... can you? Should you? Do you?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If the Session 0 expectation is that everyone is &amp;quot;also one of the fierciest combatants in existence, just because&amp;quot;, then I think it's a good thing that Exalted supports this. You can be great at combat AND great at something else which is interesting. Many games make you choose (like the Careers in Edge of the Empire), and these sorts of players don't choose the &amp;quot;something interesting&amp;quot;. But if you do that, then you're playing Saitama. You're playing the 2E game of &amp;quot;you succeed, these are the unforseen concequences&amp;quot;. I loved 2E, I'd happily play that game. This is my default Exalted expectation, to be honest.<br /> <br /> Or, you don't. You don't need to take Dexterity 5, Melee 5, Specailty in Swords, Awareness 5, Specialty in Join Battle. It's <i>completely </i>unneccessary. The game I'm STing has nearly hit Essence 3 on Dexterity 3, Melee 3, Awareness 2 (granted she's raised that with Dragon Experience) and no Excellency. Danireya has faced down a Nephwrack and a Second Circle Demon (socially) and beaten a bear to death in melee. No-one is forcing you to become a combat god. Even the combat focused characters, like Isthus (a &amp;quot;properly terrifying Exalted Assassin&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and Volfer (the <i>signature</i> Dawn caste) are not built 5/5+1.<br /> <br /> You're making a rod for your own back.<br /> <br /> No-one is telling you to make your loremaster a combat god.<br /> <br /> Character Creation begins on Page 120: &amp;quot;Before you begin, ask your Storyteller about her plans&amp;quot;. Step 1 of character creation is to come up with a heroic concept for your character, then you assign dots to match that concept. I freely concede that mechanically, it's easy to bolt &amp;quot;combat god&amp;quot; onto a concept when talking about assigning dots. But when actually following the character creation rules, step by step for an actual game? I think you have to go seriously out of your way and into min-max territory to do this.<br /> <br /> And I get how an inexperienced group might over-shoot: in Mutants and Masterminds you have to build to hit the absolute limit of your combat ability, because that's where the game is balanced (same for Pathfinder 1 and most versions of D&amp;D). If you're used to having to optimize to stay alive, then you're going to overshoot in 3E -- and playing past editions of Exalted isn't much help with that. And the lack of a Storytelling chapter does not help.<br /> <br /> But you're going out of your way to create a problem. You can't even get to Melee 5 without spending bonus points. If your bookish loremaster is already a renowned swordsman well above the level of a trained soldier (Melee 3)... then follow the rules of the game: speak to your ST, respect your character concept and don't spend bonus points to make them the greatest swordsman in the world. Going out of your way to find a heroic archtype to justify why your bookish loremaster is also an unstoppable swordsman is hard.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t personally experience it from the player side of the screen. My two Ex3 Solars so far have started with 1-2 dots in a combat ability and 3 dex. One was a Dawn even. It\u2019s from the ST side where I\u2019m seeing this from and having some issues. They\u2019re not issues I can\u2019t deal with, I just don\u2019t like the waste of word count or how it can trivialize encounters to the point where they don\u2019t even cost motes. It would be eminently easier if people did build for concept rather than mechanics, and made sure their concept didn\u2019t also include one of the greatest fighters in the direction. <br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t help that the ability minimums for so many cool charms are so high, like even Iron Raptor needs 4 melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T09:40:04-08:00","id":1371033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371021#post1371021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> XP-based character creation mostly solves this issue I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Does it take a greater percentage of your starting resources to get those 5s?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T09:48:32-08:00","id":1371036,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> My players hated it though. Too fiddly.<br /> And it does mean people don't want to &quot;waste&quot; points on Sail, Bureaucracy, etc, so you end up with rather dull characters in some cases.<br /> <br /> I actually think the best thing is to not give a discount on Ability scores over 3 for being Favoured/Caste.<br /> Then instead of being able to have 7 abilities at 5, people can only have 3. Which is definitely enough to be the best at whatever they want to be the best at, but not to randomly be amazing swordsmen/socialites/etc as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-28-2020, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T10:21:26-08:00","id":1371042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371033#post1371033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? Does it take a greater percentage of your starting resources to get those 5s?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you raise favored abilities to 5, you get 6xp's worth of stuff per BP. If you buy Charms, you get 2xp's worth of stuff per BP.<br /> <br /> Turns out, if you eliminate the gross efficiency disparity between the &quot;use chargen resources to buy more numbers&quot; and &quot;use chargen resources to buy options that are actually cool and interesting to use in play&quot; options, people will be more willing to go with the latter.<br /> <br /> (But limiting the XP total of stuff they get to the amount accessible to characters made with a more organic approach also helps, yes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T14:57:22-08:00","id":1371093,"title":"","content":"I agree with aluminiumtrioxid that the fact that xp to BP ratios incentivize you to take 5s at character creation, and this isn't ideal. But in my current (and first) game we used XP-based character creation and I still had multiple 5s (I forget how many - I have tons now as I am Essence 4). In fact I wonder if one could go in the other direction, with some house rule where getting 5s costs extra XP at character creation - sort of going in the reverse direction.<br /> <br /> I definitely think experience in other games is a big factor, as JohnDoe244 suggested. But I don't think &quot;build to hit the absolute limit of your combat ability&quot; is a good description of the problem. In games like D&amp;D, maxing out your combat ability requires carefully weighing different choices against each other and looking for powerful combinations. That helps a lot in Exalted too, but the problem we're talking about here is more like &quot;That ability looks useful - I guess I'll take a four or five in it.&quot; That habit is a lot harder to break!<br /> <br /> It's certainly true, though, that it would help to pay closer attention to the &quot;5 = best in the world&quot; idea at character creation. But if your character concept involves combat in any way, it seems quite easy to spend a few points in character creation, end up with 4s in key abilities and attributes, and be very powerful, when you have so many to start with. Most core concepts require you to take, at most, a 5 in one or two abilities, some high attributes, and a pile of Charms - you'll have plenty left over, and the (perhaps) trap of shoring up your combat skills is easy to fall into. <br /> <br /> The fact Chausse mentioned that combat protects from death is also very relevant. I would add that a starting player can be a lot more sure that, if they put points in combat, those points will help them out, even if they don't understand and master the combat system, then they can be for abilities relevant to other systems like social abilities or Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T16:18:22-08:00","id":1371108,"title":"","content":"Pointed question for people who want to diminish the 5eness of chargen: <br /> How do you intend to tackle the issue of <i>so many</i> charms needing [Ability] \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022? Pretty much everything ESS 2 and up in Solars does on top of a bunch of stuff at ESS 1. <br /> How are you going to prevent players from maxing out combat at an intermediate level and then immediately blowing their splat XP into Fight Good \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022? <br /> Are you going to actually be able to solve the problem, or just kick it down the road a bit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T17:43:49-08:00","id":1371123,"title":"","content":"Well, not throwing fights at the PCs that they feel they <i>need</i> Awareness 5, Melee 5, Dodge 5, Resistance 5, Athletics 5 to <i>handle</i> will probably help. And you're right, <i>most </i>of the &quot;Damn I want that&quot; Charms of an Ability in 3e require four or five dots. But I'd also argue that more than a few <i>really cool</i> Charms need no more than Ability 3 to pick up, and that it's really easy to lose one's appreciation of even a really good dinner if all one is staring at is the dessert.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love Crafty Observation Method, Living Shadow Preparedness, and Spurious Presence, even if they're no Fate-Shifting Solar Ar\u00eate, and I feel that players might enjoy them as well if they can curb their instinct to have dessert first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T18:08:39-08:00","id":1371127,"title":"","content":"So, you're all deep into a discussion about how to encourage lower defenses for PC's. This was prompted by the observation that there are a great number of cool NPC's that can't be used in fights because they'd never be able to hit the PC's.<br /> <br /> Is there some particular reason why we're not discussing the hows and whys of adding one to four points to their attack values, or is it just the way that the conversation happened to develop?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 02-28-2020, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T18:27:20-08:00","id":1371131,"title":"","content":"Because then those same enemies are pretty much TPKs for low-op parties or mortals, instead of \u201cmerely\u201d dangerous. Plus it feels kinda immersion-breaking for the world to conveniently scale with you; it\u2019s the same reason folks groused about marauders* in <i>Oblivion</i> wearing Daedric armor as they mug you for coins, or Dragon Quest games where they never stop throwing slimes at you but palette-swap the things and tack some more hit points or an immunity to magic on so it remains level-appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> _____________<br /> *This post originally said \u201cbandits,\u201d but I remembered that bandits only wear light armor, and the light armor-equivalent for Daedric is Glass, which doesn\u2019t sound as impressive if you\u2019re not an Elder Scrolls player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-28-2020, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T18:45:07-08:00","id":1371140,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370962#post1370962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370962#post1370962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I explicitly want this.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I mean, if that\u2019s the sort of story you want to tell. In my case, I played a powerful brawler because I wanted to have fun brawling things.</span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370962#post1370962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If you don't want this, don't play Saitama.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>I understand that this is a sort of \u2018coming out of character creation having already caught the car\u2019 situation common to E3. I get that.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">E3 shows you how to build a Dawn caste in Volfer. Volfer can take on any of the Essence 1 corebook enemies 1-on-1. Bring him up to the level of a starting character and he can take on most of the Essence 2 enemies. Volfer is a very solid Genus -- he's an unbelievably powerful warrior. S-class hero.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can build a powerful Solar Brawler like Volfer/Genus and be a powerful warrior who is still challenged. And you can invest your left-over charms into doing something cool (like Craft or Sail or Presence).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">E3 allows this. Look at the enemies in the Corebook. Look at the static difficulties. You don't have to go all-in to be a formiddable warrior. 3 Dexterity, 4 Brawl and artifact Smashfists makes you the greatest Brawler in Prasad after 3-4 Charms. Enjoy your epic fights. The drama is now about whether you find a foe who can beat you.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Right, I follow you. It\u2019s true that with minimal investment into combat fights can be more dynamic and contested. I\u2019ve seen this first hand in my games.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>But... </i>if you want to start at the top, you can Supernal Brawl, go Dex 5/Brawl 5, spend 8 of your starting Charms on Brawl and be Saitama. <i>If you want to. </i>The drama is now about what you do in a world where nothing* can beat you.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Where are my epic fights, though? They\u2019re not here, certainly. There is no longer a dramatic back and forth. Here we\u2019ve reached the domain of Parry 6 and Leaping Tiger Attack. Fights might not even be two rounds, as my experience with Simurgh has shown me. We\u2019ve got alpha strikes online at this level.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The beauty of Exalted to me is that you are not a level 1 peasant. You are the champions of the gods who are <i>actually good</i> at what you choose to be good at. Not &quot;you will be good at this in six months after you've leveled up twice&quot;. Not &quot;you're good, but every NPC is actually better&quot;.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Yeah, I love that part of Exalted. Being one of the best in the world from character generation is a fantastic feeling. I love having the ability to say something like \u2018my character is the most dangerous weapon in Kamthahar\u2019 while making him and then have it be the plain-faced, unexaggerated truth when it comes time to play.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;I don't like playing a character who is the best in the world, even though the system explicitly shows me how to create a character who is merely above average because I want the characters in Exalted to be weaker&quot; is a complaint which <i>completely misses </i>the point of Exalted: </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Right, and it\u2019s also very much not my complaint. I have not stated whatsoever that I want the characters in Exalted to be weaker, nor have I said that I don\u2019t like playing a character who is the best in the world.</b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And &quot;I want to optimize my character but still suck because the game is more fun when you fail but I don't want to be suboptimal&quot; is a viewpoint which is perfectly suited to Call of Cthulu or Paranoia: it's not a bad viewpoint, it's not a wrong viewpoint, and if house-ruling Exalted that way makes it more fun for you then enjoy yourself. But it is not, and it never has been, the default viewpoint for <i>Exalted</i>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fascinatingly, this is also very much not my viewpoint. This feels totally out of left-field from what I said in my last post and I\u2019m not really sure how interpreted this as my desire.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is not a version of Exalted where a Griffen or a Zombie or a Blood Ape is a meaningful threat to a combat optimized starting Solar.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is not a version of Exalted where you <i>cannot </i>build a Solar <i>who is </i>meaningfully threatened by these foes <i>if that's what you want.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is not a version of Exalted which does not have a character creation example, and in that example the character is never combat optimized but an organically grown character.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>I\u2019m not advocating for Solars to be weaker. I\u2019m really not sure where you got that from.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You've gone out of your way to ignore all the advice in the Corebook and push the game to its utmost limits, found that it still explicitly fits within the lore and mythos of the game world, and that in setting out to create an unstoppable warrior you've succeeded in creating an unstoppable warrior. I am sorry that this disappoints you, and I understand why you're frustrated -- </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>I\u2019m not sure what your intended tone was here, but you\u2019re coming across as incredibly patronizing. On top of that, you seem to be deliberately ignoring the point I was trying to make in my post and ascribing behaviors to me that seem like complete conjecture on your part. I don\u2019t see how making a Brawl Supernal Solar \u2018ignores all of the advice in the corebook\u2019 or \u2018pushes the game to its utmost limits.\u2019 Isn\u2019t there a whole sidebar about not being afraid to start the game with 5s in Attributes and Abilities?</b></span></span><b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The fact of the matter is that, when I set out to create my character, I wanted to play (and I quote) \u201ca big badass dude who has bombastic awesome fights with powerful Dragonblooded and behemoths and giant godlings and takes on armies with nothing but his bare hands.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I built this character following the rules of character generation. Turns out, heavy investment into combat makes combat boring and repetitive and totally uninteresting. I think that this is a design flaw. Surely I should be able to play an unstoppable warrior and still get to have cool battles, right?</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> I get why you're disappointed: RPGs don't usually let you do this, and it wasn't an unreasonable expectation to think Exalted wouldn't let you do this.<br /> <br /> <b>Many RPGs would allow me to create the character I want and play them in the exact manner I want to play them.</b><br /> <br /> But Exalted is <i>explicitly</i> different from other RPGs in that it lets you succeed. That's a feature, not a bug: it is, in fact, the core-selling point of the game.<br /> <br /> <b>I was sold on Exalted from the player side because I thought that it would let me play a powerful world-shaping character and have dynamic and cinematic kung-fu battles for the fate of love and empire and destiny. My experience was that ultimately combat became boring and one-note. I think that Exalted should reward investment in combat by providing tools to make combat more interesting and enjoyable, as opposed to numerical advantages that grant the character unflappable supremacy over all opponents.</b></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T01:21:41-08:00","id":1371208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371108#post1371108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pointed question for people who want to diminish the 5eness of chargen:<br /> How do you intend to tackle the issue of <i>so many</i> charms needing [Ability] \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022? Pretty much everything ESS 2 and up in Solars does on top of a bunch of stuff at ESS 1.<br /> How are you going to prevent players from maxing out combat at an intermediate level and then immediately blowing their splat XP into Fight Good \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022?<br /> Are you going to actually be able to solve the problem, or just kick it down the road a bit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually don't care about the Ability requirement for a Charm as long as the character seems competent enough in the story to learn it. I usually accept that someone with Ability-1 can take a Charm, or Ability-2 if they give a good explanation on how they demonstrated their skills about the ability in question to learn the Charm.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar872_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"872\" data-vbnamecard=\"872\">Apromor</a> It's a solution I use as well as trying to un-specialize a little bits my players. In the link in my signature you can find a small part of my home-brew where I try to put all the useful statistics for NPCs depending on how strong I need them to be. I don't think the case mentioned by CountAlucard (aka every bandit is godlike) is likely to appear in my games, but for &quot;special magic characters&quot; I actually don't care to give them more dices to attack, damage and such because no one really knows their scores and what they are supposed to do exactly anyway (in my playerbease at least)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T04:29:08-08:00","id":1371221,"title":"","content":"As a Storyteller, I want to say things... As a moderator I want to point out that this thread's been off topic for four pages.<br /> <br /> *Explodes*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T04:43:21-08:00","id":1371222,"title":"","content":"[EDIT]<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371221#post1371221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Storyteller, I want to say things... As a moderator I want to point out that this thread's been off topic for four pages.<br /> <br /> *Explodes*</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was typing when you posted this and didn't see it. Could you maybe split this off into its own thread, please?<br /> <br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371108#post1371108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pointed question for people who want to diminish the 5eness of chargen: <br /> How do you intend to tackle the issue of <i>so many</i> charms needing [Ability] \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022? Pretty much everything ESS 2 and up in Solars does on top of a bunch of stuff at ESS 1. <br /> How are you going to prevent players from maxing out combat at an intermediate level and then immediately blowing their splat XP into Fight Good \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022? <br /> Are you going to actually be able to solve the problem, or just kick it down the road a bit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Charms have ridiculously high minimums, yes.<br /> <br /> Does your character concept need those Charms? Because Excellent Strike and Dipping Swallow Defence on Melee 3/Dex 3 makes you pretty deadly. Yes, you can't shoot beams of golden light from your sword... but you don't need to if your Twilight Scholar is fighting Brides of Ahlat, Fog Sharks and Claw Striders. Intermediate combat skill is enough.<br /> <br /> Give that Twilight plenty of chance to use Lore and Medicine Charms -- start them on the Wyld Shaping Charm tree and Sorcerous Workings and they probably won't buy combat abilities if they already feel badass.<br /> <br /> If you're winning every combat encounter but struggling with mental and social encounters, why would you dump more XP into combat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371127#post1371127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you're all deep into a discussion about how to encourage lower defenses for PC's. This was prompted by the observation that there are a great number of cool NPC's that can't be used in fights because they'd never be able to hit the PC's.<br /> <br /> Is there some particular reason why we're not discussing the hows and whys of adding one to four points to their attack values, or is it just the way that the conversation happened to develop?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's Dragon Ball Z. PCs and ST in an arms race. The players want to succeed, the ST doesn't let them, PCs get bigger numbers, ST gets bigger numbers until every random encounter is between war gods who can destroy planets with a gesture.<br /> <br /> If the PCs want to be good at something, arbitrarily upping the difficulty to under-cut them is bad form.<br /> <br /> Also, it's a case of using the wrong opponents. There's no need to add four dice to a Blood Ape when you can fight Octavian. There's no need to add four dice to Octavian when you can fight Ligier. There's no need to add four dice to Ligier when you can fight the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> Sure, if you really like an iconic enemy but your PCs are overspecced to deal with them, you can just up their stats. But if you're doing that every encounter you're really going to wonk the power-curve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371093#post1371093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly true, though, that it would help to pay closer attention to the &amp;quot;5 = best in the world&amp;quot; idea at character creation. But if your character concept involves combat in any way, it seems quite easy to spend a few points in character creation, end up with 4s in key abilities and attributes, and be very powerful, when you have so many to start with. Most core concepts require you to take, at most, a 5 in one or two abilities, some high attributes, and a pile of Charms - you'll have plenty left over, and the (perhaps) trap of shoring up your combat skills is easy to fall into.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to build characters with nine 5s and a 1.<br /> <br /> I love Fives.<br /> <br /> But I take those 5s expressly and explicitly because I intend to trample over NPCs with one hand tied behind my back in those specific areas. These are the vectors which my character will use to try and change the world. Every other stat represents the areas I can be meaningfully challenged in -- and I expect to be challenged in those areas.<br /> <br /> But that's a Session 0 thing. <br /> <br /> Certainly the published NPCs (and therefore the &quot;default&quot; playstyle) are made with only one or two fives -- and following this playstyle is my advice to anyone who doesn't like playing with nine 5s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371140#post1371140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure what your intended tone was here, but you\u2019re coming across as incredibly patronizing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not my intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371140#post1371140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, I follow you. It\u2019s true that with minimal investment into combat fights can be more dynamic and contested. I\u2019ve seen this first hand in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. That's 99% of my point -- if this is the only thing we agree on, then I'm satisfied TBH. I'm going to respond to your other points because I think I can help you: but if you don't want my help then just say so and I'll shut up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371140#post1371140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are my epic fights, though? They\u2019re not here, certainly. There is no longer a dramatic back and forth. Here we\u2019ve reached the domain of Parry 6 and Leaping Tiger Attack. Fights might not even be two rounds, as my experience with Simurgh has shown me. We\u2019ve got alpha strikes online at this level.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your ask is stats for Ligier and more enemies like Mahicara, then great. I back you 100%.<br /> <br /> If you're up for it, I'd love to see an Arena fight of your character vs Octavian or your character vs four Experienced Dynasts or your character vs Mahicara.<br /> <br /> Heck, post your character and I'll run an appropriate fight myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371140#post1371140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not advocating for Solars to be weaker. I\u2019m really not sure where you got that from.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371140#post1371140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of that, you seem to be deliberately ignoring the point I was trying to make in my post and ascribing behaviors to me that seem like complete conjecture on your part. I don\u2019t see how making a Brawl Supernal Solar \u2018ignores all of the advice in the corebook\u2019 or \u2018pushes the game to its utmost limits.\u2019 Isn\u2019t there a whole sidebar about not being afraid to start the game with 5s in Attributes and Abilities?<br /> <br /> The fact of the matter is that, when I set out to create my character, I wanted to play (and I quote) \u201ca big badass dude who has bombastic awesome fights with powerful Dragonblooded and behemoths and giant godlings and takes on armies with nothing but his bare hands.\u201d<br /> <br /> I built this character following the rules of character generation. Turns out, heavy investment into combat makes combat boring and repetitive and totally uninteresting. I think that this is a design flaw. Surely I should be able to play an unstoppable warrior and still get to have cool battles, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've picked the most powerful splat (Solars), picked the most powerful combat subclass (Dawns), optimized for combat to be the best in the world (when the Corebook example of an assassin describes Melee 4 as &quot;properly terrifying Exalted&quot;). You've made &quot;prodigy even among other prodigies of his field, a living legend whose feats might defy belief. [...] an unsurpassed master&quot;. You've done so having read the very sidebar on page 149 that states a professional soldier only has two dots, and someone able to dominate a kingdom can do so at three dots, and that you should let your concept determine your dot ratings.<br /> <br /> You can fight, and beat, &quot;powerful Dragonblooded and behemoths and giant godlings and takes on armies with nothing but [your] bare hands&quot;.<br /> <br /> You find this boring... Because you win in two rounds.<br /> <br /> You don't want to be weaker, but accept fights would be more &quot;dramatic&quot; if you were.<br /> <br /> I'm not deliberately misunderstanding, but you're right: I don't understand.<br /> <br /> You don't want battles to be &quot;repetitive&quot; and &quot;totally uninteresting&quot;: I don't understand why your fights are uninteresting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371140#post1371140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many RPGs would allow me to create the character I want and play them in the exact manner I want to play them.</div> </div> </div> </div>An example would <i>really</i> help me. No example too obscure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371140#post1371140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was sold on Exalted from the player side because I thought that it would let me play a powerful world-shaping character and have dynamic and cinematic kung-fu battles for the fate of love and empire and destiny. My experience was that ultimately combat became boring and one-note. I think that Exalted should reward investment in combat by providing tools to make combat more interesting and enjoyable, as opposed to numerical advantages that grant the character unflappable supremacy over all opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear:<br /> <br /> You don't think the published Solar Brawl Charms give you tools to make fights more interesting? And you don't want optimized Solars to have &quot;unflappable supremacy over all opponents&quot;, but you also don't want Solars to be weaker?<br /> <br /> Heaven Thunder Hammer, Thunderclap Rush Attack, Ox-stunning Blow, Force Rending Strike, Blade Rebuking Wrath, Sledgehammer Fist Punch, Burning Proof of Authority, Cancel the Apocalypse, Dragon Coil Technique, Superior Violent Knowledge, Apocalpse Flare Attack, Ascendant Battle Visage... not doing it for you? Why?<br /> <br /> Can you explain this slowly to me? (Pretend I don't know anything about Exalted: I think our experiences are so vastly different that we're talking past each other.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-29-2020, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T15:56:45-08:00","id":1372048,"title":"","content":"I made a fight with an Essence 3 Fire Dragon + Steel Devil stylist against a pair of bloodapes. It got....weeeeird.<br /> <br /> The Fire Dragon Stylist has artifacts, 3/5/3 physical stats and 5 wits.<br /> <br /> fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Fire Dragon uses 15m for Flash Fire and Naked Fang Draw, rolling 13+3 for 7 and 12, taking the 12 for a total of 15i<br /> <br /> Bloodape1 rolls 8 dice for 6i<br /> Bloodape2 rolls 8 dice for 7i<br /> <br /> FD maxes out charge with an additional 7i reflexive and uses 7m to enter FD form.<br /> <br /> FD 8i 14/4 6wp 8 charge<br /> BA1 6i<br /> BA2 7i<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> Fire Dragon anima rolls no damage.<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon will wither BA1 with 2m excellency, 1m fire anima, and 3m Double Attack technique. Rolling 18 dice for 7. 7-3-2-1=1, so we have 1 extra damage from overflow and triple attack technique hits. TAT adds 2+charge/2+Dex+charge/2=15 damage.<br /> <br /> 29 damage - 7 soak= 22 rolled damage. Rolling gets 11 successes of damage after rerolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rather than go up 17i, FD will instead elect to use Steel Devil Strike for 5m 1wp. Rolling 11 dice +3 successes for SDS, getting 8 against a parry of 1, and due to Flash Fire Technique adding 5 damage to the roll.<br /> <br /> Rolling 22 damage for 10 damage, killing BA1.<br /> <br /> FD enters Fire Aura<br /> <br /> FD 8i 7/0 5wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 7i<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> BA2 will use Principle of Motion to make two attacks against FD, spending a willpower on each, rolling 11 dice on the first for 6, hitting FD, but with a 1 on the roll FD will use Flame Flicker Stance to add +1 parry and negate it, inflicting no onslaught.<br /> <br /> Attack 2 rolls 8 and hits. FD will use 3m 3charge to parry it anyway with Twin-Blade Defense.<br /> <br /> FD 8i 1/0 5wp 5 charge<br /> BA2 7i<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> FD 8i 1/5 5wp 5 charge<br /> BA2 7i<br /> <br /> FD anima deals 1L<br /> <br /> FD withers BA2 with 3m DAT, rolling 16 dice for 10. 10-3-2-1=4. So TAT activates with 4 extra successes. Damage total of 21 after soak, rolling for 10 damage, crashing BA2. FD elects to refill charge with 3 of the initiative.<br /> <br /> FD 21i 1/2 5wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 -3i 1L<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> BA2 will use PoM. Attacking once with 11 dice for 5 and missing, and again with a willpower for 7, hitting.<br /> <br /> Rolling 8 damage for 7, pulling out of crash.<br /> <br /> FD 14i 1/2 5wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 4i 1L<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> FD 14i 1/7 5wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 4i 1L<br /> <br /> <br /> Fire Dragon attacks with 3m DAT, rolling 16 dice for 10. Rolling 25 damage for 14. Rather than go up 15i FD elects to launch a 5m 1wp SDS. The autosuccesses alone being enough to make it, then rolling 15i for.............one......damage......<br /> <br /> FD 14i 0/0 3wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 -10i 1L<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> BA2 will wither with Brutal Ape Pounce, rolling 11 dice for only 3 and missing.<br /> <br /> FD 14i 0/0 3wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 -10i 1L<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ===========<br /> <br /> FD 14i 0/5 3wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 -10i 1L<br /> <br /> FD rolls no anima damage again!<br /> <br /> FD will just opt to withering strike, rolling 16 dice for 6, hitting, and then rolling 9 damage for 2.....<br /> <br /> FD 17i 0/5 3wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 -10i 1L<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> BA will wither with BAP, rolling 11 dice for 6 and hitting. Rolling 7 damage for 5<br /> <br /> FD 12i 0/5 3wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 -4i 1L<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ===========<br /> FD 12i 0/10 3wp 8 charge<br /> BA2 -4i 1L<br /> <br /> Fire Anima deals 1L<br /> <br /> FD will attack again with 3m DAT, 1m excellency. Rolling 17 dice for 10, then rolling 25 damage for 13 after rerolls.<br /> <br /> FD will use 5m 1wp SDS, and 1m excellency. Autohitting and rolling 14i for 8 damage, slaying the ape.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> The next fight is the same guy, without artifacts this time, fighting a pair of Vaktri and trying to conserve motes and willpower as well as not flare anima. Priceless art around, wanting to keep a low profile, something like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> FD uses Naked Fang Draw for 13+3, getting an awesome 16i, dumping the full 7 into charge.<br /> <br /> Vaktri rolls 8 for 6i<br /> Vaktri rolls 8 for 5i<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> FD 9i 2/35 6wp 8 charge<br /> V1 6i<br /> V2 5i<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ============<br /> Fire Dragon attacks V1 with 3m TAT, 1m excellency, V1 defends with 5m 3i Unbreakable Gemstone Armor. Rolling 16 dice for only 5, but with 12 dice coming up non-successes Vaktri gains 12 soak. Even still, with a raw damage of 24 FD still rolls 3 dice for damage, getting 2, and with the 3 extra lost for Searing Edge, crashes V1.<br /> <br /> FD 13i 2/31 6wp 8 charge<br /> V1 -2i<br /> V2 5i<br /> <br /> --------<br /> V2 ueses Diamond Needle Strike for 7m to decisive Fire Dragon. Rolling 11 dice for 7 and hitting, but with 3m Flame Flicker Stance cancels the attack with no onslaught. Due to Fire Dragon Form V2 loses 4i.<br /> <br /> FD 13i 2/28 6wp 8 charge<br /> V1 -2i<br /> V2 1i<br /> <br /> --------<br /> V1 attempts the same, rolling 11 dice for 6, and missing.<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ============<br /> FD 13i 2/33 6wp 8 charge<br /> V1 -2i<br /> V2 1i<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon launches a decisive Firey Blade Attack against V1, with a 1m excellency. Rolling 12 dice for 8 and easily hitting, then rolling 9i for 6L, and igniting V1.<br /> <br /> FD 3i 0/29 6wp 8 charge<br /> V1 -2i 6L<br /> V2 1i<br /> <br /> --------<br /> V2 will try to wither FD, spending a willpower, rolling 11 dice for 8. With Flame Flicker not enough to block it, FD uses 3m 2 charge Twin Blade Defense to cancel the attack.<br /> <br /> FD 3i 0/26 6wp 6 charge<br /> V1 -2i 6L<br /> V2 1i<br /> --------<br /> <br /> V1 rolls 9 dice to avoid being burned, failing with 4, and then dieing to another 3L levels<br /> <br /> FD 3i 0/26 6wp 6 charge<br /> V2 1i<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ============<br /> FD 3i 0/31 6wp 6 charge<br /> V2 1i<br /> <br /> FD will attack with 3m TAT, 1m excellency. Rolling 16 dice for........2, missing.<br /> <br /> FD 3i 0/28 6wp 6 charge<br /> V2 1i<br /> --------<br /> <br /> Vaktri will attack with 11 dice and a willpower, rolling 7 and hitting, but getting canceled by 3m Flame Flicker.<br /> <br /> FD 3i 0/25 6wp 6 charge<br /> V2 1i<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ============<br /> FD 3i 0/30 6wp 6 charge<br /> V2 1i<br /> <br /> FD will attack with 3m TAT, 1m excellency. Rolling 16 dice for 11. Then rolling 16 damage for 9, crashing V2.<br /> <br /> FD 18i 0/26 6wp 6 charge<br /> V2 -8i<br /> <br /> --------<br /> V2 will attack with 11 dice and willpower, rolling 4 and missing.<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ============<br /> FD 18i 0/31 6wp 6 charge<br /> V2 1i<br /> <br /> <br /> FD will try a decisive rolling 11 dice for 7, hitting, then 18i for 7, slaying Vaktri.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> It's not apparent to me that between the Fire Aura of Flame Flicker Stance and the defensive power of Twin-Blade Defense you really can afford to just not pump your parry when you're being attacked. Either way I think you're pretty solid for taking them.<br /> <br /> Next lets see artifact guy in a no-holds barred fight against the wandering deathknight, unmounted.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Fire Dragon spends 15m to make a double roll naked fang draw. Rolling 13+3 for 11 and 10, taking the 11 for 14i.<br /> <br /> Wandering DK uses 7m for 16 dice, rolling 7 for 10i.<br /> <br /> FD 7i 18m 6wp 8 charge<br /> WD 10i 49m 6wp<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> <br /> WD attempts to wither FD with a 10m attack. FD will not spend motes to defend. Rolling 22 dice for ONLY 7! With two 1s FD uses 3m Flame Flicker to block the attack.<br /> <br /> FD 7i 15m 6wp 8 charge<br /> WD 10i 39m 6wp<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> FD will attempt a withering strike with 3m TAT, 3m Searing Edge, 4m excellency, WD defends with 10m excellency, 2m Eleggant Flowing Deflection. Rolling 20 dice for 15 against a defense of 11, FD hits. Rolling 4 damage for only 1, but due to Searing Edge knocking down another 3i.<br /> <br /> FD 9i 5m 6wp 8 charge<br /> WD 6i 27m 6wp<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> FD 9i 10m 6wp 8 charge<br /> WD 6i 32m 6wp<br /> <br /> FD attacks with another 3m TAT, 3m Searing Edge, 4m excellency. WD defends the same way. Rolling 20 dice for 7 this time, missing.<br /> <br /> FD 9i 0m 6wp 8 charge<br /> WD 6i 20m 6wp<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> WD attempts to wither with a 10m exccellency attack, rolling 22 dice for 17, hitting, and rolling 20 damage for...an abyssmal 3.<br /> <br /> FD 6i 0m 6wp 8 charge<br /> WD 10i 10m 6wp<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> FD 6i 5m 6wp 8 charge<br /> WD 10i 15m 6wp<br /> <br /> WD this time just makes a moteless withering attack, conserving motes for his final decisive, rolling 12 dice for...three.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> FD attacks with a 3m searing edge attack, WD defending with 6m excellency. Rolling 16 dice against parry 9 for 7 and missing.<br /> <br /> FD 6i 2m 6wp 8 charge<br /> WD 10i 9m 6wp<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ===========<br /> FD 6i 7m 6wp 8 charge<br /> WD 10i 14m 6wp<br /> <br /> WD makes another attack, with 4m excellency, rolling 16 dice for 9. FD will spend 3m and 4 charge to Twin-Blade Defense and block this attack.<br /> <br /> FD 6i 4m 6wp 4 charge<br /> WD 10i 10m 6wp<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> FD attacks with 3m Searing Edge, WD will defend with 6m. Rolling 16 dice for 8, FD just misses.<br /> <br /> FD 6i 1m 6wp 4 charge<br /> WD 10i 4m 6wp<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ===========<br /> FD 6i 6m 6wp 4 charge<br /> WD 10i 9m 6wp<br /> <br /> WD will attack with 6m excellency, rolling 16 dice for 7, and with 4 1s FD will cancel for 3m with Flame Flicker.<br /> <br /> FD 6i 3m 6wp 4 charge<br /> WD 10i 3m 6wp<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> FD will attack with 3m Searing Edge. WD will defend with 2m excellency. Rolling 16 dice for 6 FD just misses<br /> <br /> FD 6i 0m 6wp 4 charge<br /> WD 10i 1m 6wp<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That really didn't go as I expected. I don't have time to finish the fight but it's way less one-sided than I thought. Even by round 5 it's anyone's game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T16:52:31-08:00","id":1372056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370654#post1370654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have seen it. In fact my last two Solar characters deliberately had defence scores of 2 to start out and I had an absolute blast. Combats felt more engaging, there was rising and falling initiatives, I used different tactics, good stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah... the thing is you CAN make characters like that. The published Solar circle has a few. The Dawn has a parry of 5-6, the Zenith of 5, but the Twilight and Eclipse only have 2-3 and they\u2019re all made legit with the chargen rules. Barring specialties, and a couple charms and a couple bonus points. Awareness is another one, no foe will ever successfully ambus a party of PCs with everyone sporting awareness 5. Which puts a lot of antagonists in bad positions.<br /> <br /> Not impossible ones, I think the rough little example adventure adventure I just made up makes okay use of what\u2019s there, but there\u2019s just a lot of stuff that\u2019s nearly useless. Which is sad, foes like the basilisk or the scorpion-man are really cool, but they\u2019ll never really be useful.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re all consistent with eachother at least, ta just such a waste to give them cool powers and fluff only to have them sit on the shelf gathering dust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you run a fight between an Essence 1 Solar built like that (Defense 3 is also fine) against one of the cool monsters? Bigger teams on each side would also be good if you think that's better.<br /> <br /> The goal would be to provide advice for building characters like this, and to demonstrate the more fun combat.<br /> <br /> This obviously has bearing on the other thread but I think it's pretty clearly on-topic for this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T17:45:23-08:00","id":1372063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372056#post1372056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you run a fight between an Essence 1 Solar built like that (Defense 3 is also fine) against one of the cool monsters? Bigger teams on each side would also be good if you think that's better.<br /> <br /> The goal would be to provide advice for building characters like this, and to demonstrate the more fun combat.<br /> <br /> This obviously has bearing on the other thread but I think it's pretty clearly on-topic for this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bigger teams are usually better but I don't have the mental capacity to run them often sadly. Only if the combatants are very simple. I could run some more lower optimization fun fights. I ran a few earlier against a bunch of death moa and they were fun.<br /> <br /> I might also run consecutive fights until the Solar dies just to show the benefit of not relying on just one combat to make challenging encounters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T00:21:56-08:00","id":1372106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372063#post1372063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might also run consecutive fights until the Solar dies just to show the benefit of not relying on just one combat to make challenging encounters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did that, remember? Would like to see more of it though it in a more natural &quot;real game&quot; style environment.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349857#post1349857\">Solar easily kills 3 DBs in an epic battle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349916#post1349916\">Solar, low on motes is immediately ambushed again and pulls out all the stops to desperately stay alive</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349993#post1349993\">Ambushed again whilst totally drained, the Solar dies</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T07:26:28-08:00","id":1372150,"title":"","content":"How do the social martial arts fair?<br /> <br /> Black Claw, Silver Voiced Nightengale, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, White Veil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T07:56:05-08:00","id":1372154,"title":"","content":"I've not actually made a character for the arena fights using social MAs, but based on what I know from say, Black Claw, it kind of really helps to lay some groundwork beforehand.<br /> <br /> Like, if you could get someone to have a Defining Positive intimacy for you ahead of time, and you are doing stealthy tricks to JB, then you could presumably Heart Ripping Claw them to Malfeas and back.<br /> <br /> But barring that, its a bit of a more defensive style (it doesn't have any withering boosters, for example) that helps if you have a bunch of people around to leap in and start roughing the other guy over for bruising the poor delicate flower that you are.<br /> <br /> White Veil has the same kind of thing, you really want to not have the other guy roll JB until the fight is over and your poison has worked its way through his system.<br /> <br /> prototype00<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T09:45:51-08:00","id":1372163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372063#post1372063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bigger teams are usually better but I don't have the mental capacity to run them often sadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, 1v1s are cool too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only if the combatants are very simple. I could run some more lower optimization fun fights. I ran a few earlier against a bunch of death moa and they were fun. </div> </div> </div>Thanks for pointing that out. But do you think it could be more fun to go even lower optimization than that?<br /> <br /> <br /> For some inspiration / possibly a dire warning I tried to stat out a character whose combat skill was on the lower end of Exalted characters, based on your and JohnDoe244's remarks. I didn't go all the way down to defense 2, but I kept the combat abilities and physical attributes to at most 3. This character is part of Sail Team 6, my somewhat silly idea of having a circle of Solars on a boat together who are all expert sailors but all take different parts of the Sail charm tree. His job description is Sugar Daddy Captain and he's the one who owns the boat. He's Essence 1 and has only a couple charms that are relevant in combat.<br /> <br /> If you find this amusing, you could run a combat with him vs. whatever foe you think he could beat if he finds himself stranded alone and off his ship.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sugar Daddy Captain</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eclipse Caste</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Attributes (8 BP)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Strength 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dexterity 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stamina 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charisma 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Manipulation 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Appearance 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Perception 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Intelligence 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wits 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eclipse Caste Abilities (6 BP)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bureaucracy 4 (Trading, Running a naval organization)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Linguistics 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Presence 4 (I look like a million bucks)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Sail 5</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Socialize 3 (with the rich and powerful)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Favored Abilities (1 BP)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Brawl 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dodge 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Integrity 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Investigation 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Martial Arts - Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Performance 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merits (Native Language: Seatongue)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Followers 2 (50 loyal sailors)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Martial Arts</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resources 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charms</span></span></span><ul><li>Sail: Ship-Claiming Stance</li> <li>Sail: Hull-Preserving Technique</li> <li>Sail: Ship-Leavening Meditation</li> <li>Sail: Hull-Taming Transfusion</li> <li>Sail: Blood and Salt Bondage</li> <li>Sail: Ship-Sustaining Spirit</li> <li>Sail: Burning Anima Sails</li> <li>Sail: Ship-Sleeking Technique</li> <li>Sail: Tide-Cutting Essence Infusion</li> <li>Sail: Wave-Riding Discipline</li> <li>Martial Arts: Elegant Weapon Repertoire</li> <li>Martial Arts: Pearlescent Filigree Defense</li> <li>Bureaucracy: Frugal Merchant Method</li> <li>Bureaucracy: Insightful Buyer Technique</li> <li>Presence: Harmonious Presence Meditation</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Evasion 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Parry 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Unarmed: Accuracy 10 (Decisive 6) Damage 7 (OV 1), Bashing, Grappling</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire: Accuracy 10 (Decisive 6) Damage 7 (OV 2), tags vary</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(With Pearlescent Filigree Defense) Soak 5 Hardness 0</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resist Poison</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Joint Battle 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rush 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Disengage 6</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Willpower 5 (1 committed - Blood and Salt Bondage</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Personal motes 13</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Peripheral motes 33 (17 committed - Harmonious Presence Meditation and Blood and Salt Bondage, 16 available)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Heath Levels: -0 x 6, -1 x2, -2 x 2, -4, and Incapacitated (+5 for Blood and Salt Bondage on Blue Water Merchant)</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T09:54:15-08:00","id":1372165,"title":"","content":"Some notes:<br /> 1) You don't generally commit Willpower; it's just spent, and when you get the WP back, it doesn't matter if the Charm you powered with it is still running or not.<br /> \u200b2) That Blood and Salt Bondage is gonna get <i>scary</i> once he gets his hands on a First Age warship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T11:21:20-08:00","id":1372174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372106#post1372106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did that, remember? Would like to see more of it though it in a more natural &quot;real game&quot; style environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's more what I meant, like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar Fighter<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> phys 4/5/3<br /> Ment 2/2/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Daiklave 14 (Damage 16/5)<br /> Parry 7<br /> 14/10<br /> <br /> Motes 45 willpower 5<br /> <br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> Excellent Strike<br /> Fire and Stones Strike<br /> Rising Sun Slash<br /> Hungry Tiger Technique<br /> One Weapon Two Blows<br /> Peony Blossom Technique<br /> Iron Whirlwind Attack<br /> Invicible Fury of the Dawn<br /> Dipping Swallow Deffense<br /> Bulwark Stance<br /> Fivefold Bulwark Stance<br /> Hail Shattering Practice<br /> Call the Blade<br /> Iron Raptor Technique<br /> <br /> <br /> Sensory Acuity Prana<br /> Surprise Anticipation Method<br /> Keen Sight<br /> Keen Hearing<br /> Awakening Eye<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Charging the Satrap's palace first attacking the outer gate, with a mortal commander and a size 2 battlegroup of troops<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Dawn joins battle with 5m excellency, rolling 15 dice for 7i<br /> Commander joins with 10 dice and a willpower, rolling for 10i<br /> Troops join with 6 dice for 6i<br /> <br /> <br /> Da 7i 40m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> Tr 6i size 2<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==========<br /> Commander will command troops to engage, stunting and spending a willpower for 10+1 dice. Rolling for a total of 2.<br /> <br /> Da 7i 40m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> Tr 6i size 2<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Dawn will wither the troops, rolling 14 dice against parry 5 for 7, then rolling 8 damage for 5.<br /> <br /> Da 8i 40m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> Tr 6i size 2 5L<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Troops roll 11 dice to engage against the Dawn, spending a willpower. Dawn will spend 4m to raise parry to 9. They miss with 6.<br /> <br /> Da 8i 36m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> Tr 6i size 2 5L<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ==========<br /> Da 8i 41m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> Tr 6i size 2 5L<br /> <br /> Again the commander demands they engage this solar, stunting and spending a wp. Rolling 10 dice for a total of 4.<br /> <br /> Da 8i 41m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> Tr 6i size 2 5L<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Dawn rolls to wither the troops again, this time spending 3m on an excellent strike and 3m on Fire and Stones Strike. Rolling 14+1 for 7, hitting. Then rolling 11 damage for 6, dropping the troops a size.<br /> <br /> The battlegroup rolls to rout, succeeding and staying on the field.<br /> <br /> Da 14i 35m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> Tr 6i size 1 2L<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Battlegroup attempts to engage with 12 dice spending a willpower, Dawn will defend by spending 4m to raise parry to 9. The BG rolls 8 total, just missing.<br /> <br /> Da 14i 31m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> Tr 6i size 1 2L<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ==========<br /> Da 12i 36m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> Tr 6i size 1 2L<br /> <br /> Dawn rolls to wither the troops, spending another 3m on excellent strike and 3m on Fire and Stones. Rolling 14+1 dice for 10 after rerolls, and then 15 damage for 10, killing the battlegroup.<br /> <br /> Da 20i 30m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Commander tries to wither the Dawn, spending a willpower. Dawn will not spend motes to defend. Rolling 11 dice for only 4, missing.<br /> <br /> Da 20i 30m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ==========<br /> Da 20i 35m 5wp<br /> Co 10i<br /> <br /> Dawn decisive attacks with 3m excellent strike, rolling 11+1 for 6. Then rolling 20i damage for 5, putting the commander in his last -2s. He promptly surrenders and is slain or flees.<br /> <br /> Da 20i 32m 5wp<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay easy, next in the courtyard there's the Satrap's mortal sorcerer with a summoned bloodape who's looking to peg the Solar with a powerful Flight of the Brilliant Raptor from Medium range across the yard, with the ape interposing itself at short range.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Solar joins battle with 5m excellency, rolling 15 dice for 11i<br /> Sorcerer rolls join battle with 7 dice for 7i<br /> Bloodape joins battle with 6 dice for a crazy 9i<br /> <br /> Da 11i 27m 5wp<br /> Sa 7i<br /> Ba 9i<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> =========<br /> Dawn will use 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn, backed by 3m Excellent Strike, 3m Fire and Stones Strike, dividing 16i up 3/3/3/3/4.<br /> <br /> First moving in to attack the bloodape, rolling 11+1 dice for 6, strikging by 2, then rolling 5i for just 1 damage.<br /> <br /> Then moving past the ape to attack the sorcerer, rolling 11+1 dice for 11, rolling 6i for 2L.<br /> <br /> Third attack also on the sorc, hitting by only 2, rolling 5i for 1L<br /> <br /> fourth attack, rolling well over and then with 6i dealing 2L<br /> <br /> Fifth attack, rolling well over again and with 6i getting 3L, killing the sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Da 4i 16m 4wp<br /> Ba 9i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Bloodape will move in to withering attack, using 1wp for Principle of Motion. Dawn will not spend motes to defend against the first wither, rolling 11 dice for 5 and missing. Second attack the Solar uses 5m Bulwark Stance the bloodape rolls 8, hitting anyway, but will be Hail Shattering Practice'd away for 2m on the two 1s.<br /> <br /> Da 4i 9m 4wp<br /> Ba 9i<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =========<br /> Da 4i 14m 4wp<br /> Ba 9i<br /> <br /> Bloodape uses 1wp to make another two withering attacks. The first rolling 5 and missing, the second rolling 6 and missing as well.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Dawn will wither the bloodape, spending no motes. Rolling 14 dice for 7, hitting by 3, then rolling 12 for 6 damage.<br /> <br /> Da 11i 14m 4wp<br /> Ba 3i<br /> <br /> Dawn will use 3m One Weapon Two Blows to wither again, rolling 14 dice for 4, and then 10 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Da 23i 11m 4wp<br /> Ba -3i<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> =========<br /> Da 23i 16m 4wp<br /> Ba -3i<br /> <br /> Dawn will decisive with no additional motes. Rolling 11 dice for 4, hitting, and then 23 damage for 9, killing the ape.<br /> <br /> Da 4i 16m 4wp<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Solar is having NONE of that magic nonsense.<br /> <br /> Next is the Satrap's throneroom itself, with a size 1 battlegroup of elite trained elite bodyguards, a mortal huntsmaster and the satrap, an experienced Dragonblood herself.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Solar joins battle with 5m 1wp Awakening Eye, rolling 22 dice for 15i<br /> Dragonblunt joins with 4m excellency, rolling 14 dice for 9i<br /> Elite bodyguards join with 12 dice for 7i<br /> Hunt captain joins with 12 dice for 6i<br /> <br /> <br /> Da 15i 11m 3wp<br /> Db 9i 49m 7wp<br /> Eb 7i Size 1<br /> Hc 6i<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==========<br /> Solar uses 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn, supplemented by 3m Excellent Strike, 3m Hungry Tiger Technique. Splitting initiative up 1/4/5/5/5<br /> <br /> First attack he closes with the elite bodyguards, rolling 11+1, rolling 5 and missing.<br /> <br /> Second attack rolling 10 and hitting, then rolling 7i damage for 4L +2 for decisive against battlegroup.<br /> <br /> Third attack rolling 5 and hitting, then rolling 6i for 3L + 2. Elite battlegroup is slain<br /> <br /> Fourth attack into the Dragonblood, who will defend with 4m parry. Rolling 11+1 for 8, hitting and rolling 6i damage for only 1.<br /> <br /> Fifth attack the DB defends with 5m 1wp Indestructible Battle Mantle, Solar rolls 11+1 for 7, then 3i damage for 1, putting the DB into -1s<br /> <br /> <br /> Da 4i 0m 2wp<br /> Db 9i 40m 6wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 6i<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Experienced Dragonblood will attack with 6m excellency, 1wp, and 3m Thousand-Ton Hammer Smash, making a smashing attack. Rolling 16+1 dice for 7, hitting the Solar. Then rolling 5 damage for only 1<br /> <br /> Da 3i 0m 2wp<br /> Db 11i 31m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 6i<br /> ------------<br /> Hunt captain will fire a withering shot, spending a willpower. Rolling 13+1 dice for 6, hitting, then rolling 1 damage for 1.<br /> <br /> Da 2i 0m 2wp<br /> Db 11i 31m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 8i<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ==========<br /> Da 2i 5m 2wp<br /> Db 11i 36m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 8i<br /> <br /> Dragonblood makes another withering attack, spending 6m and using 3m Thousand Ton Hammer Smash. Rolling 16 dice for 8, hitting rolling 8 withering damage for 3, crashing the Dawn.<br /> <br /> Da -1i 5m 2wp<br /> Db 20i 27m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 8i<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Hunt Captain makes a decisive attack, rolling 13 dice and spending a willpower, getting it with 6 and rolling 8 damage for 2<br /> <br /> Da -1i 5m 2wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 20i 27m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 3i<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Solar will spend 5m 1wp to activate Fivefole Bulwark Stance<br /> <br /> Da -1i 0m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 20i 27m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 3i<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ==========<br /> Da -1i 5m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 20i 27m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 3i<br /> <br /> Dragonblood will make a decisive attack, using 3m Thousand Ton Hammer, 6m excellency and a willpower. Solar will defend with 1m Dipping Swallow. Dragonblood gets 9 and hits, but will be Hail Shattered into missing for 2m.<br /> <br /> Da -1i 2m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 17i 18m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 3i<br /> ----------<br /> Hunter will wither, rolling 13 dice, Solar will defend with 1m dipping swallow. Hunter will miss with 6.<br /> <br /> Da -1i 1m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 17i 18m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 3i<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Solar will flurry a rise from prone with a withering attack against the DB, rolling 4 dice to rise, making it with 4, and then attacking with 10 dice, hitting with 6 and rolling 5 damage for 2, pulling out of crash.<br /> <br /> Da 2i 1m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 17i 18m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 3i<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ==========<br /> Da 2i 6m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 17i 23m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 3i<br /> <br /> Dragonblood takes an aim action against the Solar.<br /> <br /> Da 2i 6m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 17i 23m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 3i<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Hunter makes a withering attack, rolling 13 dice for 7 and actually hitting, then rolling 1 damage for nothing.<br /> <br /> Da 2i 6m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 17i 23m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 4i<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Solar makes another withering attack against the DB, rolling 13 dice for 8, and then 5 damage for a crazy 7!<br /> <br /> Da 10i 6m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 10i 23m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 4i<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ==========<br /> <br /> Da 10i 11m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 10i 23m 5wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 4i<br /> <br /> Solar and DB clash, the Solar using 3m Excellent Strike and 8m Excellency, the DB using 6m Excellency 3m Thousand Ton Hammer and a willpower. The Solar rolls 21+1 dice for 12, the DB rolls 19+1 dice for also 12. I roll a die, evens it's solar, odds DB, it's a 10.<br /> <br /> Solar strikes, rolling 5 damage for a crazy 6, which becomes 8 due to the clash.<br /> <br /> Da 19i 0m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 2i 14m 4wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 4i<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Hunter withers with 13 dice and a willpower, making it with 7, rolling 1 die for 1 damage.<br /> <br /> Da 18i 0m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 2i 14m 4wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 6i<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> ==========<br /> Da 18i 5m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 2i 14m 4wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 6i<br /> <br /> Solar will wither DB again with a 2m Fire and Stones Strike, rolling 13 dice and hitting with 10, then rolling 9 damage for 2, crashing the DB.<br /> <br /> Da 26i 3m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 0i 14m 4wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 6i<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Hunter makes another wither, missing with 5.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> DB makes a smashing wither with 6m and 3m thousand ton and a willpower, Solar will defend with dipping swallow, rolling 16+1 for 10, the Solar unable to hail shatter it away. Then rolling 5 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Da 20i 2m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 7i 5m 3wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 6i<br /> <br /> Round 7<br /> ==========<br /> Da 20i 7m 1wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 7i 10m 3wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Hc 6i<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar will use 5m 1wp Invincible Fury of the Dawn and 2m Hungry Tiger Technique, splitting initiative 1/6/6/6/6.<br /> <br /> <br /> First attack Solar rolls 10 dice for 7, hitting, rolling 3i damage for nothing.<br /> <br /> Second attack Solar rolls 10 dice for 5, hitting, rolling 8i damage for 2L<br /> <br /> Third attack Solar hits easily, rolling 8i damage for 5L<br /> <br /> Fourth attack 8i damage for 4L<br /> <br /> Fifth attack 8i damage for 2L<br /> <br /> <br /> Da 4i 0m 0wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 7i 10m 3wp 15L(-2s)<br /> Hc 6i<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> DB will make a withering smash with 3m Thousand ton Hammer, rolling 9 dice for 0 and missing.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Hunter will attack with a withering strike rolling 13 dice for....13 successes. Rolling 4 damage for 2.<br /> <br /> Da 2i 0m 0wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 7i 7m 3wp 15L(-2s)<br /> Hc 9i<br /> <br /> Round 8<br /> ==========<br /> Da 2i 5m 0wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 7i 12m 3wp 15L(-2s)<br /> Hc 9i<br /> <br /> Hunter makes another withering strike, Solar defends with 1m dipping swallow rolling 13 dice for 8 and hitting again, but being hail shattered for 1m.<br /> <br /> Da 2i 3m 0wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 7i 12m 3wp 15L(-2s)<br /> Hc 9i<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> DB makes another smash with 3m Tousand Ton Hammer, and 3m excellency. Solar will defend with 1m Dipping Swallow, rolling 11 dice for 7 and missing.<br /> <br /> Da 2i 2m 0wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 7i 6m 3wp 15L(-2s)<br /> Hc 9i<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Solar makes a withering attack against the DB, rolling 13 dice for 6, and then 5 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Da 9i 2m 0wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 1i 6m 3wp 15L(-2s)<br /> Hc 9i<br /> <br /> Round 9<br /> ==========<br /> Da 9i 7m 0wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Db 1i 11m 3wp 15L(-2s)<br /> Hc 9i<br /> <br /> Solar makes a decisive attack with 3m Hungry Tiger, 3m excellent strike, 1m excellency, DB defends with 4m excellency. Rolling 14+1 dice for 8, and then 12 damage for 9 the Solar slays the experienced dragonblood, the hunter surrenders.<br /> <br /> Da 9i 0m 0wp 2L(-1s)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> By the grace of crazy solar power and Fivefold Bulwark Stance the victory is assured. Now though, backup has finally arrived from the rooftop, a Fire aspect immaculate monk and a cadre of size 2 warrior monks.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Solar joins battle with 9 dice for 7i<br /> Fire joins with 4m excellency and willpower, 11+1 dice for 12i<br /> Warrior Monks enter with 6 dice for 7i<br /> <br /> <br /> Da 7i 0m 0wp 2L(-1s)<br /> Fi 12i 40m 4wp<br /> Wm 6i Size 2<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> Fire monk launches a decisive attack, with 3m excellency, 3m 1wp Fiery Blade Attack, and 5m Essence-Igniting Nerve Strike. Rolling 17 dice for 10 and hitting, then rolling 14 damage for 7, putting the Solar into -2s, and setting him ablaze.<br /> <br /> Da 7i 0m 0wp 9L(-2s)<br /> Fi 3i 29m 3wp<br /> Wm 6i Size 2<br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Dawn rolls 8 dice to avoid bonfire damage, rolling 3 and failing, then taking 2 lethal levels of damage.<br /> <br /> Dawn will attempt to wither Fire, who will defend with 6m full parry, rolling 12 dice for 3 and missing.<br /> <br /> Da 7i 0m 0wp 11L(-2s)<br /> Fi 3i 29m 3wp<br /> Wm 6i Size 2<br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Warrior monks attempt to engage the Solar with hook swords, spending a willpower and rollingg 8 dice for 6, hitting. In a contested control roll they use 6 dice against 4 for 5 against 2, making it with 3 rounds.<br /> <br /> First round they withering savage, rolling 8 dice for 3 to hit, then rolling 3 withering damage for one.<br /> <br /> Da 6i 0m 0wp 9L(-2s)<br /> Fi 3i 29m 3wp<br /> Wm 4i Size 2<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> Da 6i 5m 0wp 9L(-2s)<br /> Fi 3i 34m 3wp<br /> Wm 4i Size 2<br /> <br /> Dawn rolls 8 dice to avoid burning, rolling 3 and failing, and taking no damage as a result.<br /> <br /> Dawn attempts to wither the battlegroup, rolling 11 dice for 7 and hitting, then rolling 16 damage for 6, not enough to drop them a size, but enough to drop them down to 1 round of control left.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Fire will attempt to wither Dawn, using 6m excellency, 2m Searing Edge Attack, the Solar will defend with 2m Dipping Swallow. Rolling 20 dice for 14 and hitting. Rolling 7 damage for 5, plus 2 from searing blade crashes the Solar.<br /> <br /> Da -1i 3m 0wp 9L(-2s)<br /> Fi 14i 26m 3wp<br /> Wm 4i Size 2<br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Monks savage with a willpower, the Solar will spend 2m to dipping swallow, and the monks miss, giving up their engage.<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> Da -1i 6m 0wp 9L(-2s)<br /> Fi 14i 31m 3wp<br /> Wm 4i Size 2<br /> <br /> Fire will decisive attack with a 3m excellency, Solar will defend with 2m Dipping swallow and 2m Excellency rolling 17 dice for a crazy 17, and then rolling 14i damage for 8, slaying the Solar.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With that, the Solar gave his life to end the rule of the Satrap. Or you as the ST could just stop before that fight. On the other hand you could also go even further and have more fighters arrive from other parts of the palace.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, that's only one character, but also not a very great showing by the palace of a satrap. It only had two terrestrials in it, one mortal sorcerer with only one summoned demon and no other previously prepared spells. If you had another 3-4 characters I think you could up the challenge a lot and still be reasonable, as long as those characters weren't also pretty optimized Dawns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T18:16:41-08:00","id":1372210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372163#post1372163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you find this amusing, you could run a combat with him vs. whatever foe you think he could beat if he finds himself stranded alone and off his ship.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about against a Hellboar? A creature described in the book as something so powerful that hunters don't fight them, only foolhardy Dynasts.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Hellboar joins battle with 5 dice, getting 8i<br /> Sugardaddy joins with 4 dice, getting 7i<br /> <br /> <br /> Sd 7i 16m 5wp<br /> Hb 8i 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> =========<br /> Hellboar makes a decisive bite attack against Sugardaddy, spending a willpower, Sugardaddy defends with 1m Pearlescent Filigree, rolling 8 dice and hitting with 6. Pearlescent Filigree activates 10 hardness, negating the attack.<br /> <br /> Sd 7i 15m 5wp<br /> Hb 6i 4wp<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Sugardaddy withering attacks with a 3m Elegant Weapon, hitting with a 5, and then dealing no damage.<br /> <br /> Sd 8i 15m 5wp<br /> Hb 6i 4wp<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =========<br /> Sd 8i 15m 5wp<br /> Hb 6i 4wp<br /> <br /> Sugardaddy attacks again, easily hitting with 7, and dealing 2 damage this time.<br /> <br /> Sd 11i 15m 5wp<br /> Hb 4i 4wp<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Hellboar tries a withering bite attack now, spending a willpower to attack. Sugardaddy spends 6m to defend. The Hellboar hits with 8 successes, and then rolls 11 damage for 3<br /> <br /> Sd 8i 9m 5wp<br /> Hb 8i 3wp<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> =========<br /> Sd 8i 14m 5wp<br /> Hb 8i 3wp<br /> <br /> The two withering clash eachother, Sugardaddy spending 6m to roll 16 dice, and the hellboar spending another willpower. Sugardaddy gets 13 whereas the hellboar only gets 5.<br /> <br /> Rolling 3 damage from 3 dice, and dealing an extra two because of clash.<br /> <br /> Sd 14i 8m 5wp<br /> Hb 3i 2wp<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> =========<br /> Sd 14i 13m 5wp<br /> Hb 3i 2wp<br /> <br /> Sugardaddy goes for a decisive hit, rolling 7 dice for 5 successes, easily striking the hellboar. Then rolling 14i initiative for 5! Causeing the the Hellboar to flee the field!<br /> <br /> Sd 3i 13m 5wp<br /> Hb 3i 2wp<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I was actually planning on using the fact that the Hellboar was at 3i to decisive and force another clash, which can deal an automatic 2 extra damage, but then it turns out 14i was just enough to make it flee.<br /> <br /> I also totally messed up in round 1, the Hellboar should have reset to base initiative, not act as though he missed because that's how Hardness works... That would have made this whole thing even easier because Sugardaddy could have just launched a decisive turn one as well, and forced a clash at a range that would ensure a crash as long as he dealt any damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T22:33:44-08:00","id":1372224,"title":"","content":"I should also say that with sugar daddy the pendulum swung petty far, not to say too far, after all he drove off a friggin hellboar on his own, but there are definitely things that are scary for him. He shouldn't try to fight a manticore solo, for example. His main hurdles aren't really attack and defence, it's soak and damage.<br /> <br /> On the other hand he'll beat the pants off professional assassins, war ghosts, walking skeletons, disease gods, dinosaurs, etc. all on his own without any backup, which if you're running him in an actual game is probably rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T05:47:56-08:00","id":1372259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372165#post1372165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some notes:<br /> 1) You don't generally commit Willpower; it's just spent, and when you get the WP back, it doesn't matter if the Charm you powered with it is still running or not.<br /> \u200b2) That Blood and Salt Bondage is gonna get <i>scary</i> once he gets his hands on a First Age warship.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Oh thanks for the tip.<br /> <br /> 2) I guess if instead of Martial Arts I gave him a normal combat style, he could start with <i>Horizon Endeavour</i>. That would truly be a vehicle worthy of his grandeur...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372224#post1372224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should also say that with sugar daddy the pendulum swung petty far, not to say too far, after all he drove off a friggin hellboar on his own, but there are definitely things that are scary for him. He shouldn't try to fight a manticore solo, for example. His main hurdles aren't really attack and defence, it's soak and damage.<br /> <br /> On the other hand he'll beat the pants off professional assassins, war ghosts, walking skeletons, disease gods, dinosaurs, etc. all on his own without any backup, which if you're running him in an actual game is probably rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for doing this!<br /> <br /> Good point with regards to the soak and damage. I guess the main &quot;solution&quot; to that is better weapons and armor - it's funny that he could have Melee 3, Excellent Strike, Dipping Swallow Defense, a daiklave, and artifact heavy armor, instead of his martial arts build, for only one dot more of investment and be a lot more powerful in combat.<br /> <br /> I definitely want to try lower-combat-power-level characters for my next campaign, if I ever get to that.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 03-02-2020, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T05:53:36-08:00","id":1372260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372150#post1372150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the social martial arts fair?<br /> <br /> Black Claw, Silver Voiced Nightengale, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, White Veil</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of characters do you want to do this with?<br /> <br /> I think it might make sense to assume the characters are very socially focused and have only a little combat skill - maybe not quite so low as the one I made.<br /> <br /> Could give them 3/3/3 physical stats and 5s in the relevant social abilities and attributes, and something like Martial Arts 3 / Essence 1, Martial Arts 4 / Essence 2, or Martial Arts 5 / Essence 3 to get a sample, most, or all of the Martial Arts charms.<br /> <br /> Another interesting question is if the Martial Artists, or their opponents, should start with any Intimacies. Personally I think it makes sense in a MA vs. MA duel to give them each a Minor Tie to the other, but in a MA vs. Monster duel for the Monster to be Intimacy-free.<br /> <br /> What do you think? What is the ideal test of social martial arts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T06:47:25-08:00","id":1372263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372259#post1372259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I guess if instead of Martial Arts I gave him a normal combat style, he could start with <i>Horizon Endeavour</i>. That would truly be a vehicle worthy of his grandeur...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, this is fine. Honestly I prefer seeing characters that feel more organic, like this.<br /> <br /> \u200b(That said, he could've seen <i>Horizon Endeavor</i> on the seas once himself, back when he was a mortal; claiming it seems like a pretty worthy adventure.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T07:10:13-08:00","id":1372266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372163#post1372163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough, 1v1s are cool too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for pointing that out. But do you think it could be more fun to go even lower optimization than that?<br /> <br /> <br /> For some inspiration / possibly a dire warning I tried to stat out a character whose combat skill was on the lower end of Exalted characters, based on your and JohnDoe244's remarks. I didn't go all the way down to defense 2, but I kept the combat abilities and physical attributes to at most 3. This character is part of Sail Team 6, my somewhat silly idea of having a circle of Solars on a boat together who are all expert sailors but all take different parts of the Sail charm tree. His job description is Sugar Daddy Captain and he's the one who owns the boat. He's Essence 1 and has only a couple charms that are relevant in combat.<br /> <br /> If you find this amusing, you could run a combat with him vs. whatever foe you think he could beat if he finds himself stranded alone and off his ship.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sugar Daddy Captain</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eclipse Caste</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Attributes (8 BP)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Strength 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dexterity 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stamina 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charisma 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Manipulation 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Appearance 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Perception 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Intelligence 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wits 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eclipse Caste Abilities (6 BP)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bureaucracy 4 (Trading, Running a naval organization)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Linguistics 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Presence 4 (I look like a million bucks)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Sail 5</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Socialize 3 (with the rich and powerful)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Favored Abilities (1 BP)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Brawl 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dodge 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Integrity 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Investigation 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Martial Arts - Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Performance 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merits (Native Language: Seatongue)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Followers 2 (50 loyal sailors)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Martial Arts</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resources 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charms</span></span></span><ul><li>Sail: Ship-Claiming Stance</li> <li>Sail: Hull-Preserving Technique</li> <li>Sail: Ship-Leavening Meditation</li> <li>Sail: Hull-Taming Transfusion</li> <li>Sail: Blood and Salt Bondage</li> <li>Sail: Ship-Sustaining Spirit</li> <li>Sail: Burning Anima Sails</li> <li>Sail: Ship-Sleeking Technique</li> <li>Sail: Tide-Cutting Essence Infusion</li> <li>Sail: Wave-Riding Discipline</li> <li>Martial Arts: Elegant Weapon Repertoire</li> <li>Martial Arts: Pearlescent Filigree Defense</li> <li>Bureaucracy: Frugal Merchant Method</li> <li>Bureaucracy: Insightful Buyer Technique</li> <li>Presence: Harmonious Presence Meditation</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Evasion 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Parry 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Unarmed: Accuracy 10 (Decisive 6) Damage 7 (OV 1), Bashing, Grappling</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire: Accuracy 10 (Decisive 6) Damage 7 (OV 2), tags vary</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(With Pearlescent Filigree Defense) Soak 5 Hardness 0</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resist Poison</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Joint Battle 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rush 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Disengage 6</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Willpower 5 (1 committed - Blood and Salt Bondage</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Personal motes 13</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Peripheral motes 33 (17 committed - Harmonious Presence Meditation and Blood and Salt Bondage, 16 available)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Heath Levels: -0 x 6, -1 x2, -2 x 2, -4, and Incapacitated (+5 for Blood and Salt Bondage on Blue Water Merchant)</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, White Rooming Guybrush here is not in any way interesting to me.<br /> <br /> Running though a sample session? Hells yes.<br /> <br /> Full disclosure, I'm giving him a Warfan and a Whip. Note these weapons have the same traits as Unarmed attacks, but different tags.<br /> <br /> Also, damn that's a weak character (combat wise). I'm going to assume you made this character step by step following the character creation guidelines and you read the Staying Alive sidebar and deliberately chose to make your character this way despite Session 0 expectations. That said, Sugar Daddy Captain is an expert Martial Artist who is excellent at Dodging, so let's have some fun.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <s>Guybrush</s> Sugar Daddy Captain (SDC) stands astride the deck of the \u201cBay Max\u201d (his blue water merchant ship). Wind whips about his face and the spray of the sea soaks the crew. Dark clouds gather on the horizon:<br /> <br /> SDC: \u201cAll hands! Position 6! There\u2019s a storm a-brewing!\u201d<br /> <br /> Winds lash the Bay Max, a large blue water ship full of rare cargo from the North, and SDC bellows at the helmsman to keep her running \u201cStraight and true!\u201d<br /> <br /> Controlling the ship and the crew in the midsts of a storm is the stuff of heroes, and SDC rolls (Wits+Sail+Stunt=11 dice) against Difficulty 1 to keep the vessel on track!<br /> <br /> SDC is pleased with the performance of his crew (5 successes) as he confidently steers them through the storm, anticipating every danger with wits like lightning. The crew set their backs to it, brining the ship on course and filling the sails with storm wind.<br /> <br /> Syker, the first mate, approaches SDC: \u201cI don\u2019t like this storm cap\u2019n. It squalled up out of no-where!\u201d<br /> <br /> SDC turns to reassure his mate, with a throaty laugh he tosses his hair back and bellows: \u201cAye! There\u2019s something strange on these winds, but we\u2019ll face it down together matey!\u201d (Charisma+Presence+Looking Good+Stunt+Harmonious Presence Meditation-1 dice situational penalty from high wind-3 for multiple targets= 9 dice, 4 successes, SDC Inspires \u201cconfidence\u201d in Syker and, indeed, the whole crew (average Resolve 1 as per Militia stats with Sail 2)).<br /> <br /> As if from no-where, the Bay Max runs on a reef! SDC surges Essence into the ship with Hull-Preserving Technique (13/11m, 4WP).<br /> <br /> Syker: \u201cWhere\u2019d THAT come from!\u201d<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no time to answer, slinging round a rocky outcropping comes the red flags of the Blood Reavers! This scurvy gang of all female pirates are known to be ferocious man eaters who take no prisoners. Whilst the Bay Max should easily be able to outrun them with SDC at the helm, who knows what damage sailing over the reef may cause! But to stand and fight risks the whole crew being slaughtered by blood thirsty pirates. SDC makes his decision.<br /> <br /> SDC: \u201cTO ARMS! Prepare to repel boarders!\u201d<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> As Followers, SDC\u2019s sailors are normal men of average to competent sailing ability. They shall use the stats of Militia, with Sail 2 and bonus from SDC\u2019s charms if relevant. Fifty of them puts them on the upper end of Size 2.<br /> The Blood Reavers will use the traits of Lintha Reavers (though, of course, they have no connection to the Lintha who are cursed rivals on the seas of creation). A scale will board the Bay Max, also Size 2.<br /> <br /> Red Mane, captain of the Blood Reavers, is an elite warrior and so will use the stats of the Champion with Sail 4 added.<br /> <br /> Calling on the Resolving Battles and Skip It sidebars, I\u2019m content for the fight between the crew of the Bay Max and the Reavers to play out narratively: it\u2019s going to mirror the fight between SDC and Red Mane. If either party uses a Command action, or specifically attacks the battle-group (they won\u2019t), then I\u2019ll roll them into combat and use them as full combatants.<br /> <br /> The ever increasing storm is imposing a -3 penality on all actions. Anyone fighting on a ship they are familiar with can reduce this by 1, as can anyone with a Sail score of 4 or more (keeping in mind that Sail 2 is the level of skilled professionals). Red Mane thus acts at -2 (-1 from the storm, -1 from Ship Claiming Stance) and SDC acts at -1.<br /> <br /> SDC rolls (Wits+Stunt-1) 5d for Initiative and comes in at 6i.<br /> Red Mane rolls 8d for 7i.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 7i: As the Reavers swing aboard the Bay Max, one woman, larger and fiercer than the others singles out SDC. She muscles her way up to SDC\u2019s position and lunges at him with her cutlass (9d).<br /> <br /> SDC doesn\u2019t want to get hit, red will ruin his outfit! With Excellent skill he dodges, tucking and rolling his body away from the blow (7/11m, 7 Evasion). Red Mane\u2019s attack goes wide (5 successes vs Evasion 7).<br /> <br /> 6i: The whip is an elegant weapon. SDC lashes out with Excellency and Elegant Weapon Repertoire (5/8m, 14d). Red Mane twirls her sword to parry, but the whip easily gets past her defences (7 successes vs Parry 5). The whip lashes at Red Mane (13 damage-Soak 10 = 2i), knocking her off-balance. (9i/5i)<br /> <br /> SDC: 9i (7/16m, 4WP)<br /> Red Mane: 5i<br /> <br /> Narrative: The crew of the Bay Max clash against the red haired pirates in a desperate battle as rain soaks them through.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> 9i: Drawing on his bond with the ship, SDC lashes the boom above Red Mane with his whip and swings in to kick her with both feet (Ship Claiming Stance, Excellent Martial Arts, Elegant Weapon Repertoire, level 2 stunt, 7/12m, 4WP, 17d+2 successes). The blow connects (11 successes vs Parry 4, 7 threshold) crashing into Red Mane (18 damage \u2013 Soak 10 = 5i) and sending her sprawling (20i/0i).<br /> <br /> 0i: Red Mane shakes her head to clear it and barrels into SDC, swinging wildly (9d) as SDC lashes his whip from side to side trying to stop her closing in as he strengthens his clothing with Essence (Pearlescent Filigree Defense, 7/11m). Red Mane ducks under his guard (4 successes vs Parry 3+1), and slashes against his clothing (12 damage-5 soak = 4i). (5i/16i)<br /> <br /> SDC: 16i (7/16m, 4WP)<br /> Red Mane: 5i<br /> <br /> Narrative: The crew of the Bay Max push the boarders back to the rails of the ship, but with their backs to the sea, the experienced Reavers hold their ground in a determined stand.<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> 16i: As Red Mane has stepped past his guard, SDC does the unexpected: instead of backing up, he steps closer still and tries to tackle her (6+6+2-1=13d, 1/16m). Rolling 7 successes vs Parry 5, SDC grapples Red Mane and rolls 16i vs Difficulty 2 to confirm (14i). Red Mane rolls 6 dice to oppose the grapple, and SDC uses a 4m Excellency+stunt to roll 12d, and establishes 3 rounds of control.<br /> <br /> Crashing into Red Mane, SDC hoists her up and throws her from the Bay Max, into the side of her own pirate ship for (14i+3 rounds of control= 6B). The badly bruised pirate captain (-4) crashes into the sea and the spray.<br /> <br /> SDC: 6/16m 4WP<br /> Red Mane: -4 wound penalty and overboard<br /> <br /> Narrative: Seeing their leader so thoroughly defeated, the Reavers turn tail and flee back to their ship before Sugar Daddy Captain can turn on them too. The crew of the Bay Max give a great cheer!<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Carefully, the captain sees the crew make their way off the reef without suffering further damage (Difficulty 2, 11d, 4 successes).<br /> <br /> Wounds are tended to and look-outs strain their eyes to look for any more red sails.<br /> <br /> Once more the Bay Max sets on course, and driving rain and howling wind give way to fog.<br /> <br /> Cautious of running into any more reefs, SDC calls to proceed slowly. Lamps are lit.<br /> <br /> A piercing scream shrieks out from the mists. SDC runs out on deck to investigate, heroically charging headlong into danger.<br /> <br /> \u201cT-T-There! In the mists!\u201d A sailor calls pointing a arm out.<br /> <br /> Syker calls out dismissively: \u201cDon\u2019t be so jumpy, there\u2019s nothing there.\u201d<br /> <br /> At that moment a giant shark appears, flying in the mists and bites the arm of the terrified sailor clean off!<br /> <br /> SDC grabs his war-fan and leaps into the air towards the shark!<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> The Fog adds a 1d situational penality to SDC and the crew. The Fog Shark ignores this penalty.<br /> The Fog Shark does not take the Ship Claiming Stance penalty, as they are not on the ship: swimming instead through the mists.<br /> <br /> The crew won\u2019t act unless ordered to do so by the captain.<br /> <br /> SDC: (5d+3) = 5i<br /> Fog Shark: (6d) = 6i<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 6i: The Fog Shark tries to take a bite out of SDC. Biting with 7d vs Parry 3 (Pearlescent Filigree Defense, 6/15m). Fog Shark rolls 4 successes, hitting, but the attack bounces off the Solar\u2019s Hardness \u2013 surprisingly SDC\u2019s silk sleeves break the shark\u2019s teeth. (3i/5i)<br /> <br /> 5i: Elegantly and Excellently (6/6m, 1a), SDC twirls his war-fan and slashes the Fog Shark across the nose (17d vs Evasion 4, 9 successes). The shark\u2019s skin is tough (16 damage vs Soak 8 = 4i), but the blow cuts through the delicate snout, enraging and confusing the beast as the mark of the Eclipse appears on SDC\u2019s forehead. (15i/-3i)<br /> <br /> SDC: 15i (6/11m, 1a)<br /> Fog Shark: -3i<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> 15i: SDC lands on the deck after his lunge at the shark, dropping into a super-hero landing. Caste mark glowing, the expert martial artist twirls his war-fan with practiced grace and pushes up hard, striking the shark\u2019s underbelly (0/11m, 1a; 13d vs Evasion 3). The blow hits and tears open the shark for 6L, putting the beast in its -2s. (3i/-3i)<br /> <br /> -3i: The shark twists and bites at SDC, as he tries to twist out of the way (5d vs Evasion 3). SDC almost avoids the shark\u2019s killer jaws, but is still battered by the bulk of the beast (16 damage \u2013 Soak 5 = 5i). The blow knocks SDC off-balance, and dramatically shifts the flow of the battle with an Initiative Shift. (11i/-2i)<br /> <br /> SHIFT: The Fog Shark decisively bites down (5d) on the Solar, who spins his war-fan hoping to use it to Excellently wedge the beast\u2019s jaws open (Parry 5, 0/14m). SDC easily catches the kill jaws and turns the blow aside. (8i/-2i)<br /> <br /> SDC: -2i (0/16m, 4WP, 1a)<br /> Fog Shark: 8i (6L, -2 wound penalty)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> 8i: The Fog Shark tries to bites down again (5d), SDC braces himself against his war-fan, stopping the jaws from closing on him (Parry 3+1-1). (8i/-2i)<br /> <br /> -2i: Reasoning that the shark\u2019s skin is too thick to damage from the outside, SDC uses his vantage point to slash against the inside of the shark\u2019s mouth, climbing up and inside the beast for a better vantage point. Such an audacious ploy counts as a 3-point stunt, and SDC goes all in offensively (0/5m, 2a, 5WP; 13d+3 vs Evasion 2; 8 threshold successes; 8i) and tears and slashes the shark\u2019s soft mouth.<br /> <br /> SDC gains 1i for hitting (-1i), and deals 8i in damage (7i). Fog Shark recovered from Crash last round, so no Initiative break bonus. For Crashing the foe who Crashed him, SDC trips Initiative Shift (12i).<br /> <br /> SHIFT: SDC gives one last, heroic push into the shark\u2019s guts, disappearing entirely from view (6d+2-1 vs Evasion 1). The blow hits the soft parts of the beast, gutting it from the inside (12i, 4L).<br /> <br /> The dead fog shark flops to the deck of the Bay Max with a thump, and SDC pulls himself free of the beast to the triumphant cheers of his crew as burning Solar essence lights up the fog like a shining beacon of hope on an otherwise gloomy sea.<br /> <br /> SDC: \u201cSomeone draw me a bath!\u201d<br /> <br /> SDC: 0/10m, 5WP, 2a<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> SDC scrapes the shark guts from his body and luxuriates in a bath, fresh clothes waiting for him.<br /> <br /> The next hour passes blissfully without incident as he relaxes (4/16m).<br /> <br /> But the peace is not to last, Syker barrels in on the captain and insist he come to the deck immeidately. SDC doesn\u2019t have time to dress, but he grabs a bath robe to cover his modesty and heads up on deck.<br /> <br /> When they were attacked by the Reavers, a stow-away snuck aboard the Bay Max: this blonde haired woman was clearly a captive of the pirates, and is no threat to the crew.<br /> <br /> But a blonde haired woman is bad luck.<br /> <br /> If SDC had found her first, he could easily have swayed the crew into accepting her as a valued human being, but SDC didn\u2019t find her first. A Storm Mother did.<br /> <br /> The hag-goddess has stopped the ship and is demanding the sailors drown the woman to appease her.<br /> <br /> SDC, an Eclipse well used to dealing with gods, strides out on deck wearing only his robe, tied at the waist with his whip, to bargain for the woman\u2019s life.<br /> <br /> Storm Mother: THROW THE HARLOT INTO THE SEA IN SACRIFICE AND I SHALL PUT MY BLESSING ON YOUR SHIP.<br /> <br /> SDC reads the Storm Mother\u2019s intentions, rolling 6 dice against Guile 2. The Storm Mother seems to be sincere as she\u2019ll gain more power from the sacrifice than she\u2019d spend on calming the weather.<br /> <br /> Not looking like a million bucks, SDC is going to take a penalty on his rolls of -1 (this might not be a formal situation, but it\u2019s rarely a good idea to negotiate in a robe).<br /> <br /> SDC: \u201cWise and mighty Storm Mother. Well a being of your power,\u201d [he guesses, knowing nothing about Storm Mothers and having no training in Occult matters] \u201cmust know that it is ill-luck to cast good fortune into the sea. We mean you no disrespect, of course, and we offer you our humble prayers in return for your favor. We are both beings of the sea, you and I, surely we can pass in mutual respect.\u201d<br /> <br /> SDC rolls Manipulation+Presence+3 Harmonious+2 stunt-1=12d robe against the Storm Mother\u2019s Resolve of 4 as a Bribe. The Storm Mother has a Major Intimacy against Beautiful Women, which raises her Resolve to 7, but also a Defining Intimacy towards being worshipped, which brings her back to 4. SDC rolls 4 successes, and the Storm Mother agrees to provide safe passage, calm seas and fair winds, in exchange for prays from the crew of the Bay Max.<br /> <br /> Seizing his chance, SDC sanctifies the pact with his Anima (4/6m, 4WP, 2a), blazing brightly with the light of the Sun.<br /> <br /> Outraged by being tricked by one of the Sun\u2019s Chosen, the Storm Mother agrees she\u2019ll honor their pact: the Bay Max will sail safely.<br /> <br /> With a swish of her arm, a great wave crashes over the ship. Miraculously the water bends around the crew, not touching them with so much as a drop of water, but SDC is swept out to sea!<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> SDC washes up on a beach. He\u2019s reassured that the Storm Mother is bound by her oath not to harm the ship and the crew, and clearly the oath was strong enough to see that he was merely marooned instead of drowned. He doesn\u2019t know how long he has been at sea, but he feels strangely rested and his anima is dim (4/16m).<br /> <br /> SDC looks around to get his bearings. He sees some ruined ships: not having Craft, he cannot technically Craft a new boat. But as I\u2019m a nice ST, I let him make a Sail roll to cobble together a delicate raft.<br /> <br /> Then, over the dunes in the distance, SDC sees something that makes his blood run cold:<br /> <br /> The body of a lion, the head of a man, and the wicked barbed tail of a scorpion. A being of myth and legend. The dreaded Manticore!<br /> <br /> Sugar Daddy Captain must roll 10 successes on a Strength + Athletics roll to push his raft off the beach and into the sea. Each round, he gains one automatic success as the tide comes in. The manticore is sure to wreck the delicate raft is SDC runs away, so the Captain can\u2019t simply run away for 10 rounds. The manticore starts at long range.<br /> <br /> SDC: 7i (4/16m, 4WP)<br /> Manticore: 8i, Long Range<br /> <br /> <b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 8i: The Manticore closes to Medium range.<br /> <br /> 7i: SDC grabs his raft and starts pushing it to sea, bracing the raft at all the weak points and pushing with his legs (4d, 1 success = 9 remaining).<br /> <br /> Manticore: 8i, Medium Range<br /> SDC: 7i (9/16m, 4WP)<br /> Raft: 8 rounds remaining<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> 8i: The Manticore closes to Short range and Rushes. Both parties roll 8 dice, and SDC is Rushed.<br /> <br /> 7i: SDC keeps pushing, throwing his back into it, desperate to sail away. He drops his commitment to Harmonious Presence Meditation.<br /> <br /> Manticore: 8i, Short Range, Rush<br /> SDC: 7i (9/21m, 4WP)<br /> Raft: 5 rounds remaining<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> 8i: The Manticore closes to Close range and swipes at SDC with his claws (13d). SDC ducks and weaves, spinning around the grasping beast\u2019s deadly blows (9/14m, 1a, Evasion 7, Pearlescent Filigree Defense). The blow connects (7 successes) and SDC shunts Essence into his clothing (9/10m; Soak 9 vs Damage 12). The blow knocks the wind from SDC, but he avoids getting cut in half. (12i/4i)<br /> <br /> 4i: With a flourish, SDC cracks his whip like a Dynastic lion tamer, striking out at the Manticore with everything he\u2019s got as he blazes with Solar Essence (10 Accuracy+6 Excellency+2 Stunt+Willpower = 18d+1; 9/1m, 2a). The Manticore dodges, more deftly than even a graceful great cat could move, but the blow still connects (16 Damage vs 9 Soak). (8i/9i)<br /> <br /> Manticore: 9i<br /> SDC: 8i (9/6m, 3WP)<br /> Raft: 4 rounds remaining<br /> <br /> <b>Round 4</b><br /> <br /> 9i: The Manticore\u2019s tail lashes out with its deadly sting (8d). SDC, lashes out with his whip taking careful aim at the arc of the Manticore\u2019s attack (Parry 3+Stunt+2m Excellency; 9/4m). The whip deflects the blow.<br /> <br /> 8i: SDC launches forward with another all out attack (4/0m, 2WP), hitting again for 4i. (13i/5i)<br /> <br /> SDC: 13i (4/5m, 2WP)<br /> Manticore: 5i<br /> Raft: 3 rounds remaining<br /> <br /> <b>Round 5</b><br /> <br /> 13i: Not knowing if he\u2019ll get another opening, SDC launches a Decisive attack against the dread beast, striking for the eyes with a whip crack. His anima flares totemic, shining it\u2019s nautical message out for miles around (4/0m, 1WP; 10d+1 vs Evasion 4). The blow hits, for a spectacular 10B on 13 dice, knocking the beast into its -2s. (3i/5i)<br /> <br /> 5i: With an inhuman roar of rage, the Manticore bears down on SDC, throwing Willpower behind a Grapple attempt (7d+1). SDC spends the last of his motes to loosen his body, bending elegantly away from the blow (Evasion 3+Stunt+2; 0/0m). The Manticore\u2019s blow goes wide. (3i/3i)<br /> <br /> SDC: 3i (0/5m, 1WP, 2a)<br /> Manticore: 3i (4WP, 10B (-2))<br /> Raft: 2 rounds remaining<br /> <br /> <b>Round 6</b><br /> <br /> Clash: Man and Manticore Clash together in a desperate struggle of fist and fang. The beast claws as SDC. Sugar Daddy Captain draws on his years of experience, and Sun given skill, ducking into the swirling pattern of his totemic anima, co-ordinating his blows with the shifting pattern of light. The Manticore claws for him (3WP; 11d+1 = 9 successes) and he puts everything he has behind his attack (10 Accuracy+5m Excellency+2-point Stunt+Willpower=17d+2; 10 successes).<br /> <br /> SDC strikes true, the Manticore\u2019s hide soaks him down to minimum damage, but he still rolls 1i, plus 3i for winning the Clash. (13i/-1i)<br /> <br /> SDC: 13i (0/5m, 0 WP, 3a)<br /> Manticore: 3i (3WP, 10B (-2)) CLASH, CRASH<br /> Raft: 1 rounds remaining<br /> <br /> <b>Round 7</b><br /> <br /> 13i: SDC keeps pushing forward and strikes out with a Decisive blow: aiming to choke the beast to death. Carried forward by the momentum from the Clash, SDC jumps on the beast\u2019s claw leaps at its neck, wrapping the whip handle over its all-too-human throat, and throwing the weight of his body back against that lever to crush its windpipe (1WP). SDC rolls (Martial Arts 3+Dexterity 3+Stunt) 8 dice vs Evasion (5-2 Wound Penalty-1 Onslaught-2 Clash=) 0, and hits. 13i rolls 4 damage, killing the manticore.<br /> <br /> SDC strides aboard his raft as the tide rises.<br /> <br /> SDC: 0/10m, 1WP<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> The tide lifts the raft at takes it out to sea. SDC casts his blazing anima into the air, and it crawls over the wrecked ship\u2019s mast, replacing the sails with the burning light of his Essence (Burning Anima Sails, 0/4m, 0WP). His make-shift raft is now a worthy sea vessel he can use to find his beloved Bay Max.<br /> <br /> With the light of the Unconquered Sun shining on his brow, he wonders what adventures tomorrow will bring.<br /> <br /> Link to Part 2: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380906#post1380906\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...06#post1380906</a><br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <u><b>Too long: didn't read</b></u><br /> <br /> Sugar Daddy Captain sails the ship through a storm, calms a terrified crew, magically stops the ship taking damage from a reef, defeats a pirate captain in single combat (without flaring his anima), sails the ship off the reef without taking any further damage, solo's a fog shark, bargains with a Storm Mother (which seperates him from his ship) then, after a full day of adventuring (and without his ship and crew to help him) he beats a Manticore single handedly before turning a ship-wreck into a servicable sea faring vessle.<br /> <br /> We've got grapples. We've got Initiative Shifts. We've got a Clash. We've got a fight without flaring anima. We've got a seven round fight that watches a timer tick away.<br /> <br /> And this is one, suboptimal Solar on his own, deliberately played out of his element.<br /> <br /> This is Exalted baby. Even when you suck, you're freakin' awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-13-2025, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T07:45:27-08:00","id":1372273,"title":"","content":"How are you getting that much damage? Nine successes against an evasion of 4 for the fog shark is 5 over, so add five to the damage of 7 and you get 12, subtract the soak of 9 for 3 dice of damage rolled, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T08:08:47-08:00","id":1372278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372266#post1372266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, White Rooming Guybrush here is not in any way interesting to me.<br /> <br /> Running though a sample session? Hells yes.<br /> <br /> Full disclosure, I'm giving him a Warfan and a Whip. Note these weapons have the same traits as Unarmed attacks, but different tags.<br /> <br /> Also, damn that's a weak character (combat wise). I'm going to assume you made this character step by step following the character creation guidelines and you read the Staying Alive sidebar and deliberately chose to make your character this way despite Session 0 expectations. That said, Sugar Daddy Captain is an expert Martial Artist who is excellent at Dodging, so let's have some fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool!<br /> <br /> Just for clarity I didn't make this character for a specific game, so there was no Session 0. I made this character as an experiment to try to understand better what people (including you) were saying in this thread that you shouldn't always make characters that are super-strong in combat, and in fact should maybe go the other way and make characters quite weak (in combat). I wanted to see what this would look like. So your detailed session was exactly the sort of experimental confirmation I was looking for. (I might have more comments on it when I read it more carefully later.)<br /> <br /> Well there was sort of a Session 0 in my head where I imagined the players and ST getting together and saying &quot;You know what's cool? Sailing!&quot; and deciding to have a game that takes place almost entirely on a ship, where multiple players take Sail charms to handle different aspects of running the ship. This is why SDC doesn't have any charms that relate to actually sailing the thing - that's his employees's job. (At least from his point of view they're employees - they might see it differently.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T08:11:09-08:00","id":1372279,"title":"","content":"Personally I feel like it's a waste to roll Presence with HPM up and <i>not</i> spend that one mote Presence Excellency for 2 dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T08:30:09-08:00","id":1372281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372273#post1372273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are you getting that much damage? Nine successes against an evasion of 4 for the fog shark is 5 over, so add five to the damage of 7 and you get 12, subtract the soak of 9 for 3 dice of damage rolled, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Elegant Weapon Repertoire. 3m: Add Accuracy to Damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372279#post1372279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I feel like it's a waste to roll Presence with HPM up and <i>not</i> spend that one mote Presence Excellency for 2 dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, I'd agree. But I was trying to save motes.<br /> <br /> Does HPM help Read Intentions? I erred on the side of &quot;no&quot;, but... IDK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-02-2020, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T08:40:48-08:00","id":1372284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372281#post1372281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, I'd agree. But I was trying to save motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that. But then again, Carter's also got two different Charms that help him recover motes from social encounters (Preeminent Gala Knife and Undying Solar Resolve), so I'm a little biased. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372281#post1372281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does HPM help Read Intentions? I erred on the side of &quot;no&quot;, but... IDK.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the devs said &quot;no&quot; as well, but I can't be arsed to look that up right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T09:34:03-08:00","id":1372294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372281#post1372281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Elegant Weapon Repertoire. 3m: Add Accuracy to Damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang, I missed that. For only 3m? I issue a retraction, there's not really that many enemies that Sugar can't fight and reasonably hope to beat. Although some of them might rely on a Storyteller who's a bit biased in stunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T11:22:03-08:00","id":1372308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372294#post1372294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there's not really that many enemies that Sugar can't fight and reasonably hope to beat. Although some of them might rely on a Storyteller who's a bit biased in stunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stunting rules do say to be biased in favor of the PCs. That doesn't mean &quot;never stunt&quot;, but I try not to kill my PCs, and Guybrush needed the help.<br /> <br /> Also the NPCs never opened with Decisives (except the 9i one I knew Guybrush could get Hardness 10 against). Rarely spent Willpower.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to kill Guybrush, I could have had Moray Darktide show up in a First Age ship and blow him out of the water. I didn't want to kill him. I wanted to tell a story and I wanted him to look epic.<br /> <br /> That's how I run my games.<br /> <br /> But no character is going to survive an ST that really wants them dead.<br /> <br /> Also, whilst the Melee build is two dots more expensive, it's a lot closer to what I expect from a starting Solar (though 13/5m is pretty limiting -- are we sure the sailor needs heavy armor, and it'd be nice to have an Ox-Body in case the ship gets damaged). Maybe add in Fire and Stones Strike, Athletics and Awareness 3 and two Ox-bodies if the character wants to be &quot;good&quot; at combat. Sugar Daddy Captain is firmly a &quot;non-combat&quot; build in my book: but that's ok. The Dawn can fight the Dynast Captain. The 5 combat charm Zenith can fight the Dynast's bound Blood Ape. Sugar Daddy can fight the mortal First Mate. The Dawn can fight two Fog Sharks, the Zenith and SDC can fight one each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T12:24:45-08:00","id":1372314,"title":"","content":"I'd normally say a sailor might not want heavy armor, that's a -2 mobility penalty to any swimming you might want to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T21:59:43-08:00","id":1372380,"title":"","content":"So my pet love in 3e is actually Supernal Martial Arts that focuses on the social styles, because it results in a pretty diverse and toolboxy character that can approach combat different ways and focus on outcomes that aren't murder the other guy.<br /> <br /> That said, how social styles impact not combat primary characters is probably relevant, too--debatably more relevant.<br /> <br /> I feel like as far as main combat tactics go, SVN, especially up to Heart Reading Melody, is probably the way to go for offense. Black Claw has some of the best defense in the game (especially when supplemented by Solar Dodge/Resistance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-03-2020, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T22:27:27-08:00","id":1372386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372380#post1372380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my pet love in 3e is actually Supernal Martial Arts that focuses on the social styles, because it results in a pretty diverse and toolboxy character that can approach combat different ways and focus on outcomes that aren't murder the other guy.<br /> <br /> That said, how social styles impact not combat primary characters is probably relevant, too--debatably more relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be difficult to run for, just because the social aspect is so contextual. Somebody may be hopelessly susceptible to Black Claw just because of their intimacies, while another may be extremely resilient to them. <br /> <br /> There may be a satrap who found ancient and terribly heretical texts that spoke of the golden first age of the Solar Exalted, which grew into an obsession to the point where she has a defining principle that the Solars are the rightful rulers of Creation, or her parents and brother may have died at the Battle of Futile Blood and she\u2019s sworn vendetta against all Solar anathema. Or maybe your Silver Voiced Nightingale is just trying to get her to host the damn ball already like she SAID SHE WOULD A YEAR AGO! Obviously needing to kung-fu fight her for that. Which is awesome, awesome awesome, but I have no baseline for the intimacies that either character has in that regard, and I worry that giving them would just be me fiat granting a victory or defeat. Either they have the intimacies to exploit or they don\u2019t, and how much groundwork did the socialite do beforehand to discover them or grow them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T17:46:30-07:00","id":1374460,"title":"","content":"JohnDoe244, by running an entire mini-session for one solar all by himself, inspired me to do the same thing for a party of 3 Solars. Now, you might say that is overly complicated and you would certainly be right. Anyways I thought it might be fun to post some of the naval battles I did on this thread, as I don't think that combat system has been discussed much.<br /> <br /> My first battle was an attempt to see if ships captained by mortals can be an appropriate threat to ships captained by the Exalted, with an appropriate choice of scenario. In this case, the Solars come across an innocent merchant ship being menaced by 2 corsairs. <br /> <br /> Our intrepid heroes:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The ship is the Bay Max, a Blue Water Merchant. Its captain, Rose's Thorn, has the following relevant stats:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wits 5<br /> Sail 5 (the Bay Max)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Charms:<ul><li>Sail: Immortal Mariner\u2019s Advantage</li> <li>Sail: Legendary Captain\u2019s Signature</li> <li>Sail: Sea Ambush Technique</li> <li>Sail: Deck-Sweeping Fusillade</li> <li>Sail: Ship Breaker Method</li> <li>Sail: Superior Positioning Technique</li> </ul>She's quite good at sailing. She starts with 13 personal motes and 23 peripheral motes.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The other ships are as follows<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The corsairs sail modified large yachts, with catapaults and a ramming prow. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The corsair captains are experienced sailors, with 9 die sailing pools (I used the stat block of an Elite Troop and borrowed their Senses pool). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> The merchants also sail a large yacht. It is so harmless that it does not <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">ever contribute to a -2 penalty for having multiple ships oppose. The captain is skilled, but unprepared for combat with a 4 die pool.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The fight (in which I forgot to give anyone stunt dice, and also found and corrected several math errors when I went to post it, so there's probably more errors hiding in there).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Round 1: Everyone has 0 momentum and take a positioning stratagem. Bay Max opposes Corsair 1, Corsair 1 and Corsair 2 oppose Merchants, Merchants oppose Corsair 2. Rose\u2019s Thorn uses a four-mote excellency and Superior Positioning Technique. (11/19 motes).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bay Max rolls 15 dice, gaining 4 successes, spending 1 mote (11/18) to reroll two 1s with Immortal Mariner\u2019s advantage, giving an additional success</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 1 rolls 8 dice, gaining 3 successes, with no 1s</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 2 rolls 8 dice, gaining 2 successes</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merchants roll 1 die, gaining 1 success</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Momentum:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bay Max - 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 1 - 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 2 - 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merchant - 0</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Round 2: Everyone takes the same strategy (9/15 motes).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bay Max rolls 15 dice, gaining 8 successes, spending 1 mote to double 9s, gaining an additional success, and 1 mote to reroll three 1s, gaining four additional successes, both with Immortal Mariner\u2019s Advantage. (9/13 motes)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 1 rolls 8 dice, gaining 0 successes, with one 1, giving Bay Max 2 additional successes, for a total of 15.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 2 rolls 8 dice, gaining 10 successes.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merchant rolls 1 die, gaining 1 success.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Momentum:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bay Max - 17</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 1 - 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 2 - 10</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merchant - 0</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Unfortunately the Bay Max can do nothing to stop Corsair 2 from boarding the merchant ship. However, they will at least board Corsair 1.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bay Max chooses Drowning Tide, opposing Corsair 1, spending 2 motes (9/11). Corsair 1 chooses Positioning, opposing Corsair 2. Corsair 2 chooses Seize the Initiative!, opposing Merchant.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bay Max rolls 13 dice, gaining 7 successes, spending 1m to double 9s with Immortal Mariner\u2019s Advantage, gaining 2 additional successes (9/10).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 1 rolls 8 dice, gaining 3 successes.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 2 rolls 8 dice, gaining 3 successes.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merchant rolls 3 dice, gaining 2 successes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Momentum:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bay Max - 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 1 - 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corsair 2 - 0</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merchant - 0</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bay Max boards Corsair 1, and Corsair 2 boards Merchant. </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well those were some weird rolls, but it probably demonstrates that even a Solar sailor needs to spend quite a few motes if she wants to be sure that she gets to her enemies before they get to the poor innocent civilians.<br /> <br /> What likely happens next is that, especially with the crazy bonuses, the Solars make quick work of their mortal foes on Corsair 1, which leads to the crew of Corsair 2 attempting to essentially take the merchants hostage to plead for their life.<br /> <br /> However the Sail rolls aren't great for this kind of situation. For instance if the Corsairs were to get scared of the Bay Max and try to escape, it would not make sense for them to shift to opposing the Bay Max, but rather keep opposing the merchant ship to take advantage of its low dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T19:33:05-07:00","id":1374476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1374460#post1374460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However the Sail rolls aren't great for this kind of situation. For instance if the Corsairs were to get scared of the Bay Max and try to escape, it would not make sense for them to shift to opposing the Bay Max, but rather keep opposing the merchant ship to take advantage of its low dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that part does seem to be a bit of an oversight. I know that some parts of the sail rules were patched last minute, like when people pointed out that facing off at 1 to 10 odds if you were just a much better captain, like a Solar PC, you basically didn't care, so they added the multiple ship penalty which gives you a -18 die penalty in that situation.<br /> <br /> This also has me curious does naval combat count for per-turn mote regeneration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T05:59:11-07:00","id":1374551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1374476#post1374476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah that part does seem to be a bit of an oversight. I know that some parts of the sail rules were patched last minute, like when people pointed out that facing off at 1 to 10 odds if you were just a much better captain, like a Solar PC, you basically didn't care, so they added the multiple ship penalty which gives you a -18 die penalty in that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to rule it might be that, in a multi-ship vs. multi-ship fights, either you leave the battle or the ship you Escaped leaves the battle, whichever is most advantageous for the other side.<br /> <br /> I wonder if anyone has played a naval-combat heavy game and came up with a bunch of house rules and stuff. I don't think I've seen anyone mention it on the forums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This also has me curious does naval combat count for per-turn mote regeneration? </div> </div> </div>I assumed not because I don't think there's anything in the corebook saying it does, and basically no other rule from ordinary combat applies to naval combat. But I agree it's intuitive that it does.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it makes more sense to not regenerate than it at at first appears: There's not nearly as much to spend motes on in naval combat, so mote regeneration would probably lead to less interesting decisions. Also, because momentum is one-way, naval battles can't really drag on as much as ordinary battles. (The only situation I can think of is if your PCs are super outnumbered so you send them up against a bunch of ships at once and they have to chew through all of them.)<br /> <br /> I imagine this must have come up in &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; at some point...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T09:42:47-07:00","id":1375446,"title":"","content":"Question for this thread!<br /> <br /> How many Ox-Bodies is enough Ox-Bodies? That is, is always picking Ox-Body the optimal combat choice if it is available? If it isn't, what is the optimal cutoff point?<br /> <br /> I have a similar question for Solar Athletics. Excluding Ox-Body, above, is Foe-Vaulting Method and Thunderbolt Attack Prana (a five charm investment for both, 3 charm for one of them) always the best investment?<br /> <br /> Do these answers change once you get some key Essence 1 charms (say 5 or less) from your primary attack/defense stat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T12:08:49-07:00","id":1375462,"title":"","content":"Foe-Vaulting Method is best combined with charms that work off surprise attacks. Otherwise I don't think it's amazing. Thunderbolt Attack Prana is both good and one of its prereqs is really good.<br /> <br /> For Ox-Bodies... eh, it depends on the rest of your group, your soak, your Defence, how combaty the game is, etc. There's a lot of variables.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T01:26:53-07:00","id":1375559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1375446#post1375446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for this thread!<br /> <br /> How many Ox-Bodies is enough Ox-Bodies? That is, is always picking Ox-Body the optimal combat choice if it is available? If it isn't, what is the optimal cutoff point?<br /> <br /> I have a similar question for Solar Athletics. Excluding Ox-Body, above, is Foe-Vaulting Method and Thunderbolt Attack Prana (a five charm investment for both, 3 charm for one of them) always the best investment?<br /> <br /> Do these answers change once you get some key Essence 1 charms (say 5 or less) from your primary attack/defense stat?</div> </div> </div> </div>For what purpose?<br /> <br /> You can play a strict pacifist. In which case you don't need any Ox-Bodies. Exalted supports this, but most STs do not.<br /> <br /> With unlimited resources, against the toughest opponents, more Ox-Bodies is always better.<br /> <br /> For a real game, I think I just conclusively proved that you can have a lot of fun in combat with Dex/Melee 3 and two combat Charms.<br /> <br /> That said, if you want to play a non-combatant, I'd advise starting with a defensive Charm or two (such as Dipping Swallow Defense and Pearlescent Filigree Defense), a single Ox-Body Technique, Dexterity 3 and Melee 2 with a mundane medium weapon (like a sword, or a shield if you want to be really non-combat). That gives you enough health levels to survive most alpha strikes and Defense 4 so you're not instagibbed by mortal farmers wielding sharp sticks. At this level, you are almost certainly a Supernal Craft scholar who can't afford to buy combat Charms: buying Ox-Bodies with XP is not a priority for you -- one will do. Socialite characters <i>can</i> run at this level, but I don't recommend it: consider taking one of the Social Martial Arts (Silver Voiced Nightingale, Black Claw, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, Righteous Devil or Crane) and running at the next level below. Dawns should not run at this level: you are not being unique and clever, don't do it.<br /> <br /> If you want to build a starting character who is capable in combat, but not a combat monster, I'd take one Ox-Body and four other combat Charms which fit your character concept. For example Ox-Body Technique, Excellent Strike, Dipping Swallow Defence, Fire and Stones Strike, &amp; Call the Blade. You can buy all these Charms with Melee 3, Resistance 1 (though I'd recommend Resistance 3). You need some (1-3 dots and Excellency) Awareness, Dodge and Athletics, and consider one or two combat appropriate Specialities. Your choice of mundane light (offense) or mundane medium (defense) weapon. Light mundane armor is essentially essential at this level; heavier armor should only be considered by mounted characters or characters agnostic to battlefield positioning. You'll want to buy up a couple more Ox-Bodies with XP, but this shouldn't be a priority unless you have no healer in the Circle (I'd still buy them before buying any other combat Charms though) or you are a Dawn Caste (in which case, <i>consider</i> starting with upto three Ox-bodies, five other combat Charms and five dots in Dexterity and your primary Combat Ability). This is the level appropriate for the majority of PCs, from Dawns (who <i>might</i> want to invest a <i>little</i> more than average, as described above) to Twilights (providing they aren't Supernal Crafters). If the Tomb of Dreams characters were at full starting character strength, they'd be about here. Looking at the character creation and NPC guidance, this is the default Exalted power level.<br /> <br /> If combat is your main focus, and you want to be a combat monster right out the gate, then I suggest starting with between 6-9 bonus health levels (so three-ish Ox-Bodies), an Onslaught negator, seven other Charms that directly effect your combat effectiveness (Thunderbolt Attack Prana counts as one of the seven but not it's prereqs), and four mobility Charms to help with Rush and Disengage. Definitely include Thunderbolt Attack Prana. Work on buying Sensory Acuity Prana through to Awakening Eye with XP (then buy up to the maximum 5 Ox-Bodies). Consider buying 5 dots in one ranged and one close Combat Ability, and in every other Ability marked &quot;this Ability is important in combat&quot;, with your Bonus Points. Take a broadly applicable Specialty in your primary combat ability. Take an artifact weapon. You need armor that fits your play style -- artifact is best if you can afford it, as heavy as mobility penalty allows (if you are mounted or can ignore mobility penalty then you want Heavy armor). You've now made a combat monster that can breeze over 90% of antagonists without trying. You are One Punch Man: prepare for a campaign where you weep bitterly about not having any opposition who can challenge you.<br /> <br /> In any case, you should talk with the ST and other players to get a feel for common expectations and power level.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Foe Vaulting Method is insanely good, but only if you have something that keys off Surprise Attacks. Pick up Blinding Battle Feint, some Ebon Shadow Style and you don't even need to launch Withering attacks anymore. Just spam back to back 7i Decisives, backed by TAP where possible (and because Decisives are weapon agnostic, you can take a fighting chain for the +1 Parry and make all your attacks unarmed to combo with other Martial Arts). Poison also helps this build.<br /> <br /> Without powers that key off Suprise Attacks FVM is still okay. It's not brilliant but it's okay -- very flavorful if you're playing an Athletic Nightwing-esque character who achieves victory by superior mobility. (If your foe can't ignore the Unexpected Attack penality to their DV and you are combat optimized then you were never going to struggle against that foe FVM or not. If your not combat optimized then you shouldn't care if FVM is optimal.)<br /> <br /> TAP is just crazy good. You have to move and it costs WP. But it's a big damage bump. It is absolutely not necessary for combat. You can have a lot of fun without it, and be effective in combat encounters. But if you want an optimal build, you want TAP (unless you are a ranged fighter).<br /> <br /> The Corebook recommends you have 2-5 combat Charms including at least one Ox-Body. This is good advice. Follow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-20-2020, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T00:31:44-07:00","id":1376678,"title":"","content":"I want to see what Mirror on Water Focus is like in practice. What should an Essence 5 water DB fight, and what should her supplementary abilities be, if any? Like resistance, brawl, dodge, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T00:52:34-07:00","id":1376685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1376678#post1376678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to see what Mirror on Water Focus is like in practice. What should an Essence 5 water DB fight, and what should her supplementary abilities be, if any? Like resistance, brawl, dodge, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahlat; Brawl, Occult, and Larceny. She has her weapon hidden at the start of the fight so Ahlat can\u2019t use Measure the Wind on her, lets him underestimate her, and then whips out the sword and starts whoopin\u2019 ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-26-2020, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T15:58:05-07:00","id":1376866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1376685#post1376685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahlat; Brawl, Occult, and Larceny. She has her weapon hidden at the start of the fight so Ahlat can\u2019t use Measure the Wind on her, lets him underestimate her, and then whips out the sword and starts whoopin\u2019 ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't go very well for the DB. Maybe somebody who's not a directional war god.<br /> <br /> Character<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Fist 15 (Damage 10/1)<br /> T. River 12 (Damage 17/5)<br /> Parry 6<br /> Soak 5<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3/5/5<br /> <br /> Wits 4<br /> Awareness 4<br /> Brawl 5 specialty unarmed<br /> Melee 5 specialty Thundering River<br /> Resistance 3<br /> Occult 5<br /> <br /> Awareness excellency<br /> <br /> Melee charms up to Mirror on Water focus, Roaring River Slash, Graceful Flowing Defense and Root and Hand Merging<br /> <br /> Occult charms up to Anathema-Sealing Tomb<br /> <br /> Resistance charms up to 3 Ox Bodies and Flowing Dragon-Body Endurance<br /> <br /> Larceny up to Naked Thief Style and Flowing God-Dragon Stance<br /> <br /> Brawl up to Fist Spinning Maelstrom, Smashing Tidal Wave Technique and Embracing the Violent Flow.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Alhat won't spend motes to join battle, spending 5 motes and rolling 10i<br /> Ezeri rolls 8+2 dice for 4m peripheral and getting 9i<br /> <br /> <br /> Alhat 10i 115m 10wp<br /> Ezeri 9i 16ps 34pp 7wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> Alhat will go for a withering strike, spending 5m to excellency. Ezeri will spend 4m on Skin of Stone, and 2m on Eternal Tide Endurance.<br /> <br /> Alat rolls 19 dice, getting 6, with two 1s. Then rolling 9 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Alhat 17i 110m 10wp<br /> Ezeri 3i 10ps 34pp 7wp<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Ezeri will take a full defense action, spending a mote to fill the area with a smell of the sea<br /> <br /> Alhat 17i 110m 10wp<br /> Ezeri 3i 10ps 33pp 7wp<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> Alhat 17i 115m 10wp<br /> Ezeri 3i 10ps 38pp 7wp<br /> <br /> Alhat will go for a withering strike, spending 5m to excellency. Ezeri will spend 6m on parry and 1i for Blade-Deflecting Palm.<br /> <br /> Alat rolls 19 dice, getting 9 and missing.<br /> <br /> Alhat 17i 110m 10wp<br /> Ezeri 2i 10ps 32pp 7wp<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Ezeri spends 1a 3m to retrieve her direlance from her anima, then 7m 1wp on Mirror-On Water Focus.<br /> <br /> Alhat 17i 110m 10wp<br /> Ezeri 2i 3ps 29pp 6wp<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> Alhat 17i 115m 10wp<br /> Ezeri 2i 3ps 34pp 6wp<br /> <br /> Alhat makes a decisive strike, using a 10m full excellency, 10m 1wp Blood Kisses Sand, and 15m 5i 1wp Ruin-Smiting Strike.<br /> <br /> Ezeri will end MoWF to make a decisive counterattack, spending 6m on the excellency, 3m on Burning Fury Wreath, 3m wp on Crimson Fang Bite, Alhat will defend with 10m 1wp to add his current initiative to hardness.<br /> <br /> with a hardness of 22 Alhat can not be damaged by the attack so it fizzles.<br /> <br /> Alhat 17i 70m 8wp<br /> Ezeri 2i 3ps 22pp 5wp<br /> <br /> Alhat returns with a 24 die decisive, Ezeri will defend with 5m full excellency. Rolling 24 dice for 11, hitting by 2. Then rolling 14i+4 damage for a total of 13 levels of lethal, along with a wound that won't close<br /> <br /> Alhat 6i 70m 8wp<br /> Ezeri 2i 3ps 17pp 5wp 13L (-2s)<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Ezeri will attempt a withering strike, spening 6m to excellency along with 3m 1wp for Crimson Fang Bite. Alhat will not spend motes to defend. Rolling 15 dice and getting only 6, then rolling 5 damage for nothing.<br /> <br /> End of turn Ezeri loses 2i and one more L to the wound<br /> <br /> Alhat 6i 70m 8wp<br /> Ezeri 2i 3ps 17pp 5wp 14L (-2s)<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> Alhat 6i 75m 8wp<br /> Ezeri 2i 3ps 22pp 5wp 14L (-2s)<br /> <br /> Alhat will give a withering strike, spending 10m to excellency then 4m on Horned God Prowess. Ezeri will defend with 4m Skin of Stone and 4m Ripples on Water, and 2m Eternal Tide Endurance. Rolling 24 dice for 15 against a parry of 8, with one 1.<br /> <br /> Rolling 24 damage dice for 12, with two 1s making it 10 damage, crashing Ezeri.<br /> <br /> Alhat 17i 61m 8wp<br /> Ezeri -8i 3ps 12pp 5wp 14L (-2s)<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Ezeri makes a withering strike, with a full excellency and CFB, Alhat will not spend motes to defend. 15 and getting 7, then rolling 5 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> End of round Ezeri loses another 2i and a health level<br /> <br /> Alhat 17i 61m 8wp<br /> Ezeri -10i 3ps 3pp 4wp 15L (-4s)<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> Alhat makes a decisive attack with 10m, Ezeri will defend with 6m excellency. The attack hits and with 17i yeilding 7 damage Ezeri is slain.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Turns out when Alhat decides to get serious and start using his charms, especially in combination with eachother, it gets pretty crazy. He didn't even use Whispering Warrior Souls or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T18:09:47-07:00","id":1376881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1376866#post1376866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Turns out when Alhat decides to get serious and start using his charms, especially in combination with eachother, it gets pretty crazy. He didn't even use Whispering Warrior Souls or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ouch. Alhat's Charm that adds his initiative to his hardness is basically a hard counter against Mirror-On-Water's effect of attacking an enemy with their own initiative, so he may not be the best opponent to demonstrate that Charm in action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T18:21:27-07:00","id":1376883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1376881#post1376881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ouch. Alhat's Charm that adds his initiative to his hardness is basically a hard counter against Mirror-On-Water's effect of attacking an enemy with their own initiative, so he may not be the best opponent to demonstrate that Charm in action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T03:21:43-07:00","id":1376939,"title":"","content":"I'm reasonably sure no DB build can take Ahlat one-on-one.<br /> <br /> Fight the Wandering Deathknight (Mounted Version).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T08:23:04-07:00","id":1376965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1376883#post1376883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd be intrigued to see how long Ezeri can last against Octavian, but for a fair fight I'm not sure myself, maybe 1-2 lower essence exalts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T12:30:45-07:00","id":1376984,"title":"","content":"There is a theoretical Solar Death Ray build that involves getting Larceny 5 and two Fate-Shifting Solar Aretes as well as a Jewel of the Rabbit's Sword Hearthstone to optimize the initial attack roll. You also of course have Intelligence 5, Occult 5, a specialty, and 10 Willpower. This gives you a pretty crazy expected number of successes, recurring every turn. Probably you should take Resistance 5 and Aegis of Invincible Might for defense since you're making a Decisive every turn. Could such a build defeat an Essence 5 Solar Melee build? Is this even a reasonable question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T13:19:09-07:00","id":1376987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1376984#post1376984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a theoretical Solar Death Ray build that involves getting Larceny 5 and two Fate-Shifting Solar Aretes as well as a Jewel of the Rabbit's Sword Hearthstone to optimize the initial attack roll. You also of course have Intelligence 5, Occult 5, a specialty, and 10 Willpower. This gives you a pretty crazy expected number of successes, recurring every turn. Probably you should take Resistance 5 and Aegis of Invincible Might for defense since you're making a Decisive every turn. Could such a build defeat an Essence 5 Solar Melee build? Is this even a reasonable question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what other supplemental abilities, but almost certainly not. Thunderclap Rush Attack allows a Solar to always attack first in combat regardless of actual initiative values, and an Essence 5 melee Solar can kill basically anything given an action and enough motes/willpower to do so.<br /> <br /> Which, I mean, come on. The Solar sorcerer can touch the ground and bless it into an eternal fertile Eden, explode the top off a mountain, blight an entire kingdom to certain death and famine for decades, and summon and bind into servitude Ligier, who rivals the Unconquered Sun himself in power. It's probably a good thing they can't also match the warrior who's dedicated their entire character to fighting people in personal combat.<br /> <br /> If you want your Essence 5 Solar Sorcerer to beat an Essence 5 Dawn in combat have him summon and bind Ligier, Erembour, Jacint, and Orabilis during Calibration and have that hit squad bomb down and fight the Dawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T15:04:08-07:00","id":1376999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1376987#post1376987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends what other supplemental abilities, but almost certainly not. Thunderclap Rush Attack allows a Solar to always attack first in combat regardless of actual initiative values, and an Essence 5 melee Solar can kill basically anything given an action and enough motes/willpower to do so.<br /> <br /> Which, I mean, come on. The Solar sorcerer can touch the ground and bless it into an eternal fertile Eden, explode the top off a mountain, blight an entire kingdom to certain death and famine for decades, and summon and bind into servitude Ligier, who rivals the Unconquered Sun himself in power. It's probably a good thing they can't also match the warrior who's dedicated their entire character to fighting people in personal combat.<br /> <br /> If you want your Essence 5 Solar Sorcerer to beat an Essence 5 Dawn in combat have him summon and bind Ligier, Erembour, Jacint, and Orabilis during Calibration and have that hit squad bomb down and fight the Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all fair points. <br /> <br /> I don't think an Essence 5 Solar Sorcer should beat an Essence 5 Solar Melee specialist in single combat.<br /> <br /> I'm just amused by the idea that, if you do want to defeat someone in single combat using only sorcery (maybe they challenged you to a duel and those are the rules - sounds like the kind of stuff Solars might have gotten up to right before the Usurpation) you may want to spend your life studying Larceny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T15:22:48-07:00","id":1377001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1376987#post1376987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thunderclap Rush Attack allows a Solar to always attack first in combat regardless of actual initiative values...</div> </div> </div> </div>...if, and only if, he is at the correct range to use it. If the fight starts at Medium range, Melee Solar will have to wait until he can close to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T16:12:23-07:00","id":1377006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377001#post1377001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...if, and only if, he is at the correct range to use it. If the fight starts at Medium range, Melee Solar will have to wait until he can close to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you're at medium you can always close with your reflexive move and then do it. It's not impossible to win, especially since &quot;Essence 5 Dawn&quot; covers a WIIIDE range of characters and concepts. I just wouldn't expect it to make up the difference in single combat between your character and a Dawn dedicated to single combat without stacking things unfairly in your favour to start out.<br /> <br /> You don't want to take one of the biggest issues with DnD and put it into Exalted, where the guy who can turn into a dragon, tear open gateways between worlds, immortalize themselves with ageless clones, peer into the distant future and faraway planes with divination, can then also just totally clown the level 20 fighter in single combat with a no-save Forcecage and cloudkill or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T16:22:27-07:00","id":1377010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377006#post1377006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if you're at medium you can always close with your reflexive move and then do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no, Thunderclap Rush Attack includes movement, so you can't move <i>and</i> TRA in the same turn.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T16:24:02-07:00","id":1377011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377010#post1377010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, Thunderclap Rush Attack includes movement, so you can't move <i>and</i> TRA in the same turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thunderclap Rush specifically says it doesn't count as the character's movement. Solar charms are very very good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T16:42:50-07:00","id":1377013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377011#post1377011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thunderclap Rush specifically says it doesn't count as the character's movement. Solar charms are very very good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I misremembered - I thought it used up your movement and attack, when it just uses up your attack. <i>That said</i>, if the Solar is having to wait until his turn to use his move to get in range to Thunderclap Rush Attack, then he's <i>still</i> having to actually go on his turn, and can't just decide &quot;I go first.&quot; He's actually got to win Initiative.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Which, y'know, he can very likely do unless the sorcerer is equally invested in JB.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T17:16:02-07:00","id":1377018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377013#post1377013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I misremembered - I thought it used up your movement and attack, when it just uses up your attack. <i>That said</i>, if the Solar is having to wait until his turn to use his move to get in range to Thunderclap Rush Attack, then he's <i>still</i> having to actually go on his turn, and can't just decide &quot;I go first.&quot; He's actually got to win Initiative.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Which, y'know, he can very likely do unless the sorcerer is equally invested in JB.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What if we start them at long enough range that the sorcerer at least gets an attack in? I guess if it's just one attack the Melee type can still win by using Seven Shadows Evasion.<br /> <br /> It might also be interesting to force the Melee type to only use Melee charms (or only Melee among the main combat abilitiies) so Thunderclap Rush Attack is not allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T19:45:48-07:00","id":1377047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377018#post1377018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if we start them at long enough range that the sorcerer at least gets an attack in? I guess if it's just one attack the Melee type can still win by using Seven Shadows Evasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking Athletics as well as Melee Long Range isn't actually enough. A Solar can move once reflexively, move again with One More Step, move a third time with Invincible Fury of the Dawn, and then a fourth range band with Thunderbolt Attack Prana. They can close into melee distance in a single action from the first range band of Extreme if they really want to.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't propagate to six range right away. You start at Short and then grow it successively, which gives them more rounds to rush in. Or alternatively just back away past six range bands and wait for you to get sick of channeling death ray, then charge in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377018#post1377018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might also be interesting to force the Melee type to only use Melee charms (or only Melee among the main combat abilitiies) so Thunderclap Rush Attack is not allowed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Restricting to just melee charms might be enough. Solar melee though is really, really fucking good, in almost all situations. For example if you're facing a Dawn with Death Ray at Long range. So you're going to attack with your awesome 13 die attack with 5 auto-successes, and counting both 1s and 2s as 10s, that's pretty damn awesome. The defense you're going up against to hit that though is a parry of 12, and any 1s and 2s might count as 10s, but up to 5 of them also subtract 1 success due to Hail Shattering Practice.<br /> <br /> Even with that though, you're still likely to hit. Maybe only just, but a hit is a hit. After that though, Heavenly Guardian Defense comes into play, stripping one flat success of damage for 1i each, and if the full damage is nullified then Protection of Celestial Bliss activates. Up to 5 1s and 2s on the damage roll get banked for the next Heavenly Guardian Defense, which can be doubled for 4m 1wp by Protection of Celestial Bliss.<br /> <br /> If you can get to the point where they're out of initiative to Heavenly Guardian Defense before they reach Short range though, you're still not in the clear, because they might just decide to run if they're smart. So they're at medium range, and you blast them back to long, they can then get up and start withdrawing which gives you a short period of time to chew through their health levels before they're gone. If they don't think to or refuse to leave though, then at that point, basically you win, since they can't get closer to you, and your awesome to-hit roll will always hit.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand you could flub the attack roll, or the roll to generate 25 sm just by getting unlucky. If that happens and you can't muster at least 12 successes, then you're in mega trouble.<br /> <br /> <br /> I know the instant gut reaction to seeing Death Ray with Solar Arete is &quot;How could anything, how could <i>ANYTHING </i>stand up to that!?&quot; but Essence 5 Dawn casts are the greatest warriors in all of the Exalted host bar absolutely none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T20:41:33-07:00","id":1377054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377047#post1377047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking Athletics as well as Melee Long Range isn't actually enough. A Solar can move once reflexively, move again with One More Step, move a third time with Invincible Fury of the Dawn, and then a fourth range band with Thunderbolt Attack Prana. They can close into melee distance in a single action from the first range band of Extreme if they really want to.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't propagate to six range right away. You start at Short and then grow it successively, which gives them more rounds to rush in. Or alternatively just back away past six range bands and wait for you to get sick of channeling death ray, then charge in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think invincible fury of the dawn and thunderbolt attack prana can be used together - thunderbolt attack prana lets you make an attack, not take an action. Either way it's still enough to attack starting from long range though.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the best defense might be solar charms, not distance. To pull this off you only really need 9 charms (FSSA and prerequisites, 3 sorceries), leaving you pretty free to take additional defensive charms like Adamant Skin Technique or Uncanny Shroud Defense or Hail-Shattering Practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377047#post1377047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Restricting to just melee charms might be enough. Solar melee though is really, really fucking good, in almost all situations. For example if you're facing a Dawn with Death Ray at Long range. So you're going to attack with your awesome 13 die attack with 5 auto-successes, and counting both 1s and 2s as 10s, that's pretty damn awesome. The defense you're going up against to hit that though is a parry of 12, and any 1s and 2s might count as 10s, but up to 5 of them also subtract 1 success due to Hail Shattering Practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>FSSA would need to targets 2s and 3s, but you can use Jewel of the Rabbit's sword to reroll 1s.<br /> I think that if you're rerolling 1s and counting 2s as 10s, you don't have any 1s or 2s in your final roll, so Hail Shattering Practice is, I think, useless against you.<br /> Also, it might make sense to give up the auto-successes and use an excellency for dice (or use supernal control method). Given you get 1 success per die, you're basically spending 10m for 5 successes on average, ie. the same as the ordinary excellency.<br /> Which averages 24 successes (counting spending a willpower for a success. Ideally use Flowing Intention Cultivation to preserve your actual willpower for extra damage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T20:57:20-07:00","id":1377057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377054#post1377054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think invincible fury of the dawn and thunderbolt attack prana can be used together - thunderbolt attack prana lets you make an attack, not take an action. Either way it's still enough to attack starting from long range though.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the best defense might be solar charms, not distance. To pull this off you only really need 9 charms (FSSA and prerequisites, 3 sorceries), leaving you pretty free to take additional defensive charms like Adamant Skin Technique or Uncanny Shroud Defense or Hail-Shattering Practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, best defense probably is Solar charms. If you're wielding Death Ray with FSSA, Aegis of Invincible Might, Seven Shadow Evasion and Uncanny Shroud Defense, against a Dawn who doesn't have anything but Melee charms I think you'll do quite well.<br /> <br /> Also, just to reiterate, if this is a combo that decimates an expertly built Dawn cast at Essence 5, there is a problem that should be fixed.<br /> <br /> TAP can be used with IFoD though, it probably only doubles the damage of the first attack, but it's a supplemental charm that supplements an attack just like Excellent Strike or Fire and Stones Strike.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377054#post1377054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FSSA would need to targets 2s and 3s, but you can use Jewel of the Rabbit's sword to reroll 1s.<br /> I think that if you're rerolling 1s and counting 2s as 10s, you don't have any 1s or 2s in your final roll, so Hail Shattering Practice is, I think, useless against you.<br /> Also, it might make sense to give up the auto-successes and use an excellency for dice (or use supernal control method). Given you get 1 success per die, you're basically spending 10m for 5 successes on average, ie. the same as the ordinary excellency.<br /> Which averages 24 successes (counting spending a willpower for a success. Ideally use Flowing Intention Cultivation to preserve your actual willpower for extra damage).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah right, they don't give you two successes they literally are 10s, that would stop Hail Shattering Practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:17:41-07:00","id":1377083,"title":"","content":"Doesn\u2019t a Supplemental Charm need to be able to enhance every attack in the flurry in order to be compatible with a multi-attack Charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:30:17-07:00","id":1377091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377083#post1377083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn\u2019t a Supplemental Charm need to be able to enhance every attack in the flurry in order to be compatible with a multi-attack Charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why, it says the cost only needs to be paid once to enhance every attack in the flurry, not that you must use supplemental charms on every attack in the flurry in the same way, and if you can't you have to stop attacking. Like you could use Hungry Tiger Technique on it and only choose to activate that supplemental charm against crashed foes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T23:15:04-07:00","id":1377105,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is Ezeri using Mirror on Water Focus against the mounted abyssal. To give the Abyssal a chance I'm going to say Ezeri still isn't using any armor and needs to avoid all the damage from that direlance with her resistance charms.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Abyssal rolls 16 dice for 9i<br /> Ezeri rolls 8+2 dice for 7i<br /> <br /> Abyss 9i 16p 22h 6wp<br /> Ezeri 7i 16p 34h 7wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> Abyss charges in to Short range and rushes, rolling 13 dice against 10 for 9, beating Ezeri's 4.<br /> <br /> Abyss 9i 16p 22h 6wp<br /> Ezeri 7i 16p 34h 7wp<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Ezeri dashes forward, closing the rest of the distance, and attacks with a withering 6m excellency 1m anima stunt, Abyssal will defend with a 10m full excellency. Rolling 18 dice for 9 Ezeri misses.<br /> <br /> Abyss 9i 16p 12h 6wp<br /> Ezeri 7i 10p 34h 7wp<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> Abyss 9i 16p 17h 6wp<br /> Ezeri 7i 11p 38h 7wp<br /> <br /> Abyss gives a withering strike with a 10m excellency behind it. Ezeri defends with 4m ISoS, 2m Eternal Tide Endurance, both stunt. Rolling 25 dice for 14 successes, and four 1s. Then rolling 9 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Abyss 16i 16p 17h 6wp<br /> Ezeri 1i 5p 38h 7wp<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Ezeri will spend 7m 1wp on Mirror On Water Focus.<br /> <br /> Abyss 16i 16p 17h 6wp<br /> Ezeri 1i 0p 36h 6wp<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> Abyss 16i 16p 22h 6wp<br /> Ezeri 1i 3p 38h 6wp<br /> <br /> Abyss attacks with 10m excellency, 2m Savage Shade Style, 2m 2i Artful Maiming Onslaught.<br /> <br /> Ezeri will end Mirror on Water Focus to strike back with a 6m excellency with 3m Burning Fury Wreath and 3m 1wp Crimson Fang Bite. Abyss will defend with a 10m excellency. Rolling 17 dice against a parry of 11 she actually makes it JUST with 11.<br /> <br /> Rolling 7i damage for 4L<br /> <br /> Abyss 10i 16p 0h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 1i 3p 26h 5wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Abyssal will continue with attack, Ezeri will defend with 5m 1wp Root-And-Hand Merging, 3m excellency and 4m Ripples on Water Defense. Rolling 24 dice against a parry of 10 for 10, just hitting. Then rolling 10 damage for 4L<br /> <br /> <br /> Abyss 3i 16p 0h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 1i 3p 14h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Ezeri will attack with a 6m excellency'd strike, Abyss will defend with a 10m excellency. Rolling 16 dice against 10 for 11 and actually hitting, then rolling 5 damage for 2.<br /> <br /> Abyss 1i 6p 0h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 4i 3p 8h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ===========<br /> Abyss 1i 11p 0h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 4i 3p 13h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Ezeri launches another withering with 5m full excellency, 1m anima activation, Abyssal will defend with 2m Elegant Flowing Deflection and 8m excellency. Rolling 16 dice aggainst a parry of 10 for 10 again. Then rolling 5 damage for only 1, still crashing the Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Abyss 0i 1p 0h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 11i 3p 8h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Abyssal will strike back with an unenhanced attack, Ezeri will defend with a 2m full excellency, 2m 1i Graceful Flowing Defense. Rolling 12 dice against a parry of 9 for only 6.<br /> <br /> Abyss 0i 1p 0h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 10i 3p 4h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ===========<br /> Abyss 0i 1p 5h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 10i 3p 9h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Ezeri will attack with a 3m full excellency, Abyss will defend with a 4m excellency, 2m Elegant Flowing Deflection. Rolling 16 dice against a parry of 8 for 7, missing.<br /> <br /> Abyss 0i 0p 0h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 10i 3p 6h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Abyss will attack unenhanced, Ezeri will defend with 4m full excellency. Rolling 12 dice against parry 8 for 3, missing.<br /> <br /> Abyss 0i 0p 0h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 10i 3p 2h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> ===========<br /> Abyss 0i 0p 5h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 10i 3p 7h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Ezeri will strike another withering blow with a 5m full excellency. Abyssal will not spend motes to defend. Rolling 16 against parry 5 for 9, then 6 damage for 4.<br /> <br /> Abyss -3i 0p 5h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 15i 3p 2h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Abyssal resets to base initiative and attacks Ezeri with 5m excellency. Ezeri will defend with 2m full excellency. Rolling 12 dice for 7 the Abyssal misses, just.<br /> <br /> Abyss 3i 0p 0h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 15i 3p 0h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Round 7<br /> ===========<br /> Abyss 3i 0p 5h 6wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Ezeri 15i 3p 5h 4wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Ezeri will attack with 3m full excellenncy, 5m 1wp Roaring River Slash, Abyssal will defend with 4m excellency. Rolling 15 dice against parry 7 for 8 Ezeri hits, then rolling 30 damage for a very dissapointing 5.<br /> <br /> Abyss 3i 0p 5h 6wp 9L(-2s)<br /> Ezeri 3i 0p 0h 3wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Abyssal will attack with a 1m excellency, Ezeri will defend with a free excellency rolling 11 dice against parry 8 for only 5 and missing.<br /> <br /> Round 8<br /> ===========<br /> Abyss 3i 0p 5h 6wp 9L(-2s)<br /> Ezeri 3i 0p 5h 3wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Abyssal and Ezeri will attack eachother in a clash, Ezeri spending 0m to almost full excellency and 5m to crossfire flash. The abyssal spending 5m to excellency. The abyssal rolls 15 dice for 10, Ezeri rolls 15 dice for 9, but rerolls 5 non-1 failures for a total of 13.<br /> <br /> Then rolling 5 damage for 1, which due to a winning clash becomes 3 damage, crashing the abyssal again.<br /> <br /> Abyss 0i 0p 0h 6wp 9L(-4s)***Just realized 9L means -4s<br /> Ezeri 12i 0p 0h 3wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Round 9<br /> ===========<br /> <br /> Ezeri attacks with a decisive strike, using a free full excellency. Abyssal defends with 2m excellency 2m Elegant Flowing Defense. Rolling 15 dice against a parry of 7 she misses with only 4.<br /> <br /> Abyss 0i 0p 1h 6wp 9L(-4s)***Just realized 9L means -4s<br /> Ezeri 8i 0p 5h 3wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Abyssal strikes with a 1m excellency, Ezeri spends 4m to full excellency the defense. Rolling 10 dice and getting only 6 the abyssal misses.<br /> <br /> Abyss 0i 0p 0h 6wp 9L(-4s)***Just realized 9L means -4s<br /> Ezeri 8i 0p 1h 3wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Round 10<br /> ===========<br /> Abyss 0i 0p 5h 6wp 9L(-4s)***Just realized 9L means -4s<br /> Ezeri 8i 0p 6h 3wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> <br /> Ezeri will aim at the Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Abyss 0i 0p 5h 6wp 9L(-4s)***Just realized 9L means -4s<br /> Ezeri 8i 0p 6h 3wp 4L(-2s)*Due to crippling maiming<br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Abyssal will attack with a 5m full excellency, Ezeri will clash with 4m 1wp Portenteous Comet Deflection and 3m excellency. The abyssal rolls 15 dice for 8, Ezeri rolls 19 for 10. Then rolling 8 damage for 4, killing the Abyssal.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wow that was super close. I'm noticing that Mirror on Water Focus requires a kind of ST buy-in to make it very useful. You can't launch Decisive attacks while crashed, which means if the abyssal just went and crashed Ezeri while it was up, the effect would be useless. It's not like crashing is a bad idea either, the only bad thing about crashing a opponent before decisive attacking them is that they can get an initiative shift on you after if they don't die.<br /> <br /> Some other stuff is like that too Aegis of Invincible Might has a perfect counter in that if you never decisive the person who's got it unless they're crashed, they never activate it.<br /> <br /> When it does go off though, I did like the effect. Stripping your opponent of initiative just before they hit you, while dealing damage and potentially giving them a wound penalty to deal with is a pretty badass effect. I feel though that it might be better combined with a Defend Other action. You can't use it if you've attacked that turn anyway, and that way somebody could get crashed, be about to be annihilated, but then you defend them and counterattack on their behalf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T04:31:42-07:00","id":1377152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377083#post1377083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn\u2019t a Supplemental Charm need to be able to enhance every attack in the flurry in order to be compatible with a multi-attack Charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's 2E. Rules for 3E are on page 252.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T05:23:11-07:00","id":1377158,"title":"","content":"Vance actually already answered this in the Ask a Dev thread (when asked if TAP could affect every attack of IFoD)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1368584#post1368584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. You could use it on the first attack, but the others wouldn't benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semi-related question: If two Melee-optimized Dawns (but using Charms from other Abilities if necessary) fought each other, who would win? Would it simply be (starting at close range) whoever has the higher initiative roll or (starting at greater range) whoever has the better Thunderclap Rush Attack stunt? Or are the counterattack charms good enough that they both kill each other? Or are the defensive Charms good enough that both get to take a turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 03-29-2020, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T06:02:22-07:00","id":1377161,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re right; in fact, I was the one who asked last time. I can\u2019t believe how forgetful I am getting these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T22:44:29-07:00","id":1377454,"title":"","content":"Man, it's been a while since I've been here.<br /> <br /> With the new errata on TAP, does that mean the Shining Topaz build that can kill a hearth of DBs is dead? I hope so, it was kinda cheesy. But I think it just means the DBs need to start at Short instead of close for the thing to work?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, this talk of a fight sequence makes me want to toss Topaz against a bunch of badass dudes in sequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 03-31-2020, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T23:27:25-07:00","id":1377457,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call that &quot;errata&quot; so much as &quot;a clarification.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T23:28:24-07:00","id":1377458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377454#post1377454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, it's been a while since I've been here.<br /> <br /> With the new errata on TAP, does that mean the Shining Topaz build that can kill a hearth of DBs is dead? I hope so, it was kinda cheesy. But I think it just means the DBs need to start at Short instead of close for the thing to work?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, this talk of a fight sequence makes me want to toss Topaz against a bunch of badass dudes in sequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Circle of Bright Reaving you can still slay an entire Wyld Hunt or Lunar Pack or Abyssal Circle in one attack before they can act.<br /> <br /> It only works if they're within close range of eachother, but if a Lunar hunting pack is assaulting a Solar circle it's not unreasonable to have them all charge in. Going in one at a time to get dogpiled is not a good idea even if you know the Dawn can do that. The only other option is to have everyone sit at different range bands using ranged weapons, which is really only a thrown thing. Either that or if you want you can just start giving everyone Perfect level defenses 2e style. Not really an option with DBs but you can at least avoid a whole circle of Abyssals or Lunars going down without a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T00:14:47-07:00","id":1377465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377458#post1377458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Circle of Bright Reaving you can still slay an entire Wyld Hunt or Lunar Pack or Abyssal Circle in one attack before they can act.<br /> <br /> It only works if they're within close range of eachother, but if a Lunar hunting pack is assaulting a Solar circle it's not unreasonable to have them all charge in. Going in one at a time to get dogpiled is not a good idea even if you know the Dawn can do that. The only other option is to have everyone sit at different range bands using ranged weapons, which is really only a thrown thing. Either that or if you want you can just start giving everyone Perfect level defenses 2e style. Not really an option with DBs but you can at least avoid a whole circle of Abyssals or Lunars going down without a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically it was Heaven Sword Flash. The build didn't have room for Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T13:11:52-07:00","id":1377789,"title":"","content":"I've decided that I'm going to try to show off the power of Melee via Shining Topaz, so I'll be giving her 50 xp and 40 solar xp to round her out and put her at E2. She will fight a bunch of the strongest QCs in the corebook and etc in sequence. I plan on at least Ahlat and Octavian and Lilith. Any QCs or PC builds people would like to see go up against Shining Topaz as she attempts to earn the Invincible Sword Princess sobriquet by defeating all comers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T15:04:36-07:00","id":1377803,"title":"","content":"If you have access to the Hundred Devil Night Parade Mata-Yadh is pretty badass, so is Zicnal of the Asmani. Throwing either Berit or Cathak Cainen in there might be good too. Do you mean to actually do consecutive fights where like, you battle Alhat, and as soon as he goes down join battle against Octavian, and then as soon as he goes down join battle against Lilith and see how many you get through?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T16:59:41-07:00","id":1377821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377803#post1377803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have access to the Hundred Devil Night Parade Mata-Yadh is pretty badass, so is Zicnal of the Asmani. Throwing either Berit or Cathak Cainen in there might be good too. Do you mean to actually do consecutive fights where like, you battle Alhat, and as soon as he goes down join battle against Octavian, and then as soon as he goes down join battle against Lilith and see how many you get through?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>It is the site of a great victory feast! Deep in the Southlands the Fae massed an army not seen since the Balorian Crusade! Yet heroes rose to meet them. Lunars, Solars, Dragonblooded Scions of the Realm and beyond, Gods and demons and the dead, and of course mortal men in their tens of thousands. On the site of their victory, where the Raksha leading the crusade was vanquished, the armies of Creation throw a great feast. And as they drink, and eat, and revel, the great heroes of the day give their speeches.<br /> <br /> Soon it is the turn of Shining Topaz, the Forsaken of Terek, vanquisher of Wild Hunts, master of the blade. Instead of a speech celebrating their deeds, the impetuous young woman lays down a challenge. She declares herself the Invincible Sword Princess, and throws down the gauntlet: She thinks that she can beat anyone here in a 1 on 1 fight and she will take all comers who want to prove her wrong.<br /> <br /> The other exalts at the feast rise to her challenge, and shortly an arena is marked out for the combats and sanctified by the southern god of martial arts that although injuries will seem real, none shall die of injuries sustained in the ring. Shining Topaz shall start in the ring, taking all comers, and no sooner has a loser been dragged away than a new contender will step up. The first of her opponents is the great hero: [Insert person here]</i><br /> <br /> Yeah, as soon as you beat one you immediately join battle with the next, no refreshment of resources and scene-long charms stay up. Just an endless stream of foes until she goes down.<br /> <br /> The nature of the narrative framing means only one person with any given artifact, no fae, Fakharu is not available because the fight is taking place in the wrong direction, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 04-01-2020, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:10:18-07:00","id":1377838,"title":"","content":"Hmm, that makes a lot of sense as something that could actually happen. It's probably going to end up going faster for you if you start off slow and build up to the real heavy hitters rather than start off big and finish small. Like if you beat Alhat, Octavian, and Lilith, then you're going to have not a lot left over for Mata-Yadh, Zicnal, Berit, etc. On the other hand you can probably beat them without spending a lot of motes anyway, it'll just take forever.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you go up against Alhat with zero motes left it's going to be a relatively hard fight, unless you have a lot of really good scene-long charms active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:13:31-07:00","id":1377857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377838#post1377838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, that makes a lot of sense as something that could actually happen. It's probably going to end up going faster for you if you start off slow and build up to the real heavy hitters rather than start off big and finish small. Like if you beat Alhat, Octavian, and Lilith, then you're going to have not a lot left over for Mata-Yadh, Zicnal, Berit, etc. On the other hand you can probably beat them without spending a lot of motes anyway, it'll just take forever.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you go up against Alhat with zero motes left it's going to be a relatively hard fight, unless you have a lot of really good scene-long charms active.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds good. What kind of fights should I do to build up to Alhat and Octavian and Lilith? I actually think I might draw up Death Kitty, The Knight of Bone and Ivory, and maybe another lunar to gate Lilith behind. I also need to figure out an order, would be kinda a let down to do the Wandering Deathknight from the corebook after Lilith, yanno?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T22:15:02-07:00","id":1377884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377857#post1377857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sounds good. What kind of fights should I do to build up to Alhat and Octavian and Lilith? I actually think I might draw up Death Kitty, The Knight of Bone and Ivory, and maybe another lunar to gate Lilith behind. I also need to figure out an order, would be kinda a let down to do the Wandering Deathknight from the corebook after Lilith, yanno?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Berit &gt; Wandering Deathknight &gt; Octavian &gt; Lilith &gt; Alhat or something along those lines? Maybe stick the Ivory Bone Knight in front of Lilith if you want. The start of the QC chapter says the charm lists are examples, not exhaustive so you might want to give them one or two others if you feel like they\u2019re not quite up to snuff.<br /> <br /> If you can get through all that alive then you\u2019re decidedly an invincible sword princess. Take a few minutes to look at each of their charms before the fight though, some of them have particular strategies that they might want to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T22:59:20-07:00","id":1377890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377884#post1377884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe Berit &gt; Wandering Deathknight &gt; Octavian &gt; Lilith &gt; Alhat or something along those lines? Maybe stick the Ivory Bone Knight in front of Lilith if you want. The start of the QC chapter says the charm lists are examples, not exhaustive so you might want to give them one or two others if you feel like they\u2019re not quite up to snuff.<br /> <br /> If you can get through all that alive then you\u2019re decidedly an invincible sword princess. Take a few minutes to look at each of their charms before the fight though, some of them have particular strategies that they might want to use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds good. I think I'll stick the Barbarian Warlord Lunar QC in front of...would it be better to put him in front of Octavian or in front of the Deathknight? I'd <i>like</i> to go up against the Knight of Bone and Ivory, but actual PCs are way more complicated than QCs and I'm not sure my mastery of Lunars is up to snuff to do a Lunar PC justice (pretty sure it isn't, actually).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T06:04:42-07:00","id":1377935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1377890#post1377890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sounds good. I think I'll stick the Barbarian Warlord Lunar QC in front of...would it be better to put him in front of Octavian or in front of the Deathknight? I'd <i>like</i> to go up against the Knight of Bone and Ivory, but actual PCs are way more complicated than QCs and I'm not sure my mastery of Lunars is up to snuff to do a Lunar PC justice (pretty sure it isn't, actually).</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably best to put the warlord in front of the deathknight. That way you\u2019re going DB-Lunar-Abyssal-Demon-Lunar Elder-Directional War God. Also the complexity increases there too, Alhat, Octavian and Lilith are all more complex characters than the lunar warlord or the deathknight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T15:23:58-07:00","id":1379075,"title":"","content":"<i>It is the site of a great victory feast! Deep in the Southlands the Fae massed an army not seen since the Balorian Crusade! Yet heroes rose to meet them. Lunars, Solars, Dragonblooded Scions of the Realm and beyond, Gods and demons and the dead, and of course mortal men in their tens of thousands. On the site of their victory, where the Raksha leading the crusade was vanquished, the armies of Creation throw a great feast. And as they drink, and eat, and revel, the great heroes of the day give their speeches.<br /> <br /> Soon it is the turn of Shining Topaz, the Forsaken of Terek, vanquisher of Wild Hunts, master of the blade. Instead of a speech celebrating their deeds, the impetuous young woman lays down a challenge. She declares herself the Invincible Sword Princess, and throws down the gauntlet: She thinks that she can beat anyone here in a 1 on 1 fight and she will take all comers who want to prove her wrong.<br /> <br /> The other exalts at the feast rise to her challenge, and shortly an arena is marked out for the combats and sanctified by the southern god of martial arts that although injuries will seem real, none shall die of injuries sustained in the ring. Shining Topaz shall start in the ring, taking all comers, and no sooner has a loser been dragged away than a new contender will step up. The first of her opponents is the great hero: Berit.<br /> <br /> \u201cTruly,\u201d Berit exclaims as she enters the ring, \u201cthe arrogance of the Solar Anathema know no bounds. I will gladly put you in your place, little girl.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Fight 1:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/8217\" target=\"_blank\">Shining Topaz</a> spends 5m on Sensory Aucity Prana (committing them) and 10m on the Awareness Excellency. She rolls 22 dice with double 9s, for 7 sux. She starts with 10i.<br /> <br /> Berit spends 4 dice on Join Battle excellency. She rolls 13 dice for 5 sux. She starts with 8i.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (23/33m, 8wp, -0): 10i<br /> Berit (38/38m, 8wp, -0): 8i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz commits 5m and spends 1wp to activate Fivefold Bulwark Stance.<br /> <br /> Berit makes a Decisive Attack. She spends 6m on the excellency to add four dice and 3m, 1wp on Crimson Fang Bite, she also stunts to add 2 dice. Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense, stunts, and spends 4m on the melee excellency to bring her parry up to 11.<br /> <br /> Berit rolls 21 dice for 10 sux against Parry 11, missing. She loses 2i for missing a decisive putting her at 6i. Topaz gains 1i for blocking with Dipping Swallow Defense, putting her at 11i. Berit enters fire aura<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 2:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (23/28m, 7wp, -0): 11i<br /> Berit (34/38m, 7wp, -0, Fire): 6i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 6i on Strength Increasing Excerise to raise her strength to 5 for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> Berit makes a withering attack, she spends 6m on the excellency and stunts to add 8 dice. Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense, 2m on the Melee Excellency, and stunts to raise her parry to 10.<br /> <br /> Berit rolls 21 dice for 10 sux. Topaz pays 1m for Hail-Shattering Practice to make Berit miss. Topaz gains 1i from Dipping Swallow Defense, putting her at 6i.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 3:<br /> <br /> Berit (33/38m, 7wp, -0, Fire): 6i<br /> Shining Topaz (25/28m, 7wp, -0): 6i<br /> <br /> Berit and Topaz Clash!<br /> <br /> Berit makes a withering attack, spending 6m and stunting to add 8 dice, spends 3m,1wp on Crimson Fang Bite, and spends 1wp for an automatic sux. She rolls 21 dice for 7+1=8 sux.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 3m on Excellent Strike to reroll 1s and have an automatic sux, 1m on Divine Executioner Stance and 4m on the Melee Excellency and stunts to add 10 dice. She rolls 21 dice, rerolling 1s, for 16+1=17 sux.<br /> <br /> Topaz wins the clash with 11 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 14+5(str)+11(threshold)-14=16. Topaz rolls 16 dice for 12 sux, dealing 12+3=15i of damage to Berit. Putting Topaz at 21i and Berit at -11i. Berit has been crashed, Topaz gains an Initiative Break of 5i, putting her at 26i.<br /> <br /> (Topaz had 2 more dice of raw damage here than she should, but I caught this error way to late to fix it.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 4:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (22/28m, 7wp, -0): 26i<br /> Berit (29/38m, 7wp, -0, Fire): -11i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a decisive attack, spending 3m on Excellent Strike for an auto-sux and rerolling 1s, she also spends 1m on Divine Executioner Stance and stunts to add 6 dice to her roll. Berit spends 6m and stunts to raise her Parry to 8, and spends 4m on Ripples-on-Water Defense, ending her Aura.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 17 dice for 8+1=9 sux, hitting.<br /> <br /> 26+2(SIE)=28 dice of raw damage. Topaz rolls 28 dice, with up to three 1s rerolling sux, for 14sux and 0 1s, inflicting 14 Lethal Damage. Berit now suffers from a -2 wound penalty. Topaz Resets to 4i<br /> <br /> Topaz spends 1m, 1wp, 3a on Peony Blossom Attack! She makes a withering attack, spending 1m on Divine Executioner Stance and stunting to add 6 dice to the attack. Berit spends 4m on Ripples-on-Water Defense and spends 4m and stunts to raise her Parry to 4.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 18 dice for 10 sux, hitting with a threshold of 7.<br /> <br /> 12+5(str)+7-14=10. Topaz rolls 10 dice, with up to three 1s subtracting sux, for 7-1=6 damage. Topaz is at 10i, Berit is at -19i.<br /> <br /> Berit makes a withering attack. She spends 4m and stunts to add 6 dice. Topaz stunts to raise her parry to 8.<br /> <br /> Berit rolls 17 dice for 15(!) sux, hitting with a threshold of 8.<br /> <br /> 16+8-11=13. Berit rolls 13 dice for 5 sux. Berit inflicts 5i of damage, putting her at -14i and Topaz at 6i.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 5:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (21/28m, 6wp, -0): 6i<br /> Berit (11/38m, 7wp, -2): -14i<br /> <br /> Topaz makes a withering attack, stunting to add two dice. Berit spends 6m,1wp and stunts to raise her parry to 9.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 16 dice for 7 sux, missing.<br /> <br /> Berit makes a withering attack. She spends 1wp for an auto-sux and stunts to add 2 dice. Topaz pays 1m for Dipping Swallow Defense and stunts to raise her parry to 9.<br /> <br /> Berit rolls 13 dice for 7+1=8 sux, missing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 6:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (25/28m, 6wp, -0): 6i<br /> Berit (10/38m, 6wp, -2): -14i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a withering attack, she spends 3m on Excellent Strike for an auto-sux and rerolling 1s, and stunts and spends 1m on Divine Executioner stance to add six dice to her roll. Berit spends 6m,1wp and stunts to raise her parry to 9.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 20 dice for 12+1=13 sux, hitting with 5 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 12+5 (str)+5(threshold)-14=8. Topaz rolls 8 dice for 2 damage. This puts Topaz at 8i and Berit at -16i.<br /> <br /> Berit makes a withering attack. She spends 1wp to add an auto-sux and stunts to add 2 dice. Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense and stunts to raise her defense to 9.<br /> <br /> Berit rolls 13 dice for 9+1=10 sux. Topaz pays 2m for Hail Shattering Practice to make her miss. Topaz gains 1i from Dipping Swallow Defense, putting her at 7i.<br /> <br /> Berit has been crashed for 3 turns, she resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Round 7:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (24/28m, 6wp, -0): 7i<br /> Berit (9/38m, 5wp, -2): 3i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz takes the aim action, due to Shining Ice Mirror\u2019s attunement bonus this raises her Parry to 9.<br /> <br /> Berit makes a withering attack. She spends 1wp to add an auto-sux and stunts to add two dice. Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense and stunts to raise her parry to 11.<br /> <br /> Berit rolls 13 dice for 7+1=8 sux, missing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 8:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (28/28m, 6wp, -0): 7i<br /> Berit (14/38m, 4wp, -2): 3i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a withering attack. She spends 3m for Excellent Strike for an auto-sux and rerolling 1s, she stunts and pays 1m for Divine Executioner Stance to add 6 dice, and she aimed for 3 more dice. Berit spends 4m for Ripples-on-Water Defense, and spends 6m, 1wp and stunts to bring her Parry up to 9.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 23 dice, rerolling 1s, for 11+1=12 sux, hitting with 4 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 17+4(threshold)-14=7. Topaz rolls 8 dice, with up to three 1s subtracting sux, for 4-1=3 damage. This puts topaz at 11i and Berit at 0i. Berit is crashed, and it has been more than one round since she recovered from her last crash so Topaz gains an Initiative Break of 5, putting her at 16i.<br /> <br /> Berit makes a withering attack. She spends 1wp for an auto-sux and stunts for 2 extra dice. Topaz spends 1m for Dipping Swallow Defense and spends 4m on the melee excellency and stunts to raise her Parry to 11.<br /> <br /> Berit rolls 13 dice for 5+1=6 sux, missing. Topaz gains 1i, putting her at 17i.<br /> <br /> Berit enters Water Aura.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 8:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (24/28m, 6wp, -0): 16i<br /> Berit (9/38m, 3wp, -2, Water): 0i<br /> <br /> <br /> Shining Topaz launches a decisive attack! She spends 3m on Excellent Strike to add an auto-sux and reroll 1s, and spends 1m on Divine Executioner Stance and spends 4m on the melee excellency and stunts to add 10 dice to the roll. Berit spends 4m on Ripples-on-Water Defense, and spends 4m,1wp and stunts to raise her Parry to 7<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 24 dice, rerolling 1s, for 14 sux, hitting.<br /> <br /> 16+2(SIE)=18. Topaz rolls 18 dice, with up to 3 1s causing sux to be rerolled, for 9 sux and 2 1s. Both sux reroll into more sux (!). Topaz deals 9 lethal damage, Berit falls.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>There is a moment of silence as one of the greatest scions of the Realm falls, her neck cut open. Then a cheer goes up, the crowd loving the spectacle of the fight. Once Berit is dragged out of the ring, she sits up, hand at her neck as she looks confused, before she shrugs. </i><br /> <br /> \u201c<i>A worthy fight!\u201d She declares, and another cheer goes up.</i><br /> <br /> <i>A young looking man with a confident smirk on his face stands, clapping. A silver disk burning on his forehead. \u201cYou have defeated a Dragon-Blooded, sure.\u201d He stops clapping and throws his arms wide, \u201cBut how will you fare against a champion of the MOON!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>So saying, he steps into the ring.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Fight 2:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Topaz still has Sensory Acuity Prana up and she spends 5m to add five dice. She rolls 17 dice, doubling 9s, for 9 sux. She starts with 12i.<br /> <br /> The Lunar stunts and spends 7m, to add a total of 9 dice to his roll. He rolls 17 dice for 8 sux. He starts with 11i.<br /> <br /> (Note: Topaz\u2019s following Scenelongs are 