ls 20 dice for 8 sux, missing.<br /> <br /> The Lunar will perform a grapple gambit. He stunts and pays 10m to add 12 dice and spends 1wp for an auto-sux. Topaz stunts spends 1wp on Perfect Strike Discipline to raise her parry to 13.<br /> <br /> The Lunar rolls 20 dice for 14+1=15 sux, hitting.<br /> <br /> He rolls 8i against a difficulty of 2 for 3 sux, succeeding in his gambit. He loses 3i, putting him at 5i.<br /> <br /> Topaz stunts and spends 6m on the Single Point Excellency to add 8 dice to the control roll, she rolls 18 dice for 9 sux.<br /> The Lunar stunts and spends 7m to add 9 dice to the control roll, he rolls 19 dice for 12 sux.<br /> The Lunar wins the grapple with 4 rounds of control.<br /> <br /> The Lunar makes a savaging attack, stunting to add 2 dice. Topaz spends 4m on Heavenly Guardian Defense to make her parry of 7 applicable, she also stunts to raise it to 8.<br /> <br /> The Lunar rolls 14 dice for a total of 7 sux, missing. 4 rounds of control remain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 4:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (12/28m, 5wp, -0): 18i<br /> Barbarian Warlord Lunar (9/59m, 4wp, -0): 5i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a withering attack. She stunts to add 2 dice. The Lunar stunts to raise his parry to 3 and pays 5m for Impenetrable Beast Armor.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 15 dice for 12 sux, hitting with a threshold of 10 dice.<br /> <br /> 17+10-15=12. 12/2=6. Topaz rolls 6 dice for 5 damage. Putting her at 24i and the Lunar at 0i. Crashing him and breaking the clinch, also giving her an initiative break of +5i putting her at 29i.<br /> <br /> The Lunar punches her in the face again (withering attack). The lunar stunts to add 2 dice to his attack. Topaz stunts and spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense to raise her Parry to 9.<br /> <br /> The Lunar rolls 14 dice for 9 sux. Topaz spends 1m on Hail-Shattering Practice to make him miss. Topaz gains 1i from Dipping Swallow Defense for a successful parry, putting her at 30i.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 5:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (16/28m, 5wp, -0): 30i<br /> Barbarian Warlord Lunar (9/59m, 4wp, -0): 0i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a decisive attack. She stunts and pays 1m to add 6 dice. The Lunar stunts and pays 4m to raise his parry to 7 and pays 5m for Impenetrable Beast Armor.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 17 dice for 8 sux, hitting.<br /> <br /> 30+2-3=29. Topaz rolls 29 dice for 15 Lethal Damage. Incapacitating the Lunar and resetting Perfect Strike Discipline.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>As cheers once again ripple through the crowd, one of the dead stands. </i><br /> <br /> \u201c<i>You seem a worthy enough foe, I shall take you on!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Topaz grins, even as the lunar is dragged from the stage, \u201cI am the invicible sword princess.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>The deathknight shakes his head, \u201cNot yet. Maybe if you prove yourself against all comers here, but not yet.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Topaz frowns, \u201cThen enter the ring, and taste defeat.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Deathknight hefts his Direlance, and laughing, enters the ring.</i><br /> <br /> Fight 3<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (I realize that since the narrative of this is Topaz trying to earn the \u201cInvincible Sword Princess\u201d sobriquet, I should have been giving her the damage buff from DES, and will do so going forward.)<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz still has Sensory Acuity Prana up. She rolls 12 dice, doubling 9s, for 5 sux. She starts with 8i.<br /> <br /> The Wandering Deathknight pays 7m to add 7 dice. He rolls 16 dice for 11 sux. He starts with 14i.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1:<br /> <br /> Wandering Deathknight (49/56m, 6wp, -0): 14i<br /> Shining Topaz (15/28m, 5wp, -0): 8i<br /> <br /> The Wandering Deathknight makes a decisive attack. He spends 10m to add 10 dice to the roll, he also spends 2m, 2i on Artful Maiming Onslaught to inflict a crippling penalty if his attack succeeds, and he spends 2m on Savage Shade Style to give him double 10s on the damage roll. This puts him at 12i. Topaz stunts and spends 1wp on Perfect Strike Discipline to raise her Defense to 13.<br /> <br /> The Deathknight rolls 22 dice for 8 sux, missing. He loses 3i for missing while above 9i, putting him at 9i.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a withering attack. She stunts and pays 1m on Divine Executioner Stance to add 6 dice to the roll. The Deathknight stunts and pays 8m to raise his parry to 11.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 20 dice for 10 sux, missing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 2:<br /> <br /> Wandering Deathknight (32/56m, 6wp, -0): 9i<br /> Shining Topaz (19/28m, 4wp, -0): 8i<br /> <br /> The Wandering Deathknight makes a decisive attack. He stunts and spends 10m to add 12 dice to the roll and he spends 2m on Savage Shade Style to give him double 10s on the damage roll. Topaz stunts and pays 1m for Dipping Swallow Defense and 8m for the melee excellency to raise her parry to 13.<br /> <br /> The Deathknight rolls 24 dice for 17 sux, hitting.<br /> <br /> Deathknight rolls 9 dice, doubling tens, for 7 damage. (I misread HGD and thought it could be paid for after the attack hits, but it can\u2019t, so Topaz goes down here because I don\u2019t know how to play the game.)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>The crowd, ever fickle, cheers their new champion.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 04-06-2020, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T17:58:10-07:00","id":1379113,"title":"","content":"Thoughts. Ripples on Water Defense is really good. Heavenly Guardian Defense makes grapples less scary than I thought they'd be. Impenetrable Beast Armor was nerfed into the ground in Fangs at the Gate.<br /> <br /> I probably could have beaten the deathknight if I hadn't punted on the timing for various charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:59:09-07:00","id":1379131,"title":"","content":"Considering it only took 5 motes to beat Berit and another eight to beat the Lunar warlord, I would fully expect you to get through the Deathknight, Lilith and Octavian under normal circumstances.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You could maybe keep running it and just assume you used HGD on that last attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-06-2020, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T00:29:16-07:00","id":1379188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379113#post1379113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ripples on Water Defense is really good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure what you're basing this on. On the first activation, it did nothing (because her opponent didn't roll any 1s). On the second, it reduced withering damage by a grand total of 1. Were she not statted up as a quick character, she could've used the prerequisite, Impervious Skin of Stone, for the same cost and could've expected to retain more initiative on average. On the third, it did nothing once more, because the rerolled dice also turned up as successes.<br /> <br /> So, over the course of the fight, she spent 8m to not do anything, then another 4 to get outclassed by an Essence 1, Ability 2 Charm that sits literally at the root of its tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T11:43:48-07:00","id":1379288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379188#post1379188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you're basing this on. On the first activation, it did nothing (because her opponent didn't roll any 1s). On the second, it reduced withering damage by a grand total of 1. Were she not statted up as a quick character, she could've used the prerequisite, Impervious Skin of Stone, for the same cost and could've expected to retain more initiative on average. On the third, it did nothing once more, because the rerolled dice also turned up as successes.<br /> <br /> So, over the course of the fight, she spent 8m to not do anything, then another 4 to get outclassed by an Essence 1, Ability 2 Charm that sits literally at the root of its tree.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I don't have much experience with the DB charms your talking about. Ripples on Water Defense felt like it greatly drew out how long it took to take down Berit's Init.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T12:26:50-07:00","id":1379297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379288#post1379288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't have much experience with the DB charms your talking about. Ripples on Water Defense felt like it greatly drew out how long it took to take down Berit's Init.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in this case the only thing it did was stop 2i worth of damage the whole fight, that's not very good for 12m, even for Dragonblooded. Also technically you couldn't even use it when you did because it requires Water Aura, which Berit wasn't in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T13:15:56-07:00","id":1379310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379297#post1379297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, in this case the only thing it did was stop 2i worth of damage the whole fight, that's not very good for 12m, even for Dragonblooded. Also technically you couldn't even use it when you did because it requires Water Aura, which Berit wasn't in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess I messed it up then. Oops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T13:23:07-07:00","id":1379312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379310#post1379310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess I messed it up then. Oops.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I'm pretty sure I messed up when I gave you the advice that HGD can't be used after being hit. It uses very similar wording to other charms which DO explicitly allow you to activate them after being hit, and it's probably just a mistake on the writer's part not to include the exception to the rule in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T18:35:33-07:00","id":1379367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379312#post1379312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries, I'm pretty sure I messed up when I gave you the advice that HGD can't be used after being hit. It uses very similar wording to other charms which DO explicitly allow you to activate them after being hit, and it's probably just a mistake on the writer's part not to include the exception to the rule in it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, I believed you. Not least because neither of the other two perfects (Seven Shadows Evasion and Adamant Skin Technique) let you activate them in post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T23:27:37-07:00","id":1379654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379312#post1379312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries, I'm pretty sure I messed up when I gave you the advice that HGD can't be used after being hit. It uses very similar wording to other charms which DO explicitly allow you to activate them after being hit, and it's probably just a mistake on the writer's part not to include the exception to the rule in it.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1379572#post1379572\">Word of Vance</a> confirms you don't declare HGD (in mode 1) when declaring defensive Charms, but declare post roll instead.<br /> <br /> (I REALLY didn't think it worked that way, but that was the community interpretation in the old Ask the Devs thread as well, so I accept that I'm wrong here. Charms do what they say they do. Specific trumps general.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T07:13:49-07:00","id":1379755,"title":"","content":"So I'm doing the Lilith fight. And have come up against a difficulty in regards to beating her. Lilith can fly.<br /> <br /> This makes her basically impossible to hit, since I didn't give Topaz Blazing Solar Bolt. Lilith can just retreat to Medium range and rain down arrows.<br /> <br /> I asked around and you can't double jump with just the charms Topaz has available, not without something to jump off of. The only way I can think of for Topaz to get to Lilith is this dumb, super anime bullshit where she tosses the utility/backup knife I gave her into the air to provide a platform for the second jump.<br /> <br /> Which I would totally allow if I was ST and a player tried it, but feels like cheese when I'm running every character involved.<br /> <br /> Edit: And Vance has declared that even that is no good. I guess I'll just call it for Lilith and post the fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 04-09-2020, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T08:42:12-07:00","id":1379768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379755#post1379755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm doing the Lilith fight. And have come up against a difficulty in regards to beating her. Lilith can fly.<br /> <br /> This makes her basically impossible to hit, since I didn't give Topaz Blazing Solar Bolt. Lilith can just retreat to Medium range and rain down arrows.<br /> <br /> I asked around and you can't double jump with just the charms Topaz has available, not without something to jump off of. The only way I can think of for Topaz to get to Lilith is this dumb, super anime bullshit where she tosses the utility/backup knife I gave her into the air to provide a platform for the second jump.<br /> <br /> Which I would totally allow if I was ST and a player tried it, but feels like cheese when I'm running every character involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't win mechanically then you'll need to create a narrative opportunity, possibly by using a Gambit. For instance, you could retreat towards an area with strong weather to force Lilith to lose altitude, or lure her towards other threats she wouldn't want to face at the same time as Topaz, creating a virtual wall to back her against.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T09:05:00-07:00","id":1379776,"title":"","content":"<i>It is the site of a great victory feast! Deep in the Southlands the Fae massed an army not seen since the Balorian Crusade! Yet heroes rose to meet them. Lunars, Solars, Dragonblooded Scions of the Realm and beyond, Gods and demons and the dead, and of course mortal men in their tens of thousands. On the site of their victory, where the Raksha leading the crusade was vanquished, the armies of Creation throw a great feast. And as they drink, and eat, and revel, the great heroes of the day give their speeches.<br /> <br /> Soon it is the turn of Shining Topaz, the Forsaken of Terek, vanquisher of Wild Hunts, master of the blade. Instead of a speech celebrating their deeds, the impetuous young woman lays down a challenge. She declares herself the Invincible Sword Princess, and throws down the gauntlet: She thinks that she can beat anyone here in a 1 on 1 fight and she will take all comers who want to prove her wrong.<br /> <br /> The other exalts at the feast rise to her challenge, and shortly an arena is marked out for the combats and sanctified by the southern god of martial arts that although injuries will seem real, none shall die of injuries sustained in the ring. Shining Topaz shall start in the ring, taking all comers, and no sooner has a loser been dragged away than a new contender will step up. The first of her opponents is the great hero: Berit.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> \u201c<i>Truly,\u201d Berit exclaims as she enters the ring, \u201cthe arrogance of the Solar Anathema know no bounds. I will gladly put you in your place, little girl.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Fight 1:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/8217\" target=\"_blank\">Shining Topaz</a> spends 5m on Sensory Aucity Prana (committing them) and 10m on the Awareness Excellency. She rolls 22 dice with double 9s, for 7 sux. She starts with 10i.<br /> <br /> Berit spends 4 dice on Join Battle excellency. She rolls 13 dice for 5 sux. She starts with 8i.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (23/33m, 8wp, -0): 10i<br /> Berit (38/38m, 8wp, -0): 8i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz commits 5m and spends 1wp to activate Fivefold Bulwark Stance.<br /> <br /> Berit makes a Decisive Attack. She spends 6m on the excellency to add four dice and 3m, 1wp on Crimson Fang Bite, she also stunts to add 2 dice. Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense, stunts, and spends 4m on the melee excellency to bring her parry up to 11.<br /> <br /> Berit rolls 21 dice for 10 sux against Parry 11, missing. She loses 2i for missing a decisive putting her at 6i. Topaz gains 1i for blocking with Dipping Swallow Defense, putting her at 11i. Berit enters fire aura<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 2:<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz (23/28m, 7wp, -0): 11i<br /> Berit (34/38m, 7wp, -0, Fire): 6i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 6i on Strength Increasing Excerise to raise her strength to 5 for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> Berit makes a withering attack, she spends 6m on the excellency and stunts to add 8 dice. Topaz spends 1m on Dipping Swallow Defense, 2m on the Melee Excellency, and stunts to raise her parry to 10.<br /> <br /> Berit rolls 21 dice for 10 sux. Topaz pays 1m for Hail-Shattering Practice to make Berit miss. Topaz gains 1i from Dipping Swallow Defense, putting her at 6i.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 3:<br /> <br /> Berit (33/38m, 7wp, -0, Fire): 6i<br /> Shining Topaz (25/28m, 7wp, -0): 6i<br /> <br /> Berit and Topaz Clash!<br /> <br /> Berit makes a withering attack, spending 6m and stunting to add 8 dice, spends 3m,1wp on Crimson Fang Bite, and spends 1wp for an automatic sux. She rolls 21 dice for 7+1=8 sux.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz spends 3m on Excellent Strike to reroll 1s and have an automatic sux, 1m on Divine Executioner Stance and 4m on the Melee Excellency and stunts to add 10 dice. She rolls 21 dice, rerolling 1s, for 16+1=17 sux.<br /> <br /> Topaz wins the clash with 11 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 14+5(str)+11(threshold)-14=16. Topaz rolls 16 dice for 12 sux, dealing 12+3=15i of damage to Berit. Putting Topaz at 21i and Berit at -11i. Berit has been crashed, Topaz gain