, hitting with 3+ threshold sux.<br /> 1+2(SIE)+3(FSS)+4(DES)=10. Topaz rolls 10 dice for 2 lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Attack 5: Topaz rolls 20 dice vs Parry 2 for 7(!) sux, hitting with 3+ threshold sux.<br /> 34+2(SIE)+3(FSS)+4(DES)=43. Topaz rolls 43 dice for 15 lethal damage. Octavian is incapacitated, resetting Perfect Strike Discipline.<br /> <br /> (The dice in this fight were insane. The variance was super fucking high. Also, if Octavian had lived I would totally have Peony Blossom Attack\u2019d him to try and finish him off.)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>As Octavian\u2019s dismembered torso hits the floor of the arena, and the limbs and head hit the floor elsewhere, there is dead silence from the onlookers. No cheers, no applause, just the sound of Shining Topaz catching her breath. </i><br /> <br /> <i>The instant stretches, and for a moment it seems like none will rise to challenge her again. Then the woman with feathers in her hair stands, and claps softly.</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cImpressive.\u201d She says as she walks towards the ring. \u201cOf all the swordsmen the Solar Host has produced, you are surely the most talented. Not the best, not yet, but you are still young, still far from the fullness of your potential.\u201d </i><br /> <br /> <i>She pauses at the edge of the ring, summons her Powerbow and Direlance, and dons her helm. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Lilith enters the ring.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Fight 5:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Shining Topaz stunts to add 2 dice to her roll. She rolls 14 dice for 8 sux, she starts at 11i.<br /> <br /> Lilith stunts and spends 10m to add 12 dice to her roll. She rolls 23 dice for 10 sux. She starts at 13i.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1:<br /> Lilith (39/49m, 8wp, -0,): 13i<br /> Shining Topaz (1/33m, 3wp, -0): 11i<br /> <br /> Lilith spends 4m on Hybrid Body Body Transformation. This lets her reflexively activate Deadly Beastman Transformation for 1m,1wp. This lets her reflexively activate White Reaper Form for 8m.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz takes aim at Lilith. Shining Ice Mirror\u2019s attunement bonus raises her parry to 9.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 2:<br /> Lilith (31/36m, 7wp, -0,): 13i<br /> Shining Topaz (6/33m, 3wp, -0): 11i<br /> <br /> Lilith makes a decisive attack with her Direlance. She stunts and pays 10m to add 12 dice to her roll, she pays 5m for Bleeding Crescent Strike to double up to five 9s on her attack roll, she pays 5m for Falling Sycthe Flash to add five dice of raw damage, she pays 3m,1wp for Greatest Killer Attitude to convert five dice of raw damage to sux, she pays 3m,1wp for Limb Maiming Flourish, and pays 1wp to add an auto-sux to the roll. Topaz stunts and pays 1wp for Perfect Strike Discipline to raise her parry to 15.<br /> <br /> Lilith rolls 24 dice, doubling the first five 9s, for 12+1=13 sux, missing. She loses 3i for missing a decisive attack with 10i or more, putting her at 10i.<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a withering attack. She stunts and spends 1m on Divine Executioner Stance to add 6 dice to the roll. Lilith stunts to raise her parry to 6.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 23 dice for 9 sux and three 1s, hitting with 4 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 17+4(DES)+3-20=4. Topaz rolls 5 Overwhelming Dice for 7(!) damage. Putting her at 19i and Lilith at 3i. (Here\u2019s the roll: 10,10,7,4,10. The variance hasn\u2019t stopped apparently.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 3:<br /> Shining Topaz (10/33m, 2wp, -0): 19i<br /> Lilith (10/36m, 4wp, -0,): 3i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz makes a withering attack. She stunts and pays 1m for Divine Executioner Stance to add 6 dice to her roll. Lilith stunts to raise her parry to 5.<br /> <br /> Topaz rolls 20 dice for 10 sux, hitting with 6 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 17+4(DES)+6-20=7. Topaz rolls 7 dice for 6(!) damage. Putting her at 26i and Lilith at -3i. Lilith is crashed, Topaz gains an initiative break of 5i, putting her at 31i. (The Roll: 4,6,4,10,10,7,9. What is up with the dice this fight.)<br /> <br /> Lilith attempts to disengage. She rolls her move pool vs Topaz\u2019s Dex+Athletics. Topaz spends 4m and stunts to add 6 dice to her roll, Topaz stunts to add two dice to her roll.<br /> <br /> Lilith rolls 22 dice for 8 sux.<br /> Topaz rolls 7 dice for 2 sux.<br /> <br /> Lilith is now at short range above Topaz. She loses 2i, putting her at -5i<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 4:<br /> Shining Topaz (14/33m, 2wp, -0): 31i<br /> Lilith (11/36m, 4wp, -0,): -5i<br /> <br /> Topaz makes a social action. \u201cGet down here, that\u2019s against the spirit of the challenge and you know it.\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolls 3 dice for 2 sux against Lilith\u2019s resolve 5, and Lilith responds with \u201cThe greatest Solar Swordsmen could hit me from here, from further away even!\u201d<br /> <br /> Lilith moves to medium range above Topaz and takes a ready weapon action, switching to her Powerbow.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 5:<br /> Shining Topaz (19/33m, 2wp, -0): 31i<br /> Lilith (16/36m, 4wp, -0,): -5i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz takes aim at Lilith. Shining Ice Mirror\u2019s attunement bonus raises her parry to 9.<br /> <br /> Lilith takes aim at Shining Topaz.<br /> <br /> Round 6:<br /> Shining Topaz (24/33m, 2wp, -0): 31i<br /> Lilith (21/36m, 4wp, -0,): -5i<br /> <br /> Shining Topaz takes aim at Lilith. Shining Ice Mirror\u2019s attunement bonus raises her parry to 9.<br /> <br /> Lilith fires a medium range withering attack. She stunts and pays 9m to add 11 dice to her roll. Topaz stunts and pays 1m to raise her parry to 9.<br /> <br /> Lilith rolls 22 dice for 14 sux, hitting with 5 threshold sux.<br /> <br /> 17+5-11=11. Lilith rolls 11 dice for 5 damage. Putting her at 1i and Topaz at 26i.<br /> <br /> Round 7:<br /> Shining Topaz (28/33m, 2wp, -0): 26i<br /> Lilith (17/36m, 4wp, -0,): 1i<br /> <br /> (At this point I\u2019m calling it for Lilith. Topaz could have won probably if she had Thunderbolt Attack Prana\u2019d instead of attempting social with 3 friggen dice. She still would have needed to hit, but with aim assist, and against base parry 5, I feel good about her chances. Also, varience was real. You aren't supposed to be able to do that kind of withering damage to someone with 20 soak)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 04-09-2020, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T09:52:17-07:00","id":1379785,"title":"","content":"Wow, getting past Octavian completely unscathed is very impressive, if Lilith couldn't fly I'd give you serious odds of beating Alhat. <br /> <br /> Also sadly, the combo of monkey leap +TAP doesn't technically work RAW anyway, they both count as your movement so you can use one or the other. For the Lilith fight you'd probably just have to say it's unsporting to fly and use the bow so she has to stay on the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:15:42-07:00","id":1379794,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11917_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11917\" data-vbnamecard=\"11917\">Aranfan</a> Got a link to Topaz's Essence 2 character sheet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:28:07-07:00","id":1379798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379785#post1379785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, getting past Octavian completely unscathed is very impressive, if Lilith couldn't fly I'd give you serious odds of beating Alhat.<br /> <br /> Also sadly, the combo of monkey leap +TAP doesn't technically work RAW anyway, they both count as your movement so you can use one or the other. For the Lilith fight you'd probably just have to say it's unsporting to fly and use the bow so she has to stay on the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. And Iron Whirlwind Attack/Invincible Fury of the Dawn works the same way I'm assuming. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for Octavian, yeah. I felt like Topaz's back was to the ropes the entire fight. The Black Oil is fucking nasty, it doesn't even need to do damage to apply the poison. And because it definitely sounds like it &quot;effects the senses&quot; it penalizes parry through Fivefold Bulwark Stance, which is a massive debuff. Incidentally, I was cutting it really close with the final decisive there. If the variance had gone the other way, and I had rolled poorly instead of well on the decisive damage then Octavian could easily have survived and done an Initiative Shift and wrecked me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379794#post1379794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11917_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11917\" data-vbnamecard=\"11917\">Aranfan</a> Got a link to Topaz's Essence 2 character sheet?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fixed. It's in Fight 1 now, but here it is directly. <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/8217\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/8217</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:45:50-07:00","id":1379806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379798#post1379798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. And Iron Whirlwind Attack/Invincible Fury of the Dawn works the same way I'm assuming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah you can\u2019t TAP with IfotD more than once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379798#post1379798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for Octavian, yeah. I felt like Topaz's back was to the ropes the entire fight. The Black Oil is fucking nasty, it doesn't even need to do damage to apply the poison. And because it definitely sounds like it &amp;quot;effects the senses&amp;quot; it penalizes parry through Fivefold Bulwark Stance, which is a massive debuff. Incidentally, I was cutting it really close with the final decisive there. If the variance had gone the other way, and I had rolled poorly instead of well on the decisive damage then Octavian could easily have survived and done an Initiative Shift and wrecked me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Black oil is a pretty nasty effect and definitely would get through bulwark stance, but I think you would have been fine if Octavian didn\u2019t die, with 10 motes left to raise defence and doHail Shattering combined with Octavians -2 or -4 wound penalty you\u2019d be sitting pretty to not get shifted on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:16:27-07:00","id":1379815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379806#post1379806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Black oil is a pretty nasty effect and definitely would get through bulwark stance, but I think you would have been fine if Octavian didn\u2019t die, with 10 motes left to raise defence and doHail Shattering combined with Octavians -2 or -4 wound penalty you\u2019d be sitting pretty to not get shifted on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, I had 1 mote left in the tank at the end of the Octavian fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:58:11-07:00","id":1379823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379815#post1379815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, I had 1 mote left in the tank at the end of the Octavian fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right, completely blanked on the math there, although surviving a 43 damage attack when you have 12 health levels left is also really hard to do. It also occurs to me that when you get to Alhat you're going to have a difficult choice to make due to Whispering Warrior Souls. It's a 1wp reflexive charm that he can activate once per fight to give himself a 5i bonus, but it can also be used to give himself the entire evocation tree for an artifact, or giving him an entire martial art specifically to counter powerful foes.<br /> <br /> <i>In theory </i>if he's been watching Topaz for all of these fights he could pick a martial art or weapon evocation tree that helps him against her specifically and use that alongside his own native charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T12:22:54-07:00","id":1379828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379823#post1379823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh right, completely blanked on the math there, although surviving a 43 damage attack when you have 12 health levels left is also really hard to do. It also occurs to me that when you get to Alhat you're going to have a difficult choice to make due to Whispering Warrior Souls. It's a 1wp reflexive charm that he can activate once per fight to give himself a 5i bonus, but it can also be used to give himself the entire evocation tree for an artifact, or giving him an entire martial art specifically to counter powerful foes.<br /> <br /> <i>In theory </i>if he's been watching Topaz for all of these fights he could pick a martial art or weapon evocation tree that helps him against her specifically and use that alongside his own native charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure but... what evocation tree or martial art would even work for that? Melee is just really strong and has tools for basically anything. DES is probably the strongest dice adder in the entire friggen game, and fivefold bulwark stance + Hail Shattering Practice + HGD is probably second only to the dodge tree as far as defensive suites go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T12:54:26-07:00","id":1379835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379828#post1379828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure but... what evocation tree or martial art would even work for that? Melee is just really strong and has tools for basically anything. DES is probably the strongest dice adder in the entire friggen game, and fivefold bulwark stance + Hail Shattering Practice + HGD is probably second only to the dodge tree as far as defensive suites go.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's just some that are really good in general. Like Spring Razor, to add deadly poison to every decisive attack or maybe Single Point to gain two initiative tracks to attack with.<br /> <br /> <br /> DES is probably too strong to be in the game as it is, especially since you can give yourself an omni-applicable defining intimacy that works with it. Solars are supposed to be powerful, but Octavian is the most powerful second circle demon in Hell, and Lilith is a First Age Lunar warrior, they should probably be putting up more resistance to a young Solar. The mechanics should reflect the setting, not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:08:25-07:00","id":1379874,"title":"","content":"Divine Executioner Stance is probably too strong to allow in games, yeah. Most of the Miracles Charms are pretty busted, but that one especially. IIRC it's the most efficient dice adder in the game?<br /> <br /> Edit: DB Melee excellency is better if your on a streak, but DES is much more reliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 04-09-2020, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:04:31-07:00","id":1379888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379874#post1379874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Divine Executioner Stance is probably too strong to allow in games, yeah. Most of the Miracles Charms are pretty busted, but that one especially. IIRC it's the most efficient dice adder in the game?<br /> <br /> Edit: DB Melee excellency is better if your on a streak, but DES is much more reliable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, much more reliable there is an understatement. The DB excellency is only as efficient if you have an unbroken streak of attacks against a single opponent for 14 straight attacks, never once failing, and never have to parry against anyone else and it doesn't even add to the damage either. Compare DES to Hungry Tiger Technique, which costs 3m 2i, can't be used in crash, doesn't add to accuracy, can only be used against crashed opponents, and only adds overflow attack successes to the damage.<br /> <br /> The problem is you can swear to a principle of &quot;I will never be defeated in combat&quot; in which case anyone attacking you is obviously threatening that intimacy, so you get the accuracy bonus all the time. Then on top of that anyone fighting you is obviously acting against your intimacy that you will never be defeated in combat, so take their highest opposed intimacy and add it to damage.<br /> <br /> In the example for DES the Solar swears an oath to protect the Urchins of Nighthammer district in Nexus, so the effect doesn't really apply outside of that, or outside of anyone actually trying to hurt them or destroy Nexus or whatever. Furthermore, they actually need an intimacy against children, or the homeless of Nexus or something to get the damage. Assuming that you can't do something like twist &quot;I will rule the Realm&quot; into applying by saying that technically the Realm isn't good for Nexus, so it isn't good for the Urchins, and rulership of a place that isn't good for the place that the urchins live means that this person triggers my Divine Executioner Stance.<br /> <br /> That's all not even counting that against Creatures of Darkness it gets an additional free success to hit, and damage, and the damage is aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:13:33-07:00","id":1379894,"title":"","content":"I may have misapplied DES during the tourney then. Oops. I think Octavian was kosher, but the uses against the Deathknight and Lilith probably fucked it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:16:45-07:00","id":1379896,"title":"","content":"Lilith isn't a Creature of Darkness is she?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:07:57-07:00","id":1379912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379896#post1379896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith isn't a Creature of Darkness is she?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, but neither does she have an intimacy that is opposed to Topaz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:07:57-07:00","id":1379913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379896#post1379896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith isn't a Creature of Darkness is she?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, but neither does she have an intimacy that is opposed to Topaz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:07:57-07:00","id":1379914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379896#post1379896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith isn't a Creature of Darkness is she?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, but neither does she have an intimacy that is opposed to Topaz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:17:49-07:00","id":1379920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379835#post1379835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DES is probably too strong to be in the game as it is, especially since you can give yourself an omni-applicable defining intimacy that works with it. Solars are supposed to be powerful, but Octavian is the most powerful second circle demon in Hell, and Lilith is a First Age Lunar warrior, they should probably be putting up more resistance to a young Solar. The mechanics should reflect the setting, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like everything else in the game, DES is predicated around not having players looking to break the game system over their knee. You can break the system, but if you do that you're going to be way more powerful than anything else in the game world that hasn't been cheesed up especially for you.<br /> <br /> Octavian isn't getting dropped by Volfer any time soon. Lilith can take down Isthus. The mechanics do reflect the game world. There's nothing wrong with taking DES to protect the Urchins of Nighthammer district.<br /> <br /> But Solars need to be ambiguous enough in power that they <i>could be</i> Topaz, or the setting falls apart. I see nothing wrong with building a Topaz and kicking-ass... but this is not the normal Solar baseline. And it's ridiculous to treat one heavily cheesed PC as representative of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:33:32-07:00","id":1379928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379920#post1379920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like everything else in the game, DES is predicated around not having players looking to break the game system over their knee. You can break the system, but if you do that you're going to be way more powerful than anything else in the game world that hasn't been cheesed up especially for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but used that way it's a bit out of scale with the other Solar charms too. It's just so much better than anything else in the set if you twink out the defining principle the right way. On the other hand I'm having trouble thinking of a concise way to word intimacy guidelines except &quot;This intimacy should be something specific enough that it doesn't come up in every possible combat.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379920#post1379920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Solars need to be ambiguous enough in power that they <i>could be</i> Topaz, or the setting falls apart. I see nothing wrong with building a Topaz and kicking-ass... but this is not the normal Solar baseline. And it's ridiculous to treat one heavily cheesed PC as representative of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, if every Solar is Shining Topaz every DB is Imminent Thunder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:42:48-07:00","id":1379933,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Topaz isn't &quot;a Solar&quot;. She is a woman who has been obsessed with swords since before she could walk. Who dedicating her life to swording to the limits of human ability, and who the Sun then Exalted so she could sword <i>even better</i>. Her performance specialty is swords, her <i>lore background</i> is swords. She has bent her entire life, and all the supernal prowess the sun has given her, to the sole purpose of swording as best she can. Her non sword related skills are requirements of her station, and every single charm she has is dedicated to either swording better, or letting her sword things she otherwise couldn't.<br /> <br /> She is an absurd outlier.<br /> <br /> Edit: She isn't even the character I most want to play. The character I most want to play is a Stealth Supernal Night who has like, Blinding Battle Feint and Call the Blade for combat charms at the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 04-09-2020, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:00:03-07:00","id":1379943,"title":"","content":"I may also just be worried about a return to 2e which ended up feeling a lot less Ninja Scroll and a lot more &quot;What if Silver Age Superman were put into Christopher Nolan's Batman universe?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:07:02-07:00","id":1379947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379943#post1379943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may also just be worried about a return to 2e which ended up feeling a lot less Ninja Scroll and a lot more &quot;What if Silver Age Superman were put into Christopher Nolan's Batman universe?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh no, that's valid. Topaz was precisely an attempt to port the 2e Invincible Sword Princess over to 3e. <br /> <br /> Even then, if I were to actually try to play her in a game, I'd pitch the Athletics charms, and the Awareness charm, for Fervent Blow/Blazing Solar Bolt line/Sword MA Charms. I wouldn't actually bring the Topaz that can solo a wyld hunt to a table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:34:24-07:00","id":1379964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379920#post1379920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like everything else in the game, DES is predicated around not having players looking to break the game system over their knee. You can break the system, but if you do that you're going to be way more powerful than anything else in the game world that hasn't been cheesed up especially for you.<br /> <br /> Octavian isn't getting dropped by Volfer any time soon. Lilith can take down Isthus. The mechanics do reflect the game world. There's nothing wrong with taking DES to protect the Urchins of Nighthammer district.<br /> <br /> But Solars need to be ambiguous enough in power that they <i>could be</i> Topaz, or the setting falls apart. I see nothing wrong with building a Topaz and kicking-ass... but this is not the normal Solar baseline. And it's ridiculous to treat one heavily cheesed PC as representative of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like there's a scale from &quot;Have to work hard to make your character overpowered to break the system&quot; from &quot;Have to work hard to not make your character overpowered to not break the system&quot; and DES is a lot further to the second end of the scale than most other charms in Exalted. It seems really easy to realize your intimacy is relevant to a fight and totally wreck something that was supposed to be a tougher battle. I I haven't played with it though (don't have Miracles) so I could be totally off base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 04-09-2020, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T00:42:28-07:00","id":1380045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1379964#post1379964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like there's a scale from &quot;Have to work hard to make your character overpowered to break the system&quot; from &quot;Have to work hard to not make your character overpowered to not break the system&quot; and DES is a lot further to the second end of the scale than most other charms in Exalted. It seems really easy to realize your intimacy is relevant to a fight and totally wreck something that was supposed to be a tougher battle. I I haven't played with it though (don't have Miracles) so I could be totally off base.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can pretty easily start play with seven abilities at 5. Being a peerless master of seven different abilities, with Excellency is far more OP than DES.<br /> <br /> You really don't have to work hard to make your Exalt OP, even without Miracles.<br /> <br /> Let me be clear: some Charms are better than others, and if you can apply DES to 50% or more of your combats then it is ridiculously powerful. I don't dispute that from a mechanical optimisation POV, DES is way above the Solar baseline level of power. But for actual play, I'd veto &quot;No-one will beat me in combat&quot; for DES just like I'd veto &quot;every weapon that wasn't made by Hitori Hanzo&quot; as a Melee Specialty, or &quot;my aging Twilight scholar has Melee 5 just because&quot;. Sure, it's technically allowed but it's clearly not the intent.<br /> <br /> It rolls back to Session 0 expectations. If a player wants to be Saitama, rolling over all opposition except ennui, then Exalted supports that -- DES or no. (And it should support that, and I'm glad it supports that, and removing DES doesn't change that -- you pretty much have to nerf every Charm in the game to &quot;fix&quot; that.) If a player wants to build a &quot;realistic&quot; superhuman champion of the gods who is actually challenged by ancient monsters and brutal devils, then Exalted supports that too, and you don't need to ban DES to get this, you just have to follow the guidance the game gives you instead of cheesing it into every attack roll you make.<br /> <br /> That said, I think the easiest &quot;fix&quot; is to throw &quot;apocryphal&quot; on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-10-2020, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T06:47:29-07:00","id":1380104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380045#post1380045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for actual play, I'd veto &quot;No-one will beat me in combat&quot; for DES just like I'd veto &quot;every weapon that wasn't made by Hitori Hanzo&quot; as a Melee Specialty, or &quot;my aging Twilight scholar has Melee 5 just because&quot;. Sure, it's technically allowed but it's clearly not the intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, would you veto it on Topaz's &quot;I will be the Invincible Sword Princess!&quot; intimacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:28:13-07:00","id":1380108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380045#post1380045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can pretty easily start play with seven abilities at 5. Being a peerless master of seven different abilities, with Excellency is far more OP than DES.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it, game-mechanically? I agree 5 makes you a peerless master in the lore but it's only 2 extra dice (or 4 for 2 extra motes) compared to a reasonable Ability score for &quot;I'm good at this, for a hero, and great at this, for an ordinary person&quot; of 3.<br /> <br /> For a lot of noncombat checks, 3 Attribute + 3 Ability + full Excellency is plenty, and mote efficiency isn't an issue. On the other hand, in tough combats, every mote and die counts, and you make a larger number of rolls per session. <br /> <br /> Also if you don't have a Session 0 where players agree not to take a bunch of 5s, then probably everyone has a significant number of 5s, or at least 4s, and within-player balance is restored (though the ST may need to up the difficulty of rolls a bit.) I think DES may be more likely to help you overshadow another player. Say, in a crucial fight for the story where multiple characters have a defining intimacy that is obviously relevant, wouldn't you be playing as intended to go all Divine Executioner Stance while the chips are down? But then the other character doesn't have it, or any charms of similar power level, and they are made less relevant.<br /> <br /> OK I'm exaggerating a bit (you would probably have to already have a more-efficiently-built character to see a big effect (though with Melee that's pretty easy to accidentally achieve)) but it seems like an easy thing to fix by just banning the charm outright or houseruling the mote cost a bit higher.<br /> <br /> I would also support XP-based character generation as a not-completely-easy fix to make it still very possible to be a badass with multiple 5s at character creation but not possible to have an absurd amount of 5s and not pushed so hard in that direction by the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You really don't have to work hard to make your Exalt OP, even without Miracles.<br /> <br /> Let me be clear: some Charms are better than others, and if you can apply DES to 50% or more of your combats then it is ridiculously powerful. I don't dispute that from a mechanical optimisation POV, DES is way above the Solar baseline level of power. But for actual play, I'd veto &quot;No-one will beat me in combat&quot; for DES just like I'd veto &quot;every weapon that wasn't made by Hitori Hanzo&quot; as a Melee Specialty, or &quot;my aging Twilight scholar has Melee 5 just because&quot;. Sure, it's technically allowed but it's clearly not the intent. </div> </div> </div>If your game has a main story arc (say, fighting the forces of a particular Deathlord) would you allow a Major or Defining Intimacy that applies to every fight / most fights in that story arc? <br /> <br /> (I also think having a Melee specialty in &quot;my weapon&quot;, while I think 100% intended by the game, is a bit weird - won't it apply to basically all rolls? - but I'm not going to try to get rid of it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It rolls back to Session 0 expectations. If a player wants to be Saitama, rolling over all opposition except ennui, then Exalted supports that -- DES or no. (And it should support that, and I'm glad it supports that, and removing DES doesn't change that -- you pretty much have to nerf every Charm in the game to &quot;fix&quot; that.) If a player wants to build a &quot;realistic&quot; superhuman champion of the gods who is actually challenged by ancient monsters and brutal devils, then Exalted supports that too, and you don't need to ban DES to get this, you just have to follow the guidance the game gives you instead of cheesing it into every attack roll you make. </div> </div> </div>I think having discussions like this on the forums are a part of making it easier for people to build a more grounded character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I think the easiest &quot;fix&quot; is to throw &quot;apocryphal&quot; on it. </div> </div> </div>Wait what do you mean by &quot;apocryphal&quot;? That the Charm may or may not actually exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:51:58-07:00","id":1380114,"title":"","content":"Apocryphal was a Keyword introduced in the <i>Miracles of the Solar Exalted</i> supplement, it indicates that the Charm does not canonically exist in Creation, but might be suitable for <i>your</i> game, if that's the kind of game you want to be playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T10:06:09-07:00","id":1380153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380104#post1380104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, would you veto it on Topaz's &amp;quot;I will be the Invincible Sword Princess!&amp;quot; intimacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of this conversation? Yes.<br /> <br /> In an actual game? Topaz's player clearly wants to be The Best(tm) at combat. So long as they understand that they won't ever be challenged in combat, and I will only rarely be asking them to roll dice in combat, I'm actually fine with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:02:50-07:00","id":1380158,"title":"","content":"Okay, this next post is for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25834\" data-vbnamecard=\"25834\">habitableexoplanet</a>.<br /> <br /> It is not my intent to insult or belittle you or your opinions. We have <i>different </i>opinions, and I'm going to explain why. I'm aware that the tone here could be read as a little harsh: this is not my intent, but I'm not eloquent enough to phrase my argument in a manner which isn't blunt. I really enjoyed reading your post, and you make a good case. I ask that you read what follows in the friendliest, most charitable way that you can imagine.<br /> <br /> But long story short: I disagree with everything you just said. Here's why:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it, game-mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It's huge.<br /> <br /> 6 dice averages 3 successes, and hits 2 successes (challenging fare for heroes with a complication) 81% of the time. With a Full Excellency you hit 5 successes 73% of the time and hit Parry 8 (Dex 5+Melee 5+Specialty+Stunt+Medium Weapon) 48% of the time.<br /> 10 dice averages 5 successes, and hits 2 succcesses 96% of the time. It hits 5 successes 57% of the time, rising to 97% of the time with a Full Excellency. It hits Parry 8 (Dex 5+Melee 5+Specialty+Stunt+Medium Weapon) 89% of the time.<br /> <br /> Scores of 3 make you obviously talented, and capable enough to dominate a kingdom. The rules of the game reflect this, both in terms of static difficulty and the difficulty of NPCs.<br /> Scores of 5 make you the best in the world.<br /> <br /> The hardest, Difficulty 5, Feats can be overcome by Exalted with scores of 3. But to do so, they need to spend Essence. So if you have to leap a bottomless pit, then shrug off the effect of poison fog, then heal your badly wounded ally, then (when you fight the Mini-Boss at the end of the dungeon) you enter combat down a bunch of motes. And there's a decent chance that if four(ish) PCs are each rolling against three(ish) challenges back-to-back then someone is going to fail, adding in real danger (and Wound Penalties during that Boss Fite). When you face one of the most dangerous foes in Creation, fully half your attacks miss when you go all-out.<br /> <br /> With scores of 5... not so much. You breeze through the dungeon, not bothering to spend motes on the easier tasks and with no chance of failure on the hard tasks. Then when you get to the boss fight, you chunk them in 2 rounds, because even though they're supposed to be one of the most powerful combatants in the world you're hitting them 90% of the time.<br /> <br /> Then you consider the Charms you might not qualify for if only running at 3 instead of 5, and how that limits your tactical choices.<br /> <br /> Then you multiply that by all the characters in the Circle.<br /> <br /> ~4 PCs rolling ~6 dice against an assassin's Stealth attempt is probably going to succeed.<br /> ~4 PCs rolling ~10 dice against that isn't rolling to see <b>if </b>they spot her, but who spots her <b>first</b>.<br /> <br /> And there's nothing wrong with that. Exalted is fun because it allows this. But a game where most PCs have most relevant stats at 5 is a very different game from the default, intended powerlevel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a lot of noncombat checks, 3 Attribute + 3 Ability + full Excellency is plenty, and mote efficiency isn't an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>If mote efficiency isn't an issue and failure isn't probable, I suggest not rolling. You succeed. Enjoy being awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if you don't have a Session 0</div> </div> </div> </div>Without ill-will or sarcasm: good luck playing Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if you don't have a Session 0 where players agree not to take a bunch of 5s</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted literallty walks you through, step-by-step, how to make a character. A properly terrifying Solar assassin, has a single Attribute at 5 and only two Abilities above 3 -- Stealth and Melee 4. Exalted also walks you through how to make NPCs: it says keep their dice pools below 11 &quot;so that players do not feel forced to maximize their stats&quot;.<br /> <br /> In Tomb of Dreams, they showcase 5 pregen Solar Characters. They have 8 Abilities at 5 between the five characters -- one of which not having any 5s.<br /> <br /> By default, you shouldn't be taking a bunch of 5s.<br /> <br /> That said, I <i>like </i>starting with 5s. The only character I play took nine 5s at character creation.<br /> <br /> I took them wanting to cake-walk anything in my area of expertise and really struggle against anything outside my comfort-zone <i>because </i>I wanted to play a street-smart fish-out-of-water who never made it in their own world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(though the ST may need to up the difficulty of rolls a bit.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Bleuh. Why?<br /> <br /> If climbing a wall is difficulty 1, climbing that wall shouldn't be <i>harder</i> because I'm <i>good </i>at climbing walls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think DES may be more likely to help you overshadow another player. Say, in a crucial fight for the story where multiple characters have a defining intimacy that is obviously relevant, wouldn't you be playing as intended to go all Divine Executioner Stance while the chips are down? But then the other character doesn't have it, or any charms of similar power level, and they are made less relevant.<br /> <br /> OK I'm exaggerating a bit (you would probably have to already have a more-efficiently-built character to see a big effect (though with Melee that's pretty easy to accidentally achieve)) but it seems like an easy thing to fix by just banning the charm outright or houseruling the mote cost a bit higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're playing DES as intended, then yes, when the chips are down and the Intimacy counts, one PC will be markedly better than another.<br /> <br /> But if you're playing as intended, then on every scene leading up to this point, the other player would have had an extra Charm helping them.<br /> <br /> The problem with DES is when the latter doesn't happen, and one PC constantly overshadows the others in <b>every</b> combat. And that problem occurs when you let people pick an Intimacy which is broader than the example Intimacy given in the Charm. And that's what I suggest people &quot;fix&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also support XP-based character generation as a not-completely-easy fix to make it still very possible to be a badass with multiple 5s at character creation but not possible to have an absurd amount of 5s and not pushed so hard in that direction by the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a lot of bean-counting. I don't like it. If it works for you, then have fun. If there wasn't Session 0 expectations pushing me against it, I'd still push for 5s based on Exalted's mechanics and liking to win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your game has a main story arc (say, fighting the forces of a particular Deathlord) would you allow a Major or Defining Intimacy that applies to every fight / most fights in that story arc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't run that kind of game. It strikes me as incredibly dull.<br /> <br /> But for the purpose of this converstation: &quot;no, I wouldn't allow it&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I also think having a Melee specialty in &quot;my weapon&quot;, while I think 100% intended by the game, is a bit weird - won't it apply to basically all rolls? - but I'm not going to try to get rid of it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone has a Specialty in their weapon, and you aren't using Disarms, or forcing them to leave their weapon behind for diplomatic reasons, or giving them enemies their weapon can't hurt, or tempting them with more powerful weapons to upgrade...<br /> <br /> Then, honestly, you're better off scrapping Specialties and just increasing Stunt bonuses to +3.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with using Shining Ice Mirror and having a Melee Specialty in &quot;Swords&quot;. There's something wrong with a Melee Specialty in &quot;Any weapon that isn't my grand-father's old blacksmithing hammer&quot; then melting that hammer down into slag. And we're discussing a Charm which gives you +6 dice, not +1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380108#post1380108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what do you mean by &quot;apocryphal&quot;? That the Charm may or may not actually exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Apocryphal keyword is described on Page 5 of the book Divine Exectutioner's Stance is in. And as a Melee power which draws strength from your oppoenent's feelings and beliefs, I think it's a pretty good fit. (&quot;<b>Your</b> hatred of orphans, which <i>I don't know about</i>, makes <b>my </b>sword more deadly&quot; is really not prime Solar design space. DES is tenuous at best as a Solar Charm. It feels a lot more Abyssal/Liminal/Lunar-y to me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-10-2020, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:33:10-07:00","id":1380176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380153#post1380153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the context of this conversation? Yes.<br /> <br /> In an actual game? Topaz's player clearly wants to be The Best(tm) at combat. So long as they understand that they won't ever be challenged in combat, and I will only rarely be asking them to roll dice in combat, I'm actually fine with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. I would have let it happen, but only let the intimacy apply when up against the kind of opposition fitting to an Invincible Sword Princess. Multiple DBs, Celestial Exalts, Demons on the level of Mara or Octavian, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:37:53-07:00","id":1380179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380176#post1380176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting. I would have let it happen, but only let the intimacy apply when up against the kind of opposition fitting to an Invincible Sword Princess. Multiple DBs, Celestial Exalts, Demons on the level of Mara or Octavian, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory: that's an excellent idea.<br /> In practice: &quot;you don't get DES if what you're fighting is so weak that you didn't need it anyway&quot; isn't really any different to &quot;you get DES always&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:45:29-07:00","id":1380182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380179#post1380179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In theory: that's an excellent idea.<br /> In practice: &quot;you don't get DES if what you're fighting is so weak that you didn't need it anyway&quot; isn't really any different to &quot;you get DES always&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You sound like an experienced and talented GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:45:29-07:00","id":1380183,"title":"","content":"Why is double posting happening? I didn't ask for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:06:07-07:00","id":1380189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380158#post1380158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this next post is for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25834\" data-vbnamecard=\"25834\">habitableexoplanet</a>.<br /> <br /> It is not my intent to insult or belittle you or your opinions. We have <i>different </i>opinions, and I'm going to explain why. I'm aware that the tone here could be read as a little harsh: this is not my intent, but I'm not eloquent enough to phrase my argument in a manner which isn't blunt. I really enjoyed reading your post, and you make a good case. I ask that you read what follows in the friendliest, most charitable way that you can imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's totally fine! I'm glad to have someone seriously engage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But long story short: I disagree with everything you just said. Here's why:<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes. It's huge.<br /> <br /> 6 dice averages 3 successes, and hits 2 successes (challenging fare for heroes with a complication) 81% of the time. With a Full Excellency you hit 5 successes 73% of the time and hit Parry 8 (Dex 5+Melee 5+Specialty+Stunt+Medium Weapon) 48% of the time.<br /> 10 dice averages 5 successes, and hits 2 succcesses 96% of the time. It hits 5 successes 57% of the time, rising to 97% of the time with a Full Excellency. It hits Parry 8 (Dex 5+Melee 5+Specialty+Stunt+Medium Weapon) 89% of the time. </div> </div> </div>Doesn't this demonstrate that the biggest differences are in combat?<br /> <br /> Or for other types of opposed rolls. (It's strange to me that &quot;<span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">removing an appendix in the dead of night, without su</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">fficient light, in the midst of a howling storm&quot; (difficulty 2) is similar in difficulty to sneak past an ordinary soldier (4 dice pool), and &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">leaping over the rail of a sorcerer\u2019s flying chariot </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">to land safely in a hay cart hundreds of feet below&quot; (difficulty 5) is similar in difficulty to sneaking past an elite soldier (9 dice pool)&quot;.)</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scores of 3 make you obviously talented, and capable enough to dominate a kingdom. The rules of the game reflect this, both in terms of static difficulty and the difficulty of NPCs.<br /> Scores of 5 make you the best in the world.<br /> <br /> The hardest, Difficulty 5 Feats, can be overcome by Exalted with scores of 3. But to do so, they need to spend Essence. So if you have to leap a bottomless pit, then shrug off the effect of poison fog, then heal your badly wounded ally, then (when you fight the Mini-Boss at the end of the dungeon) you enter combat down a bunch of motes. And there's a decent chance that if four(ish) PCs are each rolling against three(ish) challenges back-to-back then someone is going to fail, adding in real danger (and Wound Penalties during that Boss Fite). When you face one of the most dangerous foes in Creation, fully half your attacks miss when you go all-out.<br /> <br /> With scores of 5... not so much. You breeze through the dungeon, not bothering to spend motes on the easier tasks and with no chance of failure on the hard tasks. Then when you get to the boss fight, you chunk them in 2 rounds, because even though they're supposed to be one of the most powerful combatants in the world you're hitting them 90% of the time. </div> </div> </div>That's fair. The game I play hasn't had a lot of dungeon-style play, where mote economy over a series of challenges is crucial. It's more free-form challenges in a city setting, which amplifies the difficulty of combat encounters (which can run you out of motes all on their own) compared to other characters.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of times the hardest challenges are when we have to roll our low stats, which getting a lot of 5s would make harder, not easier (because the other stats would likely end up lower).<br /> <br /> It's true that having 5s in combat (in particular in the main combat stat) is a big effect. When I was talking about the balance effects of a lot of 5s, I was mostly thinking about noncombat stats. When I started my character, I think I had 5s in Lore, Occult, and Medicine but 4 in Melee.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you consider the Charms you might not qualify for if only running at 3 instead of 5, and how that limits your tactical choices. </div> </div> </div>Sure, although the Three Stat Mafia probably have more Charms, or else what did they spend those points on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you multiply that by all the characters in the Circle.<br /> <br /> ~4 PCs rolling ~6 dice against an assassin's Stealth attempt is probably going to succeed.<br /> ~4 PCs rolling ~10 dice against that isn't rolling to see <b>if </b>they spot her, but who spots her <b>first</b>.<br /> <br /> And there's nothing wrong with that. Exalted is fun because it allows this. But a game where most PCs have most relevant stats at 5 is a very different game from the default, intended powerlevel. </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't the relevant stats to one PC be different from the relevant stats to another PC? I agree 100% that if everyone takes 5s in the most combat relevant stats, including Athletics and Awareness, so they also all trivialize the same noncombat challenges while they're at it, that's unbalanced and kinda silly. (But at least it will hopefully be balanced between the different players in their combat encounters). <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If mote efficiency isn't an issue and failure isn't probable, I suggest not rolling. You succeed. Enjoy being awesome. </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is good advice, but I think rolling dice pools is fun and doesn't take that much time and generally prefer to do it even if it's not necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without ill-will or sarcasm: good luck playing Exalted. </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying this is how I play exalted. My next game will have a serious session 0, and surely include a low number of 5s per player, possibly even lower power than Solars to start.<br /> <br /> The discussion was about the system generally. You said that taking a lot of 5s unbalanced the game. I said that if you took a lot of 5s, it's likely the other players took a lot of 5s as well, and that mitigates it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exalted literallty walks you through, step-by-step, how to make a character. A properly terrifying Solar assassin, has a single Attribute at 5 and only two Abilities above 3 -- Stealth and Melee 4. Exalted also walks you through how to make NPCs: it says keep their dice pools below 11 &quot;so that players do not feel forced to maximize their stats&quot;. </div> </div> </div>In the character creation section it also says<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">If you don\u2019t have a solid idea of what you want to spend bonus points on, it\u2019s generally most cost-e</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">ff</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">ective to use them to raise Caste and Favored Abilities; new powers such as Charms and spells give the lowest return-on-investment. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you follow this advice, rather than imitate the example character (who spends a lot of BPs on Charms), you are almost certainly going to end up with multiple 5s.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Tomb of Dreams, they showcase 5 pregen Solar Characters. They have 8 Abilities at 5 between the five characters -- one of which not having any 5s. </div> </div> </div>Surely this is helpful to groups that start with the Tomb of Dreams. If you just look at the core book, and try to learn from that, I don't think the intended style of play (and I agree that this is the intended style of play) is as clear as you make it sound.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By default, you shouldn't be taking a bunch of 5s.<br /> <br /> That said, I <i>like </i>starting with 5s. The only character I play took nine 5s at character creation. </div> </div> </div>It looks like 11 is the maximum. I would post &quot;Pathetic.&quot; but it wouldn't be completely 100% obvious I'm joking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I took them wanting to cake-walk anything in my area of expertise and really struggle against anything outside my comfort-zone <i>because </i>I wanted to play a street-smart fish-out-of-water who never made it in their own world. </div> </div> </div>Cool, sounds like a fun character. It's weird to me that the system as written pushes characters into doing that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bleuh. Why?<br /> <br /> If climbing a wall is difficulty 1, climbing that wall shouldn't be <i>harder</i> because I'm <i>good </i>at climbing walls. </div> </div> </div>I mean, if your characters are more badass, you can give them more badass challenges. Describe how the wall is really tall and/or very smooth, and give the players a higher difficulty, and make them feel cool for doing it. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're playing DES as intended, then yes, when the chips are down and the Intimacy counts, one PC will be markedly better than another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But if you're playing as intended, then on every scene leading up to this point, the other player would have had an extra Charm helping them. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but most powerful combat charms are useless when you're not fighting and still not useful in every fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem with DES is when the latter doesn't happen, and one PC constantly overshadows the others in <b>every</b> combat. And that problem occurs when you let people pick an Intimacy which is broader than the example Intimacy given in the Charm. And that's what I suggest people &quot;fix&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is a good step. I again think having one example doing things a certain way is not very clear instruction when the pitfalls of doing things the other way are large.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a lot of bean-counting. I don't like it. If it works for you, then have fun. If there wasn't Session 0 expectations pushing me against it, I'd still push for 5s based on Exalted's mechanics and liking to win. </div> </div> </div>We have a custom google sheet that does the calculations, and some other ones, automatically, which makes it a lot easier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone has a Specialty in their weapon, and you aren't using Disarms, or forcing them to leave their weapon behind for diplomatic reasons, or giving them enemies their weapon can't hurt, or tempting them with more powerful weapons to upgrade...<br /> <br /> Then, honestly, you're better off scrapping Specialties and just increasing Stunt bonuses to +3. </div> </div> </div>I agree that disarms, diplomatic difficulties, and upgrades are all good ideas, but doing them specifically to counter someone's specialty seems strange. I would prefer it if what counts as an appropriate specialty were a bit more formalized, but it's only +1 die and not a big deal either way.<br /> <br /> I'm also probably not as big a fan as the specialty system as the average Exalted player, but scrapping it because one player has one overly powerful specialty seems a bit extreme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's nothing wrong with using Shining Ice Mirror and having a Melee Specialty in &quot;Swords&quot;. There's something wrong with a Melee Specialty in &quot;Any weapon that isn't my grand-father's old blacksmithing hammer&quot; then melting that hammer down into slag. And we're discussing a Charm which gives you +6 dice, not +1. </div> </div> </div>I agree that it's not so relevant to our current discussion - I just felt like bringing it up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Apocryphal keyword is described on Page 5 of the book Divine Exectutioner's Stance is in. And as a Melee power which draws strength from your oppoenent's feelings and beliefs, I think it's a pretty good fit. (&quot;<b>Your</b> hatred of orphans, which <i>I don't know about</i>, makes <b>my </b>sword more deadly&quot; is really not prime Solar design space. DES is tenuous at best as a Solar Charm. It feels a lot more Abyssal/Liminal/Lunar-y to me.) </div> </div> </div>My mistake. (I don't have the book, and I just looked up what it did when I first saw people discuss it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:56:53-07:00","id":1380224,"title":"","content":"Moderately relevant to the above, but this was a fight I posted in the DB Builds thread (didn't want to disrupt <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11917_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11917\" data-vbnamecard=\"11917\">Aranfan</a>'s epic fight) that I'll stick here as suggested by <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/\" target=\"_blank\">JohnDoe244</a> (thanks!) now I've fixed the mistake I made in the write-up. It features Volfer from Tomb of Dreams against a DB character \u2013 built to try some of the new charms from Heirs and to use as an antagonist in a game \u2013 who has 5s in the big combat abilities but who I personally wouldn't see as problematic at the table (obviously, I made him, others may differ).<br /> <br /> In short, think Heirs has given Earth melee a couple of fun new toys.<br /> <br /> Chargen Earth Aspected Melee Dynast <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> House of Bells<br /> <br /> ATTRIBUTES (8 BP used here)<br /> <br /> 5 Strength<br /> 5 Dexterity<br /> 3 Stamina<br /> <br /> 1 Charisma<br /> 2 Manipulation<br /> 4 Appearance<br /> <br /> 3 Perception<br /> 2 Intelligence<br /> 4 Wits<br /> <br /> ABILITIES (8 BP used here)<br /> <br /> Aspect<br /> <br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Craft 0<br /> Integrity 2<br /> Resistance 5<br /> War 3 (Exploiting Terrain)<br /> <br /> Favoured<br /> <br /> Lore 1<br /> Occult 1<br /> Thrown 1 (Javelins)<br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Melee 5 (Tetsubo)<br /> <br /> Other<br /> <br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Socialise 3<br /> Dodge 3<br /> Brawl 1<br /> <br /> MERITS (2 BP used here)<br /> <br /> (Native Language: High Realm)<br /> <br /> Artefact 3 (Grand Goremaul)<br /> Artefact 3 (Reinforced Breastplate)<br /> Pain Tolerance 4<br /> Resources 3<br /> Backing 3 (House Ragara)<br /> Hearthstone 2 (Stone of the Ram\u2019s Horn)<br /> Language 1 (Low Realm)<br /> Language 1 (Riverspeak)<br /> <br /> CHARMS<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> Athletics<br /> Awareness<br /> Integrity<br /> Melee<br /> War<br /> <br /> 1. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 2. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 3. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 4. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 5. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 6. Resistance: Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> 7. Melee: Flame-Born Interception<br /> 8. Melee: Blinding Spark Distraction<br /> 9. Melee: Crossfire Flash<br /> 10. Melee: Dragon-Scale Shield<br /> 11. Melee: Rumbling Earth Rebuke<br /> 12. Awareness: Deep-Listening Palm<br /> 13. Awareness: All-Encompassing Earth Sense<br /> 14. Awareness: Pasiap Preempts Haste<br /> 15. War: Roaring Dragon Officer<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Fight</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Starts at medium range<br /> One-point stunts assumed<br /> <br /> Join Battle<br /> <br /> Earth Aspect rolls 12 dice + 3 successes (6m Excellency) + willpower + Pasiap Preempts Haste (3m) for 11i. Anima at glowing.<br /> Volfer rolls 16 dice (6m Excellency) + willpower for 9i<br /> <br /> TURN 1<br /> <i>EA: 11i (13p/11ph, 4 WP, 1a)<br /> Volfer: 9i (13p/27ph, 5 WP)</i><br /> <br /> EA delays turn (-0i because of Pasiap Preempts Haste).<br /> <br /> Volfer closes to short and uses Thunderclap Rush (3m) to launch a withering attack using Excellent Strike (3m), Fire and Stones Strike (5m), Excellency (6m) and willpower for 18 dice + 2 successes.<br /> <br /> EA boosts his parry to 12 with Dragon-Scale Shield (1m, 1i, +1 non-charm to parry when used with a heavy weapon), a full Excellency (6m) and willpower. Anima at burning.<br /> <br /> Volfer gets 11 successes, attack misses.<br /> <br /> EA makes a withering smashing attack (-1i) using a 3m Excellency, the Pasiap Preempts Haste bonus (3 dice) and willpower for 20 dice + 1 success.<br /> <br /> Volfer defends with full Excellency (8m), Durability of Oak (3m) and willpower for a parry of 11.<br /> <br /> EA gets 11 successes, attack hits. Damage pool of 19 (5 Strength + 14 Weapon Damage), Volfer uses Spirit Strengthens the Skin (4m) to boost his soak to effectively 13 (including the Durability of Oak bonus).<br /> <br /> 6 dice of damage gives two successes.<br /> <br /> Volfer is prone. EA enters earth aura.<br /> <br /> TURN 2:<br /> <i>Mote regen<br /> EA: 12i (13p/6ph, 2 WP, 2a)<br /> Volfer: 7i (8p/5ph, 3 WP, prone)</i><br /> <br /> EA makes a withering attack using a full Excellency (5m) for 20 dice. Anima at bonfire.<br /> <br /> Volfer defends with Excellency (2m), Durability of Oak and willpower for a parry of 6 after onslaught and being knocked prone.<br /> <br /> EA gets 9 successes, attack hits. Damage pool of 22. Volfer repeats his use of Spirit Strengthens the Skin (4m) to boost his soak to 13.<br /> <br /> 9 dice of damage gives four successes.<br /> <br /> EA: 17i (13p/1ph, 2 WP, 3a)<br /> Volfer: 3i (4p/0ph, 2 WP, prone)<br /> <br /> Volfer flurries rise from prone, spending 1 willpower to make sure he makes it, with an unenhanced withering attack, rolling 9 dice after the flurry penalty.<br /> <br /> EA\u2019s parry is 7.<br /> <br /> Volfer gets 9 successes, attack hits. Damage pool is 15. At bonfire, EA soak is at 17, so Volfer is reduced to overwhelming damage. 1 dice gives no successes.<br /> <br /> TURN 3:<br /> <i>Mote regen<br /> Anima flux does nothing<br /> EA: 17i (13p/6ph, 2 WP, 3a)<br /> Volfer: 4i (4p/5ph, 1 WP)</i><br /> <br /> EA delays to clash (drops to 15i).<br /> <br /> Volfer goes all out with a withering attack using Excellent Strike, 6m Excellency and willpower for 18 dice + 2 successes.<br /> <br /> EA clashes with a withering smashing attack (-1i) using full Excellency (6m), Crossfire Flash (5m) and willpower for 22 dice + 1 success.<br /> <br /> Volfer gets 10 successes, EA gets 12 success after Crossfire Flash re-rolls.<br /> <br /> Damage pool is 21, resulting in 14 dice damage and 4 successes. Volfer is knocked prone and crashed.<br /> <br /> EA: 27i (8p/0ph, 1 WP, 3a)<br /> Volfer: 0i (0p/0ph, 0 WP, prone)<br /> <br /> EA activates Rumbling Earth Rebuke (4m, 1wp), triggering a reflexive disarm gambit. Volfer\u2019s parry is 2 (-1 prone, -2 from losing a clash).<br /> <br /> EA rolls 11 dice for 5 successes. Attack hits, and he passes the initiative roll easily (-4i). Volfer\u2019s chopping sword is destroyed.<br /> <br /> TURN 4:<br /> <i>Mote regen<br /> Anima flux does nothing<br /> EA: 23i (4p/5ph, 0 WP, 3a)<br /> Volfer: 0i (0p/5ph, 0 WP, prone)</i><br /> <br /> EA makes a withering attack using a full Excellency (5m) for 20 dice.<br /> <br /> Volfer\u2019s parry is now at 0 (Brawl parry of 4, -1 prone, -2 from losing a clash, -1 from Rumbling Earth Rebuke in Earth aura). He stunts and uses a 4m Excellency to reach parry 3.<br /> <br /> EA gets 9 successes, attack hits, damage pool of 25. 18 dice give 4 successes (yet AGAIN).<br /> <br /> EA: 28i (4p/0ph, 0 WP, 3a)<br /> Volfer: -4i (0p/1ph, 0 WP, prone)<br /> <br /> Volfer flurries rise from prone with a withering brawl attack. He makes the rise from prone and rolls 10 dice. EA uses a 1m Excellency and Blinding Spark Distraction (1m, 1i) for a parry of 8. Volfer rolls 3 successes, misses and is blinded.<br /> <br /> TURN 5:<br /> <i>Mote regen<br /> Anima flux inflicts 1 HL and knocks Volfer prone<br /> EA: 25i (2p/5ph, 0 WP, 3a)<br /> Volfer: -4i (0p/6ph, 0 WP, blinded, prone)</i><br /> <br /> EA makes a decisive attack using a full Excellency (4m) for 19 dice. Volfer uses 6m Excellency to boost his parry to 4 (Parry of 4 + 3 Excellency + 1 Stunt \u2013 1 prone \u2013 3 blinded).<br /> <br /> 6 successes, attack hits. 25 initiative give 13 successes, Volfer is down.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Notes<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> - I may have screwed up here in turn 2 on the melee excellency when Volfer hit \u2013 if I don\u2019t use the charm (having already used it that turn) but fail to parry does that attack count in terms of resetting the discount?<br /> <br /> - Dragon-Scale Shield giving heavy weapons a boost was the difference in turn 1.<br /> <br /> - Rumbling Earth Rebuke worked here and is powerful if held back for when motes are low, but obviously situational \u2013 Dragon-Graced Weapon or Call the Blade make it an inconvenience. Still, not having to give up an attack but still being able to use a disarm and turn your typical white room Melee 5, Dex 5 nightmare sword fighter into a Dex 5, Brawl 0 target is nice. Perversely, Volfer, as non-optimised as he is, actually has some brawl and was only knocked back a couple of pegs in effectiveness. I \u2018declared\u2019 Rumbling Earth Rebuke in the initial attack \u2013 I probably need to clarify if that\u2019s necessary with devs.<br /> <br /> - Speaking of white rooms, one-on-one duels in particular, I think DB melee probably does \u2018better\u2019 in these than it would in an actual game with extras, battle groups, archers or the like \u2013 the excellency discount and the clash enhancing charms thrive in this environment.<br /> <br /> - I really like Pasiap Preempts Haste \u2013 charms that help you do two things (win JB and improve your first attack) are okay with me.<br /> <br /> - I\u2019ve thought this before, but earth\u2019s anima power seems OP to me. Leaving aside the soak, being able to knock people prone is a most massive debuff, no?<br /> <br /> - Benchmarking builds against Volfer \u2013 as has been noted elsewhere he doesn\u2019t have all his charms/merits etc so I should probably not do that any more as that way lies non-fun \u2018If you can\u2019t beat Volfer are you even Exalted?\u2019 thinking. Also, while this fight was straightforward, as maligned as he is as a Dawn, Volfer has a good shot at landing that opening attack on a pretty-near optimised DB and then going into a One Weapon, Two Blows combo to suck defensive motes and potentially inflict a wound penalty. The clash could have gone his way too with a little luck. Still think the DB would win if either of those had happened, he has too many health levels and artefacts, but Volfer\u2019s not that bad \u2013 y\u2019know, like Scroll of Exalts Solars bad. He\u2019s incomplete.<br /> <br /> - I've got to get better at writing these up if I'm going to do any more of them...<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T16:16:14-07:00","id":1380230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380224#post1380224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moderately relevant to the above, but this was a fight I posted in the DB Builds thread (didn't want to disrupt <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11917_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11917\" data-vbnamecard=\"11917\">Aranfan</a>'s epic fight)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No need to wait on my account. This thread is for everybody.<br /> <br /> And it certainly looks like the new charms give DB Melee some sweet new tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T23:11:59-07:00","id":1380323,"title":"","content":"Two fights with Exalted outnumbered by mortals<br /> <br /> Jazel the Twilight archer vs two gator-riding Horse Nomads. The thigh-high much gives -3 die penalty to defense, and the dark combined with the fog a -3 penalty to ranged attacks. The gators let the nomads ignore the muck but not the vision penalties.<br /> <br /> Originally she was going to fight spirits but I decided fuck it let's do mortals.<br /> <br /> Jazel<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> str 3<br /> dex 3<br /> sta 3<br /> <br /> cha 3<br /> man 2<br /> app 2<br /> <br /> per 5<br /> int 5<br /> wit 3<br /> <br /> <br /> 5 Archery (Wooden Recurve)<br /> 4 Dodge (Taking Cover)<br /> 5 Occult (Gods)<br /> <br /> <br /> Bow Short 13(Damage 12/1)<br /> Evasion 4<br /> Soak 8 (medium armor)<br /> <br /> 16/40 motes 6wp<br /> <br /> Spirit Detecting Glance<br /> Spirit Cutting Attack<br /> Spirit Repelling Diagram<br /> Spirit Caging Mandala<br /> Spirit Draining Mudra<br /> Spirit Shredding Exorcism<br /> <br /> <br /> Wise Arrow<br /> Sight WIthout Eyes<br /> Force Without Fire<br /> Accuracy Without Distance<br /> <br /> Drifting Leaf Elusion<br /> Reed in the Wind<br /> Shadow over Water<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> through Lur's Swamp. There's a crossing however where for a few hundred feet it's washed out and she has to trudge across thigh-high swamp. Jazel thinks she hears something. Spending 2 motes to roll 10 dice on perception awareness for 7 successes she hears two entities slithering towards her in the swamp. Roll Join Battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> Spending 4m to excellency her join battle she gets 8i<br /> Sol1 5i<br /> Arc2 9i<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ============<br /> <br /> Jazel 8i 16|34m 6wp<br /> Sol1 5i<br /> Arc2 9i<br /> <br /> Arc2 will attempt a withering shot against Jazel, who will use 2m Shadow over Water to ignore penalties to evasion, and 2m to raise evasion to 5. Rolling 8 dice for 4 the archer misses.<br /> <br /> Jazel 8i 16|30m 6wp<br /> Sol1 5i<br /> Arc2 9i<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Jazel will flurry a Take Cover action with a bow shot against the Archer. First spending 2m to roll 7 dice on take cover she gets 2 successes and takes heavy cover behind a nearby tree. Then spending 1m for Sight Without Eyes to ignore the fog and dark, 1m Wise Arrow, and 2m excellency. Rolling 15 dice for 4 against Evasion 2, then rolling 6 damage for 5<br /> <br /> Jazel 14i 16|26m 6wp<br /> Sol1 5i<br /> Arc2 4i<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Soldier will try to wither Jazel, getting around the tree to avoid cover. Jazel will spend 2m to ignore penalties and another 2 to boost evasion. Attacking with the Scimitar and rolling 9 dice he gets 3 successes and misses.<br /> <br /> Jazel 14i 16|22m 6wp<br /> Sol1 5i<br /> Arc2 4i<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ============<br /> <br /> Jazel goes to make a decisive attack against the soldier, spending 1m 1wp to use Accuracy Without Distance, doing so automatically hits his defense, so she will roll damage of 10 on 14 dice, killing the soldier!<br /> <br /> Jazel 3i 16|26m 5wp<br /> Arc2 4i<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Archer will spend a turn trying to outflank Jazel with movement, and fire a withering shot at her. She will spend 2m to ignore penalties to her evasion, and another 2 to raise her evasion to effectively 7. Rolling 8 dice come up with 6 and just miss.<br /> <br /> Jazel 3i 16|22m 5wp<br /> Arc2 4i<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ============<br /> <br /> Archer will spend movement rolling around and getting into a position where Jazel's cover doesn't apply anymore, and fires another withering shot. Jazel spends 2m to ignore cover and 6m to boost evasion. Rolling 8 dice for 5 against evasion 6 he misses again.<br /> <br /> Jazel 3i 8|27m 5wp<br /> Arc2 4i<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Jazel will fire a withering shot, spending 1m to ignore penalties, 1m on Wise Arrow and 2m on an excellency. Rolling 15 dice for 10 and easily hitting, then rolling 11 damage for 7, crashing the archer.<br /> <br /> Jazel 16i 8|23m 5wp<br /> Arc2 -3i<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ============<br /> Jazel 16i 8|28m 5wp<br /> Arc2 -3i<br /> <br /> Jazel will fire a decisive shot this time, spending the same 4m to roll 9 dice, just hitting with 2 successes, then rolling 16 damage for 6, enough to drive the archer back into the swamp.<br /> <br /> Jazel 16i 8|24m 5wp<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Pretty easy fight for Jazel, but it took some motes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Next is Karen, an immaculate air monk who gets an attempted ambush in a warehouse, the ground is strewn with broken crates so the whole thing is difficult terrain. She gets ambushed by one sword fighter and one archer, who's positioned himself in heavy cover at the back of the warehouse.<br /> <br /> Karen<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> phs 3/3/3<br /> soc 3/2/2<br /> men 4/3/4<br /> <br /> <br /> 5 Air Dragon (Chakram Attacks)<br /> 4 Dodge<br /> 3 awareness<br /> <br /> <br /> Infinite Jade Chakram 14(damage 13/3)<br /> Evasion 4<br /> Soak 6 (Light armor)<br /> 13/26m<br /> <br /> All Essence 2 Air Dragon charms<br /> Dodge up to Nimble Zephyr Defense<br /> Athletics up to Incense Smoke Ladder<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Karen enters the abandoned warehouse, spending 2m to add a success to her roll to spot the ambush. Getting 5 successes she beats all her ambushers. An archer at short range away tucked away in Heavy cover among some boxes, and a soldier down in among the scattered crates, difficult terrain.<br /> <br /> Rolling join battle she uses another 2m to add a success getting 7i<br /> Arc 6i<br /> Sol 5i<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> =========<br /> Karen will use 5m for Cloud-Treading Method, 5m for Wind Dragon Speed, to disengage without penalty for flurry for difficult terrain toward the archer, also spending 4m to get 4 dice. Rollign 11 dice against six nets 4 successes against 3.<br /> <br /> Karen 5i 13|8 5wp<br /> Arc 6i<br /> Sol 5i<br /> <br /> Karen then attacks the archer, rolling an attack without flurry penalty, rolling 14 dice for 3 successes, and just hitting, then rolling 5 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Karen will spend 8m to enter Air Dragon Form, trying to keep from going totemic so spending that from peripheral.<br /> <br /> Karen 9i 5|8 5wp<br /> Arc 3i<br /> Sol 5i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> The Soldier will go rushing after Karen, using his reflexive move to start moving across difficult terrain, and then rushing, which Karen will not oppose.<br /> <br /> Karen 9i 5|8 5wp<br /> Arc 3i<br /> Sol 5i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> The archer will attempt to disengage Karen, rolling 3 dice due to difficult terrain and failing with no successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =========<br /> Karen 9i 5|13 5wp<br /> Arc 3i<br /> Sol 5i<br /> <br /> Karen will smack the archer with another withering, rolling 9 successes to hit, then 7 withering damage.<br /> <br /> Karen 17i 5|13 5wp<br /> Arc -4i<br /> Sol 5i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> The soldier closes into range with his reflexive move, then decisive attacks Karen, who will defend with 1m Nimble Zeyphr Defense. Rolling 9 dice to hit and getting 7, hitting. Then rolling 5 decisive damage for 2, putting Karen into -1s.<br /> <br /> <br /> Karen 17i 5|12 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -4i<br /> Sol 3i<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Archer will try another disengage, rollign 3 dice for 3 successes, against Karen's 7 dice for 2, getting away!<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> =========<br /> Karen 17i 5|17 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -4i<br /> Sol 3i<br /> <br /> Karen will throw a chakram after Karen, with 4m to enhance the roll. Rolling 13 dice for 6, hitting, then 17 damage for 6, putting him to -4s.<br /> <br /> Karen 3i 5|13 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -4i -4s<br /> Sol 3i<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Soldier will smack Karen, who will use 1m Zephyr Defense and 2m Excellency. Rolling 9 dice for 3, he misses, losing a point of initiative.<br /> <br /> Karen 3i 5|10 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -4i -4s<br /> Sol 2i<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Archer fires an arrow, rolling 7 dice to hit, Karen spendin 1m to Zephyr Defense and 2m to excellency. The archer misses with 2 to hit.<br /> <br /> Karen 3i 5|7 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -5i -4s<br /> Sol 2i<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> =========<br /> <br /> Karen 3i 5|12 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -5i -4s<br /> Sol 2i<br /> <br /> Karen will try to hit Sol, using 4m to attack and only just now do I remember the DB excellecny ability. Getting 12 successes to hit, then rolling 14 damage for 4, crashing sol.<br /> <br /> Karen 13i 5|8 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -5i -4s<br /> Sol -2i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Sol will wither, Karen uses 1m Zephyr Defense and 2m excellency. Rolling 9 to hit for 5, but still missing due to Zeyphr Defense. <br /> <br /> Karen 13i 5|5 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -5i -4s<br /> Sol -3i<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Archer rolls to attack as well, Karen will spend 2m to excellency and 1m for Zephyr Defense. Rolling 7 dice for 2, missing<br /> <br /> Karen 13i 5|2 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -5i -4s<br /> Sol -3i<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> =========<br /> <br /> Karen 13i 5|7 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -5i -4s<br /> Sol -3i<br /> <br /> Karen makes a decisive attack against Sol, with 4m excellency, getting 5 to hit, and then rolling 6 damage, also putting him in his -4s and ending the fight<br /> <br /> Karen 13i 5|3 5wp -1 wound penalty<br /> Arc -5i -4s<br /> Sol -3i -4s<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This fight probably shouldn't have been as hard as it was, I totally forgot about the DB excellency ability for the first 80% of the fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> To me these fights are a lot more like actual in-game battles should be. They characters aren't optimized to all hell, but they're not deliberately bad either. There wasn't any real danger in either of these but it was just a couple of mortals and it's not like the PC analogues came out of it unscathed and without spending motes. One important thing was calling the fights when I did to stop it from dragging on, and also stop people just meandering about regenerating motes due to combat regen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T23:42:13-07:00","id":1380328,"title":"","content":"Do we have a thread about chargen? I have a question about how to de-optimize a character concept I've been kicking around for years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T00:59:37-07:00","id":1380334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380328#post1380328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have a thread about chargen? I have a question about how to de-optimize a character concept I've been kicking around for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe so but I'd love to see one.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I like making optimized 5/5/1 characters. I like playing 5/5/1 characters. I enjoy them for all the reasons people complain about them. Because people complain about them, I suggest people don't play them. It's a complicated topic that I'd love to give some thoughts on.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T09:54:39-07:00","id":1380401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380334#post1380334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe so but I'd love to see one.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I like making optimized 5/5/1 characters. I like playing 5/5/1 characters. I enjoy them for all the reasons people complain about them. Because people complain about them, I suggest people don't play them. It's a complicated topic that I'd love to give some thoughts on.)</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I don\u2019t get is if I take two different martial art styles at 5 and buy both complete styles as fast as I can, it\u2019s because I want to do lots of kinetic, high octane action scenes. Hopefully in Session 0 we decided this wasn\u2019t an Intrigue in High Castle style game with minimal fighting. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to feel like every peasant mugger is pushing me to my limits, on the occasion that those fights show up they should be a breeze. Just as often though I want my martial arts badass to be pushed to his limits of martial arts badassitude, because that\u2019s where meaningful decisions happen and I actually feel like my martial arts skills are required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:02:47-07:00","id":1380421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380401#post1380401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing I don\u2019t get is if I take two different martial art styles at 5 and buy both complete styles as fast as I can, it\u2019s because I want to do lots of kinetic, high octane action scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then play a Deeb.<br /> <br /> Because as a Solar you're now Solomon David, and finding a foe who can draw even a single drop of blood is going to be the goal of an entire story arc.<br /> <br /> Exalted doesn't, and has never adequately, provided high end opposition suitable for that kind of character. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t want to feel like every peasant mugger is pushing me to my limits, on the occasion that those fights show up they should be a breeze. Just as often though I want my martial arts badass to be pushed to his limits of martial arts badassitude, because that\u2019s where meaningful decisions happen and I actually feel like my martial arts skills are required. </div> </div> </div>And that's really hard. Because NPCs don't really exist which can do that. Either mechanically (with maybe a couple of exceptions) or narratively, because whilst every mortal and their grandmother can challenge an Exalt <i>played at the appropriate level</i> basically nothing can challenge a top-end Solar.<br /> <br /> Take 3 dots in two Martial Arts and enjoy exactly the high octane battles you are asking for as a returning Solar God-King... and buy upto 5 during play as you build up to the epic climax of your campaign.<br /> Play a Deeb, burning as bright as a Terrestrial can, and optimize as ruthlessly as you can against the rising tide of Anathema.<br /> <br /> But starting play as a maxed out Solar always has been what it is now.<br /> <br /> Exalted has never sold itself on &quot;min-max as much as possible to have more fun&quot;. 3E is very clear about the level of competence expected for PCs, and &quot;two maxed martial arts&quot; is WAAAY outside that ballpark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-11-2020, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:10:56-07:00","id":1380423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380334#post1380334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe so but I'd love to see one.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I like making optimized 5/5/1 characters. I like playing 5/5/1 characters. I enjoy them for all the reasons people complain about them. Because people complain about them, I suggest people don't play them. It's a complicated topic that I'd love to give some thoughts on.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Posted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread\"> Character building, optimization, and deoptimization thread. - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I want to build a stealth game protagonist night. The thing about stealth protags is that, unless they are batman, they are typically very good at sneaky but only so so at fighty. They aren't bad at fighty, but they aren't great. In exalted however, Dex governs both fighty and sneaky. I want my Night Caste to be sneaking into and out of deathlord stronghold, taking vital intelligence. Can I get away with Dex 3? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T17:51:20-07:00","id":1380524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380421#post1380421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted doesn't, and has never adequately, provided high end opposition suitable for that kind of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that for the most part you can challenge that kind of character, you just have to take the epic scale of Creation into account. Shining Topaz is doing really well in the arena fights against really powerful foes, but if she was in my game and just decided &quot;Hey, the Scarlet Throne is open right? Ima go sit on it and tell anyone who doesn't feel like calling me Empress to start digging their grave.&quot; without any plan beyond that, she would meet her end fairly quickly.<br /> <br /> Or more likely since I try not to be a dick, run into enough things that she might decide to either change her mind or formulate some kind of plan. Or run into some people that already have a plan just waiting for an epic hero to hinge it on.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I don't get though, is why you would <i>want </i>to play a character so powerful that they meet no meaningful resistance in anything. Especially to the point where the ST skips 90% of the combats you might find yourself in, which I would think is the reason you took 15 combat charms in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:46:39-07:00","id":1380535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380524#post1380524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that for the most part you can challenge that kind of character, you just have to take the epic scale of Creation into account. Shining Topaz is doing really well in the arena fights against really powerful foes, but if she was in my game and just decided &quot;Hey, the Scarlet Throne is open right? Ima go sit on it and tell anyone who doesn't feel like calling me Empress to start digging their grave.&quot; without any plan beyond that, she would meet her end fairly quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>In particular, won't being outnumbered by significant foes be a challenge to all but the most extreme combat-optimized starting solars? My recollection from earlier in this thread was that the builds that could take down multiple DBs were mostly high essence, and/or in the &quot;take all the most powerful melee charms&quot; style, rather than &quot;take some 5s and take a bunch of charms that seem cool&quot;.<br /> <br /> You don't have to declare yourself Empress to get in a fight with multiple DBs - though it would be hilarious - as offending the nearest Satrap seems like a healthier path to take, and should be a pretty achievable one anywhere in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:53:00-07:00","id":1380539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380535#post1380535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, won't being outnumbered by significant foes be a challenge to all but the most extreme combat-optimized starting solars? My recollection from earlier in this thread was that the builds that could take down multiple DBs were mostly high essence, and/or in the &quot;take all the most powerful melee charms&quot; style, rather than &quot;take some 5s and take a bunch of charms that seem cool&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, multiple DBs is a hard thing to do, multiple DBs in groups one after the other after the other is drastically more so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380535#post1380535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to declare yourself Empress to get in a fight with multiple DBs - though it would be hilarious - as offending the nearest Satrap seems like a healthier path to take, and should be a pretty achievable one anywhere in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you would think that...but in a 2e game I was in one of the players went to the Imperial city with an ultimatum and an unstable Proto Shinmaic Vortex. They declined to hear what he had to say so he dropped it, nuked the city PD'd the explosion and walked out again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T19:03:56-07:00","id":1380543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380524#post1380524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that for the most part you can challenge that kind of character, you just have to take the epic scale of Creation into account. Shining Topaz is doing really well in the arena fights against really powerful foes, but if she was in my game and just decided &quot;Hey, the Scarlet Throne is open right? Ima go sit on it and tell anyone who doesn't feel like calling me Empress to start digging their grave.&quot; without any plan beyond that, she would meet her end fairly quickly.<br /> <br /> Or more likely since I try not to be a dick, run into enough things that she might decide to either change her mind or formulate some kind of plan. Or run into some people that already have a plan just waiting for an epic hero to hinge it on.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I don't get though, is why you would <i>want </i>to play a character so powerful that they meet no meaningful resistance in anything. Especially to the point where the ST skips 90% of the combats you might find yourself in, which I would think is the reason you took 15 combat charms in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, she has a major intimacy that paperwork is mindnumbingly boring. So she wouldn't want to become the Empress. She'd be much more interested in finding progressively stronger stuff to test herself against, as well as learning and mastering the Sword MAs. And you could get a couple interesting stories out of her finding sifus and convincing them to train her.<br /> <br /> But yeah. Eventually the Saitama problem will rear it's head tho.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380535#post1380535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In particular, won't being outnumbered by significant foes be a challenge to all but the most extreme combat-optimized starting solars? My recollection from earlier in this thread was that the builds that could take down multiple DBs were mostly high essence, and/or in the &quot;take all the most powerful melee charms&quot; style, rather than &quot;take some 5s and take a bunch of charms that seem cool&quot;.<br /> <br /> You don't have to declare yourself Empress to get in a fight with multiple DBs - though it would be hilarious - as offending the nearest Satrap seems like a healthier path to take, and should be a pretty achievable one anywhere in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In fact, Topaz was the stress test to try and find a starting solar able to take on a hearth of DBs. It required Heaven Sword Flash+Thunderbolt Attack Prana+Sensory Acuity Prana. There were a few charms left over, but no other build we tried seemed to be able to overcome the action and mote economy advantage of a hearth. And it also left her completely mote tapped and ate most of her wp as well, so she'd be easy pickings if they brought a second wave of Deebs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 04-11-2020, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T19:32:05-07:00","id":1380550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380543#post1380543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, she has a major intimacy that paperwork is mindnumbingly boring. So she wouldn't want to become the Empress. She'd be much more interested in finding progressively stronger stuff to test herself against, as well as learning and mastering the Sword MAs. And you could get a couple interesting stories out of her finding sifus and convincing them to train her.<br /> <br /> But yeah. Eventually the Saitama problem will rear it's head tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>(1) Create a Twilight or Eclipse that loves bureauacracy<br /> (2) Convince Topaz to become your waifu<br /> (3) Declare yourself Empress/Shogun/whatever you feel like, and Topaz your bodyguard<br /> (4) Topaz has to take on multiple Warstriders piloted by Essence 5 DBs or whatever will challenge her at this point<br /> <br /> More seriously, it might be fun to have a game with a full circle of Solars, everyone really min-maxed, trying to take over the Realm as soon as possible (by finding the Sword of Creation combined with scheming, not by fighting every single DB, but fighting quite a lot of DBs along the way).<br /> <br /> Although not THAT seriously - that seems quite likely to be a trainwreck in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T00:12:07-07:00","id":1380591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380524#post1380524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that for the most part you can challenge that kind of character, you just have to take the epic scale of Creation into account. Shining Topaz is doing really well in the arena fights against really powerful foes, but if she was in my game and just decided &amp;quot;Hey, the Scarlet Throne is open right? Ima go sit on it and tell anyone who doesn't feel like calling me Empress to start digging their grave.&amp;quot; without any plan beyond that, she would meet her end fairly quickly.<br /> <br /> Or more likely since I try not to be a dick, run into enough things that she might decide to either change her mind or formulate some kind of plan. Or run into some people that already have a plan just waiting for an epic hero to hinge it on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god no.<br /> <br /> I'm just one person Dr!<br /> <br /> I'm not running five DBs per PC every other session to challenge optimized Solars. There's no way. It's not happening.<br /> <br /> Maybe if I had a team of three assistant STs. Or Exalted didn't play like an 18-ton truck on an ice drift.<br /> <br /> In my Creation, you're not going to run into 25 strong gangs of powerful Terrestrials, precisely spaced to deny you HSF/IfotD/TAP. At least not with any regularity.<br /> <br /> Running nine QC Terrestrials vs a single Solar in this thread as a white room was a chore. I'm not doing that in an actual game.<br /> <br /> And the alternative? Full thousand dooms.<br /> <br /> Today we fight the Kukla. Tomorrow Chejop. Then Leviathan. Then Ma-Ha-Suchi (try not to think about how he lives on the opposite side of the world). Then the second coming of Balor. Then the Yozi escape...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380524#post1380524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't get though, is why you would <i>want </i>to play a character so powerful that they meet no meaningful resistance in anything. Especially to the point where the ST skips 90% of the combats you might find yourself in, which I would think is the reason you took 15 combat charms in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to because it's <i>friggen awesome</i>. I don't want the ST to waste my time and theirs by presenting every insignficant obstacle as twenty minutes of dice rolling. But for pure power fantasy, playing someone who could break Ahlat hits all my buttons.<br /> <br /> I want those 10% of combats to be suitably thematic though. Fights that you might not win. Fights you can definitely win, but at what cost. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> But that's just me. Many, if not most, players don't enjoy that. Or they think they'll enjoy it then get bored two sessions in.<br /> <br /> Which is why I suggest people follow the advice in the book and take 2-5 combat Charms instead of 15. Enjoy tense fights against the dreaded manticore! Experience the thrill of a reversal as you decimate a wolf pack. Test your mettle against Fae beings who can turn your own insecurities against you. Play Exalted.<br /> <br /> Take some social Charms. Take some Sail Charms. Build a character who is cool outside of combat instead of a one-dimensional 15 Charm murder-machine.<br /> <br /> &quot;But Circle of Bright Reaving is really cool!&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, it is really cool. But no-one is going to sit there and roll Initative twenty-six times for an entire Scale of Dragon-Blooded and their Sidereal general. Content yourself with Iron Whirlwind Attack.<br /> <br /> Maybe HDNP/AotR will change that dynamic. Maybe Exalted Essence will.<br /> <br /> But right now, if you want to experience epic battles against legendary foes, you want Dexterity 3 Melee 3 and five combat Charms. If you want to be Saitama, then go all-in -- but unless you are playing a character like Topaz, you really don't need those 5s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T07:08:54-07:00","id":1380647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380591#post1380591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to because it's <i>friggen awesome</i>. I don't want the ST to waste my time and theirs by presenting every insignficant obstacle as twenty minutes of dice rolling. But for pure power fantasy, playing someone who could break Ahlat hits all my buttons.<br /> <br /> I want those 10% of combats to be suitably thematic though. Fights that you might not win. Fights you can definitely win, but at what cost. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> But that's just me. Many, if not most, players don't enjoy that. Or they think they'll enjoy it then get bored two sessions in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the concept of &quot;power fantasy&quot;. Maybe a different way to say the same advice is that most Exalted players should think about what <i>other</i> power fantasies they may be interested in, like flying at 100 miles per hour or healing the wounds of a serious battle in a single day. Most other things the system implements without 20 minutes of dice rolling but also without never rolling the dice at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Experience the thrill of a reversal as you decimate a wolf pack. </div> </div> </div>Do people actually fight wolf packs frequently in Exalted? I've seen it come up a few times on the forums now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Test your mettle against Fae beings who can turn your own insecurities against you. </div> </div> </div>I've actually found Fair Folk Loreleis are actually one of the better enemies in the game to fight against Solars who are on the powerful end in combat (though not fully specced-out war machines), because they attack the character on a different axis where they may be weaker, but their defenses are not high, so the fights are dynamic and quick. Cataphracts are also surprisingly tough, but not as fun to face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take some Sail Charms. </div> </div> </div>This is a good advice although I worry that a lot of the Sail charms have to do with naval combat, and you might run into the same issue there where you're so strong you don't get to use your charms. Still I bet it's not nearly as bad, in part because the naval combat system is much, much easier to run.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T07:45:24-07:00","id":1380652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380647#post1380647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a good advice although I worry that a lot of the Sail charms have to do with naval combat, and you might run into the same issue there where you're so strong you don't get to use your charms. Still I bet it's not nearly as bad, in part because the naval combat system is much, much easier to run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar sail is bonkers. While toying with the idea of an Armored-Karaken Lunar I came to the conclusion she could pretty confidently take on a first-age warship helmed by a decent DB captain, but she would get punked by a solar sail supernal with a merchant barge.<br /> <br /> Sail 5 and 1-2 charms should be fine though, you'll be a better sailor than anyone who isn't a solar but you wont be completely unstoppable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-12-2020, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:39:38-07:00","id":1380661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380652#post1380652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solar sail is bonkers. While toying with the idea of an Armored-Karaken Lunar I came to the conclusion she could pretty confidently take on a first-age warship helmed by a decent DB captain, but she would get punked by a solar sail supernal with a merchant barge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what rules were you looking at to determine this? Is she fighting these ships in Kraken form? Or using Charms? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sail 5 and 1-2 charms should be fine though, you'll be a better sailor than anyone who isn't a solar but you wont be completely unstoppable. </div> </div> </div>If I calculated right a Solar with 5 Wits 5 Sail, a relevant Specialty and Immortal Mariner's Advantage must spend 6 motes to match a Sidereal Sailor with 5 Wits, 5 Sail, a relevant Specialty, and a 4 Motes Sidereal Excellency (assuming no Maneuverability bonus or penalty). So the Sidereal could possibly win a long battle.<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree that this is excellent advice. (Maybe get some more of the not-combat-relevant Sail charms as well). <br /> <br /> The Storyteller could also rely on outnumbering the PCs, which is a lot easier than for ordinary combat if they're all in one ship and a lot more pleasant than in ordinary combat too. It's not like a fleet of 6 ships is unheard of, and trying to beat one solo bestows a -10 penalty. But I agree the players should not build characters capable of that at the start, if only to give them something to ramp up to as the game progresses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:45:31-07:00","id":1380663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380647#post1380647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people actually fight wolf packs frequently in Exalted? I've seen it come up a few times on the forums now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, <i>god no</i>, it's a meme.<br /> <br /> (I used to start all my 2E games with a battle against wolves. I'm pretty sure I'm the only person suggesting fighting them. I suggest it a lot.)<br /> <br /> That said...<br /> <br /> If you start with Dex 3, Melee 3, Medium Weapon... then you have a Parry of 4 (5 with a Stunt) which you can bump to 7 (8) with Excellent Melee.<br /> <br /> If you run the wolves as individual characters, in a pack of 4+, with each wolf spending Willpower, you're rolling 9 (11 with a Stunt) dice + 4 automatic successes against that Parry 4-7 (5-8).<br /> <br /> With Onslaught, you're even likely to land the 6d grapple.<br /> <br /> That's a pretty decent fight right there.<br /> <br /> (Wolves also flee after 4HL, making it easy to drive them off for an opening encounter if things start to go wrong, or if the PCs display a dramatic reversal of fortunes -- which is likely to happen after they pull themselves back together after the initial shock-and-awe.)<br /> <br /> If you can start unlocking Latent abilities on those wolves (Lunar Mistress? Angry Forest King? Wood Outcaste? Wolf-Lord Exigent?) then Hold at Bay and Snarling Guardian Attack/Loyal Guardian gives you the basis of a pretty decent boss fite.<br /> <br /> Wolves are pretty much the perfect starter enemies if you're using characters built like the canon pregens.<br /> <br /> But if you're starting with 15 Melee Charms, Melee/Dex 5, plus Specialty, plus Artifact Weapon and Armor and running the wolves as a battlegroup because you don't think they're narratively signficant enemies... then it's frankly not worth running the combat. &quot;I roll six successes on nine dice, plus four automatic successes, and either still miss else roll a single die of damage... <i>woot</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-12-2020, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T09:26:23-07:00","id":1380675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380663#post1380663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, <i>god no</i>, it's a meme.<br /> <br /> (I used to start all my 2E games with a battle against wolves. I'm pretty sure I'm the only person suggesting fighting them. I suggest it a lot.)<br /> <br /> That said...<br /> <br /> If you start with Dex 3, Melee 3, Medium Weapon... then you have a Parry of 4 (5 with a Stunt) which you can bump to 7 (8) with Excellent Melee.<br /> <br /> If you run the wolves as individual characters, in a pack of 4+, with each wolf spending Willpower, you're rolling 9 (11 with a Stunt) dice + 4 automatic successes against that Parry 4-7 (5-8).<br /> <br /> With Onslaught, you're even likely to land the 6d grapple.<br /> <br /> That's a pretty decent fight right there.<br /> <br /> (Wolves also flee after 4HL, making it easy to drive them off for an opening encounter if things start to go wrong, or if the PCs display a dramatic reversal of fortunes -- which is likely to happen after they pull themselves back together after the initial shock-and-awe.)<br /> <br /> If you can start unlocking Latent abilities on those wolves (Lunar Mistress? Angry Forest King? Wood Outcaste? Wolf-Lord Exigent?) then Hold at Bay and Snarling Guardian Attack/Loyal Guardian gives you the basis of a pretty decent boss fite.<br /> <br /> Wolves are pretty much the perfect starter enemies if you're using characters built like the canon pregens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any justification for not running the wolves as a battlegroup? Do they have wolf names, wolf family relations, and wolf noble titles? Does the lead wolf hold a wolfy grudge against the player characters after one of them stole their deer, and they swore wolf revenge?<br /> <br /> I hope it's clear I just like saying &quot;wolf&quot;...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if you're starting with 15 Melee Charms, Melee/Dex 5, plus Specialty, plus Artifact Weapon and Armor and running the wolves as a battlegroup because you don't think they're narratively signficant enemies... then it's frankly not worth running the combat. &quot;I roll six successes on nine dice, plus four automatic successes, and either still miss else roll a single die of damage... <i>woot</i>.&quot; </div> </div> </div>If you're doing it with Martial Arts, or otherwise don't have the right sorts of mass-attack charms, it's probably even worse to do it without a battlegroup, because you have no chance of defeat but you have to make 10 separate withering attacks and 10 separate decisive attacks or whatever to defeat all the wolves.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And any ST silly enough to send 10 wolves against this character is also silly enough to not have the wolves flee after the first couple get defeated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 04-12-2020, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T09:27:05-07:00","id":1380676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380661#post1380661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what rules were you looking at to determine this? Is she fighting these ships in Kraken form? Or using Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>In kraken form and using charms (Armored Kraken is a Devils Night Parade relase), really only the excellency because lunars dont have any sail charms beyond their general naviagion charms, You can substitute your own dicepools if they're better than an animals as a lunar so you can just roll your own wits + sail + speciality + excellency for up to 23 dice. The kraken form supplies hull levels (assuming an ox-body or two) and weaponry equivalent to a first-age warship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380661#post1380661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I calculated right a Solar with 5 Wits 5 Sail, a relevant Specialty and Immortal Mariner's Advantage must spend 6 motes to match a Sidereal Sailor with 5 Wits, 5 Sail, a relevant Specialty, and a 4 Motes Sidereal Excellency (assuming no Maneuverability bonus or penalty). So the Sidereal could possibly win a long battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but why would you have a long battle? The thing about naval combat is the only thing that really matters is the Positioning roll, and with Immortal Mariner's Advantage + Salty Dog a Wits 5 Sail 5 solar with a speciality and a maneouverability +1 ship averages an absurd 18 successes. Hull levels for anything but first-age ships and armored-kraken lunars are too low to stand up to more than a hit or two.<br /> <br /> Granted sidereals will have their own Sail charms that might let them keep up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-12-2020, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T09:40:18-07:00","id":1380679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380676#post1380676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In kraken form and using charms (Armored Kraken is a Devils Night Parade relase), really only the excellency because lunars dont have any sail charms beyond their general naviagion charms, You can substitute your own dicepools if they're better than an animals as a lunar so you can just roll your own wits + sail + speciality + excellency for up to 23 dice. The kraken form supplies hull levels (assuming an ox-body or two) and weaponry equivalent to a first-age warship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool, I'll check it out whenever I actually end up running a Sail-focused campaign. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah but why would you have a long battle? The thing about naval combat is the only thing that really matters is the Positioning roll, and with Immortal Mariner's Advantage + Salty Dog a Wits 5 Sail 5 solar with a speciality and a maneouverability +1 ship averages an absurd 18 successes. Hull levels for anything but first-age ships and armored-kraken lunars are too low to stand up to more than a hit or two. </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point.The Sidereal will have to bring in five ships of allies to make it a fair fight, I guess.<br /> <br /> This is maybe another good argument for the idea I've heard that it might be more interesting to play God-Blooded with Charms but no Excellencies, forcing you to lean harder on your fun charms (like the Solar Sail ones that enhance a particular naval maneuver) and not the more repetitive excellencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:32:14-07:00","id":1380739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380591#post1380591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh god no.<br /> <br /> I'm just one person Dr!<br /> <br /> I'm not running five DBs per PC every other session to challenge optimized Solars. There's no way. It's not happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah you don't give someone like Shining Topaz a decent exciting combat encounter by just upping the number/power of enemies.<br /> <br /> spoilered for space.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> First you have a DB/Sidereal agent sit with them at the teahouse they're visiting, using social influence to wear them down a bit while the DB medicine charm-enhanced hemlock in her tea is working.<br /> <br /> Then on her way out of town, feeling seriously queasy with poisonous essence coursing through her system the ground falls away under her, an undermined trap built by Terrestrial charms, sorcery, or summoned/allied elementals, at least Short range, maybe deeper, and seeded with buried steel blades. Let's say it's a Medium range fall, but even through her mobility penalized, poison penalty suffering roll she reduces it to Short and saves herself the Lethal damage from the blades at the same time. So we've got 2 dice of lethal from the Hemlock, 3 bashing levels from the fall and 5 bashing dice from the fall so far.<br /> <br /> Now Shining Topaz is in kind of a bad way, suffering from poison and wound penalties, at the bottom of a deep hole, with almost no health left. Maybe some Imperial battlefield engineers start collapsing the hole in on itself or something, but let's say they don't do that. So Shining Topaz climbs out using Monkey Leap Technique and her Daiklave, pissed off and wondering who has the balls.<br /> <br /> That's when arrows start flying from the woods, mounted dragonblooded archers who are ignoring the effects of the underbrush on both their archery attacks and difficult terrain on their movement lead Topaz on a chase through the woods. Topaz having to use willpower based charms to keep up with them, or fight against a -4 hemlock penalty, -3 difficult terrain penalty, -2/-4 wound penalty and -2 mobility penalty. Assuming the archers don't peg her with Life Swelling Sap arrows to increase the mobility penalty even further.<br /> <br /> All of that is just a trap though, the archers know they can't win against someone like Topaz, that's why they're leading her to a clearing to be surrounded by a size 3 battlegroup of elite soldiers, lead by a Dragonblooded commander and supported at range by the woodland archers. Then the Sidereal hit squad shows up....<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, maybe not that last part. Either way, after all of that is done Topaz is probably sitting in the forest, sick, badly wounded, full of arrows, and thinking that maybe this isn't going to be quite as easy as she thought. Maybe she even needs to gather some like minded Solar allies and/or meet up with some Lunar resistance fighters to pool their ideas. Or maybe she decides that surely that MUST be the only defense they could muster, and merrily continues on her way with the assumption that the throne now stands unguarded. In which case no mercy next time.<br /> <br /> <br /> If it's a game with a full circle of Solars, it becomes a lot easier, because I assume if somebody is going to go down it isn't Topaz, just like I assume if somebody is going to fall prey to the wiles of a Fair Folk Lorelei it isn't the Integrity Supernal chaste Zenith. That does put a bit more pressure on Topaz though, since it's her job to keep that Integrity Supernal Zenith safe in combat, she has to go hard on offense not just defense.<br /> <br /> Unless it's a full circle of Shining Topaz, in which case I would probably suggest we use Godsend or whatever. A system where the mechanics are actually designed so that a character can say &quot;First thing I'm going to topple the Realm, then split the Blessed Isle down the middle, making two big islands in the center of the world. From there I'm going to shunt all the remaining Dynasty onto one, and the Lunar dominions can have the other. They can visit, but any kind of assassins or invasion fleet will be turned into pillars of basalt as a monument to their new enforced non-aggression.&quot; and do that all dicelessly and automatically.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380591#post1380591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;But Circle of Bright Reaving is really cool!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a problem. Becoming a character that spends his nights weeping because there are no foes in the world who can match him, or has a near permanent vacant stare of ennui because nothing in life is interesting anymore shouldn't be a hidden feature of otherwise cool/fun looking charms and abilities. Ascendant Battle Visage looks so god damned cool, but I can't take it because then the ST will just skip almost every combat scene with a &quot;Yup, you are victorious, next scene.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:15:38-07:00","id":1380749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380675#post1380675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any justification for not running the wolves as a battlegroup?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically just to make it more dangerous/fun. Having a 3 round combat against a wolf pack where individual characters get to Crashing Wave Throw one wolf into another, or feathering one with arrows that's currently got it's jaws clamped around your ward.<br /> <br /> It's Exalted, a world of mythic high fantasy. You've got tidal waves that look like <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/30/3b/64/303b648080afad4fb57a23615ffd3368.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, wolves that look like <a href=\"https://i.redd.it/tovm6b4wh1331.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, bears that look like <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/54caefd342c5a93577105b22867cb51b/tumblr_pamtispV4Q1ssokpeo1_1280.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, naval battles that look like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aobNxeft_no\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, cities that look like <a href=\"https://db4sgowjqfwig.cloudfront.net/campaigns/166462/assets/797750/1_Palaquin.jpg?1510327461\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. That last one is even official Exalted art for the city of Palanquin. The Exalted are big, powerful epic characters in a world that's likewise huge and epic. Hurricanes exist in Creation the likes of which have never happened in the span of human life on Earth, so like, more than <a href=\"https://youtu.be/unV5KcSrY-I?t=132\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> Unless we're content to say that Pirates of the Caribbean, Dungeons and Dragons, and Game of Thrones have more epic fantasy settings than Exalted does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:31:12-07:00","id":1380754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380749#post1380749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically just to make it more dangerous/fun. Having a 3 round combat against a wolf pack where individual characters get to Crashing Wave Throw one wolf into another, or feathering one with arrows that's currently got it's jaws clamped around your ward.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes total sense, but is it following the rules as written?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Battle groups are an abstraction used whenever there are more than two combatants on the battlefield who are reasonably similar to one another in terms of capabilities and equipment, who aren\u2019t especially noteworthy to the story as individuals, and who aren\u2019t potent supernatural beings </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">such as Exalt </span></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you're going to say we should not follow that rule, or at least not take it literally. I guess that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's Exalted, a world of mythic high fantasy. You've got tidal waves that look like <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/30/3b/64/303b648080afad4fb57a23615ffd3368.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, wolves that look like <a href=\"https://i.redd.it/tovm6b4wh1331.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, bears that look like <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/54caefd342c5a93577105b22867cb51b/tumblr_pamtispV4Q1ssokpeo1_1280.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, naval battles that look like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aobNxeft_no\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, cities that look like <a href=\"https://db4sgowjqfwig.cloudfront.net/campaigns/166462/assets/797750/1_Palaquin.jpg?1510327461\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. That last one is even official Exalted art for the city of Palanquin. The Exalted are big, powerful epic characters in a world that's likewise huge and epic. Hurricanes exist in Creation the likes of which have never happened in the span of human life on Earth, so like, more than <a href=\"https://youtu.be/unV5KcSrY-I?t=132\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> Unless we're content to say that Pirates of the Caribbean, Dungeons and Dragons, and Game of Thrones have more epic fantasy settings than Exalted does. </div> </div> </div>I actually don't see how this is relevant to the point of if you should run wolves as a battlegroup - maybe you could explain it to me?<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a problem. Becoming a character that spends his nights weeping because there are no foes in the world who can match him, or has a near permanent vacant stare of ennui because nothing in life is interesting anymore shouldn't be a hidden feature of otherwise cool/fun looking charms and abilities. Ascendant Battle Visage looks so god damned cool, but I can't take it because then the ST will just skip almost every combat scene with a &quot;Yup, you are victorious, next scene.&quot; </div> </div> </div>This is a great way of explaining it. </span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 04-12-2020, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:32:04-07:00","id":1380755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.