aybe deeper, and seeded with buried steel blades. Let's say it's a Medium range fall, but even through her mobility penalized, poison penalty suffering roll she reduces it to Short and saves herself the Lethal damage from the blades at the same time. So we've got 2 dice of lethal from the Hemlock, 3 bashing levels from the fall and 5 bashing dice from the fall so far.<br /> <br /> Now Shining Topaz is in kind of a bad way, suffering from poison and wound penalties, at the bottom of a deep hole, with almost no health left. Maybe some Imperial battlefield engineers start collapsing the hole in on itself or something, but let's say they don't do that. So Shining Topaz climbs out using Monkey Leap Technique and her Daiklave, pissed off and wondering who has the balls.<br /> <br /> That's when arrows start flying from the woods, mounted dragonblooded archers who are ignoring the effects of the underbrush on both their archery attacks and difficult terrain on their movement lead Topaz on a chase through the woods. Topaz having to use willpower based charms to keep up with them, or fight against a -4 hemlock penalty, -3 difficult terrain penalty, -2/-4 wound penalty and -2 mobility penalty. Assuming the archers don't peg her with Life Swelling Sap arrows to increase the mobility penalty even further.<br /> <br /> All of that is just a trap though, the archers know they can't win against someone like Topaz, that's why they're leading her to a clearing to be surrounded by a size 3 battlegroup of elite soldiers, lead by a Dragonblooded commander and supported at range by the woodland archers. Then the Sidereal hit squad shows up....<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, maybe not that last part. Either way, after all of that is done Topaz is probably sitting in the forest, sick, badly wounded, full of arrows, and thinking that maybe this isn't going to be quite as easy as she thought. Maybe she even needs to gather some like minded Solar allies and/or meet up with some Lunar resistance fighters to pool their ideas. Or maybe she decides that surely that MUST be the only defense they could muster, and merrily continues on her way with the assumption that the throne now stands unguarded. In which case no mercy next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't actually need Topaz to be seeking the throne for the Wyld Hunt to try this shit. That she is a solar sufficies to provide cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:52:36-07:00","id":1380759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380754#post1380754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes total sense, but is it following the rules as written?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I guess you're going to say we should not follow that rule, or at least not take it literally. I guess that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Battle groups are an abstraction used whenever there are more than two combatants on the battlefield who are reasonably similar to one another in terms of capabilities and equipment, who aren\u2019t <b>especially noteworthy to the story as individuals</b>, and who aren\u2019t potent supernatural beings </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">such as Exalt</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What makes a character noteworthy to the story?<br /> <br /> If the story is &quot;the Exalted face a challenging combat encounter&quot;, then the characters involved in that combat are, by default, noteworthy individuals. They're challenging the Exalted Protagonists.<br /> <br /> Likewise if the story is &quot;the Exalted breeze over a horde of NPCs&quot;, then the characters involved in that combat are, by default, not noteworthy individuals. They're mooks getting mowed down.<br /> <br /> Does not the Core also say:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Battle groups are there to reduce the Storyteller\u2019s workload</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:09:59-07:00","id":1380764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380754#post1380754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes total sense, but is it following the rules as written?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you're going to say we should not follow that rule, or at least not take it literally. I guess that makes sense.[/QUOTE]<br /> There's an <i>awful </i>lot of creatures in the corebook and Hundred Devil Night Parade that serve as antagonists, but have abilities that are either really unsuited to battlegroup formation, or outright impossible to use.<br /> <br /> Pack Hunting, for example, just doesn't do anything for creatures all massed up in a battlegroup, so why have it? You might say &quot;Well, because as a latent feature it can be unlocked for use with non-wolves when they're a familiar.&quot; but why not just make it a latent feature exclusively then? Even more telling is Silverwights, that can't be summoned or bound or anything, have the feature but no latent ability to use it with anything else. Sometimes you have a swarm of silverwights attacking because of the birthing cries of a pregnant woman, then you run them individually. Sometimes a massive army of the Wyld marches upon creation with hundreds of silverwights, and more, under the command of a noble fairy, then you run them as a battlegroup with elite drill.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380754#post1380754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't see how this is relevant to the point of if you should run wolves as a battlegroup - maybe you could explain it to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically wolves in Exalted can be big and scary enough to be essentially monsters on their own. To the point where taking the time to actually duke it out with them individually is warranted. Not to the point where your characters are in any serious danger, but yes to the point where it's a fun combat that illustrates how dangerous this area of the woods really is.<br /> <br /> If they're particularly big and scary you might even give the wolf statline a bump to represent truly dire wolves. Maybe a pack leader is even a god-blooded wolf, progeny of the god of wolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380755#post1380755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't actually need Topaz to be seeking the throne for the Wyld Hunt to try this shit. That she is a solar sufficies to provide cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I wouldn't want to unleash that kind of competent Wyld Hunt on players who weren't basically asking to have it happen. The Hunt is supposed to be diminished from what it once was, giving players the idea that they should do their best to keep their heads down, but also have enough breathing room that not every single campaign is just a trap of constant fear that every teahouse attendant is a secret agent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:29:29-07:00","id":1380769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380739#post1380739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, maybe not that last part. Either way, after all of that is done Topaz is probably sitting in the forest, sick, badly wounded, full of arrows, and thinking that maybe this isn't going to be quite as easy as she thought. Maybe she even needs to gather some like minded Solar allies and/or meet up with some Lunar resistance fighters to pool their ideas. Or maybe she decides that surely that MUST be the only defense they could muster, and merrily continues on her way with the assumption that the throne now stands unguarded. In which case no mercy next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that most games are not one-on-one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380739#post1380739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's a game with a full circle of Solars, it becomes a lot easier, because I assume if somebody is going to go down it isn't Topaz, just like I assume if somebody is going to fall prey to the wiles of a Fair Folk Lorelei it isn't the Integrity Supernal chaste Zenith. That does put a bit more pressure on Topaz though, since it's her job to keep that Integrity Supernal Zenith safe in combat, she has to go hard on offense not just defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lethality problem here, whereby the foes that can challenge the rest of the Circle can't challenge Topaz.<br /> <br /> And the foes that can challenge Topaz, make the rest of the party want to level up to avoid getting splatted. Which, in my experience, inevitably leads us to...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380739#post1380739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it's a full circle of Shining Topaz, in which case I would probably suggest we use Godsend or whatever. A system where the mechanics are actually designed so that a character can say &quot;First thing I'm going to topple the Realm, then split the Blessed Isle down the middle, making two big islands in the center of the world. From there I'm going to shunt all the remaining Dynasty onto one, and the Lunar dominions can have the other. They can visit, but any kind of assassins or invasion fleet will be turned into pillars of basalt as a monument to their new enforced non-aggression.&quot; and do that all dicelessly and automatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>At which point your advice becomes &quot;don't play Exalted&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let me be clear: this is not bad advice. But my advice is based around &quot;how do you keep playing Exalted at this level&quot;.<br /> <br /> (I've always advocated using Wild Talents or Mutants and Masterminds instead. I have no strong opinion on Godsend, but I trust that it'd work just fine. You have a great grasp of Exalted's mechanics, I trust your opinion.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380739#post1380739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah you don't give someone like Shining Topaz a decent exciting combat encounter by just upping the number/power of enemies.<br /> <br /> First you have a DB/Sidereal agent sit with them at the teahouse they're visiting, using social influence to wear them down a bit while the DB medicine charm-enhanced hemlock in her tea is working.</div> </div> </div> </div>And are you not giving Topaz Awareness rolls to notice this poison? Or Resistance rolls to shrug it off?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380739#post1380739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then on her way out of town, feeling seriously queasy with poisonous essence coursing through her system the ground falls away under her, an undermined trap built by Terrestrial charms, sorcery, or summoned/allied elementals, at least Short range, maybe deeper, and seeded with buried steel blades. Let's say it's a Medium range fall, but even through her mobility penalized, poison penalty suffering roll she reduces it to Short and saves herself the Lethal damage from the blades at the same time. So we've got 2 dice of lethal from the Hemlock, 3 bashing levels from the fall and 5 bashing dice from the fall so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't feel <i>too </i>bad if I fell in a pit by ST fiat.<br /> <br /> But again, I expect some kind of roll to avoid. And I'm finding it hard to think of a roll that wouldn't leave Topaz down motes instead of health levels.<br /> <br /> (It feels a bit Wiley Coyote to fall into a pit of blades and be able to slow your fall but not avoid the pit all together.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380739#post1380739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now Shining Topaz is in kind of a bad way, suffering from poison and wound penalties, at the bottom of a deep hole, with almost no health left. Maybe some Imperial battlefield engineers start collapsing the hole in on itself or something, but let's say they don't do that. So Shining Topaz climbs out using Monkey Leap Technique and her Daiklave, pissed off and wondering who has the balls.<br /> <br /> That's when arrows start flying from the woods, mounted dragonblooded archers who are ignoring the effects of the underbrush on both their archery attacks and difficult terrain on their movement lead Topaz on a chase through the woods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Topaz just goes back inside the tea-house though, right?<br /> <br /> So these Archers are at, what, Medium range? Aiming at the pit, firing then riding off to Long range through difficult terrain?<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't Topaz just Withdraw at this point?<br /> <br /> How, realisticly, is Topaz supposed to catch the archers at this point?<br /> <br /> What dicepools are these archer's using? 5 Dex + 5 Archery + 1 Specialty + 3 Artifact = 14d? Against Topaz's Parry? Is this a battlegroup of Terrestrial Archers adding Size and Might to these rolls? Or are we relying on weight of numbers to get a lucky shot or two in? I assume the horses are immune to Terrestrial anima, because these Deebs are going to be blowing a lot of motes.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't do this.<br /> <br /> What I would do to challenge Topaz, would look very much like this.<br /> <br /> How many archers are we talking here? Two? Three? I said I didn't want to run 5 DBs per PC (having run 9 against a Solar earlier in this thread). It's too much work.<br /> <br /> So three Archers and a Poisoner at the tea house?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380739#post1380739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Topaz having to use willpower based charms to keep up with them, or fight against a -4 hemlock penalty, -3 difficult terrain penalty, -2/-4 wound penalty and -2 mobility penalty. Assuming the archers don't peg her with Life Swelling Sap arrows to increase the mobility penalty even further.<br /> <br /> All of that is just a trap though, the archers know they can't win against someone like Topaz, that's why they're leading her to a clearing to be surrounded by a size 3 battlegroup of elite soldiers, lead by a Dragonblooded commander and supported at range by the woodland archers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now how many DBs are we up to? Five and a battlegroup?<br /> <br /> I said I didn't want to run five DBs per PC.<br /> <br /> This is a very intelligent way of running five DBs per PC. It's exciting. It's interesting. It presents ever escalating stakes (and thus the ability to dial down if it looks like we're heading for a TPK). The Solar can't immediately win with TAP+HSF. This is exactly the kind of thing I'd run if I wanted to try and beat down an optimized Solar.<br /> <br /> But it's too much work for one PC. And it's impossible to run for a Circle of five PCs. (Well, not <i>impossible</i>: run the DB Archers as a battlegroup and have them rain arrows on all the PCs. One poisoner can poison all the PCs. Etc.)<br /> <br /> You've given a great scenario, but it doesn't change my basic complaint.<br /> <br /> And, be honest, how many times do you expect this to work?<br /> <br /> Because I would immediately start buying Charms to become immune to poison after the first time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T15:54:34-07:00","id":1380782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380769#post1380769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the foes that can challenge Topaz, make the rest of the party want to level up to avoid getting splatted. Which, in my experience, inevitably leads us to...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally you're not actually going super pita-nutso and killing characters left and right, both because your PCs are smart enough not to march into Hell and piss on an effigy of Ligier under the assumption that they can never be killed ever, and also because you as the ST give your party appropriate obstacles to overcome. As long as you don't get to the point where even Shining Topaz can't protect her circle, hopefully everyone isn't going to feel the need to all re-roll as Dawns.<br /> <br /> That's easier said than done, of course, since a lot of players will just do it anyway because it's so easy, but that's a different problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380769#post1380769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I've always advocated using Wild Talents or Mutants and Masterminds instead. I have no strong opinion on Godsend, but I trust that it'd work just fine. You have a great grasp of Exalted's mechanics, I trust your opinion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always found Mutants and Masterminds to be just a touch too generic for my tastes, but I can see the appeal. Although I'm not sure if PCs are getting the same level of &quot;Untouchable gods playing in a world of ants&quot; that you'd get from Godsend and Exalted without crazy opposition. Maybe if you just put a limit on the Power Level of enemies?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380769#post1380769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And are you not giving Topaz Awareness rolls to notice this poison? Or Resistance rolls to shrug it off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, for sure, but with Poisoner's Deft Hand the difficulty to fully resist it is something like 7, and she's taking penalties on the roll to notice it due do the superhumanly engaging conversation. Other Solars would notice it in an instant with their awareness charms, but Topaz isn't built like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380769#post1380769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't feel <i>too </i>bad if I fell in a pit by ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Topaz is suffering from hemlock poisoning her (Dexterity + Dodge) pool to leap off a crumbling flat of earth is like, 2 with her armor's mobility penalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380769#post1380769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Topaz just goes back inside the tea-house though, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but then you could just burn down the teahouse and leave her in a massive bonfire. It's not like the Wyld Hunt hasn't razed entire villages to the ground to kill anathema before. She'll break out at that point, duh, but then she either runs with the hunt chasing her down, or chases the hunt down which is what they want anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380769#post1380769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So these Archers are at, what, Medium range? Aiming at the pit, firing then riding off to Long range through difficult terrain?<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't Topaz just Withdraw at this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually thinking at Short range, although maybe spread out wide and willing to split up. If one of them gets caught unable to withdraw, somehow, that's a sacrifice willing to be made against the strongest foe the Realm will ever face.<br /> <br /> If she withdraws the archers can just ride her down and keep shooting. If she sprints down the road there's no guarantee it isn't laden with more surprises, and into the woods you're fleeing through difficult terrain against mounted archers that ignore the difficult terrain. The Wyld Hunt doesn't win by playing fair. The arrows might even be dipped in Arrow Frog venom or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm imagining basically this, a high ranking Bronze Faction Sidereal throws a report down at a meeting in the Bureau with Kejak stating, simply, &quot;Shining Topaz is the single greatest threat to the Dragonblooded hegemony, and perhaps even Creation itself. If she succeeds in taking over the Realm, the greatest power in the world will be under the control of a nearly invincible, completely reckless Solar who represents everything that triggered the Usurpation in the first place.&quot; and then imagining what force they might muster to stop it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380769#post1380769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How, realisticly, is Topaz supposed to catch the archers at this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking you could TAP into close range, then Peony Blossom for another withering attack, then Invincible Fury of the Dawn to deal decisive damage, spending enough motes to Peony blossom again or something. It's maybe, barely, doable. It might be better to stop sometime before that, depending on what Shining Topaz has done up to that point to prompt such an overwhelming response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380769#post1380769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now how many DBs are we up to? Five and a battlegroup?<br /> <br /> I said I didn't want to run five DBs per PC.<br /> <br /> And, be honest, how many times do you expect this to work?<br /> <br /> Because I would immediately start buying Charms to become immune to poison after the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's 5 plus a battlegroup, but there's just one social scene, one combat scene chasing the archers, and then another combat scene with two actors, plus any remaining archers. It's something that I think might actually just kill Topaz, but if a full circle was involved I bet they could get through it. If they were on their way to go lay siege to the Imperial City all on their lonesome though it might give them an idea of exactly how big a task that is, and something that might require more finesse and time than a single session.<br /> <br /> That was 5 Dragonblooded, an elemental, and a tiny fraction of their mortal soldiers, the Imperial City has hundreds of dragonblooded and thousands of soldiers, with guardian spirits, artifact constructs, spies, assassins, ancient magic, astrological blessings, elder Sidereal agents and more. This is what it feels like to fight the whole world at once, and why even the might of the Solar Exalted doesn't let you faceroll effortlessly over any and all opposition. With some careful application, connections, and time, it might be enough strength to topple the Realm though, which is something you could forge a campaign around.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you could also say that because of that toppling the Realm is maybe not the first thing you want to do, or even something you need to do at all, and either freeing a satrapy from the clutches of the Empire, or battling the forces of death in Thorns, or sitting in a lonely Threshold town on the boarders of Creation holding off chaos might be something you can get into. At least as a first step.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course if you want as an ST you could also fast track it. Some redobut deep in the Threshold somewhere has a teleporter that gets you right to the control room of the Imperial Manse, and the Empress left it all in perfect working order, so you just flip the switch, fire it at Thorns, tell everyone you're the new Empress. It might work and that could be accomplished without even taking the whole session. Then move on to the fact that each direction is being assaulted by a new Primordial out of the Wyld and what do we do now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T16:13:01-07:00","id":1380784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380782#post1380782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively you could also say that because of that toppling the Realm is maybe not the first thing you want to do, or even something you need to do at all, and either freeing a satrapy from the clutches of the Empire, or battling the forces of death in Thorns, or sitting in a lonely Threshold town on the boarders of Creation holding off chaos might be something you can get into. At least as a first step.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld idea might be an important suggestion, because as far as I know the forces of the Wyld are the main foe in Creation whose powers are completely undefined.<br /> <br /> One option for a powerful Solar who found it nearly impossible to find a foe they couldn't beat in one-on-one battle, but wasn't foolhardy enough to take on the entire Realm at once, would be to find a Solar who knows Wyld-Shaping Technique, head off into the Wyld, and protect them from the Wyld creatures that appear to attack them. As far as I know, when you use Wyld-Shaping Technique, you are attacked by Wyld creatures, with the difficulty increasing as you continue to use the Charm, but otherwise undefined by the setting. I guess a wise ST would declare that (1) the number of enemy creatures or battlegroups appearing in each phase is whatever number they feel comfortable running, (2) the complexity of these enemy's special abilities is whatever level they prefer, and (3) the stats of the enemies keeps increasing until they reach a point where they challenge the Solars by an amount they are happy with, then exceed it. Of course their description of the enemies should increase appropriately in awesomeness - I'm not saying to just raise all the dice pools of a hobgoblin by 3 points each round, but rather to pass from hobgoblins and loreleis to cataphracts to strange raksha nobles to stranger beasts to behemoths to behomoths that feed on those behemoths like whales feed on plankton, if that's what it takes to challenge Topaz and her friends.<br /> <br /> Might this be a better approach if someone, for some reason, wants to take every Melee Charm in the book and then use them in combat?<br /> <br /> Of course if Topaz is traveling with a Circle of Solars built like the Tomb of Dreams characters this will probably not result in everyone having a fun time at once, but if we stipulate that our players all build optimized characters, would this be a way to entertain them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T16:45:45-07:00","id":1380790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380784#post1380784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyld-Shaping Technique,</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this this an idea fit for the Arena. I have Mata-Yadh, are there any other behemoths published yet that I should look up for this sort of thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:08:04-07:00","id":1380793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380790#post1380790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now this this an idea fit for the Arena. I have Mata-Yadh, are there any other behemoths published yet that I should look up for this sort of thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mahicara is the only other published behemoth I think so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:13:12-07:00","id":1380794,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I guess I could refluff various Warstriders as Behemoths. Any fan behemoths availiable I could use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:18:42-07:00","id":1380795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380784#post1380784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might this be a better approach if someone, for some reason, wants to take every Melee Charm in the book and then use them in combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly could be another option. There's also Hell, where Ligier the Green Sun is said to be somewhere equal in combat to The Unconquered Sun, along with an almost, perhaps literal, endless supply of other demons. The entire united Exalted Host, with the support of Autocthon and Gaia warred against the Primordials before, one chargen character shouldn't really be up to doing the same, so you'll eventually find some balance point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:28:07-07:00","id":1380797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380794#post1380794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I guess I could refluff various Warstriders as Behemoths. Any fan behemoths availiable I could use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, well I made one kinda, once. It's completely untested though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1356871#post1356871\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1356871#post1356871\"> The After-shock war, in the Age of Sorrows - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1356871#post1356871\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1356871#post1356871 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Many thanks to Omicron of SB, whom I cant seem to contact https://forums.spacebattles.com/thre...#post-12209803 (https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/general </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:51:21-07:00","id":1380807,"title":"","content":"TBH, if I did bring topaz to the table, being actually challenged in combat would be a sometimes food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T18:01:47-07:00","id":1380811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380807#post1380807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBH, if I did bring topaz to the table, being actually challenged in combat would be a sometimes food.</div> </div> </div> </div>That should probably be true for any game. Winning all the time by the enemies never, ever hitting you, and you always, always one-shotting everything you point at is dull, and repetitive. Likewise every single fight being a desperate scramble where you just barely hang on and have to constantly remember everything your character has to take advantage of any changing scenario is also repetitive, and stressful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T18:14:49-07:00","id":1380814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380795#post1380795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It certainly could be another option. There's also Hell, where Ligier the Green Sun is said to be somewhere equal in combat to The Unconquered Sun, along with an almost, perhaps literal, endless supply of other demons. The entire united Exalted Host, with the support of Autocthon and Gaia warred against the Primordials before, one chargen character shouldn't really be up to doing the same, so you'll eventually find some balance point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I don't like about this is it's not clear what doing it would actually accomplish. A Wyld-shaping campaign would be very odd but you would mix venturing into the Wyld to create land with meeting the people in the land you created, trying to organize them into some kind of government, and solving lesser problems they might have. It sounds very hard to ST properly but possibly quite fun.<br /> <br /> I'm still more excites about doing a low-combat-power-level-solars or not-solars campaign (possibly even God-Blooded), but it's fun to speculate about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T18:15:57-07:00","id":1380815,"title":"","content":"So I'm reading Mahicara, and I don't think Topaz can beat him alone. Even if she can get enough initiative to buzzsaw its limbs and torso to bits, they'll regen by the time she rebuilds enough initiative to get at the head. Not even the most generous reading of Heaven Sword Flash will let you hit both the legs and the head of a thing that's a mile tall. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380811#post1380811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That should probably be true for any game. Winning all the time by the enemies never, ever hitting you, and you always, always one-shotting everything you point at is dull, and repetitive. Likewise every single fight being a desperate scramble where you just barely hang on and have to constantly remember everything your character has to take advantage of any changing scenario is also repetitive, and stressful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most challenges for Topaz should be social. She has intimacies and a character. Getting instruction in Fire Dragon Style is something she wants really badly, because it's a form of swordsmanship she wants to master. She's also a known Anathema, so actually getting that instruction is a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T18:39:56-07:00","id":1380817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380814#post1380814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only thing I don't like about this is it's not clear what doing it would actually accomplish. A Wyld-shaping campaign would be very odd but you would mix venturing into the Wyld to create land with meeting the people in the land you created, trying to organize them into some kind of government, and solving lesser problems they might have. It sounds very hard to ST properly but possibly quite fun.<br /> <br /> I'm still more excites about doing a low-combat-power-level-solars or not-solars campaign (possibly even God-Blooded), but it's fun to speculate about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you were going into Hell to kill everything that's not a great campaign. It's kind of aimless. Going into Hell to convince a third circle demon there to forge a literal soul patch for your friend who got half-killed by a soulbreaker orb, and then having the option to scale up the stakes into fighting the Unconquered Sun level enemies is a better way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380815#post1380815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most challenges for Topaz should be social. She has intimacies and a character. Getting instruction in Fire Dragon Style is something she wants really badly, because it's a form of swordsmanship she wants to master. She's also a known Anathema, so actually getting that instruction is a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a much better way to go. Or even just any concept that doesn't encourage your character to immediately kill any problems they come across. From what I know of Dace and Volfer they basically just do that, but Demetheus actually seems like somebody who could punch almost anyone clean in half, but decides not to for not entirely selfish reasons.<br /> <br /> Although, as a Dawn, Topaz could just learn Fire Dragon Style out of nowhere just by wanting to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T19:43:51-07:00","id":1380831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380815#post1380815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm reading Mahicara, and I don't think Topaz can beat him alone. Even if she can get enough initiative to buzzsaw its limbs and torso to bits, they'll regen by the time she rebuilds enough initiative to get at the head. Not even the most generous reading of Heaven Sword Flash will let you hit both the legs and the head of a thing that's a mile tall.</div> </div> </div> </div>She'll have to stick to half-mile-tall behemoths for now, I guess.<br /> <br /> (If you're going to use warstriders as behemoths, maybe start with the walking devil tower, an ex-behemoth?) You could throw an appropriate lunar character in there to fill out its stats, although dealing with the Limit counting may be tricky.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most challenges for Topaz should be social. She has intimacies and a character. Getting instruction in Fire Dragon Style is something she wants really badly, because it's a form of swordsmanship she wants to master. She's also a known Anathema, so actually getting that instruction is a story. </div> </div> </div>I'm amused by imagining the scene:<br /> <br /> Topaz, surrounded by Immaculate monks. Most are dead, a few are bleeding out, and will be dead soon. &quot;So as I was SAYING, despite my obviously superior sword-fighting skills, I think I could learn a lot from you people. If you could just get over your irrational prejudices... Ah well, maybe the next monastery will do better. See you!&quot;<br /> <br /> I know you would probably not take this strategy ingame.... (Could she enlist a sorcerer to fly her thousands of miles away where the monks not might recognize this particular Anathema, and try to join, disguising her nature for as long as possible?) <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380817#post1380817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, if you were going into Hell to kill everything that's not a great campaign. It's kind of aimless. Going into Hell to convince a third circle demon there to forge a literal soul patch for your friend who got half-killed by a soulbreaker orb, and then having the option to scale up the stakes into fighting the Unconquered Sun level enemies is a better way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll keep that in mind...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that's a much better way to go. Or even just any concept that doesn't encourage your character to immediately kill any problems they come across. From what I know of Dace and Volfer they basically just do that, but Demetheus actually seems like somebody who could punch almost anyone clean in half, but decides not to for not entirely selfish reasons. </div> </div> </div>This is one reason I don't like the Volfer fiction in the core book. Walk into a room to beat people up for no reason is not how I, personally, would enact my war against the Realm. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although, as a Dawn, Topaz could just learn Fire Dragon Style out of nowhere just by wanting to. </div> </div> </div>Where is this written?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T21:09:30-07:00","id":1380854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380831#post1380831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one reason I don't like the Volfer fiction in the core book. Walk into a room to beat people up for no reason is not how I, personally, would enact my war against the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember from the castebooks the Bull of the North and Dace were both kind of like that too. Lyta was definitely like that but she was also written to be an insane villain. Demetheus didn't like the Realm, for pretty obvious reasons, but didn't actually hate Dynasts, just evil people in general, which too often included Dynasts. For that matter he didn't like Solars who declared themselves immortal god-kings either, thinking they were arrogant and foolish, and debating if the Userpation was justified or not.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure he didn't even want to be the king of anything. He just wanted to wander around finding people who needed help with either his divine athletics or his big meaty fists, and then move on to the next people. Coupled though with the realities that he has to eat, and grew up winning bareknuckle boxing tournaments, so he frequently bets tough guys that he can beat the crap out of them, and then proceeds to do so without trying to hurt them too bad.<br /> <br /> He's just a <i>good, </i>if imperfect, guy who isn't letting his strength go to his head, and doing what he does best. I would love it if more of my PC Dawns were like that.<br /> <br /> He had a pretty good demi-character arc too in the comics. First just hanging out with his circle because they seemed like okay people for the most part. Then after a douchebag monk thrust his fist into Kidale* and killed him he went into a big mopey slump because he fucking <i>liked</i> Kidale.<br /> <br /> *which might ultimately have been a good thing since Kidale was going a bit bonkers with his past-life memories. Saying things like &quot;Now is the time for our vengeance! I will slay all!&quot; in his head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380831#post1380831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this written?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to my foggy recollection in 2e you needed a sifu to learn martial arts from, but with the caveat that Solars could use basically anything as their sifu. Like you could look at a housecat and learn Tiger Style, or look at a candle and learn Fire Dragon all on your own. In 3e I don't think the stipulation that you need a sifu for anything exists, you can just buy dots of an ability or charms by investing in training times. So for a Dawn with MA favoured you can pick up the ability dots in a few days, dual training charms and dots after the first couple of dots if you want.<br /> <br /> In theory Topaz could just light a candle or a campfire and look at it going &quot;Huh, so that's how fire is.&quot; and master Fire Dragon over a fortnight. That makes for a pretty bland story though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also something that I think was dropped in 3e was the idea that in the world of martial arts you always respected your master, even former master. Which lead to cool things like a Solar master martial artist carefully bowing and paying respects to his aged, first mortal sifu. Anyone who didn't show such respect was basically an automatic villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-13-2020, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T21:24:26-07:00","id":1380857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380854#post1380854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory Topaz could just light a candle or a campfire and look at it going &quot;Huh, so that's how fire is.&quot; and master Fire Dragon over a fortnight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I refuse. That's a terrible narrative. At least go delving into lost shogunate ruins for Immaculate Martial Art Style Manuals. Barter with the Silver Pact to acquire one of their captured copies. Break into Yu-Shan and beg the god of swords to teach you. Any of those is a better story than fucking off into the middle of nowhere and just looking at a candle and figuring how to sword good from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T22:53:48-07:00","id":1380870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380857#post1380857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I refuse. That's a terrible narrative. At least go delving into lost shogunate ruins for Immaculate Martial Art Style Manuals. Barter with the Silver Pact to acquire one of their captured copies. Break into Yu-Shan and beg the god of swords to teach you. Any of those is a better story than fucking off into the middle of nowhere and just looking at a candle and figuring how to sword good from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say definitely. Unfortunately a lot of the players I've had in the past disagree. Having to be beholden to a sifu to learn something when you could just be awesome and make it up yourself, the choice is obvious. That goes double if the person their learning from is a lower class of being, like a spirit, or a DB or Heaven forbid a mortal.<br /> <br /> Thankfully the one player I've had in 3e who really went hard into MA actually decided he'd go seeking out a Sifu to learn him in Single Point style after he got 1v1'd by a DB princess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T23:23:51-07:00","id":1380872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380870#post1380870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say definitely. Unfortunately a lot of the players I've had in the past disagree. Having to be beholden to a sifu to learn something when you could just be awesome and make it up yourself, the choice is obvious. That goes double if the person their learning from is a lower class of being, like a spirit, or a DB or Heaven forbid a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, but, but... humbling yourself before a master is such a massive trope. What is WRONG with these people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I remember from the castebooks the Bull of the North and Dace were both kind of like that too. Lyta was definitely like that but she was also written to be an insane villain. Demetheus didn't like the Realm, for pretty obvious reasons, but didn't actually hate Dynasts, just evil people in general, which too often included Dynasts. For that matter he didn't like Solars who declared themselves immortal god-kings either, thinking they were arrogant and foolish, and debating if the Userpation was justified or not. </div> </div> </div>Demetheus was great. I've wondered about making a thread where everyone offers their own versions of some of the favourite named characters from previous editions - fixing weird skill selections, more sensible charm selections etc.<br /> <br /> I remember being especially perplexed by Wind's character sheet. And the fact he was yet another Snake guy. In 3e I'd totally make him Crane...<br /> <br /> That and the fact nearly all the DBs in Scroll of Exalts were powerhouses. Show me how to make a viable starting Deeb 2e...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T23:36:37-07:00","id":1380873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380872#post1380872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and the fact nearly all the DBs in Scroll of Exalts were powerhouses. Show me how to make a viable starting Deeb 2e...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have access to the caste/aspect books? They had some good stuff. What kind of viable are we talking for 2e, like what would you want him to do? It's been a while but I'm sure I could come up with something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T23:49:51-07:00","id":1380876,"title":"","content":"Ah, sorry, my bad I meant port them to 3e - maybe partially addressing the relative lack of powerful antagonists currently available in the process. Very generous offer though...<br /> <br /> Completely agree the Caste books (even more the aspect books, although been ages since I read them) are gold although I missed 1e and came to them late.<br /> <br /> The 2e DB gripe was more me remembering how few examples of an an Essence 1 DB there was - the engineer sorcerer was about it if I remember right...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-13-2020, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T00:21:11-07:00","id":1380879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380870#post1380870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say definitely. Unfortunately a lot of the players I've had in the past disagree. Having to be beholden to a sifu to learn something when you could just be awesome and make it up yourself, the choice is obvious. That goes double if the person their learning from is a lower class of being, like a spirit, or a DB or Heaven forbid a mortal.<br /> <br /> Thankfully the one player I've had in 3e who really went hard into MA actually decided he'd go seeking out a Sifu to learn him in Single Point style after he got 1v1'd by a DB princess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A dungeon crawl is a <i>story</i>. Lunar politics or Yu-Shan politics is a <i>story</i>. Attempting to infiltrate an immaculate monastary to learn one of their styles is a <i>story</i>.<br /> <br /> Holing up in the middle of nowhere to train is <i>downtime</i>.<br /> <br /> If you take Topaz's desire to learn all forms of sword mastery seriously, there is actually a lot of story left for her. Because learning all those styles is not an easy thing for a peniless anathema whose only skill is violence and who doesn't actually try to kill all her problems. If she has to learn Violet Bier Style and Fire Dragon Style and whatever other style from <i>somewhere</i>, that's an interesting story about how far away true mastery can be even for someone who seems to already be at the top.<br /> <br /> Cause where the hell is she going to learn Violet Bier or Fire Dragon style? Who alive that knows those styles is going to be willing to teach her? If they are, at what price? <br /> <br /> What if the only way she can actually learn fire dragon style is by watching immaculates that try to kill her with it? Even as good at swording as Topaz is, deliberately picking a fight with the Wyld Hunt to observe fire dragon stylists is not a healthy life choice.<br /> <br /> So maybe you try to delve shogunate ruins for manuals that might not exist. Or try to barter with Lunars for manuals they might not have, and you can bet your ass that the Silver Pact is going to want something in exchange. Maybe the only ones the Pact has are on the Caul and Topaz needs to fight with the Black Lion against the Realm there. Traveling from the Scavenger Lands (where Topaz starts out by default) to the caul is a trek across basically the entirety of Creation. That is not an easy trip, and it isn't a short one, and unless she can swim to the Caul its not a cheap one. The journey to the Caul to find Sha'a Oka to negotiate with him for a Fire Dragon Style manual alone could be an epic chronicle of adventure, before even setting foot on the Caul.<br /> <br /> Then there's Violet Bier Style. Is that even taught in Creation? Topaz might only know it from Bronze faction assassins trying to kill her or the complaints of lunars who faced the same. So if it can only be learned in Yu-Shan, then Topaz has to get into Yu-Shan somehow. Getting to Yu-Shan is even more trouble than getting to the Caul from the Scavenger Lands! Even if she gets into Yu-Shan, she'll need to deal with Yu-Shan Politics to actually learn Violet Bier. Even if she isn't interested in the politics, you can bet your bottom dollar Yu-Shan Politics is going to be very interested in her. So she'll need to juggle the politics as she learns the style. <br /> <br /> And that's just Fire Dragon and Violet Bier of Sorrows. What about sword MAs that can only be learned in Hell? What if the Seal of Eight Divinities gets broken and the Autochthonians have sword styles that are completely new and different? Where will she have to go and what will she have to do to learn those styles? <br /> <br /> Fuck. Now I actually want to play Topaz. Those stories sound fun and interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T01:33:17-07:00","id":1380882,"title":"","content":"So I've pretty much always been of the opinion that you start in Creation where basically nothing can stop you, progress to the Underworld where your power is actually rationed and everyone can use Essence, move on to the Demon Realm where you can still find opposition that challenges you, then finish in Yu Shan to make war on the Most High and become the new King of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Holden explicitly disliked this and tried to shift the focus back to Creation for 3E.<br /> <br /> That said... I really like the Wyld Shaping idea. Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25834\" data-vbnamecard=\"25834\">habitableexoplanet</a>!<br /> <br /> I haven't played with Wyld Shaping in 3E: it looks like a massive chore. But as an ST... making the NPCs I want to run, who can conceivably challenge optimized Solars, serving a plot point which engages with Creation, as the players carve their legend on the game world... seems like the ideal set up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T03:40:53-07:00","id":1380895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380854#post1380854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3e I don't think the stipulation that you need a sifu for anything exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of like the Off-Hand penalty - everything seems to be written from the assumption that the restriction exists, but the Core book forgot to actually go into it in detail.<br /> <br /> Here's what the Core has to say that I could find :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charms (Core p251)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the specific case of Martial Arts Charms, for example (detailed in Chapter Seven), these Charms are known to the Exalted by name and are passed among them, with an Exalted sifu training younger Chosen in the ways of her style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also learning MAs by looking at a cat or a campfire seems to be out :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Training Times (Core p178)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts Charms always require rigorous training.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 04-13-2020, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T04:35:20-07:00","id":1380906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372163#post1372163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sugar Daddy Captain</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eclipse Caste</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Attributes (8 BP)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Strength 2</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dexterity 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stamina 2</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charisma 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Manipulation 4</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Appearance 4</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Perception 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Intelligence 4</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wits 4</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eclipse Caste Abilities (6 BP)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bureaucracy 4 (Trading, Running a naval organization)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Linguistics 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Presence 4 (I look like a million bucks)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Sail 5</b></span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Socialize 3 (with the rich and powerful)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Favored Abilities (1 BP)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Brawl 1</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dodge 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Integrity 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Investigation 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Martial Arts - Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Performance 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merits (Native Language: Seatongue)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Followers 2 (50 loyal sailors)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Martial Arts</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resources 4</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charms</span>[/FONT]</span><ul><li>Sail: Ship-Claiming Stance</li> <li>Sail: Hull-Preserving Technique</li> <li>Sail: Ship-Leavening Meditation</li> <li>Sail: Hull-Taming Transfusion</li> <li>Sail: Blood and Salt Bondage</li> <li>Sail: Ship-Sustaining Spirit</li> <li>Sail: Burning Anima Sails</li> <li>Sail: Ship-Sleeking Technique</li> <li>Sail: Tide-Cutting Essence Infusion</li> <li>Sail: Wave-Riding Discipline</li> <li>Martial Arts: Elegant Weapon Repertoire</li> <li>Martial Arts: Pearlescent Filigree Defense</li> <li>Bureaucracy: Frugal Merchant Method</li> <li>Bureaucracy: Insightful Buyer Technique</li> <li>Presence: Harmonious Presence Meditation</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Evasion 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Parry 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Unarmed: Accuracy 10 (Decisive 6) Damage 7 (OV 1), Bashing, Grappling</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire: Accuracy 10 (Decisive 6) Damage 7 (OV 2), tags vary</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">(With Pearlescent Filigree Defense) Soak 5 Hardness 0</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resist Poison</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Joint Battle 4</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rush 3</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Disengage 6</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Willpower 5 (1 committed - Blood and Salt Bondage</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Essence 1</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Personal motes 13</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Peripheral motes 33 (17 committed - Harmonious Presence Meditation and Blood and Salt Bondage, 16 available)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Heath Levels: -0 x 6, -1 x2, -2 x 2, -4, and Incapacitated (+5 for Blood and Salt Bondage on Blue Water Merchant)</span>[/FONT]</span></div> </div> </div> </div>After his adventure with the manticore, Sugar Daddy Captain sails his raft to the nearest port.<br /> <br /> He pulls in, Solar sails still blazing with the power of the Solar Exalted, to find a heavy-set, bald woman wielding a giant warclub waiting for him.<br /> <br /> As he pulls ashore she points a finger at him and yells: &quot;Anathema!&quot;<br /> <br /> Imma, the Immaculate of Earth: 8d (31m) 7i<br /> Sugar Daddy Captain: 4d 6i<br /> Medium range<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 7i: Imma points at Daddy from the beach, then performs the katas of Earth Dragon style (23m 1a). She begins to glow with a white light that reflects from the shimmering sand.<br /> <br /> 6i: Daddy knows that this is going to be a tough fight. He uses <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire on his weighted captain's sash (13/20m).<br /> <br /> Imma: 7i (28m, 1a) Earth Dragon Form<br /> SDC: 6i (13/23m) Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> 7i: Imma charges towards Daddy (Short range) and Rushes him (6d, 26m vs 3d). Daddy is Rushed.<br /> <br /> 6i: Daddy closes to Close, and strikes out with his sash, trying to Disarm the Immaculate! He whips the sash in a wide arc, like winding up a slingshot and sends it flying at Imma with the full power of his Excellenct Martial Arts (6d+2d+6d=14d, 13/17m, 4WP). Imma really doesn't want to be disarmed, and defends with a Full Excellency, her anima rising a level (Parry 9, 20m, 2a). Daddy rolls 8+1 successes, hitting, and rolls 6i gaining two successes, yanking the great jade tetsubo from her attacker's hands, sending it flying into the surf! Daddy's caste mark starts to glitter on his brow.<br /> <br /> Imma: 7i (25m, 2a) Earth Dragon Form, Disarmed<br /> Daddy: 4i (13/22m, 4WP, 1a) Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> 7i: Unperturbed, Imma smashes her fist into the sand beneath her feet with a massive Earthshaker Attack (20m, 6WP, 3i, 3a). Her anima flares iconic.<br /> <br /> Daddy tries to ride out the shockwave, as if it were rough seas, he rolls back on the cresting wave of sand, steadying himself on his makeshift raft the better to throw himself back at his foe! Bracing his feet against the rising sands on the hull of his vessel, he leaps back into the battle! (Difficulty 4: 3d+2d+1+1, 3WP; 5 successes.)<br /> <br /> Even as Daddy rides out the initial shockwave, Imma focuses the blast into a Decisive tremor of sand! Daddy activates Pearlescent Filigree Defense, shunting Essence into his Captain's Uniform, and the sand breaks against him like a wave against the shore!<br /> <br /> 4i: Daddy lashes out again with his sash, striking at the Dragon (8d+6d, 13/16m, 2a)! Imma defends with a Full Excellency (14m, Parry 9), and batters the weighted end of the sash away with the palm of her hand.<br /> <br /> Imma: 3i (19m, 3a, 6WP) Earth Dragon Form, Disarmed, -1 Onslaught<br /> Daddy: 4i (13/21m, 2a, 3WP) <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> Imma's raging anima fails to damage Daddy.</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> 4i: Daddy strikes out again, whipping his sash around for a head-strike as his anima goes totemic (13/15m, 3a)! Imma doesn't want to get hit (because she aims on Crashing Daddy) so spends a Full Excellency (13m), but also realizes that Daddy still has a good chance of hitting her, so activates Unmoving Mountain Stance as well (10m). Daddy hits with 8 successes (5i), and rolls 2 dice of Overwhelming damage for 2 successes -- which is denied to him from Unommoving Mountain stance. (5i/1i)<br /> <br /> 1i: Imma, rises up in a a powerful uppercut, striking wirth the Force of the Mountain (6m) and Stillness of Stone Atemi (0m). Daddy really doesn't want to get hit by this (Evasion 3) and rolls like a ship on the sea (Evasion 4) backed by the full scale of his Exalted prowess (13/9m, Evasion 7). Imma rolls 7 successes, hitting. Rot roh. Daddy uses Pearlescent Filigree Defense spending his three phatom motes and 1 ph (13/8m) to max his soak to 9. Imma rolls 4d with double-9s, gaining two successes, knocking Daddy down to 3i and adding a -1 Mobility Penalty.<br /> <br /> Imma: 1i (5m, 3a, 6WP) Earth Dragon Form, Disarmed<br /> Daddy: 3i (13/13m, 3a, 3WP) <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing), -1 Mobility Penalty<br /> <br /> <b>Round 4</b><br /> <br /> Imma's anima blunts Daddy's attack (2i).<br /> <br /> 2i: Daddy strikes again with a Full Excellency, breathing in time with the crashing sea behind him, he throws himself into the assault (13/7m, 14d). Imma elects not to defend with Essence, conserving her power to attack (Parry 6). Daddy rolls 9 successes, hitting (3i) and getting soaked down to minimum damage. Daddy rolls 1 success on two dice, Crashing Imma (8i/0i).<br /> <br /> 0i: Going for a Shift, Imma goes all out on her attack (0m, 17d). Daddy uses a Full Excellency</span>[/FONT]</span> Parry (13/1m, 6 Parry). Imma rolls 10 successes, hitting (1i) with a Threshold of 4. Daddy uses Pearlescent Filigree Defense to raise his Soak to 9 (10/0m), for 6d in damage. Imma rolls 4 successes. (5i/4i)<br /> <br /> Imma: 5i (5m, 3a, 6WP) Earth Dragon Form, Disarmed<br /> Daddy: 4i (10/5m, 3a, 3WP) <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <b>Round 5</b><br /> <br /> Imma's anima does nothing.<br /> <br /> 5i: Imma launches a grapple against Daddy (0m, 12d). Slippery as the tides, Daddy rolls under Imma's clasping hands, his movements fluid with Essence (9/0m, Evasion 7). Imma hits (7 successes, 3i), and rolls 9d of control vs Daddy's 5d, gaining two rounds of control. Imma raises Daddy above her head and slams him down to the ground! She rolls 5 dice of Decisive damage, for 2 successes, inflicting 2B on Daddy (-0). She then Reflexively moves into the sea, where her tetsubo lies like a tiny sea stack, and resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> 4i: Tasting the sand, Daddy considers running away. Instead he rises from prone, tossing the sand from his hair and looks at Imma with a cold stare. &quot;Really? Is that all you've got?&quot; He throws a (8+2-3=)7d Threaten roll against Imma's Resolve of 4. The Immaculate grits her teeth, and pushes down the surge of fear (5WP)<br /> <br /> Imma: 3i (5m, 3a, 5WP) Earth Dragon Form, Disarmed<br /> Daddy: 4i (10/10m, 3a, 3WP, 2B/-0) <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> Short Range<br /> <br /> <b>Round 6</b><br /> <br /> Imma's anima is not in range.<br /> <br /> 4i: Daddy pulls back then surges forward, lashing out with his sash as he closes the distance between them (10/4m). Imma defends on Parry 6. Daddy hits (5i), and rolls 2 dice of damage for 0.<br /> <br /> 3i: Imma flurries. First she takes a Draw/Ready action to retieve her tetsubo, then she makes a Withering Smash attack backed by a 5m Excellency (12d-3d Flurry+5d=14d Excellency, 1i, -1 Defense). Not wanting to be knocked Prone, Daddy dodges with a Full Excellency and Willpower, rolling back with the tide, slipping and ducking around the powerful blows (8/0m, 3WP, Evasion 8). Imma roles 5 successes, overextending and missing.<br /> <br /> Imma: 1i (5m, 3a, 5WP) Earth Dragon Form (-3 Defense: Flurry, Draw/Ready/Smashing)<br /> Daddy: 5i (8/5m, 3a, 3WP, 2B/-0) <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <b>Round 7</b><br /> <br /> Imma's anima does nothing.<br /> <br /> 5i: Seeing an opening, Daddy slips like water under Imma's guard, trying to grapple her (7/0m). Imma doesn't want to get grappled, now she's holding her two-handed weapon and spends a 4m Excellency for Parry 5. Daddy rolls 13d for 6 successes, grabbing Imma and rolls another Full Excellency with Willpower (1/0m, 2WP) on the Control Roll 14d+1 vs 10d (0m). Daddy rolls 10 successes vs 3 for 7 rounds! Daddy uses Restrain/Drag, to drag Imma into the sea! (5 rounds remain.)<br /> <br /> 1i: Imma is restrained.<br /> <br /> Imma: 1i (5m, 3a, 5WP) Earth Dragon Form, Grappled<br /> Daddy: 5i (1/5m, 3a, 2WP, 2B/-0) <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing), 5 rounds of control<br /> <br /> <b>Round 8</b><br /> <br /> Imma's anima batters Daddy down to 4i.<br /> <br /> 4i: Daddy savages Imma, rolling 14 dice against Defense 0 as he tries to drown her in the ankle deep waters. Rolling 10 successes (5i) for 17 damage... and getting soaked down to the minimum of 2. Rolling 2 dice for 3i (8i/-2i), Crashing Imma (13i/-2i). 4 rounds of control.<br /> <br /> -2i: Imma works her tetsubo round to strike at Daddy, rolling (12-3)9d</span>[/FONT]</span>. Daddy boosts his Parry of 1 to 5 with a Full Excellency and Willpower (0/0m, 1WP). Imma rolls 4 successes, missing. 3 rounds of control remain.<br /> <br /> Imma: -2i (10m, 3a, 5WP) Earth Dragon Form, Grappled<br /> Daddy: 13i (0/5m, 3a, 1WP, 2B/-0) <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing), 3 rounds of control</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <b>Round 9</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Imma's anima batters Daddy down to 12i.</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> 12i: Daddy Decisively Slams Imma into the surf, boosting his damage by 2 for 14d. The blow inflicts a devestating 6B, knocking Imma into her -2s. Daddy resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> -2i: Imma rises from prone (4+2-2=4d+1 vs Difficulty 2; 8m, 4WP).<br /> <br /> Imma: -2i (13m, 3a, 4WP, 6B/-2) Earth Dragon Form, Grappled<br /> Daddy: 3i (0/10m, 3a, 1WP, 2B/-0) <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing)</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <b>Round 10</b><br /> <br /> Imma's anima does nothing.<br /> <br /> 3i: Daddy pushes his advantage, launching another Decisive attack slamming his palm into Imma's face (0/4m, 14d). Imma defends on a full excellency for Parry (6-2+3) 7 (7m). Daddy hits with 7 successes, and rolls a single level of damage for 7B/-2. Daddy resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> -2i: Imma strikes with a full excellency, withering tetsubo attack (1m; 12+6-2=16d). Daddy slips like water under the slow and powerful blow, putting what little Essence he has left into the defense (Evasion 3+1+2=6). Imma rolls 8 successes, hitting with a threshold of 2 (-1i) and rolls 15d of damage for 8i (7i/-5i), Crashing Daddy (12i/-5i) and causing Initative Shift (14i/-5i).<br /> <br /> Shift: Imma strikes again with another Withering attack, backed by her last mote of Essence (12+1-2=11d). Daddy defends with Parry 3, desperately throwing his arms in front of him in a double-up guard against the punishing war-club. Imma hits with a threshold of 2, and rolls 15d for 10i, (25i/-15i).<br /> <br /> Imma: 25i (5m, 3a, 4WP, 7B/-2) Earth Dragon Form<br /> Daddy: -15i (0/5m, 3a, 1WP, 2B/-0) <span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Disarm, Flexible, Bashing), -2 Onslaught</span>[/FONT]</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Round 11</b><br /> <br /> On the back foot, Imma's raging anima batters Daddy for 1L (1L2B/-0).<br /> <br /> 25i: &quot;It's over!&quot; Imma roars, bringing her tetsubo down in a deadly overhead strike (12-2+5=15d, 0m). Daddy throws the everything he has into dodging the blow, throwing himself back as hard as he can (Evasion 3+1+2=6, 0m 0WP). Imma rolls 7 successes, hitting, and rolls 25d of Bashing damage for 10B.<br /> <br /> Daddy is Incapacitated </span></span></span>with 2L 10B in his Health Track. He slumps into the surf, limp and unconcious.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Thoughts</b></u><br /> <br /> That went pretty much as expected. Guybrush got through 7/11 of the Earth Immaculate's health levels. If he had his crew acting as a militia battlegroup backing him up, or was fighting on his own ship with Ship Claiming Stance leveling its penalty on the Immaculate, he might even have won (or at least been able to throw her overboard).<br /> <br /> Still, I think Sugar Daddy Captain put in a damn good showing against an Exalted foe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-13-2020, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:51:59-07:00","id":1380979,"title":"","content":"GREAT fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T12:57:06-07:00","id":1381067,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380794#post1380794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I guess I could refluff various Warstriders as Behemoths. Any fan behemoths availiable I could use?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I looked into refluffling Karvara as a monster. I think it's reasonable to assume the pilot spends the entire fight in limit break. I'm also going to assume the pilot is a Lunar or Solar, although I haven't decided on the best statblock to use for the pilot. Some relevant stats are:</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>Attunement: </b>15m<br /> <b>Soak: </b>15; <b>Hardness: </b>10<br /> <b>Damage track: </b>\u22120x5/\u22121x5/\u22122x15/\u22124x25<br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>Bite: +1 ACC, +14L DMG, +0 DEF, OVW 6, Natural, Piercing</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>Claws: +5 ACC, +10L DMG, +0 DEF, OVW 3, Natural, Piercing</b><br /> </span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The most relevant charms are:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Berserker Fury Blitz: 6m, 3i. Add 10 non-Charm bonus dice to a damage roll. (Essence 2).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Roaring God-Monster Fury: 5m, 3i, 1wp: Make a Threaten roll with 10 bonus successes. If Topaz fails, she must spend 3 Willpower to keep fighting and takes a -3 penalty on all actions for the remainder of the scene (Essence 3).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Solipsistic Dreaming God-Beast: 4m, 4i, 3a: Subtract 10 successes from all damage rolls for one tick. (Essence 3).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Undying Behomoth Rebirth: 4m, 1wp: As a devastating action, roll (Initiative), healing a single level of damage for each tick. Does not reset to base Initiative. (Essence 3).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I don't like the Essence 5 powers that much. Do you think Topaz could beat an Essence 3-4 QC (maybe Vanamaithri) in this thing, with these charms?<br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380882#post1380882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've pretty much always been of the opinion that you start in Creation where basically nothing can stop you, progress to the Underworld where your power is actually rationed and everyone can use Essence, move on to the Demon Realm where you can still find opposition that challenges you, then finish in Yu Shan to make war on the Most High and become the new King of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Holden explicitly disliked this and tried to shift the focus back to Creation for 3E.<br /> <br /> That said... I really like the Wyld Shaping idea. Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25834\" data-vbnamecard=\"25834\">habitableexoplanet</a>!<br /> <br /> I haven't played with Wyld Shaping in 3E: it looks like a massive chore. But as an ST... making the NPCs I want to run, who can conceivably challenge optimized Solars, serving a plot point which engages with Creation, as the players carve their legend on the game world... seems like the ideal set up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. Thanks for running another cool fight using my silly character! For round 3 you can visualize his iconic anima manifestation, which I decided on after his previous adventure.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">When Guybrush\u2019s anima banner is glowing, his head is wreathed in a faint golden light. It grows as he is iconic, until his entire body is surrounded by a corona of radiance, as if his body was perfectly eclipsing a sun matching his size and shape - though he is not darkened in any way. At this level, falling from the sky appear orichalcum coins, seemingly minted in the First Age, with Old Realm lettering on one side and his face on the other, that audibly pile up on the ground behind him.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:01:41-07:00","id":1381175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380882#post1380882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've pretty much always been of the opinion that you start in Creation where basically nothing can stop you, progress to the Underworld where your power is actually rationed and everyone can use Essence, move on to the Demon Realm where you can still find opposition that challenges you, then finish in Yu Shan to make war on the Most High and become the new King of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Holden explicitly disliked this and tried to shift the focus back to Creation for 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna lie. I had a pretty visceral negative reaction to that first paragraph. So I get where Holden was coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:32:48-07:00","id":1381186,"title":"","content":"The closest I've seen to a meta-plot that games take is players healing the rifts between the different Exalted in the second age and trying to reform some kind of united nation with everyone working together again, while trying not to repeat the mistakes of the first age.<br /> <br /> How they go about <i>doing</i> that though ended up being crush everyone in opposition and enforce cooperation, somehow.<br /> <br /> In 3e the over arching campaign plots we've had a bit of a change though. The plots have been to stop a war between a nation and Vaneha, weed out and block a demonic incursion in a southern satrapy, stop an archipelago in the West from descending into civil war over a powerful artifact, follow up a missing Realm exploration group in the far north, and slay a resurgent Solar general who was in stasis since the First Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T20:03:24-07:00","id":1381196,"title":"","content":"We're all the way to Essence 4 in my game and we've <i>mostly </i>just tooled around Nexus. Though admittedly we're presently in the process of breaking into a Nephwrack's shadowland fortress to kick his ass, but to be fair, he kidnapped a member of our circle and gouged out her eyes as part of a nefarious plot. But when we're done with that, we've got business in Nexus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:59:38-07:00","id":1381284,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I've only really felt like there's any kind of metaplot in Realm games (there's a civil war, Houses align against each other, PCs scheme/fight and end up in charge). Outside the Realm, there's too many variables. I play an Essence 5 game where the Realm is invading, and a cabal of gods is trying to conquer the region, and Autocthon has replaced the Unconquered Sun and a group of dodgy gods are impersonating the Maidens. I play an Essence 4/5 game where we mostly just hang out in one small country in the south-east. I run an Essence 2 game where the world went through an apocalypse.<br /> It's never really felt to me like it has to go a certain way. Though I suppose 2nd ed maybe pushed moving beyond Creation a bit more than 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> (Actually, my 2nd ed game did start in Creation where not much stopped the PCs, then went to the Underworld, then went back to Creation, then briefly to Heaven, then back to Creation where it ended with a giant fight... in Creation. 2/5 PCs died, the others were permanently weakened. It really depends who you're fighting, since demons and Deathlords and so on do like to come to Creation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T06:09:31-07:00","id":1381303,"title":"","content":"It's good to know other people have high essence Solar games where they've mostly had adventures in one small region, and I definitely agree Exalted should support that in addition to the cosmic stuff. (Fun fact: In our current game, the furthest we've traveled from our starting region so far was because of a misunderstanding, though that might change soon.)<br /> <br /> I definitely have always thought the idea of &quot;unite all the exalt types&quot; makes a lot of sense given the game's backstory, but it seems hard to implement in practice. It's difficult enough getting the first five Exalts you meet to cooperate, let alone all the Exalts of their types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T07:11:02-07:00","id":1381310,"title":"","content":"Ha, that's true!<br /> <br /> (Actually, interestingly enough our higher-essence games are more focused on a small area than our low-essence games. I think because low-essence characters have little infrastructure and investment in a certain area, whereas higher-essence characters are more likely to rule an area and so be very invested in it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T07:27:10-07:00","id":1381315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380882#post1380882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've pretty much always been of the opinion that you start in Creation where basically nothing can stop you, progress to the Underworld where your power is actually rationed and everyone can use Essence, move on to the Demon Realm where you can still find opposition that challenges you, then finish in Yu Shan to make war on the Most High and become the new King of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Holden explicitly disliked this and tried to shift the focus back to Creation for 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I must say that is not at all what I got from reading The Exalted Core Book, and this isn't what got me into the game or shaped my fantasy of Solar games. I actually find this kind of reasoning seems more in line with DD (or Scion ? I've read only edition, the one with the wheel for initiative), or Diablo 3.<br /> <br /> It's not a critic, it's just totally not how I envision playing Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T12:59:46-07:00","id":1382813,"title":"","content":"&quot;What was behind the door Kinsh?&quot;<br /> <br /> Crashes-The-Waves looks at Cynis Ganan with harrowed eyes, and hands him the Key of Earth in silence.<br /> <br /> Ganan sets it to the door, and walks through. On the other side he sees... himself?<br /> <br /> &quot;Who are you?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm you. But better.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1382327-challenge-remaking-your-characters?p=1382771#post1382771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hint hint potential Arena post...?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Earth: Joins Battle on 9 dice, +3 successes for 6m (33m, 1a) = 10i<br /> Twilight: Joins Battle on 9 dice, +8 dice for 8m (33m, 1a) = 8i<br /> Medium Range<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Round 1</b><br /> <br /> 10i: Earth performs the Katas of Earth Dragon Form (24m, 2a) and moves to Short<b>.</b><br /> <br /> 8i: Twilight activates Chambered Fist Charge (31m, 7i).<br /> <br /> Earth: 10i (29m, 2a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Twilight: 7i (36m, 1a, 1 Charge) Aim bonus<br /> Short<br /> <br /> <b>Round 2</b><br /> <br /> 10i: Earth moves to Clost and launches a Full Excellency (26m) Withering Smash (9i) backed by Force of the Mountain (23m,3a). (Henceforth, referred to as a 6m Standard. Rolling 19 dice.) Twilight defends with a Full Martial Arts Excellency (28m, 2a) for Parry 8. Earth rolls 7 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> 7i: Twilight launches a Full Excellency (20m) Withering Smash (6i, -1 Defense) against Earth (17 dice+3 Aim). Earth defends with Unmoving Mountain Stance (17m). Twilight rolls 7 successes, hitting (7i) with Threshold 1. Twilight has 20 damage, Earth has 17 soak. Twilight rolls five Overwhelming dice of damage for 3i, Unmoving Mountain Stance reducing the amount gained by 1. (9i/6i)<br /> <br /> Earth: 6i (22m, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form, Onslaught -1<br /> Twilight: 9i (25m, 3a)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 3</b><br /> <br /> 9i. Twilight launches a Full Excellency Withering Smash (17m, 7i, -1 Defense). Earth defends with a Full Excellency (Parry 9) Unmoving Mountain Stance (10m). Twilight rolls 7 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> 6i. Earth attacks with a 6m Standard (4m, 5i). Twilight defends with a Full Excellency for Parry 8 (9m). Earth hits (6i) with 8 successes. Earth rolls (19+5-10) 14 dice of damage for 6i, and knocks Twilight Prone. (12i/1i)<br /> <br /> Earth: 12i (9m, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Twilight: 1i (14m, 3a) Prone, Onslaught -1<br /> <br /> <b>Round 4</b><br /> <br /> 12i. Earth attacks with a 6m Standard (3m, 11i). Twilight defends with his Melee Parry (1), backed by Dipping Swallow Defense (Parry 3, 12m) and a Full Excellency (Parry 6, 6m). Earth rolls 4 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> 1i: Twilight flurries a Rise from Prone, with a 3m Excellency (3m) and WP, rolling 4 dice for 1+1 success. Twilight then attacks with a 3m Excellency, rolling 9 dice. Earth does not defend with Essence, Parry 6. Twilight rolls 6 successes, hitting (2i), and 5 OVR for 2i. (4i/9i)<br /> <br /> Earth: 9i (8m, 3a, 5WP) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Twilight: 4i (5m, 3a, 4WP)<br /> <br /> <b>Round 5</b><br /> <br /> 9i. 6m Standard (8i, 2m). Twilight defends with Durability of Oak Meditation (2m). Earth rolls 10 successes, for 6 threshold (9i), knocking Twilight prone. 18 damage for 12i. Crash. (26i/-8i)<br /> <br /> -8i. Twilight attacks from prone with a 2m Excellency plus WP. Earth defends on Parry 6. Twilight hits with 7 successes (-7i) and rolls OVR for 2i. (-5i/24i)<br /> <br /> Earth: 24i (7m, 3a, 5WP) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Twilight: -5i (5m, 3a, 3WP) Prone<br /> <br /> <b>Round 6</b><br /> <br /> 24i. Earth throws a 3m Excellency, Decisive, Force of the Mountain, with WP against the Prone Twilight (1m; 17 dice +1 success). Twilight defends with a 4m Excellency and WP, bringing his Parry to 6. Earth rolls 10 successes, hitting, and rolls 24i (double-10s, reroll 6s) for 16B.<br /> <br /> Twilight's health track is now as follows:<br /> <br /> -0 - X<br /> -1 - X<br /> -1 - X<br /> -1 - /<br /> -1 - /<br /> -2 - /<br /> -2 - /<br /> -2 - /<br /> -2 - /<br /> -2 - /<br /> -2 - /<br /> -4 - /<br /> Incap - /</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Twilight is unconcious. Earth resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Cynis Ganan is victorious.<br /> <br /> (Given that battlegroups don't grant Initiative, I don't think either version of Ganan can actually beat a Cataphract.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-20-2020, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T15:53:31-07:00","id":1382835,"title":"","content":"Damnit, I lost the notes and have to start over with the Wyld Shaping Technique thing.<br /> <br /> One thing I noticed is that the Fights with multiple Cataphracts and battle groups is a huge slog, even if Topaz is blocking everything and winning, because battle groups are beefy and don't give any initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T16:35:01-07:00","id":1382846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1382835#post1382835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damnit, I lost the notes and have to start over with the Wyld Shaping Technique thing.<br /> <br /> One thing I noticed is that the Fights with multiple Cataphracts and battle groups is a huge slog, even if Topaz is blocking everything and winning, because battle groups are beefy and don't give any initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I've thought of possibly using before in a &quot;get players to spend motes&quot; kind of thing. If you have enemies who aren't really dangerous if you go hard on defense, but who have a ton of soak and health levels, you might end up with your PCs just getting fed up with not dealing any damage and pull out a doomcombo just to end it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T17:26:46-07:00","id":1382853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1382846#post1382846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something I've thought of possibly using before in a &quot;get players to spend motes&quot; kind of thing. If you have enemies who aren't really dangerous if you go hard on defense, but who have a ton of soak and health levels, you might end up with your PCs just getting fed up with not dealing any damage and pull out a doomcombo just to end it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Battlegroups are... interesting. A battlegroup with a commander basically has an excellency. And the way they fail to interact with the initiative system makes them dangerous on a completely different axis than most enemies. <br /> <br /> That said, it is super annoying fighting them. Because they don't interact with the inititive system in the typical way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T17:48:14-07:00","id":1382859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1382853#post1382853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Battlegroups are... interesting. A battlegroup with a commander basically has an excellency. And the way they fail to interact with the initiative system makes them dangerous on a completely different axis than most enemies.<br /> <br /> That said, it is super annoying fighting them. Because they don't interact with the inititive system in the typical way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Battlegroups are usually there to give everyone a chance to kick some mooks through walls and be badasses and to show the few standing against the many, and from a mechanical standpoint to give the big enemies effectively a big pool of health levels that need to be chewed through so the fight doesn't last 2 rounds while also letting you have fights with thousands of combatants that you don't have to roll thousands of dice for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T11:30:51-07:00","id":1383008,"title":"","content":"Don't battlegroups give 5 initiative (as though you had crashed a target) when you reduce their Size through magnitude loss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T12:02:44-07:00","id":1383013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383008#post1383008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't battlegroups give 5 initiative (as though you had crashed a target) when you reduce their Size through magnitude loss?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but by comparison that\u2019s not much. A size 5 battlegroup of normal troops has 13 soak and 12 magnitude. If you smack them for 12i damage you end up getting 6i yourself, but against any other target you\u2019re racking up 18i if you crashed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T12:38:46-07:00","id":1383016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383013#post1383013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but by comparison that\u2019s not much. A size 5 battlegroup of normal troops has 13 soak and 12 magnitude. If you smack them for 12i damage you end up getting 6i yourself, but against any other target you\u2019re racking up 18i if you crashed them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's true, but battlegroups directly convert the initiative you would have gained into progress towards eliminating a foe, whereas against normal targets you have to launder it through a difficult decisive attack. <br /> <br /> I've found the ones in my games more pleasant than annoying to fight, because their low stats make it much easier to get a hit in without spending an ton of motes, and you only have to get a few hits in to knock them down a size.<br /> <br /> But these are battlegroups of size 1-3. I agree size 5 battlegroups are much tougher to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T12:50:31-07:00","id":1383019,"title":"","content":"I also find that battlegroups go down in like, one round, but that\u2019s with 4-5 PC attacks in a round, Arafan is fighting them solo and trying to do so while keeping enough motes left to fight the next battle after this one. Which means spending much more on the attack than DES is going to be difficult to sell, and also using full defense to regen motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T01:59:05-07:00","id":1383311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1382813#post1382813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;What was behind the door Kinsh?&quot;<br /> <br /> Crashes-The-Waves looks at Cynis Ganan with harrowed eyes, and hands him the Key of Earth in silence.<br /> <br /> Ganan sets it to the door, and walks through. On the other side he sees... himself?<br /> <br /> &quot;Who are you?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm you. But better.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>FIGHT!</b></i></span><br /> <br /> Twilight is unconcious. Earth resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> Cynis Ganan is victorious.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Go Ganan MK I...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T02:09:45-07:00","id":1383312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383311#post1383311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go Ganan MK I...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was pleasantly surprised.<br /> <br /> DB Ganan was gunning pretty hard for optimal combat (swap Int and Wit and throw in Mela's Coil instead of Well Bred and Lore and that's about as hard as I can go).<br /> <br /> Solar Ganan was going for organic story development. I was <i>still</i> worried Solar would curb-stomp.<br /> <br /> That said... now I want to make a Solar Smash fighter. I'm thinking Smashfists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-23-2020, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:28:41-07:00","id":1383560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383312#post1383312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said... now I want to make a Solar Smash fighter. I'm thinking Smashfists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That should be terrifying. I was trying to make a brawl DB for a player the other day and Smashfists seem really top tier as weapons go given how frustrating smashing attacks are to face \u2013 +5 accuracy to knock someone prone seems a very effective debuff booster against most opponents, not to mention the maxed out clash bonuses they offer.<br /> <br /> Struggle to think off the top of my head of better 'generic' artefact weapons before charms are taken into account.<br /> <br /> Was thinking that might be something to be explored in the Arena \u2013 the best ways to utilise different weapont tags for different splats \u2013 but probably too dry/niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-24-2020, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T08:44:28-07:00","id":1383605,"title":"","content":"I actually don\u2019t see solars using weapon tags or really even gambits apart from Grapple very often. They\u2019re usually just strong enough that nobody really thinks of using those kinds of tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T09:08:20-07:00","id":1383609,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the fact I'm pretty much only thinking about DBs - who may find the bonus from, say, piercing or the like useful on occasion - at the minute is probably showing.<br /> <br /> Popped into my head from your Immaculate investigator character actually and how he seemed to be built to be an armour buster.<br /> <br /> Would imagine Lunar don't much bother with tags either - or is that not the case Lunar players?<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Smashing feels like the big one as rising from prone/the flurry penalty is such a debuff unless you're spec'd for it. Has anyone ever had a moment when one of the others has been vital? Reaching must have been useful to someone on occasion I'd imagine.<br /> <br /> Potentially not the most gripping topic though, I admit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-24-2020, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T10:25:44-07:00","id":1383621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383609#post1383609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the fact I'm pretty much only thinking about DBs - who may find the bonus from, say, piercing or the like useful on occasion - at the minute is probably showing.<br /> <br /> Popped into my head from your Immaculate investigator character actually and how he seemed to be built to be an armour buster.<br /> <br /> Would imagine Lunar don't much bother with tags either - or is that not the case Lunar players?<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Smashing feels like the big one as rising from prone/the flurry penalty is such a debuff unless you're spec'd for it. Has anyone ever had a moment when one of the others has been vital? Reaching must have been useful to someone on occasion I'd imagine.<br /> <br /> Potentially not the most gripping topic though, I admit...</div> </div> </div> </div>Reaching was absolutely ESSENTIAL in the Death Kitty vs The Invulnerable fight. The Invulnerable would have destroyed Death Kitty, no contest, without it.<br /> <br /> I am... less than impressed with chopping and piercing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:15:20-07:00","id":1383650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383621#post1383621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am... less than impressed with chopping and piercing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chopping and piercing are situational, especially before charms, but not bad in those situations.<br /> <br /> The defense penalty is meaningless if you leapfrog your opponents in the initiative order, or if you plan on using penalty ignoring magic anyway. It can also be worth it if you think you'll need that extra oomph to crash an opponent, or simply if some enemy is at like 25i and is about to end somebody. Then it's not really about how much initiative you're trading for what, and more just about taking down a foe who's got lethal momentum.<br /> <br /> There's still lots of cases where you don't want to use it, like against an already crashed enemy when you're already sitting at the top of the initiative order and have a half a dozen foes who will be taking advantage of your -1 defense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:17:32-07:00","id":1383651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383609#post1383609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Smashing feels like the big one as rising from prone/the flurry penalty is such a debuff unless you're spec'd for it. Has anyone ever had a moment when one of the others has been vital? Reaching must have been useful to someone on occasion I'd imagine.<br /> <br /> Potentially not the most gripping topic though, I admit...</div> </div> </div> </div>Disarming and Flexible both have the opportunity to be totally game changing. A lot of enemies with weapons are near totally useless without them. Flexible is also really powerful against Crane stylists or people using Shining Ice Mirror.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T14:50:13-07:00","id":1383674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383605#post1383605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don\u2019t see solars using weapon tags or really even gambits apart from Grapple very often. They\u2019re usually just strong enough that nobody really thinks of using those kinds of tactics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to use Disarm more, now that I think of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T16:43:05-07:00","id":1383685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383609#post1383609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would imagine Lunar don't much bother with tags either - or is that not the case Lunar players?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, balanced is always good, though I suspect that the guy with a sword would still use a sword if he didn't have it.<br /> One Full Moon has a grand grimcleaver (which has Reach). I guess it's helped him against mounted foes once, but I think they were ones a Full Moon would have crushed anyway.<br /> That's it. I don't think I have seen any of them use any tag that requires a choice to use it (smashing, chopping, etc). Two of them fight unarmed and one uses either a bow or claws.<br /> <br /> Hmmm.. the Lunars in mixed games I play also don't use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-25-2020, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T16:55:51-07:00","id":1383687,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen Solars use them, I haven't gotten the chance to run DBs yet, but I do know that my group used the hell out of them when they were mortals, which is why I assumed that the Solar ability to just blow past opposition is why they get forgotten. As a mortal though knocking a strong enemy down with smashing so that your ally can smash them with the poleaxe is pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T18:48:31-07:00","id":1383704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1383687#post1383687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen Solars use them, I haven't gotten the chance to run DBs yet, but I do know that my group used the hell out of them when they were mortals, which is why I assumed that the Solar ability to just blow past opposition is why they get forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, the reason I haven't used Disarm as Knight Raiton is because most of the time we've taken out the dice to fight, most of the foes have either been a) using natural weapons, or b) trying to run away, or c) too far away so I threw boomerangs instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T21:33:31-07:00","id":1386247,"title":"","content":"Tomorrow I'm running a test fight to help get my friend back into Exalted, we ran one a few days ago with a couple of war ghosts vs his chargen DB archer, but now we're running one where he's an archer and has an elite soldier buddy.<br /> <br /> What should they face, and what environment should they face it in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:23:28-07:00","id":1386276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386247#post1386247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tomorrow I'm running a test fight to help get my friend back into Exalted, we ran one a few days ago with a couple of war ghosts vs his chargen DB archer, but now we're running one where he's an archer and has an elite soldier buddy.<br /> <br /> What should they face, and what environment should they face it in?</div> </div> </div> </div>How optimized are they? Got a c-sheet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:10:06-07:00","id":1386312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386276#post1386276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How optimized are they? Got a c-sheet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually one of the least optimized PCs I've seen in a long while, here's the relevant combat bits, but he's primarily a social character.<br /> <br /> phys 2/4/3<br /> wits 4<br /> <br /> Archery 5 with specialty<br /> dodge 4<br /> Athletics 3<br /> Awareness 3<br /> Stealth 3<br /> <br /> artifact longbow<br /> mundane chain shirt<br /> <br /> Archery up to Death from Nowhere and Harvest the Hunter. Also a wood aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:12:03-07:00","id":1386313,"title":"","content":"Also, what's the rationale behind having the soldier buddy, out of interest? Is there an element of combat you're looking at exploring in detail or is it primarily a general refresh?<br /> <br /> Given the soldier, my brain has gone escort mission. Maybe the DB desperately trying to get his important/trusty/wounded (delete as appropriate) companion to safety while being stalked from two different directions through a storm by a party of grizzled icewalker brigands and their wolf-taming beastmaster leader?<br /> <br /> Maybe fussier than you're looking for though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:18:43-07:00","id":1386315,"title":"","content":"No, that\u2019s not bad, I could do that fussy, or less.<br /> <br /> I think the idea is last combat he was the only person on his side so the interplay between characters changing initiatives and working together wasn\u2019t there, when it would be in a real game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:55:51-07:00","id":1386324,"title":"","content":"Amongst these 58 pages, are there any fights between 1 Dawn and a whole hearth of Dragonblooded?<br /> <br /> Because of the Essence discussion about how powerful a Solar is vs Dragonblood, I was discussing the other day with a friend about a Dawn fighting a Dragonblooded hearth. Now, I actually don't think it's necessary for the setting for a Dawn to be able to beat 5 Dragonblood, but I just said that I think his Essence 5 Dawn (supernal Resistance, a few melee charms, artefact superheavy plate and daiklaive) probably could (I assume a 0xp Dawn couldn't, they'd run out of motes coping with so many attacks). He thought it would be too difficult even with his ridiculous toughness.<br /> <br /> So I was just curious what fights like that you guys have run, but over 58 pages it's hard to search. I'm just interested, essentially, at how good a Dawn is compared to a Dragonblood combat character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T03:41:29-07:00","id":1386342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386324#post1386324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amongst these 58 pages, are there any fights between 1 Dawn and a whole hearth of Dragonblooded?<br /> <br /> Because of the Essence discussion about how powerful a Solar is vs Dragonblood, I was discussing the other day with a friend about a Dawn fighting a Dragonblooded hearth. Now, I actually don't think it's necessary for the setting for a Dawn to be able to beat 5 Dragonblood, but I just said that I think his Essence 5 Dawn (supernal Resistance, a few melee charms, artefact superheavy plate and daiklaive) probably could (I assume a 0xp Dawn couldn't, they'd run out of motes coping with so many attacks). He thought it would be too difficult even with his ridiculous toughness.<br /> <br /> So I was just curious what fights like that you guys have run, but over 58 pages it's hard to search. I'm just interested, essentially, at how good a Dawn is compared to a Dragonblood combat character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to illuminate, whilst you ruminate the possibilies:<br /> <br /> Wyld Hunt kills starting Solar Resistance monster: <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1348972#post1348972\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1348972#post1348972\"> Exalted: Arena - Onyx Path Fo