t uses Heirs charms to kill Volfer:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380224#post1380224\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380224#post1380224\"> Exalted: Arena - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380224#post1380224\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380224#post1380224 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> LLLLLET'S GET READY TO RUMBLEEEEE!!! In this thread we pit foes against eachother and I roll out the fights. Exalted is a big complex system with lots of moving parts, how much does soak impact the game, how good is this combo of grapple enhancing charms, ect. Sometimes it's just hard to figure out what to do or how good something is in context. To that end we now have the Arena. Now, the arena isn't necessarily a white room, we might import some trees for cover, or make the whole thing submerged in waist high water. Let's talk about what it is, and what it is not. What it is: A place to gain some </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T03:48:06-07:00","id":1386344,"title":"","content":"There are. But forum ate my links.<br /> <br /> Search: <br /> Topaz<br /> Heaven Sword Flash<br /> Volfer<br /> Challenge<br /> Aegis<br /> <br /> Short answer is a starting Solar can kill an entire Hearth of Essence 2 DBs. An Essence 5 Solar can take on an entire Essence 3 Hearth. <br /> <br /> But a starting DB can solo a Solar (three successful builds so far -- two Earth, one Water). <br /> <br /> A Solar elder doesn't need HSF to kill upto 6 DBs (can solo 3 DBs without taking a single hit or flaring anima), but 7+ DBs have a good shot at bringing a Solar elder down -- if they ambush and the Solar doesn't have time to prepare. <br /> <br /> Resistance Solars aren't actually that good at killing entire Hearths of DBs in practice. <br /> <br /> An Essence 2 Solar can back-to-back kill some of the strongest fighters in Creation, acing Berit <i>casually</i> as a warm up.<br /> <br /> It all depends on how &quot;optimized&quot; you build.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-07-2020, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T04:14:26-07:00","id":1386345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386344#post1386344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are. But forum ate my links.<br /> <br /> Search:<br /> Topaz<br /> Heaven Sword Flash<br /> Volfer<br /> Challenge<br /> Aegis<br /> <br /> Short answer is a starting Solar can kill an entire Hearth of Essence 2 DBs. An Essence 5 Solar can take on an entire Essence 3 Hearth.<br /> <br /> But a starting DB can solo a Solar (three successful builds so far -- two Earth, one Water).<br /> <br /> A Solar elder doesn't need HSF to kill upto 6 DBs (can solo 3 DBs without taking a single hit or flaring anima), but 7+ DBs have a good shot at bringing a Solar elder down -- if they ambush and the Solar doesn't have time to prepare.<br /> <br /> Resistance Solars aren't actually that good at killing entire Hearths of DBs in practice.<br /> <br /> An Essence 2 Solar can back-to-back kill some of the strongest fighters in Creation, acing Berit <i>casually</i> as a warm up.<br /> <br /> It all depends on how &quot;optimized&quot; you build.</div> </div> </div> </div>Links to some of these below:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> did an Essence 5 Dawn fight against Corebook shikari. Brutal: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1349857#post1349857\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...57#post1349857</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11917_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11917\" data-vbnamecard=\"11917\">Aranfan</a> ran Shining Topaz character against five pretty spec'd up Immaculates here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1343699#post1343699\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...99#post1343699</a><br /> <br /> Plus some other run throughs: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344030#post1344030\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...30#post1344030</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1344312#post1344312\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...12#post1344312</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> ran this one, an Essence 2 Dawn against three DBs: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1308235#post1308235\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...35#post1308235</a><br /> <br /> And this one against E2 Deebs: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1340725#post1340725\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...25#post1340725</a><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Do suspect Heirs has narrowed the 'white room' gap a little for chargen DBs against chargen HSF-less Solars thanks to stuff like Victory-Seeking Insight and Tiger-and-Dragon Combination, but, yeah, optimisation still decides things.<br /> <br /> And at Essence 5 aren't all bets kinda off in terms of anticipating how powerful a character is without seeing a sheet? You could just be <i>hella</i> tough or you could be 'a whole Direction trembles in my wake' tough...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T04:32:02-07:00","id":1386349,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Resistance Solars aren't actually that good at killing entire Hearths of DBs in practice. </div> </div> </div>Because they have to spend too many motes?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T04:35:42-07:00","id":1386351,"title":"","content":"Reading those links, it honestly seems really variable. Sometimes an amazing Solar gets killed dead. Other times a Solar rips through a bunch of DBs with nary a wound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T04:48:52-07:00","id":1386352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386351#post1386351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading those links, it honestly seems really variable. Sometimes an amazing Solar gets killed dead. Other times a Solar rips through a bunch of DBs with nary a wound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, combat in 3e is incredibly swingy. It doesn't matter how much you optimize your character in many cases. Even a Dawn Caste Solar built to be the greatest swordsman in Creation can roll poorly at the start of a fight, begin with low Initiative, get Crashed, and then die on round 2. That's just how dicepools be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T04:59:49-07:00","id":1386355,"title":"","content":"Well, could be annoying, but better than 2nd ed where half the time you knew who'd win based on mote pools.<br /> <br /> My players tend, 60-70% of the time, to do combat by having one guy go forward and fight the bad guy while the rest stand behind and collect their 2 Role XP (unless it looks like the guy fighting is in big trouble), so swingy works for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:30:12-07:00","id":1386363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386349#post1386349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks.<br /> Because they have to spend too many motes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? It's mostly swing.<br /> <br /> If a Melee based Solar gets unlucky then they lose 3i or they gain a Wound Penalty that they can DSD away. If they get lucky they kill all their enemies and win.<br /> <br /> If a Resistance Solar gets unlucky, their Charms shut down and they die. If they get lucky... nothing different happens to if their luck was average.<br /> <br /> Fighting 5 on 1... that's a lot of chances to get unlucky.<br /> <br /> But in general, yes: Solars die when they run out of motes. Melee Solars can novastrike their foes into oblivion, spending all their motes but killing all their foes. Resistance Solars get bled dry by the fact that 5 DBs are regening 25m each round to their 5m.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386351#post1386351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading those links, it honestly seems really variable. Sometimes an amazing Solar gets killed dead. Other times a Solar rips through a bunch of DBs with nary a wound.</div> </div> </div> </div>A large percentage of this is luck of the dice.<br /> <br /> But a larger percentage is character creation.<br /> <br /> I mathed it out in another thread, but the difference between an optimized and suboptimal PC is something like 150XP at character generation. Most pregen characters (like the Corebook example Solar and the Tomb of Dreams PCs) are built with one or two stats at 5. Combat optimized characters are built with 7+ fives.<br /> <br /> There is a massive, <i>massive</i> difference in power between Dex 3 Melee 3 and Dex 5 Melee 5. (Not sure if I posted the percentages here or in the character optimization thread, but allow me to say &quot;<b>massive</b>&quot; one last time.)<br /> <br /> I've run a few Solar vs Solar fights, and seen similiar crushing victories.<br /> <br /> An optimized character (or Hearth of characters) is going to crush a character made within Exalted's default expectations.<br /> <br /> (Other factors like Stunt bonuses also help.)<br /> <br /> But this is as it should be. Cynis What's-His-Name killed a Solar boy who was trying to stop the opium trade way back in 1E. Being a Solar shouldn't be an automatic &quot;Win&quot; button. Dragon-Blooded should have the potential to be a meaningful threat. But Solars are the most powerful Exalted for a reason, and the Wyld Hunt is a dangerous duty. I think 3E really nailed the balance point. (And if you really miss the old days of Solars breezing through DBs, run Young Dynasts in a Battlegroup.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:43:55-07:00","id":1386370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386363#post1386363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in general, yes: Solars die when they run out of motes. Melee Solars can novastrike their foes into oblivion, spending all their motes but killing all their foes. Resistance Solars get bled dry by the fact that 5 DBs are regening 25m each round to their 5m.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But a larger percentage is character creation.<br /> <br /> I mathed it out in another thread, but the difference between an optimized and suboptimal PC is something like 150XP at character generation. </div> </div> </div>Very true, but some of the Solars who lost the fights in this Arena looked pretty optimised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:49:35-07:00","id":1386476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386315#post1386315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that\u2019s not bad, I could do that fussy, or less.<br /> <br /> I think the idea is last combat he was the only person on his side so the interplay between characters changing initiatives and working together wasn\u2019t there, when it would be in a real game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you run anything in the end? Feel like you'll want at least two opponents to fully experience initiative bouncing around...<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to do something similar with a friend, running a DB magistrate rescuing his archon and being ambushed by brigands who are going to try to exploit different weapons tags/gambits (if we can make it work).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:30:17-07:00","id":1386492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386324#post1386324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amongst these 58 pages, are there any fights between 1 Dawn and a whole hearth of Dragonblooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will do this one time. This time I'm going to be spending willpower on more than just charms, and give everyone an equal Essence 3 capability with their charms. Everyone 100% maximized for combat, or at least as far as I can tell. To keep it simple though all the DBs will be immaculates, with the wood one also using archery. Also with so many charms all over the place I'm bound to miss something, but I'll do my best.<br /> <br /> <br /> The first time I did this the Heaven Sword Flash missed so I just rerolled it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Solar uses 5m 1wp Awakening Eye, stunts rolling 23 dice for 17i<br /> Every DB uses 6m to get 3 sux<br /> <br /> Air gets 13i<br /> Earth gets 11i<br /> Fire gets 14i<br /> Water gets 17i<br /> Wood gets 10i<br /> <br /> Every DB then uses 4m Victory-Seeking Insight to transfer 1i to every other DB. Due to being hearthmates this results in a net +4 initiative for all of them.<br /> <br /> Fire wins join battle and reflexively enters Fire Dragon form for 7m<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar 17i 19p 25h 8wp<br /> Air 17i 14p 16h 9wp<br /> Earth 15i 14p 14h 9wp<br /> Fire 18i 14p 9h 9wp<br /> Water 21i 14p 15h 9wp<br /> Wood 15i 14p 16h 9wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==========<br /> Water aspect moves forward and spends a mote to get into water aura.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Fire aspect moves forward<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Solar reflexively moves into short range with Wood, Earth and Air, then uses 4m 1wp Thunderbolt Attack Prana with 1m Divine Executioner Stance, 7m 1wp Heaven Sword Flash, 3m Excellent Strike, 3m Fire and Stones Strike, 4m excellency. The DBs will all spend 6m to defend, and a willpower spent all around.<br /> <br /> Rolling 19+2 dice the Solar gets 9 successes, with a straight, so he uses 1m Rising Sun Slash to roll 3 more dice, and hitting Earth and Air with only 1 more success.<br /> <br /> Rolling 12 damage for 7, doubling to 14, both DBs get put into their -2s<br /> <br /> Solar 5i 19p 3h 5wp<br /> Air 17i 14p 10h 8wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 15i 14p 8h 8wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 18i 14p 9h 9wp<br /> Water 21i 14p 14h 9wp<br /> Wood 15i 14p 10h 8wp<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Air then attacks Solar with a 3m 1wp Avenging Wind Strike, using 6m excellency. The Solar will defend with 6m excellency. Willpower being spent all around. Rolling 15 dice Air Dragon gets only 7 successes, and misses.<br /> <br /> Solar 5i 13p 3h 4wp<br /> Air 14i 14p 10h 6wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 15i 14p 8h 8wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 18i 14p 9h 9wp<br /> Water 21i 14p 14h 9wp<br /> Wood 15i 14p 10h 8wp<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Wood Dragon goes next, using 3m 2i Soul Marking Style, spending a willpower and 6m excellency. Solar will use 2m Dipping Swallow and 4m excellency to defefnd. Wood Dragon rolls 17 dice for 8, missing.<br /> <br /> Solar 6i 10p 0h 4wp<br /> Air 14i 14p 10h 6wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 15i 14p 8h 8wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 18i 14p 9h 9wp<br /> Water 21i 14p 14h 9wp<br /> Wood 10i 14p 1h 7wp<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Earth Dragon will make a withering smashing attack with 6m excellency and 3m Force of the Mountain, and a willpower. Solar will defend with 6m Iron Kettle Body<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon rolls 18 dice for 12, Solar uses 1i to activate Essence Gathering Temper to regain 10m.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon rolls 5 damageg for 4 and knocking the Solar to the ground.<br /> <br /> Solar 1i 4p 10h 4wp<br /> Air 14i 14p 10h 6wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 20i 13p 0h 7wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 18i 14p 9h 9wp<br /> Water 21i 14p 14h 9wp<br /> Wood 10i 14p 1h 7wp<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ==========<br /> Solar 1i 4p 15h 4wp<br /> Air 14i 14p 15h 6wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 20i 13p 5h 7wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 18i 14p 14h 9wp<br /> Water 21i 14p 19h 9wp<br /> Wood 10i 14p 6h 7wp<br /> <br /> <br /> Water moves back into melee range and attacks with a withering strike with 4i Theft-of-Essence Method, 5m Rippling water Strike and 6m Excellency, as well as a willpower. The Solar will defend with 5m Bulwark Stance. Rolling 24+1 dice for 18 successes, Water hits.<br /> <br /> Then rolling 15 damage for 8, crashing the Solar, and stealing 3m from his peripheral pool.<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 4p 7h 4wp<br /> Air 14i 14p 15h 6wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 20i 13p 5h 7wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 18i 14p 14h 9wp<br /> Water 31i 14p 8h 8wp<br /> Wood 10i 14p 6h 7wp<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Earth Dragon rolls 1 anima damage.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon will now attempt a disarm gambit, using 3m 1wp Shattering Fist Strike, 6m excellency, expended Earth Arua and willpower. Solar will defend with 6m excellency and a willpower. Rolling 15+1 dice for 13 the Earth Dragon hits with only one 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> Rolling 20i the dragon easily makes the gambit and disarms the Solar, breaking attunement to his blade and cracking it.<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 4p 1h 3wp 1L(-0s)<br /> Air 14i 14p 15h 6wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 0h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 18i 14p 14h 9wp<br /> Water 31i 14p 8h 8wp<br /> Wood 10i 14p 6h 7wp<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Fire Dragon moves back into range with the Solar and attacks with a decisive 5m 4i Fiery Blade Attack with 6m Excellency and 3m 1wp Perfect Blazing Blow. Solar will not spend anything to defend.<br /> <br /> Rolling 17 dice to hit and getting it with 10, then rolling 14i damage for 9 after rerolls, setting the Solar on fire.<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 4p 1h 3wp 10L(-1s)<br /> Air 14i 14p 15h 6wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 0h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 3i 14p 0h 9wp<br /> Water 31i 14p 8h 8wp<br /> Wood 10i 14p 6h 7wp<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Air Dragon rolls 1 damage for anima<br /> <br /> Air dragon will spend 5m to flurry a disengage with a decisive attack, and spend 6m and a willpower on the attack. The Solar will not spend motes to defend. Rolling 15+1 dice the Air Dragon hits. Rolling 12i damage after Bulwark Stance for 8L.<br /> <br /> Then rolling to disengage with 9 dice opposed by the prone, wounded Solar's 6. Failing with 4 against 6 successes.<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 4p 1h 3wp 19L(-2s)<br /> Air 3i 12p 0h 4wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 0h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 3i 14p 0h 9wp<br /> Water 31i 14p 8h 8wp<br /> Wood 10i 14p 6h 7wp<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Wood Dragon rolls 1L of anima damage. Solar has to roll against poison. Rolling 9 dice for 5, he's poisoned for 3 rounds.<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon attempts another 3m 2i Soul-Marking Style with a 6m excellency and willpower. Solar will not spend motes to defend. Rolling 22 dice for 15 Wood Dragon hits, then rollign 8i damage for 4L, hitting the Solar with Soul-Marking Style.<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 4p 1h 3wp 23L(-2s)<br /> Air 3i 12p 0h 4wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 0h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 3i 14p 0h 9wp<br /> Water 31i 14p 8h 8wp<br /> Wood 3i 5p 6h 6wp<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Solar rolls 9 dice to resist burning, rolling 9 dice and failing with 4, taking 1L damage<br /> <br /> Solar activates Bulwark Stance for 5m 1wp.<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 0p 0h 2wp 23L(-2s)<br /> Air 3i 12p 0h 4wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 0h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 3i 14p 0h 9wp<br /> Water 31i 14p 8h 8wp<br /> Wood 3i 14p 6h 7wp<br /> <br /> Wood Anima deals no damage.<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ==========<br /> Solar -7i 0p 5h 2wp 23L(-2s)<br /> Air 3i 12p 5h 4wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 5h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 3i 14p 5h 9wp<br /> Water 31i 14p 13h 8wp<br /> Wood 3i 14p 11h 7wp<br /> <br /> Solar uses 1m to reflexively draw his sidearm mundane blade.<br /> <br /> Water anima deals 1L damage<br /> <br /> Water Dragon uses 7m 1wp Twin Dragon's Dancing to attack with the Air aspect, who will supplement it with 8m 1wp Lightning Strike Style. The Water Dragon herself will use 5m 1wp Essence-Dousing Wave Attack and 3m Drowning in Blood Technique. Willpower will be used all around to boost attacks and defenses.<br /> <br /> The Water dragon goes first, the Solar spending 2m to raise defense and 1m on Dipping Swallow. Water Dragon rolls 19+1 dice for 11, hitting the Solar.<br /> <br /> Then rolling 31i damage for 12L, and choosing to deactivate Fivefold Bulwark Stance with Essense Dousing.<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 0p 1h 0wp 36L(-3s)<br /> Air 3i 12p 5h 4wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 5h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 3i 14p 5h 9wp<br /> Water 31i 14p 13h 8wp<br /> Wood 3i 14p 11h 7wp<br /> <br /> Air then attacks, rolling 17 dice for 8, easily hitting defense zero, then rolling 40i damage for 13L damage.<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 0p 1h 0wp 49L(-3s)<br /> Air 3i 9p 0h 2wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 5h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 3i 14p 5h 9wp<br /> Water 3i 14p 13h 8wp<br /> Wood 3i 14p 11h 7wp<br /> -----------<br /> Earth anima deals no damage<br /> <br /> Earth dragon makes a decisive attack with 1m excellency and 3m Force of the Mountain, hitting easily and dealing 5L<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 0p 1h 0wp 54L(-3s)<br /> Air 3i 9p 0h 2wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 1h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 3i 14p 5h 9wp<br /> Water 3i 14p 13h 8wp<br /> Wood 3i 14p 11h 7wp<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Wood uses 6m excellency with 5m 1wp Unbreakable Facination Kata, easily beating the Solar's resolve with 10 successes on 19 dice, and without willpower to resist the Solar is bound by unbreakable facination.<br /> <br /> Solar -7i 0p 1h 0wp 54L(-3s)<br /> Air 3i 9p 0h 2wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Earth 16i 9p 1h 5wp 14L(-2s)<br /> Fire 3i 14p 5h 9wp<br /> Water 3i 14p 13h 8wp<br /> Wood 3i 14p 0h 6wp<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> As far as I'm aware, that's what it looks like when a full hearth of ultimate legendary super optimized DBs battles a likewise ultimate legendary Solar, at Essence 3 anyway. With too many health levels to chew through to knock down opponents quickly, and with tricks like Essence Dousing Wave that deactivate ongoing scenelong charms, or poison, or burn, there's just too much weight of things the Solar needs to deal with using motes and willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:32:03-07:00","id":1386495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386476#post1386476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you run anything in the end? Feel like you'll want at least two opponents to fully experience initiative bouncing around...<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to do something similar with a friend, running a DB magistrate rescuing his archon and being ambushed by brigands who are going to try to exploit different weapons tags/gambits (if we can make it work).</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't yet, but there's still time. Still not sure what to run. Maybe two hungry ghosts or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:53:07-07:00","id":1386570,"title":"","content":"Well we ran it, 3 hungry ghosts at night during a storm. It worked out pretty well! The three ghosts got off some claws against his mortal friend, who went dry on willpower, and he didn't end up dipping too far into peripheral motes but did come out of it a bit drained. I say success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:31:45-07:00","id":1386595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386570#post1386570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well we ran it, 3 hungry ghosts at night during a storm. It worked out pretty well! The three ghosts got off some claws against his mortal friend, who went dry on willpower, and he didn't end up dipping too far into peripheral motes but did come out of it a bit drained. I say success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell us the best stunt to come out of the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T20:22:50-07:00","id":1386602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386595#post1386595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell us the best stunt to come out of the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there wasn't much stunting going on. It's kind of hard to stunt while going back and forth with the lag saying things like &quot;Okay, but this is withering so I double tens, but also it's a clash right so I just have to beat their roll. Oh I deal extra damage if I win the clash? Can I clash a Decisive with a withering?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T23:01:45-07:00","id":1386620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386492#post1386492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone 100% maximized for combat, or at least as far as I can tell..</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd like to see the Solar sheet please and tactics cause uhhh<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T23:19:51-07:00","id":1386622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1386620#post1386620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd like to see the Solar sheet please and tactics cause uhhh</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t have a sheet, I just assumed everyone had 5s in every relevant ability and any charm I could thing would be useful at the time.<br /> <br /> Tactic was to take out as many DBs in an alpha strike as to not get buried under a full five times the actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T19:05:39-07:00","id":1389158,"title":"","content":"Shining Topaz is... less optimized than she could be. I could totally get away with 5/5/1 physical instead of 3/5/3. I also spent her BP mostly on charms instead of WP or maximizing attributes.<br /> <br /> She's close to optimized in combat tho. Although she could do with more investment in the range tree that keys off call the blade and excellent strike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T19:07:37-07:00","id":1389159,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> Something you brought up in another discussion brings something to my mind...<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you were to build the protagonist of <i>Sekiro</i> in Exalted, what would you have him be?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T19:33:39-07:00","id":1389165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1389159#post1389159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIf you were to build the protagonist of <i>Sekiro</i> in Exalted, what would you have him be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the questions isn't for me but I just have to say...<br /> <br /> Sekiro is an undying champion with a strong tie to the child who brought him back to life. He is tasked with killing things which violate the natural order of life and death. I don't know what I'd make him from the currently released splat, but among all splats? It's hard to be more Liminal than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T19:47:49-07:00","id":1389169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1389159#post1389159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIf you were to build the protagonist of <i>Sekiro</i> in Exalted, what would you have him be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, tough call. I'd definitely say he is like a Dawn Single Point stylist, but for some reason I keep feeling like he fits night better. Maybe its just because he's so damn athletic most of the time, and stealth is a major part of what he does. If I was building him as a DB I wouldn't have him go single point, but rather melee. Especially since he has exactly Lightning-Drinking Blade.<br /> <br /> Epitome is right though that Liminal might fit the best. He's even got swappable arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T11:37:27-07:00","id":1390593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387071-naval-combat-system?p=1390560#post1390560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you might need to go with like, 5-6 rather than 3. The upshot is that the outnumbered penalty doesn't count the caliber of ship you're facing, so two corsairs and four fast attack ships still count as a -10 penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see if this works and how hard it is to run. An Eclipse heavily invested into Sail, at Essence 1 in a Blue Water Merchant ship with no Essence 3 charms vs two Corsairs and 4 fast attack pirate ships.<br /> <br /> The Solar's base dicepool will be 11, the pirates will use the stats of The Bloodthirsty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 0 Eclipse 46m 5wp<br /> 0 Cors1<br /> 0 Cors2<br /> 0 Fasa1<br /> 0 Fasa2<br /> 0 Fasa3<br /> 0 Fasa4<br /> <br /> <br /> First roll, the Solar will use 2m for Immortal Mariner's Advantage, 2m for Superior Positioning Technique, 5m for Sea Serpent Flash, 4m for Implacable Sea Wolf Spirit, 1m Ocean Conquering Avatar, opposing Cors1<br /> <br /> <br /> Eclipse rolls 9+1 dice for 7, then rerolling 2 dice for a total of 8.<br /> <br /> Cors1 gets 5<br /> Cors2 gets 6<br /> Fasa1 gets 6<br /> Fasa2 gets 5<br /> Fasa3 gets 3<br /> Fasa4 gets 3<br /> <br /> Eclipse beats all and wins by 3, which due to Sea Serpent Flash gives 6 momentum<br /> <br /> 6 Eclipse 32m 5wp<br /> 0 Cors1<br /> 0 Cors2<br /> 0 Fasa1<br /> 0 Fasa2<br /> 0 Fasa3<br /> 0 Fasa4<br /> ========================<br /> Next round, the eclipse will attempt a ram against Cors1, using 2m for Immortal mariner's Advantage, and 2m for Superior Positioning Technique, and 3m for Ship Breaker Method, along with a 10m excellency.<br /> <br /> Rolling 11 dice for 6, then rerolling 4 dice for a total of 9.<br /> <br /> Cors1 gets 5<br /> Cors2 gets 6<br /> Fasa1 gets 3<br /> Fasa2 gets 2<br /> Fasa3 gets 5<br /> Fasa4 gets 5<br /> <br /> Cors1 takes 3 levels of hull damage<br /> <br /> 1 Eclipse 15m 5wp<br /> 0 Cors1 3L (-4s)<br /> 0 Cors2<br /> 0 Fasa1<br /> 0 Fasa2<br /> 0 Fasa3<br /> 0 Fasa4<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think I'm going to call that there since the Solar doesn't even have enough motes left to do that again, and without being able to full excellency the rolls that's a mighty big penalty to be eating. My suggestion at this point for the Eclipse is to instead of staying to fight, use the first two turns to gather up to 10 momentum and then use the Escape maneuver, which will lead to a pursuit that does not suffer stacking multiple opponent penalties.<br /> <br /> I also don't necessarily think that two corsairs and four fast attack ships is an unreasonable fleet, it even says that's standard procedure for the Bloodthirsty. It would still be nice to have some more powerful sail based antagonists, but I'm confidant that a legendary Peleps captain at the head of a battlegroup of six Realm triremes is certainly enough to challenge a Solar sailor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T13:51:09-07:00","id":1390618,"title":"","content":"Is it a fun encounter?<br /> <br /> I don't particularly care if the Solar always wins or never wins. What am I actually doing with Sail?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T14:10:44-07:00","id":1390622,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1390593#post1390593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I also don't necessarily think that two corsairs and four fast attack ships is an unreasonable fleet, it even says that's standard procedure for the Bloodthirsty. It would still be nice to have some more powerful sail based antagonists, but I'm confidant that a legendary Peleps captain at the head of a battlegroup of six Realm triremes is certainly enough to challenge a Solar sailor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you consider just making up some Sail antagonists by picking a dice pool and some charms? I tried to do this once but didn't end up running the fight with them. It doesn't seem nearly as complicated as designing enemies for the ordinary combat system. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1390618#post1390618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it a fun encounter?<br /> <br /> I don't particularly care if the Solar always wins or never wins. What am I actually doing with Sail?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that this is the most important question to ask but it's probably not so relevant to answer until DrLoveMonkey runs an encounter that the PC wins, because, even if the encounter were super fun, if the heroes are defeated it's not the kind of fun you can have very often. (although if the Eclipse is supported by a full Circle they might not have trouble escaping the destruction of their ship, swimming or flying to one of the attacking ships, defeating its crew, and taking it over, to possibly then be blown up by the remaining ships, until they finally get their enemies down to a manageable number or otherwise escape with a ship off to the next battle. For an Essence 1 Eclipse alone that might be a tall order.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 05-21-2020, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T22:26:24-07:00","id":1390705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1390618#post1390618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it a fun encounter?<br /> <br /> I don't particularly care if the Solar always wins or never wins. What am I actually doing with Sail?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, although I didn't really make this to be fun, I didn't include any environmental effects or anything like that. My opinion was formed by the one and only time I've seen a Sail supernal Solar in a game, and it really quickly ended up with him not taking any more sail charms, and skipping or avoiding combats because it was boring and pointless. By the end of the campaign he had a rival captain that he had to face down, and he defeated them in two rounds, one to build up a huge amount of initiative, and the other to ram his ship in half.<br /> <br /> It did so little to endear the sail system to everyone that we basically all agreed it was not something we were going to use again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1390622#post1390622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bDid you consider just making up some Sail antagonists by picking a dice pool and some charms? I tried to do this once but didn't end up running the fight with them. It doesn't seem nearly as complicated as designing enemies for the ordinary combat system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the above example was with a homebrew exigent but the ST had to invent basically the whole thing himself, and with the rule that nobody else's charms are allowed to be as good as Solar charms, it made it pretty difficult. He had a slightly smaller dicecap and maybe double 9s on the roll or something, but compared to all the crazy things the Eclipse was bringing out it was totally hopeless.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's impossible, duh, I could just say &quot;This Raksha has 30 dice to his sail rolls, and a charm that lets him re-roll a failed die for every one of yours that comes up a fail&quot; and yeah, that guy would be strong enough to battle a Solar. That's also not at all congruant with basically any other statblock in the game. I'm totally cool with making some slight modifications, like a walking statue with two heads that can flurry a command action with an attack without penalty, or a dire-bear who's got a little dice bump here or there.<br /> <br /> Making something that powerful, though, when I have nothing really to base it off of though is hard. Particularly since the few examples we do have like the Armored Kraken are super weak, so whatever behemoth or captain I come up with would just have to be literally three times as powerful as anything else printed. Do such things exist? Is there only one ever? I don't know. Should I try to balance it other ways?<br /> <br /> Regular combat shakes out that way as well. Nothing can challenge a player directly, but innumerable stacked troubles actually can. Even still though, there's enemies like the Haloed Husk who basically have no business being in the game whatsoever. They're not a Lunar form, they're not a familiar, and they're so piss weak I couldn't even justify using them in a mortals campaign. If all I had to work with was Haloed Husks, I would not really feel up to creating Alhat myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1390618#post1390618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that this is the most important question to ask but it's probably not so relevant to answer until DrLoveMonkey runs an encounter that the PC wins, because, even if the encounter were super fun, if the heroes are defeated it's not the kind of fun you can have very often. (although if the Eclipse is supported by a full Circle they might not have trouble escaping the destruction of their ship, swimming or flying to one of the attacking ships, defeating its crew, and taking it over, to possibly then be blown up by the remaining ships, until they finally get their enemies down to a manageable number or otherwise escape with a ship off to the next battle. For an Essence 1 Eclipse alone that might be a tall order.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There are definitely ways you could win that for sure, but they, blessedly, do not involve absentmindedly shrugging and saying &quot;Full excellency?&quot; and then just moving on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:05:26-07:00","id":1391273,"title":"","content":"Okay, so what if a Solar is neither hopelessly outnumbered, nor are they in a 1v1 fight against something that can never beat them?<br /> <br /> The setup here is that Eduward the Eclipse Caste pirate captain has been using the large seaside town of Pargon as a home base. Captain Peleps Emeril has gotten word of this heresy and is coming to raze the town to the ground. Maybe not kill everyone there, but definitely burn their houses down, they're heretics harboring demons and word needs to spread that this kind of behavior is liable to get you killed.<br /> <br /> Eduward and his small circle have learned that Emeril plans on taking a fast battlegroup of three triremes and land at three different spots, ordering his marines to get to work. Sadly even Solars can't be in three places at once, and although they'd surely win the fight eventually, that doesn't save half the town from being engulfed in flame. They're going to intercept the battlegroup before they make landfall in their Blue-Water Merchant ship equipped with ballistae.<br /> <br /> We'll start out with a pursuit of Eduward after Emeril's battlegroup to catch them before they make landfall. Eduward's blue-water merchant ship has an empty cargo hold but Emerils ships have their oars out.<br /> <br /> Eduward's Stats<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Sail 5 with specialty, wits 4 (Base pool 10+9)<br /> Essence 2 with 5 motes committed to a weapon giving 51 motes<br /> <br /> Speed currently +4, maneuverability +0<br /> <br /> Crew has Sail 3<br /> <br /> Salty Dog Method<br /> Ship-Sleeking Technique<br /> Immortal Mariner's Advantage<br /> Legendary Captain's Signature<br /> Deck Sweeping Fusillade<br /> Superior Positioning Technique<br /> Tide-cutting Essence Infusion<br /> Wave-Riding Discipline<br /> Hull-Taming Transfusion<br /> Indomitable Voyager's Perseverance<br /> Ocean Conquering Avatar<br /> Implacable Sea Wolf Spirit<br /> Sea Serpent Flash<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Emeril's Stats<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Sail 5 with specialty, wits 4 (Base pool 10+6)<br /> Essence 3 with 5 motes committed to a weapon, giving 44 motes<br /> <br /> Speed of triremes is currently +5, maneuverability +2<br /> <br /> Allied triremes have a naval maneuver pool of 8<br /> <br /> Fine Passage Negotiating Style<br /> Storm Outrunning Technique<br /> Ocean Darting Maneuver<br /> Sea Dragon's Cunning<br /> Sturdy Bulkhead Concentration<br /> Hull Shattering Avalanche Impact<br /> Mountain-Hull Meditation<br /> Vanishing Fog-Bank Escape<br /> Bellowing Thunder Admiral<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Pursuit<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Eduward uses 4m Ship-Sleeking Technique, 5m 1wp Wave-Riding Discipline to gain a bonus +3 speed<br /> Emeril is unable to boost the speed of all her ships with charms<br /> <br /> The trireme captains roll 13 dice for 6 successes<br /> Eduward rolls 17 dice for 10 successes after rerolling 6s, catching the battlegroup well before they make landfall.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The small Realm battlegroup catches sight of a ship, Eduward's <i>Sunbeam</i> coming up hard behind them, planing up out of the water with impossible speed and sending a spray of salt water from its bow. Emeril turns and orders his crew to prepare to repel boarders and man the ballista.<br /> <br /> Battle<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Eduward 42m 4wp<br /> Emeril 44m 5wp<br /> Tri1<br /> Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ================<br /> Eduward targets Emeril, spending 1m for Ocean-Conquering Avatar, 2m Superior Positioning Technique, 2m for Immortal Mariner's Advantage, 3m Legendary Captain's Signature, 4m Implacable Sea Wolf Spirit, 5m Sea Serpent Flash. Rolling 14+1 dice with rerolling 6s, 1s, and double 9s for 10 successes. Then spending 1wp for Indomitable Voyager's Perseverance for another 3 successes, totaling 13.<br /> <br /> Emeril uses 6m excellency, 3m Sea Dragon's Cunning, rolling 18 dice with rerolling 6s and double 9s, getting 12 successes after rerolls.<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 rolls 10 dice for 7 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 rolls 10 dice for 8 successes.<br /> <br /> The only one who wins out here is Eduward, with 6 successes over Trireme 1, which ends up doubled with Sea Serpent Flash for 12 momentum<br /> <br /> <br /> 12 Eduward 25m 3wp<br /> 0 Emeril 35m 5wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> 0 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =================<br /> Eduward makes for a broadside maneuver using first age weaponry, spending 2m for Immortal Mariner's Advantage, 2m for Deck-Sweeping Fusillade, and 4m for excellency. Rolling 14 dice and getting 11 successes after rerolls. This maneuver costing only 3 momentum due to Sea Wolf Spirit<br /> <br /> Emeril uses 6m Excellency, 3m Sea Dragon's Cunning, rolling 18 dice and getting 12 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 rolls 10 dice for 7 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 rolls 10 dice for 7 successes.<br /> <br /> Foom! The barrage of first age weaponry pummels the first trireme, inflicting massive damage. Again only Eduward achieves victory, but Sea Dragon's Cunning means Emeril still gets 1 momentum.<br /> <br /> <br /> 9 Eduward 17m 3wp<br /> 1 Emeril 26m 5wp<br /> 0 Tri1 2hul (-1s)<br /> 0 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =================<br /> Eduward comes around for another broadside on the same trireme, using another 2m for Immortal Mariner's Advantage, and 2m for Deck-Sweeping Fusillade. Rolling 10 dice for 7 successes.<br /> <br /> Emeril again tries the same maneuver, with full excellency and sea dragon's cunning. Getting an impressive 15 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 rolls 9 dice for 9 successes, amazingly actually just slipping past Eduward's fusillade<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 rolls 10 dice for 6 successes and fails to gain momentum.<br /> <br /> 6 Eduward 13m 3wp<br /> 8 Emeril 17m 5wp<br /> 0 Tri1 2hul (-1s)<br /> 0 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> =================<br /> Eduward tries again for another broadside, this time spending 2m for IMA, 2m DSF, and 8m for an excellency. Rolling 18 dice for only 6 successes, but then rerolling for a total of 11.<br /> <br /> Emeril uses 6m excellency, and 6m 1a 1wp Hull-Shattering Avalance Impact, rolling 18 dice for only 9 even with double 8s, missing the hull shattering impact.<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 rolls 9 dice for 4 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 rolls 10 dice for 2 successes<br /> <br /> A second bout of explosions rocks the trireme as the first age weaponry breaks the hull in half and sends the sailors and marines scattering among the waves!<br /> <br /> 0 Eduward 1m 3wp<br /> 1 Emeril 5m 4wp<br /> 0 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> =================<br /> Eduward selects the second trireme as his target, spending 1m to double 9s and rolling 8 dice for 5 successes after rerolls<br /> <br /> Emeril tries a positioning maneuver, and spends 1m, rolling 13 dice for 8 successes.<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 rolls 10 dice for 8 successes.<br /> <br /> 0 Eduward 0m 3wp<br /> 4 Emeril 4m 4wp<br /> 3 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> =================<br /> Eduward tries to position again, rolling 8 dice for 3 successes.<br /> <br /> Emeril spends another mote, rolling 13 dice for 11 successes after rerolls.<br /> <br /> Tri2 rolls 10 dice for 4 successes.<br /> <br /> 0 Eduward 0m 3wp<br /> 13 Emeril 3m 4wp<br /> 4 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> =================<br /> Eduward gets 6 successes<br /> <br /> Emeril gets 7<br /> <br /> Trireme gets 8<br /> <br /> 0 Eduward 0m 3wp<br /> 14 Emeril 2m 4wp<br /> 6 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 7<br /> =================<br /> Eduward gets 6 successes<br /> <br /> Emeril gets 6 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme gets 5 successes<br /> <br /> 1 Eduward 0m 3wp<br /> 14 Emeril 1m 4wp<br /> 6 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 8<br /> =================<br /> Eduward gets 5 successes<br /> <br /> Emeril attempts a ram, getting 8 successes, and dealing 2 damage.<br /> <br /> Trireme also attempts a ram, getting 3 successes<br /> <br /> 1 Eduward 0m 3wp 2hul(-1s)<br /> 9 Emeril 0m 4wp<br /> 1 Tri2<br /> <br /> <br /> I think at this point it's a foregone conclusion.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay, so that strategy didn't work, since you can't really kill enemy ships fast enough and efficiently enough, so let's go for the lead vessel first this time<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Eduward 42m 4wp<br /> Emeril 44m 5wp<br /> Tri1<br /> Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ================<br /> Eduward targets Emeril, spending 1m for Ocean-Conquering Avatar, 2m Superior Positioning Technique, 2m for Immortal Mariner's Advantage, 3m Legendary Captain's Signature, 4m Implacable Sea Wolf Spirit, 5m Sea Serpent Flash. Rolling 14+1 dice with rerolling 6s, 1s, and double 9s for 10 successes. Then spending 1wp for Indomitable Voyager's Perseverance for another 3 successes, totaling 13.<br /> <br /> Emeril uses 6m excellency, 3m Sea Dragon's Cunning, rolling 18 dice with rerolling 6s and double 9s, getting 12 successes after rerolls, and giving Emeril another 4 successes with his 1s.<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 rolls 10 dice for 7 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 rolls 10 dice for 8 successes.<br /> <br /> The only one who wins out here is Eduward, with 5 successes over Emeril, which ends up doubled with Sea Serpent Flash for 10 momentum<br /> <br /> <br /> 10 Eduward 25m 3wp<br /> 0 Emeril 35m 5wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> 0 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ================<br /> Eduward goes for a broadside again, with 2m Immortal Mariner's Advantage, 2m Deck Sweeping Fusilade, and 4m excellency. Rolling 12 dice for 5 successes after rerolls.<br /> <br /> Emeril uses 6m excellency, 3m SDC, for 8 successes after rerolls, just beating Eduward.<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 rolls 10 dice for 5 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 rolls 10 dice for 3 successes<br /> <br /> 7 Eduward 17m 3wp<br /> 2 Emeril 26m 5wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> 0 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ================<br /> Eduward attempts another broadside, with the same charms, getting 8 successes this time, and then spending a willpower to reroll all failed dice for another 4 successes.<br /> <br /> Emeril uses a positioning maneuver with the same, getting 10 successes after rerolls<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 gets 4 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 gets 5 succesess<br /> <br /> Eduward explodes a massive hole in the side of Emeril's trireme<br /> <br /> 4 Eduward 9m 2wp<br /> 2 Emeril 17m 5wp 1hul(-1s)<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> 0 Tri2<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ================<br /> Eduard goes for the kill with another fusillade from first age weaponry, getting 6 successes, and spending a willpower to reroll for another 6<br /> <br /> Emeril spends 9m to excellency and SDC, and a willpower for an auto success. Rolling 17+1 dice for 10 successes. In a last desperate attempt to avoid the trireme going down he uses 4m 1a Sturdy Bulkhead Concentration, rolling 5 dice for 6 successes, preventing the final level of damage from going through.<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 rolls 3 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 rolls 6 successes<br /> <br /> 1 Eduward 1m 2wp<br /> 2 Emeril 4m 5wp 3hul(-4s)<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> 0 Tri2<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay that was a bit of a fluke though, if Sturdy Bulkhead concentration didn't go through though Eduward would still be in a pretty bad way, with no motes left facing more maneuverable ships at 2v1 odds. Still taking out the most powerful enemy ship first seems to be better.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to run it one more time but with just two triremes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> =============<br /> Eduward targets Emeril, spending 1m for Ocean-Conquering Avatar, 2m Superior Positioning Technique, 2m for Immortal Mariner's Advantage, 3m Legendary Captain's Signature, 4m Implacable Sea Wolf Spirit, 5m Sea Serpent Flash. Rolling 16+1 dice with rerolling 6s, 1s, and double 9s for 14 successes. Then spending 1wp for Indomitable Voyager's Perseverance for another 4 successes, totaling 18.<br /> <br /> Emeril spends 9m to excellency and 3m to SDC, rolling 18 dice for 14<br /> <br /> Trireme 2 gets 5<br /> <br /> 8 Eduward 25m 3wp<br /> 0 Emeril 35m 5wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =============<br /> Eduward goes for a broadside with 2m Immortal Mariner Advantage, 2m Deck Sweeping Fusillade, and 4m excellency. Rolling 14 dice for 10 successes after rerolls.<br /> <br /> Emeril uses full excellency and Sea Dragon Cunning to roll 18 dice, for a powerful 14 after rerolls.<br /> <br /> 5 Eduward 17m 3wp<br /> 3 Emeril 26m 5wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> =============<br /> Eduward goes for another broadside with the same charms, getting 13 successes on 14 dice<br /> <br /> Emeril uses the same and ends up with 12, who will then spend 4m 1a on Sturdy Bulkhead Concentration, rolling 5 dice and getting only one success, the full broadside goes through.<br /> <br /> 2 Eduward 9m 3wp<br /> 3 Emeril 13m 5wp 1hul(-1s)<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> =============<br /> Eduward goes for a positioning maneuver, with 2m for IMA, and 2m for Superior Positioning Technique, and a 4m excellency. Rolling 14 dice for 12 successes after rerolls<br /> <br /> Emeril uses full excellency and sea dragon cunning for 5 successes on 17 dice.<br /> <br /> 9 Eduward 1m 3wp<br /> 3 Emeril 4m 5wp 1hul(-1s)<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> =============<br /> Eduward fires one last broadside with 1m to double 9s. Rolling 8 dice for 4 successes, spending a willpower to reroll for no help<br /> <br /> Emeril spends 2m to excellency and rolls 11 dice, getting 6 and stopping the broadside</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so I think that the combination of triremes having +2 maneuverability compared to a blue water merchant combined with the -2 or -4 penalty for being outnumbered is just too much to overcome even for Solar charms. Let's give Eduward his own trireme, and also Sea Devil Training to his crew is super elite.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Round 1<br /> ===============<br /> Eduward targets Emeril, spending 1m for Ocean-Conquering Avatar, 2m Superior Positioning Technique, 2m for Immortal Mariner's Advantage, 3m Legendary Captain's Signature, 4m Implacable Sea Wolf Spirit, 5m Sea Serpent Flash. Rolling 20+1 dice with rerolling 6s, 1s, and double 9s for 13 successes. Then spending 1wp for Indomitable Voyager's Perseverance for another 3 successes, totaling 16.<br /> <br /> Emeril full excellency Sea Dragons for 14 successes on 18 dice after rerolls, but with one 1, giving Eduward another 2 successes.<br /> <br /> 8 Eduward 25m 3wp<br /> 0 Emeril 35m 5wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===============<br /> Eduward goes to broadside Emeril, spending 2m on IMA, and 2m on Fusillade, and 4m excellency. Rolling 18 dice for 14 successes after rerolls.<br /> <br /> Emeril tries for another full excellency sea dragon and gets 13 successes, failing to stop the broadside.<br /> <br /> 5 Eduward 17m 3wp<br /> 0 Emeril 26m 5wp 2hul (-1s)<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===============<br /> Eduward goes for the same tactic, getting ready to blow Emeril out of the water. getting 16 successes<br /> <br /> Emeril tries to maneuver, but only gets 10 successes, and Emeril's ship explodes under the fire of first age weaponry.<br /> <br /> 5 Eduward 9m 3wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ===============<br /> Eduward now goes to maneuver on trireme 1, spending 2m on IMA, rolling 14 dice for 10 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 rolls 10 dice for 6 successes<br /> <br /> 4 Eduward 7m 3wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ===============<br /> Eduward maneuvers again, rolling 14 dice for 8 successes<br /> <br /> Trireme 1 gets 6<br /> <br /> 6 Eduward 7m 3wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> ===============<br /> Eduward uses a broadside with 2m Fusillade, getting 13 successes and blowing a massive hole in the trireme, I won't roll to see if trireme 1 can match that.<br /> <br /> 6 Eduward 5m 3wp<br /> 0 Tri1<br /> <br /> Round 7<br /> ===============<br /> Eduward goes in for the kill, with no mote enhancement, getting 7 successes to his opponent's 8 and finishing off the Realm battlegroup<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay, yep, there we go. That definitely did it, and is a lot closer to my experience with actual sail in play. Maneuverability and Crew play a pretty big part, especially since the dice tricks get magnified by the number of dice you're rolling. It does seem to work, but there's not much in the way of back and forth, and it does seem like the balance is really easily tipped one way or the other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:25:26-07:00","id":1391358,"title":"","content":"After further thought, I think another issue might be that there feels like there's less to do in the naval combat stuff. Gathering momentum is just harder than gathering initiative, and you don't start with any either. If you have no momentum there's really only one thing to do, try to maneuver, and if you do have it there's not a <i>whole </i>lot you can do with it? Like you can do a concealment strategem for 2 momentum, but why? You need to win the stratagem to activate concealment, and it just gives you a bonus on your next roll, why don't you just do whatever you were going to do on the second roll with the first?<br /> <br /> I wonder if this could be fixed with enough tweaks so that the charms don't have to be re-written in a kind of alternate system for Crucible of Legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:45:47-07:00","id":1391362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1391358#post1391358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if this could be fixed with enough tweaks so that the charms don't have to be re-written in a kind of alternate system for Crucible of Legends.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought about this a little, but given that the Solar Sail charmset does not seem well-balanced and also isn't particularly exciting (except for some Charms that don't interact directly with the naval combat system), the Dragonblooded Sail charmset is OK, and the Lunar Sail charmset is nonexistant, it might be better to redesign the system and redo a bunch of Charms rather than stay shackled to the current approach.<br /> <br /> I guess they're not very likely to do that in Crucible of Legends though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 05-24-2020, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:55:53-07:00","id":1391365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1391362#post1391362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought about this a little, but given that the Solar Sail charmset does not seem well-balanced and also isn't particularly exciting (except for some Charms that don't interact directly with the naval combat system), the Dragonblooded Sail charmset is OK, and the Lunar Sail charmset is nonexistant, it might be better to redesign the system and redo a bunch of Charms rather than stay shackled to the current approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's possible, but probably out of scope for just a small section of the DMG. With that you're probably looking at introducing a new book titled Victory at Sea or something like that and just having all the new sail charms in there with the new sail system.<br /> <br /> In doing so you might also be able to solve the kind of decker problem that Sail has right now as well. I'd do one myself if I thought anyone but me would use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T18:42:40-07:00","id":1391823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1391365#post1391365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In doing so you might also be able to solve the kind of decker problem that Sail has right now as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the decker problem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd do one myself if I thought anyone but me would use it. </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to make one right now, and currently working on converting the DB charmset (charm-by-charm, keeping all the sweet flavor). I'm going to think about Lunars next, and then Solars, which seem like the hardest, after.<br /> <br /> If you make something I'll at least playtest it to see how it compares, and maybe use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T18:50:27-07:00","id":1391825,"title":"","content":"Are there any posts that have a figth with the MA, 1- Steel Devil, 2- Single Point, 3- White Reaper 4- Black claw, 5- Courtesan Styles? Either DB or Solar.<br /> Im asking before diving into the 60 posts of this thread. Lets see what i find first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T18:54:38-07:00","id":1391827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1391823#post1391823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the decker problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>The name comes from the game Shadowrun, where a decker is basically a super computer whiz, but like, taken to a cyberpunk extreme. Something they used to be able to do is plug their brains into a computer and hack things at literal lightning speeds, like half a second and they had the whole compound on lockdown.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, that process involved a lot of battling your way through the computer system's cyber defenses, almost like actual combat just with computer programs. The thing is, for the decker this takes place in real time, and for every other character it takes place in the literal blink of an eye. So what happens in gameplay terms is everyone around the table grabs a book or goes out to get something to eat with the gamemaster and the decker play through their little side adventure.<br /> <br /> So any time an otherwise team based RPG like DnD or Shadowrun or Exalted has a mechanic that takes 100% of the focus and puts it on one player while the rest get to do nothing for extended periods of time, it's often called &quot;the decker problem&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sail kind of has that, with the slight exception that ending a sail combat could theoretically be quick, and lead into a personal scale combat with boarding actions, which if it was more common or encouraged might mitigate the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1391823#post1391823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you make something I'll at least playtest it to see how it compares, and maybe use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking of doing it in a way that works and changes the absolute minimum of charms, I think I've got something semi-decent but there's still some things I have to work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T18:58:53-07:00","id":1391828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1391825#post1391825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any posts that have a figth with the MA, 1- Steel Devil, 2- Single Point, 3- White Reaper 4- Black claw, 5- Courtesan Styles? Either DB or Solar.<br /> Im asking before diving into the 60 posts of this thread. Lets see what i find first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Single point definitely, and I think steel devil, if not I might run one anyway. What are you looking for specifically? And do you care if they're mixed, like Steel Devil + Fire Dragon or something?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T19:22:03-07:00","id":1391836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1391825#post1391825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any posts that have a figth with the MA, 1- Steel Devil, 2- Single Point, 3- White Reaper 4- Black claw, 5- Courtesan Styles? Either DB or Solar.<br /> Im asking before diving into the 60 posts of this thread. Lets see what i find first.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's been a few, mostly Single Point, and mostly by JohnDoe244, IIRC.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1314371#post1314371\">Steel Devil DB vs. Blood Apes</a> </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367602#post1367602\">Single Point Solar vs. Melee Solar</a> </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367860#post1367860\">Single Point Solar vs. Volfer</a> </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368070#post1368070\">Single Point DB vs. Volfer</a> </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372266#post1372266\">Dreaming Pearl Courtesan mini-adventure</a><br /> <br /> I don't remember any fights with White Reaper or Black Claw.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T19:52:02-07:00","id":1391842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1391828#post1391828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Single point definitely, and I think steel devil, if not I might run one anyway. What are you looking for specifically? And do you care if they're mixed, like Steel Devil + Fire Dragon or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont mind if they are mixed, but i want to see how good is their special trick.<br /> Like how many chain attacks a Steel Devil can realistically do and how usefull that is, how White Reaper works if its figthing a BG + one or two DB commanders.<br /> A representation of how a battle with Black claw (or White Veil) is supposes to look (im attacking, but people think im a victim. Or im in a figth while playing poker).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T23:26:23-07:00","id":1393014,"title":"","content":"Back in February I asked about Single Point versus Melee, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> posted a great battle wherein Melee trounced Single Point. I'd like to settle another such <i>Who Would Win</i> comparison: Melee or Brawl. <br /> <br /> Like last time, no special restrictions. Artifacts are ok, Sorcery is ok, other Skills are ok (Awareness, Dodge, Resistance etc). From Chargen. The only restriction is that Melee and Brawl must exclusively use their own combat skill- no Thrown, no MA, no Archery. Brawl is divided meaningfully between Striking and Grappling, but I don't care if you do one, the other, or both. <br /> <br /> For my money, I'd wager that if Grapple gets hands on the Melee, the fight is pretty much over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T01:07:32-07:00","id":1393033,"title":"","content":"Brawl wins because it can strike first and strip away Initiative before the attack even lands. Thunderclap Rush Attack wins the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-31-2020, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T01:35:09-07:00","id":1393037,"title":"","content":"Can the Brawler use Dodge or Resistance? Because Brawl has very poor defence compared to Melee, but on a real character this isn't a big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T01:58:41-07:00","id":1393038,"title":"","content":"yeah, I said things like Awareness, Dodge, Resistance were ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T02:41:03-07:00","id":1393043,"title":"","content":"Also, what Essence? I think Brawl gets very powerful from E3 onwards, though don't know if others would agree with that.<br /> <br /> And I assume this is Solars, not Dragonblood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T03:06:09-07:00","id":1393045,"title":"","content":"The goal is to test a Solar Melee Supernal vs a Solar Brawl Supernal, to see which of them is a better fighter. <br /> <br /> <u>Solar Melee vs Solar Brawl</u><br /> <br /> each solar can use <b>Artifact</b> <b>stats</b> for their weapons and armor, but no special evocations or effects. That makes the fight about specific artifacts and not the skills Melee or Brawl.<br /> <br /> for Sorcery, just Invulnerable Skin of Bronze is allowed. <br /> <br /> other <b>non-combat</b> Skills are ok (Awareness, Dodge, Resistance, Athletics etc).<br /> <br /> The battle takes place right out of character generation. <br /> <br /> <i>The only restrictions are: </i><br /> <br /> that Melee and Brawl must <u><b>exclusively</b></u> use their own <u><b>combat skill</b></u>- no Thrown, no MA, no Archery. They can't take each others skill either. <br /> <br /> As this is a Melee vs Brawl test, so no Command, Familiar, Followers, Allies, Elementals/Demons etc. just a One on One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T04:33:02-07:00","id":1393056,"title":"","content":"Awareness, Dodge, and Resistance are all combat skills. Are you sure you don\u2019t mean just \u201cskills you attack with?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:02:46-07:00","id":1393080,"title":"","content":"I think it's reasonable to read that as a reasonable synonym for Combat Abilities, the system term which specifically refers to Archery, Brawl, Melee and Thrown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T11:42:19-07:00","id":1393161,"title":"","content":"I don't see any way for Solar Brawl to <i>reliably </i>beat Solar Melee, based on Solar Charms alone.<br /> <br /> Solar Melee can use a Medium Weapon (Parry 7) with Hail Shattering Practice as a cap-breaking boost to Defence. Five Fold Bulwark Stance shuts down half the Solar Brawl tree and gives another +1 Parry for 1m.<br /> <br /> Brawl Decisives, Brawl Grapples and Brawl Disarms are trying to hit Parry 8-13+ on 11-21 dice.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean Brawl can't win. Get lucky <i>once </i>with Heaven Thunder Hammer and you've won. Knockout Blow. Ox-Stunning Blow. The tools are there. But they require you to make a wildly improbable roll to get their effects off.<br /> <br /> With Artifacts, it's much better. Heaven and Earth Gauntlets and you get Clash bonuses and can Smash your foe Prone. Frost Thorn Knuckles or Mela's Coil also good (though I'm going to move away from using any Artifact 5s in the Arena from now on). But even then, you can Hail Shatter on a Clash, but you can't use use Reckless Fury Discard (and RFD costs Initative to use, even if the mote costs are approximately equal at this level -- I'd still argue RFD is WAAY more expensive). But even then, the most powerful Brawl effects (like * Fists of Battle) require unarmed attacks. Which is great because that means you can never be disarmed, have 5 more motes etc.... but also means you lose out on Artifact statlines to hit and damage.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't know how to build the characters to duel them (does the Brawl character take any Charms that key off Onslaught at all?). But I don't see a winning strategy for Brawl here (except, like Single Point, open with an improbable nova strike and hope to Heaven Thunder Hammer one-shot kill Melee).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-01-2020, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T11:57:27-07:00","id":1393167,"title":"","content":"From my experience JohnDoe has it about right. Especially where you need to ask do you build a brawl character to specifically kill a melee one, or one who's just good all around and might have several charms be nearly useless against the melee fighter?<br /> <br /> Also making these chargen characters and not 5s in everything every single charm characters changes things a whoooole lot. When you can easily take five ox bodies and Iron Skin Concentration and stuff it changes the calculus of the combat completely. It's why epic BS Solar can win against 5 DBs built normally, but then loses against 5DBs who have BS statlines and charm lists, having 30 health levels just does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T16:05:45-07:00","id":1393245,"title":"","content":"Is the forum double posting for anyone else? Or is it just me?<br /> <br /> On topic, build me a brawler and I'd be willing to run a fight against Topaz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T17:50:38-07:00","id":1393268,"title":"","content":"I haven't posted in this thread in a while, but I just got done statting out two dummies for this test.<br /> <br /> Bobby the Brawler is a grapple monster that relies on his crazy soak of 27 and Essence Gathering Temper for defence.<br /> <br /> Sally the Swordmaster has a fairly balanced build, with a parry of 8 from horseback and using Invincible Fury of the Dawn for damage.<br /> <br /> you can check them out on LCA: cdPHKcPxJx9cLu3CjqV5fHT6<br /> <br /> I predict that it'll be hard for Bobby to land the grapple without some outstanding luck, hopefully he can survive long enough to get a couple of tries in, since once he gets crashed he'll most likely be chopped to bits. If he does land the grapple though then it'll be an instant kill for sure.<br /> I'll post the fight later.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:09:37-07:00","id":1393312,"title":"","content":"Just finished the fight, I'm dumb and don't know how to use spoilers so here's the battle report:<br /> <br /> Bobby and Sally both roll join battle with a full excellency: Bobby rolls 21 dice for 12 successes and starts at 15, Sally rolls 22 dice for 8 successes and starts at 11. Both rise to Glowing anima.<br /> <br /> ROUND 1<br /> <br /> Bobby goes first, goes for the grapple gambit:<br /> Vicious Lunge + Devil Strangling Attitude + River Binding Wrath + Dragon Coil Technique + 10 excellency dice and 1 willpower for 21 dice rerolling 5s and 6s and 1 automatic success for 16 motes and 1 willpower. Rises to Burning anima.<br /> Sally defends with 10 excellency dice and 1 willpower + being mounted for 14 Parry for 10 motes and 1 willpower. Rises to Burning anima.<br /> Bobby rolls 10 successes so he misses. He loses 3 initiative and drops to 12.<br /> Sally swings a withering attack:<br /> Divine Executioner Stance + Fire and Stones Strike x5 for 17 dice and +5 post soak damage for 6m. Rises to Bonfire anima.<br /> Bobby defends with Essence Gathering Temper for 5 Parry for 1 initiative.<br /> Sally rolls 9 successes so she hits with 4 threshold successes, meaning her raw damage is 21. Bobby has 27 soak so he reduces it to overwhelming 5 plus Fire and Stones Strike for 10 post soak damage. Bobby gains 5 motes from Essence Gathering Temper.<br /> Sally rolls 10 dice for damage and rolls 2 successes. She raises to 14 initiative and Bobby drops to 9. She triggers One Weapon Two Blows and does the same withering attack for 9 motes.<br /> Bobby defends with 4 Parry.<br /> Sally rolls 4 successes so she hits with 0 threshold. Post soak damage is 10.<br /> Sally rolls 10 dice for damage and rolls 4 successes. She raises to 19 initiative and Bobby drops to 5.<br /> <br /> ROUND 2<br /> <br /> Sally delays her action, paying 2 initiative and dropping to 17.<br /> Bobby tries another grapple gambit:<br /> Vicious Lunge + Devil Strangling Attitude + River Binding Wrath + Dragon Coil Technique + 6 excellency dice and 1 willpower for 17 dice rerolling 5s and 6s and 3 automatic successes for 12 motes and 1 willpower. Rises to Bonfire anima.<br /> Sally clashes with a withering attack:<br /> Divine Executioner Stance + Excellent Strike + 4 excellency dice and 1 willpower for 21 dice rerolling 1s and 2 automatic successes for 8 motes and 1 willpower.<br /> Bobby rolls 14 successes, Sally rolls 22 successes; Sally wins the clash. Her post soak damage is 5.<br /> Sally rolls 5 dice for damage and rolls 1 success; she deals 3 automatic damage from wining the clash. She rises to 22 and Bobby drops to 1. She pays 1 mote, 1 willpower and 3 levels of anima to activate Peony Blossom Attack and makes a withering attack with no additional charms. Her anima drops to Dim.<br /> Bobby has 0 Parry.<br /> Sally rolls 13 dice for 5 successes so she hits. Her post soak damage is 5.<br /> She rolls 5 dice for 5 successes and crashes Bobby. She rises to 33 initiative and Bobby drops to -4.<br /> <br /> ROUND 3<br /> <br /> Sally activates Iron Whirlwind Attack + Gleaming Sever for 7m 1w 1i. Her anima increases to Glowing. She is at 0 motes now. She makes 5 decisive attacks.<br /> Bobby still has 0 Parry. Gleaming Sever gives 1 automatic success to the attack roll and extra successes don\u2019t matter so I\u2019m just gonna roll damage.<br /> First attack, 9 dice, Bobby uses Invincible God Metal Flash for 10 motes and 3 anima, shattering the Invincible Skin of Bronze to reduce the raw damage by 6. His anima drops to Dim. Sally rolls 3 dice for 0 damage.<br /> Second attack, 9 dice for 5 lethal damage. Bobby takes a crippling injury, losing an arm and negating all damage.<br /> Third attack, 8 dice for 4 lethal damage.<br /> Fourth attack, 8 dice for 2 lethal damage.<br /> Fifth attack, 8 dice for 4 lethal damage, exactly enough to incapacitate Bobby.<br /> <br /> End of fight status:<br /> Sally has 0 motes and 2/5 willpower left. Her anima is Dim. She is at full health.<br /> Bobby has 2 motes and 3/5 willpower left. His anima is Dim. He is dying.<br /> <br /> Soooo yeah, pretty much as expected. What surprised me but should have been obvious in hindsight is that at essence 1 neither had enough essence to use their Supernal wombo combos, so really only their basic sets of charms came into play. That said this was basically the perfect matchup for Sally, high overwhelming and high defense were pretty much the best counter for an infinite soak 1 hit kill monster. If Bobby was put up against a glacier-type boss like Ahlat or Octavian or a DBT build Lunar he'd tear them to pieces. I still think his build, the Solar tank grappler, works better with Resistance Supernal, since in general I've found its better to get your defensive stuff before your offense. If I were to build a Brawl supernal to counter Sally I'd probably have them go unarmed and mundane light armor and try and use Stealth to land a grapple from ambush and finish it quickly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:21:49-07:00","id":1393317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393312#post1393312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ROUND 2<br /> <br /> Sally delays her action, paying 2 initiative and dropping to 17.<br /> Bobby tries another grapple gambit:<br /> Vicious Lunge + Devil Strangling Attitude + River Binding Wrath + Dragon Coil Technique + 6 excellency dice and 1 willpower for 17 dice rerolling 5s and 6s and 3 automatic successes for 12 motes and 1 willpower. Rises to Bonfire anima.<br /> Sally clashes with a withering attack:<br /> Divine Executioner Stance + Excellent Strike + 4 excellency dice and 1 willpower for 21 dice rerolling 1s and 2 automatic successes for 8 motes and 1 willpower.<br /> Bobby rolls 14 successes, Sally rolls 22 successes; Sally wins the clash. Her post soak damage is 5.<br /> Sally rolls 5 dice for damage and rolls 1 success; she deals 3 automatic damage from wining the clash. She rises to 22 and Bobby drops to 1. She pays 1 mote, 1 willpower and 3 levels of anima to activate Peony Blossom Attack and makes a withering attack with no additional charms. Her anima drops to Dim.<br /> Bobby has 0 Parry.<br /> Sally rolls 13 dice for 5 successes so she hits. Her post soak damage is 5.<br /> She rolls 5 dice for 5 successes and crashes Bobby. She rises to 33 initiative and Bobby drops to -4.</div> </div> </div> </div>What lead to Bobby having 0 parry against the second attack? His onslaught reset at the start of his turn so he's at -1 onslaught. Losing a clash gives another -2, but I'd assume he has more than 3 base defense.<br /> I don't think that the Peony Blossom Defense would ignore defense because it's on the same turn as a clash - the seems like an odd interpretation of the clash rules.<br /> <br /> I don't think it would change much, since with the penalties his defense is probably only going above 5 if he spends a lot of motes, but it might be worth it to prevent the crash.<br /> Same for the attacks on the next round - given Sally is out of motes for the attack it seems likely it's worth it to spend some of those 10m making an attack miss instead of on Invincible God-Metal Flash.<br /> <br /> Actually - I had interpreted Invincible God-Metal Flash as costing (10m, 2a) or (3a), but it looks like you view it as costing 10m,(2a or 3a). Now that I read it with that in mind it looks ambiguous to me - how did other people interpret this?<br /> I'm not sure if this would be able to save Bobby - I assume he still ends round 3 with very few motes and a wound penalty, but he might have a shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:50:39-07:00","id":1393329,"title":"","content":"You're right I fucked that up cause I forgot to refresh his onslaught. He should have had Parry 2 against the Peony Blossom and 1 against the first hit of the IWA. For the Peony Blossom it wouldn't have affected the outcome since Sally would need to get over 15 threshold successes to deal anything more than her Overwhelming, but if he had used the 10 motes for a full excellency and willpower to put parry 7 against the first hit of the flurry he might have managed to block it. As you said I don't think it'd have changed the outcome, but you're right that it wasn't the most optimal play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:59:47-07:00","id":1393332,"title":"","content":"It also doesn\u2019t hurt that Divine Executioner stance is kind of broken if you make even a small effort to make it so. I\u2019m probably just not going to use it from now on. Certainly in my games the intimacy tied to it is going to be heavily policed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T23:26:55-07:00","id":1393369,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10131_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10131\" data-vbnamecard=\"10131\">BadassOverlord</a>. I was hoping Brawl would do better. <br /> <br /> You don't need to run it, but do you think the outcome would meaningfully change as Essence 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T05:15:14-07:00","id":1393399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393312#post1393312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo yeah, pretty much as expected. What surprised me but should have been obvious in hindsight is that at essence 1 neither had enough essence to use their Supernal wombo combos, so really only their basic sets of charms came into play. That said this was basically the perfect matchup for Sally, high overwhelming and high defense were pretty much the best counter for an infinite soak 1 hit kill monster. If Bobby was put up against a glacier-type boss like Ahlat or Octavian or a DBT build Lunar he'd tear them to pieces. I still think his build, the Solar tank grappler, works better with Resistance Supernal, since in general I've found its better to get your defensive stuff before your offense. If I were to build a Brawl supernal to counter Sally I'd probably have them go unarmed and mundane light armor and try and use Stealth to land a grapple from ambush and finish it quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth saying:<br /> <br /> Solar Brawl (like Mastery Single Point) is an absolutely amazing, WTF-HAX, over-powered to the point of painfullness, combat suite.<br /> <br /> When you look at a Solar combat suite, you compare it to every combat suite ever made, that was not made using Solar Melee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T05:51:16-07:00","id":1393401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393399#post1393399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth saying:<br /> <br /> Solar Brawl (like Mastery Single Point) is an absolutely amazing, WTF-HAX, over-powered to the point of painfullness, combat suite.<br /> <br /> When you look at a Solar combat suite, you compare it to every combat suite ever made, that was not made using Solar Melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it worth trying to run Solar Brawl vs. Solar Single Point? Are there other reasonable guesses for the second-best combat tree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T05:56:16-07:00","id":1393402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393369#post1393369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>. I was hoping Brawl would do better. <br /> <br /> You don't need to run it, but do you think the outcome would meaningfully change as Essence 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I somewhat doubt it. Brawl definitely gets better with more Essence, but there\u2019s a lot in Melee that gets crazy with it too. Like Rising Sun Slash or Hail Shattering, where effectively all your opponents 1s and 2s on an attack roll subtract from their successes. There\u2019s also some pretty crazy defence in Heavenly Guardian Defence, especially with Celestial Bliss. Melee has the advantage of being both one of the best offensive AND defensive abilities for Solars. Brawl need to try and use Dodge to close that gap, but then you\u2019re sacrificing heavy armor to do so.<br /> <br /> Also Solar melee has an infinite combo as long as motes/willpower last. Peony Blossom attack lets you reflexively launch Invincible Fury of the Dawn, and if you spend 15 motes in addition to it you have enough anima to reflexively trigger Peony blossom attack, which lets you reflexively trigger Invincible Fury of the Dawn again. <br /> <br /> As John says though, Solar Brawl Will absolutely destroy anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:05:31-07:00","id":1393411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393161#post1393161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you can Hail Shatter on a Clash</div> </div> </div> </div>Not according to Vance, and if you want to go by RAW you can Hail Shatter when clashing with Brawl because the strange way the rules for charm-ability compatibility are laid out*.<br /> <br /> RAW there's also the broken interaction of Supremacy of War Meditation and Brilliant Sentinel (full Brawl excellencies for 3m forever) that go in the favor of Brawl.<br /> <br /> *Or, arguably, Hail-Shattering Practice and a bunch of other Reflexive charms can't be used at all, ever, because they don't follow the rules for Reflexive charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 06-01-2020, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:06:56-07:00","id":1393412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393401#post1393401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Is it worth trying to run Solar Brawl vs. Solar Single Point? Are there other reasonable guesses for the second-best combat tree?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s pretty hard to pin down a second best tree, since a lot of them are so different, and also just because they might lose out to melee doesn\u2019t actually mean that they\u2019re bad, just that they\u2019re not better than melee at dueling.<br /> <br /> Also when you\u2019re talking about things like Thrown or especially Archery a major factor for them is they can sit a range band back from the action and pelt away with attacks without even having to worry about defending themselves. That means no motes spent on dodging, no risk of getting a lucky hit and losing health levels, 100% aggro damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:25:30-07:00","id":1393417,"title":"","content":"I think also, because of that, Thrown and Archery often probably do better in real play than in white-room arena, because you've got other PCs (or demons, or troops, or whatever) to tarpit the enemies while you sit a range band back.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, sometimes fights start in real play with everyone right up next to each other, or inside with little room to manouevre, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:28:31-07:00","id":1393419,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if it\u2019s a claustrophobic space with no room to get away that\u2019s a pretty big problem, but with Leaping Dodge Method starting in close is much less of an issue, you can just hammer your Evasion against the first attack you receive and you\u2019re away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:35:20-07:00","id":1393420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393332#post1393332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also doesn\u2019t hurt that Divine Executioner stance is kind of broken if you make even a small effort to make it so. I\u2019m probably just not going to use it from now on. Certainly in my games the intimacy tied to it is going to be heavily policed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really good for sure, but not any more broken than Thunderbolt Attack Prana or Heavenly Guardian Defense or any other solar charms you care to mention imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393401#post1393401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it worth trying to run Solar Brawl vs. Solar Single Point? Are there other reasonable guesses for the second-best combat tree?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Brawl will yeet Single Point into the atmosphere no contest. SP doesn't have any defense or accuracy enhancements beyond the excellency and can't negate penalties to parry, and Dodge at essence 1 doesn't provide enough since it caps at the same place as parry with a medium weapon. The first time SP attacks just use Blade Rebuking Wrath into Thunderclap Attack Rush + either a grapple doomcombo or Hammer on Iron Technique and the martial artist is d e a d.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393369#post1393369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10131_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10131\" data-vbnamecard=\"10131\">BadassOverlord</a>. I was hoping Brawl would do better.<br /> <br /> You don't need to run it, but do you think the outcome would meaningfully change as Essence 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might. Sally gets a bunch of offensive improvements, most remarkably Increasing Strength Exercise x5 and the Melee clash suite, but her defense doesn't meaningfully improve other than raising the cap on Hail-Shattering Practice: she already has pretty much all she needs at chargen; Fivefold Bulwark Stance and Victorious Wreath x2 are crazy good against multiple opponents but in a duel they aren't worth spending the motes, especially against a grappler.<br /> Her main strength is also her weakness: since her build is just Melee charms on top of more Melee charms, she suffers diminishing returns as she grows in essence. Awareness is a good candidate for spending some xp just to join battle harder and cheaper, but outside of that I don't know what off-Melee improvements to give her. If I wanted to cheese it I'd probably go into Ride and Survival and switch her horse out for a shieldback lizard or something since it's tanky af and they can reflexively defend each other with War Lion Stance and Worthy Mount Technique. Plus it can join battle with Ambush Predator Style and then immediately give half that initiative to Sally with Immortal Rider's Advantage for extra alpha striking. But I don't know if the side-grade into mounted tactics dilutes the pure-Melee premise too much, so I'd like to hear people's opinion.<br /> <br /> Bobby though gets a LOT better at essence 5. His defense, which previously was just having high soak, has been massively upgraded with Resistance charms all the way up to Aegis of Invincible Might. Against withering attacks, he can now get up to 10 motes each time he's hit, and Iron Kettle Body + the upgraded effect of Spirit Strengthens the Skin make it trivial to reset it every time. Against decisive attacks, any single attack gets massively reduced by Adamant Skin Technique + Ruin Abasing Shrug, and any followup attacks in a flurry will get negated by Aegis of Invincible Might unless Sally can somehow get past 20 hardness. The mote regen from Essence Gathering Temper makes it easy to maintain for several turns. To top it off, with Ox Body Technique x5 and Iron Skin Concentration he has 32 health levels in total, so I'd add Bloodthirsty Sword-Dancer Spirit to negate all wound penalties and add extra essence Regen.<br /> Offensively, Dragon's Coil Technique becomes a full excellency for both the attack and control roll for only 3m, making his grapple game incredibly efficient. He can ditch the artifact smashfists to free up some motes since Adamantine Fists of Battle ensures that even if Sally were to switch to a soak-heavy build he still has an overwhelming of 6.<br /> In addition, if it is allowed, then Incomparable Body Arsenal is a huge boost in power, providing heavy artifact armor traits with no essence committed and giving double 9s to all grapple attack and control rolls thanks to Devil-Strangling Attitude. He can also use God-Weapon Armament to create artifact weapons with any tags he wants, such as reach for getting Sally off her high horse or balanced to up his overwhelming value even higher.<br /> Even if Sally chooses to go the enhanced mount route he can Use Dragon's Coil Technique and just yeet it away; he doesn't have to kill it, just Crashing Wave Throw it 5 range bands away while farming a ton of initiative.<br /> <br /> So tl;dr I think essence 5 Bobby with a full Resistance suite could beat essence 5 Sally, but I think that showcases the strength of Solar Resistance moreso than Brawl. So if you want my nominee for second-strongest combat tree then there it is; Solar Resistance doesn't get mentioned nearly often enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:07:27-07:00","id":1393430,"title":"","content":"At E5 Bobby should definitely pick up Heaven-and-Earth Gauntlets (well all solar Brawl characters should [or shouldn't], because they're really broken). With Fire-Eating Fist, Ascendant Battle Visage, and Comet-Diverting Guard he withering clashes with Accuracy +5 and a +5 (non-charm) clash bonus, which if he wins against an E5 opponent feeds his attack on his own turn +5 attack and damage dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:35:31-07:00","id":1393435,"title":"","content":"Heaven and Earth Gauntlets are definitely top tier but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a> specified generic artifacts with no Evocations for the experiment.<br /> <br /> I just had a wild thought: maybe at essence 1 Bobby could win going for a Knockout Blow wincon? I generally really don't like that charm but here it might allow Brawl to snatch a cheesy win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:39:42-07:00","id":1393437,"title":"","content":"Ah, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:46:53-07:00","id":1393440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393420#post1393420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's really good for sure, but not any more broken than Thunderbolt Attack Prana or Heavenly Guardian Defense or any other solar charms you care to mention</div> </div> </div> </div>You can smack once for your attack, trigger 1W2B, then use Peony Blossom, then IFoF, and for 4m that turn DES got you got 32 dice of accuracy and 32 bonus damage. Four motes for 64 bonus dice.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say it\u2019s solidly better than TAP and TAP is already near the limits of what I think is acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T21:21:01-07:00","id":1393579,"title":"","content":"How well do you feel Centipede synergizes with Ebon Shadow? One of my players wants to give it a shot. His weapon of choice is a fighting chain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-02-2020, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T07:29:55-07:00","id":1393624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1393579#post1393579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How well do you feel Centipede synergizes with Ebon Shadow? One of my players wants to give it a shot. His weapon of choice is a fighting chain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly. They are both good styles but they do different things. I guess if you have access to the Mastery effect then Numberless Blows Technique + Throat-Slitting Shadow Atemi can be a pretty brutal combo, but then Brawl can do the same with far fewer charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:26:23-07:00","id":1395371,"title":"","content":"<i>Warning: Lengthy, rambling post\u2026</i><br /> <br /> This was the culmination of a \u2018cooperative\u2019 prologue session, the idea being to get myself and my fellow player/ST back up to speed(ish) with <i>actually</i> playing 3e while engaging with weapon tags and gambits more than we did in our previous game.<br /> <br /> Harnos is going to be an NPC in the game proper, which is aimed to build towards an investigation into his (pre-ordained) disappearance. We played this with the intention that this <i>could</i> be the fight that he loses to explain his disappearance, so the criminals were played to win, burning willpower and stunting throughout. We explicitly didn\u2019t want to run them as a battle group so it was a harder fight and we got to try out different tactics.<br /> <br /> Write-up below, but fair warning, it\u2019s a long \u2018un that may simply make folk go, \u2018Gah, what the hell is <i>this</i>?\u2019 If you just wanna skip to the musings on tags, tactics and Harnos as a character, I\u2019ve stuck them in the spoiler at the end \u2013 basically interested in musing/learning about fun ways people have combined tags and gambits and other not especially charm focused tactics.<br /> <br /> Also, apologies also for the corny intro text below\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>--</i><br /> <br /> <i>Picking his way along the sodden, littered walkway, his bulky form illuminated by the occasional flash of lightning, Ledaal Varun Harnos prayed \u2013 as he had throughout the climb up the cliff face to this Dragons-forsaken warehouse \u2013 that Baodin had made it to the coast. The archon\u2019s sharp eyes would have been welcome now but he could never have made that climb, certainly not in this storm. Better he secured their passage to Arjuf. Harnos would join him \u2013 somehow \u2013 once he finally had proof. Proof as to what was behind all those disappearances. Proof that Teruk and Jald hadn\u2019t died in vain. Proof that blasphemy lay at the heart of House Ragara\u2019s doings in Jau Dei.</i><br /> <br /> <i>An all-too-familiar sensation, a ripple of intense energy up the back of his neck directing his attention to a ragged opening in the warehouse\u2019s roof, stopped the magistrate in his tracks. A grim smile spread across his lips as his hands darted quicksilver-fast into the discarded mining tools in search of something blunt and heavy.</i><br /> <br /> <i>He was being watched\u2026</i><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Magistrate Ledaal Vaurn Harnos (The Third...)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Chargen DB<br /> Water Aspect<br /> House of Bells<br /> <br /> Strength 4, Dexterity 1, Stamina 2<br /> Perception 5, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> Appearance 3, Manipulation 3, Charisma 3<br /> <br /> Aspect Abilities<br /> Brawl 5 (Improvised Weapons)<br /> Bureaucracy 0<br /> Investigation 5 (Undercover Work)<br /> Larceny 4<br /> Sail 0<br /> <br /> Favoured Abilities<br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Awareness 4<br /> Integrity 4<br /> Socialise 4<br /> Stealth 4<br /> <br /> Other Abilities<br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Lore 1<br /> Resistance 2<br /> War 2 (Archons)<br /> Dodge 3 (While Armoured)<br /> Survival 2<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> Languages 3 (Low Realm, Old Realm, Flametongue)<br /> Contacts 3 (Realm Underworld)<br /> Influence 2 (Reputable Magistrate)<br /> Allies 1 (Ledaal Varun Piet \u2013 Mortal Dynast)<br /> Followers 1 (Archons)<br /> Quick Draw 4 (Brawl)<br /> Pain Tolerance 4<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> 1. Indisputable Physical Analysis (Investigation Excellency)<br /> 2. Permeating Insight<br /> 3. Scent-of-Crime Method<br /> 4. Bloodhound\u2019s Nose Technique<br /> 5. Precision Observation Method (Awareness Excellency)<br /> 6. Deep-Listening Palm<br /> 7. All-Encompassing Earth Sense<br /> 8. Underground River\u2019s Flow (Larceny Excellency)<br /> 9. Flowing Body Disguise<br /> 10. Observer Awareness Method<br /> 11. Distracting Breeze Meditation (Stealth Excellency)<br /> 12. Granite Curtain of Serenity (Integrity Excellency)<br /> 13. Effortlessly Rising Flame (Athletics Excellency)<br /> 14. Threshold Warding Stance (Dodge Excellency)<br /> 15. Become The Hammer (Brawl Excellency)<br /> 16. Flotsam-and-Jetsam Approach<br /> 17. Water Dragon\u2019s Coil<br /> 18. Inescapable Whirlpool Hold<br /> 19. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 20. Ox-Body Technique<br /> <br /> 13p/31ph, 5wp<br /> Wears a Reinforced Buff Jacket<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Scenario<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Four criminals in the pay of House Ragara, aware the magistrate is closing in on their trafficking operation and fearful their Ragara contact may have them killed to tie up loose ends, attempt to set up an ambush at the cliff-top warehouse they use to access the tunnels underneath Jau Dei. Harnos\u2019 charms and senses allow him to scale the cliff and spot his would-be ambushers \u2013 a fight ensues inside the crumbling warehouse (i.e. the ambush failed, everyone Joins Battle normally). Beyond medium range towards the back of the warehouse are the dimly lit walkways leading down the mineshaft, which counts as difficult terrain with a -1 environmental penalty to vision (not really used in this session).<br /> <br /> Harnos has used All-Encompassing Earth Sense (3m), Observer Awareness Method (1m) and his Athletics Excellency (2m) so starts with 13p/25ph, 5wp. He begins with an improvised \u2018hammer\u2019 (medium weapon with the Smashing tag) ready.<br /> <br /> The criminals use the Grizzled Mercenary stats from p.497 of the core, except with tweaked weapons/tags (we didn\u2019t bother varying their parry between those with light weapons and those with medium for sake of simplicity). They have names but I\u2019ve just called them by their weapons for the sake of making this write-up a<i> bit</i> easier to digest.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> JOIN BATTLE<br /> <br /> Harnos buys two successes with the Awareness Excellency (4m), activates Floatsam-and-Jetsam Approach (1m), and rolls 9 dice, fluking 7 successes for 12i. Anima at glowing. Enters Water aura.<br /> <br /> Cestus gets 6 successes for 9i<br /> <br /> Whip gets 4 successes for 7i<br /> <br /> Javelin gets 4 successes for 7i. Starts at short range.<br /> <br /> Axe gets 4 successes for 7i<br /> <br /> TURN 1<br /> <i>Harnos: 12i (13p/20ph, 5wp)</i><br /> <i>Cestus: 9i</i><br /> <i>Whip: 7i</i><br /> <i>Javelin: 7i</i><br /> <i>Axe: 7i</i><br /> <br /> Harnos grapples Cestus, activating Water Dragon\u2019s Coils (3m), Inescapable Whirlpool Hold (5m) and a 2m Excellency. Anima at burning. Strength 4 + Brawl 5 + Stunt 2 + Excellency 2 = 13 dice. Cestus defends with willpower for parry 6. Harnos rolls 8 successes, attack hits. Initiative roll of 13 (12 + 1 from threshold successes from Water Dragon\u2019s Coils), re-rolling 6s. 5 successes.<br /> <br /> Harnos doesn\u2019t want to spend more motes, but if he wins the control roll he gets the initiative back from his gambit and potentially more rounds of control, which would give him a chance of doing enough decisive damage to put Cestus (provisionally supposed to be the gang\u2019s leader) down. He uses a 2m Excellency, taking his pool to 13, re-rolling 6s. Cestus spends willpower for a pool of 8 + 1 success. 8 successes versus 5, Harnos wins and is refunded the grapple\u2019s initiative cost.<br /> <br /> Harnos makes a decisive slam, forsaking 3 rounds of control. He rolls 15 dice of damage, re-rolling 6s. 7 successes, Cestus is out of action. Harnos resets to 3i. One down.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Whip uses a disarm gambit, aiming to drop Harnos\u2019 defence so his allies can dog pile him. He rolls 11 dice and spends willpower. Harnos\u2019 parry is (Brawl 5 + Specialty 1 + Dex 1)/2 + Medium Weapon 1 + Stunt 1 for 6. He boosts it to 8 with a 2m Excellency and willpower.<br /> <br /> Whip rolls 10 successes. He makes the initiative roll of 2 (reduced from 3 because of his weapon\u2019s disarming tag). Harnos is disarmed. Whip drops to 4i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Javelin withers Harnos, aiming to stack onslaught and maybe crash him before Axe takes a swing. He rolls 9 dice and spends 1 willpower. Harnos\u2019 parry is now just 4. 5 successes. Damage pool is 13, Harnos\u2019 soak is 7, so 6 dice of damage. Javelin gets 2 successes and climbs to 10i, Harnos drops to 1i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe makes a withering chopping attack. He rolls 9 dice and spends 1 willpower. Harnos\u2019 parry is 3. Axe rolls 3 - 6 - 1 - 4 - 2 - 5 - 6 - 4 - 5, completely fluffing his attack. He drops to 6i.<br /> <br /> TURN 2<br /> <i>Anima withers 1i from Whip</i><br /> <i>Javelin 10i</i><br /> <i>Axe 6i</i><br /> <i>Whip 3i</i><br /> <i>Harnos 1i (13p/11ph, 4wp)</i><br /> <br /> Javelin withers. He rolls 9 dice and spends 1 willpower. Harnos\u2019 parry is 2, he boosts it to 6 with a full Excellency and willpower. 6 successes. Damage pool is 5 after soak. He rolls 4 successes. Harnos is crashed at -3i, Javelin is at 20i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe makes a decisive attack. He rolls 9 dice and spends 1 willpower. Harnos\u2019 parry is at 1, he boosts it to 5 with a full Excellency and willpower. Axe rolls 6 successes, damage pool is 6 and gives 2 successes, Harnos is at -1. Axe resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Whip makes a decisive attack. He rolls 11 dice and spends 1 willpower. Harnos parry is 0. He gets 10 successes, 3 damage dice nets 1 success. Harnos loses another -1 health level. Whip resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Harnos wants to crash Whip, which would stop him using gambits next turn and also allow his anima to start burning off health levels. He flurries readying another improvised \u2018hammer\u2019 (in this case a massive brass cog lying on the floor) and withers Whip with a 4m Excellency. His pool is Strength 4 + Brawl 5 + Specialty 1 + Accuracy 2 + Stunt 2 + Excellency 4 \u2013 1 (flurry, reduced thanks to Quick Draw) \u2013 1 Wound Penalty = 16 dice. Whip defends with willpower, parry 6. 7 successes. Damage pool is reduced to 6 after soak and gives 4 successes. Whip is crashed at -1i, Harnos is at 7i.<br /> <br /> TURN 3<br /> <i>Anima does 1 HL to Whip</i><br /> <i>Javelin 20i</i><br /> <i>Harnos 7i, -1 (8p/5ph, 2wp)</i><br /> <i>Axe 3i</i><br /> <i>Whip -1i</i><br /> <br /> Javelin moves to medium range, looking to preserve his initiative and aim at Harnos while his comrades keep him busy.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Harnos makes a withering smashing attack on Axe with a 1m Excellency, figuring the defence penalty is acceptable now he\u2019s only facing two attacks this turn, one of them hopefully from someone having to flurry a rise from prone. He rolls 14 dice. Axe defends with willpower, parry 6. Harnos rolls 6 successes, and does 2 damage, just missing out on crash. Axe is at 1i and prone, Harnos climbs to 8i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe flurries a rise from prone with an attack, spending one willpower on the attack. He makes the rise from prone and rolls 6 dice. Harnos\u2019 parry is 4. Rolls 3 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Whip makes a withering attack, rolling 11 dice and spending 1 willpower. Harnos\u2019 parry is 3 and he boosts it to 6 with a full Excellency. Whip gets 7 successes. His damage pool is 3 and he gets one success, climbing out of crash to 1i, Harnos drops to 7i.<br /> <br /> TURN 4<br /> <i>Anima does nothing</i><br /> <i>Javelin 20i</i><br /> <i>Harnos 7i, -1 (6p/5ph, 2wp)</i><br /> <i>Axe 1i</i><br /> <i>Whip 1i</i><br /> <br /> Javelin aims.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Harnos withers Whip using a 1m Excellency for 14 dice, Whip defends with willpower for parry 6. Harnos gets 12(!) successes. Damage pool is 11 and yields 7 successes. Whip is crashed again at -6i, Harnos climbs to 15i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe withers Harnos, spending willpower and rolling 9 dice. Harnos\u2019 parry is 5 and he boosts it to 7 with a 4m Excellency. Axe nets 4 successes, attack misses.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Whip makes a withering attack Harnos, spending his last willpower and rolling 11 dice. Harnos\u2019 parry is 4. 6 successes. Damage pool is 5, netting 1 success. Whip is at -4i, Harnos is at 14i.<br /> <br /> TURN 5<br /> <i>Anima does nothing</i><br /> <i>Javelin 20i</i><br /> <i>Harnos 14i, -1 (6p/5ph, 2wp)</i><br /> <i>Axe 1i</i><br /> <i>Whip -3i</i><br /> <br /> Javelin moves to short and makes what he hopes is the crucial decisive attack, rolling 11 dice and spending 1 willpower. Harnos\u2019 parry is 3, he boosts it to 7 with a full Excellency and willpower. 9 successes, 20i yields just 6 damage. Harnos is badly wounded but thanks to Pain Tolerance is still in his last -1 Health Level. Javelin resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Harnos makes a withering smashing attack on Axe using a 1m Excellency, rolling 14 dice. Axe defends with willpower, parry 6. Gets 10 successes. Damage pool of 9, gives 5 successes. Axe is crashed at -4i and prone. Harnos gains 1 (hits) + 5 (successes) + 5 (crash) initiative, rises to 23i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Whip withers Harnos with 11 dice. Harnos\u2019 parry is 4. Whip get 4 successes. Damage pool of 3 dice gives 1 success. Whip rise to -1i, Harnos drops to 22i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe flurries a rise from prone with an attack. He makes the rise and rolls 6 dice, Harnos\u2019 parry is 3. Axe rolls 5 successes. Damage pool of 7 gives 2 successes. Axe rises to -1i. Harnos drops to 20i.<br /> <br /> TURN 6<br /> <i>Anima strips 1 HL from Whip, who is now at -1</i><br /> <i>Harnos 20i, -1 (4p/5ph, 1wp)</i><br /> <i>Javelin 3i</i><br /> <i>Whip -1i, -1</i><br /> <i>Axe -1i</i><br /> <br /> Harnos wants to end someone this turn. He\u2019d like to use a grapple to maximise his chances of doing lasting damage but he can\u2019t blow the motes he used in the first turn and figures with a little luck he has enough initiative to do the job with a normal decisive anyway. He attacks Whip using a 1m Excellency, rolling 12 dice. Whip\u2019s parry is 4. Harnos gets 6 successes. 20 dice gives 9 successes after re-rolls, Whip is down. Harnos resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Javelin withers Harnos. He rolls 9 dice and spends 1 willpower. Harnos\u2019 parry is 5. 7 successes. Damage pool soaked to 7, gives 1 damage. Harnos is at 2i, Javelin is at 5i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe withers, rolling 9 dice. Harnos\u2019 parry is 4, Harnos wants to keep him crashed and below him in the initiative order, so boosts his parry to 7 with a full Excellency. Axe rolls 6 successes, attack misses.<br /> <br /> TURN 7<br /> <i>Anima strips 1 HL from Axe</i><br /> <i>Javelin 5i</i><br /> <i>Harnos 2i, -1 (2p/5ph, 1wp)</i><br /> <i>Axe -1i</i><br /> <br /> Javelin moves back to medium and prepares to aim, hoping Axe will keep Harnos busy.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Harnos makes a withering smashing attack against Axe, using a 1m Excellency, rolling 14 dice against parry 5. 6 successes, damage pool of 6 gives 3 successes, Axe is at -4i, Harnos is at 4i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe flurries rising from prone and an attack, but fails the initial roll so his attack is at -6 (-3 prone, -3 flurry) for a pool of 3. Harnos\u2019 parry is 4. Attack misses with 2 successes.<br /> <br /> TURN 8<br /> <i>Anima does nothing</i><br /> <i>Javelin 5i</i><br /> <i>Harnos 4i, -1 (2p/9ph, 1wp)</i><br /> <i>Axe -4i, prone</i><br /> <br /> Javelin aims.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Harnos withers once again with a 1m Excellency. Axe\u2019s parry is 4. 6 successes and a damage pool of 7 gives 3 successes. Harnos is at 8i, Axe is at -7i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe flurries rising from prone with an attack. He makes the rise from prone and rolls 6 dice. Harnos\u2019 parry is 5. He rolls 6 successes and does 2 damage. Axe is at -4i, Harnos is at 6i.<br /> <br /> TURN 9<br /> <i>Anima strips 1 HL from Axe, dropping him to -1</i><br /> <i>Axe resets to 3i on his turn</i><br /> <i>Harnos 6i, -1 (2p/13ph, 1wp)</i><br /> <i>Javelin 5i</i><br /> <i>Axe -4i, -1</i><br /> <br /> Harnos withers Axe again, using a 1m Excellency against parry 4 He doesn\u2019t use a smashing attack as he needs every bit of parry he can get against Javelin\u2019s impending attack. Gets 10 successes and ultimately 6 damage, Harnos at 13i, Axe at -10i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe resets to 3i. He would really like to attempt a distract gambit but doesn\u2019t have the initiative. He withers for 8 dice to stack onslaught. He rolls 4 successes against parry 5. Attack misses.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Javelin moves to short and makes a decisive attack, rolling 11 dice and spending his last willpower, hoping to drop Harnos to his -3 health level and turn the fight. Aware this is crunch time Harnos defends with a full Excellency and willpower for parry 8. 5 successes, attack misses. Javelin drops to 3i.<br /> <br /> TURN 10<br /> <i>Anima does nothing</i><br /> <i>Harnos 13i, -1 (2p/9ph, 0wp)</i><br /> <i>Javelin 3i</i><br /> <i>Axe 3i, -1</i><br /> <br /> Harnos makes a withering smashing attack on Axe with a 1m Excellency against parry 4. 9 successes, damage pool of 14 gives 7 damage, Harnos is at 19i, Axe is at -4i and smashed out to short range towards Javelin. Harnos reflexively follows, closing with Javelin and Axe.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Javelin flurries a withering attack with a disengage. He rolls 7 dice on the attack. Harnos\u2019 parry is 4 and he boosts it to 6 with a 4m Excellency. 5 successes, attack misses. Javelin rolls 6 dice on the disengage attempt, Harnos contests with 7 dice and buys two successes with his Excellency. Javelin rolls 4 successes, Harnos gets 6. Disengage fails. Javelin drops to 1i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe makes a withering attack with 8 dice. Harnos\u2019 parry is 3. 2 successes, attack misses.<br /> <br /> TURN 11<br /> <i>Anima strips 1 HL from Axe</i><br /> <i>Harnos 19i, -1 (0p/7ph, 0wp)</i><br /> <i>Javelin 1i</i><br /> <i>Axe -4i, -1</i><br /> <br /> Harnos thinks about attacking Javelin, but decides that the better odds of finishing off Axe with the initiative he has makes more sense. He makes a decisive attack against Axe using a 3m Excellency, rolling 14 dice against Parry 4. Rolls 3 successes, attack misses. Harnos drops to 16i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Javelin tries his luck again with flurrying a withering attack with a disengage. He rolls 7 dice on the attack, Harnos\u2019 parry is 5. 5 successes, damage pool of 5 yields 2 damage. Javelin rises to 4i, Harnos drops to 14i.<br /> <br /> Disengage pool of 6 versus 7, with Harnos also buying 2 successes. 4 v 3 successes, disengage succeeds, Javelin moves to short.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe withers with 8 dice against parry 4. 5 successes, damage pool of 6 gives 2 successes. Harnos drops to 12i, Axe rises to -2i.<br /> <br /> TURN 12<br /> <i>Anima does nothing</i><br /> <i>Harnos 12i, -1 (0p/5ph, 0wp)</i><br /> <i>Javelin 4i</i><br /> <i>Axe -2i, -1</i><br /> <br /> Harnos makes another decisive attack against Axe using a 3m Excellency, rolling 14 dice against parry 4. 4 successes, attack hits. 12 initiative gives 3 damage, Axe is at -4. Harnos resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Javelin moves to medium and begins to withdraw, fleeing down the crumbling mineshaft walkways (difficult terrain) while taunting Harnos that this isn\u2019t over yet\u2026<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Axe, badly wounded and abandoned, surrenders. The fight ends as the spent magistrate stops to interrogate his new prisoner as to where <i>exactly</i> the tunnels lead.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Witterings<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> ^ Harnos got real lucky on Turn 5.<br /> <br /> ^ Axe (in-game name: Joru) felt spectacularly inept throughout this fight after Turn 2. We were really pleased that things ended with him captured and potentially spilling the beans to Harnos.<br /> <br /> ^ We were reminded that being able to negate onslaught somehow is, right after Excellencies, pretty much the thing that makes you go, \u2018Yep, you\u2019re a setting badass\u2019. If Harnos was, say, a melee fighter with Flame-Born Interception and Graceful Flowing Defence this fight would have been a cinch.<br /> <br /> ^ Harnos was a deliberate attempt to play someone fun to fight with who wasn\u2019t a powerhouse (Will, who played him, made utter merchants of death in 2e. Physical tertiary was a new one on him, although he couldn\u2019t keep himself from adding Pain Tolerance to the initial build). He felt Harnos was a lot of fun (thanks to DrLoveMonkey for the suggestion) \u2013 having grapples and smashing available to him made it feel like he still had combat choices to make even though he didn\u2019t have many combat charms. We\u2019ve been spitballing ways to make him more important to what we want to do down the line.<br /> <br /> ^ Dex 1, even with the great fun Flotsam-and-Jetsam Approach from Heirs, is unsurprisingly a real kick in the nethers, it affects too many important things like disengage, rushes and <i>preventing</i> people from disengaging with you. Will was paranoid about being knocked prone (he\u2019s had irritating experiences of that in the past), and as a result Harnos ended up with a lot of Excellencies (and had to burn motes in earlier scenes) that another starter character might have foregone in order to be able to do what Will wanted him to do. As mentioned above, a 2/3/2 melee-ist with the starting melee charms and artefact weapons and armour instead of Pain Tolerance and Quick Draw is going to be more effective in most scenarios. But Harnos felt characterful...<br /> <br /> ^ On the actual fight, we couldn\u2019t decide if Javelin aiming then moving to close range next turn with the bonus intact was kosher, but it felt right so we let it go. Not sure about aura of Join Battle either...<br /> <br /> ^ Harnos really should have clashed some of those attacks to save motes, but given we had a clash-happy fire aspect in our last game we wanted to see what a different approach would do. The lesson? Should have clashed more\u2026<br /> <br /> ^ Mixing ranged and melee fighters is a really obvious way of making a simple fight harder against Exalts with weak ranged options, need to do that more in the future.<br /> <br /> ^ We wanted to use more gambits than we were ultimately able to, often the timing or initiative pool wasn\u2019t there. I was a bit obsessed with trying to find a point to use Distract. Looking back, Axe maybe should have used it in Turn 1 to boost Javelin (as the person most likely to preserve initiative), but then he was the one who actually dropped Harnos into his -1s in Turn 2 which made a difference, and 7i against a difficulty minimum of 3 isn\u2019t great. Distract feels like something that\u2019s tricky to use well unless you\u2019ve got two cooperating fighters already in a strong position. Has anyone else used it well?<br /> <br /> ^ Disarm = good and fun \u2013 although Harnos was spec\u2019d to negate it (we ruled Quick Draw and the surroundings meant there was plenty of stuff to hand) \u2013 and is a pretty handy tag for making not-that-threatening mooks matter in a fight \u2013 thugs armed with fighting chains are probably going to crop up in our games down the line.<br /> <br /> ^ Chopping, as mentioned elsewhere many times by EVERYONE, is so niche that you\u2019d pick almost any other weapon over a chopping sword as far as I can see.<br /> <br /> ^ Smashing is still the bestest tag for my money, being prone is such a nerf.<br /> <br /> ^ If you\u2019ve read this far \u2013 thanks! And apologies for length.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 06-09-2020, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T15:18:05-07:00","id":1395464,"title":"","content":"Join Battle doesn't give Aura.<br /> <br /> You can Aim then Move the next round, but you can't move out of range, or put your target behind full cover, and you have to Attack that round or you lose the bonus. So you played that kosher.<br /> <br /> Smashing is A1. Plenty of effects negate Prone though.<br /> <br /> Chopping sucks.<br /> <br /> On Turn 1, Axe should probably have Decisived, setting his allies up for the Crash bonus and maybe stacking wounds. He missed anyway, but still.<br /> <br /> With Harnos mote tapped, out of Willpower and on his last -1, I'd have him grab Axe by the collar and hoist him into the air. The bloodied magistrate screams in the mercenary's face, &quot;Who do you work for!&quot; From out of the shadows, Javelin reappears at the side of a six foot tall, four foot wide, Dynast in Ragara colors.<br /> <br /> Ragara BBEG snarls one word &quot;Me&quot;. Harnos sees a meaty fist the size of a sledgehammer heading straight for his face, then his world goes black.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-10-2020, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T15:28:50-07:00","id":1395467,"title":"","content":"Also &quot;I want to try avoiding clashes this time.&quot; mixed with &quot;I have 1 dexterity, but a charm that makes my attacks, including clashes, key off my strength.&quot; is not a great combo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T17:04:33-07:00","id":1395694,"title":"","content":"Distract sucks ass unless you've got charms that key off of it. The only time I've seen an unenhanced vanilla distract was when the fight was basically won already and the player with the high initiative wanted to hand the finishing blow to another player for flavour reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T18:22:22-07:00","id":1395713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1395694#post1395694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Distract sucks ass unless you've got charms that key off of it. The only time I've seen an unenhanced vanilla distract was when the fight was basically won already and the player with the high initiative wanted to hand the finishing blow to another player for flavour reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's happened in my game where the PC who had the huge pile of Initiative didn't have any damage-adder Charms, so he passed his Initiative over to a character who <i>did</i> have those kind of Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T05:48:31-07:00","id":1395817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1395464#post1395464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Join Battle doesn't give Aura.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, by the time I caught that he had assumed aura from JB and (thus got those benefits from Inescapable Whirlpool Hold in turn 1) it was turn 6. Sloppy.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1395467#post1395467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also &quot;I want to try avoiding clashes this time.&quot; mixed with &quot;I have 1 dexterity, but a charm that makes my attacks, including clashes, key off my strength.&quot; is not a great combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. He reasoned to himself he\u2019d end up blowing full Excellencies on his offense every clash to guarantee he won so wouldn\u2019t have saved many motes compared to what he actually spent on attacks (typically 1m) and defence anyway, but even if that is true (doubtful) he\u2019d have racked up initiative far faster winning clashes while also dropping his victim\u2019s defence for a follow-up (plus negating his less than stellar soak/parry).<br /> <br /> We might play one more session of him exploring the mineshaft and play him a bit better (failing that, yeah, big haymaker to the face followed by nap nap sounds good...).<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> +1 on both BadassOverlord and Count\u2019s points. Adding extra opportunities to fail rolls to actually use the initiative you\u2019ve earned rather than just attack yourself seems ill-advised unless the recipient can boost decisive damage (or you're after style/flavour points!).<br /> <br /> I guess combining a distract with someone attacking with a chopping weapon has some (extremely) niche uses for mortals, or boosting someone so they can use a useful gambit they otherwise couldn\u2019t, but it\u2019s all a bit nickel and dime.<br /> <br /> We were trying to think of mechanics that would make them more useful to non-Exalted, but failed to come up with anything that was that either interesting or not too powerful compared to the other gambits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T15:16:01-07:00","id":1397162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1395817#post1395817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were trying to think of mechanics that would make them more useful to non-Exalted, but failed to come up with anything that was that either interesting or not too powerful compared to the other gambits.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might work better if the target gained more initiative than the attacker lost, like even just one or two more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, here's a Steel Devil Stylist wracking up an insane number of attacks against a pair of Pestletails. In this setup I'm saying the pestletails are wrecking a town, and safely trying to plink away at them with minor damage is not going to cause them to stop destroying buildings, so it's just a race to kill them before they level the town.<br /> <br /> I also didn't have enough motes to finish the first combo so I went back and made the Steel Devil stylist Essence 2 and took away his artifact armor. Don't do that in a real game, your ST won't appreciate it.<br /> <br /> Steel Devil<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 3/5/3<br /> <br /> Dual Blades 16 (13/3 damage)<br /> <br /> Parry 6<br /> Soak/Hardness 8/0<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The Steel Devil opens up with a 5m Naked Fang Draw and a 6m Excellency, and a stunt, rolling 18 dice for 12 successes, beating opponents for a free point of charge.<br /> <br /> <br /> Amazingly with stunts one pestletail gets 7 successes and the other gets 3<br /> <br /> Steel Devil will fill the rest of his 9<br /> <br /> Steel 9i 40m 5wp 7charge<br /> Pest1 10i<br /> Pest2 6i<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==============<br /> Pestletail 1 drags its bony tail through the ground floor of a house, collapsing half of it to the ground and sending people hiding in the top floors tumbling hard into the rubble.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> Steel Devil slashes at Pest2, the Steel Devil using 3m Double Attack Technique, and 5m excellency. Devil rolls 12 successes against 2.<br /> <br /> This attack beats the Pestletail by 6, and then beats its defense of 1 by 5, and then its defense of 0 by 5. This adds first 8, then 12 damage, and then the remainder of the overflow for +25 damage, and a final damage value of 38, which is soaked down to 21. Note here that without the Steel Devil charms this light weapon attack would deal only 2 dice of withering damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> This deals 11 points of damage, crashing the second Pestletail. The Devil will spend 10m 1wp to activate Whirling Guillotine Dance.<br /> <br /> Steel 25i 22m 4wp 8charge<br /> Pest1 10i<br /> Pest2 -5i<br /> <br /> <br /> The Devil will spend 2m 1wp to Steel Devil Strike, easily hitting and rolling 16 damage for 6 damage, enough to trigger a 4m 1wp Empty Mind Strike.<br /> <br /> Hitting again easily and rolling 10 damage for 6 levels<br /> <br /> Steel 9i 16m 3wp 0charge<br /> Pest1 10i<br /> Pest2 -5i 12L<br /> <br /> <br /> Devil will now use 12m 1wp Dervish Blade Frenzy, Rolling 16 dice for 11 successes, and thus dealing 13+5+6+6+11 with two automatic successes on the damage roll and rerolling two failures. Dealing a total of 11 damage.<br /> <br /> Steel 20i 3m 3wp 1charge<br /> Pest1 10i<br /> Pest2 -16i 12L<br /> <br /> Devil will now use 3m 1wp to Steel Devil Strike, this time aiming it at the other pestletail, hitting easily and rolling 2 damage on 11 dice again.<br /> <br /> Steel 9i 0m 3wp 1charge<br /> Pest1 10i 2L<br /> Pest2 -16i 12L &lt;= Fleeing<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ==============<br /> Steel 9i 5m 3wp 1charge<br /> Pest1 10i 2L<br /> <br /> Pestletail 1 bucks and bowls into another structure, causing the frame to rack and crunch as it leans onto its neighbor.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> the Steel Devil attacks with 2m Double Attack, rolling 9 successes, overflowing by 7, then 6, giving a damage of 13+5+6+6, then rolling 13 damage for 7 after rerolls. Reflexively transferring 2 to charge.<br /> <br /> Steel 15i 3m 3wp 3charge<br /> Pest1 3i 2L<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ==============<br /> Steel 15i 8m 3wp 3charge<br /> Pest1 3i 2L<br /> <br /> <br /> The Steel Devil will attack again with 2m Double Attack, rolling 6 to attack, adding 13+6+8+6 damage, rolling 16 damage for 7, crashing Pestletail 1 and gaining 13 initiative<br /> <br /> Steel 15i 6m 3wp 3charge<br /> Pest1 3i 2L<br /> <br /> <br /> Then spening 3m 1wp Steel Devil will launch a Steel Devil Strike, hitting and dealing 5 damage with 13 dice, which causers this pestletail to flee as well.<br /> <br /> Steel 15i 3m 3wp 3charge<br /> Pest1 3i 7L &lt;= Fleeing<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Not too bad, only two buildings destroyed before the pestletails were forced to flee. I normally would have just removed Pestletail 2 after getting to the point of fleeing, but Dervish Blade Frenzy can't be re-targeted so to get the rull thing off it had to hang around even after Empty Mind Strike passed its threshold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 06-17-2020, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T17:01:50-07:00","id":1397170,"title":"","content":"Not bad, especially considering it took the martial artist something on the order of ~6-10 seconds to disperse them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T17:24:29-07:00","id":1397171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397162#post1397162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This attack beats the Pestletail by 6, and then beats its defense of 1 by 5, and then its defense of 0 by 5. This adds first 8, then 12 damage, and then the remainder of the overflow for +25 damage, and a final damage value of 38, which is soaked down to 21. Note here that without the Steel Devil charms this light weapon attack would deal only 2 dice of withering damage.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure since Tripple Attack Technique is an upgrade to Double Attack Technique and the text says the bonus is added to base damage<br /> <br /> &quot;This Charm upgrades Double Attack Technique, allowing extra successes from the second blow to roll over the target\u2019s Defense again and create a third attack. If Triple Attack Technique is successful, add (Dexterity + Charge) to the attack\u2019s base damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> you don't get to add the 8 from a regular successfull double attack plus the 12 from tripple attack together, so you only get +17.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T17:32:27-07:00","id":1397173,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty sure you do, but I should probably ask the devs. It doesn\u2019t say it\u2019s damage replaces the damage of the second attack, it says it creates a third attack that deals that damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T17:34:38-07:00","id":1397175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397170#post1397170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not bad, especially considering it took the martial artist something on the order of ~6-10 seconds to disperse them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubly considering light weapons are in their worst matchup against low defence but high soak enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T18:59:53-07:00","id":1397191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397175#post1397175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doubly considering light weapons are in their worst matchup against low defence but high soak enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although Steel Devil is at its best against low defense high soak enemies, to the point of being almost useless against high defense Exalts, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T20:03:40-07:00","id":1397209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397191#post1397191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although Steel Devil is at its best against low defense high soak enemies, to the point of being almost useless against high defense Exalts, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Exalts with high defense, penalty negating charms, and high soak. If that happens though the Steel Devil stylist should just target things that aren't that Exalt in the combat. Unless there are no other combatants, in which case your circle is just going to dogpile that one exalt into oblivion. It only actually becomes a problem if an entire group of exalts show up who all have high defense and penalty negating charms. It's a hole in Steel Devil's capabilities, but considering how good it is everywhere else it's a pretty small one.<br /> <br /> Even then it has a form charm that gives +2 parry for the scene, and has a cap-bursting parry enhancer that chains into a reflexive disarm gambit that chains into a Medium Range AoE. So still pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T23:18:27-07:00","id":1397246,"title":"","content":"Cons: Steel Devil is only good against foes you could have beaten anyway.<br /> <br /> Pros: You are a Solar PC. ALL foes are foes you could have beaten anyway.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested in how well it holds up for Deebs, or any cool Lunar synergies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T16:19:30-07:00","id":1397400,"title":"","content":"At essence one, Lunars have two cap breakers in dex; Finding the Needle's Eye and Striking Mospid Method. I think they're each three motes to activate and they look to me like they could pull some value out of double attack technique and triple attack technique in situations where those two charms would otherwise be ineffective. But that's just theory crafting. I haven't seen it in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":".  clarity 06-18-2020, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T17:39:10-07:00","id":1397410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397246#post1397246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested in how well it holds up for Deebs</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty good it looks like. I did a fight with two Greenmaws against a DB Steel Devil Master and her Nomadic Horse Archer friend.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Darla uses Naked Fang Draw for 5m, rolling 11+3 dice and starting with 12i<br /> Rag rolls 6 dice for 5i<br /> Maw1 rolls 8 dice for 6i<br /> Maw2 rolls 8 dice for 4i<br /> <br /> <br /> Darla maxes out her charge by trasnferring 7i into it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Darla 5i 39m 8charge<br /> Rag 5i<br /> Maw1 6i<br /> Maw2 4i<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==========<br /> <br /> Maw1 attempts to withering tail slam Darla, who will not spend any motes to defend. Rolling 10 dice for 5 successes, just missing.<br /> <br /> Darla 5i 39m 8charge<br /> Rag 5i<br /> Maw1 6i<br /> Maw2 4i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Darla lets rag go first, who will fire a withering bowshot at Maw1, who will defend with 4m 1i Unbroken Root Endurance. Rolling 11 dice and hitting with 7, then rolling 1 damage for two with a 10!<br /> <br /> Darla 5i 39m 8charge<br /> Rag 8i<br /> Maw1 3i (has 15 soak)<br /> Maw2 4i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Darla will now go, spending 10m 1wp for Whirling Guillotine Dance.<br /> <br /> Darla 5i 29m 4wp 8charge<br /> Rag 8i<br /> Maw1 3i (has 15 soak)<br /> Maw2 4i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Maw2 now triest to wither Darka with a tail slam, spending a willpower and rolling 10 dice for a total of 7, once more just missing.<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ==========<br /> Darla 5i 34m 4wp 8charge<br /> Rag 8i<br /> Maw1 3i (has 15 soak)<br /> Maw2 4i<br /> <br /> Rag goes first again, rolling a withering attack against Maw1, rolling 10 dice for 7 again, and rolling a die of damage for nothing.<br /> <br /> Darla 5i 34m 4wp 8charge<br /> Rag 9i<br /> Maw1 3i (has 15 soak)<br /> Maw2 4i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Darla goes now, attacking with a 4m excellency and 2m Double Attack Technique, rolling 20 dice for 10 successes. Not that it matters but there were six 9s in that roll.<br /> <br /> Needing 6 successes for Triple Attack Technique, this gives 13+6+9+4-15= 17 damage. Rolled for 11 damage after rerolls, and netting 17 total initiative due to crashing Maw1. She'll transfer 2 of that to increase her charge to 10.<br /> <br /> Darla 20i 28m 4wp 10charge<br /> Rag 9i<br /> Maw1 -8i (has 15 soak)<br /> Maw2 4i<br /> <br /> Darla will then spend 3m 1wp for Steel Devil Strike, hitting easily and rolling 15 damage for 8L<br /> <br /> Darla 5i 25m 3wp 10charge<br /> Rag 9i<br /> Maw1 -8i (has 15 soak) 8L(-2s)<br /> Maw2 4i<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Next Maw 2 goes, spending a willpower for a tail slam against Darla, getting 5 successes total and missing.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Maw1 does the same, rolling 8 dice for only 4 successes.<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ==========<br /> Darla 5i 30m 3wp 10charge<br /> Rag 9i<br /> Maw1 -8i (has 15 soak) 8L(-2s)<br /> Maw2 4i<br /> <br /> Rag fires a withering shot at Maw2, who will spend a willpower to defend as well as increase its soak. Rag gets 7 successes and hits anyway, dealing 1 damage.<br /> <br /> Darla 5i 30m 3wp 10charge<br /> Rag 10i<br /> Maw1 -8i (has 15 soak) 8L(-2s)<br /> Maw2 2i (has 15 soak)<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Darla withers Maw2 with 4m excellency, 2m Double Attack, Maw 2 will spend a willpower to defend. Rolling 20 dice for 11 successes, just avoiding triple attack techniue. 13+7+2-15, rolling 7 damage for 2 damage, but still crashing Maw2.<br /> <br /> Darla 13i 24m 3wp 10charge<br /> Rag 10i<br /> Maw1 -8i (has 15 soak) 8L(-2s)<br /> Maw2 0i (has 15 soak)<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Maw 2 tries to tail slam, getting 4 successes and missing.<br /> -----------<br /> Maw 1 triest to tail slam as well, getting 3 successes and also missing<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ==========<br /> Darla 13i 29m 3wp 10charge<br /> Rag 10i<br /> Maw1 -8i (has 15 soak) 8L(-2s)<br /> Maw2 0i (has 15 soak)<br /> <br /> Darla takes aim at Maw1<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Rag makes a decisive attack against Maw1, who will spend a willpower to defend. Getting only 2 successes on 10 dice rag misses.<br /> <br /> Darla 13i 29m 3wp 10charge<br /> Rag 8i<br /> Maw1 -8i (has 15 soak) 8L(-2s)<br /> Maw2 0i (has 15 soak)<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Maw2 makes a tail slam, getting 6 successes and missing.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Maw1 throws out a tail slam against Darla, who counterattacks with Dual Slaying Stance, enhancing it with 1m excellency, and 3 initiative from her pool, hitting with 4 successes. Rolling 13 damage for 6 damage, putting Maw1 into its -4s.<br /> <br /> Maw1 misses its tail slam with only 3 successes.<br /> <br /> Darla 10i 28m 3wp 10charge<br /> Rag 8i<br /> Maw1 3i (has 15 soak) 14L(-4s)<br /> Maw2 0i (has 15 soak)<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ==========<br /> Darla 10i 33m 3wp 10charge<br /> Rag 8i<br /> Maw1 3i (has 15 soak) 14L(-4s)<br /> Maw2 0i (has 15 soak)<br /> <br /> Darla is now going to aim at Maw2<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Rag fires a decisive attack at Maw2, rolling 10 dice and hitting with an amazing 11, and dealing 2 damage.<br /> <br /> Darla 10i 33m 3wp 10charge<br /> Rag 8i<br /> Maw1 3i (has 15 soak) 14L(-4s)<br /> Maw2 0i (has 15 soak) 2L(-1s)<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Maw2 tries to tail slam Darla, who returns with a counter, spending 3i and 1m into it. Rolling 15 dice and hitting easily with 6, then rolling 13 damage for an amazingly bad 2.<br /> <br /> Maw2 misses with the tail slam, and that's where I call it because all that's going to happen now is Darla is going to regen motes.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You just max out your join battle, and fill your charge gauge right off the bat. Then enter your double-form technique and laugh. You have a 2e style +2 to your parry constantly, your withering attacks can be enhanced for 2m to get Triple Attack Technique, and when you want to start dealing decisive damage you can either spend willpower to decisive off Double Attack technique.<br /> <br /> The decisive attacks are killer though, since you can respond to any attack against you with a free decisive counterattack with a base damage of Charge, which is 10, and up to Essence initiative if you want. Since you can't attack on your turn if you want to respond like that you can either aim or take a Full Defense. That's <i>really</i> fucking good. It didn't show up in the last test since that was just a pure damage race.<br /> <br /> Also any teamwork helps a lot, having somebody else to raise wound penalties and give onslaught penalties makes the TAT a lot easier to pull off. Which is good because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1397406#post1397406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It replaces it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been completely fucking wrong about how TAT works.<br /> <br /> I would have said &quot;Man that really sucks.&quot; yesterday, but after seeing how Dual-Slaying Stance works, with its Infinite Ability Mastery style parry booster and free counterattacks that have high base damage and don't burn any initiative, it's probably a good thing for balance that it doesn't add such crazy damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T17:45:24-07:00","id":1397413,"title":"","content":"I think I might have to face that Steel Devil off against tougher enemies or drop her dex or something to not have such a boring fight. In an actual team fight the greenmaws could target someone else, or gang up 2-3 more attacks at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T19:28:21-07:00","id":1397426,"title":"","content":"I worry that the most iconic ability of Steel Devil Style, Double Attack Technique, ranges from worthless to decent to your enemy is weak enough why bother, while Dual-Slaying Stance is weirdly outside of the rest of the style and incredibly strong.<br /> Especially since Triple Attack Technique is reliant on Double Attack Technique, and barely adds any damage when it works (half charge-[their defense after 2 attacks]), Steel Devil Strike, Empty Mind Strike and Dervish Blade Frenzy are reliant on Double Attack Technique, Steel Devil form is incompatible with Dual-Slaying Stance until Whirling Guillotine Dance.<br /> It sort of feels like you could end up with a character with basically 4 useful charms (Naked Fang Draw, Dual-Slaying Stance, Seconds Between Strife, Twin Blade Defense), 3 upgrade charms (Sonic Slash, Whirling Guillotine Dance, Iron Lotus Unfurling), and 5 deadweight charms. I'm not even certain how useful Seconds Between Strife and Sonic Slash are - how often does your enemy move away while you're rushing them?<br /> It's not necessarily weak - Dual-Slaying stance is terrifying, Twin Blade Defense is good, and number of charms matters way less than how good your best few charms are, but it doesn't feel good to me.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;I use full defense because doing so makes my form charm give me free counterattacks&quot; is basically Crane Style, and it annoys me that Steel Devil Style is stealing Crane's thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T20:45:15-07:00","id":1397439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397426#post1397426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I worry that the most iconic ability of Steel Devil Style, Double Attack Technique, ranges from worthless to decent to your enemy is weak enough why bother</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious about where this is coming from. Is it just a symptom of everyone being combat monsters so every enemy needs to have defense 7+ with penalty negation? The damage bonus of DAT and TAT work out like this:<br /> <br /> DAT<br /> <br /> Defense 0 = +9 damage needing 1 success<br /> Defense 1 = +9 damage needing 2 successes<br /> Defense 2 = +8 damage needing 3 successes<br /> Defense 3 = +7 damage needing 5 successes<br /> Defense 4 = +6 damage needing 7 successes<br /> Defense 5 = +5 damage needing 9 successes<br /> <br /> And TAT does this<br /> <br /> Defense 0 = +13 damage needing 1 success<br /> Defense 1 = +13 damage needing 2 successes<br /> Defense 2 = +12 damage needing 4 successes<br /> Defense 3 = +10 damage needing 6 successes<br /> Defense 4 = +8 damage needing 9 successes<br /> Defense 5 = +6 damage needing 12 successes<br /> <br /> For either 2 or 3 motes, it does 8 bonus damage and triples your onslaught penalty against a foe with Defense 4 if you get TAT off. The enemy doesn't even have to have a base defense of 4, it could be like a Boar-Tusk Crocodile with a base parry of 5 but already hit with an onslaught or wound penalty.<br /> <br /> It only becomes useless or nearly useless against things like Fakharu, who's got Evasion 7 and doesn't suffer onslaught penalties unless you've got a warstrider. If it's just Fakharu though, you don't need any tricks, just facing 5 to 1 odds against combat Solars is going to be way more than enough to kill him easily. If he's not alone target the things that don't have legendary size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T06:08:26-07:00","id":1397495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397439#post1397439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious about where this is coming from. Is it just a symptom of everyone being combat monsters so every enemy needs to have defense 7+ with penalty negation? The damage bonus of DAT and TAT work out like this:<br /> <br /> DAT<br /> <br /> Defense 0 = +9 damage needing 1 success<br /> Defense 1 = +9 damage needing 2 successes<br /> Defense 2 = +8 damage needing 3 successes<br /> Defense 3 = +7 damage needing 5 successes<br /> Defense 4 = +6 damage needing 7 successes<br /> Defense 5 = +5 damage needing 9 successes<br /> <br /> And TAT does this<br /> <br /> Defense 0 = +13 damage needing 1 success<br /> Defense 1 = +13 damage needing 2 successes<br /> Defense 2 = +12 damage needing 4 successes<br /> Defense 3 = +10 damage needing 6 successes<br /> Defense 4 = +8 damage needing 9 successes<br /> Defense 5 = +6 damage needing 12 successes<br /> <br /> For either 2 or 3 motes, it does 8 bonus damage and triples your onslaught penalty against a foe with Defense 4 if you get TAT off. The enemy doesn't even have to have a base defense of 4, it could be like a Boar-Tusk Crocodile with a base parry of 5 but already hit with an onslaught or wound penalty.<br /> <br /> It only becomes useless or nearly useless against things like Fakharu, who's got Evasion 7 and doesn't suffer onslaught penalties unless you've got a warstrider. If it's just Fakharu though, you don't need any tricks, just facing 5 to 1 odds against combat Solars is going to be way more than enough to kill him easily. If he's not alone target the things that don't have legendary size.</div> </div> </div> </div>My 3 categories correspond roughly to defense 1-3 (if you have optimized stats and combat charms it doesn't really matter how strong those charms are) , defense 4-5 (3m for a conditional +5 or 6 to damage is decent - compare to Elegant Weapon Repertoire, Kiss of the Sun Concentration, Seven Points of Weakness Strike, Striking Cobra Technique - as is a charm that adds 1 or 2 conditional extra damage for 0 extra motes), and defense 6+ (you are very unlikely to frequently roll 11 successes, and doing so only adds 4 damage for 3m)<br /> Also, all of this seems to assume you have dex 5 charge 8 or similar, which costs 8i to get the charge<br /> <br /> On the topic of combat monsters: The attack roll successes needed to to trigger double or triple attack technique against defense x always exceed x. Unless everyone is at such low stats that the bonus dice for withering accuracy make up the difference, triggering double and triple attack technique require the optimization of the attacker exceed the of the defender. Triggering them reliably enough that the mote efficiency doesn't drop below similar charms require even more optimization - if you roll 14 dice against defense 4, you have a 57% chance of triggering DAT for +6 damage, and a 27% chance of triggering TAT for an extra +2, for a total of 3.96 extra damage for 3m and 2 charms. Very few characters roll 14 dice to attack and have defense 4.<br /> <br /> All of this seems to be assuming a dex 5, martial arts 5, essence 3 exalt, who has similarly high wits+awareness. Yes, this is a combat monster. Insofar as we pay attention to how well it can fight, the question should be how well it fights in battles that challenge a combat monster. &quot;Can kill 2 greenmaws alongside a friend&quot; is a low bar for a dex 5, martial arts 5, wits 5, awareness 5 essence 3 dragon blood. The greenmaws did not land an attack the entire fight, while spending willpower. Darla never missed, and Rag, the mortal, missed once.<br /> <br /> Also - the scorebook exalted quick characters, assuming full excellency, a 1-point stunt, and willpower, have defenses ranging from 8 to 13. Fakharu can enhances his 7 evasion with stunt, willpower, and causing 1s and 2s to subtract successes (which admittedly is weaker against Steel Devil Style than just a defense boost would be)<br /> <br /> I think I have been downplaying existing onslaught penalty, though it does play into the &quot;if your exalts outnumber the greenmaws, you can win without charms, or with weak charms, or with strong charms&quot; category. I also tend to allow NPCs to stunt their defense, which makes it slightly worse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T08:23:44-07:00","id":1397514,"title":"","content":"I might need to run a test with an actual full circle of exalts to show what I mean. If I don\u2019t track the spirit\u2019s motes or use enemies without charms I think I can do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T09:20:24-07:00","id":1397530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397514#post1397514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might need to run a test with an actual full circle of exalts to show what I mean. If I don\u2019t track the spirit\u2019s motes or use enemies without charms I think I can do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess my request is, please run a fight where the two sides are close-ish to evenly matched, where the Steel Devil Stylist struggles, where they take hits and are close to losing, or close to taking damage. I want to see how well Double Attack Technique fairs in a fight where every iota of power counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T09:26:47-07:00","id":1397532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397530#post1397530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess my request is, please run a fight where the two sides are close-ish to evenly matched, where the Steel Devil Stylist struggles, where they take hits and are close to losing, or close to taking damage. I want to see how well Double Attack Technique fairs in a fight where every iota of power counts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m thinking five DBs built as the system expects, as in Tomb of Dreams, vs five clawstriders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T09:31:06-07:00","id":1397534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1397439#post1397439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious about where this is coming from. Is it just a symptom of everyone being combat monsters so every enemy needs to have defense 7+ with penalty negation? The damage bonus of DAT and TAT work out like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, I will say that when I commented, I hadn't thought very carefully about it - I just remembered previously glancing at Steel Devil and thinking it wasn't very good. It's why I used a question mark. For instance, I think when I first looked at Steel Devil I probably thought you had to build up Charge slowly over time as described in the sidebar, and didn't realize you could max it on your Join Battle roll. <br /> <br /> That said, I think that for evaluating Martial Arts styles on power level concerns for Solars, a typical scenario that comes up in a lot of Solar games and that will be somewhat difficult is a Wyld hunt or other fight against multiple DBs. Evaluating against, specifically, the Immaculates in the core book might be a good starting point. With stunt and excellency, their defenses are 8, 10, and 10.<br /> <br /> One could also go to the other end of the spectrum and try a Essence 1, Dex 3, Martial Arts 3, Naked Fang Draw, Double Attack Technique non-combat-optimized Solar against easier foes.<br /> <br /> The other thing is maybe it's better to say that the mechanics of Steel Devil Style are just a bit weird. For instance, having something called &quot;charge&quot; which you don't have to charge but in fact can max out before taking your first turn is a bit odd. Also, the fact that Triple Attack Technique is so devastating against weaker foes and comparably weaker against stronger ones is odd. Like, in general having some weaker allies in the fight is a risk, because they can be used to farm Initiative, but it's also a benefit, as they can steal a few points of Initiative, threaten a crash, threaten a decisive, or save you from losing Initiative. Steel Devil Style, by being so effective at farming initiative, makes them much more of a liability. I think it's probably possible to set up a fight of a Steel Devil stylists vs. another Exalt where the other Exalt easily wins if they don't bring their mortal retainer and easily loses if they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T09:46:22-07:00","id":1397536,"title":"","content":"Fighting a group of immaculate monks is about the only time you\u2019re ever going to be fighting multiple opponents with excellencies and penalty negating charms though. That\u2019s not just a bad place to start it\u2019s basically Steel Devil\u2019s worst matchup for judging if DAT works. Well okay a worse one would be multiple on one combat against the SD stylist. <br /> <br /> I think we should start with the claw striders and if that works then maybe work up from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T10:29:57-07:00","id":1397546,"title":"","content":"I'll note that Lunars get a nice bonus to Double Attack Technique with Finding the Needles Eye subtracting 1 from defense which means they need to roll 2 less successes for a successfull double attack technique.<br /> <br /> The real power of the style is in Dual-Slaying Stance though, which is a very strong form charm with the major drawback of costing 1wp. Since unlike Crane you don't have to use full defense you can take other actions like commanding battlegroups, casting spells. or singing battle-anthems while sitting at +2 parry and counterattacking.<br /> <br /> If you save your wp and only go with the defensive form in harder fights and othewise use DAT to finnish the cannon fodder faster it doesn't look like a bad MA. It's not Single-Point or Righteous Devil but I feel it's on the level of Snake, Tiger, or Dreaming Pear Courtesan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T10:41:22-07:00","id":1397550,"title":"","content":"It depends a lot on ST style and campaign as well, but that\u2019s just how some MAs work. Golden Jannisary in a campaign where you only ever fight Creatures of Darkness once is a pretty bad choice for example. <br /> <br /> When you\u2019ve got things like Bloodapes or Clawstriders hanging around in the combat though, they\u2019re not TOO hard to put down, but they\u2019re pretty deadly. Being able to end and/or cripple a bloodape in one attack can make a pretty big difference. Then again that depends a lot on your party makeup though, if everyone is a Super combatant who are effectively immune to the Attacks of the enemies then you don\u2019t really give a crap, and you\u2019re probably fighting some homebrew mega-epic things anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T23:35:22-07:00","id":1397632,"title":"","content":"So I literally just took characters from Tomb of Dreams and remade them using basically the same stats, but occasionally changing their combat ability, adding a few combat charms, and in the case of Darla the Devil a lot of combat charms. As well as giving some of them artifacts and specialties where it makes sense.<br /> <br /> Avery the Archer ripped off MIrror Flag<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 2/3/2<br /> <br /> 6 Join Battle<br /> <br /> Jade Longbow 10+2 (Damage 15/4) 5+2 accuacy for decisive attacks.<br /> Evasion 2+1<br /> Soak 7<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Relevent Charms<br /> <br /> Unobstructed Hunter's Aim<br /> Sky Calming Draw<br /> <br /> Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Flickering Candle Meditation<br /> <br /> Awareness Excellency<br /> <br /> Ox Body Technique x2<br /> <br /> -0x1/-1x2/-2x6/-4x1/I<br /> <br /> 39m<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Darla the Devil, ripped off Faka Kun<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 2/5/2<br /> <br /> 10 Join Battle<br /> <br /> Jade Dualblades 16+6 (Damage 12/4) 11+6 for decisive<br /> Parry 6<br /> Soak 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Relevent charms<br /> <br /> All of Steel Devil up to Essence 2 and Become the Hammer.<br /> <br /> two ox bodies<br /> <br /> Awareness excellency<br /> <br /> -0x1/-1x2/-2x6/-4x1/I<br /> <br /> <br /> 39m<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sally the Swordsman, ripped off Fire Orchid<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 3/3/3<br /> <br /> 7 Join Battle<br /> <br /> Straightsword 10+5 (Damage 12/5) 8+5 for decisive<br /> Parry 5+2<br /> Soak 8<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Relevant charms<br /> <br /> Stoking Bonfire Style<br /> Burning Fury Wreath<br /> Graceful Flowing Defense<br /> Crimson Fang Bite<br /> Crossfire Flash<br /> <br /> Oxbody x2<br /> <br /> Awareness excellency<br /> <br /> -0x1/-1x4/-2x4/-4x1/I<br /> <br /> 44m<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And Thorton the Thrower, ripping off Iay Selak<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">2/2/3<br /> <br /> 6 join battle<br /> <br /> Throwing Knives 8+3 (Damage 9) 5+3 for decisive<br /> Evasion 3+2<br /> Soak 6<br /> <br /> <br /> Relevent charms<br /> <br /> Seekign Throw Technique<br /> Armor-Rupturing Fang<br /> <br /> Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Flicering Candle Meditation<br /> Hopping Firecracker Evasion<br /> <br /> oxbody x2<br /> <br /> Awareness excellency<br /> <br /> <br /> -0x1/-1x4/-2x4/-4x1/I<br /> <br /> 44m<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I also had Brent the Brawler ripping off Volfer, but with some less combat focused charms because I gave so many to Faka Kun, but I couldn't run a 5v5. It's a shame though, with a charm that adds the enemy's onslaught penalty to your damage combined with onslaught penalties up to -5 in this fight, it could have been good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Avery will join battle, spending 2m rolling 6 dice for 7i<br /> Darla will spend 5m for Naked Fang Draw, rolling 10 dice for 9i<br /> Sally will spend 2m rolling 7 dice for 8i<br /> Thorton will spend 2m for 9i<br /> <br /> Claw1 rolls 4 dice +1wp for 5i<br /> Claw2 rolls 4 dice +1wp for 7i<br /> Claw3 rolls 4 dice +1wp for 4i<br /> Claw4 rolls 4 dice +1wp for 9i<br /> <br /> <br /> Darla fills her charge gauge<br /> <br /> Avery 7i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla 2i 34m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally 8i 42m 5wp<br /> Thorton 9i 42m 5wp<br /> Claw1 5i 4wp<br /> Claw2 7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 4i 4wp<br /> Claw4 9i 4wp<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ==============<br /> Claw4 is going to attempt a decisive claw attack against Thorton, spending a willpower to boost the damage, Thorton will clash, spending 3m into his throwing knife attack. Clawstrider rolls 12+3 for 7 successes, and Thorton rolls 13 for only 5.<br /> <br /> Clawstrider deals 12 damage and gets 6 successes.<br /> <br /> Avery 7i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla 2i 34m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally 8i 42m 5wp<br /> Thorton *9i 39m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 5i 4wp<br /> Claw2 7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 4i 4wp<br /> Claw4 *3i 3wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Sally then goes, attempting to wither Claw2, spending 5m to excellency and 3m 1wp on Crimson Fang Bite. Rolling 15 successes for 6, then rolling 10 damage for 6, just barely missing the crash.<br /> <br /> Avery 7i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla 2i 34m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally *15i 34m 4wp<br /> Thorton *9i 39m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 5i 4wp<br /> Claw2 1i 4wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> Claw3 4i 4wp<br /> Claw4 *3i 3wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Avery attempts to go for Claw1, spending 2m for 12 dice, getting 8, and then rolling 12 damage for 10, crashing Claw1.<br /> <br /> Avery *23i 35m 5wp<br /> Darla 2i 34m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally *15i 34m 4wp<br /> Thorton *9i 39m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 -5i 4wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> Claw2 1i 4wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> Claw3 4i 4wp<br /> Claw4 *3i 3wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Claw3 goes, decisive Sally with a claw attack, spending a willpower to boost damage and rolling 12+4 dice, Sally will defend with a 4m excellency. Claw3 gets a total of 9 successes and hits sally, rolling 7 damage for 4, putting Sally into -1s.<br /> <br /> Avery *23i 35m 5wp<br /> Darla 2i 34m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally *15i 30m 4wp Onslaught(-1) 4L(-1s)<br /> Thorton *9i 39m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 -5i 4wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> Claw2 1i 4wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> Claw3 *3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 *3i 3wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Darla will now wither Claw2, with a 6m full excellency and 3m DAT, and stunt, Claw2 will stunt. Rolling 24 dice for 13 successes, then rolling 17 damage for 11 after rerolls. Crashing Claw2<br /> <br /> Avery *23i 35m 5wp<br /> Darla *19i 25m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally *15i 30m 4wp Onslaught(-1) 4L(-1s)<br /> Thorton *9i 39m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 -5i 4wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> Claw2 -10i 4wp Onslaught(-4)<br /> Claw3 *3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 *3i 3wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Claw1 will now go, firing off a withering bite against Sally, spending a willpower, who will spend 4m to excellency, and 2m 1i for Graceful Flowing Defense. Rolling 8+4 dice for 7, hitting by 1. Then rolling 8 damage for 6.<br /> <br /> Avery *23i 35m 5wp<br /> Darla *19i 25m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally *8i 24m 4wp Onslaught(-2) 4L(-1s)<br /> Thorton *9i 39m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 *1i 3wp<br /> Claw2 -10i 4wp Onslaught(-4)<br /> Claw3 *3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 *3i 3wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Claw 2 will now attack Sally with a withering bite, who will defend the same way, and just barely hit with 6 successes, then rolling 7 damage for 3<br /> <br /> Avery *23i 35m 5wp<br /> Darla *19i 25m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally *5i 24m 4wp Onslaught(-2) 4L(-1s)<br /> Thorton *9i 39m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 *1i 3wp<br /> Claw2 *-7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 *3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 *3i 3wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ==============<br /> Avery 23i 39m 5wp<br /> Darla 19i 30m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally 5i 29m 4wp Onslaught(-2) 4L(-1s)<br /> Thorton 9i 44m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 1i 3wp<br /> Claw2 -7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 3i 3wp Onslaught(-1)<br /> <br /> <br /> Avery will go for a decisive strike against Claw4, spending 2m to get 7 dice, and missing with only one success.<br /> <br /> Avery *20i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla 19i 30m 5wp 7charge<br /> Sally 5i 29m 4wp Onslaught(-2) 4L(-1s)<br /> Thorton 9i 44m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 1i 3wp<br /> Claw2 -7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 3i 3wp<br /> Claw4 3i 3wp Onslaught(-2)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Darla will strike Claw4 with a withering attack, using 6m excellency and 3m DAT, Claw4 will stunt to defend and spend a willpower. Rolling 24 dice for 11 successes, then rolling 15 damage for 7, crashing Claw4.<br /> <br /> Darla will reflexively use 5m 1wp to reflexively lauch Steel Devil Strike against Claw3, who will defend with a willpower. Rolling 11+2 dice for 6, hitting Claw3, and rolling 13 damage for...only 3. not enough to make them flee.<br /> <br /> Avery *20i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla *19i 16m 4wp 7charge<br /> Sally 5i 29m 4wp Onslaught(-2) 4L(-1s)<br /> Thorton 9i 44m 5wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 1i 3wp<br /> Claw2 -7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 3i 3wp Onslaught(-1) 3L(-1s)<br /> Claw4 -4i 3wp Onslaught(-5)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Thorton will go next, attempting to finish off claw4 with a decisive strike, spending 2m to get 5 dice, and hitting defense 0, with only one success. Then rolling 9 damage for 3, causing Claw4 to flee.<br /> <br /> Avery *20i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla *19i 16m 4wp 7charge<br /> Sally 5i 29m 4wp Onslaught(-2) 4L(-1s)<br /> Thorton *3i 42m 5wp 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 1i 3wp<br /> Claw2 -7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 3i 3wp Onslaught(-1) 3L(-1s)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Sally will then attempt to wither Claw3, spending 5m to excellency. Rolling 14 dice for 9 successes, then rolling 12 damage for 5, crashing Claw3.<br /> <br /> Avery *20i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla *19i 16m 4wp 7charge<br /> Sally *16i 24m 4wp 4L(-1s)<br /> Thorton *3i 42m 5wp 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 1i 3wp<br /> Claw2 -7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 -2i 3wp Onslaught(-2) 3L(-1s)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Claw1 will attempt a decisive claw strike on sally, boosting damage, who will defend with 4m, and 2m 1i Graceful Flowing Defense. Rolling 12+2 and hitting with 8, then rolling 3 damage for 2L<br /> <br /> Avery *20i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla *19i 16m 4wp 7charge<br /> Sally *15i 18m 4wp Onslaught(-1) 6L(-2s)<br /> Thorton *3i 42m 5wp 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 *3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 -7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 -2i 3wp Onslaught(-2) 3L(-1s)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Claw3 will now attempt to withering bite sally, who will defend with 4m and 2m 1i GFD. Rolling 8+2 for 6, hitting Sally, and dealing only one damage on 8 dice.<br /> <br /> Avery *20i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla *19i 16m 4wp 7charge<br /> Sally *14i 12m 4wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Thorton *3i 42m 5wp 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 *3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 -7i 4wp<br /> Claw3 0i 3wp 3L(-1s)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> Claw2 will now wither Sally, who won't bother spending motes to defend, getting 7 to hit and then rolling 13 damage dice for 8 damage, pulling out of crash.<br /> <br /> Avery *20i 37m 5wp<br /> Darla *19i 16m 4wp 7charge<br /> Sally *4i 12m 4wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Thorton *3i 42m 5wp 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 *3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 1i 4wp<br /> Claw3 0i 3wp 3L(-1s)<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ==============<br /> Avery 20i 42m 5wp<br /> Darla 19i 21m 4wp 7charge<br /> Sally 4i 17m 4wp Onslaught(-2) 6L(-2s)<br /> Thorton 3i 44m 5wp 6L(-2s)<br /> Claw1 3i 3wp<br /> Claw2 1i 4wp<br /> Claw3 0i 3wp 3L(-1s)<br /> <br /> <br /> Avery tries to decsive Claw2, spending a willpower and 2m to get 7 dice, hitting with 6, and dealing 6 damage, enough to cause it to flee and end the fight.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> That Steel Devil Strike dealing only 3 damage on 13 dice really sucked, if it hadn't been for that it would have taken out two potential decisive damage dealers in one turn. I think I'd need to do more testing, but I think this crew might be a bit soft to take on their like number in greenmaws, so maybe like 2-3 greenmaws or something.<br /> <br /> I forgot how well the system actually works at making tense meaningful battles when not everyone is min-maxed to the fullest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T20:10:23-07:00","id":1398107,"title":"","content":"Okay so I swapped out Avery for Brent and ran it against three Greenmaws.<br /> <br /> This really gave me the feeling of &quot;This is how Exalted is meant to be played.&quot; I kind of wish I'd listened to my own advice and launched a decisive slam attack with the first grapple gambit, but it worked out anyway.<br /> <br /> I'm not really impressed by the way Steel Devil performed, but I don't necessarily hate it either. Building onslaught and wound penalties to easily get off your Triple Attack Technique definitely seemed to work, but it did involve occasionally delaying her action to get the most out of onslaught, and convincing her ally to launch a low initiative decisive to get her wound penalty stacking. Although the upside is that her penalty stacking with triple onslaught penalty really put the Greenmaw into the ground, and let the Water Brawl character take a huge advantage of that. Getting five damage for 2m with Pounding Surf style was great.<br /> <br /> You really feel the combination of stunt+willpower against DAT though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something else I noticed though is that Steel Devil can keep you pretty safe, interestingly. Because of the way it attacks, and deals decisive damage with Steel Devil Strike, you can stay at relatively high initiative, without being SO high at enemies want to wither you to try and bring you down before you hit them.<br /> <br /> Brent the Brawler - Ripped off of Volfer<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getE