-Yadh: 3i (50m, 0WP, 6L4B), -4 Wound Penalty (10), -3 Bone Crushing, Prone<br /> <br /> Round 31<br /> <br /> 12i. Ganan uses a Full Excellency Earthshaker Attack (0/3m, 3WP, 7i). He rolls 17 dice for 5 successes. Mata-Yadh resists with 3 dice for 3 successes, failing. Ganan inflicts 8B and a Short range fall, which inflicts another 4B. Ganan resets to 3i. MY is knocked to Short Range. Ganan reflexively moves to Close.<br /> <br /> 3i. MY stands up (2 successes).<br /> <br /> Ganan: 3i (0/8m, 3WP, 3a, 1L (-0)) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form, 4 Charges<br /> Mata-Yadh: 3i (50m, 0WP, 6L16B), -4 Wound Penalty (10), -3 Bone Crushing<br /> <br /> Round 32<br /> <br /> 3i. MY Clashes with 9 dice for 3 successes. Ganan Clashes with a Withering, Smash, Force of the Mountain, 3m Excellency for 21 dice, rolling 12 successes, 12 dice of damage for 9i (12i/-6i).<br /> <br /> Ganan: 12i (0/7m, 3WP, 3a, 1L (-0)) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form, 4 Charges<br /> Mata-Yadh: -6i (50m, 0WP, 6L16B), -4 Wound Penalty (10), -3 Bone Crushing, Prone</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Round 33<br /> <br /> Anima: Zero damage.<br /> <br /> 12i. ONLY ONE! Ganan Decisives against Mata-Yadh\u2019s Parry 1 with a 1m Excellency, rolling 12 dice, hitting and rolling 12i of damage for 7 successes, easily incapacitating the beast with a grand total of 6 Lethal and 23 Bashing, which fills the 26 Health Levels of the Behemoth and rolls round to inflict a final total of 9 Lethal and 17 Bashing.<br /> <br /> And yes, I only now realize that Ganan forgot the discount for Pasiap Preempts Haste in Round 1, so should have had 3m more the entire fight. Oh well.<br /> <br /> I would be very interested in how this performs with a Lorarli riding it, a Cataphract fighting by its side, and maybe a Silverwright battlegroup against a Circle of Celestials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-07-2020, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T18:05:45-08:00","id":1427658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427655#post1427655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be very interested in how this performs with a Lorarli riding it, a Cataphract fighting by its side, and maybe a Silverwright battlegroup against a Circle of Celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking something similar, although I can't run that on my own. Mata-Yadh is an okay centerpiece to a much larger fey force. Why the Lorelei riding it though? Surely a cataphract riding it as well as one beside commanding the BG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T18:47:45-08:00","id":1427660,"title":"","content":"Has anyone done fights of Exalts vs. mortal battlegroups? Like how many battle-ready troops would it take to seriously challenge a starting character, or to defeat one of the QC's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T20:44:54-08:00","id":1427674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427660#post1427660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone done fights of Exalts vs. mortal battlegroups? Like how many battle-ready troops would it take to seriously challenge a starting character, or to defeat one of the QC's?</div> </div> </div> </div>One built like a PC? Even size 5 wouldn't be enough to threaten them really. Maybe if they had multiple highly skilled commanders that couldn't be dealt with quickly you could do something with a lucky engage action. They'd be able to threaten QC characters pretty good though.<br /> <br /> You might be able to get away with one commander if the PC didn't have a full tank, but it depends, if they have enough left to get rid of that commander right off the hop still no.<br /> <br /> In all cases, if it's a Dawn we're talking about, there is zero chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T03:18:16-08:00","id":1427690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427660#post1427660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone done fights of Exalts vs. mortal battlegroups? Like how many battle-ready troops would it take to seriously challenge a starting character, or to defeat one of the QC's?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, any soakbeast lunar is beyond the reach of mortal weapons (even of battlegroups).<br /> <br /> Or I may be wrong, tell me can a size 5 mortal battlegroup defeat a demigod with 25 soak?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T05:36:57-08:00","id":1427701,"title":"","content":"Volfer vs Size 5 Battle Group of Battle Ready Troops (Average Drill) \u2013 No Stunts<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Join Battle<br /> <br /> Volfer spends 6m to Full Excellency his Join Battle (7/33m) for 7i<br /> Battle-Group spends rolls 6 dice for 4i.<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> 7i. Volfer attacks with Excellent Strike and a 4m Fire and Stones Strike (4/29m) rolling 10 dice with an automatic success, rerolling 1s against Defense 5. He rolls 8 successes, hitting (8i), then rolls (14+3-13) 4+4 dice of damage for 3 magnitude.<br /> <br /> 4i. The BRTs will try to Engage with their Chopping swords. They spend Willpower and roll 12 dice. Volfer defends with a Full Excellency (0/25m) for Parry 9. BRT roll 4+1 successes, missing (1i).<br /> <br /> Volfer: 8i (0/30m, 6WP)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 1i, Magnitude 8, Size 5, 3WP<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> 8i. Volfer attacks with Excellent Strike and a 1m Fire and Stones Strike (0/26m). He rolls 11 successes, hitting (9i), then rolls (14+6-13) 7+1 dice of damage for 5 magnitude.<br /> <br /> 1i. BRTs try a WP backed Wither. Volfer defends on a 4m Excellency (0/22m). BRTs get six successes, missing.<br /> <br /> Volfer: 9i (0/27m, 6WP)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 1i, Magnitude 3, Size 5, 2WP<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> 9i. Volfer attacks with Excellent Strike and a 1m Fire and Stones Strike (0/23) for 7 successes. He rolls (14+2-13) 3+1 dice of damage for 1 magnitude.<br /> <br /> 1i. BRTs try the same as before. Volfer defends on a 4m Excellency (0/19m). BRTs get four successes, missing.<br /> <br /> Volfer: 10i (0/24m, 6WP)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 1i, Magnitude 2, Size 5, 2WP<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> 10i. Volfer attacks with Excellent Strike and a 1m Fire and Stones Strike (0/20m) for 5 successes. He rolls (14+1-13) 2+1 dice of damage for 0 magnitude.<br /> <br /> 1i. BRTs try the same as before. Volfer defends on a 4m Excellency (0/16m). BRTs get 3 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> Volfer: 11i (0/21m, 6WP)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 1i, Magnitude 2, Size 5, 1WP<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> 11i. Volfer attacks with Excellent Strike and a 1m Fire and Stones Strike (0/17m) for 8 successes. He rolls (14+3-13) 4+1 dice of damage for 2 magnitude.<br /> <br /> BRTs check for rout and succeeds. Volfer gets an Initiative Break for 17i. Hundreds of troops break and flee.<br /> .<br /> 1i. The BRTs will try to Wither with their Chopping swords. They spend Willpower and roll 11 dice. Volfer defends with a 4m Excellency (0/13m) for Parry 7. BRT roll 6+1 successes, hitting. Volfer spends 4m on Spirit Strengthens the Skin (0/9m). They roll (16-7-4) 4 dice of damage for 3i (1i/14i).<br /> <br /> Volfer: 14i (0/14m, 6WP)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 1i, Magnitude 11, Size 4, 0WP<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> 14i. Volfer attacks with Excellent Strike and a 1m Fire and Stones Strike (0/10m) for 8 successes. He rolls (14+3-13) 4+1 dice of damage for 4 magnitude.<br /> <br /> 1i. BRTs are out of Willpower. They attack on 11 dice. Volfer boosts Parry to 6 (0/8m). BRTs roll 5 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> Volfer: 15i (0/13m, 6WP)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 1i, Magnitude 7, Size 4, 0WP<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> 15i. Volfer attacks with Excellent Strike and a 1m Fire and Stones Strike (0/9m) for 8 successes. He rolls (14+3-13) 4+1 dice of damage for 7 magnitude.<br /> <br /> BRTs check for rout, passing. Volfer gets a Crash Bonus (21i).<br /> <br /> 1i. BRTs attack, now on 10 dice. Volfer boosts Parry to 6 (0/7m). BRTs roll 9 successes (WFT, hax), hitting. Volfer boosts Soak by 4 (0/3m). They roll (15+3-7-4) 7 dice of damage for 4i (1i/17i).<br /> <br /> Volfer: 17i (0/8m, 6WP)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 1i, Magnitude 10, Size 3<br /> <br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> 17i. Volfer Aims.<br /> <br /> 1i. BRTs attack on 10 dice. Volfer boosts Parry to 6 with WP (5WP) and 7 with 2m (0/6m). BRTs roll 6 successes, missing.<br /> <br /> Volfer: 17i (0/11m, 5WP)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 1i, Magnitude 10, Size 3<br /> <br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> 17i. Volfer spends 4m on the Excellency to Decisive (3+5+4+3) rolling 15 dice vs Parry 5, hitting. He rolls 17i in damage with a bonus of levels for 11 Magnitude.<br /> <br /> BRTs check for rout and fail.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Using only Excellent Strike, Fire and Stone\u2019s Strike, and Spirit Strengthens the skin, Volfer beats a Size 5 Battle-group of Battle-Ready Troops without flaring, Clashing, using any equipment not given in his starting Tomb of Dreams write up, or taking a single level of damage. No disengauging, no kiting, no delaying. One use of Aim.<br /> <br /> I've posted several starting Dragon-Blooded builds that have turned Volfer into red paste in two rounds. You would need multiple size 5 battle-groups to take down an Exalt even moderately invested in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-08-2020, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T08:59:52-08:00","id":1427714,"title":"","content":"Yeah, BGs just straight-up don't work as a whole fight unto themselves.<br /> <br /> I also think BGs are too weak. But what power they have is in (1) party-wise attacks, which are irrelevant against a lone combat character, (2) the ability to gain 3-10 bonus dice on all those attacks based on who's leading them, and (3) unrewarding to attack and slow to die, due to having 20+ &quot;-0 hls&quot; and only giving you 1i for hitting them regardless of damage. That all makes them really useful for steadily bleeding the resources of a group who are mostly fighting a few named characters, but as Volfer just showed, all it means alone is a boring and one-sided fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T09:04:11-08:00","id":1427716,"title":"","content":"Yeah if you want something to fight a full circle who are fresh and full of motes, maybe a size 5 battlegroup of Silent Legionaires with might 1+ from their alchemical battle transformation, elite drill, and lead by Cathak Cainen and at least one other DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T10:17:46-08:00","id":1427724,"title":"","content":"Battlegroups work fine if they have a commander and you're fighting a whole circle -- and thus getting an attack against each of them every round. Five Size 5 Battlegroups against 5 Volfers would be a closer fight. And, okay, Volfer didn't flare or anything... but he's finishing that fight with just 7 peripheral motes left -- if a Dragon-Blooded officer were to suddenly appear at this point whilst he's trapped in a burning tea room, he would be in <i>serious </i>trouble. Battlegroups absolutely work as an encounter, but the goal of an encounter isn't to kill the PCs.<br /> <br /> That said, I tried running this again against the Young Dynast QC and hit an interesting rules snag.<br /> <br /> If you are Crashed, do you get to apply Soak against a Battlegroup's attack? If so, the Young Dynast actually managed to scrape a win (cost all her motes and Willpower, and three health levels, but she did it). If not then she died... horribly... like a stuck pig.<br /> <br /> Here's the fight:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Young Dynast vs Size 5 Battlegroup of Battle-Ready Soldiers<br /> <br /> \u201cIdentify yourself! We have you surrounded!\u201d<br /> <br /> Gifty unslings her daiklave, \u201cI am Dragonsgift Saber Edge. And all I am surrounded by is fear and dead men.\u201d<br /> <br /> Join Battle<br /> <br /> Gifty spends 2m to roll 8 dice on Join Battle for 7i (10/17m)<br /> Battle Ready troops roll 6 dice for 6i<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> 7i. Young Dynast delays to Clash (5i)<br /> <br /> 6i. BRTs Engage with Willpower rolling 12 dice for 7 successes. YD uses a 4m Excellency and 2m Stoking Bonfire Style, with Willpower (10/11m, 4WP), rolling 13 dice for 8 successes. She rolls (15+1+4-13) 7 dice of damage plus Clash for 6 Magnitude.<br /> <br /> Young Dynast: 6i (10/16m, 4WP, 1a)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 4i, Magnitude 5, Size 5, 3WP<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> 8i. YD delays to clash (6i).<br /> <br /> 4i. BRTs do the same again rolling 12 dice for 6 successes. YD does likewise rolling 8 successes. She rolls 8 dice of damage for another 6 Magnitude.<br /> <br /> BRTs test for rout and pass.<br /> <br /> Young Dynast: 5i (10/15m, 3WP, 2a)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 2i, Magnitude 11, Size 4, 2WP<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> 5i. YD delays to clash (3i).<br /> <br /> 2i. BRTs Wither for 11 dice and YD does the same as last round. 6 successes to 7. YD rolls 7 dice of damage for 5 magnitude.<br /> <br /> Young Dynast: 4i (10/14m, 2WP, 3a)<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 2i, Magnitude 6, Size 4, 1WP<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Anima Flux deals 1 damage.<br /> <br /> 4i. YD delays (2i)<br /> <br /> 2i. Clash, willpower all that good stuff. BRTs actually hit \u2013 8 successes to 3. They roll (16+5-11) 10 dice +3 of damage for 8i. YD is Crashed at -6i.<br /> <br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 2i, Magnitude 6, Size 4, 0WP<br /> Young Dynast: -6i (10/13m, 1WP, 3a), Clash, Onslaught<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Anima Flux Whiffs<br /> <br /> 2i. 11 dice to Wither. YD spends 4m to defend on Parry (4+2-2-1) 3. BRT roll 6 successes, rolling (16+3-11) 8 dice of Lethal Damage for 3L. <b>NB </b>If you can't soak a Battlegroup's attack, then they instead roll 19 dice of Lethal damage for 8 levels, killing the Young Dynast outright from full health.<br /> <br /> -6i. YD rolls the standard combo plus Raging Firestorm Blade, plus Willpower to roll 12 dice against Parry 5, hitting with 7 successes (-5i, 10/1m, 0WP). YD converts (15+2+4-13) 8 dice of damage to 8 magnitude<br /> <br /> Battlegroup passes rout check. YD gets crash break, Initiative Shifting (8/1m) for 7i.<br /> <br /> YD Withers with standard combo (2/1m), hitting for another 2 Magnitude (8i).<br /> <br /> Young Dynast: 8i (2/6m, 0WP, 1a, 3L (-1))<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 2i, Magnitude 6, Size 3, 0WP<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> 8i. YD delays to Clash (6i).<br /> <br /> 2i. BRT roll 10 dice. YD standard combos for 12 dice. YD wins 5 successes to 4 (7i). YD rolls 7 dice of damage plus Clash for 6 magnitude.<br /> <br /> BRTs pass rout. YD rises to 12i.<br /> <br /> Young Dynast: 12i (2/5m, 0WP, 2a, 3L (-1))<br /> Battle-Ready Troops: 2i, Magnitude 9, Size 2, 0WP, Onslaught, Clash<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> 12i. YD Decisives on the standard combo rolling 12 dice against Parry 2, hitting. Then rolling 12+2 decisive damage plus 4 bonus levels for 9 magnitude.<br /> <br /> BRT fails rout check and flees.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-08-2020, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T10:42:55-08:00","id":1427726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427724#post1427724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are Crashed, do you get to apply Soak against a Battlegroup's attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, you can always soak a BGs attack, at least I've never seen anyone suggest otherwise. Good fight though, if that battlegroup had passed its last route check the YD might have lost? It was a much better fight from an interest standpoint than the Volfer one either way.<br /> <br /> Of course Volfer isn't built like a PC either so...<br /> <br /> The funny thing is I think battle ready troops are actually on the higher end of the power scale. Compared to Brides of Alhat and warrior monks they've got much better soak, and their accuracy/damage is about equal or more. Zombies have bonus magnitude for being fearless, but their soak and attack dice also suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T17:55:53-08:00","id":1427783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427674#post1427674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One built like a PC?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe my players build their characters to be much less combat-focused than a typical PC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even size 5 wouldn't be enough to threaten them really. </div> </div> </div>Well, if the enemy army has 3,000 troops, that's three size 5 battlegroups, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe if they had multiple highly skilled commanders that couldn't be dealt with quickly you could do something with a lucky engage action. They'd be able to threaten QC characters pretty good though.<br /> <br /> You might be able to get away with one commander if the PC didn't have a full tank, but it depends, if they have enough left to get rid of that commander right off the hop still no.<br /> <br /> In all cases, if it's a Dawn we're talking about, there is zero chance. </div> </div> </div>Fair - and thanks to you and everyone who responded.<br /> <br /> I was wondering about two questions:<br /> <br /> (1) in regions of the world where nations and armies are not typically led by Dragonblooded (which I think is supposed to be most of the world that's not a Realm satrapy, Lookshy, or Prasad, although I'm not really sure), can an enemy nation be a threat to the PC's nation that demands more thought than &quot;We'll just walk up to their army and fight it until it's routed&quot;? If so, what kind of numbers do they need?<br /> <br /> (2) Wait, are any of these nations not led by Dragonblooded? Can an Outcaste DB just walk up to one of them and become the leader by asking nicely and then single-handedly fighting that nation's army if they decline?<br /> <br /> Of course question (1) is complicated by the existence of other fighting strategies than straight-up battle, while question (2) is complicated by this and the fact that offscreen battles between an NPC Exalt and an NPC army do not necessarily follow the combat rules.<br /> <br /> It seems like a nation that can field an army of multiple thousands is a threat to starting characters that is worthy of doing something interesting like finding allies, sowing dissension in the enemy ranks, or stealthily attacking supply lines to deal with, but no less, unless the Storyteller uses them in an indirect way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T18:37:49-08:00","id":1427789,"title":"","content":"While most nations are probably not led by outcastes, there are more than enough Threshold outcastes to go around whenever you need a nation/army that is led by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T19:25:08-08:00","id":1427796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427783#post1427783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, maybe my players build their characters to be much less combat-focused than a typical PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to find that dex 5, combat ability 5, omni-applicable specialty, artifact weapons/armor and 3-5 combat charms is about standard for any PC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427783#post1427783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if the enemy army has 3,000 troops, that's three size 5 battlegroups, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but probably only one at a time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427783#post1427783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in regions of the world where nations and armies are not typically led by Dragonblooded (which I think is supposed to be most of the world that's not a Realm satrapy, Lookshy, or Prasad, although I'm not really sure), can an enemy nation be a threat to the PC's nation that demands more thought than &quot;We'll just walk up to their army and fight it until it's routed&quot;? If so, what kind of numbers do they need?</div> </div> </div> </div>...not mechanically no. If you don't have supernatural power, pretty big supernatural power, on your side against a nation who has PCs then you will fail spectacularly. The Dawn and the Zenith will play rock-paper-scissors for who gets to be the one to single handedly take them apart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427783#post1427783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, are any of these nations not led by Dragonblooded? Can an Outcaste DB just walk up to one of them and become the leader by asking nicely and then single-handedly fighting that nation's army if they decline?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm has something like 500 satrapies. So go get a map of Creation, then put 500 dots on it in places that aren't the Blessed isle, or generally the river province, and that's about the scope you're looking at. Most places of interest in Creation are in some way run by exalts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427783#post1427783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course question (1) is complicated by the existence of other fighting strategies than straight-up battle, while question (2) is complicated by this and the fact that offscreen battles between an NPC Exalt and an NPC army do not necessarily follow the combat rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the combat system is not meant to be a rock on which you can extrapolate setting facts from. The system says it works one way, the setting says it works another, the system is wrong, the setting is right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427783#post1427783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like a nation that can field an army of multiple thousands is a threat to starting characters that is worthy of doing something interesting like finding allies, sowing dissension in the enemy ranks, or stealthily attacking supply lines to deal with, but no less, unless the Storyteller uses them in an indirect way.</div> </div> </div> </div>A nation that can field several thousand mortals without supernatural commanders is grossly insufficient to challenge even a group of PCs alone, much less a nation run by PCs.<br /> <br /> For one if they're going to mess with the PCs they need to make sure they're not seen doing it, otherwise the PCs can just walk over and knock down their castle and tell them to stop it. Even sowing seeds of dissension in the ranks is iffy. Remember Solars aren't just fighting powerhouses, if the Zenith or Eclipse gives a little speech to the troops all those thoughts of dissension just melt away.<br /> <br /> Basically treat a nation of mortals fighting a nation with PCs like mortals fighting Superman, except there's no such thing as kryptonite. The only power you have over them is maybe if you do something like hold somebody hostage, or have information they want that would be lost if they kill you, or something like that. Any attempt to actually hurt them directly is pretty much doomed to failure, except in the most insanely lucky and extreme circumstances. Like you planned out a 16 stage plot assuming they'd easily handle everything in every stage and planned around that.<br /> <br /> That's just mechanically though. In the lore fighting an entire nation is dangerous, you might get knifed in your sleep by an assassin, or poisoned, or simply overwhelmed by numbers. The 1e corebook even says specifically &quot;The Wyld Hunt of the Dragon-Blooded is hardly their only fear. They might be stoned or ridden down - no matter how mighty the hero, enough men with bows will eventually wear him down.&quot; So at least in the fluff in theory mortals can do that kind of thing, they just can't mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T19:54:18-08:00","id":1427799,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there are enough Outcastes to go around, whether as leaders, allies, or mercenaries. Toss one of those in a battlegroup, give them solid defenses and Roaring Dragon General, and you'll be on your way.<br /> <br /> But you don't even have to go that far. An unexalted general with a 9-12 dice Command pool still adds 3-5 dice to all a BG's attacks, which is a great force multiplier. You implied your PCs don't very optimized builds, so maybe you could protect that general with soak 10, parry 6-7, and a horse (for a little more defense in melee, and also a nice 11-15 die Disengage pool), but more likely you'll want to hide them off the field, and let them give orders using Intelligence - maybe there's an elaborate system of flags, or they're appearing like a hologram to address the troops with sorcery. These methods also allow some non-combat skills to shine, should the PCs try to disrupt their communication and/or hunt down the general directly.<br /> <br /> And, of course, there are non-DB options for a supernatural leader. They might be a sorcerer on a Cirrus Skiff at Extreme range above the battlefield as they are protected by Invulnerable Skin of Bronze and a Virtuous Guardian of Flame (and assisted by some other spell or working to get a few more Command dice, as needed). Or perhaps in desperation, this nation has accepted the aid of the Fair Folk - a Cataphract has good Command and is hard to kill quickly - establishing their Villain credentials by allowing such an &quot;ally&quot; to feed upon their own citizens in exchange for help. Or a summoned demon, local god, etc. The really important thing is that they add those dice, and don't just get sniped out immediately.<br /> <br /> (I would also advise 1-2 other named enemies, probably more based on mobility and/or ranged attacks, to both make the fight more memorable and give people a reason to struggle with moving around in a BG, but that's more personal taste. Again, you know your group to best determine whether than means Elite Soldiers on horses, demons similar to flying Blood Apes, or DB mercenaries.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T00:51:06-08:00","id":1427824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427783#post1427783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, maybe my players build their characters to be much less combat-focused than a typical PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huzzah!<br /> <br /> Backstrapolating, the Young Dynast is Dex 3 Melee 3 with an Artifact weapon and armor, and she struggled against a Size 5 battlegroup. As a battlegroup can hit all the PCs at once, something like a Size 5 battlegroup of Battle Ready Soldiers led by a Champion (use their Threaten pool to command the battlegroup) and a Size 4 battlegroup of Horse Archers led by a Brigand Leader (stick them on a horse), might be sufficient to challenge ~3 PCs. <br /> <br /> If you post a summary of your PCs stats, I'm happy to come up with a bespoke challenge. It would also help to know the details of the enemy kingdom and why they are fighting in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, if the enemy army has 3,000 troops, that's three size 5 battlegroups, right? </div> </div> </div>Eh. Sure? I guess. But it's kinda hard to meaningfully engage half-a-dozen folks with three thousand. You could have a battlegroup charge them and two more ready to cut them off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was wondering about two questions:<br /> <br /> (1) in regions of the world where nations and armies are not typically led by Dragonblooded (which I think is supposed to be most of the world that's not a Realm satrapy, Lookshy, or Prasad, although I'm not really sure), can an enemy nation be a threat to the PC's nation that demands more thought than &quot;We'll just walk up to their army and fight it until it's routed&quot;? If so, what kind of numbers do they need? </div> </div> </div>Most states are ruled by mortals. But most states have access to something supernatural. Paragon is ruled by a mortal, but they have a Solar. Gem is ruled by a mortal, but they hire Solars. Nexus is ruled by mortals but guarded by a supernatural being who smacked down a 3CD and home to a Solar and his mercenary company. Harborhead is ruled by a mortal but blessed with a priesthood of warrior nuns directly empowered by the god of war. My own homebrew kingdom of Dovak is ruled by a mortal but protected by a warlike elemental.<br /> <br /> Then we add in Realm Satraps and Garison Commanders, Wyld Hunt and Immaculate Monks, Seventh Legion patrols, Outcasts mercenaries. There's no reason why a mortal kingdom can't get a little supernatural help.<br /> <br /> But none of that is <i>necessary</i>. It's just helpful.<br /> <br /> In a straight fight, you want to look for force multipliers. Good commanders. Abusing combined arms to exploit the action economy. Elite drill. An army the size of a Realm Legion is something like 5 Size 5 blocks of infantry, plus Auxiliary archers plus Cavalry. Plus over a thousand officers -- put just the ten Dragonlords in play as individual Elite Troops and the action economy really swings in your favor, but you could homebrew another Size 5 Battlegroup that can give commands to all the other battlegroups simultaneously on top of that to represent the junior officers. If the PCs just have one Size 3 unit of Tiger Warriors in their nation, that could be a pretty significant threat.<br /> <br /> But generally, you don't want a straight fight.<br /> <br /> Let the PCs destroy a Size 5 army of enemy mortal troops. Let them be bad-ass. Don't have the enemy's other two thousand troops just waiting to fight the PCs -- have them sack your PCs capital city and burn the fields whilst the PCs are busy fighting. Let them rout enemy armies, but they just run away and fight a guerrilla war -- welcome to the endless quagmire of military occupation. Let them slaughter enemy armies, but now there is a Shadowland. Let them conquer an enemy nation, but now the whole region fears them, has united against them, and is calling in The Realm to save them.<br /> <br /> Or give them a reason not to conquer enemy nations. Bonds of friendship and trade. Blessings of gods. Romeo and Juliet style live stories. A common enemy (The Realm, the Red Tide, The Bull of the North). What if the enemy has hostages?<br /> <br /> Or just say &quot;fudge it&quot; and give the mortals a Wandering Deathknight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (2) Wait, are any of these nations not led by Dragonblooded? Can an Outcaste DB just walk up to one of them and become the leader by asking nicely and then single-handedly fighting that nation's army if they decline? </div> </div> </div>There are more city-states in Creation than there are Exalted. And in that Young Dynast fight, the Exalt was left totally drained and nearly dead -- assassin time.<br /> <br /> There are lots of states run by mortals.<br /> <br /> Then you have mortals with neat tricks, like a Raksha best friend, or a First Age artifact, or Sorcery. Mortals who just hire Outcastes to protect them.<br /> <br /> But... yeah... walking into a kingdom of mortals and just conquering it is totally in scope for a Dragon-Blooded. The Signature Fire Aspected Dragon-Blooded (Left Hand Chalima) literally did exactly that (and now struggles to manage the treasury, complete her paperwork, balance the cultural and religious concerns of her people, and has to hunt down the Anathema). It's a very appropriate Exalted thing to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems like a nation that can field an army of multiple thousands is a threat to starting characters that is worthy of doing something interesting like finding allies, sowing dissension in the enemy ranks, or stealthily attacking supply lines to deal with, but no less, unless the Storyteller uses them in an indirect way. </div> </div> </div>I think the big question is &quot;what next&quot;.<br /> <br /> If an enemy nation has three thousand soldiers, they have them for a reason. No-one keeps the expense of a massive army if they don't need it.<br /> <br /> Your five starting Exalts might be able to kill them all on the field... But how do they now defend their conquered nation's boarders? And if they don't defend it, what are the consequences?<br /> <br /> Whereas, if they build up allies and raid supply lines and make the enemy soldiers switch sides, they might find themselves in a far better position to actually <i>rule</i> once the dust has settled.<br /> <br /> Then we've got stuff like PTSD. Shadowlands. Folks swearing revenge. Assassins. The Wyld Hunt. Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Just because the PCs <i>can</i> take an army head-on, doesn't mean they <i>should</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-09-2020, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T12:45:21-08:00","id":1427895,"title":"","content":"Orrrrrrrr...<br /> <br /> If your PCs seem like they'd enjoy soloing an army, maybe just focus on making that a cool and fun thing to do for their first outing. Then, afterwards, have NPCs they like point out how reckless that was, and all the things which could have gone wrong. And if they do it again, without taking appropriate precautions, hit them with all the cruel unintended consequences you can think of.<br /> <br /> In my experience, players respond better to that than to getting hit with the &quot;how dare you fight people&quot; hammer their first time out in an RPG with literal hundreds of combat powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T14:27:42-08:00","id":1427905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427895#post1427895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orrrrrrrr...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's cool too. But the ST specifically said they thought an entire nation should challenge the PCs and they detailed the kind of story they intended to tell.<br /> <br /> In my experience, PCs want to earn their successes. Being told &quot;that was easy mode&quot; after the fact tends to make them feel cheated.<br /> <br /> Buuuut... this is still good advice. &quot;The Exalted take down an entire army&quot; is well in scope and could be a great way to kick off a Story. Getting the chance to kickass and be awesome is what Exalted is all about. My point is only that there's not a &quot;right&quot; way to do this and anything else will piss your players off: it's that however you do it there are potential pitfalls and you need to make sure everyone is on the same page","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T08:53:23-08:00","id":1427982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427796#post1427796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to find that dex 5, combat ability 5, omni-applicable specialty, artifact weapons/armor and 3-5 combat charms is about standard for any PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see! My players haven't built their characters yet, I'm just speculating. I doubt they will get that high to start - at least we weren\u2019t in the previous game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right, but probably only one at a time. </div> </div> </div>I mean, maybe the enemies can try to sandwich the PCs between a group of infantry and a group of cavalry, and, if they meet the enemies on the open field, have a group of archers attack before they close in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...not mechanically no. If you don't have supernatural power, pretty big supernatural power, on your side against a nation who has PCs then you will fail spectacularly. The Dawn and the Zenith will play rock-paper-scissors for who gets to be the one to single handedly take them apart. </div> </div> </div>Well, the current planned PCs are a Changing Moon and a No Moon, so at least it won't be quite that bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Realm has something like 500 satrapies. So go get a map of Creation, then put 500 dots on it in places that aren't the Blessed isle, or generally the river province, and that's about the scope you're looking at. Most places of interest in Creation are in some way run by exalts. </div> </div> </div>This question is in part due to the fact that in our previous game we overthrew a satrapy, then had to fight off the Realm legion that came to reclaim it, with a break to disrupt a nearby satrapy in between. So I want satrapies, specifically, to be less of a focus in the next game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For one if they're going to mess with the PCs they need to make sure they're not seen doing it, otherwise the PCs can just walk over and knock down their castle and tell them to stop it. Even sowing seeds of dissension in the ranks is iffy. Remember Solars aren't just fighting powerhouses, if the Zenith or Eclipse gives a little speech to the troops all those thoughts of dissension just melt away. </div> </div> </div>By dissension I mean the PCs trying to sow dissension in the enemy's ranks. Like, I want to make the combat challenge sufficient to, at the very least, motivate the players to think creatively about how to use their noncombat powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427799#post1427799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there are enough Outcastes to go around, whether as leaders, allies, or mercenaries. Toss one of those in a battlegroup, give them solid defenses and Roaring Dragon General, and you'll be on your way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! This, and the other stuff, is helpful. After thinking about it, I decided that I like the idea of Outcaste mercenaries a lot. It seems like their personality and style could be distinct enough from satrap/garrison commander/Wyld hunt types, and plus who would want to conquer a petty kingdom and have to worry about running the damn thing when you can just be a mercenary and still get plenty rich?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427824#post1427824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huzzah!<br /> <br /> Backstrapolating, the Young Dynast is Dex 3 Melee 3 with an Artifact weapon and armor, and she struggled against a Size 5 battlegroup. As a battlegroup can hit all the PCs at once, something like a Size 5 battlegroup of Battle Ready Soldiers led by a Champion (use their Threaten pool to command the battlegroup) and a Size 4 battlegroup of Horse Archers led by a Brigand Leader (stick them on a horse), might be sufficient to challenge ~3 PCs.<br /> <br /> If you post a summary of your PCs stats, I'm happy to come up with a bespoke challenge. It would also help to know the details of the enemy kingdom and why they are fighting in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks so much!<br /> <br /> This is all speculation, currently, as we\u2019re still planning the campaign. Thus I can both suggest the players to keep their PCs on the low side and think up ways to up the challenge of potential foes\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most states are ruled by mortals. But most states have access to something supernatural. Paragon is ruled by a mortal, but they have a Solar. Gem is ruled by a mortal, but they hire Solars. Nexus is ruled by mortals but guarded by a supernatural being who smacked down a 3CD and home to a Solar and his mercenary company. Harborhead is ruled by a mortal but blessed with a priesthood of warrior nuns directly empowered by the god of war. My own homebrew kingdom of Dovak is ruled by a mortal but protected by a warlike elemental.<br /> <br /> Then we add in Realm Satraps and Garison Commanders, Wyld Hunt and Immaculate Monks, Seventh Legion patrols, Outcasts mercenaries. There's no reason why a mortal kingdom can't get a little supernatural help. </div> </div> </div>I want to largely avoid specifically the satraps, garrison commanders, Wyld Hunts, and Immaculate Monks because we fought a lot of those in the previous game. But thanks for pointing out all the other supernatural possibilities. I guess for a lot of them it\u2019s not very clear exactly how powerful the supernatural aid actually is, but I predict the answer will turn out to be \u201cexactly as powerful as it needs to be to create an interesting plot\u201d\u2026<br /> <br /> The other stuff you said is helpful too, but let me not make this post too enormous by responding to all of it\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T09:18:19-08:00","id":1427991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427655#post1427655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ganan vs Mata-Yadh</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow it\u2019s never occurred to me just how much clashes are the solution to enemies with more damage and soak than you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T10:04:50-08:00","id":1427999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427991#post1427991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Somehow it\u2019s never occurred to me just how much clashes are the solution to enemies with more damage and soak than you.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re also just good in general and especially in 1v1 circumstances. They let you both defend and attack using the same excellency, and also boost your dice pool considerably usually. Normally weapons add 0-1 defense, but 1-5 offensive dice, and also there\u2019s a lot more dice tricks for boosting accuracy for everyone. <br /> <br /> Also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25834\" data-vbnamecard=\"25834\">habitableexoplanet</a> there are certainly some non-dragonblooded supernatural threats out there. There\u2019s Lunars, Abyssals, other Solars. Also for non-exalts a size 5 battlegroup of Silverwights or Hobgoblins led by a fair folk Cataphract or two or three should be okay and not unrealistic to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T10:50:09-08:00","id":1428009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427991#post1427991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Somehow it\u2019s never occurred to me just how much clashes are the solution to enemies with more damage and soak than you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Clashes are broken good.<br /> <br /> But, to be fair, Ragara Smash (a starting character DB) has a higher Soak than Mata-Yadh: 25 is not that much, Cynis Ganan is 20, the Knight of Bone and Ivory is 33 (at character creation, rising to 37). And after Force of the Mountain, Ganan's damage is higher than Mata-Yadh's. Give him time to pull his tetsubo out of a rock and aim twice (i.e. start the fight at Long Range instead of Close) and Ganan is sitting on a static 24 damage compared to Mata-Yadh's 22. (And then you add Force of the Mountain to hit 29.)<br /> <br /> Like, literally put Ganan in a suit of armor and roll join battle once Mata-Yadh comes into view on the horizon and his damage and soak are higher than the behemoth's.<br /> <br /> A Wood Aspect with a Medium Weapon could be sitting on a static Parry of 9 (Dragon-Scale Shielding upto 11), which with Mata-Yadh's Accuracy of 16 would be a pretty solid option. I think you could win this with a Deeb <i>without</i> abusing Clashes -- it's just that I had Ganan's character sheet sitting right there. An archer build should do well, actually: a Deeb in Emerald Chevailier would turn Mata-Yadh into paste.<br /> <br /> Mata-Yadh is a very worthy steed. A marvellous centerpiece to a Fae army. But remember, it's only a <i>baby</i> behemoth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427999#post1427999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They let you both defend and attack using the same excellency</div> </div> </div> </div>Clashes are great for a bunch of reasons, but for arena fights this is the main reason.<br /> <br /> QC monsters run their abilities on Initiative (<i>why?</i>).<br /> PC Exalts run their abilities on motes.<br /> <br /> Running out of motes kills PCs.<br /> <br /> Attacking and defending on the same Excellency is absolute huge.<br /> <br /> (Bonus non-Charm Clash dice, bonus Clash damage, using Accuracy as defense, Clash enhancing Charms, ignoring penalties and boosts to defense, etc. are all good as well. I agree with everything DrLoveMonkey posted. But attacking and defending with the same Excellency is what makes Clashes so good.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-10-2020, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T11:08:49-08:00","id":1428011,"title":"","content":"A lot of fueling abilities off of initiative is very not good. Especially defensive ones. If they were mostly offensive, like \u201cinstead of dealing 5 damage with that 5i, create a 5L environmental hazard against all enemies in range.\u201d That\u2019s okay, but on the defence, especially the DECISIVE defence, it\u2019s just something they\u2019ll basically never use. Even a withering defence it would have to spare them from more damage than the initiative is likely to do.<br /> <br /> Also soak and damage in general is a bit too easy to stack anyway. A lot of enemies in the game are statted out to seem like 12-14 damage is solid, but a lot of PCs have at least 10 soak, and many PCs have 15+, which without the benefit of minimum damage means that you barely care on the few times you do get hit. Again though this is dependant on players, you might have someone who decides to just take medium mundane armour or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T12:18:32-08:00","id":1428017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428011#post1428011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of fueling abilities off of initiative is very not good. Especially defensive ones. If they were mostly offensive, like \u201cinstead of dealing 5 damage with that 5i, create a 5L environmental hazard against all enemies in range.\u201d That\u2019s okay, but on the defence, especially the DECISIVE defence, it\u2019s just something they\u2019ll basically never use. Even a withering defence it would have to spare them from more damage than the initiative is likely to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is spending Initiative on Defense bad? Is Heavenly Guardian Technique bad? I can see why it is in a 1 v 1 fight, but in a team vs. team fight that most QCs were probably designed for, you could be Decisively attacked while at high Initiative for a number of reason. <br /> <br /> Some of the effects are really good. Adding half the attacker's die pool to your Soak or Hardness (Unbreakable Gemstone Armor) can be very good - in our game, it let a Vaktri meaningly contribute to a battle between a Warstriders and two Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also soak and damage in general is a bit too easy to stack anyway. A lot of enemies in the game are statted out to seem like 12-14 damage is solid, but a lot of PCs have at least 10 soak, and many PCs have 15+, which without the benefit of minimum damage means that you barely care on the few times you do get hit. Again though this is dependant on players, you might have someone who decides to just take medium mundane armour or something. </div> </div> </div>I guess the secret is to get players who think running around in light or no armor being all swashbuckling is &quot;cool&quot; (and turning your skin intro bronze is &quot;weird&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T12:42:39-08:00","id":1428018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428017#post1428017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is spending Initiative on Defense bad? Is Heavenly Guardian Technique bad? I can see why it is in a 1 v 1 fight, but in a team vs. team fight that most QCs were probably designed for, you could be Decisively attacked while at high Initiative for a number of reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>HGD is pretty good, partially just because it\u2019s way better than almost any QC charm that costs initiative, but mostly it\u2019s better because QCs just don\u2019t crash PCs, but the reverse is not true. Generally what I try to do is throw maybe 1.5 times the number of enemies as PCs into a fight, the PCs will all go first, each PC will crash one enemy with one attack each, then the remaining enemies can go and hopefully launch decisive attacks against targets without enough hardness to stop it, then the crashed enemies wither, then the PCs go again and decisive destroy over half the enemies and end the fight. Hopefully if the enemies were strong enough they spent motes doing that though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428017#post1428017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I guess the secret is to get players who think running around in light or no armor being all swashbuckling is &amp;quot;cool&amp;quot; (and turning your skin intro bronze is &amp;quot;weird&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would indeed be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T12:48:06-08:00","id":1428019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428017#post1428017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the secret is to get players who think running around in light or no armor being all swashbuckling is &quot;cool&quot; (and turning your skin intro bronze is &quot;weird&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly, the secret is not to get a mix of players who think that and players who don't. The QC stats seem to think that 2-10 soak is normal, and semi-optimized PCs will make a world where 10-20 soak is normal and you can set up enemies accordingly. But there's not so much relief when the range of PC soak is 2-20.<br /> <br /> A lot of the anime, JRPG, and even mythic roots of Exalted encourage you to think that cool people don't wear real armor. It's kind of crazy what a paradigm shift the stuff can be in game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T13:43:28-08:00","id":1428023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428019#post1428019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly, the secret is not to get a mix of players who think that and players who don't. The QC stats seem to think that 2-10 soak is normal, and semi-optimized PCs will make a world where 10-20 soak is normal and you can set up enemies accordingly. But there's not so much relief when the range of PC soak is 2-20.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can also work, but straaange things can start to happen then. Like if a bloodape\u2019s 15 damae is supposed to be 5 more than a high soak character, I can bump it up to 25. Likewise boosting soak and stuff across the board to deal with crazy damage boosts. It sucks to have to do that for 200+ antagonists when the PCs could just do it for their five characters, but whatever.<br /> <br /> The weirdness comes in when occasionally something happens like the PC loses their weapon. Now, normal, that\u2019s okay, if they\u2019ve got a few dots in brawl they can still fight and stuff. It\u2019s just that now their bare fist plinks off an unarmoured monk like he\u2019s made of stone, because his bare chest is 13 soak and he doesn\u2019t have his mega twink damage for unarmed attacks, and mega twink damage is the new standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T15:38:56-08:00","id":1428035,"title":"","content":"Just let the optimized PCs destroy everything without challenge. That's the point of optimizing. *Free Shrugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T15:40:40-08:00","id":1428036,"title":"","content":"That's Exalted all over, though. Like, in every edition.<br /> <br /> The downside of the &quot;CCG RPG&quot; paradigm is that all of these little mechanical widgets reward you for heavily specializing... but either that's total overkill, or anything calibrated for specialized builds just destroys anyone who's not in their element. Which is tough enough when it's like &quot;the social character gets pwned,&quot; but much nastier when someone gets disarmed or something and then abruptly cannot do the thing they built around.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there's much to be done without giving up on &quot;loads of exception-based powers&quot; as a concept, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T22:19:36-08:00","id":1428052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428017#post1428017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I guess the secret is to get players who think running around in light or no armor being all swashbuckling is &quot;cool&quot; (and turning your skin intro bronze is &quot;weird&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>My Sunday group\u2019s circle goes mostly Light armor and no ISoB, but our Lunar <i>does</i> use a big ankylosaurus shell for high soak in her warform.<br /> <br /> But, y\u2019know, <i>Lunar</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T23:26:49-08:00","id":1428059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428035#post1428035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just let the optimized PCs destroy everything without challenge. That's the point of optimizing. *Free Shrugs*</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree if it took a lot to get there and you couldn't do much else. Like if you decided &quot;my character is the fucking invincible-ist motherfucker who ever existed&quot; and then you bent every single dot and charm on your page to that end, and you wound up with somebody who, even with 0xp spent, was pretty well immune to things trying to fight them, that's one thing. What it ends up being though is you just toss a couple of bonus points here, or a few merit dots there, and you become nearly immune to way too many otherwise epic things.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking like, barnyard animals. I'm talking the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-QaVGMYdV-w&amp;feature=youtu.be&amp;t=153\" target=\"_blank\">sandworms</a> from dune except they're undead monsters who are clever enough to try and lure you into them with a ghostly figure, or an underworld spirit made of nothing but damned souls, blood, and barbed wire.<br /> <br /> It's not every antagonist, but it's just way way too many of the coolest ones for my taste.<br /> <br /> It's hard not to do too, like it's hard not to just shuffle those points there, because it feels like you're playing the game wrong. It's like if playing a wizard in DnD became unreasonable past 15 int, and there's several easy ways to start with 16.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428036#post1428036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Exalted all over, though. Like, in every edition.<br /> <br /> The downside of the &quot;CCG RPG&quot; paradigm is that all of these little mechanical widgets reward you for heavily specializing... but either that's total overkill, or anything calibrated for specialized builds just destroys anyone who's not in their element. Which is tough enough when it's like &quot;the social character gets pwned,&quot; but much nastier when someone gets disarmed or something and then abruptly cannot do the thing they built around.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there's much to be done without giving up on &quot;loads of exception-based powers&quot; as a concept, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kind of okay with that part actually. Like if a fight breaks out against a battlegroup that everyone is really worried about because one attack is going to crash them, that's what the Dawn is for. He can't sit back and play conservatively to avoid spending any motes, he's got to destroy that size 4 battlegroup, right down to route, right now before they get to act. That's what the Dawn is <i>for</i>. Part of that only works though if in the next scene the Dawn is likewise screwed, like they have a demonic parasite in their neck that will absolutely kill them, or a soulbreaker orb is about to go off in their face unless it gets disarmed, or some incredible social force is going to convince them to do something very bad. That's when the Twilight or the Night or the Zenith steps in and shows off their stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T01:56:14-08:00","id":1428067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428036#post1428036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Exalted all over, though. Like, in every edition.<br /> <br /> The downside of the &amp;quot;CCG RPG&amp;quot; paradigm is that all of these little mechanical widgets reward you for heavily specializing... but either that's total overkill, or anything calibrated for specialized builds just destroys anyone who's not in their element. Which is tough enough when it's like &amp;quot;the social character gets pwned,&amp;quot; but much nastier when someone gets disarmed or something and then abruptly cannot do the thing they built around.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there's much to be done without giving up on &amp;quot;loads of exception-based powers&amp;quot; as a concept, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is... Exalted <i>doesn't</i> (really) reward you for specializing. Stuff like scaling XP costs and high ability minimums on Charms make it look like you should specialize... But you can reliably pick a lock in the dark without lockpicks with Dex 3 Larceny 0. You can reliably run for three days straight with Stamina 3 Atheltics 3 and the Excellency. You can beat 12 strong men in combat, single-handedly, with Dex 1 Melee 0. Ahlat, god of war, has the highest Resolve in the game. You can convince him to go to war for you With Charisma 2 and Presence 2. Not &quot;in theory&quot; but <i>reliably</i>. Sail 2, 2 dot attribute, Excellency and Stunt makes you a bigger threat on the sea than a 30&quot; armored Kraken.<br /> <br /> 1E lists, like, nine abilities that Dragon-Blooded should take two dots in.<br /> <br /> 2E was the hyper specialized edition. A character with Dex 3 Ride 3 literally could not pilot a Seige Strider -- you needed 5/5.<br /> <br /> 3E really, really, does not want you to specialize. And it works with generalists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T06:26:34-08:00","id":1428082,"title":"","content":"3e character generation seems to be written with the idea that it\u2019s more like: hmm well my character likes to travel, so a few dots in sail, survival, and ride, they\u2019re pretty good with their hands so two dots in brawl, toss a dot into larceny because hey sometimes on the road not everything is so easy to come by. Speaking of, crafting woodworking stuff to keep my equipment all in working order, that\u2019d make sense, and also a few dots in archery for hunting...<br /> <br /> But then it ends up being like: okay well I\u2019ve got 5s in combat abilities, I\u2019ll pick up 5 in awareness for join battle and general utility, definitely need integrity for social influence, resistance because poisons and environmental hazards exist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T19:37:38-08:00","id":1428143,"title":"","content":"Right, that's the thing right there.<br /> <br /> Ex3 doesn't seem to <i>want</i> you to specialize. But then it lays out abilities to reward you for doing just that, so we end up in a situation where you can average around 15 successes on a lockpicking roll, but no support for that actually mattering.<br /> <br /> And it really comes to a head with combat, partially because it's a lot more plausible that you'll run into someone with 25+ soak than it is that you'll have to see if your Awareness pool can keep up with Perfect Mirror, or what have you. But also, it's partially because there are just so <i>many</i> combat tricks you can buy, and it's really odd if the more you invest in combat, the less interesting it gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T20:29:04-08:00","id":1428144,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428059#post1428059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of that only works though if in the next scene the Dawn is likewise screwed, like they have a demonic parasite in their neck that will absolutely kill them, or a soulbreaker orb is about to go off in their face unless it gets disarmed, or some incredible social force is going to convince them to do something very bad. That's when the Twilight or the Night or the Zenith steps in and shows off their stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have social forces trying to convince the players to do bad stuff often in your games? In the game we played, it pretty much only came up as part of combat (vs. foes like Loreleis - one of my favorite enemies in the book, by the way) and I have a hard time imagining how it would come up in a game and how it would be fun to play.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428067#post1428067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahlat, god of war, has the highest Resolve in the game. You can convince him to go to war for you With Charisma 2 and Presence 2. Not &quot;in theory&quot; but <i>reliably</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain this? I'm not experienced with the social influence system. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sail 2, 2 dot attribute, Excellency and Stunt makes you a bigger threat on the sea than a 30&quot; armored Kraken. </div> </div> </div>Yes, although I think almost everyone agrees the Kraken's dice pool is set unusually low compared to the standards of the system and other dice pools (out-sailing a kraken is easier than sneaking past an ordinary bodyguard, spotting an ordinary human assassin, or evading an ordinary human horse archer (although one could argue that some of these dice pools are a little high by the official standards)).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3E really, really, does not want you to specialize. And it works with generalists. </div> </div> </div>Well, there are the cool-sounding Charms that require a 4 or 5 Ability rating, only at Essence 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428143#post1428143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, that's the thing right there.<br /> <br /> Ex3 doesn't seem to <i>want</i> you to specialize. But then it lays out abilities to reward you for doing just that, so we end up in a situation where you can average around 15 successes on a lockpicking roll, but no support for that actually mattering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like people have discussed this before, but would it help to lower all the Ability requirements for Charms by 1? Maybe except all Charms whose prerequisites normally require a 5. Would it unbalance anything? It would make the Solar Dodge and Socialize excellencies easier to acquire, I guess. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it really comes to a head with combat, partially because it's a lot more plausible that you'll run into someone with 25+ soak than it is that you'll have to see if your Awareness pool can keep up with Perfect Mirror, or what have you. But also, it's partially because there are just so <i>many</i> combat tricks you can buy, and it's really odd if the more you invest in combat, the less interesting it gets. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's fairly counterintuitive. I think it's fairly common in RPGs for combat to get less interesting at high levels, but I think Exalted 3E is more unusual in that combat with no special combat powers is quite interesting and adding powers makes it less exciting starting almost immediately from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T20:39:38-08:00","id":1428145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428144#post1428144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you explain this? I'm not experienced with the social influence system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I agree that you could get Ahlat to actually <i>go</i> to war for you. But what I suspect <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> was talking about was this: Ahlat has a Resolve of 5. But one of his Defining Intimacies involves war, and if someone's Defining Intimacy supports a social influence attempt you're making against them, that's a -3 penalty to their Resolve. So assuming that the ST agreed that Ahlat's Defining Intimacies of either &quot;War is the crucible of heroes.\u201d or \u201cI suffer neither cowards nor traitors.\u201d actually supported your argument that he should go to war on your behalf, and that he had no other Intimacies that ran counter to your request, he'd be at effectively Resolve 2. And you only need to equal Resolve to convince someone to do something, and the average result on 4 dice (Charisma 2 + Presence 2) is 2 successes, meaning you'd convince him half the time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T20:41:48-08:00","id":1428146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428144#post1428144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there are the cool-sounding Charms that require a 4 or 5 Ability rating, only at Essence 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> I feel like people have discussed this before, but would it help to lower all the Ability requirements for Charms by 1? Maybe except all Charms whose prerequisites normally require a 5. Would it unbalance anything? It would make the Solar Dodge and Socialize excellencies easier to acquire, I guess.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes it would. There were arguments around this. It would be better to have a few more charms at Ability 1/2/3 to allow for more shallow dipping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T22:23:37-08:00","id":1428153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428144#post1428144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have social forces trying to convince the players to do bad stuff often in your games? In the game we played, it pretty much only came up as part of combat (vs. foes like Loreleis - one of my favorite enemies in the book, by the way) and I have a hard time imagining how it would come up in a game and how it would be fun to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in my next campaign one of the first antagonists is going to attempt to convince the PCs that eating people is a great idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428144#post1428144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, there are the cool-sounding Charms that require a 4 or 5 Ability rating, only at Essence 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, but there\u2019s also often almost nothing in the book, debatably nothing, that warrants specializing as hard as those charms let you do. <br /> <br /> For example, awareness. A Solar with awareness charms against a stealth assassin doubles 9s, rerolls 6s, applies a -3 penalty to their roll, reroll (Essence) failures and then cascade roll for each further success, all opponents 1s count as your 10s, and all opponents 2s count as your 9s which is explicitly doubled by sensory acuity Prana, reroll the whole roll again if failed, and, of course, 20+ dice for an excellency.<br /> <br /> One of most stealthy antagonist is a fair folk Lorelei who has a stealth pool of 11 dice. So it kind of feels like what\u2019s the point? If you just take like, 2 of those charms you\u2019re pretty well safe from the stealthiest assassins in all of existence, at that point you might as well start branching out into other areas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428144#post1428144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, that's fairly counterintuitive. I think it's fairly common in RPGs for combat to get less interesting at high levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>So not for nothing, in my level 18 DnD game last week the fighter was terribly wounded for the last fight, so he hung back and opted to use some of his other tricks. Unfortunately the final enemy was a balor, who explode on death and would have possibly ended us all if he was allowed to get into a protected fight to take our hp down before the explosion. So the wizard cast enlarge on me, the fighter used one of seven one-use-only gemstones to tear open a crevasse to Hell, the warlock distracted him, and I picked him up and suplexed him into the Hell portal. It was fuckin\u2019 awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T04:07:51-08:00","id":1428169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428144#post1428144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain this? I'm not experienced with the social influence system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> Ahlat is Resolve 5. To convince him to do something you need to beat his Resolve and hit an Intimacy that justifies the action you are asking him to take.<br /> <br /> Charisma 2 give you two dice.<br /> Presence 2 gives you two dice.<br /> The Excellency gives you another 4 dice.<br /> Spending a point of Willpower gives you one success.<br /> Acting out what you say to Ahlat gives you at least two dice. But if you give a rousing speech, the pivotal moment in your chronical where your honest warrior moves the Southern God of War and Cattle with a heart-felt plea, you also get two automatic successes.<br /> <br /> So now you are rolling 10 dice and trying to get two successes. Even without the Excellency, it's 6 dice.<br /> <br /> Only you're not, because you are also hitting an Intimacy which lowers Ahalt's Resolve. But without knowing exactly what Intimacy you are hitting and what he's defending with, things get tricky. But realistically you're looking at needing between -1 (1) and 4 successes -- perfectly doable on 10 dice. Let's say you hit &quot;can't abide a traitor&quot; -- the Realm has betrayed Harbourhead and you're not hitting on his brides or adverse to war or attacking Harbourhead yourself -- even if Ahalt Stunts his Resolve and spends Willpower, you succeed if you roll 1 success on 10 dice (or 1 success on 6 dice if you don't have Excellent Presence). (It's 2 or 3 successes if he level 2 or level 3 stunts, respectively, which becomes a little tricky without the Excellency but is still doable.)<br /> <br /> Heck, with the Excellency, you can outright lie about the Realm attacking Harborhead and take the -5 penalty* (or you could show up at his temple naked and covered in blood) and you're still rolling 5 dice trying to get one success. With Charisma/Presence 3 you could outright lie <b>and</b> show up naked and be rolling 4 dice vs difficulty 1 (with Ahlat stunting and Willpower against you, remember).<br /> <br /> (Oh, and if you are inhumanly attractive (Appearance 6+ or Charms) then you might get bonus dice from appearance. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768056-is-appearance-kind-of-rubbish-or-am-i-missing-something?p=769441#post769441\">For more on doing nasty things to Ahlat with a high Appearance, see here</a>.)<br /> <br /> *Personally, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1178525#post1178525\">I agree with Vance</a> that NPCs are not mindless robots waiting for you to hit their Intimacy switches and that the -5 penalty is specific to Instill attempts and you can't just lie to hit an Intimacy on Pursuade. But that's a minority opinion, apparently, and it's a useful point of illustration as to why you don't have to specialize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, although I think almost everyone agrees the Kraken's dice pool is set unusually low </div> </div> </div>Is there a published antagonist with a better Sail pool? (Genuine question, I can't remember. But I can't think of one.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, there are the cool-sounding Charms that require a 4 or 5 Ability rating, only at Essence 1. </div> </div> </div>I did specifically address this. But if you want concrete advice:<br /> <br /> Take a 5 in your Supernal.<br /> Take a 3 in everything you are exceptionally good at.<br /> Take a 2 in everything you are good at.<br /> Take a 1 in anything you are vaguely interested in.<br /> <br /> If you don't meet the Charm minimums, don't buy the Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-12-2020, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T10:37:45-08:00","id":1428186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428169#post1428169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a 5 in your Supernal.<br /> Take a 3 in everything you are exceptionally good at.<br /> Take a 2 in everything you are good at.<br /> Take a 1 in anything you are vaguely interested in.<br /> <br /> If you don't meet the Charm minimums, don't buy the Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually believe this is the intention behind the high ability requirements. It's supposed to gate characters so that, supposedly, you need to actually be really invested in something in order to add the really powerful charms to it. You won't have three different characters in the party with Iron Whirlwind Attack because you won't have three people with maxed out melee, that's just silly.<br /> <br /> It's just that the assumption that people will take 5s in abilities that aren't absolutely core to their character concept is totally wrong. Just throw in a line in your backstory like &quot;my neighhbor was one of the greatest swordsman in the direction and he trained me while I took beaks from studying the occult&quot; and you're good to go for that 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T11:57:19-08:00","id":1428194,"title":"","content":"Likewise, I tend to limit characters to a single attribute at 1, and a single attribute at 5. Lunars can have two 5s, naturally.<br /> <br /> I don't really agree that Ex3's combat gets worse with Charms - I run the fights that I post here because I think it can be pretty cool and interesting. The issues are that (1) it's very slow, especially with an actual group, (2) it calls for a level of system mastery that I've seen people even want (much less have) in an RPG, and (3) making appropriate challenges is tricky and the books barely provide any.<br /> <br /> I have a deep fondness for 3E combat, I'd just never run a campaign using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T13:36:53-08:00","id":1428199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428194#post1428194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, I tend to limit characters to a single attribute at 1, and a single attribute at 5. Lunars can have two 5s, naturally.<br /> <br /> I don't really agree that Ex3's combat gets worse with Charms - I run the fights that I post here because I think it can be pretty cool and interesting. The issues are that (1) it's very slow, especially with an actual group, (2) it calls for a level of system mastery that I've seen people even want (much less have) in an RPG, and (3) making appropriate challenges is tricky and the books barely provide any.<br /> <br /> I have a deep fondness for 3E combat, I'd just never run a campaign using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>For clarity when I criticize 3E combat I don't mean it can't be an interesting strategic challenge. I mean mostly (1), with a dash of (3). It's slow enough that fights, in an actual game, often wear out their welcome, or, conversely, you see something fun coming up on your next turn or the turn after but have to wait a while to get to it. (We didn't have as big a problem with (3) in my game because the ST was willing to build and run enough Dragonblooded enemies to challenge our Solars, but this didn't help with (1).) <br /> <br /> There's also another aspect that differs between campaigns and arena fights - in campaigns you will care about your character a lot more and want to lose a lot less. The fact that a loss for high-level, powerful characters, if it happens, will probably happen slowly (First I'll run out of motes, then the enemies will start hitting me with a lot of Withering attacks, until they build up enough Initiative to hit me with Decisives, at which point I'll start taking Wound penalties, which will make it easier for them to hit me, ...) can create a kind of creeping feeling of doom, in my experience, which I didn't find particularly enjoyable, but which I don't think would be a problem in the arena.<br /> <br /> I actually think Exalted's noncombat systems require more system mastery, in some ways, than the combat system, and this sometimes motivates people to take combat Abilities and Charms - If I get +1 Melee to boost my attacks, I know that will help me every time I get in a fight, but if I get +1 Socialize to boost my Read Intentions, this will only help me if I use the information about Intimacies I glean strategically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T16:53:41-08:00","id":1428220,"title":"","content":"I can see that, but also, when social stuff breaks out, everyone makes jokes (IC or OOC, honestly) while the Social Expert (tm) handles it.<br /> <br /> Combat doesn't tend to be so opt-in, and therefore everyone needs to have some kind of idea what's going on there. Not unrelatedly, when everyone is doing things all the time, it's a lot more chaotic, and easy for people to miss small but vital details (&quot;oh, wait, that was a Decisive attack? Of course I would have gone with a full Excellency in that case...&quot;), which is a big deal in asystem where push-your-luck mechanics are arguably the single largest factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T17:02:58-08:00","id":1428221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428169#post1428169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a 5 in your Supernal.<br /> Take a 3 in everything you are exceptionally good at.<br /> Take a 2 in everything you are good at.<br /> Take a 1 in anything you are vaguely interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if that leaves you with eight ability dots and thirteen bonus points left to spend? Because in my experience the biggest reason for characters having half a dozen 5s is that the only way to not be able to afford half a dozen 5s is to make a character who can do everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T17:51:18-08:00","id":1428222,"title":"","content":"I'm going to make a Dawn Caste. Let's make them a knight in shining armor who does battle from the back of their horse.<br /> <br /> We'll have Strength 3, Dex 5, Stamina 3.<br /> We'll have Charisma 3, Manipulation 2, Appeance 2.<br /> We'll have Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 4.<br /> <br /> We'll make Awareness, Thrown, Dodge, Resistance, and Melee Caste, with Melee as Supernal. We'll make Athletics, Ride, Integrity, Survival, and War favored.<br /> <br /> We'll put 3 dots in each Awareness, Dodge, Resistance, Melee, Ride and War.<br /> We'll put 2 dots in Thrown, Athelitcs, and Integrity.<br /> 1 dot in Socialize, Presence, Linguisitics, and Survival.<br /> <br /> That's all 28 Ability dots spent.<br /> <br /> We'll put 2BP to bump Melee to 5. 4BP to raise Willpower to 7. 4BP to take Wits to 5. Let's buy an extra Charm for another 4BP and spend our last BP on... Survival 2.<br /> <br /> We can fight, we can do a little socailizing, and we're (barely) literate. We can't make arms or armor. We can't treat wounds. We can't run a business, but we're pretty good at surviving in the wild and dealing with animals.We're completely ignorant of the criminal scene, and we'd better hope we don't need any book-learning, because we haven't been to school. Oh, and I hope we don't need to fight spirits.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Let's make a Zenith preacher.<br /> <br /> We'll have Strength 2, Dex 3, Stamina 2.<br /> We'll have Charisma 5, Manipulation 3, Appeance 3.<br /> We'll have Perception 3, Intelligence 3, Wits 3.<br /> <br /> We'll make Presence Supernal and take Athletics, Integrity, Performance, and Resistance as Caste. We'll have Bureaucracy, Linguisitics, Larceny, Occult and Socialize as favored.<br /> <br /> We put three dots in Presence, Integrity, Performance, Linguistics, Larceny and Socialize.<br /> We put two dots in Resistance, Bureaucracy, and Occult.<br /> We throw one dot in Athletics, Awareness, Brawl, and Dodge.<br /> <br /> That's all 28 Ability dots spent.<br /> <br /> We spend 2BP on our Supernal, 8BP to take Appearance to 5, 2BP on an extra point of Willpower, and 3BP to take Stamina 3 for the Ox-Body benes.<br /> <br /> We're really good at social stuff. We can kinda fight (mortals and blood apes beware, other Exalted... not so much). We can't ride a horse, or rough it in the wild, or sail on the ocean. We can commit crimes but not investigate them. We can read, but we don't know much about history.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Let's make a mortal Dynast who Exalted as a Twilight.<br /> <br /> We'll have Strength 2, Dex 2, Stamina 3.<br /> We'll have Charisma 1, Manipulation 5, Appeance 3.<br /> We'll have Perception 3, Intelligence 5, Wits 3.<br /> <br /> Supernal Craft, with Integrity, Linguistics, Lore, and Occult as Caste. Awarenesss, Melee, Presence, Socialize, and Resistance favored.<br /> <br /> As a Dynast, we really should have two dots in Archery, Brawl, Melee, Performance, Presence, Ride, Lore, Socialize, and War. That's 18 Ability dots spent on the basic &quot;stuff a Dynast should know&quot;.<br /> We'll put 3 dots in Craft Armor, 3 in Craft Artifact, 3 in Craft Mechanical Devices, and 1 in Craft Cooking.<br /> <br /> We'll take Craft Armor and Craft Artifact to 5 for 4BP. Add a dot to Lore to take it to 3 dots each for 1BP. Buy Occult 3 for 3BP. Take Craft Cooking to 3 dots for 2BP. Take one dot of Awareness and Resistance for 2BP. Buy a lot of Linguistics to be literate 1BP. And 2BP in Integrity.<br /> <br /> Your Twilight can't heal. Has no Athletics. Can't run a business. Can't Investigate crimes. Can't Sail. We've spent all our BP on Ability dots but only have two Abilities outside of our Supernal above 3. Good job we picked Brawl and not Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> I really don't think you're going to struggle to spend all your dots here. There's an example of Character Creation on page 129 of the Corebook that you might also find helpful.<br /> <br /> But if you find yourself unable to make a character except for a character who can do everything... make a character who can do everything. Put one dot in every ability, and an extra two dots in your Supernal, then spend 2BP on your Supernal and have 1 dot in everything else. Sounds kinda fun. Fifteen Charms, ten caste/favored abilities... you could start with an Excellency in everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-20-2021, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T19:20:14-08:00","id":1428227,"title":"","content":"And with<i>out</i> deliberately going out of your way to spend all your BP on anything except what the book itself recommends spending them on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T19:38:33-08:00","id":1428229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428186#post1428186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just that the assumption that people will take 5s in abilities that aren't absolutely core to their character concept is totally wrong. Just throw in a line in your backstory like &quot;my neighhbor was one of the greatest swordsman in the direction and he trained me while I took beaks from studying the occult&quot; and you're good to go for that 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>This can get hilarious. <br /> <br /> &quot;My neighbour was one of the greatest swordsman in the direction and whenever I went over on weekends for chess he trained me.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;The lady fishmonger was one of the best sailors in the high seas, capable of fishing even in the worst of the storms and treacherous waters, which is how I got Survival 4 and Sail 5&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;The old man teaching in the nearby school is a retired government official/ priest who due to political shenanigans had to be exiled. He taught me Occult 5 and Lore 5.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The young woman singing by the roadside is a legendary travelling singer who loved our village so much she decided to stay.&quot; <br /> <br /> You can have an entire village of old retired masters who are pretty much all badasses by any name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T23:40:43-08:00","id":1428239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428227#post1428227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And with<i>out</i> deliberately going out of your way to spend all your BP on anything except what the book itself recommends spending them on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the book suggests favoured abilities, tertiary attributes, and merits, and in the example character generation they spend 2 BP on getting stealth and melee 4 each. You should pretty easily be able to go down the ability list and find places for those dots. <br /> <br /> Like if you're a Dawn who Exalted as a soldier when his squad got attacked by a raging beast and he was the lone survivor. You take melee 5 because you're a genius swordsman, but what about war, thrown, archery and brawl? You're a professional solider and nobody ever decided that you should know even the basics of how to shoot a bow, or hurl a sling? You never picked up anything from the inevitable barracks or bar room brawls? No inkling of wider war tactics? No survival based tracking, or scrounging while out on patrol? You want to use a parry defence so you take zero dots in dodge, but you're a legendary warrior, shouldn't at least the basics of Evasion be something you know about? Battlefield triage was never something you'd picked up or forced to learn, never learned to ride a horse in the event that you should be put in a cavalry position, don't know the first thing about moving stealthily in spite of the fact that ambushes are a key part of military strategy. Never been a marine either, you don't know the first thing about boats, and if you have no presence you must have had a pretty weak countenance for a sergeant. Same on integrity, and socialize even for that matter as keeping a poker face is pretty important.<br /> <br /> Maybe you learned a thing or two from your less upright fellows and so toss a dot or so into larceny, maybe you have a hobby instrument and pick up a dot of performance. Which is all in addition to the things you were going to take anyway, like athletics, awareness, resistance, melee and the like.<br /> <br /> When you look at it like that it's not that hard to use up the dots and start needing bonus points to get your favoured abilities to 2-3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T02:19:18-08:00","id":1428243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428227#post1428227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And with<i>out</i> deliberately going out of your way to spend all your BP on anything except what the book itself recommends spending them on?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Twilight spent all their BP on Caste and Favoured abilities. In fact, all these builds spend BP on Caste Abilities. And the Zenith buys Terrtiary Attributes. None of them buy Merits, true, but only because I couldn't be bothered to make a full character -- buying Merits as the book recommends wouldn't give them 5s in their Abilities though. I can't help but feel you are very much mistaken in your statement here.<br /> <br /> The actual example of Character Creation given in the book spends 8BP on Charms -- something none of these builds does.<br /> <br /> Willpower isn't quite as cost effective as buying the 4th and 5th dot of a favoured Ability in terms of BP efficiency, but it's a 1:4 exchange which is a lot better than a Charms 1:2. Or a Merits 1:3 -- and the book recommends buying Merits with your BP.<br /> <br /> Bumping Wits from 4 to 5 costs 16XP: buying that for 4BP likewise isn't dumb.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> Nix the Willpower, Charm and Wits on the Dawn. Take Craft Weapons 2 and Craft Armor 2 so you can maintain your equipment. Take Medicine 2 so you can do field surgery. Take Occult 2 so you can fight spirits and recite the superstitions of soldiers. Bump Integrity to 3 and Presence to 2. Finally we take 2 dots of Brawl. That's every single BP spent on Caste and Favoured Abilities. If you don't like Craft, take Lore so you can recite old war stories for Introduce a Fact, and Stealth (&quot;take the bullets out your gun&quot;)<br /> <br /> We still can't run a business or do anything on the criminal scene. We can move Ahlat with an impassioned speech, warrior to warrior, but we're not exactly built for courtly intrigue.<br /> <br /> But if my answers are still not to your satisfaction, give me a character concept and I'll build it and run it through some Arena challenges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428229#post1428229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This can get hilarious. <br /> <br /> You can have an entire village of old retired masters who are pretty much all badasses by any name.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair... that does give you a reason to visit the PC's childhood homes. And it's a great justification as to why they don't have a tragic backstory. I'm not against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-13-2020, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T07:12:35-08:00","id":1428265,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428222#post1428222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you find yourself unable to make a character except for a character who can do everything... make a character who can do everything. Put one dot in every ability, and an extra two dots in your Supernal, then spend 2BP on your Supernal and have 1 dot in everything else. Sounds kinda fun. Fifteen Charms, ten caste/favored abilities... you could start with an Excellency in everything.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Let's do this! The first think to be careful about is that some abilities don't have an Ability 1 Charm. Unless I made a mistake, there are 8 of these -</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Archery, Awareness, Dodge, Performance, Presence, Sail, Socialize, Stealth</span></span>. (I'm not sure if we're counting Martial Arts. Let's not count it, because getting Martial Arts 1 achieves very little when we already have at least a 1 in every combat ability, and get two different Crafts at 1.)<br /> <br /> We have to have at least three of these as a Caste ability. Zenith gets two and Twilight doesn't get any, so we can't play those, but we can play a Dawn (3 Caste), a Night (4 Caste), or an Eclipse (3 Caste). One thing that's tricky is our Caste XP trigger - being equally good at almost everything, we may find ourselves playing against our Caste type a lot, so we probably want to choose our Essence 5 Ability to be as broadly applicable to the Caste's themes as possible, to push us in that direction - maybe Melee for a Dawn, Stealth for a Night, and Presence for an Eclipse.<br /> <br /> The funny thing about the Melee version is we could be a Dex 5 Melee 5 god of combat who can also do everything else. That doesn't quite seem to be the point of this exercise, so I'll build the Night instead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">We need to take 1 of Athletics, Investigation, Larceny, Ride as a Caste ability. The starting Charms in all these Abilities are really cool, although Master Horseman\u2019s Technique is not great if you don\u2019t actually want to ride a horse (but then why take it as a Caste ability?). I\u2019ll take Athletics, because Graceful Crane Stance doesn\u2019t seem as exciting without the further Abilities that build on it, and getting (eventually) high Athletics and Stealth seems like a good combo for sneaking around. For my last Favored ability, I\u2019ll take Lore, because I don\u2019t like Essence-Lending Method, and I would like to eventually get Harmonious Academic Methodology instead.<br /> <br /> Supernal: Stealth<br /> Caste: Athletics, Awareness, Dodge, Socialize,<br /> Favored: Archery, Lore, Performance, Presence, Sail,<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> Brawl: Fists of Iron Technique<br /> Bureaucracy: Frugal Merchant Method<br /> Craft: Flawless Handiwork Method<br /> Integrity: Enduring Mental Toughness<br /> Investigation: Watchman's Infallible Eye<br /> Larceny: Seasoned Criminal Method<br /> Linguistics: Whirling Brush Method<br /> Medicine: Ailment-Rectifying Method<br /> Melee: Dipping Swallow Defense<br /> Occult: Spirit-Detecting Glance<br /> Resistance: Ox-Body Technique<br /> Ride: Master Horseman\u2019s Techniques<br /> Survival: Food-Gathering Exercise<br /> Thrown: Precision of the Striking Raptor<br /> War: War God Descendent<br /> <br /> Abilities: Everything 1, not counting Martial Arts, but counting Craft (Military Engineering) and Craft (Cooking), and Stealth 5. 2 BP spent.<br /> <br /> Attributes (6 BP spent):<br /> Strength 3<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 3<br /> <br /> Appearance 1<br /> Charisma 5<br /> Manipulation 3<br /> <br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Perception 3<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> Merits: I actually have no clue what to put here to fit with everything else - maybe I'll think about it later.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A lot of the Essence 1 Ability 1 Charms are really powerful, and could definitely come in handy even if you don't have much of the Ability (I guess that's sort of the idea...). I think this character would be pretty fun to play, except in a Circle with four other characters that are each much better in 6 of the Abilities, or something like that.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T07:46:16-08:00","id":1428271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428243#post1428243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair... that does give you a reason to visit the PC's childhood homes. And it's a great justification as to why they don't have a tragic backstory. I'm not against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also might have given a bit much credit to players on that front. A lot of the time the explanation is just \u201cI practiced really hard\u201d. Which, like, yeah I don\u2019t want to say it\u2019s impossible for that to happen, but with 5 abilities at 5 I really want to say it\u2019s impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T12:27:07-08:00","id":1428293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428036#post1428036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Exalted all over, though. Like, in every edition.<br /> <br /> The downside of the &quot;CCG RPG&quot; paradigm is that all of these little mechanical widgets reward you for heavily specializing... but either that's total overkill, or anything calibrated for specialized builds just destroys anyone who's not in their element. Which is tough enough when it's like &quot;the social character gets pwned,&quot; but much nastier when someone gets disarmed or something and then abruptly cannot do the thing they built around.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there's much to be done without giving up on &quot;loads of exception-based powers&quot; as a concept, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been doing a lot of thinking about this lately, and came to the conclusion that I think you can have either loads of exception-based powers <i>or</i> granular base stats <i>or</i> a balanced system, but not all three. If you have exception-based powers and you want them to be balanced, those powers need to have some foundational math that they're working on, which means characters need to all be working from the same statline. For an example of a system that does this in a kludgite way, there's D&amp;D 4E, which bases all its system math on the assumption that if your class is based on Strength then you're going to max out Strength at chargen and raise it more at every opportunity. The consequence of this, combined with 4E being a relatively well-balanced tabletop, is that if you don't max out your key stat then you're objectively building your character wrong and everything becomes much harder than the devs intended. At that point, though, there's no real reason to have base stats at all other than tradition. They're not <i>adding</i> anything besides punishment.<br /> <br /> The same goes for Exalted, except in this case the punishment is that the game becomes too easy instead of becoming too hard. If you strip out the fiddly numbers and set the base dicepools to a static value, then you have more room for the little mechanical widgets to have a meaningful impact because they're no longer overkill on their own. You can still have a character who specializes in taking combat Charms to the point where they're unstoppable, but then it's the product of a long-term decision to make that specialization, not just because they picked higher base numbers than the published opposition can really handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T21:06:44-08:00","id":1428315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428243#post1428243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair... that does give you a reason to visit the PC's childhood homes. And it's a great justification as to why they don't have a tragic backstory. I'm not against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually thinking of Kung Fu Hustle. <br /> <br /> Remember that village full of powerful kung fu masters who all work day jobs? Yep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T19:03:14-08:00","id":1428541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428293#post1428293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been doing a lot of thinking about this lately, and came to the conclusion that I think you can have either loads of exception-based powers <i>or</i> granular base stats <i>or</i> a balanced system, but not all three. If you have exception-based powers and you want them to be balanced, those powers need to have some foundational math that they're working on, which means characters need to all be working from the same statline. For an example of a system that does this in a kludgite way, there's D&amp;D 4E, which bases all its system math on the assumption that if your class is based on Strength then you're going to max out Strength at chargen and raise it more at every opportunity. The consequence of this, combined with 4E being a relatively well-balanced tabletop, is that if you don't max out your key stat then you're objectively building your character wrong and everything becomes much harder than the devs intended. At that point, though, there's no real reason to have base stats at all other than tradition. They're not <i>adding</i> anything besides punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if this is exactly right - at least, depending on how high your standards are for a balanced system. You could imagine that characters of a certain type could have a &quot;main combat stat&quot;, like Intelligence for Wizards in D&amp;D or Dex/Melee for a typical Exalted character, and a number of options for special powers that would be based on various noncombat stats - like certain combat Charms in Exalted will reward you for Manipulation or some other stat. If you balance things so that characters can't max all their stats, you would have a few different options that could theoretically be balanced against each other - e.g. you could max Dexterity and Manipulation and take all the Charms / special powers that reward you for having high Manipulation, or you could max another noncombat stat, or you could take a few stats to medium levels and choose the best Charms for each type. (I'm imagining this as being like in TCGs where you can play decks of a single color to make your individual cards as reliable as possible, or multi-color decks, which will make your individual cards sometimes hard to cast, but have more options for cards, making it easier to play the most powerful cards or take advantage of synergies between cards).<br /> <br /> But it's certainly the case that these things make the game harder to balance!<br /> <br /> I would say that the biggest issue in Exalted is that the game is intentionally unbalanced in a lot of ways. Like, it's intentional that you can make a character that is just bad at combat and will lose a swordfight to a single human soldier or whatever, or a god of combat who can beat thousands of soldiers without breaking a sweat, because the game developers want to let the players tell stories about how the first character uses their other amazing abilities to get out of the situation where it looks like they might have to fight and about how the second character deals with the consequences of winning that battle. It's intentional that putting armor on makes you much more effective in battle.<br /> <br /> And I think the intentional unbalanced nature combines with the unintentional unbalanced nature, which to an extent is unavoidable, to lead to a lot of imbalance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same goes for Exalted, except in this case the punishment is that the game becomes too easy instead of becoming too hard. If you strip out the fiddly numbers and set the base dicepools to a static value, then you have more room for the little mechanical widgets to have a meaningful impact because they're no longer overkill on their own. You can still have a character who specializes in taking combat Charms to the point where they're unstoppable, but then it's the product of a long-term decision to make that specialization, not just because they picked higher base numbers than the published opposition can really handle. </div> </div> </div>Yes, although &quot;too easy&quot; is not quite the right description of what happens. Like, you might be able to build your character to the point where they can defeat anyone in Creation (or just about anyone) in a duel, but it's still trivial to find something that can challenge you - like, just step off a boat on the Blessed Isle and declare yourself Empress (or declare your friend who took 15 Bureaucracy Charms and would be able to run an empire as Empress) and you will be quickly killed by 25 DBs and 3 Sidereals, or whatever it takes. Or you can head into the Wyld, fight a behemoth, and use it as bait to fight a bigger behemoth.<br /> <br /> The issue is playing these scenarios where a powerful character is challenged (1) makes combat drag on for too long, in the length of a given character's turn, the number of actions in a round, and the number of rounds in a battle, (2) requires enemies (powerful behemoths) of which very few are statted in the books, (3) doesn't involve hardly any of the enemies which are statted in the books. The &quot;fight DBs&quot; version will have a bigger problem with (1), while the &quot;fight behemoths&quot; version will have a bigger problem with (2). <br /> <br /> Unlike the &quot;starting characters can be combat gods or below-average human warriors&quot; thing, there is nothing intrinsic to the setting of Exalted that makes these true. But it's unsurprising that (1) is true as it's hard to design a system that is fun at wildly different power levels, and it's unsurprising that given this, they would focus on writing enemies where their system shines the most (although even given that, they probably aimed a little low with some of the HDNP enemies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T01:01:55-08:00","id":1428567,"title":"","content":"So in the Godlike series of RPGs, you have three types of dice. Normal (which are d10s), Hard and Wiggle. Hard and Wiggle dice represent your godlike powers and mean you'll basically always beat out mere mortals. But, when you fight other supers, Hard and Wiggle dice cancel out.<br /> <br /> So if you have Super Human Strength (6 dice, 3 Hard Dice, 1 Wiggle Die) and fight a Super Human God of Pankration (5 Dice, 2 Hard Dice, 3 Wiggle Die) you don't both roll the maximum (10) number dice. Instead Strength would roll 6 dice (trained human level) with 1 Hard Die and Pankration would roll 5 dice with 2 Wiggle Dice.<br /> <br /> Exalted could really use something like that to simplify high level fights so they don't drag for 33 rounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T15:12:04-08:00","id":1429075,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I understand that as a solution, really - if you run a high-essence fight with everyone taking -10 dice on actions and -5 to all static values, it would take just as many rounds, though it probably would make actually rolling things and counting successes a bit faster. I definitely agree that it would be nice to have some way of condensing those fights into 3-7 really impactful, strategic rounds.<br /> <br /> <br /> ... I say as I prepare to run yet another endurance match between an attrition-minded Lunar build and 3 DBs. But I never claimed to make good choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T15:50:00-08:00","id":1429084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429075#post1429075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I understand that as a solution, really - if you run a high-essence fight with everyone taking -10 dice on actions and -5 to all static values, it would take just as many rounds, though it probably would make actually rolling things and counting successes a bit faster. I definitely agree that it would be nice to have some way of condensing those fights into 3-7 really impactful, strategic rounds.<br /> <br /> <br /> ... I say as I prepare to run yet another endurance match between an attrition-minded Lunar build and 3 DBs. But I never claimed to make good choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in Godlike, the cancelling of dice actually is there to make fights last <i>longer </i>and be less predictable. (Mostly because 2 Hard Dice instantly ends a fight without a roll against a human opponent.) You can't port that across directly to Exalted (which doesn't have hard and wiggle dice to cancel in the first place).<br /> <br /> For Exalted, I've found High Soak slows down the game the most, followed by High Defense. So I'd suggest straight cancelling the two. So if you have Parry 7 and your opponent has Parry 5, you play as if you were Parry 2 and 0 respectively. Same for Soak (with extra Overwhelming adding like Threshold Successes perhaps). I've not playtested that, and it's midnight my time. But something along those lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-19-2020, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T17:23:55-08:00","id":1429088,"title":"","content":"I, uh, would not recommend that hack. A dedicated build can already get system-distorting amounts of Soak, and the biggest reason not to do so is that it isn't worth the resources since you've already reduced most opponents to their minimum damage by Soak 20. But if 35+ Soak is both a powerful offensive tool and your only way to be sure you'll end up with any kind of Soak at all... well, fights would probably get shorter, but only because they'd be slaughters where only one participant had any defenses. Especially if most attacks auto hit, which is going to be a thing when people unleash 10-25 attack dice against defenses which are 0-2 until they add Excellencies.<br /> <br /> But maybe my intuition is off. I'd be curious to know what happens if you do test that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T04:02:57-08:00","id":1429128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429088#post1429088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be curious to know what happens if you do test that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too! The goal here is to get slogs like the 33 round Ganan vs Mata-Yadh right down to 4-5 rounds. Let's see if it works!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ganan: Soak 0, Parry 0<br /> Mata-Yadh: Soak 13, Parry 0<br /> <br /> Join Battle<br /> <br /> Mata-Yadh rolls 10 dice for 8i<br /> Ganan spends 6m on Precision Awareness Method and 3m on Pasiap Preempts Haste to roll 15 dice with double-9s for 8i. (14/20m, 1a)<br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> <br /> 8i. Mata-Yadh Clashes with Prism-Pyre Immolation, Blinding Aurora, and Willpower (35m, 5WP, 6i). Ganan responds with a Full Excellency (14/14m, 2a), Force of the Mountain (14/11m), Stillness-of-Stone Atemi (14/9m, 3a), Withering Smash backed by Willpower (7i, 4WP). Mata-Yadh\u2019s soak falls by 3 as Ganan\u2019s Anima kicks in (Soak 10).<br /> <br /> Mata-Yadh rolls 17 dice for (9+1) 10 successes. Ganan rolls (Dex 5 + MA 5 + 1 Specialty + 2 Two-Handed Clash + 6 Excellency + 1 Accuracy + 1 Unstoppable Hammering Blow \u2013 3 Blinding Aurora) 18 dice for (11+1) 12 successes, hitting (8i).<br /> <br /> Ganan rolls (19 Base + 2 Threshold Successes + 1 Stillness-of-Stone Atemi + 3 Force of the Mountain (no aura) \u2013 10 Soak) 15 dice of Withering Damage (re-rolling 6s) for (7+3) 10i, Crashing Mata-Yadh. Ganan rises to (8+10+5) 23i. Mata-Yadh falls to -4i.<br /> <br /> Ganan enters Earth Aura.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 23i (14/14m, 4WP, 3a) Earth Aura<br /> Mata-Yadh: -4i (40m, 5WP) Clash, Prone<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> <br /> Anima: No damage.<br /> <br /> 23i. Ganan Decisive Smashes (22i) backed by Force of the Mountain and a 1m Excellency (14/10m). Mata-Yadh\u2019s Parry is (0 -2 Clash \u2013 1 Prone -1 Onslaught \u2013 too low for Mata-Yadh to boost, and Foe Snatching Grasp needs 4 Initiative). Ganan rolls 12 dice to hit, which he does, with 6 successes. Mata-Yadh is knocked to Short Range<br /> <br /> Ganan rolls 22i (Double 10s, rerolling 6s) for 11B. This is capped at 8B by Legendary Size (8B, -0). Ganan falls to 3i.<br /> <br /> -4i. Mata-Yadh uses its Move Action to Rise From Prone.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 3i (14/15m, 4WP, 3a) Earth Aura<br /> Mata-Yadh: -4i (45m, 5WP, 8B (-0)) Short Range<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> <br /> Anima: 1L<br /> <br /> 3i. Ganan Reflexive Moves to Close Range. He 1m Excellency, Withering Smashes, backed by Force of the Mountain (14/11m, 2i). Mata-Yadh spends Willpower for +1 Parry. Ganan rolls 14 dice vs Parry 1, for 4 successes (3i). Mata-Yadh is knocked Prone.<br /> <br /> Ganan rolls 18 dice (rr6s) for 12 successes, burying Mata-Yadh into -16i (Ganan rises to 15i).<br /> <br /> -16i. Mata-Yadh Flurries.<br /> <br /> First a Rise From Prone. Mata-Yadh rolls its Combat Movement Pool of 10 \u2013 3 for the Flurry (7 dice, 2 successes) and lumbers to its \u201cfeet\u201d.<br /> <br /> Mata-Yadh Withers with (16 Accuracy \u2013 3 Flurry) 13 dice. Ganan pays 6m to Full Excellency his Parry (14/5m) and he spends Willpower (3WP) for Parry 4. He also spends 4m 1i on Stone Dragon\u2019s Skin and 6m on Unmoving Mountain Stance (4/5m). Mata-Yadh rolls 10 successes, hitting easily (-15i). Ganan spends his last 9m to enter Earth Dragon Form (0/0m).<br /> <br /> Mata-Yadh rolls (22+6-8) 20 dice of damage for 11 successes, denied 3. Ganan falls to 4i and Mata-Yadh rises to -7i.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 4i (0/5m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: -7i (50m, 5WP, 8B1L (-0)) Short Range<br /> <br /> Mata-Yadh\u2019s Soak is reduced to 5.<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> <br /> Anima: No damage.<br /> <br /> 4i. Spends 1m on the Excellency and 3m on Force of the Mountain to Withing Smash (0/1m, 3i). He rolls 17 dice against Mata\u2019s Parry 0 for 9 successes (4i). Mata-Yadh is knocked Prone.<br /> <br /> Ganan rolls (19+5+9-5) 28 dice of damage (rr6s) for 16 successes (20i/-23i).<br /> <br /> Ganan Reflexively Moves out to Short.<br /> <br /> -23i. Mata-Yadh resets to 3i. It rises from prone.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 20i (0/6m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 3i (50m, 5WP, 8B (-0)) Short Range<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> <br /> 20i. Ganan moves back to Medium Range.<br /> <br /> 3i. Mata-Yadh moves to Short Range and attempts to Rush. It rolls 10 dice vs Ganan\u2019s 11. The result doesn\u2019t really matter.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 20i (0/11m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 3i (50m, 5WP, 8B (-0)) Short Range, Rush<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> <br /> 20i. Ganan Reflexive moves to Close Range and Decisive Smashes with a 1m Excellency and Force of the Mountain (0/7m, 19i). Mata-Yadh decides not to Crash itself by defending. Ganan hits, and Mata-Yadh is knocked prone.<br /> <br /> Ganan rolls 19 dice (doube-10s, rr6s) for 7B. Ganan resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> 3i. Mata-Yadh Flurries a Rise From Prone with an attack.<br /> <br /> It rolls 7 dice (for 6 successes) and rises.<br /> <br /> It rolls 13 dice to attack, for 8 successes (4i). It rolls 30 dice of damage (big oof) for 9i, Crashing Ganan. (13i/-6i).<br /> It spends 1WP on God Monster Revival, rolling 13 dice and healing 1L4B.<br /> <br /> Ganan: -6i (0/12m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 13i (50m, 5WP, 11B (-0))<br /> <br /> Round 7<br /> <br /> 13i. Mata-Yadh uses Prism-Pyre Immolation to roll 17 dice to Grapple. There\u2019s nothing Ganan can realistically do to resist that. It rolls 13i and locks in the grapple (10i). With Overwhelming Might, it rolls unopposed for 9 rounds of control.<br /> <br /> First it Restrains Ganan (8 rounds remaining).<br /> <br /> -6i. Ganan is restrained and may not act. He must contend with the Prism-Pyre. He spends 4m (0/8m) to gain 2 bonus successes and reroll 6s on his face tanking of the hazard, rolling 7 dice for a total of 4 successes and takes no damage.<br /> <br /> Ganan: -6i (0/13m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 10i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0)), 8 Rounds of Control<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 8<br /> <br /> 10i. Mata-Yadh Restrains.<br /> <br /> -6i. Ganan is restrained and may not act. He must contend with the Prism-Pyre. He spends 4m (0/8m) to gain 2 bonus successes and reroll 6s on his face tanking of the hazard, rolling 7 dice for a total of 6 successes and takes no damage.<br /> <br /> Ganan: -6i (0/14m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 10i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0)), 6 Rounds of Control<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 9<br /> <br /> 10i. Mata-Yadh Restrains.<br /> <br /> -6i. Ganan is restrained and may not act. He must contend with the Prism-Pyre. He spends 4m (0/8m) to gain 2 bonus successes and reroll 6s on his face tanking of the hazard, rolling 7 dice for a total of 4 successes and takes no damage.<br /> <br /> Ganan: -6i (0/15m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 10i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0)), 4 Rounds of Control<br /> <br /> Round 10<br /> <br /> 10i. Mata-Yadh Restrains.<br /> <br /> -6i. Ganan resets to 3i. Ganan is restrained and may not act. He must contend with the Prism-Pyre. He spends 4m (0/8m) to gain 2 bonus successes and reroll 6s on his face tanking of the hazard, rolling 7 dice for a total of 4 successes and takes no damage.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 3i (0/15m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 10i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0)), 2 Rounds of Control<br /> <br /> Round 11<br /> <br /> 13i. Mata-Yadh Restrains. No rounds of control remain.<br /> <br /> 3i. Ganan frees himself from the grapple but may take no action.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 3i (0/20m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 10i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0))<br /> <br /> Round 12<br /> <br /> 10i. Mata-Yadh Withers rolling 16 dice vs Parry 0 for 6 successes (11i). It rolls 28 dice of damage for 12i (20i/-9i) and Crashing Ganan (25i).<br /> <br /> -9i. Ganan makes a Full Excellency, Force of the Mountain, Stillness-of-Stone Atemi, Withering Attack (0/9m). He rolls 17 dice vs Parry 0 for 10 successes (-8i). He rolls 30 dice of damage (rr6s) for 16i (7i/9i).<br /> <br /> Ganan: 7i (0/14m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 9i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0))<br /> <br /> Round 13<br /> <br /> 9i. Mata-Yadh Withers, rolling 16 dice to hit Parry 0, hitting with 12 successes (10i). It rolls 34 dice of withering damage for 22i (32i/-15i).<br /> <br /> -15i. Ganan makes a Full Excellency, Force of the Mountain, Stillness-of-Stone Atemi, Withering Attack (0/4m). He rolls 17 dice vs Parry 0 for 8 successes (-14i). He rolls 28 dice of damage (rr6s) for 16i (2i/16i).<br /> <br /> Ganan: 2i (0/9m, 3WP, 3a) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: 16i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0))<br /> <br /> Round 14<br /> <br /> 16i. Mata-Yadh Decisives rolling 16 dice vs Parry 0, hitting. It rolls 16i in damage for 7L and resets to 3i.<br /> <br /> 2i. Ganan makes a Withering Smash (1i), backed by a 3m Excellency, and Force of the Mountain (0/3m). He rolls (19-1) dice to hit for 14 successes (2i) knocking Mata-Yadh prone. He rolls 38 dice of Withering damage (rr6s) for 22i (24i/-19i) and getting the Crash bonus (29i). He Reflexively Moves back a range band to Short.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 29i (0/8m, 3WP, 3a, 7L(-1)) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: -19i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0)), Prone, Short Range<br /> <br /> Round 15<br /> <br /> 29i. Ganan Reflexive moves back to Medium Range.<br /> <br /> -19i. Mata-Yadh rises from Prone.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 29i (0/13m, 3WP, 3a, 7L(-1)) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: -19i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0)), Medium Range<br /> <br /> Round 16<br /> <br /> 29i. Ganan Reflexively moves back to Long Range.<br /> <br /> -19i. M-Y moves to Medium range.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 29i (0/18m, 3WP, 3a, 7L(-1)) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: -19i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0)), Medium Range<br /> <br /> Round 17<br /> <br /> 29i. Ganan Reflexively moves back to Long Range.<br /> <br /> -19i. M-Y moves to Medium range.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 29i (0/23m, 3WP, 3a, 7L(-1)) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form<br /> Mata-Yadh: -19i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0)), Medium Range<br /> <br /> Round 18<br /> <br /> 29i. Ganan uses Chambered Fist Charge to bank 2 Charge (0/21m, 28i).<br /> <br /> -19i. M-Y resets to 3i and moves to Short Range.<br /> <br /> Ganan: 28i (4/23m, 3WP, 3a, 7L(-1)) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form, 2 Charge<br /> Mata-Yadh: 3i (50m, 4WP, 11B (-0)), Short Range<br /> <br /> Round 19<br /> <br /> 28i. Ganan Reflexive moves to Close and unleashes a Decisive Smash (27i) backed by a 3m Excellency, Force of the Mountain, and Bone Crushing Strike (4/13m, 1 Charge). He rolls 18 dice vs Parry 0, hitting, then rolls 27i (doube-10s, rr6s) for (12-1) 11B capped at 8B with Bone-Crushing. Ganan resets to 3i, Mata-Yadh is knocked prone.<br /> <br /> 3i. M-Y Flurries.<br /> <br /> It spends WP (3WP) on Rise From Prone, rolling 4 dice for 3 successes, rising.<br /> <br /> It attacks for (16 \u2013 3 Bone Crushing \u2013 3 Flurry) 10 dice. Ganan will go all out to defend on Parry 4 (4/4m, 2WP). M-Y rolls 4 successes, hitting, then rolls 23 dice of damage for 10i (19i/-7i).<br /> <br /> Ganan: -7i (4/9m, 2WP, 3a, 7L(-1)) Earth Aura, Earth Dragon Form, 1 Charge<br /> Mata-Yadh: 19i (50m, 3WP, 19B (-0))</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Round 20<br /> <br /> 19i. Mata-Yadh (19B) Decisives (13 dice vs Parry 4), hitting (7 successes), rolling 19i for 9L, killing Ganan.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> This is why you playtest your House Rules kids.<br /> <br /> It <i>was</i> a lot faster... so not a <i>complete </i>failure, but clearly a failure.<br /> <br /> (And it was a darn close fight -- if Ganan delayed to Clash in round 19 and used Colossal Whirling Strike before moving back a range band, he totally would have won that fight... but the fight would have taken another four rounds and was already too long.)<br /> <br /> Maybe one roll resolution of combat is the order of the day here... condense Soak and Parry as above, but also nix damage rolls -- base it entirely off Threshold successes? Or weapon type? Lemme think about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-20-2020, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T12:07:47-08:00","id":1429206,"title":"","content":"In part, this will be hard because you're struggling against the design goals of the game.<br /> <br /> It often gets forgotten, but if people didn't have infinitely-spammable perfect defenses, 2E fights tended to be over very, very quickly. The whole reason why Withering and Decisive attacks work the way they do is to slow things down and create a lot of back-and-forth before the possibility to end the fight comes online. If you want faster fights, you probably just want to do away with that technology. My first thoughts would be: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Withering attacks just damage people's health, 2E style. You'd have to make some decisions about combining Withering and Decisive Charms on the same attacks. This is, obviously, the most extreme choice, and would have the 2.5E effect of making everyone need lots of Soak.</li> <li>Whenever someone gets Crashed, they cannot fight. In a group fight, you must become Incapacitated, Withdraw, Go To Ground, or try to take actions as a trivial combatant who will die to any hit. If you're alone, this is covered by the Hold At Bay rules. Paradoxically, this makes serious fights less deadly, because taking people alive is the default and there's relatively-little incentive to make Decisive attacks. On the other hand, it also opens a powerful combatant up to a lot less vulnerability, because they're not forced to reset down to 3i and maybe get Crashed by a lucky hit.</li> <li>Increase all damage from successful Decisive attacks by 5 levels or so. The idea here is to keep the flow of combat mostly the same, but make it so that it seldom takes more than 1-2 Decisives to finish off even supernaturally-tough enemies. It also would obviously make deadly alpha strikes a lot easier, so you might want to start everyone with less Initiative, or make this a bonus you &quot;unlock&quot; for the rest of the fight the first time you crash someone, or instead outright double Decisive damage.</li> <li>Withering hits give you something like 5+damage Initiative, instead of 1+damage. Often, fights go long because both combatants keep hitting each other for roughly the same amount of damage every round and nobody can build up enough Initiative to accomplish much (or because the Gm thinks it's cute to have enemies with mediocre stats but decent soak outnumber the PCs without collapsing them into a battlegroup), so just globally speeding up Initiative gain could be a solid hack. It would make poor Heavy weapons even more worthless than they already are, though. You might instead give every non-crashed person 3i per round automatically, which makes Withering accuracy less of a godstat, but also makes it less important for people to make Withering attacks at all. But maybe that's a feature?</li> </ol><br /> I do think it's also worth noting that Mata-Yadh being impractical for a one-on-one duel isn't necessarily a bad thing. 3E is in the unenviable position of making it cumbersome to run lots of worthy enemies, whilst also having very few tools to make boss fights work, so the best patch that OPP has come up with is enemies with a ton of -0 HLs and decent attacks, who can soak up attacks from several PCs at once. If even those can be nuked down quickly by a lone non-specialized combat build, there are even fewer options to make a fight climactic without just learning to play 10-15 Exalts at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T12:53:59-08:00","id":1429216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429206#post1429206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In part, this will be hard because you're struggling against the design goals of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the game was designed to be quick, we wouldn't need to house rule fights to be quicker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429206#post1429206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think it's also worth noting that Mata-Yadh being impractical for a one-on-one duel isn't necessarily a bad thing. [...] If even those can be nuked down quickly by a lone non-specialized combat build, there are even fewer options to make a fight climactic without just learning to play 10-15 Exalts at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that a lone combat build <i>can</i> beat Mata-Yadh down. The outcome of that fight isn't really in doubt -- the PC Exalt <b>will</b> win. Mata-Yadh <b>cannot </b>beat an optimized starting Solar Combat Build, let alone fight an entire Circle built 5/5/1 JoJo style.<br /> <br /> (It's an absolutely great opponent if you are, say, fighting the Tomb of Dreams pregens.)<br /> <br /> The problem isn't that a lone combat build can beat the Behemoth. The problem is that it takes <b><u><i>thirty-three</i></u></b> rounds to beat it.<br /> <br /> I know it doesn't seem like it, but I have a life. I don't want to spend 33 rounds playing out a foregone conclusion. And it's not like Mata-Yadh is unique here: all fights against tough opponents take too long. Even if you're fighting 10-15 Exalts at once. Especially if you're fighting 10-15 Exalts at once. Dear god, would I sure like to make fighting 10-15 Exalts at once quicker!<br /> <br /> The idea isn't to make fights <i>easier </i>or more lethal or less climactic: it's to make them <i>quicker </i>to resolve.<br /> <br /> That said I think your ideas have merit. I especially like number 3. Maybe add the Round Number to your Decisive damage? A ticking clock of lethality. I need to think about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T13:10:49-08:00","id":1429222,"title":"","content":"Oh, I agree with all of that.<br /> <br /> But in so far as the likes of Mata-Yadh have a purpose, it's providing a source of moderately-dangerous attacks which cannot be quickly sniped out or easily farmed for Initiative. Much like a battlegroup, it's there to menace the secondary combatants without being something that their more dedicated allies can trivialize, so that 1-2 real combat threats don't get overwhelmed immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T03:54:10-08:00","id":1429327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429128#post1429128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe one roll resolution of combat is the order of the day here... condense Soak and Parry as above, but also nix damage rolls -- base it entirely off Threshold successes? Or weapon type? Lemme think about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A somewhat common house rule that speeds up combat significantly IME is to nix withering damage rolls entirely. Instead, a successful withering hit steals (damage - soak, min. OWV) initiative, <i>without </i>adding threshold successes to damage.<br /> <br /> This also has the added benefit of making Strength and Stamina twice as beneficial while making Dexterity marginally less so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T13:10:00-08:00","id":1429657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429327#post1429327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A somewhat common house rule that speeds up combat significantly IME is to nix withering damage rolls entirely. Instead, a successful withering hit steals (damage - soak, min. OWV) initiative, <i>without </i>adding threshold successes to damage.<br /> <br /> This also has the added benefit of making Strength and Stamina twice as beneficial while making Dexterity marginally less so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This still needs rulings to be made on dice-tricks for damage rolls. I'm thinking, without any test whatsoever, to make it something like:<br /> <br /> - a flat +1 damage for effects that re-roll Xs.<br /> - +1/+3 for double 9s-7s.<br /> <br /> These are not sexy bonuses, but they are quick and dirty.<br /> <br /> Other thoughts:<br /> <br /> - Poison is going to be deadly in this system, but maybe that's not a bad thing. Nowadays, poison is good for the penalties, but not that deadly otherwise.<br /> - Environment Damage will be very deadly. But then again, using the environment against your opponent should count for something. <br /> - Light weapons will be penalized with this rule.<br /> - I have the feeling that solars would be penalized. What's the point of making a full excellency if you do not do more damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T22:47:51-08:00","id":1429921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429075#post1429075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I say as I prepare to run yet another endurance match between an attrition-minded Lunar build and 3 DBs. But I never claimed to make good choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short update on this: after a few runs, it seems to me that it's a pretty even fight between an optimal Essence 2 cat Lunar and three Essence 3 shikari if you CANNOT use Clashes in reply to attacks against someone you are Defend Other-ing, and a solid DB win if you can. Whatever else we have learned from this thread, it bears repeating: however good Clashes look, they're probably better. Also, Defend Other just plain should not exist as written.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should cut out the middle Exalt and run it against a different DB lineup, without any Melee users. Maybe Water Dragon, Earth Dragon, Thrown, for maximum variety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T06:33:10-08:00","id":1429939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429921#post1429921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short update on this: after a few runs, it seems to me that it's a pretty even fight between an optimal Essence 2 cat Lunar and three Essence 3 shikari if you CANNOT use Clashes in reply to attacks against someone you are Defend Other-ing, and a solid DB win if you can. Whatever else we have learned from this thread, it bears repeating: however good Clashes look, they're probably better. Also, Defend Other just plain should not exist as written.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should cut out the middle Exalt and run it against a different DB lineup, without any Melee users. Maybe Water Dragon, Earth Dragon, Thrown, for maximum variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, why do the DBs win clashes in this scenario? Or do the advantages of clashes not come from winning them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T08:37:01-08:00","id":1429953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429939#post1429939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, why do the DBs win clashes in this scenario? Or do the advantages of clashes not come from winning them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short version is: it's not about whether they can win, but how much they must spend to compete.<br /> <br /> The Lunar build in question is a &quot;murderkitty,&quot; pretty similar to what DrLoveMonkey used <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307696#post1307696\">earlier</a> (the main difference is mine being a No-Moon, which is admittedly a non-trivial difference in this fight). After I ran it twice with one close Lunar win and one close Lunar loss, I went back to check why those results were so different from the blowout I remembered, and saw it was mostly down to DLM's murderkitty running out of motes a few rounds in. There's a few reasons for that (my strategy was to only spend 0-2 motes enhancing each withering attack), but the biggest one is this:<br /> <br /> You cannot afford to lowball a clash.<br /> <br /> When you're fighting alone against multiple other excellency-users, mote economy is everything, because when one side can use excellencies and the other cannot, the fight is over. That's why the builds which can even stand a chance against three DBs fall into three categories: absurd alpha strikes which can take out two or more enemies before they get to act, game-warping edge cases that undermine the core assumptions of enemy builds, and mote-efficient attrition machines. The murderkitty falls into that last category, since a combination of Lunar charms and Tiny Creature let them sit on an effective evasion of 11 with very little actual investment. But if they get clashed, suddenly they have to spend 7-17 motes enhancing the attack, and if they do that just two or three times, they run out of motes and have no reliable way to connect with Decisive attacks to actually remove opponents from the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T03:06:39-08:00","id":1430060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429953#post1429953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The short version is: it's not about whether they can win, but how much they must spend to compete.<br /> <br /> The Lunar build in question is a &quot;murderkitty,&quot; pretty similar to what DrLoveMonkey used <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1307696#post1307696\">earlier</a> (the main difference is mine being a No-Moon, which is admittedly a non-trivial difference in this fight). After I ran it twice with one close Lunar win and one close Lunar loss, I went back to check why those results were so different from the blowout I remembered, and saw it was mostly down to DLM's murderkitty running out of motes a few rounds in. There's a few reasons for that (my strategy was to only spend 0-2 motes enhancing each withering attack), but the biggest one is this:<br /> <br /> You cannot afford to lowball a clash.<br /> <br /> When you're fighting alone against multiple other excellency-users, mote economy is everything, because when one side can use excellencies and the other cannot, the fight is over. That's why the builds which can even stand a chance against three DBs fall into three categories: absurd alpha strikes which can take out two or more enemies before they get to act, game-warping edge cases that undermine the core assumptions of enemy builds, and mote-efficient attrition machines. The murderkitty falls into that last category, since a combination of Lunar charms and Tiny Creature let them sit on an effective evasion of 11 with very little actual investment. But if they get clashed, suddenly they have to spend 7-17 motes enhancing the attack, and if they do that just two or three times, they run out of motes and have no reliable way to connect with Decisive attacks to actually remove opponents from the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you using Wood Dragon's Claws to boost MurderKitty's offense (or Last Warrior's Unity and artifact weapons)? You could be having a base accuracy of 21 (23 in clash) if you do and then the mote expenditure to get bonkers accuracy in clash becomes a lot more favorable. (I recall DrLoveMonkey was using the au-naturel kitty, which is a lot less threatening offense wise).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 12-27-2020, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T09:59:12-08:00","id":1430094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1430060#post1430060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you using Wood Dragon's Claws to boost MurderKitty's offense (or Last Warrior's Unity and artifact weapons)? You could be having a base accuracy of 21 (23 in clash) if you do and then the mote expenditure to get bonkers accuracy in clash becomes a lot more favorable. (I recall DrLoveMonkey was using the au-naturel kitty, which is a lot less threatening offense wise).</div> </div> </div> </div>DLM used Smashfists, so you're probably thinking of my earlier fight against three Blood Apes, where I did indeed use the cat with no Artifacts or mutations. This time, I've been using Claws Mutation + Claws of the Silver Moon for Light Weapon stats.<br /> <br /> Since I don't use stunts in my fights (those exist to tilt the game in favor of PCs, so it's not surprising when someone who gets them wins against bad odds), that means 19 dice. Which is good, but this fight's DB melee person is rolling about on par with that in a decisive clash, and does better in a withering one. And they're not exactly the most optimal clasher around - a really scary clash machine could average 13 successes when clashing. Add to that the fact that losing a clash is terrible news for a build that lives by being hard to hit as it grinds foes down, so they cannot risk only spending enough motes to usually win the clash, and a problem emerges. What I had been doing was spending 7m on a full excellency, and debating whether I should also use use another charm or two to lock in the win. 17 motes (Excellency, Finding The Needle's Eye, Snarling Hound Strife, and Striking Mospid Method) was an exageration, so that's my bad, but 11 motes for Excellency + Striking Mospid is not out of the question, and that hurts when you're starting out having already burned 7m on dodge charms, 10m on Join Battle, 10m on Artifact gear, and you never really get motes back for most of the fight due to spamming Golden Tiger Stance every round.<br /> <br /> You do have me wondering about a paired weapon. That means switching from Claws of the Silver Moon to an artifact + Last Warrior's Unity, which costs an extra 1m 1 wp (or using Wood Dragon's Claw like you, but that still costs 1wp), but it's probably worth it. Plus, if I go with Short Daiklaves, that gets me Balanced, which is a big deal when everyone is wearing artifact armor all the time. it does make me sad that this cat will be obviously magical - getting into a fight with a combat Celestial which genuinely appears to be a housecat is so much funnier - but that doesn't matter for this fight, since Yoruichi of Caerbannog is rushing to Totemic Anima right off the bat, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T16:08:49-08:00","id":1430149,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m personally a fan of WDC as that can get you Balanced (or Reaching or Smashing) as required, WDC are considered a paired weapon (so 21 accuracy in clash, no stunts or motes spent) and it has no attunement cost. And of course Evocations to be decided later.<br /> <br /> So overall is the math still that Optimized Celestial can pip two DBs (also combat oriented) but 3 such DBs still have the advantage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 12-27-2020, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T16:47:14-08:00","id":1430152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1430149#post1430149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So overall is the math still that Optimized Celestial can pip two DBs (also combat oriented) but 3 the DBs still have the advantage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically.<br /> <br /> My <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1427325#post1427325\">last go around</a> saw an Essence 2 Lunar win against 3 DBs, but it was very, very close. She had a pretty specialized build which is really well-suited for that kind of fight, too.<br /> <br /> I haven't tested it (though I probably should), but I feel like 3 Essence 2 DBs should be pretty doable for a number of Essence 2 Lunars (and, by extension, Essence 2 Solars without a relevant supernal). As DLM says, Essence 3 DB is a huge power upgrade, so it's no great surprise that those charms have been the most pivotal DB abilities in each fight - mostly Melee clash charms, but also Fiery Blade Attack. Obviously, you'd still have to possess the mote economy for a long fight against Exalts, but honestly that's the only challenge I foresee - the main E1-2 DB Charms which have come up are excellencies.<br /> <br /> And that's worth noting, because most DBs are Essence 2*. Especially ones who are off risking their lives in the Hunt. In an odd way, that makes E2 DBs the most important measure for power in the whole setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* At least, that's how I read &quot;Generations In The Dynasty&quot; on p.100 of What Fire Has Wrought. Someone could instead interpret &quot;young members of the current generation&quot; as including the 60-100 year olds at Essence 3, in which case, nevermind.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T19:47:00-08:00","id":1430171,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's good here, since it doesn't benefit in clashes, but I've also been thinking about Blood Lash as a weapon for Death Kitty.<br /> It's an artifact weapon with nothing committed, several tags (most are only useful for countering specific advantages, but that's better than not countering those) and a free reduction of wound penalties. It also grants some free charms, though only when you have a wound penalty. In particular, I wonder if you can exploit wings + Endless Crimson Coils to grapple people at short range from the ground, bring them into the air, then use your grapple action to drag them, and let go to drop them from medium range, potentially with literally nothing to grab onto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T21:01:49-08:00","id":1430178,"title":"","content":"Oh, I have plans for a flight + ranged grapple build, have no doubt. It seems pretty good, because Exalted inexplicably made falling damage the deadliest of natural hazards when it's totally harmless in most cinematic action fiction... of course, assuming they cannot just negate it with a moderate Athletics roll, which the book implies but doesn't expand on. But that's for later.<br /> <br /> And cat Lunars don't care a ton about wound penalties. They're not exactly Berserkers, but the worst thing about a wound penalty is the defense hit, and they're super immune to that part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T23:33:47-08:00","id":1430186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1430149#post1430149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m personally a fan of WDC as that can get you Balanced (or Reaching or Smashing) as required, WDC are considered a paired weapon (so 21 accuracy in clash, no stunts or motes spent) and it has no attunement cost. And of course Evocations to be decided later.<br /> <br /> So overall is the math still that Optimized Celestial can pip two DBs (also combat oriented) but 3 such DBs still have the advantage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think so, but there's also a lot of complexity there. With the right setup against the right, otherwise powerful, opponents a DB can go 1v5 against Solars. I think it proooobably shakes out something like a very powerful celestial build can take on three combat focused but non-optimal terrestrials at Essence 2, but it tips to the terrestrial's favour at Essence 3, or 5 terrestrials.<br /> <br /> There's also a lot of variables here. For example a Celestial might be packing 5-dot artifacts, and be empowered not only by Wood Dragon Claw, but also Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, Stalwart Earth Guardian, or even sorcerous workings to do things like cause environmental hazards whenever they take decisive damage. You could also stack that with several instances of the Twice-Striking Lightning Prism, so now all effects that use (Essence) are now (Essence + 4). At which point it's probably leaning a lot more towards the celestial, but you kind of have to decide for yourself if that's beyond reason or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T01:43:17-08:00","id":1430190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1430152#post1430152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's worth noting, because most DBs are Essence 2*. Especially ones who are off risking their lives in the Hunt. In an odd way, that makes E2 DBs the most important measure for power in the whole setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That gels with the QCs in the Corebook and my own read. (If that helps.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T02:20:31-08:00","id":1430194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1429921#post1429921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short update on this: after a few runs, it seems to me that it's a pretty even fight between an optimal Essence 2 cat Lunar and three Essence 3 shikari if you CANNOT use Clashes in reply to attacks against someone you are Defend Other-ing, and a solid DB win if you can. Whatever else we have learned from this thread, it bears repeating: however good Clashes look, they're probably better. Also, Defend Other just plain should not exist as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the DBs have clash builds and the time to set up defend other any lone celestial might be done for even if you can't clash for someone you're protecting with defend other, as you can as written, do the reverse and defend other for someone in a clash. Which at least by Vance interpretation of how that works out leaves the person in the clash without someone defending-other for them pretty screwed: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1117984#post1117984\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1117984#post111798</a> <br /> <br /> Even disregarding an edge-case the people who wrote the clash and defend-other rules probably didn't consider, I'm not a fan of how game-warping clashes are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T03:01:03-08:00","id":1430197,"title":"","content":"Just hit the defender.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> That said, Clashes don't need the bonus damage, nor do they need the defence penalty. Just being able to block with an attack (and the various Clash bonuses from Charms and equipment) is powerful enough, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T03:33:46-08:00","id":1430203,"title":"","content":"Yeah but per Vance ruling, that means the clasher still hits you and you eat the penalties for losing a clash. If you mean direct your attack against the person taking defend-other from the start there's nothing in the rules that says you can't take mutual defend-other actions.<br /> <br /> If you let two melee DBs Flame-Warden Stance eachother the one attacked can then Comet Deflection/Fire Incites Water with the other parrying in the clash, which is pretty much a guaranteed clash-loss for the attacker even when they hit the DB that's parrying.<br /> <br /> If you say no on mutual defend other it effectively limits the shenanigans to celestials who can defend other reflexively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T10:29:21-08:00","id":1430244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1430194#post1430194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even disregarding an edge-case the people who wrote the clash and defend-other rules probably didn't consider, I'm not a fan of how game-warping clashes are... If you say no on mutual defend other it effectively limits the shenanigans to celestials who can defend other reflexively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I would definitely argue that, while clashes are overtuned, it's Defend Other that breaks the game. Vance has said elsewhere (though I believe it was in logs of a campaign he was running, so not in an official capacity) that two people Defend Othering each other causes the universe to unravel. That would be a &quot;no&quot; on using that strategy, but also a scathing indictment of how nutso that particular action is. One of the most frustrating things when running fights for this thread is not getting to just implement basic fixes, such as not making a fundamental combat trick throw space-time into madness (I recommend &quot;set you parry equal to the defender's, or get +2, whichever is better&quot; - I would be sympathetic to a flat +2).<br /> <br /> As for Clashes themselves... I get why they work like they do. In other systems with similar &quot;beam war&quot; (Big Eyes, Small Mouth, Mutants &amp; Masterminds) or &quot;Iado duel&quot; (Legend of the Five Rings) mechanics, winning that kind of attack is stronger than hitting with a normal attack, which makes sense because it's (1) often harder, (2) a dramatic moment in play, and most importantly (3) rare. I bet that when Clashes got written into Exalted, they weren't yet thinking about how even DBs would be able to force them using Charms, and it even took this thread a while to adopt Delay -&gt; Clash as a major combat tactic (incidentally, I maintain that if your opponent does that, you answer by taking the Aim action, and just letting them bleed Initiative), so they expected it to be a lot less common.<br /> <br /> But there's another key difference: those other systems don't have Excellencies. When the single biggest pressure in most fights is maintaining effective attacks and defenses as cheaply as you can, only needing to spend motes half as often is a game-changer. That's the biggest way that non-Charm Clashes distort the system, and probably the reason why a damage buff on top always feels like too much. But it also gets into the always-complicated questions of whether Excellencies make for good gameplay, and I'm already running late, so nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T14:01:57-08:00","id":1430261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1430244#post1430244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I maintain that if your opponent does that, you answer by taking the Aim action, and just letting them bleed Initiative</div> </div> </div> </div>Aim is great because it's giving you 3 dice for the next Clash. Aiming every Delay to bleed Initiative probably drags out Arena fights longer than they need to be. And it's not great if it's not one-on-one. But, generally speaking, if someone Delays to Clash and you have Simple Charms to activate, then now is the time to get your buffs up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T14:54:33-08:00","id":1430269,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Simple Charms are also good. In a teamfight, it sometimes makes sense to Full Defense whilst your allies advance their portions of the battle, but that's obviously a losing plan one-on-one. Disengage, if you need an action which still makes them spend motes twice this round. If you're leading a Battlegroup, maybe try Rally For Numbers (ugh, that name), but I'm less sure of that, since I wouldn't let someone clash a BG unless they had a Charm which explicitly allowed that.<br /> <br /> Mostly, just never attack into it unless you're REALLY sure that you have the advantage - they've already spent resources trying to force you to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T02:22:50-08:00","id":1430318,"title":"","content":"Actually, having slept on it, the dramatic thing to do is probably social influence.<br /> <br /> Your foe is there, waiting for you to attack. They're not attacking until you do. Their advantage in this combat is steadily bleeding away. Now is the time to try and talk them down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-30-2020, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T08:10:15-08:00","id":1430462,"title":"","content":"Plus, mechanically speaking, lots of strong combat characters a Resolve of around 4 (6-7 with excellencies), and if you win with a Threaten action or the like, they'll have to spend WP.<br /> <br /> Not a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T22:42:18-08:00","id":1438255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438036#post1438036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've done the worst thing I could possibly imagine: now I want to run a game for this character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What's her name?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if I do it first!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's late summer afternoon in the village, the farmers who've come in that day have mostly unloaded their hauls and are now milling about socializing. Heriat is herself looking to pick up some pulleys to use as torque converters. This is when a large group of men walk into town, 30 or more, they're armed and armoured, and their leader bears the wicked scar of deadly combat on his face. They tell everyone there is a new king, a king in the forest, and he demands fealty. Everyone must offer up a token of tribute to prove this. Heriat hops up on her horse, Checkerbloom, and trots over. She tells them there's only one king collecting taxes, and nobody here is going to get grifted by some common thugs, to emphasize the point she draws her spear.<br /> <br /> Size 2 battlegroup of medium infantry and a brigand leader<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Soldiers roll in with 5i<br /> Their leader 7i<br /> Heriat spends 4m peripheral to get 10i<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> =============<br /> Heriat sweeps forward and strikes down a decisive blow against the leader, using 3m to excellent strike and 1m for an excellency. Rolling 10 dice+1 for only 3 even after the rerolls, missing!<br /> <br /> Soldiers 5i<br /> Leader 7i<br /> Heriat 8i 13per 25iph<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> The leader orders his men to get her in an engage action, rolling 7 dice for 2 successes.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> The brigands attack with an intent to engage with 10 dice, Heriat spends 4m to raise her parry to 8, but can't think up a good stunt. They miss with 5 successes<br /> <br /> Soldiers 2i<br /> Leader 7i<br /> Heriat 8i 13per 21iph<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> =============<br /> <br /> Soldiers 2i<br /> Leader 7i<br /> Heriat 8i 13per 26iph<br /> <br /> <br /> Heriat tries to decisive gain, with the same stuff, this time hitting easily, and rolling 3L damage<br /> <br /> Soldiers 2i<br /> Leader 7i 3L(-1)<br /> Heriat 3i 13per 22iph<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Soldiers leader will give them another order, don't engage, cut her down! She's just a little girl! This time getting 3 successes.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Soldiers will attack with their long spears, negating the mounted bonus, and roll 10 dice. Heriat will spend 4m and stunt to increase her parry to 8. They miss again with only 4 successes<br /> <br /> Soldiers 2i<br /> Leader 7i 3L(-1)<br /> Heriat 3i 13per 18iph<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> =============<br /> <br /> Soldiers 2i<br /> Leader 7i 3L(-1)<br /> Heriat 3i 13per 23iph<br /> <br /> <br /> Fine! I'll do it myself! The leader yells, swinging his axe at Heriat in a decisive strike, who will spend another 4 motes and stunt. Rolling 8 dice gives the commander 5 successes, missing again.<br /> <br /> Soldiers 2i<br /> Leader 5i 3L(-1)<br /> Heriat 3i 13per 23iph<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> Heriat will now act, throwing a withering strike at the leader with Excellent Strike, rolling 11+1 dice for 10 after rerolling two 1s into a 7 and a 10!<br /> <br /> Then rolling 10 damage for 8, easily crashing the leader.<br /> <br /> Soldiers 2i<br /> Leader -3i 3L(-1) -1 Onslaught<br /> Heriat 17i 13per 20iph<br /> <br /> <br /> Now Heriat will use 3m to One Weapon Two Blows, and attack him with a decisive strike, hitting easily and dealing 6 damage and evicerating the leader. The battlegroup breaks and flees at this ultimate display.<br /> <br /> Soldiers 2i Fledd<br /> Leader -3i Dedd<br /> Heriat 17i 13per 17iph Ahedd</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With that Heriat is left to wonder what on the plane that was all about, as the soldiers flee they call back that she'll be sorry. She tells them to stay out and sits back down to the cheers and applause of everyone present. She doesn't have to wonder for long though, only an hour later she hears screams coming from the edge of the village. She rides out quickly to them and finds a monstrocity. Some horrible amalgam of man, lion and scorpion stalks forward, growling about tribute to its grand self. Heriat walks out to meet it, and asks what right it has to tribute from these people. It tells her that it is in need of a champion, one as powerful as her, and that she could now offer herself as tribute or be slain here. Against this threaten roll she brings her intimacy to the village to bear, giving her a resolve of 7, Five successes fail to convince her with the threat, so she prepares to spear it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Manticore 10i<br /> Heriat 8i 13per 27iph<br /> <br /> <br /> Round 1<br /> ===========<br /> The manticore will attempt a grapple gambit, Heriat will spend 6m from her personal and use a willpower to raise her parry to 10 with a stunt, with 11 dice and a willpower the manticore misses with 8 successes.<br /> <br /> Rolling 10 dice confirms the grapple.<br /> <br /> Manticore 8i<br /> Heriat 8i 7per 23iph<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> Heriat will attack back using an excellent strike, and 4m excellency from per personal pool. Rolling 15+1 dice for a total of 6. Rolling 5 damage for only 2.<br /> <br /> Manticore 6i -1 onslaught<br /> Heriat 11i 0per 23iph<br /> <br /> Round 2<br /> ===========<br /> Manticore 6i<br /> Heriat 11i 0per 28iph<br /> <br /> Deciding she needs to get an advantage fast Heriat strikes with a decisive, spending to excellent strike and full excellency agian, sending her castemark glittering. Manticore will stunt defense and use a willpower, hissing Solar!<br /> <br /> Rolling 13 dice for 9 after rerolls, hitting easily. Then rolling 11 damage for 4L<br /> <br /> <br /> Manticore 6i 4L(-1) -2 Onslaught<br /> Heriat 3i 0per 21iph<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> The Manticore will attack, with a withering 12 dice, just wanting to crash Heriat, who will defend with a 6m excellency and stunt. Rolling 13 dice for 4 and missing terribly. Her anima is now glowing.<br /> <br /> Manticore 6i 4L(-1)<br /> Heriat 3i 0per 15iph -1 onslaught<br /> <br /> Round 3<br /> ===========<br /> <br /> The Manticore will attack, with a withering 14 dice, again just wanting to crash Heriat and stunting this time, also spending a willpower and dipping swallow, who will defend with a 6m excellency and stunt and willpower. Rolling 13 dice for 4 and missing terribly. Her anima is now blazing.<br /> <br /> Again another miss, although just barely with 9 successes<br /> <br /> <br /> Manticore 6i 4L(-1)<br /> Heriat 3i 0per 7iph -2 Onslaught<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> Heriat will attack with Excellent Strike, withering and rolling 9 dice for an amazing 9 successes against the willpower boosted defense of 5. Then rolling 9 damage for 3.<br /> <br /> Manticore 3i 4L(-1) -1 Onslaught<br /> Heriat 7i 0per 4iph<br /> <br /> Heriat will pay 3m for One Weapon Two Blows and wither again. Rolling 11 dice for 4 and hitting. Then rolling 5 damage for only one<br /> <br /> Manticore 2i 4L(-1) -2 Onslaught<br /> Heriat 9i 0per 1iph<br /> <br /> Round 4<br /> ===========<br /> Manticore 2i 4L(-1) -2 Onslaught<br /> Heriat 9i 0per 6iph<br /> <br /> Heriat will go for a decisive attack, rolling 8 dice for 6, hitting easily and then hammering 9 damage for 3, putting the manticore into -2s<br /> <br /> <br /> Manticore 2i 3L(-2) -3 Onslaught<br /> Heriat 4i 0per 6iph<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> The manticore lashes out with one last ditch effort, stunting and rolling 13 dice and spending a willpower on a withering claw, Heriat will use a 6m excellency and a willpower as well. Rolling 8 total successes it misses<br /> <br /> Manticore 2i 3L(-2)<br /> Heriat 4i 0per 0iph<br /> <br /> Round 5<br /> ===========<br /> Manticore -4i 3L(-2)<br /> Heriat 16i 0per 5iph<br /> <br /> Heriat will launch a withering attack, rolling 11 dice for 6 and hitting, and then rolling 8 for 6 damage, crashing the manticore<br /> <br /> Manticore -4i 3L(-2)<br /> Heriat 16i 0per 5iph<br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> The manticore attempts one more claw, stunting for 13 dice against Heriat's boosted 8 parry, and rolling an amazing 10, hitting by two. Rolling 10 damage dice for four, not quite getting out of crash, still a chance for initiative shift.<br /> <br /> Manticore 0i 3L(-2)<br /> Heriat 12i 0per 1iph<br /> <br /> Round 6<br /> ===========<br /> <br /> Manticore 0i 3L(-2)<br /> Heriat 12i 0per 6iph<br /> <br /> Heriat launches a decisive with excellent strike, rolling 5 successes and hitting, and then 7 damage, slaying the monster dead at last.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> She couldn't do it without causing her anima to flare up, she's now a burning pillar of unholy light in front of her entire town, but that monster is dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Soon she's going to pick up a daiklave, an elegant weapon of a bygone golden age. She's also considering investing in some armor because that fight against the manticore was legit tense. If that first grapple had hit I think she would have lost that fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T23:01:12-08:00","id":1438264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1438255#post1438255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soon she's going to pick up a daiklave, an elegant weapon of a bygone golden age. She's also considering investing in some armor because that fight against the manticore was legit tense. If that first grapple had hit I think she would have lost that fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha.'Hokey religions and ancient weapons are no match against a good crossbow at your side kid'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T19:48:58-07:00","id":1440533,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if this has been asked before: who is the better grappler? E1 Solar vs E1 Lunar. <br /> <br /> Round 1: no sorcery, no artifacts, no hearthstones, no demons or battlegroups etc. Lunar can shapeshift. 1 on 1 fight. <br /> <br /> Round 2: Artifacts, Sorcery, Hearthstones ok. Lunar can still shapeshift. No BGs or demons, 1 on 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 03-18-2021, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T20:53:24-07:00","id":1440535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1440533#post1440533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this has been asked before: who is the better grappler? E1 Solar vs E1 Lunar. <br /> <br /> Round 1: no sorcery, no artifacts, no hearthstones, no demons or battlegroups etc. Lunar can shapeshift. 1 on 1 fight. <br /> <br /> Round 2: Artifacts, Sorcery, Hearthstones ok. Lunar can still shapeshift. No BGs or demons, 1 on 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Warstriders included in artifacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T20:59:30-07:00","id":1440536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1440533#post1440533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this has been asked before: who is the better grappler? E1 Solar vs E1 Lunar.<br /> <br /> Round 1: no sorcery, no artifacts, no hearthstones, no demons or battlegroups etc. Lunar can shapeshift. 1 on 1 fight.<br /> <br /> Round 2: Artifacts, Sorcery, Hearthstones ok. Lunar can still shapeshift. No BGs or demons, 1 on 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's much of a question here. An Essence 1 Solar has access to Essence 5 Solar Brawl/MA charms. Which means stuff like Titan-Straigtening Method, which lets you sacrifice all your rounds of control to make that many withering attacks in a row, right away, and then once those attacks crash the Lunar Raging Wrath Repeated triggers and refunds all of the expended rounds of control to the Solar and also resets their combat action, which they can then use in combination with Crashing Wave Throw to boost the damage further, and also force them to contend with falling damage, that charm itself chains into Lightning Strikes Twice, allowing them to bounce off the surface they just took fall damage from, right BACK into the Solar's waiting arms and causes their initiative not to reset from that previous combo, letting them make another grapple roll to grab them and launch into ANOTHER Crashing Wave Throw, with another round of falling damage.<br /> <br /> Also they have a charm in Brawl that says even if they go second in the combat actually they go first anyway.<br /> <br /> Now Lunars have cool shit that can slay almost anything. They have cool grapple charms that do awesome stuff too, but Winding Constrictor Coils is Essence 2, Foe-Pinning Strike is Essence 3, and so is Jaws of the River Dragon. At Essence 1 they can get Legendary Size, which lets them become a creature so massive that straight up you do not get a roll to oppose their grapple, they just win, and the only question is by how much.<br /> <br /> <br /> Except against Solars, because Dragon Coil Technique wags its finger at that and says &quot;no-no, I do get to roll anyway, and I get bonus auto successes on the attack <i>and</i> control roll, and all your 10s count as successes for me as well as you. This is a 3m charm.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T00:44:37-07:00","id":1440561,"title":"","content":"Depends on the level of investment. I could see a Lunar with only one Charm beating out a Solar with only one Charm.<br /> <br /> A Physical Tertiary No Moon is probably a better grappler than a Physical Tertiary Twilight. (&quot;I turn into a Sky Titan.&quot; Makes you the best at a surprising number of things.)<br /> <br /> But there's no way a Supernal Brawl Solar loses to an Essence 1 Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T02:34:27-07:00","id":1440568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there's no way a Supernal Brawl Solar loses to an Essence 1 Lunar. </div> </div> </div>I agree that the Solar would probably win in most cases, but I still don\u2019t know that I\u2019d say \u201c<i>no</i> way.\u201d She could, for instance, trick the Solar into wasting his once-per-scenes and a shit-ton of motes attacking an illusory double, or one of his own allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T04:47:11-07:00","id":1440577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1440568#post1440568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the Solar would probably win in most cases, but I still don\u2019t know that I\u2019d say \u201c<i>no</i> way.\u201d She could, for instance, trick the Solar into wasting his once-per-scenes and a shit-ton of motes attacking an illusory double, or one of his own allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Solar could roll all 3s whilst the Lunar rolls all 9s. On every die for every roll.<br /> <br /> Likewise the OP only specified Essence 1. A starting character Solar built with Brawl 1 vs an Essence 1 Lunar who has spent 1000 Lunar Experience is going to go to the Lunar.<br /> <br /> There's an outside chance of an invested Lunar Grappler causing an upset.<br /> <br /> My use of &quot;no way&quot; was hyperbolic.<br /> <br /> But even with Lunar trickery, I don't see how a starting character Lunar could reliably beat a starting character Solar at brawling if they both have equal investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T05:50:40-07:00","id":1440583,"title":"","content":"Bottom line, you\u2019re matching a character with full access to all the Solar grapple charms, against one with access to maybe a third of the Lunar ones, and in general the Solar ones are better on top of that. It\u2019s basically a fools errand to try and match an equally invested Solar in something they\u2019re good at.<br /> <br /> Just like it\u2019s likewise a fools errand to try and match the versatility of a Lunar who maxed out their form library with merit dots. You\u2019ll spend every charm and bonus point you have on the melee/archery/mobility/stealth/survival/etc. charms to try and match them and still fall hopelessly short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T06:39:31-07:00","id":1440587,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks. <br /> <br /> When would the outcome be close to 50/50? Like say at E3 or E5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 03-19-2021, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T08:38:33-07:00","id":1440601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1440587#post1440587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, thanks. <br /> <br /> When would the outcome be close to 50/50? Like say at E3 or E5.</div> </div> </div> </div> Difficult to say, my best guess would be closest at Essence 2. The thing is when you get to Essence 5 the Lunar does have all of their tricks, finally, but also you\u2019ve got things like Dragon Coil, which adds (Essence) automatic successes to both the attack and control roll of a grapple, and getting opponents successes and letting you grapple legendary sized things. Which at Essence 5 basically equates to getting 25+ motes worth out of a 3 mote charm. <br /> <br /> I might run a fight at Essence 2 though, where most of the lunar tricks are working but the Solar (Essence) abilities haven\u2019t become stupid good yet.<br /> <br /> Really though you just don\u2019t beat Solars at their thing. Tonight I\u2019ll also do up a list of why Solars can\u2019t compete with Lunars at their thing either though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T16:15:09-07:00","id":1442903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1428169#post1428169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did specifically address this. But if you want concrete advice:<br /> <br /> Take a 5 in your Supernal.<br /> Take a 3 in everything you are exceptionally good at.<br /> Take a 2 in everything you are good at.<br /> Take a 1 in anything you are vaguely interested in.<br /> <br /> If you don't meet the Charm minimums, don't buy the Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, some versions of Shining Topaz that I've run in the thread fit this criteria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}